cmnknk460000hewhjt8155ngb	cmnknk45y000gewhjn5pl0kw9	Lesson 9 — The Dispensation of Innocence	READING	3661	0	\N	t	What would human life look like with no sin, no shame, no fear, and no knowledge of evil? That's not a fantasy — it was the actual historical condition of the first man and woman in Eden. And the dispensation of Innocence is the only time in human history that experiment was run. Understanding how it ended tells us something deeply important about free will, testing, and what God actually wants from us.\n\nLast time we watched God rebuild a ruined world in six days. Now He places two people in it — and the question becomes: what will they do with the perfect environment He's given them?\n\nAs we study each dispensation, there are nine key points you'll want to understand if you're going to really grasp what God was doing in that period. Here they are:\n\n- The definition of the name of the dispensation.\n- The length of the dispensation.\n- The favorable beginning for man in each age.\n- The test for man in each period.\n- The purpose of God in each test for man.\n- The means of God in accomplishing His purpose.\n- The failure of man to meet the test.\n- The judgment of God upon man because of his failure.\n- God's provision of redemption for man at the end of each age.\n\nOnce you learn these nine points for each of the seven dispensations, God's plan for humanity becomes remarkably simple to understand. Think of it like learning the rules of a board game—once you know the structure, every move makes sense.\n\nIf you'll study these periods carefully and concentrate on how all the parts connect to God's whole purpose, you'll find that every important question gets answered. The mysteries that once seemed so difficult will clear up, and the rest will become simple to solve as you study with these facts in mind.\n\nYou'll be able to see things from God's standpoint—what He had in mind before He even began bringing His plan to pass, as revealed in the Scriptures.\n\n---\n\n![Lesson 9 — The Dispensation of Innocence](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsCGcp5Re78vbPqVLiKnDy6up93CGaNzkh5HsQ)\n\n## I. Definition of Innocence\n\nThe word "innocence" is pretty straightforward. It simply means being without any consciousness of evil—harmlessness, freedom from crime, guilt, or sin. An innocent person is one who hasn't violated any law, who is guiltless, sinless, pure, upright, and harmless.\n\nWhen we apply "innocence" to a period of time or dispensation, we're describing an age of sinlessness on the part of the person responsible to rule for God. Adam was perfectly innocent when God placed him in the Garden of Eden.\n\nHe wasn't even self-conscious enough to be ashamed of his nakedness. "They were both naked, the man and his wife, and were not ashamed" (Gen. 2:25). It was only after sin entered that they became self-conscious: "The eyes of them both were opened, and they knew that they were naked" (Gen. 3:7).\n\nWhen a person exists in this state, we could say they're God-conscious—perfectly innocent of all wrongdoing. In the Fall, man lost this God-consciousness and gained self-consciousness instead. Conscience was awakened, and both man and woman became sinners, knowing by experience both good and evil.\n\nWe call this the Dispensation of Innocence because man was tested during this first probationary period while he was still in a state of innocence. He was tested regarding right and wrong—whether he would freely exercise his will while still sinless and free from all evil.\n\n---\n\n## II. The Length of the Dispensation of Innocence\n\nWe don't know exactly how long the Dispensation of Innocence lasted. But judging from Satan's character and how he's dealt with people throughout history, we can reasonably conclude that he didn't let God's work go very long before trying to defeat it.\n\nSatan was jealous of Adam and wouldn't have been satisfied with a man ruling in his place as governor of the earth. He no doubt got busy immediately to cause man's fall and regain dominion of the restored earth through man.\n\nOn the chart, you'll notice we've marked this dispensation as six days followed by a question mark. We don't know for certain, but putting it at about one week probably isn't far off. Here's why:\n\n> 1. Satan doesn't leave people alone for very long today, unless he already controls them and there's no fight to be had.\n\n> 2. The record of man's creation and fall flows continuously without any break or time gap between them, suggesting they followed each other in close succession.\n\n> 3. We only have record of God resting on one sabbath day (Gen. 2:1-3).\n\n> 4. The next statement about God is that He was walking in the Garden in the cool of the day (Gen. 3:8). This had to be after the sabbath of rest, since God rested on that day.\n\n> 5. Neither Adam nor Eve had yet visited or eaten from the Tree of Life. When they sinned, they were driven out of the Garden and kept from this tree so they wouldn't eat of it and live forever (Gen. 3:22-24).\n\n> 6. Both the Tree of Life and the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil were evidently shown to man so he could distinguish them from all other trees and know which was forbidden. The fact that they went first to the Tree of Knowledge suggests their curiosity was aroused—and when curiosity gets stirred up, people generally don't wait long to satisfy it.\n\n> 7. The serpent was near the forbidden tree when man came to satisfy his curiosity—curiosity that was likely aroused when God gave the commandment not to eat of it. That happened on the day of man's creation when he was placed in the Garden. Man could have sinned the very next day while God was resting, since there's no command for man to rest and no record that he did rest that day. It would have been ridiculous to ask man to rest before he'd worked even one day. His first day of work was the day he was created—he named the animals, which was a good day's work for anyone! If God had taught him to rest on the seventh day after six days' work, Adam's first sabbath would have been on the fourth day of the second week, not the seventh day.\n\n> 8. Adam fell before he knew his wife and had children, because the first children born were just as sinful as children born today—death has passed upon all men, for all have sinned (Rom. 5:12-21). This proves he sinned within just a few days. He was married to the woman on Day 6 of Earth's restoration, for he said that day, "This is now bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh: she shall be called Woman, because she was taken out of Man. Therefore shall a man leave his father and his mother, and shall cleave unto his wife: and they shall be one flesh" (Gen. 2:21-25). Judging that he was a normal man, he wouldn't have waited indefinitely to love his wife and carry out his creative purpose. Few men, if any, wait a week to fulfill the purpose of marriage—and we can believe Adam was no exception. So we conclude he sinned before Eve conceived, and man wasn't in a state of innocence very long before eating the forbidden fruit.\n\nNow, we need to add something important here: the forbidden fruit was *not* intercourse with his wife, as some who rebel against truth teach. He was created for that very purpose—otherwise he could never multiply and replenish the Earth as God commanded on the first day of his existence (Gen. 1:26-28). He was commanded to have children but forbidden to eat of the tree. These couldn't have been the same act.\n\nThe forbidden fruit was simply a natural fruit that grew on a tree, as Scripture plainly states: "The Lord God planted a garden eastward in Eden . . . And out of the ground made the Lord God to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil . . . And the Lord God commanded the man, saying, Of every tree in the garden thou mayest freely eat: But of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, thou shalt not eat of it: for in the day that thou eatest thereof thou shalt surely die . . . The woman saw that the tree was good for food . . . she took of the fruit thereof, and did eat, and gave also to her husband with her; and he did eat" (Gen. 2:9, 16-17; 3:1-6, 11-12).\n\nIt's pure nonsense to claim that such simple language about eating fruit from a tree was really about sexual intercourse. The words "food" and "eat" appear 14 times in Gen. 2-3, proving that natural food and real eating caused the Fall. The Tree of Knowledge is listed among many other trees in the Garden—it's just as easy to prove that eating from *every* tree was sexual intercourse as to prove it for just this one tree.\n\nRight from the start of our Bible study, we must learn to reject the foolish theories of men and believe what is plainly written. This is the only way to gain a working knowledge of the Bible. If we're going to question and throw out what's written, we might as well put the Bible away forever. We'll receive less judgment in the end than if we change everything it says.\n\nTaking the Bible literally enables us to get a simple knowledge of the truth about what caused man to fall and when. There's no mystery attached to the Fall, and there can be no misunderstanding if we believe what God's Word actually says.\n\nThe Fall could have been caused by doing *anything* God commanded man not to do. It wasn't the nature of the fruit that caused sin—it was disobedience to God that constituted the sin. This is plainly stated in Rom. 5:12-21: "For if by one man's offense . . . by one man's disobedience many were made sinners, so by the obedience of one shall many be made righteous."\n\nAgain, "where no law is, there is no transgression," and "sin is the transgression of the law" (Rom. 4:15; 1 Jn. 3:4). If man had been told not to do any one of a thousand different acts, breaking any one commandment would have constituted the sin that caused the Fall and brought the death penalty.\n\n---\n\n## III. The Favorable Beginning of Man in Innocence (Gen. 1:26-30; 2:8-24)\n\nMan and woman, fresh from the Creator's hand, had everything going for them:\n\n- Physical, spiritual, and eternal life\n- Communion and fellowship with God and all creatures in the new creation\n- Dominion over that creation\n- The revealed will of God, His law, and knowledge of both penalties and rewards\n- God-consciousness, or innocence\n- A natural disposition of love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith, meekness, and self-control\n- The power to make free choices and rule his dominion while defending it from all enemies\n- A right to attain an even higher glory if he proved true in his test\n\nMan was a miniature of God in his soul and spirit faculties, with a physical body made in the image and likeness of God. He was uncorrupt, free from prejudices, sinful lusts, and all evil. He existed in a highly enlightened state with a glorious spiritual, moral, and mental makeup. He could enjoy the pleasures of that state to the full.\n\nHe had power over Satan and all fallen spirits loose in the Earth. He could have resisted them and remained true to God if he had wanted to. His animal and sensitive natures were free to enjoy themselves in everything except the one forbidden tree. Nothing else he could have done would have been sin at that time.\n\nAs time went on, God would no doubt have revealed more of His moral law and government. But at that moment, there was only one command to obey.\n\nMan's body was perfect. His senses were quick and lively, able to perform their various operations with vigor and delight. He enjoyed nature in all its original beauty, purity, and harmony—revealing the goodness of the Creator.\n\nHis soul passions, appetites, feelings, and desires, along with his spirit-faculties, were in perfect union with God and were exercised with dignity over the new Earth and everything in it.\n\nHe enjoyed the fullness of natural, spiritual, and eternal life and could have remained in that condition simply by obeying one commandment. The law of his nature contained those moral principles concerning good and evil that measured his duty to God, to the universe, and to himself and his posterity. He understood fully the law, its penalties, and his great responsibility.\n\nGod placed in man's reasonable spirit and sensitive soul the principle and power of obedience, and He made a covenant with man on the condition of obedience. Man was perfectly holy, but in a changeable state. He was sinless, but capable of sin. He was eternal, but placed on probation. He was invested with power to prevent his falling, yet lived under the possibility of it. He was complete in his being, but receptive to sinful impressions.\n\nMan had a wonderful helper in his wife, created from one of his ribs. Just as it's true today, a woman can either make or break a man.\n\nOf woman's creation, Matthew Henry beautifully says, "Not out of man's head to be topped by him, nor out of his feet to be trampled on by him, but out of his side to be equal with him; under his arm to be protected by him, and from near his heart to be beloved by him."\n\nThis expresses that man and woman were meant to be partners in life. If both had cooperated with God, the curse never would have come. There would have been no sin, no sickness, no death, no pain, no failure, no unhappiness in all creation—and no cancellation of eternal life.\n\nBefore the Fall, man wasn't supposed to be lazy. God put him in the Garden to dress it and keep it (preserve it from enemies, as expressed in Gen. 3:24; 17:9-10; 18:19). He was to eat of the wonderful fruits, nuts, grains, and vegetables growing in the restored Earth. He was to reproduce his own kind and keep them obedient to God and in harmony with all creation.\n\nHe was free to use the whole creation for the best good of all concerned. He was to consecrate himself to the best and highest good of being and of the universe, and remain a free and eternal subject of the Moral Governor of all.\n\nThese and other favorable conditions made it entirely and easily possible for man to remain true to his trust and rule the Earth for God forever.\n\n---\n\n## IV. The Test—Man on Probation (Gen. 2:16-17)\n\nMan was created as a free moral agent, so he needed to be tested to see whether he would remain true to God before being placed in the eternal responsibility God had in mind for him. (See Lesson One, Point VIII, for a full discussion of why man had to be tested.)\n\nAdam had the power to choose for himself whether to obey or disobey God. He simply needed to be told what God's will was. God made known His will, the rewards of obedience, and the penalty for disobedience—so there was no excuse for man to choose evil and cooperate with the enemy of both God and man.\n\nBeing created with power to prevent his own Fall and with free choice in the matter, man was and still is held entirely responsible to God for his choice and its results.\n\nAdam was placed on probation—a trial period. Think of it like a new employee's probationary period at work, except the stakes were infinitely higher. If he had proved true, he would have attained a higher glory than before (Rom. 3:23) and could have lived forever enjoying the fruits of obedience.\n\nThe penalty for sin was eternal death, so naturally the reward for obedience was life—eternal life. He would have lived forever, physically as well as spiritually.\n\nIf you can imagine how man would have continued forever physically, multiplying and living a natural existence, you can also imagine how this will be true in the New Earth. When the curse is removed and man is again placed in the sinless state he was in before the Fall, there will be eternal generations of natural people on Earth, as we've proven in Supplement Two, Question 2.\n\nEven after the Fall, man could have lived forever if he had eaten of the Tree of Life. The reason God drove him out of the Garden and placed cherubim to guard the Tree of Life was "lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever" (Gen. 2:22-24).\n\nIf sinful man could have lived forever physically by eating of the Tree of Life, then certainly natural, redeemed man in the New Earth will also be able to eat of this tree and live forever (Rev. 21:1-7; 22:1-5).\n\nHere's an important point: the fact that man would have lived forever physically even after sinning—if he had eaten of the Tree of Life—proves that the penalty for sin wasn't merely physical death. It was *eternal* death. No fruit from the Tree of Life could have cancelled that eternal death penalty.\n\nWhat the tree *would* have done is make man incapable of dying physically—and therefore incapable of being redeemed from death, Hell, and the grave so he could become a higher being than he ever could be in his natural fallen state.\n\nGod really wanted man to live forever physically, but not in spiritual and eternal death—not separated from Him by sin. So it was in God's plan to redeem man spiritually and eternally *before* placing him back on the Earth to live forever physically.\n\nThe specific test for man in the Dispensation of Innocence was this: he was not to eat of the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil. Failure would result in losing his dominion and fellowship with God.\n\nIt would seem that sinless, perfect man could have obeyed one simple law—especially when sinful, imperfect people today are obligated to keep many laws! It would seem man could have kept himself true to God, when today redeemed man lives in righteousness and true holiness according to the gospel (Rom. 6:1-23; 8:1-13; 12:1-2; Gal. 5:16-26; Eph. 4:22-24; Titus 2:11-13; 3:5-7; 1 Jn. 1:7-9; 2:29; 3:7-10; 5:1-4, 18).\n\n---\n\n## V. The Purpose of God in This Dispensation\n\nGod's purpose in testing man while in a state of innocence was to see whether or not man would obey Him—so He could trust him with an eternal responsibility connected to the Earth and God's universal kingdom.\n\nGod had watched Lucifer, the first ruler of the Earth, become lifted up in pride and rebel against His sovereignty. So it was only natural for God to test the new ruler of the Earth to see if he would exalt himself as Satan did (Isa. 14:12-14; Ezek. 28:11-17; 1 Tim. 3:6).\n\nGod planned that if man fell, he should do it *before* eating of the Tree of Life—so he wouldn't have to live forever in a sinful state. That's why God tested man soon after creation instead of later in life.\n\nGod further intended that if man fell, he should do it *before* having offspring. That way his children could be born on the same level with himself, allowing God to have mercy upon all alike.\n\nThis kind of plan made all people equally dependent upon God for needed grace for body, soul, and spirit. It gave every person the same opportunity to be saved or lost as they freely chose.\n\nGod wanted to demonstrate to man that He wasn't the tyrant Lucifer and other fallen spirits accused Him of being. As it stands now in God's plan for man, God can speedily and eternally redeem the race and the Earth to perfection—just as it was before the Fall—and be assured His plan for man throughout all eternity will never be marred again.\n\n---\n\n## VI. The Means of God in Accomplishing this Purpose\n\nThe restriction from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil and the temptations offered by the devil—these were the means God used in testing man's ambitions to become like God (Gen. 3:1-6).\n\nBecoming like God had been Lucifer's main desire. He had said in his heart, "I will ascend into heaven, I will exalt my throne above the stars of God . . . I will be like the most High" (Isa. 14:12-14).\n\nLucifer knew that the way to become *unlike* God was to exalt self. He also knew that if he could appeal to man to misuse his faculty of humility—which is the glory of the creature and his native makeup—he could cause God to curse man.\n\nWithout the tempter, the first man might have remained true to God. But he was attacked by the most subtle of spirit-beings, who used the most subtle of Adam's creatures to cause man to fall and corrupt himself along with all his posterity (Rom. 5:12-21), as we'll study in the next point.\n\n---\n\n## Earth's Second Sinful Career (Gen. 3:1—Rev. 20:15)\n\n## VII. The Failure of Man—The Fall\n\nIn Gen. 3, Rom. 5:12-21, 1 Tim. 2:13-14, and other passages, we have a simple record of man's fall—including what caused it. Here's something vital to understand: without a clear faith in the fall of man, there can be no clear faith in the redemption of man.\n\nThose who preach and teach that man didn't really fall—or that if he did, he "fell upward"—that man is simply a victim of environment and incapable of sin—such beliefs can never lead souls to redemption from sin through Jesus Christ. They destroy the very foundation of Scripture and of man's eternal life and hope.\n\nYou must believe in the Fall to be saved. Jesus Christ didn't come to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance (Mt. 9:13). If man never had a fall, he could never be redeemed. Likewise, if a person doesn't believe they're a sinner, they can't be saved.\n\nRepentance is required for salvation (Mk. 1:4; 6:12; Lk. 13:1-10; 24:47; Acts 2:38; 3:19; 17:30; 1 Jn. 1:7-9). This is the chief fundamental of the Gospel of Christ, which is the power of God unto salvation to all who believe (Rom. 1:16; 1 Jn. 1:7-9; Rev. 1:5-6; Eph. 1:7).\n\nIn Gen. 3 we have the historical record of man's fall. If anyone denies this truth, they're incapable of true faith in any other part of the Bible, because all Scripture centers around man—his creation, Fall, and redemption through Jesus Christ.\n\nThe cause of the Fall is stated clearly: breaking God's commandment by eating of the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil. God had said, "Of every tree of the garden thou mayest freely eat: But of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, thou shalt not eat of it: for in the day that thou eatest thereof thou shalt surely die" (Gen. 2:16-17).\n\nThe whole temptation centered around this tree and its fruit. Why Adam and Eve happened to go near the forbidden tree isn't stated, so we have to believe they were curious about why God wouldn't permit them to eat from this one tree when all the others were available. At any rate, they were at this tree together, as is clear from the statement: "she took of the fruit thereof, and did eat, and gave also unto her husband with her; and he did eat. And the eyes of them both were opened, and they knew that they were naked" (Gen. 3:6-7).\n\nIt's true that the serpent talked with the woman, but that doesn't prove the man wasn't present. There's no statement that Adam was absent, so we naturally conclude he was there. Here are the main facts of the fall of man:\n\n### 1. DOUBT CONCERNING GOD'S WORD (Gen. 3:1)\n\nThe serpent raised a doubt—a question about whether God really would permit man to eat of every tree in the Garden. Thus, Satan's first utterance in Scripture shows opposition to the Word of God.\n\nSatan's opposition to the Bible accounts for so many false theories about God's Word today. Any theory that teaches God doesn't mean what He says—that adds to, misinterprets, takes from, or changes what Scripture plainly says—is satanic.\n\nAll theories claiming the Bible is hard to understand, or that it's a mystery, or that it means whatever you interpret it to mean, or that one man's interpretation is as good as another, or that it must be changed before it can be understood—these are all satanic.\n\n### 2. ADDITION TO AND MISQUOTING GOD'S WORD (Gen. 3:2-3)\n\nThe woman answered the serpent's doubt by adding to God's Word the statement "neither shall ye touch it"—which is a misquotation of Gen. 2:16-17. God didn't say touching the tree would bring death, only eating of it.\n\n### 3. CONTRADICTION OF GOD'S WORD (Gen. 3:4)\n\nNext, the serpent directly contradicted God's Word from Gen. 2:16-17. God said, "thou shalt surely die," and the devil said through the serpent, "ye shall not surely die."\n\nBoth statements can't be true. You must choose to believe one or the other.\n\nThose who believe God today believe that people will die if they sin. Those who believe Satan believe that people won't die if they sin. This is a definite contrast requiring definite decisions today—just as it required a definite stand from Adam and Eve.\n\nGod still says, "the soul that sinneth, it shall die" (Ezek. 18:4); "If ye live after the flesh, ye shall die" (Rom. 8:1-13); "he that soweth to the flesh shall of the flesh reap corruption" (Gal. 6:7-8); "the end of those things is death . . . For the wages of sin is death" (Rom. 6:14-23); "If any man defile the temple of God, him shall God destroy" (1 Cor. 3:16-17); "they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of God" (1 Cor. 6:9-11; Gal. 5:19-21); and "If we deny him, He also will deny us" (2 Tim. 2:12).\n\nIf you'll honestly read these passages, you'll see they were spoken to Christians (except Ezek. 18:4, which applies to all men). Just as Gen. 2:17 applied to everyone, these passages do too—God cannot be a respecter of persons, allowing one to die for sin but not another (Jas. 2:9).\n\n### 4. MISINTERPRETATION OF GOD'S WORD (Gen. 3:5)\n\nSatan's second statement to the woman through the serpent became the basis of many false doctrines: "Ye shall be as gods."\n\nToday this sounds like: "We all have the God-power in us," or "we are all a part of God," and all we need to do is look to the God within us and use the divine power of which we're a part.\n\n### 5. TEMPTATION TO TRANSGRESS GOD'S WORD (Gen. 3:6)\n\nSatan's appeal that man would become like God was powerful. This desire in itself isn't sin—it's actually a high ideal! Every Christian should strive to be like God.\n\nBut there are two ways to pursue this: the divine way Christ demonstrated, and the selfish, sinful way Lucifer, Adam, and Eve demonstrated. Seeking to become like God through self-gratification and rebellion makes you *unlike* God. But becoming like God through self-emptying and humiliation, as Christ did, is the true path—as we'll see in Lesson Twenty-one.\n\nWhen Eve "saw that the tree was good for food, and that it was pleasant to the eyes, and a tree to be desired to make one wise," she was tempted to sin.\n\nPaul tells us in 1 Tim. 2:13-15 that Adam was not deceived, but the woman, being deceived, was in the transgression. In 2 Cor. 11:3 we read of Eve being beguiled by the serpent.\n\nThis appeal consists of three main lines of temptation—the only three with which we ever have to deal. John calls them "the lust of the flesh, and the lust of the eyes, and the pride of life" (1 Jn. 2:15-17). These are the same three temptations Christ faced and overcame in the wilderness (Mt. 4:1-11). If you overcome these three, you're an overcomer of Satan, the flesh, and the world.\n\nHere's how these three temptations appear in Gen. 3:6:\n\n> **(1) "Good for food," or "the lust of the flesh."** In Christ's temptation, it was "command that these stones be made bread"—essentially, "you're hungry, make yourself some bread so you can live." Jesus, the second Adam, answered, "man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God." In other words: I won't use my power to satisfy personal appetites and desires. I'll only use my power for others. My appetites are crucified and controlled, and I won't yield them at your suggestion.\n\n> **(2) "Pleasant to the eyes," or "the lust of the eyes."** In Christ's temptation, it was "cast thyself down . . . He shall give his angels charge concerning thee"—essentially, you need personal protection, use your power to preserve your bodily perfection and beauty. Christ answered, "Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God." In other words: I won't use my power for any personal bodily benefit. My body is controlled and yielded to God for the bodily needs of others.\n\n> **(3) "A tree to be desired to make one wise," or "the pride of life."** In Christ's temptation, it was "All these things [the worldly kingdoms and their glory] will I give thee, if thou wilt fall down and worship me"—act wise and yield your spirit to me as Adam did, and be rewarded. Christ answered, "Get thee hence, Satan . . . Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve." In other words: true wisdom and God-likeness is to yield my whole spirit to God for the exaltation of others, not for my own personal gain and glory.\n\n### 6. TRANSGRESSION OF GOD'S WORD (Gen. 3:6)\n\nAdam and Eve went through the same progression of temptation until actual sin was committed—just as many people do today.\n\nJames said, "Every man is tempted, when he is drawn away of his own lust and enticed. Then when lust hath conceived, it bringeth forth sin: and sin when it is finished, bringeth forth death" (Jas. 1:13-16).\n\nSin isn't sin until lust has conceived and the law has been broken. Any temptation short of breaking the law is not sin. Any created faculty exercised along any line is perfectly sinless and legitimate within the bounds of the law. It's only when we exercise these faculties in breaking the law that sin is committed.\n\nThink of it like this: it's similar to driving a car. Driving isn't illegal—but driving through a red light is. The act itself isn't the problem; it's crossing the boundary of the law.\n\nIt was perfectly sinless and legitimate for Adam and Eve to eat and to desire to be like God. The sin was in eating what was *forbidden* by God's law. There's a right and wrong way, a right and wrong time, to exercise our faculties. When we're tempted to use them in self-gratification and sin, the exercise is wrong. But when they're exercised lawfully, no sin is committed.\n\n### 7. THE RESULTS OF TRANSGRESSION OF GOD'S WORD (Gen. 3:7-19)\n\nIn the Fall, man lost spiritual, physical, and eternal life—and gained instead the opposite: spiritual, physical, and eternal death (separation from God). He was cut off from the purpose for which he was created.\n\nHe was created to live forever spiritually, but spiritual death—separation from God by sin—deprives him of that privilege (Isa. 59:2; Eph. 2:1-10).\n\nHe was created to live forever physically, but physical death—the separation of soul and spirit from the body—deprives him of that benefit (Jas. 2:26).\n\nHe was created to live forever both spiritually and physically, but eternal death—eternal separation from God in Hell—deprives him of that great blessing.\n\nThus it became necessary to redeem man—body, soul, and spirit—before he could fulfill the purposes for which he was created.\n\nIn the Fall, man lost the following:\n\n> (1) Spiritual, physical, and eternal life (Isa. 59:2; Eph. 2:1-10; Mt. 25:46).\n\n> (2) Communion and fellowship with God (Isa. 59:2; Col. 1:20).\n\n> (3) Fellowship and pleasure with animals (Gen. 2:19; 9:2).\n\n> (4) Dominion over all the works of God's hands (Ps. 8:3-7).\n\n> (5) Rulership of the Earth (Jn. 14:30; Eph. 6:10-18; 2 Cor. 4:4).\n\n> (6) God-consciousness or innocence (Gen. 2:25; 3:7, 10).\n\n> (7) The power to do good and refuse evil (Gen. 6:5-7; Eph. 2:1-10; Rom. 7).\n\n> (8) God's perfect image and likeness (Phil. 3:20-21).\n\n> (9) Control of soul passions and spirit faculties (Eph. 2:1-10; Gal. 5:19-22).\n\n> (10) The right to the Tree of Life (Gen. 3:22-24).\n\n> (11\n\n---\n\nThe Dispensation of Innocence lasted only as long as the test. One command. One tree. One choice. And the entire human race failed with it. So here's the question that cuts close: God gave Adam and Eve a perfect environment, perfect communion, and one clear boundary — and they still chose the one thing He withheld. What does that tell you about the nature of your own heart? And in what specific area of your life are you currently treating God's one clear 'no' as optional?	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk460000iewhj6izjhob4	cmnknk45y000gewhjn5pl0kw9	Lesson 10 — God's Plan for the Needs of Man	READING	3418	1	\N	t	Somewhere along the way, a large portion of Christianity adopted a doctrine that God never taught: that suffering is spiritually beneficial, poverty is a mark of holiness, and sickness keeps believers humble. If you grew up in certain traditions, you may have absorbed this so thoroughly you've stopped noticing it. But ask the question plainly: Is there a single verse where Jesus told someone to stay sick for their spiritual growth? Not one. So where did this doctrine come from — and what does Scripture actually teach?\n\nLast time we watched the Dispensation of Innocence end in failure and judgment. Now we turn to what God planned for humanity's needs — not as punishment, but as provision.\n\nIn this lesson, we're going to dig into what the Bible really says about God's providence — His foresight, care, and provision for your life. You might be surprised to discover that God's plan is actually the opposite of those gloomy doctrines. If there's one teaching that gets misunderstood, it's this one. So let's take our time and be as clear as possible.\n\n![Lesson 10 — God's Plan for the Needs of Man](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os7YhNIyRlSEtNozZx4rmO6UfQcdhyY2pDqwX3)\n\n## I. The Definition of Providence\n\nMost people hear "providence" and think of a vague sense that things work out in the end — a religious way of shrugging at circumstances. But that's not what the word means.\n\nThe word "providence" means foresight and forethought — God's care over His creatures, His divine direction for all of creation. Think of it like a master architect who doesn't just design a building and walk away. He oversees every detail of construction, anticipating needs before they arise and ensuring everything comes together according to plan.\n\nWhen we talk about foresight and forethought, we're talking about having a goal in mind and a definite plan to reach it. All rational beings act with some degree of planning. Even animals provide for their young. So how much more does the infinite God make provision for everything He has made?\n\nNow, while all rational beings exercise providence to some degree, this word reaches its full meaning only when applied to God. Divine providence is the care and government God exercises over everything He has created — so that all things accomplish the purposes for which they were made.\n\nIt's the infinite attention God gives to His universe, from numbering each hair on your head to the falling of every sparrow, all the way to sustaining the vast galaxies by His power. It's His nature at work, without pause, over everything His hands have made. It's God actively preserving and governing all things — ruling out luck, fortune, or random accidents.\n\nWe can think of providence in three ways: universal (over all things), special (over moral beings), and particular (over believers). Providence is perhaps the most comprehensive word in theology. It's the foundation behind so many other doctrines. It connects the seen with the unseen, the visible with the invisible, creation with redemption, and your personal salvation with the final end of all things.\n\nSo what is providence? It's God's agency — through Christ, by the Holy Spirit, using holy angels, redeemed people, and even demons and the unsaved — to make all things work together for good for those who love Him (Rom. 8:28). It's how He makes every event in the physical and moral universe fulfill His original purpose.\n\nCreation explains why the universe exists. Preservation explains why it continues. Providence explains how God is working out His purposes in all things according to His eternal plan. It's His active control and care, ensuring that everything — past and future, great and small — moves toward the goal He has set.\n\n## II. The Fivefold Sphere of Divine Providence\n\n### 1. The Material Universe\n\nScripture makes clear that God's "kingdom ruleth over all" (Ps. 103:19) and that He "worketh all things after the counsel of his will" (Eph. 1:11). He commands the snow, the rain, the whirlwind, the cold, fair weather, and lightning (Job 37:5–38:41). "Whatsoever the Lord pleased, that did he in heaven, and in earth, in the seas, and all deep places" (Ps. 135:6-7). He "maketh his sun to rise" and "sendeth rain on the just and on the unjust" (Mt. 5:45). The sun, moon, stars, and all the Earth are under His rule (Job 37:6-24; 38:4-40; Ps. 19:1-6; 68:9-13; 104:10-30; 107:1-43; 136:4-9; Jer. 10:13; 31:35; Acts 14:17).\n\n### 2. The Vegetable and Plant World\n\nGod "causeth the grass to grow" (Ps. 104:14). He clothes "the grass of the field" and the flowers (Mt. 6:28-30). He causes the Earth to bring forth vegetables, grains, and fruits for the good of people and animals (Gen. 1:29; 2:16-17; Lev. 26:4-10; Ps. 65:9-13; 67:6; 104:10-30).\n\n### 3. The Animal World\n\nGod's providence extends to every creature. He provides food for birds, fish, and all animals (Job 38:41; Ps. 104:10-30; 136:25; 145:15-16; 147:8-13; Mt. 6:26-30). We're told that not one sparrow falls to the ground without God knowing it (Mt. 10:29).\n\n### 4. The Rational World of Spirit-Beings\n\nScripture reveals how God cares for holy angels and punishes rebellious spirits. (See Lesson Six for more on spirit-beings and their relationship to God.)\n\n### 5. The Rational World of Flesh-Beings — Man\n\nThe Bible shows that God's providence covers all nations and extends to every individual life: "He changeth times and the seasons: he removeth kings, and setteth up kings: he giveth wisdom to the wise... There is a God in heaven that revealeth secrets and maketh known what shall come to pass... the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever He will... and He doeth according to his will in the army of heaven and among the inhabitants of the earth; and none can stay his hand, or say unto him, What doest thou?" (Dan. 2:21-30; 4:17, 25-35).\n\nThe smallest detail of your life is known by God, and He helps those who follow His plan (Jer. 1:5; Gal. 1:15-16; 1 Sam. 16:1). The very hairs of your head are numbered, and sparrows are counted (Mt. 10:29-31). So if God knows all that, you can trust your Heavenly Father with your needs right now — and with the life to come.\n\nThe Bible is full of examples of God's providence in the lives of nations and individuals. His involvement extends to actions and thoughts. He has prevented sin when people would listen. He has permitted the rebellious to commit evil. He has worked out problems for those who served Him and protected them in countless ways. Reading Scripture reveals all of this. If you want God's best, get on His side and stop cooperating with the devil and the forces that oppose God's will.\n\nScripture is literally packed with God's dealings with people and with promises covering every need — for this life and the next. We don't have space to quote them all, but let's look at enough to show you that God loves you and has provided for your every need.\n\n## III. God's Free and Abundant Promises for the Needs of Man\n\nLet's put to rest a false idea that floats around in many churches: that God wants His children to suffer disease, poverty, and lack so they'll stay humble and saved. That's simply not what the Bible teaches.\n\nAll of God's promises reveal that He has provided for you here and now — even in a fallen world. You can enjoy the full benefits of these promises if you surrender your life to God, receive genuine new birth, and live a godly life according to the gospel. Many blessings are even available to the unsaved as proof that God provides for all creation — even those in rebellion. The purpose? To lead them to repentance (Rom. 2:4). If these things are for the unsaved, how much more are they for believers?\n\nSo here's the wise move: get right with God and stay right with Him. Then you won't need to question what He wants for you.\n\nGod created humanity to be prosperous, healthy, successful, happy, wise, and blessed with good things. He created everything and gave it to man for his good and enjoyment. If having these things were sinful, God wouldn't have promised them. The sin of Adam and Eve wasn't in prosperity or happiness — it was in eating the forbidden fruit.\n\nThe abundance all around us shows that God wants us to have plenty. He made enough for everyone, and anyone can have what they need by following certain principles. What parent doesn't want their children to have the best? Is God less loving than we are? Jesus said, "If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children; how much more shall your heavenly Father give good things to them that ask him?" (Mt. 7:7-11).\n\nSome people worry that prosperity leads to backsliding. But honestly, those who would backslide over blessings would backslide over anything. Some people stumble over food or clothing — should we stop eating or go naked? Of course not. Let's not use a few failures as an excuse to doubt God's generous provision. Stay faithful, use prosperity wisely to help others, and God will bless you even more.\n\nThe devil loves to spread lies about God's character to turn people away from Him. But if you read Scripture, you'll see that God abundantly promises everything good and legitimate for your enjoyment. Here's what the Bible actually says:\n\n### 1. Prosperity\n\n"Be thou strong and very courageous, that thou mayest observe to do according to all the law... thou shalt make thy way prosperous, and then thou shalt have good success" (Josh. 1:5-9). "The Lord maketh poor, and maketh rich: he bringeth low, and lifteth up" (1 Sam. 2:7-8). "Keep the charge of the Lord thy God... that thou mayest prosper in all that thou doest" (1 Ki. 2:3-4). "Both riches and honour come of thee... and in thine hand it is to make great, and to give strength to all" (1 Chron. 29:12). "The hand of our God is upon all them for good that seek Him" (Ezra 8:22). "If they obey and serve him, they shall spend their days in prosperity, and their years in pleasures" (Job 36:11). "Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly... whatsoever he doeth shall prosper" (Ps. 1:1-3).\n\nIn Deuteronomy alone, the word "prosper" appears many times (Deut. 5:16, 29, 33; 6:3, 18; 12:28; 19:13; 30:15). Prosperity is promised when we turn from sin. Yes, sometimes sinners prosper — but usually through wrong dealings (Ps. 73).\n\nNow, some might say these promises are Old Testament and don't apply to us. But here's the thing: we're under a better covenant with even greater promises! Paul argues that the glory of the Old Covenant wasn't as great as what we have now (2 Cor. 3:6-15). He says the New Covenant is "a better testament... established upon better promises" (Heb. 7:22; 8:6). If the shadow of the law produced prosperity, how much more will the reality of the New Covenant?\n\nAnd the New Testament has its own clear promises: "What things soever ye desire, when ye pray, believe that ye receive them, and ye shall have them" (Mk. 11:22-24). "Ask, and it shall be given you... how much more shall your Father, which is in heaven, give good things to them that ask him?" (Mt. 7:7-11). "Seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you" (Mt. 6:31-33). "God is able to make all grace abound toward you; that ye, always having all sufficiency in all things, may abound to every good work" (2 Cor. 9:6-8). "My God shall supply all your need according to his riches in glory by Christ Jesus" (Phil. 4:19). "Beloved, I wish above all things that thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth" (3 Jn. 2).\n\nWhat could be clearer? Why limit God's bounty because we fear backsliding? Let's decide to handle blessings wisely, use them for God's glory, and there will be no limit to what He will do.\n\n### 2. Healing and Health\n\nThere are dozens of promises about healing and health in both Testaments: "If thou wilt diligently hearken to the voice of the Lord thy God... I will put none of the diseases upon thee... for I am the Lord that healeth thee" (Exod. 15:26). Psalm 91 promises deliverance from pestilence and plague. "Who forgiveth all thine iniquities; who healeth all thy diseases" (Ps. 103:3-5). "With his stripes we are healed" (Isa. 53:4-5). "Thine health shall spring forth speedily" (Isa. 58:8).\n\nThe New Testament continues: "He cast out the spirits with his word, and healed all that were sick: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Isaiah the prophet, saying, Himself took our infirmities and bare our sickness" (Mt. 8:16-17). "The prayer of faith shall save the sick, and the Lord shall raise him up" (Jas. 5:14-16). "By whose stripes ye were healed" (1 Pet. 2:24). "Beloved, I wish above all things that thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth" (3 Jn. 2).\n\nChrist came "to destroy the works of the devil" (1 Jn. 3:9) and to deliver "all that were oppressed by the devil" (Acts 10:38) — not just for three years, but forever. He commissioned His disciples to carry on His work (Mt. 28:19-20; Mk. 16:15-20; Jn. 14:12-15; Acts 1:1-2, 8). Early believers did this until faith waned (Acts 3; 5:16; Jas. 5:14-16). We're to contend for the faith once delivered to the saints (Jude 3; 2 Cor. 10:4-6; Eph. 6:10-18).\n\nWe'll explore healing more fully in Lesson Fourteen. But for now, no one with faith in God's Word can deny that healing and health are biblical. Don't be deceived by teachings that say otherwise. Believe what Scripture says, cooperate with God against the devil, and you will be healed.\n\n### 3. Wants and Needs\n\nAll your wants and needs are covered by God's promises through Christ. The common theory is that God only provides bare necessities — and grudgingly at that. But the Bible teaches that your desires are abundantly provided for and easy to receive by faith.\n\n"All things are possible to him that believeth" (Mk. 9:23). "What things soever ye desire, when ye pray, believe that ye receive them, and ye shall have them" (Mk. 11:22-24). "Whatsoever ye shall ask in my name, that will I do" (Jn. 14:12-15). "If ye abide in me, and my words abide in you, ye shall ask what ye will, and it shall be done unto you" (Jn. 15:7, 16). "Whatsoever we ask, we receive of him" (1 Jn. 3:21-22; 5:14-15).\n\nThese verses are so clear they don't need interpretation — just faith and practice. If we believe the Bible, then we believe we can receive whatever we ask in Jesus' name. If we don't believe, there's no point in asking. It's that simple: ask and believe, you receive. Ask without faith, you don't.\n\nThink of it like a child asking a loving parent for help. The parent isn't stingy or reluctant — they delight in meeting their child's needs. That's how God is with you, only infinitely more generous.\n\nGod's plan for your needs becomes crystal clear when you accept His promises at face value. There are no limits in God's provision. All limitations come from our unbelief. Because God gives "to all men liberally, and upbraideth not" (Jas. 1:5-8), let's have faith without wavering (Heb. 11:6; Mk. 11:22-24) and receive what we need.\n\nThis doctrine of "no want" was taught in the Old Testament too. David said, "The Lord is my shepherd, I shall not want" (Ps. 23:1-6). "There is no want to them that fear him... they that seek the Lord shall not want any good thing... Delight thyself in the Lord; and He shall give thee the desires of thine heart" (Ps. 34:9-10; 37:3-6). "No good thing will he withhold from him that walketh uprightly" (Ps. 84:11).\n\n### 4. Specific Benefits God Has Promised\n\nBeyond prosperity, healing, and general provision, God has specified many blessings for this life and the next:\n\n> (1) Salvation from sin (Mt. 1:21; Eph. 1:7; 2:8-9; 1 Jn. 1:7-9).\n\n> (2) The baptism in the Holy Ghost (Mt. 3:11; Jn. 1:33; Acts 1:4-5; 2:38-39).\n\n> (3) The kingdom of Heaven (Mt. 5:3; 13:43; 25:34).\n\n> (4) Comfort (Mt. 5:4; Jn. 14:16, 26).\n\n> (5) The Earth as an inheritance (Mt. 5:5; Ps. 37:9, 29).\n\n> (6) Filling of righteousness (Mt. 5:6; 1 Jn. 2:29; 3:7-10; 5:1-4, 18).\n\n> (7) Mercy from God (Mt. 5:7; Rom. 12:1; Eph. 2:4; 1 Pet. 1:3).\n\n> (8) Heart purity (Mt. 5:8; Jn. 15:3; 1 Pet. 1:22-23).\n\n> (9) Sonship (Mt. 5:9; Jn. 1:12; Rom. 8:14-16; Gal. 3:26-28).\n\n> (10) Great reward in Heaven (Mt. 5:11-12; Rom. 8:17-18; 1 Pet. 1:3-4).\n\n> (11) Answers to all prayers (Mt. 6:4-6, 18; 7:7-11; 18:18-20; Mk. 11:22-24; Jn. 14:12-15; 15:7, 16; 16:23-26; 1 Jn. 3:21-22; 5:14-15).\n\n> (12) Abundant provision for life here and now (Mt. 6:25-33; Mk. 11:22-24; Jn. 14:12-15; 15:7, 16; 16:23-26; 2 Cor. 9:8-11; Phil. 4:19; 3 Jn. 2).\n\n> (13) Infinite Fatherhood of God (Mt. 6:33; 7:7-11; 10:29-32; Rom. 8:32).\n\n> (14) Eternal life (Jn. 3:16, 36; 5:24; 17:3; Gal. 6:7-8).\n\n> (15) Reward for the smallest work done for others (Mt. 10:39-42; 16:27).\n\n> (16) Rest to the soul (Mt. 11:28-30; Rom. 5:1-11; 8:1-13).\n\n> (17) Power with God to do all things: nothing shall be impossible to you (Mt. 17:19-21; 18:18-20; 21:21-22; Mk. 9:23; 11:22-24; Lk. 24:49; Acts 1:8).\n\n> (18) The presence of God (Mt. 18:18-20; 28:19-20).\n\n> (19) Miraculous signs and wonders (Mk. 16:15-20; Jn. 14:12-15; Acts 1:8).\n\n> (20) Power over all the power of the devil (Lk. 10:19; 24:49; Mk. 16:15-20; Jn. 14:12-15; 15:7, 16; 16:23-26; Acts 1:8; 2 Cor. 10:4-5; Eph. 6:10-18).\n\n> (21) Wisdom above all adversaries (Lk. 21:15; Jas. 1:5-8).\n\n> (22) Complete spiritual satisfaction (Mt. 5:6; Jn. 4:13-14; 6:35-63).\n\n> (23) Resurrection of the body to immortality and eternal life (Jn. 5:28-29; 6:39-54; 1 Cor. 15:51-58; Phil. 3:20-21; 1 Thess. 4:13-17).\n\n> (24) Complete knowledge of the truth beyond all doubt (Jn. 7:16-17; 8:31-32; 14:16-17, 26; 15:26-27; 16:7-15; 2 Tim. 2:15; 3:16-17).\n\n> (25) Rivers of living waters flowing out of the innermost being (Jn. 7:37-39; Acts 2:1-11, 38-39; 5:32; Eph. 5:18; Mt. 5:6).\n\n> (26) Freedom from darkness into complete light (Jn. 8:12, 31-32; Acts 26:18; 1 Jn. 1:7-9; 2 Cor. 3:18; Eph. 4:17-21; 5:8-16).\n\n> (27) Complete freedom from bondage of sin, false doctrines, and demon powers (Jn. 8:31-32; Rom. 8:1-16; Gal. 5:1-26).\n\n> (28) Security in (not out of) Christ (Jn. 8:31-32; 10:27-29; 15:1-7; Rom. 8:1-13; Col. 1:23; 2:6-7; 1 Thess. 3:8; Heb. 3:6, 12-14; 6:11-22; 10:23-39).\n\n> (29) Honor from God (Jn. 12:26; 14:12-15; 15:7, 16; 16:23-26).\n\n> (30) An eternal home in the New Jerusalem (Jn. 14:1-3; Heb. 13:14; Rev. 3:12).\n\n> (31) Power to do the works of Christ (Jn. 14:12-15; Lk. 24:49; Acts 1:8; Mk. 16:15-20; 1 Cor. 12:4-11; 2 Cor. 10:4-5).\n\n> (32) Healing and sound health (Jn. 14:12-15; 15:7, 16; 16:23-26; Mk. 9:23; 11:22-24; Rom. 8:11; 3 Jn. 2; Mt. 8:16-17; 1 Pet. 2:24; Heb. 11:6).\n\n> (33) The gifts of the Spirit (1 Cor. 1:7; 12:4-11, 31; 14:1; Rom. 12:4-8).\n\n> (34) The fruit of the Spirit (Gal. 5:22-24).\n\n> (35) Power to exercise unlimited authority in this life in all the fullness of God according to the gospel (Lk. 24:49; Jn. 14:12-15; 15:7, 16; Mk. 9:23; 11:22-24; 16:15-20; Mt. 17:20; 21:21-22; Acts 1:8; 2:38-39, 43; 3:6; 4:10-16, 29-33; 5:1-16; 6:3-8; 8:5-20; 9:17-18, 32-43; 11:21; 13:6-12; 14:3, 8-20, 27; 15:4, 12; 16:16-34; 19:1-20; 20:9-12; 28:1-10; Rom. 1:11; 15:18-19, 29; 1 Cor. 1:7, 18-24; 2:1-5; 4:19-21; 5:1-5; 9:18; 12:1-11, 28-31; 13:1-3; 14:1-40; 16:10; 2 Cor. 3:6-18; 4:7; 5:20; 6:7; 8:7; 10:3-11; 12:9, 12; 13:4, 10; Gal. 3:3-5, 14; Eph. 1:19-20; 6:10-18; Phil. 4:9; Col. 1:11; 2:10; 1 Thess. 1:5; 2:13; 2 Thess. 1:11; 2:17; 1 Tim. 4:14; 2 Tim. 1:6-8, 14; 2:21; 3:5; Titus 2:14; Heb. 2:3-4; 6:1-2; Jas. 2:18; 5:14-16; 2 Pet. 2:4; 3 Jn. 2; Jude 3, 20-24).\n\nLooking at all these promises, you can see that no believer is limited in receiving what they need for this life and the next. We've included so many Scripture references because we want you to realize just how thoroughly God has provided for you. The only thing that can hinder you is unbelief. And there's no excuse for unbelief with this many promises — especially when early believers (not just apostles, but ordinary Christians) experienced these blessings.\n\nIf early believers enjoyed these blessings, why can't we? Does God love us less? Has He lost His power? Don't we still need these benefits? Are the promises still valid? Has God changed His program? Has He withdrawn what He offered? Is He a respecter of persons? Where does Scripture say these things aren't for us today?\n\nThere's not one hint in the Bible that God has canceled the blessings available to early Christians. This idea is a theory invented by modern unbelievers who would rather create doctrines of excuse than face the facts and meet the conditions for receiving God's provision.\n\nYou'd have to be a rank unbeliever to deny that you can receive what you ask from God. If you choose the side of those who reject God's Word, don't complain when prayers go unanswered or blessings don't come. God won't force you to be blessed against your will. You're a free moral agent, and God respects your choices. He expects you to use common sense and cooperate with Him instead of His enemies.\n\n## IV. Proof of Divine Providence\n\n> 1. Scripture proves that divine providence is at work in all things and has operated in every age. Providence brought all things into existence (Isa. 45:18; Col. 1:15-19), provided redemption after the Fall (Gen. 3:15; Eph. 1:1-11), preserved the race through the flood (Gen. 6:8–8:22), dealt with humanity in each dispensation, called people to carry out divine purposes, revealed the eternal plan in Scripture, recorded God's promises, documented countless examples of His care, established order in the universe, and sent Christ to redeem all things.\n\n> 2. The continued preservation of all things since creation proves that God's providence is working out His will.\n\n> 3. God's love in creating and redeeming all things proves His desire to preserve creation and reconcile it to Himself. Parents protect their children. Makers preserve what they've made. God is no exception.\n\n> 4. Divine perfection requires God to preserve and govern all things for the best good of every being and the universe. Because of His nature — and the selfishness of some in the universe — there's a conflict between rebels and God. God is committed to preserving creation and ultimately removing all rebellion.\n\n> 5. The prevalence of order proves divine providence. Fixed and eternal laws govern everything, evidencing an all-wise ruler and preserver.\n\n> 6. History is full of proof of God's providence. What happens isn't random. A supernatural power has always guided the affairs and destinies of creation according to a plan.\n\n> 7. Religion proves divine providence. In every age, people have found God through exercising religious faculties according to Scripture.\n\n> 8. Common intelligence in all rational beings reveals divine providence. Sane people experience and recognize it in many ways.\n\n## V. The Ultimate Purpose and Final End of Providence\n\nWhat's the goal of providence? It's to create a race of beings who find their highest happiness through the highest holiness — and who, in doing so, glorify their Creator. The purpose of the universe can't be found in unconscious, unthinking, or unmoral creation. It's found in the highest, most rational, and most moral part of creation. Lower forms exist for higher ones; material and animal for the moral and spiritual.\n\nGod's final purpose is the highest development of character in free moral agents, so they can glorify Him supremely and devote themselves to the best good of themselves and the universe (Gen. 1:26-28; Isa. 43:7; 45:18; Eph. 1:12; Col. 1:15-22; Rev. 4:9-11; 5:11-14; 7:10-12).\n\nScripture shows that providence is working toward this end and that there's a special providence for saints not enjoyed by sinners (Ps. 34:7-10; 37:1-12, 23-28; Prov. 3:6; Mt. 6:33; Rom. 8:28).\n\nNow, here's where many people get confused. They think sickness, accidents, and hardships are manifestations of providence. But these things are never God's direct will or directly caused by God. They come from evil forces that currently influence the world's social order during this period of rebellion against God.\n\nThe only glory God receives from these troubles is in delivering His people from them. God wants you to take a stand against these evils and cooperate with Him to work things out for His glory. This is how He develops faith and patience in us and demonstrates His power over His enemies.\n\nIt's similar to being a soldier stationed in enemy territory. You're going to face attacks — that's part of being behind enemy lines. But your Commander has given you weapons and promised to deliver you. The battle isn't evidence that your Commander doesn't care; it's an opportunity for Him to show His power and for you to grow in trust and strength.\n\nWe must recognize that we're on enemy territory in a rebellious world. If rebels had no power to affect us, God could never demonstrate His victory over them. It's only when we stop blaming God for everything and instead trust Him for deliverance that He's pleased with us. We need to recognize Satan's works so we can stand against him with God's help.\n\nAs we saw in Lesson Six, the devil and evil spirits dominate the present world system — except among God's children. Satan is called the prince of this world. God rules among men by overruling evil forces to carry out His plan, with the ultimate goal of ridding Earth of all rebellion. Naturally, certain events happen that God doesn't directly prevent. He could prevent them, but His plan involves training His people to become rulers over all things in the end.\n\nTo say that God directly willed the Fall, Cain's murder of Abel, the rise of idolatry, or humanity's wickedness in every age is saying too much. To teach that God directly causes wars, strife, sickness, disease, accidents, and calamities is unscriptural. Blaming God for millions of evil things puts the blame on the wrong person.\n\nGod is absolutely holy and just in all His dealings. Everything He does is for our betterment and good. He has a plan for each person and tries to guide everyone toward His highest will. But when someone rebels and gets into trouble, God isn't to blame. Sin, stubbornness, rebellion, the conditions sin creates, plus the tireless efforts of evil spirits — these cause events beyond God's direct control.\n\nScripture records hundreds of instances where people deviated from truth and suffered consequences. But not once does it say God was directly responsible for the evil that came upon anyone. God has allowed Satan to test people for purification and training, but He always delivers\n\n---\n\nGod's plan for your needs is not poverty, sickness, and defeat — it's provision, healing, and abundance through faith and obedience. The only thing standing between that plan and your experience of it is belief. So here's the question: What specific need in your life right now are you meeting entirely through your own effort and strategy, without ever genuinely asking God to provide it — because some part of you doesn't actually believe He would?	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk460000kewhjdzln35vf	cmnknk45y000gewhjn5pl0kw9	Lesson 11 — The Dispensation of Conscience	READING	4404	3	\N	t	After Eden, humanity was on its own — no garden, no direct divine instruction about daily life, no Mosaic law, no written Scripture. For 1,656 years, the only guide human beings had was the conscience God had built into them. The result? The worst moral catastrophe in human history. By Genesis 6, God looked at His creation and found that "every imagination of the thoughts of his heart was only evil continually." Not mostly evil. Not often evil. *Only* evil. *Continually.* That's what conscience alone produces without divine intervention.\n\nLast time we saw God's full provision for human needs through His providence. Now we turn to a dark chapter: what happened when humanity was left to govern itself by nothing but inner moral sense.\n\n![Lesson 11 — The Dispensation of Conscience](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Ossjop3LnIFYWHUNhmRXnATM2qSZzVGaodwQ5D)\n\n## I. The Definition of Conscience\n\nThis period is called the Dispensation of Conscience because, during this time, God tested humanity based on one thing: obedience to the inner voice of conscience. You could call this "the age of freedom." People were free to follow or ignore what their conscience told them—without any formal law to hold them accountable (Rom. 2:12-16).\n\nHere's an important point: there was no revealed code of law until after the flood. The old idea that Adam had the Ten Commandments, and that people kept them before Moses, simply isn't supported by Scripture.\n\nThe law Adam broke wasn't the Ten Commandments. It was the specific command not to eat from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil (Gen. 2:16-17; 3:1-24). Any command from God carries the weight of law, but Scripture makes clear that the Ten Commandments weren't given to anyone before Moses (Deut. 5:2-21; 29:14-15).\n\n### What is Conscience?\n\n> "Conscience is the knowledge of our acts, states, or character as to right or wrong: the faculty, power, or principle which decides on the lawfulness of our actions and affections, and approves or condemns them; the moral faculty or sense."—Webster.\n\nThink of conscience like an internal alarm system. It was activated—switched on—when humanity chose to eat from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil. Ever since then, conscience has served as the guiding faculty in our moral decisions.\n\nThe Bible has a lot to say about different kinds of conscience:\n\n- "Seared" conscience (1 Tim. 4:2)\n- "Awakened" conscience (Jn. 8:9)\n- "Purged" conscience (Heb. 9:9, 14; 10:2)\n- "Pure" conscience (Acts 24:16)\n- "Weak" conscience (1 Cor. 8:7, 12, 13)\n- "Defiled" conscience (Titus 1:15)\n- "Witnessing" conscience (Rom. 2:12-15; 9:1; 2 Cor. 1:12)\n- "Good" conscience (Acts 2:13; 1 Tim. 1:5, 19; 1 Pet. 2:19; 3:16, 21; Heb. 13:19)\n- "Convicting" or "healthy" conscience (Gen. 3:10; 4:13; Mt. 27:3)\n\n---\n\n## II. The Length of the Dispensation of Conscience\n\nBy tracing the genealogies in Gen. 5:1-29 and Gen. 7:11, we can calculate that this dispensation lasted **1,656 years**—from the creation of Adam to the 600th year of Noah's life when the flood came. Here's how it breaks down:\n\n1. Adam was 130 years old when Seth was born (Gen. 5:3)\n2. Seth was 105 years old when Enos was born (Gen. 5:6)\n3. Enos was 90 years old when Cainan was born (Gen. 5:9)\n4. Cainan was 70 years old when Mahaleel was born (Gen. 5:12)\n5. Mahaleel was 65 years old when Jared was born (Gen. 5:15)\n6. Jared was 162 years old when Enoch was born (Gen. 5:18)\n7. Enoch was 65 years old when Methuselah was born (Gen. 5:21)\n8. Methuselah was 187 years old when Lamech was born (Gen. 5:25)\n9. Lamech was 182 years old when Noah was born (Gen. 5:28)\n10. Noah was 600 years old when the flood came (Gen. 7:6, 11)\n\n**TOTAL: 1,656 years from Adam to Noah's flood.**\n\n---\n\n## III. The Favorable Beginning of Man in Conscience\n\nIn Gen. 3:15, we find God's first promise of redemption—through the seed of the woman, pointing to Christ. Humanity was being given another chance, another opportunity to prove faithful to God.\n\nPeople had the promise that the curse would eventually be lifted and that they would be restored to their original position as rulers over the Earth. They had the ability to choose right from wrong. They had the capacity for faith in God and hope for redemption.\n\nHere's something fascinating: humanity also started out with a knowledge of true worship. God had slain animals in the Garden and clothed Adam and Eve with their skins (Gen. 3:21). Blood had been shed—a preview of the blood that would be shed by the coming Redeemer.\n\nWe see proof of this in the story of Cain and Abel. When they were old enough to worship, Abel brought the right kind of sacrifice—a blood sacrifice—showing that Adam and Eve had passed down the true way of worship. There was even a tabernacle for worship in those days! In Gen. 4:7, God told Cain, "If thou doest not well, sin lieth at the door." The Hebrew word *chata* here means "a sin offering" (as in Exod. 30:10; Lev. 4:3; 6:25). The "door" refers to the tabernacle door where sacrifices were offered. Gen. 4:3-5 makes clear there was a specific place where offerings were brought to God.\n\nSo humanity knew that God was just and merciful, that His Word was true, and that He would be with them if they chose obedience. They had witnessed the curse of sin firsthand. They had personal experience of both sin and the means of reconciliation with God.\n\nEverything was as favorable as it could possibly be, given the fallen state. People could have proved faithful to God—but as time went on, humanity grew worse and worse until destruction became necessary.\n\n---\n\n## IV. The Test for Man in Conscience\n\nIn Gen. 4:7, we find the specific test for this period: "If thou doest well, shalt thou not be accepted?"\n\nGod required that people obey the dictates of their conscience regarding His revealed will and their own inner knowledge of right and wrong. The test was simple: do good, refuse evil, and have faith in God and the coming Redeemer who would bruise the serpent's head (Gen. 3:15).\n\nHere's what happened at the Fall: humanity lost God-consciousness and gained self-consciousness. We lost the inner power to do good and gained the power to do evil.\n\nPeople woke up to a hard reality: they needed God's help to live rightly and obey His will. They needed divine assistance to overcome the evil spirit forces they had yielded to. On their own, they were powerless—but they still had the power of choice. They could voluntarily acknowledge their lost state and helpless condition and accept God's help. This would enable them to be redeemed and overcome their spiritual enemies.\n\nThis is still all God requires of helpless, sinful people today. The moment anyone acknowledges their sin and need for God—the moment they call upon Him for deliverance from satanic forces and sinful habits—they are instantly heard. They become a new creature in Christ, born again, empowered with righteousness and true holiness, renewed in spiritual and moral power to overcome the flesh, the world, and the devil (Eph. 2:1-19; 4:22-24; Gal. 5:16-26; 2 Cor. 5:17; Rom. 6:1-23; 8:1-16; 1 Jn. 1:7; 2:29; 3:7-10; 5:1-4, 18).\n\n---\n\n## V. The Purpose of God in This Dispensation\n\nWhat was God trying to accomplish in this age? He wanted to teach humanity—right from the beginning of the Fall—that obedience to Him, faith in His Word, and conformity to His will were the only sources of true pleasure, happiness, health, and prosperity. These were the only paths to restoration.\n\nGod wanted to test humanity under complete freedom of will, without any restraint or compulsion, to see if people would choose to follow Him instead of their new master—the devil.\n\nThink of it like this: someone might argue, "I didn't really understand right from wrong! I should get a pass for that first sin." So God met this argument by giving humanity complete freedom of action to choose for themselves which master they wanted to serve.\n\nIn this period, there was no Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil to avoid. There were no specific laws or commandments to obey. The test was simply a choice between two masters—and the free choice to conform to what their rational nature told them was right.\n\nThe broad principles of right and wrong were known. People had within them certain created faculties and knowledge of how to use their whole being for the best good of themselves, others, and the universe as a whole. They had to make the free choice to consecrate themselves to what their rational being dictated—the same end to which all society must conform if it is to continue eternally: that each person choose and wholeheartedly cooperate with others for the preservation of that society.\n\nHumanity had within them the knowledge of the principles of righteousness and true holiness that God would later require by law. Paul described it as doing by "nature the things contained in the law, these having not the law, are a law unto themselves: Which shew the work of the law written in their hearts, their conscience also bearing them witness, and their thoughts the mean while accusing or else excusing one another" (Rom. 2:12-16).\n\nThrough this test of freedom, people could learn lessons they couldn't have learned any other way. God wanted to see—and wanted humanity to see and experience—just how sinful they could become if they chose self-gratification and selfishness over the good of others.\n\nGod permitted evil spirits to operate in the human realm to teach people from the very beginning their need for dependence on God and submission to His will as the best choice for life and conduct.\n\n---\n\n## VI. The Means of God in Accomplishing This Purpose\n\nBased on what we've discussed, it's clear that God used several things to accomplish His purpose during this period:\n\n- **Human conscience** demonstrated how exceedingly sinful people could become if they chose to continue in rebellion.\n- **Complete freedom of action** demonstrated how far humanity would go in rebellion before God would have to intervene for the sake of His eternal plan.\n- **The malice of the devil** demonstrated the contrast between the two masters humanity could choose to serve while on probation.\n\nThis complete freedom of will was what humanity chose in the Fall. So God permitted people to go to the full limit of wickedness in this age, so they might learn the folly of such a course—and so all future generations throughout eternity might profit from this experience.\n\nNow, this freedom of conduct without restraint, and its results, are matters of historical record. They will serve forever as a warning against the wrong use of free will.\n\n---\n\n## VII. The Failure of Man in Conscience\n\n### 1. THE FAILURE OF ADAM\n\n> "My spirit shall not always strive with man, for that he also is flesh: yet his days shall be an hundred and twenty years" (Gen. 6:3).\n\nThis verse has been used through the ages to teach that someday God's Holy Spirit will stop striving with all people and they'll be cut off without hope. Some use it to claim that the door of mercy to Gentiles will close soon and God will only save Jews. Both of these ideas are man-made and have no place in Scripture or God's plan, as we'll see in Lesson Fifteen, Point VIII.\n\nThat Adam is personally referred to in Gen. 6:3 is clear from the following:\n\n> (1) The word "spirit" is correctly written without a capital letter and doesn't refer to the Holy Spirit. It refers to the created spirit of man manifested in his conscience and other spirit faculties. It's called "My spirit" because Adam's personal spirit was directly created and given to him by God. God is the God of all spirits, and all are considered His in the sense of creation, origin, and rulership (Num. 16:22; 27:16; Isa. 42:5; Heb. 12:9, 23).\n\n> (2) The word "strive" comes from the Hebrew word *doon*, meaning "to rule," "judge," "strive," "contend," "convict," "minister," "execute," "plead." It's translated "judge" (Gen. 15:14; 49:16), "contend" (Eccl. 6:10), "execute" (Jer. 21:12), "plead" (Prov. 31:9), and "minister" (Ps. 9:8). The Septuagint, Arabic, Syriac, and Latin versions translate this as "remain in"—that is, "My spirit I have created in man will not always remain in him."\n\n> (3) The word for "man" is singular, used with the definite article. It's the Hebrew *Adam*, and with the definite article should read "the Adam"—that is, "My Spirit will not always remain in or strive with the Adam." This is made clearer by the singular pronouns "he" and "his," proving one man is referred to, not the whole human race.\n\n> (4) The word "also" makes it clear this refers to the one man Adam. It has no meaning if "man" is read as plural. If all men are referred to, then who else besides all men could "also" refer to? It can only mean that Adam—the only one who was a direct product of creation—was also flesh, just like those born of men rather than directly created. The whole verse teaches that Adam, like other men, had become sinful and would be cut off even though he was the only created man. It reveals that God gave Adam 120 more years to live, making clear that Gen. 6:3 refers to a time 810 years after Adam's creation, since he lived only 930 years.\n\n> (5) The verse couldn't refer to cutting off all men in 120 years, because all men weren't cut off then, and all men still haven't been cut off after many times 120 years. This verse sheds light on the ungodliness of men 810 years after creation and 846 years before the flood. It shows why, even in Enoch's day, God had already determined to destroy humanity by a flood. Enoch divinely named his son "Methuselah," which in Hebrew means "when he is dead it [the deluge] shall be sent." Enoch saw such ungodliness that he even prophesied of the destruction of the ungodly at Christ's second coming (Jude 14).\n\nEnoch was born 627 years after Adam's creation and was a contemporary of Adam for 303 years. Methuselah, who died the year the flood came, was a contemporary of Adam for 238 years. So two men lived through the entire Dispensation of Conscience!\n\nThis shows that humanity was so wicked that God planned, when Methuselah was born, to send a flood—969 years before it actually came. Adam himself was so wicked that God gave him only 120 more years to live and repent. Whether Adam ever repented isn't clear. He's not mentioned among the faithful worthies of the Old Testament in Heb. 11. He's never mentioned anywhere in Scripture as being a godly man—a striking fact when you consider that Abel, Enoch, and Noah from this Antediluvian Age are mentioned thirteen times as being godly (Gen. 4:4; 5:22; 6:8, 9; 7:1; Lk. 11:51; Heb. 11:1-7; Rev. 3:20; 2 Pet. 2:5; Jude 14; 1 Pet. 3:20).\n\nIf Adam—after being a direct creation of God and after seeing God face to face—failed the Creator, what must have been the sinful condition of many others?\n\n### 2. THE FAILURE OF CAIN (Gen. 4:1-16)\n\nThis passage records the failure of the first man born on Earth, just as the passage above (Gen. 6:3) records the failure of the first and only created man.\n\nHere we have the story of two of Adam's many sons. One was humble and godly; the other was self-willed and rebellious. Both were full-grown and knew the true way of worship. They'd been taught this by Adam and by God Himself, since God was present when the brothers offered their sacrifices.\n\nGod even gave Cain another chance. He personally told Cain about the sin offering at the tabernacle door (Gen. 4:4, 7). Cain also knew when God accepted Abel's offering what he should do—but he rejected the counsel of both God and man and started his own religion.\n\nThe fire of God evidently consumed Abel's offering, as happened on other occasions when God accepted a sacrifice (Gen. 15:17; Lev. 9:24; Judg. 6:21; 1 Ki. 18:38; 1 Chron. 21:26; 2 Chron. 7:1).\n\nInstead of conforming to God's will and welcoming fellowship with Him, Cain began scheming about how to get even with Abel. This desire for vengeance led to murder. God appeared a second time to Cain, cursed him from His own presence and from other men, and condemned him to be a wanderer in the Earth.\n\nCain was afraid someone would take vengeance on him, so God gave him a pledge of protection. The Hebrew word for "mark" is *owth*, meaning "a pledge," "token" (Gen. 9:12, 17; 17:11), or "a sign" (Exodus 4:8; 8:23). It never means a literal physical mark on the body, but a pledge. This pledge is stated in the same verse (Gen. 4:15): "Therefore whosoever slayeth Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him sevenfold."\n\n### 3. THE FAILURE OF CAIN'S DESCENDANTS (Gen. 4:17-24)\n\nThis passage reveals the activities of the godless civilization produced by Cain's descendants and others associated with him. This part of the human race tried to make their land of exile into a paradise instead of following God's directions and cooperating with Him to remove the curse altogether.\n\nThey were plunderers and profligates. Cain himself set a wicked example. He started the first city. He aimed to secure everything for his own bodily pleasure, even if it harmed others. He became wealthy through violence and robbery and led others into sinful ways. He changed the simplicity of living and became the inventor of weights and measures. He set boundaries around lands and fortified cities against wild beasts and enemies.\n\nHis children became more wicked as time went on. Many marks of modern civilization appeared in this early one:\n\n> 1. City life and its attendant evils first appeared (Gen. 4:17).\n\n> 2. Jabal, the first cattleman and nomad dwelling in tents, introduced flesh and milk as food to escape tilling the soil (Gen. 4:20).\n\n> 3. Jubal invented "the harp and organ" (wind instruments) for songs, dances, and pleasures of all kinds associated with crowded populations (Gen. 4:21).\n\n> 4. Tubal-Cain, a worker in brass and iron, forged weapons of war and made things for the comfort of civilization. The Earth was filled with violence, bloodshed, and wars (Gen. 4:22; 6:14).\n\n> 5. Lamech was a murderer, the first polygamist, and the first songwriter on record (Gen. 4:23-24).\n\nFrom these few facts, you can picture the scene: envyings, strifes, deeds of licentiousness, violence, lowing of herds, strains of music and dancing to soothe the conscience, clatter of hoofs, sounding of anvils, boasting of proud men—all the mingled noise rising from a godless civilization struggling to overpower the curse.\n\n### 4. THE FAILURE OF SETH'S DESCENDANTS (Gen. 4:25–5:32)\n\nThis passage shows the failure of Seth's descendants and the line of ten generations from Adam to Noah. Some believe there were two distinct family lines in this period—the ungodly line of Cain and the godly line of Seth—but this isn't taught in Scripture:\n\n> (1) Such an idea isn't once mentioned in Scripture. Seth's descendants as a whole may not have been as ungodly as Cain's, but clearly there were more than just two branches of the human family coming from just two men. Adam had "sons and daughters" (Gen. 5:4). Every son of Adam started a branch of the race, as has generally been the case throughout history. Not all of Adam's sons and daughters are mentioned in Scripture, nor are the multitudes of other families through this whole 1,656-year period. There were also races of giants in the Earth that weren't descendants of either Cain or Seth, as we'll see below.\n\n> (2) There were many people on Earth when Cain killed Abel, or God wouldn't have protected Cain from others who might want to kill him (Gen. 4:14-15). Cain was evidently married by the time he slew Abel, for immediately afterward he went to the land of Nod with his wife, and there she had a son (Gen. 4:16-17). The curse on woman was to multiply greatly, and this was true of early women—when Cain had his first child, there were enough people even in his land of exile to build a city (Gen. 4:17). Cain wouldn't build a city for just one wife and one child.\n\n> (3) The history of the godless civilization shows a considerable population. Bible students estimate there could have been at least 150 million people at the time of the flood—a very conservative estimate. Israel multiplied in Egypt from 70 to about six million people in 215 years. When people lived nearly a thousand years, they could multiply infinitely faster than Israel did in Egypt, when lifespans were about a hundred years. The fact that Scripture doesn't explain the population before the flood suggests that growth occurred at a normal rate and the Earth was filled with people. So the idea that there were just two sons whose immediate families stayed separated for 1,656 years is absurd. We might as well argue that the few people mentioned in other genealogies were all the people who lived on Earth in those periods.\n\n> (4) Seth's line is highlighted in Gen. 5 to show the particular branch through which the seed of the woman descended. The purpose isn't to show a godly line for over 1,600 years. There couldn't be such a thing as generation after generation with all offspring being godly for that length of time. This is contrary to all history and Scripture. This won't happen until the New Heavens and New Earth, when all human and spirit rebels are confined to the Lake of Fire forever. There has never been, and never will be until the final restitution of all things, such a thing as godly people reproducing godly people by nature. So the belief that there were many generations of godly people just because they descended from Seth is ridiculous.\n\n> (5) The firstborn of Seth was ungodly—he was the one who started idolatry on Earth, according to Gen. 4:26, which says, "Then began men to call upon the name of the Lord." According to many ancient versions, this reads, "Then began men to call themselves by the name of Jehovah" and "to call their gods by the name of Jehovah." People began worshipping stars and making idols like all kinds of animals (Rom. 1:21-32). The Targum of Onkelos reads, "Then in his days the sons of men desisted from praying in the name of the Lord," and the Targum of Jonathan says, "That was the generation in whose days they began to err, and to make to themselves idols, and surnamed their idols by the name of the Lord." The Scofield Bible reads, "Then began men to call themselves by the name of Jehovah."\n\n> We know that true worship didn't begin with Enos, because Abel and others had already worshipped God the true way many years before. Enos wasn't born until 235 years after man's creation. We read of true worship during this time (Gen. 3:21; 4:1-16; Heb. 11:4), so Enos didn't start true worship—he started false worship. If Seth didn't worship the true God, and if true worship began with Enos, then Seth was ungodly—which destroys the theory of Seth and all his sons being godly men. If idolatry started with Enos, then he was ungodly—which also destroys the theory of the godly line of Seth. This proves Seth's line wasn't all godly, and that the sons of God in Gen. 6 were not godly men from his line. If there had been thousands of godly descendants from Seth, they certainly would have been mentioned somewhere in Scripture, especially when only three godly men from this period are mentioned thirteen times, as seen above. Apart from these three, the ungodliness of men in this period is emphasized throughout.\n\n### 5. THE FAILURE OF ALL MEN IN GENERAL (Gen. 6:1-7, 11-13)\n\nThe ungodliness of all people in this age is stated in many Scriptures (Gen. 4:1-26; 6:1-13; 7:1; Mt. 24:37-39; Lk. 17:26-27; 1 Pet. 3:20; 2 Pet. 2:4-5). The fact that only three men are mentioned as being godly in this entire period proves the general ungodliness of humanity.\n\nGod will judge sin wherever it's found, whether it delays His original purpose or not. If there hadn't been one godly man on Earth at the time of the flood, the present social order would have been totally destroyed, just as Lucifer's order was. God would have had to make a new social order, as He did in Adam's day, because He created the Earth "to be inhabited" (Isa. 45:18). His original purpose will be finally carried out even if He has to destroy and remake several social systems. Failure on the part of any one social system merely delays the original purpose.\n\nAt the time of Moses, God considered destroying all Israel because of sin and raising up a new nation under Moses. But Moses interceded, the nation was spared, and God's original purpose continued (Exod. 32:7-14). If He had destroyed Israel and made a new nation from Moses, His plan would have been merely delayed, not defeated.\n\nThe failure of people in general during the Dispensation of Conscience can be summarized as follows:\n\n> (1) A tendency to worship God merely as Creator and Benefactor, not as Savior or Covenant God (Gen. 4:1-7; Rom. 1:17-32).\n\n> (2) Undue prominence of the female sex and disregard of the primal law of marriage (Gen. 4:19; Mt. 24:37-39; Lk. 17:26-30).\n\n> (3) Rapid progress of mechanical arts and inventions to make the curse easier (Gen. 4:17-24; Rom. 1:30).\n\n> (4) An alliance between nominal worshippers of God and the world (Mt. 24:37-39; 1 Pet. 3:20; 2 Pet. 2:4-5).\n\n> (5) Rejection of the preaching of righteousness (2 Pet. 2:5; Mt. 24:37-39).\n\n> (6) Appearance on Earth of spirit-beings in unlawful intercourse with the human race (Gen. 6:1-7; 2 Pet. 2:4; Jude 6-7).\n\n> (7) Murders and violence of all kinds (Gen. 6:1-7, 11-13; Rom. 1:17-32).\n\n> (8) Disregard for restraint of conscience (Gen. 4:17-24; 6:1-7, 11-13; Mt. 24:37-39; 2 Pet. 2:4-5).\n\n> (9) Sins and pleasures of all kinds to satisfy every lust (Gen. 4:17-24; 6:1-7, 11-13; Mt. 24:37-39; Rom. 1:17-32. Compare 1 Tim. 4; 2 Tim. 3; 2 Pet. 2; Jude 3-19).\n\n> (10) The appearance on Earth of ungodly and inhuman giants, as discussed below.\n\n### 6. THE FAILURE OF THE SONS OF GOD (Gen. 6:1-7, 11-13)\n\nThe subject of the sons of God marrying the daughters of men is often misunderstood. We should be fair and open-minded to everything in Scripture, letting the Word of God settle every question.\n\nSome hold that the sons of God were the sons of Seth, and that they married the daughters of Cain, breaking down the godly line of Seth. But there was no such thing as a godly line producing sons of God for 1,656 years, as we've proven above—so the sons of God could not have been sons of Seth. Here's why this theory doesn't hold up:\n\n> (1) **The timing of these marriages disproves this theory.** If the sons of God were sons of Seth, these marriages couldn't have happened during the last 600 years of this age, because Noah was the only godly man in this period: "for thee have I seen righteous before me in this generation... Noah was a just man and perfect in his generations, and Noah walked with God" (Gen. 6:9; 7:1; 2 Pet. 2:4-5). There were no godly men to be called sons of God during Noah's lifetime; so these marriages, if they involved ordinary men, had to occur during only the first 1,000 years. But Gen. 6:4 says such marriages continued to "those days," which everyone agrees includes Noah's days up to the flood.\n\n> In Gen. 6:1-2, we see that the sons of God began to marry the daughters of men from the very beginning when daughters were born. Adam had the first daughters (Gen. 3:20; 5:1-5), and it must have been some of these that the sons of God began to marry. This was before Seth's birth, or at least before Seth had sons of marriageable age. Seth had no children until age 105, or 235 years after creation (Gen. 5:1-6). Enos had his first son 325 years after creation (Gen. 5:1-9). If the sons of God married daughters of men "when men began to multiply on the face of the earth" (Gen. 6:1), they couldn't be sons of Seth, because he had no sons yet.\n\n> Also, Gen. 6:4 mentions the sons of God marrying daughters of men "also after that"—that is, after the flood. If the daughters of men were ungodly daughters of Cain, how did these ungodly women survive the flood, since only Noah's family was saved by the ark? (1 Pet. 3:20; Gen. 6:18).\n\n> (2) **The expressions "sons of God" and "daughters of men" indicate that one is the product of God and the other is the product of men.** The facts above prove that Seth's sons were just as ungodly as Cain's, so they couldn't be called sons of God in the godly sense any more than Cain's sons could. Only two of Seth's sons were godly, so Seth's sons couldn't be godly sons of God. We have just as much scriptural authority to teach that Cain's sons were godly as to teach that Seth's were. We've also seen there weren't two distinct lines of the race—one of Cain, one of Seth. So teaching that these marriages broke down the separation between godly and ungodly lines is unscriptural. Scripture specifically states that "all flesh had corrupted his way upon the earth" (Gen. 6:1-7, 11-13), which is why only one family was saved in the ark. It wouldn't have been just for God to kill godly men along with sinners. If the sons of God were godly men marrying ungodly women, this wouldn't in itself make them backslidden and lost. Many saved people today are married to unsaved companions and still remain godly. So we must conclude that this theory is unscriptural.\n\n> (3) **It's only through a divine specific act of creation that any being can become a son of God.** Adam was a direct product of creation and was called a "son of God" (Lk. 3:38). Adam's sons aren't and couldn't be called sons of God by natural generation. His sons can only become sons of God in a godly sense by being born again and created anew in Christ (Jn. 3:1-5; Eph. 4:22-24; 2 Cor. 5:17). Since Seth's sons weren't godly by the new birth, they could never be called sons of God.\n\n> (4) **The expression "sons of God" is used only five times in the Old Testament, and every time it refers to angels**—unless Gen. 6 is an exception. In Job 1:6 and 2:1, it's used of angels in Heaven presenting themselves before the Lord. Satan came with them too. The scene was in Heaven, as proven by Satan having come from Earth. These sons of God couldn't have been sons of Seth, because godly men didn't go to Heaven\n\n---\n\nThe Dispensation of Conscience is a 1,656-year experiment that proved conscience alone cannot restrain human sin. The flood didn't come because people were unaware that their actions were wrong — conscience told them. They simply chose to ignore it, generation by generation, until the earth was full of violence. So here's the honest question: In what specific area of your life is your conscience currently telling you something that you've been choosing to suppress, delay acting on, or rationalize away?	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk460000lewhjfdh3nhai	cmnknk45y000gewhjn5pl0kw9	Lesson 12 — Why God's Plan for the Needs of Man is Not Realized	READING	2585	4	\N	t	If God's plan genuinely includes health, provision, and blessing for His people — and Lesson Ten proved it does — then why are so many sincere, faithful Christians sick, broke, and defeated? That's not a hostile question. It's the most urgent question in practical Christianity. And the Bible gives a clear, specific answer that has nothing to do with God's willingness and everything to do with ours.\n\nLast time we saw that conscience alone cannot contain sin — it took a global flood to reset the trajectory. Now we face a related question: if God's provision is real, what blocks it? The answer is more personal than most people want to hear.\n\nAnd honestly? Those promises are almost too good to believe. Even spiritually mature believers struggle to fully grasp them—not because the words are difficult, but because it's simply overwhelming that the Living God would make such extravagant provision for us. But it's absolutely true!\n\nNo reasonable person can look at these promises and deny what they plainly say. No Christian would dare claim God won't keep His word. But here's where the rubber meets the road: the challenge for believers is actually meeting the conditions for these promises in everyday life.\n\nLet me walk you through some of the most common reasons why people don't experience the full abundance God has provided for them.\n\n![Lesson 12 — Why God's Plan for the Needs of Man is Not Realized](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os4OCFYvL3Ls52XczwCYNqdZVf8hMUGlEvQ0nD)\n\n## 1. Christians Have Been Misled by False Teachings\n\nFalse cults and misguided religious leaders have spread all kinds of harmful ideas. Here are some of the most common ones circulating today:\n\n- That God wants you poor and struggling so you'll stay saved\n- That you're destined for defeat and powerless against sin, sickness, and failure\n- That pain and suffering are everyone's lot—secretly blessings in disguise\n- That you must sin daily in thought, word, or deed, and no one can truly live holy\n- That you should just accept these conditions as normal for everyone\n- That trying to overcome these problems shows pride and rebellion against God\n- That the age of miracles has ended\n- That healing isn't part of the atonement or God's will\n- That the baptism of the Holy Spirit and spiritual gifts were only for the apostles\n- That inspiration has ceased and we don't need supernatural confirmation of God's Word today\n- That all supernatural manifestations are just "the flesh"\n- That expecting God to do everything you ask is foolish rebellion\n- That humans aren't free moral agents\n- That God is responsible for your circumstances and whether you're saved or lost\n\nThese false doctrines fill thousands of pulpits today. Is it any wonder there's so much unbelief? Is it any wonder Christianity is plagued with confusion and bitter arguments over teachings that should be clear and unified?\n\nThis chaos wouldn't exist if everyone who claims to follow Christ would set aside church traditions and personal opinions, and simply return to wholehearted acceptance of the Bible—committing to obey whatever truth they find there.\n\nAnyone can improve their life and experience health, happiness, and prosperity by doing this. The Bible is simple and clear. Even if your pastor won't preach the truth, you can discover it yourself by reading Scripture. If you can read what it says, you can believe what it says—so there's no excuse for not knowing God's truth personally.\n\nNot one of these false teachings has any scriptural support. The promises we've studied in Lessons Ten, Twelve, Fourteen, and Sixteen disprove every single one. If people choose Satan's lies over God's truth, let them settle for their current lot. Let them refuse the gospel's power to transform their lives. Let them dishonor God's character with false doctrine—judgment will come in due time. Let them endure suffering they don't have to bear, when they could simply turn to God and His truth.\n\n## 2. Men Don't Understand They're Free Moral Agents\n\nPeople fail to receive God's benefits because they don't realize they can choose which master to serve. They don't understand they can escape the devil's work by switching allegiance from Satan to God according to the gospel.\n\nThink of it like this: you're standing at a crossroads every single day, and you get to decide which direction to walk.\n\nWe saw in Lesson Eight, Point X, that Adam received full responsibility as Earth's ruler. God's plan was for humanity to enjoy all the blessings of a perfect creation. Lesson Ten showed us that even under the present curse, God wants us to fully enjoy these benefits. Why would He make such provision and give such promises if He didn't intend for us to receive them?\n\nHere's what you need to do if you want these blessings:\n\nFirst, realize they're actually meant for you—God genuinely wants you to have them. Believe that He'll make sure you receive them if you'll cooperate with Him against demonic powers and false human teachings.\n\nRecognize that you're a free moral agent responsible for losing your dominion. Acknowledge your sinfulness, confess your sins to God, abandon the sin business, and align yourself with the gospel.\n\nThen take an aggressive, victorious stance against Satan's forces—by the Holy Spirit's help and through faith in God and Christ's blood. Overcome these powers and claim the victory that rightfully belongs to you.\n\nIf God had His perfect way in your life, you'd automatically have all these blessings without any fight. But you must sever your relationship with evil forces and fight for God's promises to manifest in your life.\n\nLet me be direct: it's a fight to get the full benefits of the gospel. There's no point hiding this from anyone. The devil tried to defeat Christ and the apostles. He wages constant war against everyone who refuses to serve him. He hates God and everyone who serves Him.\n\nSome modern false religions teach you to simply ignore biblical ideas about the devil, sin, and disease—just look to some "God-law inside." This is complete nonsense. It leads you into captivity to the very devil you're ignoring. It makes you cooperate with Satan against God.\n\nNaturally, if the devil can get people to deny the Bible and its truths, to reject Christ and the atonement, he knows they're safely headed toward Hell. He'll cooperate with such deceived souls—even helping them get material benefits that are available to everyone, saint or sinner. He'll even remove sickness and other works of his from such people, just to eventually damn their souls.\n\nThe wise path is to acknowledge truth and facts, following God's ways even when it brings opposition from Satan. God has made complete provision to overcome sin, sickness, and all the devil's works. You can get all the material and spiritual benefits that false religions offer—and be certain of eternal life in the end.\n\nYou must choose which power will operate in you and which master you'll serve. You can get some benefits from either master, and the more you consecrate yourself to one, the more you become subject to that master's operation in you.\n\nSome people sell out completely to the devil, yielding to demon spirits who possess and assist them in various activities. Others consecrate themselves wholly to God, becoming new creatures, filled and baptized in the Holy Spirit, empowered from on high to destroy the devil's works.\n\nAs we saw in Lesson Six, Point X, Satan counterfeits God in every possible way to deceive people. You must be careful to be completely free and biblical in all your religious, spiritual, and material activities—to have the right Spirit in you and the right power working through you.\n\nHere's the general rule: any power, doctrine, or spirit that reflects against God's character, rejects Christ, the cross, and blood atonement, or teaches contrary to Bible truth is from the devil and should be rejected immediately.\n\nYou're not only responsible for your choice of masters—you're responsible for your condition in life. You don't have to tolerate sin, sickness, poverty, and want. Through God, by faith in His promises and by meeting a few simple conditions, you can eliminate these things and enjoy the fullness of God's goodness.\n\nReview God's plan in Lesson Ten, then start making it personal for your life. Things will change beyond your wildest dreams.\n\n## 3. Unbelief and Too Many Manufactured Conditions\n\nPeople fail to receive all God has provided because of unbelief and because they create countless conditions they think must be met before God will answer prayer.\n\nOnce in a classroom, we asked ministry students to list all the conditions they believed must be met for God to answer every prayer. It was astonishing to hear the scores of conditions they thought were necessary. The whole room seemed filled with nothing but conditions!\n\nWhen they finished, we said, "It's no wonder we have so few prayers answered. The great wonder is how anyone could ever get a single prayer answered if they had to meet all those conditions."\n\nThen we gave them the all-inclusive condition for answered prayer: "If ye abide in me, and my words abide in you, ye shall ask what ye will, and it shall be done unto you" (Jn. 15:7).\n\nThat's really all you have to do. This implies believing God's promises from your heart, living a righteous and holy life in Christ, and expecting God to answer when you pray. Anyone who does this without wavering in faith is just as certain to receive what they've asked for as they are certain they're alive.\n\nYou must "ask in faith, nothing wavering . . . and it shall be given him" (Jas. 1:5-8). You "must believe that he [God] is, and that he is a rewarder of them that diligently seek him" (Heb. 11:6).\n\nIs this too much to ask? Is this too much to do in order to get what you want in life? God is asking very little. Why shouldn't He require unwavering faith? Why should He freely give to people who don't believe He'll keep His Word? Should anyone expect God to answer on any other basis?\n\nGod has never—not once in all human history—failed to keep a single promise. There's no reasonable excuse for unbelief. People who don't choose faith are freely choosing unbelief. There's no neutral ground.\n\nPeople easily believe Satan's suggestions to doubt God's faithfulness. But you can choose to believe God instead of Satan. And God can—and does—expect this belief before He delivers what He's promised.\n\n## 4. The Greatness of the Promises Overwhelms People\n\nIt's true that God's promises are staggering when you first encounter them. But the more you meditate on them and experience them personally, the more simple and comprehensive they become.\n\nDon't stumble over the greatness of the promises—the God behind them is infinitely great! He created everything and can do anything we ask or think, according to His power working in us.\n\nIt's similar to a small child struggling to understand that their wealthy parents can easily provide for them—the child's limited perspective makes generosity seem impossible.\n\nLet's learn to accept God's statements at face value and boldly claim the full benefits of His provision. We are greatly loved—or such provision would never have been made.\n\nNothing is impossible for the believer who will believe. Don't tolerate the slightest doubt or suggestion that God won't hear and answer. If you do, you're already defeated.\n\nJames says of the doubter: "he that wavereth is like a wave of the sea driven with the wind and tossed. For let not that man think that he shall receive anything of the Lord. A double-minded man is unstable in all his ways" (Jas. 1:5-9).\n\nThere's no limitation to the gospel's provision for body, soul, or spirit—for any legitimate need or want. The promises are too plainly unlimited to be limited by humans. If there were limitations, God should have made them. Since He didn't, how dare anyone limit them if they want what's freely given?\n\nBecause there's no limitation to the promises or the abundance promised, make sure you don't limit yourself and your faith. Don't bring condemnation on yourself by lowering the gospel standard or questioning God's goodness.\n\n## 5. Not Understanding Moral Obligation\n\nSometimes your supply is cut short because you don't understand your moral obligation and don't put forth every effort to live up to it. You are subject to moral law and moral government, under moral obligation to live accordingly.\n\n**Moral law** is simply the rule of action for moral agents, established by recognized authority to enforce justice and prescribe duty. It governs free and intelligent action, as opposed to bondage and unintelligent action. It declares what a moral agent ought to choose, will, and intend.\n\n**The purpose of moral law** is to reveal and declare the rule of moral action for free wills—concerning the highest good of being and the universe—and to govern acts and intentions in relation to God and His eternal plan.\n\n**Moral law is unchangeable.** It can never vary in requiring that all free wills consecrate themselves to the same end God pursues—the highest good of the universe and everything in it.\n\nAll free moral agents are obligated to keep moral law because it governs the best good of being. Whatever harms being and society is clearly illegal and unwise, and must be prohibited. Free moral agents must choose to cooperate for the public good and oppose whatever brings misery and hardship. It's a mutual plan benefiting each person and the whole universe, and everyone is naturally obligated to maintain it according to their understanding.\n\n**Moral government** is necessary to direct, guide, and control moral agents. It must include rewards for good deeds and punishment for evil, or no society could function harmoniously for long. There must be standards everyone conforms to, proving themselves worthy members of society. There must be ways of dealing with rebels who work to destroy it.\n\nLaw without penalties and rewards isn't really law—it's just advice that free wills can accept or reject without consequences. Moral government is obligated to faithfully execute moral law for the good of everyone governed.\n\n**A moral governor** is also necessary—someone whose will and decisions are considered infallible by all subjects. He must be authoritative, not merely advisory. He must maintain his subjects' respect through faithful, unselfish execution of duties. He must be able to dispense penalties and rewards with justice and holiness.\n\nOnly one person in the universe is qualified for this role: **God**. His natural attributes, perfect moral character, relationship to the universe as Creator and source of all, and history of absolute justice qualify Him as Supreme Moral Governor. Since His glory and our good depend on mutual conformity to the same end, He's also obligated to keep moral law and require His subjects to be holy, consecrated to the same goal of securing the highest good for everyone.\n\n**Free moral agency** consists of intellect, sensibility, and free will—these form the foundation of moral obligation. The intellect includes reason and self-determination. The sensibility includes self-consciousness, feelings, emotions, desires, passions, and appetites. Free will is the power to choose concerning moral law—the faculty of choosing good or evil without compulsion. It was originally created in humanity and will exist through all eternity.\n\n**The basis of right choice** is always acting and choosing for the best good of all. Nothing happens in life except by someone's choice. Right choices that effect the greatest public and private good are all-important.\n\nMoral obligation extends to ultimate acts of will—the intention. You're obligated to choose holiness as the means to the best good and happiness of being. You're obligated to have faith instead of unbelief, to choose God instead of the devil, good instead of evil, and living for others instead of self.\n\n**The basis of justice** is the intention to act and choose for the best good. Even civil governments judge based on intent to do good or evil. The Bible values intention more than results or outward actions (2 Cor. 8:12). All vice and virtue come from the heart (Mk. 7:15-23; Mt. 7:19-21; Jas. 1:13-15; 3:9-14). Where the heart is right, all is considered right; where the heart is evil, all is considered evil.\n\nEven sinners do some outwardly good things, but their hearts aren't right. The intention is generally selfish, and good acts don't change the heart.\n\nSince the foundation of moral obligation is the highest good of all, entire consecration of free wills to secure this end constitutes obedience to moral law. Obedience must be whole and complete. You cannot choose the best good of others while simultaneously choosing self-gratification.\n\nGod cannot tolerate half-heartedness in choice and service (Rev. 3:15-16; Mt. 22:36-40). He cannot justify partial obedience according to your light. You must walk in the light as He is in the light to be cleansed from all sin (1 Jn. 1:7).\n\nIf you're constantly falling short of full obedience to known duty, there's never a moment when you're not under the curse of broken law (Jas. 2:10; 4:17). God cannot suspend execution until repentance, forgiveness, and full obedience are realized (Rom. 8:1-4, 13; Gal. 5:16-26; Rom. 6:16-23; Jn. 8:34; 1 Jn. 3:8-10).\n\nIf obedience to moral law means entire consecration to secure the best good of all according to your light, then **sin and disobedience** mean entire consecration by free choice to secure self-gratification regardless of others' rights. It's committing your will to serve Satan and the senses instead of God and intelligent moral law. It seeks governance by impulses and passions instead of intelligence and reason.\n\nSelf-gratification is the root of all sin. Human selfishness is closely allied to Satan's self-interest. Your will is free to oppose desire and lust contrary to the law, and when it doesn't, sin is committed. Your mind knows its obligation, so choosing contrary to the law isn't ignorance—it's free action bringing condemnation. Selfishness is always unreasonable. It denies true humanity and rational nature. It shows contempt for God's law in human reason.\n\nNo sinner chooses reason and common sense, or they would turn to God and quit sinning. Sinners seldom consult reason for their actions. They usually obey lust in stubborn rebellion against moral law and reason. They're lustful in heart whether they obey all lusts or not.\n\nAs long as they remain this way, they're condemned before God and need regeneration to bring them to obedience. If they abstain from certain sins, it's for selfish reasons—for loved ones, reputation, fear of punishment or disgrace—not because they're good at heart.\n\nWith all this in mind about moral law, moral government, and moral obligation, we can see that it's actually sinful to lack faith in God and to miss the good things He's promised in His Word.\n\nIf it's God's will and Word for you to have all the good things of life, then you're under moral obligation to seek accomplishing God's known will to get them. When you're passive, indifferent, and faithless, you're sinning against moral law and government—not living up to your moral obligation to get these benefits so you can be a good example to other moral agents.\n\nIt's absolute folly to think you're living up to your moral obligation, being the best example, having faith, obeying God, and securing the best good for yourself and others—while you're weak, sickly, defeated, sinful, corrupt, depraved, helpless, unhappy, and poverty-stricken.\n\nYet multitudes of Christians think—and are taught—to be satisfied with this lot in life, to patiently endure these limitations, to accept these evils as God's will, and to make no effort to escape these conditions. They actually believe they best glorify God and exemplify Christianity by willingly enduring these sufferings "for Christ's sake."\n\nIf they could see they're really enduring evils for the sake of men's false doctrines, they'd realize they're submitting to Satan's program to dishonor God's goodness and cause thousands of sinners to stumble over such "Christian examples"—rejecting a God who would supposedly will this kind of life on His children.\n\nIf they genuinely cared about acting "for Christ's sake," they'd embrace God's plan for their lives and receive abundant life through unlimited promises. They'd understand that it's wrong and contrary to moral law to be satisfied with their current lot.\n\nChristians can point to one or two isolated examples in Scripture—like the poor beggar Lazarus—as evidence that God wills saints to endure afflictions. But they need to realize we don't know why these individuals didn't appropriate Old Testament benefits. They didn't have the New Testament promises quoted in Lesson Ten.\n\nIf Christians would forget these few exceptions and focus on the scores of examples in both Testaments who were healthy, wealthy, and wise, it would at least show some effort to glorify God.\n\nAnyone with common intelligence knows it would better glorify God to be well and able to do His will in deed and truth, rather than being sick and unable to fulfill His purpose. It would better glorify God to have victory over Satan than to be defeated by him. It would better glorify God to be materially prosperous rather than begging from an ungodly world that laughs at how God "blesses" His children with nothing.\n\nThese conditions certainly don't prove God is being glorified. They only prove lack of faith and initiative in people who've been taught false doctrines about God and His providence. These doctrines serve mainly as excuses for unbelief and failure to attain what God provides.\n\nJust as truth sets free, lies and false doctrines bind, enslave, and give false security—making people think they're getting the best of the gospel under fallen conditions when they're not.\n\n## 6. Not Using What They Have for Others\n\nPeople fail to prosper and receive from God because they don't use what they have for others. They're too selfish and stingy. They have no faith that God will replenish if they give to help others.\n\nThey're full of worry and unbelief. They're afraid to launch into new opportunities. They have no vision to tackle anything. They pray, and when God answers with material blessing, they hesitate until the opportunity passes.\n\nThey're not diligent in business and lack unselfish motives for gaining wealth, health, and happiness. These conditions must be corrected in your personal life before you can expect anything definite from the gospel's promises.\n\nWe'll see in Lesson Twenty that the New Testament program gives every believer full and absolute power over demonic powers—God has made final, complete provision for each person to attain all known needs and wants spiritually, physically, and materially.\n\nIn Lesson Twenty-two, we'll prove that every believer has full power of attorney to act in Christ's stead, representing God and demonstrating His power to fallen humanity so they can know there's greater power than the devil and sin.\n\nIn Lessons Fourteen, Twenty-three, and Twenty-four, we'll prove you can have bodily healing, health, and freedom from sin in this life. In Lessons Sixteen, Twenty-eight, and Thirty, we'll prove from Scripture how to attain this place in God.\n\nWhat remains to address here is the believer's material needs. If you think we emphasize this too much, we do so because few, if any, reveal the Bible's true teaching on this aspect of life—which is, after all, a major part of human life and concern. We simply want our students to get every phase of Bible teaching and be well grounded in knowledge and experience.\n\nWhy should we withhold this aspect from those we've promised to help? It would be sin on our part to know abundant truth on this subject and fail to make it clear to the multitudes seeking truth, salvation, health, happiness, and prosperity.\n\nNo one can be at their best when constantly oppressed and worried about the next car payment, house rent, or enough food and clothes for loved ones. These are great burdens to average people, and it's a shame that all churches don't reveal God's abundant provision for such needs.\n\nIt would benefit the churches themselves, and it would bring great glory to God when sinners see believers happy and blessed with health and material things. Conversely, when sinners see saints living far below their own standard—knowing they're prospering more than Christians—it certainly doesn't make them want to exchange their life for the Christian life.\n\nIf the full truth about material help from God were taught biblically, preachers wouldn't have to beg for money in every service or use unscriptural means to raise funds. If church members were taught the gospel of prosperity and actually experienced material help from God as they do spiritual and physical help, the minister would only need to remind them: "I've taught you and led you into prosperity. God has been good and prospered you, so come now and meet all the needs of God's work." More and more, God would bless such people of faith (Mal. 3:10-12).\n\nMembers who realize God has been good to them—that they have what they have because of His goodness—would gladly give to supply others. After all, this is what money and material things are for.\n\nNote these passages proving this: "And as ye would that men should do to you, do ye also to them likewise. For if ye love them which love you, what thank have ye? For sinners also love those that love them. And if ye do good to them which do good to you, what thank have ye? For sinners also do even the same. And if ye lend to them of whom ye hope to receive, what thank have ye? For sinners also lend to sinners, to receive as much again. But love your enemies, and do good, and lend, hoping for nothing again, and your reward shall be great, and ye shall be called the children of the Highest: for he is kind unto the unthankful and to the evil. Be ye therefore merciful, as your Father also is merciful. Judge not, and ye shall not be judged: condemn not, and ye shall not be condemned; forgive, and ye shall be forgiven. Give, and it shall be given unto you; good measure, pressed down, and shaken together, and running over, shall men give into your bosom. For with the same measure ye mete withal it shall be measured to you again" (Lk. 6:30-38).\n\nThis passage not only gives God's law and moral obligation to give, but also reveals laws of prosperity.\n\nHere are more passages on what to do with material gain: "Distributing to the necessity of the saints; given to hospitality . . . love worketh no ill to his neighbor; therefore love is the fulfilling of the law" (Rom. 12:13; 13:10); "If we have sown unto you spiritual things, is it a great thing if we shall reap your carnal things? . . . Even so hath the Lord ordained that they which preach the gospel should live of the gospel" (1 Cor. 9:7-14); "He which soweth sparingly shall reap also sparingly; and he which soweth bountifully shall reap also bountifully. Every man according as he purposeth in his heart, so let him give; not grudgingly, or of necessity: for God loveth a cheerful [hilarious] giver. And God is able to make all grace abound toward you; that ye, always having all sufficiency in all things, may abound to every good work" (2 Cor. 9:6-15); "Let him that is taught in the word communicate [give of material gain] unto him that teacheth in all good things" (Gal. 6:6); "That they do good, that they be rich in good works, ready to distribute, willing to communicate" (give of good things to others, 1 Tim. 6:17-19); "I have shewed you all things, how that so labouring ye ought to support the weak, and to remember the words of the Lord Jesus, how he said, It is more blessed to give than to receive" (Acts 20:35); "Let him that stole steal no more: but rather let him labour, working with his own hands the thing which is good, that he may have to give to him that needeth" (Eph. 4:28).\n\n"But whoso hath this world's good, and seeth his brother have need, and shutteth up his bowels of compassion from him, how dwelleth the love of God in him? My little children, let us not love in word, neither in tongue, but in deed and in truth. And hereby we know we are of the truth, and shall assure our hearts before him . . . And whatsoever we ask we receive of him, because we keep his commandments, and do those things that are pleasing in his sight" (1 Jn. 3:17-22).\n\nIf all Christians would have faith in God and follow the simple laws of prosperity in these passages and the following supplement, God would bless them abundantly—with more and more to help others. The all-inclusive law of prosperity is to consecrate yourself to helping others and use what you have, and God will give the increase.\n\nGod will make ways and present opportunities for success. Don't be afraid to launch into new ventures as you learn God's will through prayer and as possibilities arise. Have faith—reckless faith if necessary—and God will honor it. Then as you use material gains for others' good, God will enlarge your capacity for more, making you an ever-increasing channel of supply and blessing.\n\nPicture it this way: it's like a water pipe—the more freely you let water flow through, the more the source keeps filling it. But if you pinch the pipe shut, the flow stops entirely.\n\nYou must start with love for doing things for others. Love is the beginning of all worthwhile achievements in life. You cannot love God and keep the first commandment without also keeping the second.\n\nJesus said, "Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind. This is the first and great commandment. And the second is like unto it, Thou shalt love thy neighbor as thyself. On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets" (Mt. 22:34-40).\n\nIf you obey these commandments, you'll observe the golden rule. You'll be interested in helping others succeed. You'll work for others. You'll sacrifice self-interest for others' interests. You'll make many friends, and you cannot make friends without gaining prosperity yourself. Your friends will want to help you succeed in business.\n\nDon't forget to seize opportunities that come your way. Make the best of them—always intending to do good with what God prospers you with. Give without thought of getting. Serve without thought of reward. You will succeed spiritually, physically, and financially.\n\nThe law of Christ is: "whosoever will save his life shall lose it, but whosoever will lose his life for my sake shall find it" (Mt. 16:25). In doing things for Christ, you do things for others: "Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me" (Mt. 18:1-10; 25:34-40).\n\nChrist taught that the law of increase is using what we have. The man with five talents gained five more; the one with two talents gained two more; but the one with one talent hid it and gained nothing. "For unto everyone that hath shall be given, and he shall have abundance; but from him that hath not [did not use what he had, thinking it too small] shall be taken away even that which he hath" (Mt. 25:14-30).\n\nThe widow in Elisha's day simply used what she had, and there was great increase (2 Ki. 4:1-7). She wanted the money to pay debts and save her children. God met her faith, and she had more than enough.\n\nAny legitimate desire for any good thing in life is perfectly normal and right. God will not withhold it, provided proper unselfishness and faith are used. The selfish person always asks, "What will I gain?" The unselfish person asks, "How can I help others when I get what I want?"\n\nThose who go through life solely getting instead of giving seldom acquire prosperity. When we start with what we can do for others, there's every chance for success.\n\nLook forward to real service to others. Soon your hands will be full of good deeds and loving memories, and others will give back to you (Lk. 6:30-38). Look for work that helps others. Sell goods and services that solve people's problems. Give sound, godly, biblical advice to everyone you meet.\n\nBe honest in the smallest business details. Thank God for blessings you need and want. Have faith they're yours. Make plans for proper, unselfish use of blessings. Be pleasant and happy before others. Be thankful for your work.\n\nDon't try to reach the top in one day. Be diligent in business, cheerful in giving, merciful in dealings, kind and sympathetic and understanding to all. Put your faith in God and His promises. Claim their benefits. Trust God in adversity. Let any failure become a stepping-stone to something greater.\n\nUse your influence for good, for God, and for lost souls. Help those in sickness and need. Pray earnestly to succeed and be blessed with all the good things of life.\n\nAbove all, get right with God and consecrate yourself to the best good of being and of the universe—and you will prosper in all things along with God.\n\nBelieve God wants you to have prosperity, health, and the good things of life. Believe they are His will for you. Live in faith for the things you want, for "Faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen" (Heb. 11:1). It's the life principle that "calleth those things which be not as though they were" (Rom. 4:12-24).\n\nFaith is making a blueprint of what you want and working toward that end. Before you get what you want, act as though you already have it. Visualize it as yours. See it with your mind and heart. Put forth every effort to bring it about.\n\nTurn over to God the things you cannot do—He will bring them to pass. Just relax and have faith in God for matters where you're helpless. When you worry and fear that events won't work out, you actually hinder God from working things out for you.\n\n## 7. Not Following the Laws of Answered Prayer\n\nPeople fail to get what they want from God because they don't faithfully follow the laws of answered prayer as Scripture plainly states. If you want answers to prayer, faithfully observe these laws:\n\n> (1) Study the Bible promises until you're convinced your need is covered by them and it's God's will for you to have what you desire (1 Jn. 5:14-15).\n\n> (2) Concentrate on eliminating all selfishness concerning what you want; desire it for the good of being and of others (1 Jn. 3:17-24).\n\n> (3) Be sure you're right with God, in Christ, and His Words are in you, according to Jn. 15:7; 2 Cor. 5:17.\n\n> (4) Be sure you want it badly enough to firmly resist doubt and the devil (Jas. 4:7; 1 Pet. 5:8-9).\n\n> (5) Ask in faith, nothing wavering (Heb. 10:19-23; 11:6; Jas. 1:4-8).\n\n> (6) Never be fearful of the outcome. Simply cast all your anxiety and worry on God (1 Pet. 5:\n\n---\n\nGod's plan for your complete provision hasn't changed. What changes is whether the conditions on your side are being met. So here's the question that requires complete honesty: Which of the specific barriers named in this lesson — unbelief, sin, ignorance of the Word, failure to act on faith — is currently operating in your life? And what are you prepared to do about it today?	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk460000newhjoic62dez	cmnknk45y000gewhjn5pl0kw9	Lesson 13 — The Dispensation of Human Government	READING	2122	6	\N	t	After the flood, God handed human beings something He had never given before: the authority to execute judgment on other humans. Capital punishment, civil government, the power of the sword — these weren't innovations of later civilization. They were divine grants made to Noah the moment he stepped off the ark. And the experiment that followed — humanity governing itself for 427 years — ended at the Tower of Babel in the most spectacular display of collective pride in history.\n\nLast time we examined why God's provision fails to reach so many believers. Now we zoom out to the dispensational level: after the global judgment of the flood, what new framework did God establish for human society?\n\n![Lesson 13 — The Dispensation of Human Government](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsTGaIQGzI0Sg3uieQlJxkWsZOR6bnzGDtEw9a)\n\n### THE PRESENT OR POST-DILUVIAN AGE\n\n**(Gen. 8:15—Rev. 19:21)**\n\nThis age stretches from the flood all the way to the Millennium. It's a long stretch of time, and within it we find four distinct dispensations:\n\n> 1. The Dispensation of Human Government—from the flood to Abraham (Gen. 8:15–11:9).\n\n> 2. The Dispensation of Promise—from Abraham to Moses (Gen. 12:1—Exod. 12:37).\n\n> 3. The Dispensation of Law—from Moses to Christ (Exod. 12:38—Mt. 2:25).\n\n> 4. The Dispensation of Grace—Christ to the Millennium (Mt. 3:1—Rev. 19:21).\n\n## I. The Definition of Human Government\n\nSo why do we call this the Dispensation of Human Government? Because right after the flood—after that long age of freedom—God set up something new: human government by law.\n\nHe gave Noah specific laws to govern the race, and from that point on, humanity was responsible for governing itself (Gen. 9:1-7). Here's what God laid out:\n\n> 1. "Be fruitful and multiply, and replenish the earth" (Gen. 9:1, 7).\n\n> 2. "Into thine hand are they [animals] delivered" (Gen. 9:2).\n\n> 3. "Every moving thing [clean or unclean] that liveth shall be meat for you; even as the green herb have I given you all things" (Gen. 9:3).\n\n> 4. "The blood thereof [of animals] shall ye not eat" (Gen. 9:4).\n\n> 5. "Whoso sheddeth man's blood, by man shall his blood be shed: for in the image of God made he him" (Gen. 9:5-6).\n\n> 6. "I establish my covenant with you, and with your seed after you; and with every living creature that is with you . . . for perpetual generations . . . the bow shall be in the cloud; and I will look upon it, that I may remember the everlasting covenant between God and every living creature of all flesh that is upon the earth" (Gen. 9:8-17).\n\nThese few laws have formed the foundation for all laws—divine and human—in every age since the flood. This is when God instituted capital punishment, and here's the thing: He has never revoked it. It continues as an eternal law and will even be in force during the Millennium (Isa. 11:4-9; 65:20-25).\n\nPaul reaffirms this plainly in Rom. 13:1-6, teaching that even in this Age of Grace, law-enforcement officers are ordained of God. They are His ministers who do not bear "the sword in vain" but are supposed to "execute wrath upon him that doeth evil."\n\nThink of it this way: just like a family can't function if parents never address wrongdoing, societies can't survive without consequences for crime. Without punishment for wrongdoing, no human government could endure for long.\n\nHuman governments are part of God's moral government. The highest good of all creation is God's chief aim in moral government, and civil and family governments are necessary to accomplish that goal. This isn't just clear in Gen. 9 and Rom. 13—you'll find it throughout Scripture (Dan. 2:21; 4:17-25; 5:21; 1 Pet. 2:13-14).\n\nIt's the duty of all people to help establish and support human government for the preservation of society. Every person has a moral obligation to use their influence and power to promote good government that conforms to God's law and serves the highest good of all people.\n\nNow, administrators who rule contrary to God's law and the best good of all will eventually face God's punishment for misusing their authority. God never approves selfish and wicked administration, and if it continues too long, it will be overthrown.\n\nWe're obligated to obey government when its requirements don't conflict with God's moral law—regardless of the personal character or motives of the ruler. As Scripture says, Christians are always to obey "every ordinance of man for the Lord's sake: whether it be to the king, as supreme; or unto governors, as unto them that are sent by him for the punishment of evildoers, and for the praise of them that do well. For so is the will of God, that with well doing ye may put to silence the ignorance of foolish men" (1 Pet. 2:13-17).\n\nChristians shouldn't leave human government entirely to the ungodly. Upholding and assisting good government isn't neglecting the salvation of souls—it's actually one of the greatest means of saving souls! Promoting public and private good creates an environment where people can hear the gospel.\n\nIt makes no sense to say that saved people are obligated to obey government while also arguing they should have nothing to do with choosing those who govern.\n\nMany Christians have wrong ideas about government. They think they should never use the legal system against the ungodly and that they should just suffer whatever harm anyone wants to heap on them. But while the Bible does teach that we shouldn't personally avenge our wrongs, it also teaches that avenging such wrongs is exactly what law and government are for (Rom. 13:1-6; 1 Tim. 1:8-10).\n\nBelievers aren't supposed to sue each other but rather settle differences within the church, not before unbelievers (1 Cor. 6). But there's no sin in seeing justice done according to the law.\n\nSome Christians argue that if everyone walked in love and holiness, we could do away with all law. But that's not quite right. As we saw in earlier lessons, law and government are necessary even for holy beings filled with love. It's similar to how a loving family still needs house rules—love doesn't eliminate the need for clear guidelines.\n\nLaw is the rule of duty that distinguishes right from wrong between moral beings. Without it, there could be no holy, loving society where righteousness prevails. Law will always continue as the standard of right in all eternal societies. And as long as law remains, there must be penalties—otherwise law becomes mere advice. It will always be the duty and right of rulers to enforce law and administer punishment when needed.\n\nSome Christians argue that political participation is sinful because government is maintained by force, which seems inconsistent with the gospel. But these are false theories. As we've seen, God Himself instituted human government, and Christians are commanded in the New Testament to pay taxes and support government (Rom. 13:1-7; 1 Pet. 2:13-17).\n\nIn a democratic government, politics should be an important part of the Christian's religious life. No one can be fully good to the extent of their moral obligations without concerning themselves with governmental affairs.\n\nNow, Christians certainly have better things to do than follow one political party exclusively, take part in any party's evil, or meddle in politics selfishly. But they are obligated to participate in government in a godly manner. Why? Because they're obligated to seek the best good of the society they're part of, to promote the good of all people, and human government is one area of life that materially, morally, and spiritually affects everyone's well-being.\n\nEven if God didn't specifically command it, Christians would still have a duty to help establish and support human government for the best good of all. It's a basic principle of Christianity: whatever is essential to the public and private good of all moral beings, Christians have the right and obligation to pursue.\n\nBoth reason and experience, along with Scripture, make this obligatory. Since government is necessary for the best good of all, every citizen is obligated to help bring about the best government possible. When Christians fail to do their duty, they shouldn't complain when government turns bad and the wicked take control. There are enough church members in America to have excellent government in conformity with God's law—if they would all do their duty.\n\nRegarding government by force: this is necessary as long as wicked people refuse to dedicate themselves to their own good and the good of others. Just as God commanded punishment for crime in Gen. 9 and under the Mosaic law, it remains the duty of governments today to impose penalties when it's for the public good. Family governments must punish wrongdoing. God Himself does the same in His moral government.\n\nFor Christians to think their faith makes them flawless or exempts them from working toward the goals government is meant to achieve is simply wrong.\n\nHuman governments aren't founded on God's arbitrary will but on the genuine needs of human beings to secure the highest good. Picture it this way: if even a small family needs rules and consequences, how much more do communities, states, and nations need them?\n\nChristians, instead of tearing down human governments, are obligated to support them. When government becomes corrupt, it needs reforming—not abandoning. Just as we don't abandon the Church when it needs reformation, we shouldn't abandon government either.\n\nChristians are obligated to support governments when:\n- They don't require anything contrary to God's law\n- They don't demand acts that violate moral obligation\n- They don't force people to violate their conscience\n- They meet the needs of the people being governed\n\nOn these grounds, both governors and the governed should recognize their relationship and responsibility to each other in maintaining good government. If the right to govern is based on public interest, then the right and duty to use necessary means to govern must be recognized by all.\n\nIt's absurd to believe rulers have a right to govern but no right to use the necessary means to carry out government. Making this same error, many Christians object to capital punishment, dealing with mobs, suppressing rebellions, or making war. They think government can always be carried on without taking life. Others go so far as to claim government can function without force to sustain the authority of law.\n\nThese positions can't be maintained with any logic, and they're not supported by God or Scripture.\n\nIt's absurd to hold that rulers can rule only as long as subjects voluntarily obey—and when they refuse, government should cease to exist. The right to govern can't exist where the right to enforce obedience doesn't exist.\n\nThis attitude denies the right to maintain government for everyone's good. It denies the right to use force to execute law or take life to preserve government. This theory claims that governments should love others too much to use force—or that society should be loved too much to execute law upon those dedicated to destroying the good.\n\nSuch thinking overlooks the very foundation of moral obligation, which requires everyone to dedicate themselves to the public good. It destroys all morality and religion. It's foolish to think enlightened love should forbid necessary execution of law.\n\nSome claim the commandment "thou shalt not kill" means no human life should ever be taken for any crime. But this actually sets itself against God's Word while pretending to follow it.\n\nThis commandment, taken literally, would forbid killing animals or plants as much as humans. The question is: what kind of killing does it forbid? Certainly not all killing of human beings, because the very next chapter (Exod. 21) commands taking human life for certain crimes.\n\nSix times in that one chapter—and scores of times elsewhere—God commanded the death penalty. Many times God commanded Israel to kill the giant races and enemies of God in the promised land. Clearly, the commandment against murder doesn't apply to capital punishment or war.\n\nGovernments have an undoubted right to do whatever is necessary for the highest public good. Nothing is wrong with taking human life when necessary to accomplish the purpose of government. The Bible recognizes this right everywhere—and even if it didn't, this right would still exist.\n\nNo one has a right to keep their life when they forfeit it by breaking a law carrying the death penalty. Whenever someone dedicates themselves to destroying the public good, and taking their life becomes necessary to secure that good, their life is forfeited. It's the government's duty to take it.\n\nThe same principle applies to mobs, insurrections, rebellions, and wars that endanger the good of all. It must be both the right and duty of government and its citizens to use every possible means to suppress rebellion and war—which are simply crime on a massive scale.\n\nThat war is necessary under certain circumstances is clear because moral law permits it and God has commanded it. If it were wrong, God wouldn't have commanded it. Rulers are God's ministers to execute wrath upon the ungodly and preserve moral law and government for everyone's good. They're obligated to make war if that's the only way to attain the highest public good.\n\nUnder any other circumstances, war is a horrible crime. Selfish war is wholesale murder, and participating in it makes you complicit in mass murder—unless it becomes God's will and the only way to preserve society.\n\nChristians aren't obligated to support unjustly waged wars. On the other hand, just as individual criminals must be punished, there may be times when criminal nations must be punished for society's good as a whole.\n\nOur duty isn't to judge when this becomes necessary just for ourselves but for the world as a whole. When organized crime—whether a small group, a nation, or multiple nations—determines to destroy society, it becomes necessary to suppress that crime just as much as with individuals. Nations are bound by the same moral law as individuals and must be punished when they commit crimes.\n\nThus God, in replenishing the race after the flood, instituted human government and capital punishment for crime. Since He never changes, this is still His will for people and governments. God knows how to rule rebellious free moral agents and curb crime. If human governments were as strict as God commands, there would be infinitely less crime.\n\n## II. The Length of Human Government (Gen. 11:10-32)\n\nThis dispensation lasted from the flood to Abraham's call—a period of 427 years, proven by Gen. 11:10-32 as follows:\n\n| Generation | Years | Event | Reference |\n|------------|-------|-------|-----------|\n| 1. Shem | 2 years after the flood | begat Arphaxad | Gen. 11:10 |\n| 2. Arphaxad | 35 years | begat Salah | Gen. 11:12 |\n| 3. Salah | 30 years | begat Eber | Gen. 11:14 |\n| 4. Eber | 34 years | begat Peleg | Gen. 11:16 |\n| 5. Peleg | 30 years | begat Reu | Gen. 11:18 |\n| 6. Reu | 32 years | begat Serug | Gen. 11:20 |\n| 7. Serug | 30 years | begat Nahor | Gen. 11:22 |\n| 8. Nahor | 29 years | begat Terah | Gen. 11:24 |\n| 9. Terah | 205 years | died at Haran | Gen. 11:32 |\n\n**TOTAL: 427 years.** Abraham was 75 years old at this time.\n\nShem was still alive and about 525 years old when 75-year-old Abraham was called to leave Ur of the Chaldees for Canaan. Shem lived as a contemporary of Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, and Melchisedec (Gen. 11:10-32; 12:4; 25:7, 20-26).\n\n## III. The Favorable Beginning (Gen. 8:15–9:17)\n\nNoah was 601 years old—ripe in experience and wisdom. All the family were fully grown and married. They had so much going for them:\n\n- The warning of the flood behind them\n- The eternal covenant (Gen. 8:20–9:17)\n- Knowledge of true worship (Gen. 8:21-22)\n- God's will concerning human government and its laws (Gen. 9:1-7)\n- The promise of eternal preservation for humans and animals on Earth (Gen. 8:21-22; 9:1-17)\n- Full control of the Earth and responsibility to govern it for God (Gen. 9:1-7)\n- Full liberty to govern themselves\n\nThey had countless favorable conditions under which to prove true to God.\n\n## IV. The Test of Man in Human Government (Gen. 9:1-7)\n\nThe test for humanity in this age was to obey the laws of human government, prove true to God in executing these laws, remain faithful in governing the race for everyone's highest good, and have faith in God while dedicating their lives to His will according to the light they received.\n\n## V. The Purpose of God in Human Government (Gen. 9:1-7)\n\nGod's purpose in this age was to give humanity another chance to prove true to their responsibility according to His known will.\n\nGod had tested humanity in a state of innocence to see if they would prove worthy of higher glory—and they failed. He had tested humanity in the long age of freedom to see how they would follow their own conscience about right and wrong—and they failed.\n\nNow God's purpose was to give humanity some definite laws governing their actions concerning good and evil. Since humanity had failed to choose good without law, they would now be compelled by law to do good and refuse evil.\n\nGod purposed for humanity to have self-government, so He gave them all necessary laws to govern themselves. Since He planned for people to know Him personally and obey His will, He revealed the means of reconciliation.\n\nHe had Noah preserve seven clean animals for sacrifice so people could show their faith in the blood of the coming Redeemer and be reconciled to God. God planned for humanity to preserve pure Adamite stock so the seed of the woman could come into the world, bringing about full redemption of the Earth according to His eternal purpose.\n\n## VI. The Means of God in Accomplishing This Purpose (Gen. 9:1-6)\n\nThe laws of human government were established so humanity could rule itself in righteousness and justice forever. True worship of God began, and God's full revelation of His will for this period was made known so people could be fully reconciled to God and eternally redeemed.\n\nAll the giant races had been destroyed in the flood, leaving only eight pure Adamites, so human stock could remain pure until the seed of the woman could come to complete the work of eliminating all rebellion and fully restoring humanity's dominion.\n\nEverything necessary to accomplish God's will and humanity's highest good was within their control, so they could prove true to God during this probationary period.\n\n## VII. The Failure of Man in Human Government (Gen. 9:18–11:9)\n\n### 1. THE FAILURE OF NOAH (Gen. 9:20-24)\n\nNoah, a preacher of righteousness (2 Pet. 2:5), who had condemned drunkenness before the flood, became drunk himself and was shamefully uncovered in his tent.\n\nThis perhaps wasn't deliberate on his part, but it happened. Whether a sin is deliberate or not, it's still sin. Noah was old enough and had witnessed enough drunkenness before the flood to have no excuse for this condition. Regardless of all his godly living before and after this incident, the fact remains: he failed God and humanity on this occasion.\n\n### 2. THE FAILURE OF HAM (Gen. 9:22-27)\n\nHam sinned by revealing his aged father's shame. He showed lack of honor to his parents and broke the law of parental authority. For this he was cursed to be "a servant of servants" to his brethren (Gen. 9:25).\n\n### 3. THE FAILURE OF MANKIND IN GENERAL (Gen. 9:1-6; 11:1-9)\n\nIn Gen. 9:1-6 we have God's definite laws for humanity in this period. In Gen. 11:1-9 we see humanity's deliberate rebellion against God and His laws.\n\nPeople disobeyed God's command to spread across the Earth, to worship Him properly, and to live godly and upright in the fear of God. Pride, self-boastfulness, and hero-worship became prevalent in this age. Nimrod was the most conspicuous example of this failure (Gen. 10:8-9; 1 Chron. 1:10).\n\nJosephus says, "Nimrod persuaded mankind not to ascribe their happiness to God, but to think that his own excellency was the source of it. And he soon changed things into tyranny, thinking there was no other way to wean men from God and fear of Him, than by making them rely upon his own power."\n\nNimrod founded a kingdom in Shinar with four great cities—Babel, Erech, Accad, and Calneh (Gen. 10:8-10). In those days, wild beasts were so numerous they became a menace to life and property (Exod. 23:29; Lev. 23:22). Nimrod became a leader by hunting down and killing these beasts.\n\nHe taught people to build walls around cities and dwellings for protection from wild animals at night. He became the great leader and benefactor of humanity—which gave him the opportunity to lead people away from God.\n\nHe inspired people to build a city and tower to reach Heaven and make a great name for themselves. He taught them to centralize instead of spreading across the Earth as God commanded. He defied God to send another flood and taught people to seek vengeance on God for flooding their ancestors.\n\nNimrod and his queen Semiramis started the "Babylonian Cult," a new religion claiming the highest wisdom and ability to reveal the most divine secrets. The purpose of this religion was to rule the world and keep people in blind obedience to the Supreme Pontiff.\n\nOnce admitted as members, people were no longer Babylonians, Assyrians, or Egyptians—they became members of a mystical brotherhood under a high priest whose word was final in all their affairs.\n\nThe objects of worship were the Supreme Father, the Queen of Heaven, and her Son. The last two were really the only objects of worship since the Supreme Father supposedly didn't interfere with mortal affairs.\n\nSemiramis was a paragon of unbridled lust and was worshipped as "Rhea, the Mother of the Gods." Prostitution was compulsory in this religion. She made Babylon the seat of idolatry and sin.\n\nThe so-called Christian festivals such as Christmas, Lady Day, Easter, and Lent, and many other modern rituals like the sign of the cross, the Rosary, monastic orders, and certain church rituals all came from this Babylonian religion—observed centuries before Christ. For proof, see the Encyclopedia Britannica, the book of Nimrod III, page 239; Chronican Paschale Vol. 1, page 65; Hesiod Theogonia, Vol. 36, page 453; Herodotus, book 1, cap. 199, page 92; and Two Babylons by Hyslop.\n\nIn Nimrod's days, this cult gained a great hold on the whole race before the confusion of tongues scattered people abroad. This explains why religions in all heathen lands have similar traditions and practices. Changes developed over the ages to suit various peoples after they were scattered. (See our book Revelation Expounded for details.)\n\nThis religion was Satan's attempt to counterfeit true worship and satisfy people's religious nature. His effort to rule through Nimrod was his first attempt to raise up a universal ruler through whom he could control the entire race. It failed because God raised up Israel to defeat this plan.\n\nMany other attempts have been made since to control the race through one absolute ruler, but all have failed. Satan will make one last effort through the future Antichrist, who will attempt to become a worldwide dictator. He too will fail because Christ will return from Heaven to defeat him before he takes all Jerusalem—much less all the nations—as we'll see in later lessons.\n\nThere's a Babylonian description of the tower of Babel discovered in 1876. According to this description, there was a grand court about 900 x 1,156 feet and a smaller one 450 x 1,056 feet. Around the court were six gates leading to temples. Beyond that was a platform with walls and four gates on each side, enclosing a large building about 200 feet square.\n\nAround the tower's base were many small shrines dedicated to various gods. On the East were sixteen shrines; on the North, two temples; on the South, one temple; and on the West, the principal buildings including a double house with a court between two wings 58 feet wide. The wings measured 34 x 166 feet and 108 x 166 feet. In these western chambers was the main god's couch (about 7 x 15 feet), a golden throne, and other valuable objects.\n\nIn the center stood the tower itself, built in stages that decreased from bottom to top, each square:\n\n- First stage: 300 feet square, 110 feet high\n- Second stage: 260 feet square, 60 feet high\n- Third stage: 200 feet square, 20 feet high\n- Fourth stage: 170 feet square, 20 feet high\n- Fifth stage: 140 feet square, 20 feet high\n- Sixth stage: 110 feet square, 20 feet high\n- Seventh stage: 80 feet long, 60 feet wide, 50 feet high—containing a sanctuary for the God Bel-Merodach\n\nThe total height was 300 feet, matching the breadth of its base.\n\nThe tower was apparently completed since Scripture doesn't mention any work stoppage on it—only on the city (Gen. 11:4, 8). The phrase "reach unto heaven" literally means a high tower. Building a tower that could literally reach the planet Heaven, millions of miles away, would be impossible. The sun is 93 million miles away, and Heaven is beyond that.\n\nThe tower and city were Nimrod's project, stopped by the confusion of tongues. One ancient Babylonian tablet reads: "The building of this illustrious tower offended the gods. In a night they threw down what they had built. They scattered them abroad, and made strange their speech. Their progress was impeded. They wept hot tears for Babylon."\n\n### The Second Eruption of the Sons of God\n\nAs we saw in an earlier lesson, there were two eruptions of fallen angels who married the daughters of men and produced two races of giants—one before the flood and one after. This is plainly stated in Gen. 6:4, "and also after that"—meaning after the flood, the sons of God married daughters of men and they bore children who were giants.\n\nThe second eruption occurred in this dispensation, for when Abraham entered the land at the beginning of the next age, "the Canaanite was then [already] in the land" (Gen. 12:6; 13:7).\n\nThe Canaanites were offspring of the sons of God and daughters of men after the flood, as seen in earlier lessons. This second eruption happened soon after the flood, reflecting Satan's quick work to always defeat God if possible.\n\nThe giant couch in Nimrod's temple suggests giants were already on Earth in Nimrod's time—about 100 years after the flood, or the second generation according to Gen. 10:6-10. The second generation in Shem's line was Salah, born 37 years after the flood. If Nimrod was born around that time, he rose to prominence at least 100 years after the flood.\n\nThis explains how the whole race was so deep in sin by Abraham's time, 427 years after the flood. This period, like the Age of Conscience, is referred to in Rom. 1:17-32.\n\nGod had promised not to send another flood, so Satan attempted again to corrupt pure Adamite stock so the seed of the woman, Christ, couldn't come to destroy Satan's hold on the race.\n\nSince God couldn't kill the giants by flood, He had to use other means. God's plan was to raise up a strong nation through Abraham to kill the second race of giants as the flood had destroyed the first.\n\nThus the race became sinful and idolatrous, setting the stage for the next part of God's program, which we'll study in the coming lessons.\n\n## VIII. The Judgment of God upon Man in Human Government\n\nIn Gen. 11:1-9, we learn God sent confusion of tongues upon humanity and scattered them across the Earth. This was the first judgment for failure to carry out His will and purpose.\n\nBy doing this, God broke up humanity's united rebellion against Him and fulfilled His original purpose of spreading people across the Earth.\n\nThe second judgment came in Peleg's days—he died 340 years after the flood. This judgment was the division of the Earth into islands and continents, as explained in an earlier supplement.\n\nThis division happened after the confusion of tongues and the scattering of people (Gen. 11:9). Before this, the whole race spoke one language and lived centralized in one place (Gen. 11:1). After they scattered, the continents divided—explaining how different branches of the race are found on various continents and islands.\n\nThink of it like this: take a world map and remove the Atlantic Ocean, and the eastern parts of the Americas fit perfectly with the western parts of Europe and Africa. When exactly during Peleg's life the Earth divided isn't known—and it doesn't matter. The fact is, it happened in his days, explaining how the Indians got to the Americas and how other peoples reached various parts of the divided Earth.\n\nSeeing He couldn't deal with humanity as a whole, God gave them up and turned to Abraham and his descendants, dealing almost exclusively with them during the next two ages. This abandonment of humanity in general to further His plan was the worst judgment that could have come to the human race.\n\nThis is how this age ended. This is how the stage was set for the next phase of God's dealings with the human race through the chosen family.\n\n## IX. God's Provision of Redemption (Gen. 8:20; 12:8)\n\nGod's provision of redemption remained the same as in previous dispensations. Salvation was available to all who would believe in the blood of Christ that was to be shed. Animal sacrifices were tokens of faith for those who conformed to God's redeeming will.\n\n---\n\n## Questions on Lesson Thirteen\n\n- Define "The Present Age." How many dispensations are included in it?\n\n- Why is this age called "Human Government"?\n\n- Name six main laws of this period that were proposed by God to rule man.\n\n- Prove from Scripture that God has an eternal plan for man.\n\n- What will be the eternal relationship between natural generations and the resurrected saints of all ages?\n\n- Who instituted capital punishment for certain crimes?\n\n- Has God ever revoked the law of capital punishment? Will He ever revoke it?\n\n- Could human governments long endure without punishments for crime?\n\n- Are human governments part of the moral government of God?\n\n- What is the chief aim of moral government?\n\n- Why were human governments instituted?\n\n- What is the moral obligation of all men concerning human governments?\n\n- Should Christians abandon their moral obligation in times when civil rulers become corrupt? What should they do?\n\n- How long and to what extent should Christians obey human governments?\n\n- Is helping promote good government neglecting the salvation of souls?\n\n- Should Christians go to law with each other? Prove.\n\n- Is it biblical for them to go to law with the ungodly in cases of necessity?\n\n- Could all laws be dispensed with if all beings were holy? Why?\n\n- Will God have eternal laws for eternal societies? Why?\n\n- Could there be law without penalties? Why?\n\n- Is it sinful and unbiblical for Christians to partake in politics? Why?\n\n- What is one of the first principles of Christianity?\n\n- Is it biblical to carry on government by force?\n\n- Did God demand one kind of righteousness in the Old and another kind in the New Testament? Prove.\n\n- When is it the duty of governments to inflict penalties?\n\n- Upon what basis are human governments founded?\n\n- Upon what grounds should governors and those governed realize their relationship and responsibility to each other?\n\n- Is it biblical for government to make war? Upon what grounds?\n\n- Are war and murder the same thing? Why?\n\n- What broad powers do governments have the right to exercise?\n\n- When does war or participation in war become a crime?\n\n- What kind of wars can Christians justly support?\n\n- What is the length of the Dispensation of Human Government?\n\n- State the favorable beginning of man in Human Government.\n\n- What was the test for man in Human Government?\n\n- What was the purpose of God in Human Government?\n\n- What were the means of God in accomplishing this purpose?\n\n- Explain the failure of Noah, Ham, and mankind in general.\n\n- Who was the great leader and rebel against God in this age?\n\n- State fully his rebellion against God.\n\n- How did he gain such leadership among men?\n\n- What kind of religion did he start? What was its purpose? Did it succeed?\n\n- What was Satan's purpose in this religion? Has he ever succeeded? Will he ever succeed in this purpose?\n\n- State the general plan for the city and tower of Babel.\n\n- Was the tower ever completed? The city?\n\n- Did man actually conceive the idea to build a tower to reach Heaven?\n\n- When did the second eruption of the sons of God take place?\n\n- What was the result of the marriages of the sons of God and daughters of men?\n\n- What was Satan's purpose in this?\n\n- Explain fully the judgments of God upon men in Human Government.\n\n---\n\nThe Dispensation of Human Government ended at Babel — the moment humanity used its collective power to defy God outright. The lesson is brutally consistent with every other dispensation: when free moral agents are given authority, they eventually use it to build monuments to themselves rather than to God. Here's the question worth sitting with: In the authority God has given you — over your household, your work, your influence — are you using it to advance His purposes or to build something with your name on it?	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk44k000dewhj69qai8it	cmnknk44i0001ewhju56drbw5	Lesson 8 — The Story of Re-Creation	READING	2024	11	\N	t	Genesis 1:3 is not the beginning of creation — it's the beginning of restoration. What we call the creation account is actually a re-creation account: six days not of originating matter from nothing, but of rebuilding a ruined world and repopulating it with new life after Lucifer's catastrophic fall.\n\nLast time we saw that angels once governed this earth under Lucifer's rule and that his rebellion brought the first world to ruin. Now we watch God respond — not by abandoning the ruined planet, but by remaking it. This is the story of Genesis 1:3 through 2:25.\n\nThe biblical evidence we covered in Lessons Five and Seven should automatically clear up questions that naturally arise from a wrong understanding of the creation story. Questions about the original creation of the heavens and earth before the flood of Gen. 1:2, the pre-Adamite world, the chaotic period, where demons came from, how old the universe is, where Lucifer's kingdom was located and why he fell, and the cause of sin on earth — all these have been fully answered.\n\nNow we can turn our attention to how and when the present creation was made. The time of re-creation was during the six days of Gen. 1:3–2:25. Let's look at the main points of this remarkable story.\n\n![Lesson 8 — The Story of Re-Creation](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsFiPDwYbM1hRYQ2o4Z38BzgHNSP5KdLckVeFn)\n\n### I. Are the Six Days of Gen. 1 Literal Days?\n\nThe six days of Gen. 1 were literal 24-hour days, just like the days we've known ever since. Scripture makes this very clear. Here's why:\n\n> 1. The word "evening" comes from the Hebrew *ehred*, meaning dusk, evening, or night. It's translated "evening" 49 times and is never used in a figurative sense. The word "morning" comes from the Hebrew *boker*, meaning dawn, break of day, morning, or early light. It's translated "morning" 187 times — again, never figuratively.\n>\n> This shows us that "day" and "night," or "light" and "darkness," are literal periods regulated by the sun, moon, and stars, just as Scripture describes elsewhere (Gen. 8:22; Ps. 19:2; Job 38:12; Jer. 31:35-37; 33:19-26). There's no hint anywhere in Scripture that day and night ever came from a different source, or that we should understand them symbolically.\n\n> 2. It's true that the word "day," used 2,182 times as a literal day, can sometimes refer to a longer period when qualified as "the day of the Lord" or "the day of God." However, when it's used with qualifying words like "evening" and "morning" to mark its beginning and end, it can only be understood literally.\n>\n> This is further proven by the numbering of each day — first, second, third, and so on — just as you'd naturally number literal days. No symbolic period is ever numbered in Scripture.\n\n> 3. Exod. 20:8-11 and 31:14-17 definitely state that God *made* (not created) the heavens (the firmament, not heaven where God dwells) and the earth in six days. Man was told to work the same length of time it took God to do the work of Gen. 1:3–2:25: "Six days shalt thou labour . . . For in six days the Lord made heaven and earth."\n>\n> Think of it like this: it would be just as logical to argue that man was supposed to work 6,000 years or six indefinite periods before resting as it would be to argue that about God's six days of work. The exact same words are used in both passages referring to the same kind of days.\n>\n> Personal interpretation of identical words to prove two different ideas can't be a valid basis for claiming literal days are meant in one case but not the other. No one argues that the six days of Exod. 20 are long periods of time, yet they don't even have the clear qualifying words "evening" and "morning" and "first," "second," "third" that the days of Gen. 1 have.\n>\n> From the standpoint of plain language and common sense, the days of re-creation are just as literal as man's work days. Everyone knows work days for man couldn't be indefinite periods — days in Moses' time were as long as days now, and the same was true of the days of re-creation in Adam's time. Where would anyone get the idea that Genesis days aren't ordinary days? It couldn't come from the plain language of Scripture, and we must reject any other source.\n\n> 4. Remember our fundamental principle of Bible interpretation: take the Bible literally wherever possible. When the language can't be literal or when it states otherwise, then the passage is figurative.\n>\n> On this basis, we have to take the days in Genesis as literal. Couldn't God do this work in six literal days just as easily as in 6,000 years? If He can, and if the Bible says so, then let it stand and don't change it.\n\n> 5. Some might argue that Genesis days couldn't be literal because the sun, moon, and stars hadn't been created yet to regulate day and night. But we've already seen that they were created originally in the beginning when God created the heavens before the earth (Gen. 1:1; Job 38:4-7).\n>\n> If the earth existed before day 1 (as is clear in Gen. 1:2), and if the heavens were created before the earth, then the sun, moon, and stars also existed before day 1. This means the light of the first three days came from the same source it has come from every day since.\n>\n> There had been days and nights throughout Lucifer's reign, just not during the total darkness of chaos while the earth was cursed and the lights were withheld from it (Gen. 1:2; Jer. 4:23-26). The work of day 1 was simply the restoration of day and night as it had been when Lucifer ruled.\n\n> 6. The 1,000-year-day theory is ridiculous when you examine the facts. If this theory were true, it took God a very long time to do the work of these six days, and even longer originally to create all things (as we discussed in Lesson Five, Point VIII).\n>\n> If this theory were true, the waters remained on the earth at least 1,000 years before being divided. The earth was still desolate another 1,000 years before vegetation was planted. And vegetation was on earth 1,000 years before the sun, moon, and stars were created (if, as some suppose, they were created on the fourth day).\n>\n> Here's the problem: How could vegetation live so long without the sun? Furthermore, vegetation would have been here about 2,000 years before animal life, so the earth must have been a dense forest for 2,000 years. Fish and fowls would have been here 1,000 years before man and other land animals — making them rulers of the earth all that time.\n>\n> We'd also have to conclude it took God 1,000 years to create fish and fowls and another 1,000 years to create land animals and man. According to Gen. 2:7-25, man was created before the animals, and the animals were all created before the woman — meaning Adam was created at the beginning of the sixth day and Eve at the end. If this day was 1,000 years long, man was 1,000 years old before a wife was made for him!\n>\n> God rested another 1,000 years between making Eve and man's fall, so there would be about 2,000 years from Adam's creation at the beginning of the sixth 1,000-year period to the fall of man after the seventh 1,000-year period — yet Adam was only 130 years old when Seth was born (Gen. 5:1-3). How foolish human theories look when examined in the light of common sense and Scripture!\n>\n> We conclude, therefore, that the six days of Genesis were literal 24-hour days, as the facts plainly show.\n\n> 7. Some translations read "age" for "day," but that's incorrect. Even if an age were meant, we've seen in Lesson One, Point IV, 1, that an age is any period of time, whether long or short. A literal day is an age — a short one. Since "day" is limited and qualified as literal in Gen. 1:3-31, we're right to believe literal days are meant. This is the only theory that harmonizes with all the facts and scriptures on the subject.\n\n### II. The Work of the First Day—Light Restored (Gen. 1:3-5)\n\nThe work of day one was nothing more or less than the restoration of light and the division of light and darkness — bringing back day and night on earth as they had been when Lucifer ruled, before the curse of total darkness in Gen. 1:2 and Jer. 4:23-26.\n\nThis happened through the brooding of the Spirit of God over the waters covering the earth and by God's direct command: "Let there be [become] light: and there was [became] light" (Gen. 1:3-5).\n\nThe word "let" is used the same way we'd say, "Turn on the light." Both light and darkness already existed — they were created originally with the heavens and earth. The word "let" never denotes creation but rather *permission* (as in Gen. 1:3, 6, 9, 11, 14, 15, 20, 22, 24, 26) or *determination* (as in Gen. 11:3, 4, 7).\n\nThis further indicates that Gen. 1:2 describes an act of judgment, and here God is permitting that judgment to cease, allowing the sun, moon, and stars to shine again on the darkened planet according to their original creative purpose. Neither here nor in Gen. 1:14-19 is an original creative act implied. The sun, moon, and stars were created in the beginning with the heavens — before the earth, as we've seen.\n\nThe light of days 1, 2, and 3 came from the same source it has come from every day since. The work of day 4 is the permanent regulation of the solar system in connection with the restored earth that emerged on day 3. God called the light "day" and the darkness "night" — names for regular periods of light and darkness ever since.\n\nGod began His restoration work on the morning of the first day. When He said, "Let there be light," the first day began. It was day (or light) for a period until evening, when the first period of darkness after restoration began. This continued until the next morning — the second period of light.\n\nThus, the first day and night, the first period of light and darkness since the curse on earth, were divided and distinctly marked off by evening and morning — the first day. It takes evening and morning, a period of light and a period of darkness, to make one day.\n\n### III. The Work of the Second Day—Firmament Restored (Gen. 1:6-8)\n\nThe work of day two was nothing more or less than the restoration of the firmament — the clouds — to hold the waters again that had fallen on the earth to cause the first flood, destroying the first social system (Gen. 1:2).\n\nThese waters had been in the firmament and poured out as rain to water the earth throughout Lucifer's kingdom. When Satan fell, he said, "I will ascend above the heights of the clouds" (Isa. 14:12-14). The clouds were originally created to hold moisture to water the earth (Job 38:4-9, 25-30; Ps. 104:2-3, 13-14).\n\nSo the firmament was created in the beginning along with the heavens and earth, but on day 2 it was restored to its original purpose. This was done by *making*, not creating, the clouds. God put part of the waters back in the clouds and named the firmament "heaven."\n\nThe firmament is called clouds in Scripture (Job 26:8; 38:9; Ps. 77:17; Prov. 8:28). Heaven as a planet and the heavens as clouds are distinguished (Judg. 5:4; Ps. 147:8; Isa. 14:12-14; Dan. 7:13; Mt. 24:29-31).\n\nThe second day's work began on the morning of the second day (the second period of light), continued to the second period of darkness (night), and went through the night until the third morning (the third period of light). Thus, the evening ending the second period of light and the morning ending the second period of darkness were the second day.\n\n### IV. The Work of the Third Day—Earth and Vegetation Restored (Gen. 1:9-13)\n\nThe work of day three was nothing more or less than the restoration of the earth from its water baptism (which had lasted throughout chaos and through the first two days) and the restoration of vegetation that had grown on the earth when Lucifer ruled before Gen. 1:2.\n\nAs we saw in Lesson Seven, Point VI, there were fruitful places on the earth, but they had become a waste because of judgment when Lucifer rebelled. This work was accomplished by God's direct command and the creative power of the Holy Spirit.\n\nAt God's rebuke, the waters that hadn't been put in the clouds on day 2 fled and hastened away into the low places of the earth. God then set bounds around the waters to keep them from covering the earth (Ps. 104:5-9).\n\nGod called the dry land "earth." If dry land is earth, then we can read Gen. 1:1 as: "In the beginning God created the heaven, and the dry land." The dry land had become wet land by the flood of Gen. 1:2, and now dry land was being restored for the habitation of land animals and man.\n\nNeither the waters nor the earth were created on day three any more than the planets were created on day four, or the light and darkness and firmament on days one and two. All the heavens and earth were created in the beginning before Lucifer ruled. All the work of day 3 is *re-constructive*, not creative.\n\nWhen dry land appeared, vegetation could be planted and grow, since the sun was already shining — it had been for the first two days, as well as this day and all days since.\n\nThe purpose of vegetation was to sustain life on the restored earth. In all likelihood, the life germ in seeds was destroyed during the chaotic period when the earth was waterlogged for an indefinite time — no doubt longer than Noah's flood, which didn't destroy vegetation.\n\nGen. 2:5 plainly states that all vegetation on the restored earth was absolutely new: "And every plant of the field before it was in the earth, and every herb of the field before it grew." This proves all vegetation was a new work.\n\nGod began the work on the morning of day three (when the second period of darkness ended) and worked throughout the third day (period of light) until evening (the third period of darkness). He worked through the night until the morning of day four. Thus, the evening ending the third period of light and the morning ending the third period of darkness were the third day.\n\n### V. The Work of the Fourth Day—Solar Regulation Restored (Gen. 1:14-19)\n\nThe work of day four was nothing more or less than the restoration of the solar system in connection with the restored earth, which work had been completed the day before.\n\nPermanent regulation of the solar system to give light on earth and regulate times and seasons couldn't be done until the earth was restored. In this passage we learn where the light of the first three days came from and how light and darkness were divided and ruled on those days and all days since. Here God fixed the solar system in connection with the earth as it was before chaos.\n\nFrom this day on, the sun, moon, and stars were commanded to govern seasons on the newly restored earth. These lights had given light on the earth and regulated times and seasons throughout Lucifer's rule, but in the curse on the first social system they had been withheld from shining on the cursed earth (Gen. 1:2; Jer. 4:23-26). Here God commanded them to renew their original creative purpose — to sustain life on earth and regulate times, seasons, day, and night forever.\n\nSome translations read, "God *had* made two great luminaries . . . and God *had* fixed them," proving God had done this work of actually creating them in the past. When? In the beginning, before Lucifer ruled the earth and when it was first created.\n\nGod began this work on the morning of day four (period of light) and worked until evening (the fourth period of darkness). He then worked all night until the morning of day five. Thus, the evening ending the fourth period of light and the morning ending the fourth period of darkness were the fourth day.\n\n### VI. The Work of the Fifth Day—Fish and Fowl Restored (Gen. 1:20-23)\n\nThe work of day five was nothing more or less than the creation and formation of new sea animals and fowl to fly in the clouds. Here we have the second creative act of God mentioned in the Creative Ages — the first being the original creation of the heavens, earth, and all things in the beginning (Gen. 1:1).\n\nOn day 5, God creates and makes fish and fowl. Between the two creations (the dateless past and day five), God merely restores day and night, firmament, earth and vegetation, and solar regulation. The new vegetation of day three is also a creation of God, but all the rest is merely restoring already-created things as they were before in Lucifer's kingdom.\n\nGod first fixed the realms where fish and fowl were to live, then created and made them to reproduce their own kind and live according to certain laws. The bodies of all fish and fowl were formed out of the dust of the ground, and life was created in them (Gen. 2:19).\n\nThe Hebrew word for "bring forth" is *shawrats*, meaning to wriggle, swarm, abound, breed, increase, and move. Its meaning is seen in Gen. 1:20; 9:7; Exod. 8:3.\n\nThings of the animal and plant worlds multiply abundantly. Think of it like this: under the present curse, a watermelon seed reproduces a product 200,000 times its own weight, and each melon produces hundreds of seeds, each capable of producing such a product! Each grain reproduces many of its own kind. Each fruit tree produces hundreds of seed-bearing fruits, each capable of producing another tree with thousands more.\n\nLoggerhead turtles lay 1,000 eggs at a time, and a cod fish produces 10 million eggs annually. Other organisms multiply abundantly, each after its own kind as God commanded. There's an abundant supply of anything man wants — all he has to do is follow certain laws, and all things are his.\n\nThe word for "life" is *nephesh*, meaning soul or feelings, emotions, appetites, and desires, as we saw in Lesson Six, Point IX, 2, (1). All animals have souls (feelings and appetites), but their souls are not immortal and created in the likeness of God's soul, as is the soul of man.\n\nEvery creature was to bring forth "after his kind" — this expression states the law of reproduction for all things. It occurs ten times in Gen. 1:11, 12, 21, 24-25. The same law was still in force 1,656 years later after the flood (Gen. 8:19). It's still in force today, and different species cannot be crossed to reproduce other than their own kind, as is well known. Man and monkey and other animals are so far apart that they never were related.\n\nGod began this work on the morning of day five (period of light) and worked all day until evening (the fifth period of darkness). He then worked all night until the sixth period of light. Thus, the evening ending the fifth period of light and the morning ending the fifth period of darkness were the fifth day.\n\n### VII. The Work of the Sixth Day—Land Animals and Man Restored (Gen. 1:24-31)\n\nThe work of day six was nothing more or less than the creation and formation of new land animals and man to take the place of the animals and inhabitants of the first social system over which Lucifer ruled, the naming of all things by Adam, and the giving of commands by God to the new creation. The bodies of man and all animals were formed out of the dust, and life was created (Gen. 2:7, 19).\n\nThe phrase "Let us" states the divine purpose, but the divine act isn't described until Gen. 2:5-25. In other words, Gen. 1 states *what* God did and some things about *how* He created and made all new things, while Gen. 2 goes into more detail about *how* He formed and created man and animals and planted a garden. Gen. 2 explains more fully the work of days 3, 5, and 6.\n\nThe image and likeness of God referred to in Gen. 1:26 ("Let us make man in our image and likeness") was already discussed in Lesson Four, Point II, 2-3.\n\nGod began His work on day six in the morning (sixth period of light) and worked through the day to evening (sixth period of darkness). He worked through the night until the seventh morning when He ended His work. Thus, the evening ending the sixth period of light and the morning ending the sixth period of darkness were the sixth day.\n\n### VIII. The Seventh Day of Rest (Gen. 2:1-4)\n\n**(End of the Creative Ages—Beginning of the Seven Dispensations for Men)**\n\nThe seventh day was one of rest for God — not that He needed rest, but because His work of restoring the earth and its inhabitants was finished. He had worked constantly six days and six nights and was now done.\n\n"Thus the heavens and the earth were finished, and all the host of them [all the inhabitants and creatures of all kinds in the heavens and the earth]. And on the seventh day God ended his work . . . which God created and made. These are the generations [family history or productions] of the heavens and of the earth when they were created, in the day [period] that the Lord God made the earth and the heavens" (Gen. 2:1-4).\n\nThe order of all the Creative Ages (as discussed in Lesson One, Point IV, 1, (4)) is as follows:\n\n> 1. The original creation and perfection of the heavens and the Earth and all things therein as when Lucifer ruled before the six days (Gen. 1:1).\n\n> 2. The Earth part of the creation made chaos and imperfect and all life destroyed in the Earth, because of Lucifer's rebellion (Gen. 1:2).\n\n> 3. The restoration of the Earth to perfection and the creation of new life to take the place of that which was destroyed (Gen. 1:3–2:25).\n\n### IX. Why the Earth Was Restored to a Habitable State\n\nThe earth was restored because God had originally intended it to be inhabited: "For thus saith the Lord that created the heavens; God himself that formed the earth and made it; he hath established it, he created it not in vain [Hebrew, *tohu*, a waste or desolation — so if it was desolate in Gen. 1:2, it later became that way], he formed it to be inhabited" (Isa. 45:18).\n\nThe fall of Lucifer and the total rebellion of all inhabitants of the first social system under Satan didn't discourage God or cause Him to blot out the earth. He had started with a purpose — that the earth should be inhabited with free moral agents to whom He could reveal Himself and show the riches of His grace, and who would serve Him by free choice. He continued that original purpose by making a new creation when the old one had to be destroyed.\n\nThe rebellion of the new creation made in the six days didn't discourage God or cause Him to want to blot it out and start over. He had purposed that as truly as He lived, "the earth shall be full of the glory of the Lord" (Num. 14:21), and this purpose will yet be realized in the New Heavens and New Earth of the future.\n\nGod didn't create the earth to turn it over to rebels. He will yet see to it that only the meek and righteous inherit the earth (Mt. 5:5; Ps. 37:9-11, 29). So God restored the earth from chaos and ruin to replenish it with free moral agents, ensuring His original purpose will finally be realized. (See Reason for God's Dispensational Dealings, Lesson One, Point VIII.)\n\n### X. God's Plan for the New Social System on the Earth\n\nGod's plan for the new social system was the same as for the first — that all free wills consecrate themselves to the highest good of being and of the universe.\n\nThis means free moral agents must consecrate themselves to the same end God is consecrated to. They must submit wholeheartedly to what's best for all society. They must recognize God as the Supreme Moral Governor of the universe. Every thought, word, and deed should be for the betterment of society, including their own good. They must live dependent upon God for needed grace for body, soul, and spirit, and appreciate life and all it holds.\n\nGod planned to make the new creation an example to all angelic powers of His manifold wisdom concerning His eternal plan (Eph. 3:10-11; 1 Cor. 4:9). He planned to manifest His grace and goodness to man and make him ruler of all the earth, including the sun, moon, and stars (Ps. 8:3-7).\n\nHe planned that man should be faithful to his responsibility if he so desired and be greatly rewarded, continuing to rule over all. If man failed, he would be punished according to the law. God also planned redemption for man should he fall, as we saw in Lesson Seven, Points VII, IX and X, and as we'll see more fully in future lessons.\n\n---\n\n## Earth's Second Sinless Career (Gen. 2:15-25)\n\n### ADAM THE NEW RULER OF THE EARTH\n\nGod created Adam on day six of Gen. 1 to take Lucifer's place as earth's ruler. He was the earth's second worldwide dictator and could have remained so if he hadn't sinned.\n\nLucifer, the first worldwide dictator, had sinned and failed by not becoming reconciled to God. Adam also failed, and it's uncertain whether he became reconciled to God. Looking at the biblical record, it seems he never did.\n\nAdam isn't mentioned in the list of faith heroes in Heb. 11. He's not mentioned once as a righteous man in either Testament — which is striking when you consider others are mentioned several times. From the Antediluvian period, only Abel, Enoch, and Noah are mentioned as righteous ones. We know from Gen. 6:3 that Adam wasn't reconciled to God when he was 810 years old, as we'll see in Lesson Eleven.\n\nJesus Christ will be the third and final worldwide dictator, and He will eternally prove true to God and head God's government forever, as we'll see in later lessons.\n\nAdam had the greatest responsibility of any man who has ever lived, besides Christ. He was given dominion over all creation to rule for God and be subject to God forever. He was charged to keep out all enemies and resist all claims of spirit-beings concerning dominion of the earth.\n\nGod knew Lucifer and the fallen spirits were still around and would contest man's claim of dominion. God permitted this to test the new free moral governor of the earth, as we saw in Lesson Six, Point X, 9.\n\nAdam's responsibility included bringing his own kind into the world and training them to respect God, continue in righteousness and true holiness, reject all temptation, and overcome all enemies.\n\nThe charge to Adam and Eve is stated in Gen. 1:26-29 and 2:15-17:\n\n"And God said, Let us make man in our image, after our likeness: and let them have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over the cattle, and over all the earth, and over every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth. So God created man in his own image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them. And God blessed them, and God said unto them, Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth, and subdue it: and have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over every living thing that moveth upon the earth. And God said, Behold, I have given you every herb [grain bearing plant and vegetation] . . . and every tree, in the which is the fruit of a tree yielding seed; to you it shall be for meat . . . And the Lord God took the man, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it [protect, preserve it, as in Gen. 3:24; 17:9-10; 18:19]. And the Lord God commanded the man, saying, Of every tree of the garden thou mayest freely eat: But of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, thou shalt not eat of it: for in the day that thou eatest thereof thou shalt surely die."\n\nIn Ps. 8:3-9 we read that man was to have dominion over "thy heavens, the work of thy fingers, the moon, and the stars, which thou hast ordained . . . For thou hast made him a little lower than the angels, and hast crowned him with glory and honour. Thou madest him to have dominion over the works of thy hands; thou hast put all things under his feet."\n\nFrom these and other passages, we learn God's plan was for man to have dominion over everything. What a tremendous responsibility! What an incredible position!\n\nMan was fully capable of ruling over all things, possessing super-intelligence and the ability to name everything in creation. It's similar to how a brilliant CEO might be given complete authority over a vast corporation — except Adam's "corporation" was the entire earth and potentially the planets beyond! He was likely meant to have access to the planets and rule them for God, but he sinned and came "short of the glory of God" (Rom. 3:23).\n\nIn the final restitution of all things, man will again have dominion and help God administer the affairs of the universe (Rev. 1:5-6; 2:26-29; 3:21; 5:8-10; 22:4-5; 1 Cor. 6:2-3; 2 Tim. 2:12). This future dominion includes more than planet Earth, as Rom. 8:17-18 makes clear: "and if children, then heirs, heirs of God, and joint-heirs with Christ." Everything God owns will become the inheritance of the saints, and they shall reign forever and ever (Rev. 1:5-6; 2:27; 5:9-10; 22:4-5; Dan. 7:13-14, 18, 27).\n\nIf people would only realize the future that could be theirs by simply submitting to God and laying down their arms of rebellion, there would be few, if any, who wouldn't wholeheartedly surrender to God and conform to His eternal will.\n\nBut the devil keeps man occupied with trifling and temporary things, making him think there may not be a future. This causes man to neglect God and life's essentials, cutting him off from his rightful inheritance in Christ. If someone chooses to have nothing to do with God and His plan, then God has planned to separate that person from society and carry on His eternal purpose with those who will choose to be part of the plan.\n\n---\n\n## Questions on Lesson Eight\n\n- What is the subject of Lesson Eight?\n\n- When was the time of the re-creation of the Earth and all things therein?\n\n- Prove fully from Scripture that the six days were literal days and not periods of 1,000 or more years each.\n\n- Prove from the standpoint of common sense and reason that they were literal days.\n\n- Prove from the Scripture that the heavens were created before the Earth.\n\n- How does this prove that the light of the first three days came from the planets?\n\n- How does this prove that there was chaos on Earth in Gen. 1:2?\n\n- Explain fully the work of the first day.\n\n- Does day 1 include the creation of the heavens, the Earth, the darkness, and the waters that covered the Earth? Why?\n\n- When did God begin His work? Did He begin it in total darkness or in light?\n\n- When did day and night begin in the restored creation?\n\n- Explain the word "let." How does it indicate that the sun was in existence?\n\n- Prove from Scripture that there will be day and night forever.\n\n- Explain fully the work of the second day.\n\n- Had there been a firmament before this time? Prove.\n\n- Is Heaven as a planet and the heavens as clouds distinguished in Scripture?\n\n- Explain fully the work of the third day.\n\n- Was the Earth originally created on day 3 or merely restored?\n\n- Prove from Scripture that there had been vegetation on Earth before this.\n\n- What is the name for dry land? When did dry land become flooded? Why?\n\n- Did God originally create the Earth dry? Prove.\n\n- What was the purpose of God in planting vegetation on Earth again?\n\n- Prove from Scripture that no vegetation remained from the pre-Adamite period.\n\n- Explain fully the work of the fourth day.\n\n- Did God create the sun, moon, and stars in day 4 or merely regulate them?\n\n- Did the planets regulate times and seasons on Earth before Adam?\n\n- Explain fully the work of the fifth day.\n\n- Did God make a place for each and every creature before creating them?\n\n- How fast do some creatures multiply?\n\n- What is the law of reproduction given by God? Is it still in force?\n\n- Explain fully the work of the sixth day.\n\n- Why did God create land animals, fish, fowls, and man?\n\n- Were there two creations of man—one in Gen. 1 and another in Gen. 2?\n\n- What is the purpose of the two records of man's creation?\n\n- When did the Creative Ages end?\n\n- When did the seven dispensations for man begin?\n\n- What happened on day 7? Did God have to rest because He was tired?\n\n- Give the three main points on the Creative Ages.\n\n- Why was the Earth restored to a habitable state?\n\n- What was God\n\n---\n\nThe re-creation account isn't just the story of how the world began — it's a picture of how God works with ruins. He doesn't abandon what has been destroyed by rebellion. He rebuilds it, repopulates it, and commissions it again. So here's the question worth sitting with: Is there an area of your life — a relationship, a calling, a season of faith — that you've written off as permanently destroyed? And what does the God of Genesis 1:3 have to say about that?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgbc001510b8xj11lc8o	cmq76cgb9001110b8mkvodphm	Lesson 17 — The Armor of God and the Name of Jesus	READING	900	1	\N	t	![Lesson 17 — The Armor of God and the Name of Jesus](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsA08qqkG5PN9xaTQskDwozfES60B3MbGnd7mC)\n\n## The Armor of God and the Name of Jesus\n\nPaul concludes his teaching on spiritual warfare with a command to put on the whole armor of God. This is not optional equipment for super-saints; it is the standard issue for every believer who expects to stand in the day of battle.\n\n> Ephesians 6:11-12 — "Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil. For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world."\n\n### The Belt of Truth\n\nTruth is the foundation. Satan is a liar; truth exposes his deception. The Christian who lives in honesty, integrity, and the truth of God's Word has already secured the center of the battle.\n\n### The Breastplate of Righteousness\n\nThe breastplate protects the heart. When a believer walks in righteousness — not perfect sinlessness, but a life oriented toward God and away from sin — the enemy cannot penetrate the core of their being with guilt, shame, or accusation.\n\n### The Shoes of the Gospel of Peace\n\nThe believer stands firm because their standing with God is secure. The gospel of peace means we are no longer enemies of God but at peace with Him through Christ. This peace allows us to stand unshaken even when everything around us shakes.\n\n### The Shield of Faith\n\nFaith extinguishes the fiery darts of the wicked one. Every doubt, every fear, every accusation is a flaming arrow aimed at the believer's confidence. Faith — active, trusting, obedient faith — deflects them all.\n\n### The Helmet of Salvation\n\nThe helmet protects the mind. The believer must know they are saved, sealed, and secure. Satan's primary attack is often on the assurance of salvation: "Are you really saved? Will God really keep you?" The helmet answers: Yes, by grace, through faith, in Christ.\n\n### The Sword of the Spirit\n\nThe Word of God is the only offensive weapon. Jesus wielded it in the wilderness. The believer must know it, speak it, and trust it. The sword is not for show; it is for battle.\n\n### The Name of Jesus — The Secret Weapon\n\nThe armor enables us to stand; the Name of Jesus enables us to advance. Every demon must bow at the Name of Jesus (Philippians 2:10). When a believer commands a demon to leave in that Name, they are not making a request — they are executing a judgment already rendered at the cross.	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk44j0003ewhjd74baz5x	cmnknk44i0001ewhju56drbw5	Lesson 1 — God's Universal Plan for Creation	READING	2494	1	\N	t	![Lesson 1 — God's Universal Plan for Creation](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os80GxeEwQn65F0NSyXfv2WGAqVjL7icrDpPIo)\n\n# LESSON ONE\n\n## 1. General Subjects Concerning God's Plan for Man\n\nMost people who've sat in church for years still can't answer a simple question: Why does the Bible seem to contradict itself? Why does one passage say the law is holy and good, while another says you're no longer under the law? Why does one promise belonging to Israel get claimed by a modern Christian — and another gets ignored entirely? These aren't contradictions. They're what happens when you're reading a filing system without knowing how it's organized. That's what this course exists to fix.\n\nThese fifty-two lessons are divided into four main parts:\n\n> PART I The Origin of All Things, Lessons 1–8\n\n> PART II God's Historical Dealings with Man, Lessons 9–18\n\n> PART III God's Present Dealings with Man, Lessons 19–36\n\n> PART IV God's Future Dealings with Man, Lessons 37–52\n\n### I. Importance of the Study of "God's Plan for Man"\n\nIf you want to truly know the Bible and be saved for eternity, this study is the most important subject you'll ever encounter. Think of it as the backbone of the entire Bible — it covers every age, every dispensation, and every major biblical subject from eternity past to eternity future.\n\nHere's the key: once you learn to distinguish the ages and dispensations, the whole Bible will start to harmonize beautifully. The main reason so many people feel confused about Scripture is simply that they don't understand God's plan for humanity.\n\nIf you'll take the time to get a working knowledge of this blueprint, you'll find the Bible isn't nearly as difficult as you might have thought. We really can't overstate how important these lessons are — they're built on a correct understanding of Scripture itself.\n\nHere's what we recommend: memorize the name of each age and dispensation, and pay careful attention to where each one fits in God's overall plan. That way, you'll have a mental picture of exactly which time period each lesson addresses and where various scriptures apply.\n\nKeep the key features of each age in mind as we move from lesson to lesson. As you do, God's ultimate purpose for humanity will begin to dawn on you in a fresh, powerful way.\n\nIf you want a clear, balanced, and harmonious understanding of Scripture, get to know God's plan of the ages inside and out. Understand how the history of the past connects to the present, and grasp the prophecies about the future. Then — and only then — can you truly be "a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth" (2 Tim. 2:15).\n\nPaul's instruction to "rightly divide" is more significant than it first sounds. The Greek word for "dividing" is *orthotomeo* — literally, to cut straight, like a road-builder carving a path through rough terrain. A road-builder who wanders isn't just inefficient; he gets lost. Paul is saying that a Bible student who doesn't know which time period and which people a given passage addresses isn't just confused — he's spiritually disoriented inside his own interpretation.\n\nAlong with this big-picture knowledge, you'll learn how to apply Scripture to your daily life. You'll discover how to receive healing, health, prosperity, and happiness — right here and now. After all, isn't that what you need most at this moment? You won't just gain knowledge about God; you'll learn how to experience the full blessings of life by putting that knowledge to work.\n\n### II. The Simplicity of the Plan of God for Man\n\nMost people assume the Bible is impossibly complex — and you can't entirely blame them. Centuries of academic debate, theological jargon, and contradictory denominational teaching have convinced millions that understanding Scripture requires a seminary degree. But notice something Jesus never said: He never once told His disciples they needed more education to understand truth. He told them they needed more faith. The difficulty with the Bible isn't intellectual — it's volitional.\n\nHere's some good news: the Bible — God's plan in Scripture — is actually very simple to understand. No one has any real excuse for misunderstanding it.\n\nJesus constantly invited and even challenged people to study Scripture. He rebuked those who lacked knowledge of revealed truth. He pointed to ignorance of the Bible as the root cause of every error. When critics questioned Him, He answered, "Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of God" (Mt. 22:29). Notice the charge — not "you lack the right credentials," but "you don't know the scriptures." He commanded people to "search the scriptures: for in them ye think ye have eternal life: and they are they which testify of me" (Jn. 5:39).\n\nEven after more than three years of the simplest teaching by the greatest teacher who ever lived, the disciples had to be corrected. Jesus said, "O fools, and slow of heart to believe all that the prophets have spoken" (Lk. 24:25-27). Notice — this wasn't because they couldn't understand. It was because they didn't believe what Christ said.\n\nEven after Jesus rose from the dead and appeared to them in various ways, they still struggled to believe until He "upbraided them for their unbelief and hardness of heart" (Mk. 16:13-14). His words were always simple enough to grasp — but believing them was another matter entirely.\n\nYou might find the same thing true for yourself. At first, it may be hard to accept that the benefits we're promising you from Scripture are really true — and really for you. But we're going to prove every one of them from the plain words of the Bible. Start believing those promises of abundant life right now, and begin to expect these blessings for yourself.\n\nPaul taught the same principle — that simply hearing God's Word is enough to produce faith. He wrote, "How then shall they call on him in whom they have not believed? and how shall they believe in him of whom they have not heard? and how shall they hear without a preacher? . . . So then faith cometh by hearing and hearing by the word of God" (Rom. 10:14-17). The chain is beautifully simple: Word heard → faith produced → call made → salvation received. Not a chain that requires a scholar at every link — just a person willing to hear and believe.\n\nNearly ninety times in the New Testament alone, we're pointed back to what "is written" — as if everything is simple enough to understand for anyone who genuinely wants to understand and believe. In fact, nowhere in either Testament does any speaker or writer suggest that God's words are hard to understand — if people would simply believe them.\n\nThe only hint of confusion comes from those who didn't want to believe and obey. Jesus taught that the difficulty comes from human willfulness — some people simply don't want to understand. But those who do want to understand can, without exception (Mt. 13:9-17).\n\nPeter mentions "the unlearned and unstable" who twist the Scriptures to their own destruction (2 Pet. 3:16-18). But you don't have to be in that group — not if you make up your mind to believe and obey what's written, instead of rebelling against it.\n\nPride, stubbornness, and rebellion against what "is written" — these are what make the Bible hard to understand. The challenge isn't grasping the truth with your mind; it's being willing to obey what you'd rather not obey. Think of it like this: if you truly couldn't understand something, you wouldn't be able to reject it either. You can't rebel against what you genuinely cannot comprehend.\n\nThere's no excuse for misunderstanding God's Word if you'll approach it like a child — accepting the Bible for what it says and honestly committing yourself to obey it. You must accept the Bible as God's Word. You must believe that God couldn't be honest if He tried to hide the very truths He'll judge you by in the end.\n\nAccept the Bible as the final authority on its own subjects, and set aside human interpretations and distortions. Believe that God knows what He's talking about. Trust that He knows how to express Himself in human language. Accept that He said what He meant and meant what He said — and that what He says on any subject matters more than what any person says about it.\n\nYou don't have to look up every scripture reference in these lessons to get the truth. The references are provided as proof that what we're teaching is biblical, and for those who want to investigate for themselves. Looking up all the references would certainly enrich your life and bring great blessing. But since we'll state exactly what the references say, you can still grasp the truth even if you don't have time to check every citation.\n\nThat said, if you have any doubts that we're teaching sound doctrine, look up the references and see exactly what the Bible says — and believe it over any human teacher. You can't go wrong with that approach. Just make sure you stick to what's actually written, and don't let preconceived ideas make you biased. Don't try to force the Bible to match your ideas — always adjust your ideas to match the Bible.\n\nRead the plain language of Scripture and understand it the same literal way you'd understand similar statements in any other book.\n\nIn Lesson Three, we'll show you how to understand the Bible in more detail. For now, follow these simple principles. Accept that the Bible is straightforward and that God's plan for humanity is clear. Nothing will be hard to understand as we continue our study.\n\nDon't defeat yourself before you start by thinking the Bible is impossibly hard. Let go of that idea right now! We'll show you just how simple it really is. You'll be amazed at its simplicity, lesson after lesson. So-called "mysteries" that have puzzled the wise of this world are revealed to those with childlike hearts.\n\nJesus once said, "I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes. Even so, Father: for so it seemed good in thy sight" (Mt. 11:25-26). The word "babes" here isn't an insult — it's a description of posture. A babe receives. A babe doesn't argue. A babe doesn't demand that the gift conform to its expectations before accepting it. That's the posture God blesses with understanding.\n\nSo your attitude matters tremendously. Be simple and humble. Take the place of a learner and accept at face value everything God says, whether or not it fits with your theories or what you've been taught before.\n\nIf you truly want truth as it is in the Bible, you've come to the right place. We promise and guarantee that we won't twist any part of the Bible to fit our ideas or anyone else's. We'll give you chapter and verse for everything we say about God's plan for humanity.\n\nLet's move forward with an open Bible, an open heart, and an open mind. Let's be honest enough to set aside old theories for the plain, literal, simple Word of God on every topic we discuss.\n\n### III. Definition of the Terms and Expressions of the Ages\n\nBefore you can "rightly divide the word of truth" (2 Tim. 2:15), there are some words and expressions you need to understand. Knowing these terms and how Scripture uses them is essential for grasping God's Word correctly.\n\nHere are the key terms we want you to become familiar with. Come back to this section often as you study future lessons.\n\n**1. AGE.** The Greek word *aion* means an age or period of time, whether long or short. In this sense, there are countless ages:\n\n> (1) PAST AGES. Paul said of the revelation of the Church's mystery "which in other ages was not made known unto the sons of men, as it is now revealed unto his holy apostles and prophets by the Spirit" (Eph. 3:5-6; Col. 1:26). Paul also said that God, through Christ, planned the ages — "made the worlds" (Greek: *ages*, Heb. 1:1-3; 11:3).\n\n*See also: Lk. 1:70; Jn. 9:32; Acts 3:21; 15:18; 1 Cor. 2:7.*\n\n> (2) PRESENT AGE. This Age of Grace, between the first and second comings of Jesus Christ, is referred to many times in Scripture as "this world" (Greek: *age*, Mt. 13:22); "end of this world" (*age*, Mt. 13:39-40); "present evil world" (*age*, Gal. 1:4; 2 Tim. 4:10; Titus 2:12).\n\n*See also: Mk. 4:19; Lk. 16:8; 20:34; Rom. 12:2; 1 Cor. 1:20; Mt. 13:49; 24:3; 28:20.*\n\nIn another sense, "present age" refers to the period from Noah's flood to the Millennium, as we'll see in Lesson Thirteen and point (5), note c.\n\n> (3) FUTURE AGES. One particular age — the Millennium — follows "this age" and is called "the world [*age*] to come" (Mt. 12:31-32; Mk. 10:30; Eph. 1:21; Heb. 6:5) and "that world" (*age*, Lk. 20:35). After the Millennium, there will be ages following ages like links in a continuous chain. Paul speaks of the "ages to come" in which God will forever show "the exceeding riches of his grace in his kindness toward us through Christ Jesus" (Eph. 2:7).\n\n*See also: Eph. 3:21; 1 Tim. 1:17.*\n\n> (4) THE CREATIVE AGES (Gen. 1:1–2:25). By this we mean the ages in the dateless past when God created the universe and everything in it — called in Gen. 2:4 "the generations of the heavens and of the earth." During these creative ages, God brought into existence the vast heavens, including the sun, moon, stars, and planets, as well as innumerable things in the three heavens and the earth mentioned in Scripture (2 Cor. 12:2; Col. 1:15-18; Rom. 1:20). God also created various kinds of spirit and human beings to inhabit the planets, planning to reveal Himself to them and show the riches of His glory and kindness forever. In Lessons Five through Eight, we'll explore the most wonderful creation story ever told, straight from Scripture.\n\n> (5) THE FIVE MAIN AGES. There are five main ages connected with God's dealings with free moral agents:\n\n> A. THE ANTECHAOTIC AGE — from the original creation to chaos; from the beginning of the heavens and earth in Gen. 1:1 to the chaotic state in Gen. 1:2. During this period, Lucifer ruled the earth but fell through pride and caused the earth to be cursed, as we'll see in Lesson Seven.\n\n> B. THE ANTEDILUVIAN AGE — from the six days of the re-creation (Gen. 1:3–2:25) to Noah's flood; or from Lucifer's flood (Gen. 1:2) to Noah's flood (Gen. 6–8).\n\n> C. THE PRESENT AGE — from Noah's flood (Gen. 6–8) to the Millennium, which follows Christ's second coming and the Battle of Armageddon (Rev. 19:11–20:7).\n\n> D. THE AGE TO COME — the Millennium, from Christ's second coming and the Battle of Armageddon (Rev. 19:11-21) to the New Heavens and New Earth (Rev. 21–22).\n\n> E. THE AGE OF THE AGES — eternity, time without end. In Lessons Forty-nine through Fifty-two, we'll study the future and eternal conditions on earth and in the heavens in amazing detail — truths most church members have seldom, if ever, heard. Studying these truths will make you rich in knowledge and give you a concrete understanding of the eternal future.\n\n**2. WORLD.** There are ten Hebrew and Greek words translated by our single English word "world." Each has a different shade of meaning, and failing to understand which original word is used can lead to serious misunderstanding.\n\nMost people assume "world" just means "world" — the planet, human society, or maybe just everywhere. But in Scripture, the same English word can carry entirely different meanings depending on which original term was used. The context and subject matter will help you determine the true meaning.\n\nHere are the important ones:\n\n> (1) The Hebrew word *olam* means unknown time, time out of mind, eternity, always, everlasting, and perpetual. This word should never have been translated "world" — it always relates to time. For example, in Ps. 73:12, it should read "continually" instead of "in the world." In Isa. 45:17; 64:4 it should read "eternal" instead of "world without end."\n\n> (2) The Greek word *aion* means a period of time, whether long or short. It should always be translated "age," never "world," as we've already seen. Sometimes it's translated "eternal," "forever," or "for ever and ever" — and those are correct, since *aion* can mean a long or eternal period as well as a short one.\n\n> (3) The Greek word *oikoumene* means the inhabited earth, or the world of people. Sometimes it refers only to part of the inhabited earth, such as the Roman Empire (Lk. 2:1; Acts 11:28).\n\n> (4) The Greek word *kosmos* means order, regularity, arrangement, ornament, and social system. It's always translated "world," except in 1 Pet. 3:3 where it's translated "adorning." The true meaning is the social system or order on the earth. When Peter said "the world that then was, being overflowed with water perished," we should understand that only the social order on earth perished — not the ground itself (2 Pet. 3:5-7).\n\n> (5) The Greek word *aionios* means unknown time, time out of mind, eternity, always, perpetual, and forever. It corresponds to the Hebrew *olam*. The three places where it's translated "the world began" should really read "time without defined limits as to beginning or end" (Rom. 16:25; 2 Tim. 1:9; Titus 1:2).\n\nWherever *olam*, *aion*, or *aionios* are used in connection with God's plan, God Himself, eternal life, eternal punishment, or other eternal things, they literally mean everlasting, eternal, and perpetual — as we'll see in our future studies.\n\n**3. TIMES AND SEASONS.** There are twenty-eight Greek words translated "time" or "times," and eight translated "season" or "seasons." Each has a different shade of meaning, but only two need to be listed here:\n\n> (1) CHRONOS — time unlimited, unless specifically defined (Mt. 2:7, 16; Acts 1:6-7; 3:21; Gal. 4:4; 1 Thess. 5:1; 1 Pet. 1:17, 20; Rev. 10:6).\n\n> (2) KAIROS — a certain limited or definite portion of chronos, or time (Mt. 8:29; 11:25; 12:1; 13:30; Acts 3:19; Eph. 1:10; Rev. 12:12, 14).\n\nGod has spoken "at sundry times and in divers manners" about certain times and seasons in history (Heb. 1:1). To rightly divide the Word of Truth, you must understand the times when the different books of the Bible were written and the times to which they apply. There's a time and season for everything under the sun (Eccl. 3).\n\nBeyond natural times and seasons, there are also specific times and seasons for preordained events in God's eternal plan. The children of Issachar "had understanding of the times, to know what Israel ought to do" (1 Chr. 12:32). The wise men knew by a star when Christ was born and pursued Him across countries because they understood the season they were living in (Mt. 2:1-10).\n\nJesus understood the signs of His time and rebuked the Pharisees for not discerning them as clearly as they could read the weather. He said, "O ye hypocrites, ye can discern the face of the sky; but can ye not discern the signs of the times?" (Mt. 16:1-3).\n\nAfter Jesus' resurrection, the disciples asked, "Lord, wilt thou at this time restore again the kingdom to Israel?" He replied, "It is not for you to know the times or the seasons, which the Father hath put in his own power" (Acts 1:6-7). Even Satan and demons know the time of their coming doom (Mt. 8:29; Rev. 12:12).\n\nNevertheless, there are certain times and seasons we can know about the prophetic events of the last days (1 Thess. 5:1-9). What we can and should know of God's plan is what He has plainly revealed in Scripture. As Moses said, "The secret things belong unto the Lord our God: but those things which are revealed belong unto us and to our children for ever" (Deut. 29:29).\n\n**4. THE ETERNAL PAST.** By this we mean the dateless past before time as we know it — before the six days of Gen. 1:3–2:25.\n\n**5. THE ETERNAL FUTURE.** By this we mean the eternal continuation of time after the Millennium, when God will be all-in-all as He was before rebellion started in the universe through Lucifer and Adam.\n\n**6. THE TIMES OF THE GENTILES.** This refers to the dispensation or administration when Gentiles served as the rod of chastening upon Israel and to further God's purpose concerning them. It began with Israel's oppression in Egypt and continues until Christ's second coming, as we'll see in Lesson Fifteen.\n\n**7. DISPENSATION.** The Greek word *oikonomia* means an administration, a stewardship of a household or estate, a dispensation — you could call it a guardianship. In 1 Cor. 9:17; Eph. 3:2; Col. 1:25, Paul speaks of his responsibility in preaching the gospel as a "dispensation of the gospel" and "the dispensation of the grace of God." The Millennium is called "the dispensation of the fullness of times," when God will gather all things in Christ and put all enemies under His feet (1 Cor. 15:24-28; Eph. 1:10).\n\nThe word "dispensation" comes from two Greek words: *oikos* (house) and *nomos* (law). Applied to the various ages, it means a moral or probationary period in human and angelic history. In each period, God tests free moral agents according to a fixed standard of conduct, under which they're supposed to remain true to God and rule for Him on earth or elsewhere in the universe.\n\nPicture it this way: imagine a man named Ezra who works for a master builder. Early in the project, the builder assigns him to clear the land — that's his entire responsibility for that season. Later, the builder assigns Ezra to lay a foundation. Then to frame walls. Then to finish the interior. Same employer. Same master plan. Completely different instructions for each phase. Now imagine a visitor who arrives during the framing stage and starts clearing trees. He isn't being helpful — he's working from the wrong set of orders. That's precisely what happens when Christians try to live by commands given to Israel under the Law, or apply Tribulation-era promises to the Church today.\n\nNothing but confusion can come from reading meanings into Scripture that don't apply to a particular age. In each age, God has a different purpose. What He said during one dispensation may or may not apply to another.\n\n### IV. The Dispensation of Angels\n\nThe dispensation or administration of angels came before Adam's time, as we'll see in Lesson Seven. It included rulership of the earth and other planets in the heavens.\n\nPaul speaks of "invisible things" in the heavenly world as being just as real and understandable as visible things on earth (Col. 1:15-18). In fact, he says these "invisible things of him from the creation of the world are clearly seen, being understood by the things that are made, even his eternal power and Godhead; so that they are without excuse" (Rom. 1:19-23). In other words, there's no excuse for being ignorant of heavenly realities.\n\nPaul also speaks of heavenly bodies as being just as real as earthly bodies: "There are also celestial bodies, and bodies terrestrial . . . There is a natural body, and there is a spiritual body . . . As is the earthy such are they also that are earthy: and as is the heavenly, such are they also that are heavenly" (1 Cor. 15:35-50).\n\nLet's put aside the idea that heaven is some invisible nothing, or just a cloud where the redeemed float around playing harps for all eternity. The heaven where God dwells is a real planet — "a better country" than Earth (Heb. 11:14-16).\n\nAs we'll see in Lesson Forty-two, heaven is a real place with cities, mansions, food, water, trees, and other things we know in this visible world. Lucifer is described as having a throne (Isa. 14:12-14; Ezek. 28:11-17), and other thrones are mentioned in Col. 1:16-18 as existing in the heavens. These are apparently thrones of other angels, so Scripture does indeed teach the Dispensation of Angels.\n\n### V. The Seven Dispensations of Man Between the Two Eternities\n\nThere are seven dispensations in human history between the eternal past and the eternal future — between man's creation in the six days of Gen. 1–2 and his final restoration in the New Heavens and New Earth of Rev. 21–22.\n\nHere are the seven dispensations:\n\n> (1) THE DISPENSATION OF INNOCENCE (Gen. 2:15–3:21). This age stretched from man's creation and commission to rule the restored earth to man's fall and expulsion from the Garden of Eden. We'll study this in Lesson Nine.\n\n> (2) THE DISPENSATION OF CONSCIENCE (Gen. 3:22–8:14). This age ran from man's fall and expulsion from Eden to Noah's flood — a period of 1,656 years. We'll study this in Lesson Eleven.\n\n> (3) THE DISPENSATION OF HUMAN GOVERNMENT (Gen. 8:15–11:32). This age spanned from Noah's flood to the call of Abraham — 427 years. We'll study this in Lesson Thirteen.\n\n> (4) THE DISPENSATION OF PROMISE (Gen. 12:1—Exod. 12:37). This age covered the call of Abraham to Israel's Exodus from Egypt under Moses — 430 years. We'll study this in Lesson Fifteen.\n\n> (5) THE DISPENSATION OF LAW (Exod. 12:38; Mt. 2:23; 11:10-13; Lk. 16:16). This age lasted from Israel's Exodus from Egypt to John the Baptist's preaching of the kingdom of heaven — from Moses to Christ's first coming, over 1,718 years. We'll study this in Lesson Seventeen.\n\n> (6) THE DISPENSATION OF GRACE (Mt. 3:1—Rev. 19:10). This age has already lasted nearly 2,000 years since Christ's first coming and will continue until His second coming in the near future. How much longer it will last, no one knows. We'll study this in Lesson Nineteen.\n\n> (7) THE DISPENSATION OF DIVINE GOVERNMENT—THE MILLENNIUM (Rev. 19:11–20:15). This age will cover Christ's second coming to the last rebellion of Satan and man — a period of 1,000 years. We'll study this in Lesson Forty-nine.\n\n### VI. The Dispensation of the Redeemed and Faithful Angels\n\nThe final dispensation will come after the Millennium, in the New Heavens and New Earth. God's original purpose will then be fully realized, just as it was before rebellion started through Lucifer and Adam.\n\nAt that point, God will have a universe completely free from any possibility of rebellion throughout all eternity — governed solely by Himself along with redeemed human beings and faithful angels (Rev. 21:1–22:5; 1 Cor. 15:24-28). This administration will be eternal, as we'll prove in Lessons Forty-nine through Fifty-two.\n\nHumanity will be restored to original glory. In the eternal future, we'll once again have dominion over all things through Christ, becoming "heirs of God, and joint heirs with Christ" of all creation (Rom. 8:17-18; 1 Cor. 15:24-28; Heb. 2:5-11).\n\nThis doesn't mean God will dethrone the faithful angels who have remained true throughout all the ages of rebellion. All free moral agents who have proven loyal to God will share in administering the affairs of the universe forever, as we'll see in future lessons.\n\nThat angels are free moral agents — and that many have sinned — is clear from 2 Pet. 2:4; Jude 6-7; Rev. 12:7-12; Mt. 25:41. We'll study the doctrine of angels in Lesson Six.\n\n### VII. Reasons for God's Dispensational Dealings\n\nWhy does God deal with free moral agents through various dispensational or probationary tests? Here are several reasons:\n\n**1.** God created free moral agents with genuine choice rather than making them mere machines running forever with no will of their own. If you could create as God does, wouldn't you also choose to create beings with the power of choice instead of mindless robots?\n\nMost people assume God simply could have made humanity obedient from the start — and chose not to, for some mysterious reason. But think about what obedience without the possibility of disobedience actually is: it's not obedience at all. It's programming. A thermostat that "obeys" the temperature setting isn't loyal — it's mechanical. God wanted creatures who could genuinely choose Him, not systems that had no alternative.\n\nThe same is true with us. We're proud when we can make automatic machines that ease our work. How much more meaningful would it be to create a being with the ability to choose and act independently? We'd be free to do other things instead of being tied down to operating them. But if we could create such beings, we'd naturally have to regulate and limit them, holding them responsible for their moral actions.\n\nThe same is true with God. He made humanity as a wondrous machine — but a free, moral, self-acting one. So He must have reasonable restrictions and limits for the best interest of all. Otherwise, we might rebel and try to destroy the Creator. When we choose to rebel against God, there's war — just as there is whenever any two forces oppose each other.\n\nYet God continues to deal with us as free moral agents because that's how He created us. His dealings must be cooperative, for the welfare of all, or His universe would become chaotic and couldn't continue.\n\n**2.** The wills of all free creatures must be tested to see if they're willing to cooperate with God for the greatest good of everyone. They must prove themselves trustworthy before being entrusted with the eternal administration of the universe.\n\n**3.** All free moral agents must have their wills purged of any possibility of falling, so there can be complete mutual confidence. This guarantees no one will mar God's plan at any point in eternity through misuse of free will.\n\n**4.** Free wills must be put through every possible test so that no transgression against any part of the eternal plan is possible at any time. This is the only sure way to guarantee the plan's success forever.\n\n**5.** All free wills must eventually learn these lessons:\n\n> (1) God must be respected and obeyed.\n\n> (2) His laws are final and just.\n\n> (3) Sin doesn't pay and will never be excused.\n\n> (4) God's form of government is the only correct one.\n\n> (5) Loving, free submission to God is the highest and most noble principle of free moral government.\n\n> (6) Justice and righteousness must prevail, or no society can be preserved eternally.\n\n> (7) Consecration to the greatest good of all is the nature and highest glory of any creature.\n\n> (8) God is merciful and forgiving to rebels who repent and learn obedience through their experiences.\n\n> (9) God is the only absolutely just and perfect Being — the only one capable and worthy of unquestionable authority.\n\n> (10) All accusations current rebels make against God are untrue.\n\n> (11) God does only what is for the common good of all creation.\n\nBy virtue of His position as Creator, Preserver, Governor, and Lord — and His history of justice and righteousness — God should be recognized by all as the Supreme Moral Governor of the universe. Until free moral agents learn these lessons, they remain ignorant of certain facts and need such training.\n\n**6.** One of the main reasons God deals with humanity is to bring us back to where we were before the fall. Having purged us of all possibility of future falling, God will restore redeemed humanity to our original position of dominion over all things. God has no doubt whatsoever about the future success of His plan.\n\n**7.** God's dealings with free moral agents in holiness and absolute justice give Him a sound basis for punishing rebels who refuse to conform and blessing those who do. God can still be just and holy in judging and confining rebels to everlasting punishment, since they've refused all merciful dealings and hardened themselves against everything good.\n\nThere's nothing else for God to do but give justice according to deeds — for the continued good of society forever. He must make examples of both the good and the bad for the sake of all generations to come in eternity.\n\nGod cannot excuse rebels and bless them contrary to His revealed plan, or there would be no end to the breaking of His eternal laws. He would have to excuse all wrongdoing forever if He started that pattern — and free wills would have no real restraint. If He excused some but not others, showing partiality, free agents would lose proper respect for Him. If He failed to reward obedience and punish disobedience, there would be no true incentive for free wills to conform to the eternal plan.\n\nScripture plainly reveals that rebels in everlasting hell will be an eternal monument of God's wrath toward sin, causing future generations to conform to the highest good of their own being and of the universe (Isa. 66:22-24; Rev. 14:9-11).\n\nWhy shouldn't we cooperate with God for the best interest of all, if such a place exists? Why shouldn't we, since it's the creative purpose and the only natural, normal life for each creature? Why shouldn't God punish rebels who persist in destroying themselves and the eternal society He planned? Why shouldn't He finally confine all eternal rebels away from that society? Why shouldn't God bless all who voluntarily and wholeheartedly cooperate with His plan?\n\nThis plan — rewarding obedience and punishing disobedience — is the only just approach with free moral agents. Everyone can be blessed if they choose, or cursed if that's their choice. Punishment isn't compulsory for anyone. It's the free choice of the individual, and each person alone is responsible for their eternal destiny. God's will is that none should perish — but He respects the will of those who choose otherwise.\n\n---\n\nHere's the question to sit with before moving on: You've just been handed a map of the entire Bible — ages, dispensations, the shape of God's plan from eternity past to eternity future. Is there a scripture passage you've been applying to your own life — perhaps one you heard in a sermon, a song, or a devotional — that you've never actually checked against which age it was written to and whether it applies to you today?	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk44k0004ewhjn0bxbwsw	cmnknk44i0001ewhju56drbw5	Lesson 2 — The Holy Scriptures	READING	3856	2	\N	t	![Lesson 2 — The Holy Scriptures](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsENX6vAtdLWqJHyu8Q5MfmIRAjonSBKDvC0V2)\n\n# The Holy Scriptures\n\nBefore you open any book, you usually ask one silent question: can I trust this? With most books, you're trusting one person's research, one time period, one perspective. The Bible asks something harder — it asks you to trust a claim that 40 writers across 1,800 years, on three continents, who never met or compared notes, produced a single unified document without a single contradiction. Either that's the greatest literary coincidence in human history, or it requires an explanation that goes beyond human authorship.\n\nLast time we saw that the entire Bible operates like a master filing system — ages, dispensations, a structure that gives every passage its proper address. That map only matters if the document is reliable. So before we go further into the plan, we need to establish what the Bible actually is — and whether it deserves the confidence we're about to place in it.\n\n## I. Names of the Bible\n\n### 1. Bible\n\nThe word "Bible" refers to the collection of scriptures—both Old and New Testaments—that Christian churches recognize and use as they follow Jesus Christ.\n\nYou won't actually find the word "Bible" in the English versions of Scripture. It comes from the Greek word *biblia*, which simply means "books." The phrase *ta biblia* ("the books") appears in Dan. 9:2 in the Septuagint, referring to the prophetic writings. Early Christians adopted this usage for the Old Testament and eventually extended it to include the New Testament as well.\n\nHere's something interesting: around the thirteenth century, common usage shifted the term from plural ("the books") to singular—"the Book." That's how we came to speak of the Bible as one unified volume.\n\n### 2. Other Names of the Bible\n\nScripture goes by many names throughout its pages: the Scripture (Mk. 15:28; Jn. 7:38; 2 Tim. 3:16-17); the Scriptures (Lk. 24:27, 32; Jn. 5:39; Acts 17:11); the Holy Scriptures (Rom. 1:2; 2 Tim. 3:15); the Promises (Rom. 9:4-5; 15:8); the Oracles of God (Rom. 3:2; Heb. 5:12; 1 Pet. 4:11); the Lively (living) Oracles (Acts 7:38); the Law of Moses, the Prophets, and the Psalms (Lk. 24:25, 44); the Law of the Lord (Ps. 1:2); the Law and the Prophets (Mt. 5:17; 11:13; Acts 13:15); the Book of the Lord (Isa. 34:16); the Word of God (Mk. 7:13; Rom. 10:17; Heb. 4:12); the Sword of the Spirit (Eph. 6:17); the Old and New Testament (Lk. 22:20; 2 Cor. 3:6-15; Heb. 9:15); the Word of Christ (Col. 3:16); the Word of Life (Phil. 2:16); the Scripture of Truth (Dan. 10:21); the Word of Truth (2 Tim. 2:15); and the Gospel of Christ (Rom. 1:16).\n\nThe word "testament" means a document that reveals someone's will, a contract, an agreement, or a covenant between two parties. All these meanings become clearer the more you study the Bible. By the end of the second century, "Old Testament" and "New Testament" had become the permanent names for the Jewish and Christian Scriptures.\n\nThe Old Testament is largely a record of God's dealings with the Hebrew people. It reveals His will to them and through them to the whole human race, showing how He binds Himself to take into a new and special relationship all who obey His will.\n\nThe New Testament is largely the fulfillment and expansion of the Old Testament. It gives us the record of God's promises, agreements, and covenants with humanity, showing the privileges, blessings, and requirements of the gospel through Jesus Christ, the Redeemer of the world.\n\n## II. What the Bible is Not\n\n> 1. The Bible is not an amulet, a charm, a fetish, or something that works wonders just by being present—without any action on your part. The Bible makes no such claim. What it *does* claim is that if you study and practice its teachings, it will work wonders in your life now and in eternity. Think of it like a spring of cool water in the desert: it won't benefit a thirsty man if he refuses to drink.\n\n> 2. The Bible is not a book of strictly chronological events or one unbroken series of divine utterances. It was given piece by piece—"here a little, and there a little"—to many people across eighteen or more centuries (Isa. 28:9-11). Yet despite this, it forms a perfect unity, as we'll see.\n\n> 3. The Bible is not a book of heavenly utterances in some supernatural language. It's God's revelation in the simplest human language possible.\n\n> 4. The Bible is not a book of mysteries. It explains what it calls "mysteries," and it interprets itself, so that no mystery remains unsolved for those who seek.\n\n> 5. The Bible is not a book that says one thing but means another. It generally has only one simple meaning. If a few passages have a double meaning, that's made clear either in the passage itself or in parallel passages. You really can't get a thousand different meanings from any single verse, despite what some people think.\n\n> 6. The Bible is not a specimen of God's skill as a writer or logician. It's a book written by people whom God used to record His revelation. God gave these writers freedom to use their own language and ways of expressing truth. The writers were God's *penmen*, not God's *pens*. Inspiration guarantees unity of thought, not sameness of words and expressions.\n\n> 7. The Bible is not a book of systematic, topical discourses on any one subject. However, it does provide divine information on practically every subject. You must gather together all of God's information from various writers throughout the Bible to get the whole truth. When you do this, you'll find perfect harmony and clarity on everything that really matters.\n\n> 8. The Bible is not a book that conforms to the tastes, customs, or habits of any one nation, people, or time period. It's a book that all people in all ages can conform to, while still keeping their own customs and habits—as long as those aren't sinful or contrary to God's will.\n\n## III. What the Bible Is\n\nThe Bible is God's inspired revelation of the origin and destiny of all things. It's the power of God for eternal salvation and the source of present help for body, soul, and spirit.\n\nPaul writes in Romans 1:16: "I am not ashamed of the gospel of Christ: for it is the power of God unto salvation to every one that believeth." That word "power" is *dunamis* in Greek — the same root as our word "dynamite." Paul isn't using a polite metaphor. He's saying the gospel is explosive force compressed into words. It doesn't gently suggest change; it detonates it. The Book that contains that force is unlike anything else you'll ever hold in your hand.\n\nIt's God's will and testament to people in all ages, revealing His plan for you here and now, as well as in the life to come. It's the record of God's dealings with humanity—past, present, and future. It contains God's message of eternal salvation to everyone who believes in Christ, and eternal damnation for those who rebel against the gospel.\n\nAs a literary composition, the Bible is the most remarkable book ever made. It's a divine library of sixty-six books—some quite large, others no bigger than a short pamphlet.\n\nThese books include all kinds of literature: history, biography, poetry, proverbs, hymns, letters, detailed instructions for worship, laws, parables, riddles, allegories, prophecy, drama, and every other form of human expression. They embrace every manner of literary style. From any standpoint, the Bible simply cannot be surpassed.\n\nIt's the book that contains the mind of God, the state of humanity, the way of salvation, the doom of sinners, and the happiness of believers. Its doctrines are holy, its commands are binding, its histories are true, and its decisions are unchangeable.\n\nRead it to be wise, believe it to be safe, and practice it to be holy. It contains light to direct you, food to support you, and comfort to cheer you. It's the traveler's map, the pilgrim's staff, the pilot's compass, the soldier's sword, and the Christian's charter. Here heaven is opened and the gates of hell disclosed.\n\nChrist is its grand subject, your good is its design, and the glory of God is its end.\n\nRead it slowly, frequently, prayerfully, meditatively, searchingly, and devotionally. Study it constantly, perseveringly, and industriously. Read it through and through until it becomes part of your very being and generates faith that can move mountains.\n\nIt's a mine of wealth, a source of health, and a world of pleasure. It's given to you in this life, will be opened at the judgment, and will last forever. It carries the highest responsibility, rewards the smallest to the greatest labor, and condemns all who trifle with its sacred contents.\n\nIt is:\n- A mirror to reflect (Jas. 1:23)\n- A hammer to convict (Jer. 23:29)\n- A fire to refine (Jer. 23:29)\n- Seed to multiply (1 Pet. 1:23)\n- Water to cleanse (Eph. 5:26; Jn. 15:3)\n- A lamp to guide (Ps. 119:105)\n- Food to nourish—including milk for babes (1 Pet. 2:2), bread for the hungry (Mt. 4:4), meat for the mature (Heb. 5:11-14), and honey for dessert (Ps. 19:10)\n- Rain and snow to refresh (Isa. 55:10)\n- A sword to cut (Heb. 4:12)\n- A bow to avenge (Hab. 3:9)\n- Gold to enrich (Ps. 19:7-10)\n- Power to create life and faith (1 Pet. 1:23; Rom. 10:17)\n\n## IV. General Facts About the Bible\n\n### 1. How the Bible Was Given to Man\n\nThe Bible came to us through the audible voice of God (Mt. 3:16-17; 17:5; Jn. 12:28; Dt. 5:24), through angels (Acts 7:38; Heb. 2:2), through prophets (Acts 3:21; 2 Pet. 1:21), through Jesus Christ (Heb. 1:1-3; Rev. 1:1), and through the apostles (Acts 1:2; Eph. 4:7-11).\n\nIt came through visions (Isa. 6; Dan. 7–8; Ezek. 1), dreams (Dan. 2; Mt. 1:20; 2:12), revelation (Gal. 1:15-16; Eph. 3:3), and inspiration (2 Tim. 3:15-17).\n\n### 2. Languages of the Bible\n\nThe Old Testament was written in Hebrew and Aramaic. The New Testament was written in Greek.\n\n### 3. Divisions of the Bible (King James Version)\n\nThere are two main divisions: the Old Testament (39 books) and the New Testament (27 books). Each Testament is divided into five main sections.\n\n**The Old Testament:**\n- The Pentateuch (five books of Moses): Genesis through Deuteronomy\n- Twelve historical books: Joshua through Esther\n- Five poetical books: Job through Song of Solomon\n- Five Major Prophets: Isaiah through Daniel\n- Twelve Minor Prophets: Hosea through Malachi\n\n**The New Testament:**\n- Four Gospels: Matthew through John\n- One historical book: Acts\n- Fourteen Pauline Epistles: Romans through Hebrews\n- Seven General Epistles: James through Jude\n- One prophetic book: Revelation\n\nThe Bible as a whole contains 66 books, 1,189 chapters, and 31,214 verses, made up of 773,746 words and 3,566,480 letters.\n\nThere are nearly 1,250 promises to people in various ages, but only about 500 that modern Christians can definitely claim. Many promises concerned Israel and certain nations of the past, present, and future that don't specifically apply to Christian life today. However, there are still an abundance of promises for Christians covering every known need in this life and the life to come, as we'll see in the following lessons.\n\nHere are some interesting Bible facts: The two longest words are in Isa. 8:1 and the title of Ps. 56. The longest verse is Esth. 8:9; the shortest verse is Jn. 11:35. The middle book is Micah; the middle verse is Ps. 118:8. The middle and shortest chapter is Ps. 117. The longest book is Psalms; the shortest is 2 John. The longest chapter is Ps. 119.\n\nChapter divisions were made in A.D. 1236. Four verses in Ps. 107 are alike: v 8, 15, 21, and 31. Also, 2 Ki. 19 and Isa. 37 are alike, as are Ezra 2 and Neh. 7, and 2 Chron. 36:22-23 with Ezra 1:1-3a.\n\nThere are 26 unknown books mentioned in the Bible. Since the invention of printing, over 1,330,231,815 Bibles have been printed and sold in England and Europe alone. Over 30 million are now distributed annually.\n\nThe first complete English Bible was finished in 1380. The first printed Bible was the Gutenberg Bible in 1450.\n\nThe only uninspired parts of Bibles are the chapter and verse divisions, references, marginal notes, chapter and page headings, footnotes, chapter summaries, and everything except the original text.\n\n## V. The Apocryphal Books\n\nIn some large family Bibles, you'll find a section of fourteen books called the Apocrypha—a group of spurious books that were rejected from our present canon of Scripture. Here's why they were rejected:\n\n> 1. They didn't pass the tests required of inspired books.\n\n> 2. They weren't written or approved by a prophet.\n\n> 3. They weren't recognized by the Jews as inspired or as part of Scripture.\n\n> 4. They weren't recognized or even quoted by Christ and the Apostles—a striking fact, especially since Paul quotes twice from pagan poets.\n\n> 5. The last Old Testament prophet predicted that the next messenger to Israel from God would be the forerunner of Christ (Mal. 3:1). Most of these books were written during the period between Malachi and Christ.\n\n> 6. Their authors don't claim divine authority, and some virtually disown it (2 Macc. 2:23; 15:38).\n\n> 7. They contain statements that contradict biblical history.\n\n> 8. They are self-contradictory and oppose the doctrines of Scripture.\n\n> 9. Josephus, who lived at the time of the apostles, didn't regard them as Scripture. He stated that the present books of the Old Testament in our version were the only inspired books (see Josephus, Book I, section 8).\n\n> 10. They weren't part of the ancient versions of Scripture.\n\n> 11. They were first added after A.D. 300. The Laodicean Council in A.D. 363 rejected them as uninspired, proving that by then some were claiming inspiration for them. They first appeared in the Vatican Version of the fourth century. At the Council of Trent in A.D. 1546, Catholics accepted six of these books as inspired and added them to their modern versions. These are: Wisdom of Solomon, Ecclesiasticus, Tobit, Judith, and 1 and 2 Maccabees.\n\n> 12. Philo and others didn't regard them as inspired.\n\n> 13. They lack prophetic content and appear to imitate other inspired Old Testament books.\n\n> 14. They make too free a use of imagination, give rise to silly stories, and lack spiritual force and power.\n\n## VI. The Bible: An Inspired Revelation From God\n\nChristianity claims to be a revealed religion, and the record of that revelation is contained in the Sacred Scriptures. Let's look at some key points:\n\n### 1. Reasons Man Can Expect a Revelation From God\n\nYour intellectual and moral nature requires a revelation from God. Such a revelation helps you preserve and ensure the moral and spiritual progress you need—progress you cannot achieve on your own.\n\nWithin your moral makeup, there's an intuition, a reasoning, and a hunger for the supernatural and for knowledge of things that haven't been revealed. Since nothing in nature exists without a purpose, these natural cravings must be satisfied. The only way these desires can be met is through a supernatural revelation and manifestation, leading you to the end for which you were created.\n\nOnly a revelation of things beyond this life can fully satisfy the natural demands of your nature.\n\nAll history shows that in nations where biblical revelation isn't known, there's a very low standard of living. Because of imperfect knowledge, humanity's actual condition has been one of moral depravity and utter helplessness against evil forces and the higher demands of nature.\n\nWhat we know of God through nature gives us grounds to believe that this lack in human life has been met by supernatural revelation. It's only right to believe that since God made you a moral and spiritual being for spiritual purposes, He also supplied the means to achieve those purposes.\n\nIt's not natural or reasonable to think the Creator would leave His creation incomplete—creating within you this longing for the unknown without meeting your needs with divine supply.\n\nAt the same time, both conscience and reason tell you that you're a sinner deserving condemnation. But reason alone can't tell you whether God will be merciful and save you. Your doubts can only be removed by God's own word to you. This requires a divine revelation.\n\n### 2. What Man May Expect of a Divine Revelation\n\nYou should not only expect a revelation—you may also expect it to be in perfect harmony with nature, supplementing what nature already reveals. Those who are honest and rational about such proof may expect a revelation that is beyond all doubt from a supernatural source.\n\nYou may expect this revelation to come through chosen vessels and to be preserved by divine power through the ages. You may further expect it to be confirmed by miraculous works and prophetic utterances fulfilled to the letter.\n\nAll of this is true of the Bible, as we'll see in the proofs of inspiration below.\n\n### 3. The Meaning of Revelation\n\nThe word "revelation" comes from the Greek *apokalupsis*, meaning to unveil, reveal, and uncover—like lifting a curtain so everyone can see what was previously hidden.\n\nThere's no excuse for different interpretations of God's revelation when we're looking at things that can be seen alike by all—if we all look at the same thing in the same way.\n\nGod's revelation is simply the unveiling of facts and truths you couldn't know on your own but are divinely revealed by the Spirit of God. About one-fifth of the Bible is prophecy, which required revelation. Then there are many other parts—creation, Lucifer's reign, God's plan, and many other things—that had to be revealed before anyone could know the facts about them.\n\nThe historical portions of the Bible didn't have to be revealed, but they're just as inspired as the revealed portions. Inspiration simply guarantees the true recording of facts as they happened—or as they're going to happen.\n\nBoth the method of disclosure and the truth disclosed are called revelation (Eph. 3:3; Col. 1:26; Rev. 1:1; Rom. 16:25).\n\n### 4. The Meaning of Inspiration\n\nMost people think of "inspiration" the way we use it in everyday speech — a painter inspired by a sunset, an author inspired by a personal experience. Under this definition, the Bible would be one group of people's heartfelt spiritual reflections. But that's not the biblical claim at all.\n\nThe Greek word *theopneustos* literally means "God-breathed." It appears in 2 Timothy 3:16: "All scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness." Notice the scope — "all scripture." Not the parts you like, not the comfortable promises, not just the devotional sections. All of it carries the same divine breath. And "profitable for doctrine, reproof, correction, instruction" means it's designed to do work — to reshape how you think, expose where you're wrong, correct your course, and train you in righteousness. A merely-human book can inspire you. A God-breathed book can transform you.\n\nInspiration is that special influence or power of the Holy Spirit upon the minds and lives of holy people, which qualified and enabled them to make an infallible record of divine truth concerning God's will for humanity.\n\nPaul said, "All scripture is given by inspiration of God [i.e., is God-breathed], and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness; that the man of God may be perfect, throughly furnished unto all good works" (2 Tim. 3:15-17).\n\nPeter said, "God hath spoken by the mouth of all his holy prophets since the world began," and that "holy men of God spake as they were moved [borne along] by the Holy Ghost" (Acts 3:21; 2 Pet. 1:21).\n\n### 5. The Purpose of Inspiration\n\nThe purpose of inspiration is to secure truth and unity in the record—not conformity or sameness of statement. Inspiration has accomplished this beyond human comprehension, as proven in Point VII below.\n\n### 6. The Difference Between Revelation and Inspiration\n\nRevelation discovers new truth, while inspiration supervises the communicating and recording of that truth.\n\nWe have examples of:\n- Inspiration without revelation (Lk. 1:1-4)\n- Inspiration including revelation (Rev. 1:1, 11)\n- Inspiration without illumination (1 Pet. 1:11; 1 Cor. 14:13-19)\n- Revelation and inspiration including illumination (1 Cor. 2:12-16; 14:30)\n\nWe find lies of Satan and people, false statements, murders, adulteries, and many sins recorded in Scripture. Inspiration simply records the truth of what was said or done. It guarantees that Satan lied and that what is written is actually what he said—but it doesn't change the lie into truth.\n\nInspiration records the sins of people, but it doesn't sanction those sins as God's will. As you study Scripture, you must keep in mind the difference between what Satan and people say versus what God actually says. God is responsible only for what He says and what He inspires people to say—not for what others say. All He's responsible for is the true record of what people and demons have said and done.\n\n### 7. To What Degree Were the Writers of the Bible Inspired?\n\nSome words were the exact words of God (Exod. 32:16; Deut. 5:4, 24; Mt. 3:17; 17:5; Jn. 12:28). Some words were put into the mouths of speakers who spoke as the Spirit inspired them (Exod. 4:12; Num. 23:5; Ezek. 2:7; 3:10-11; Acts 3:21). Some words were written as the writers were moved by the Spirit (Exod. 34:17; 2 Pet. 1:21; Rev. 1:11).\n\nIn other parts of Scripture, the speakers and writers were inspired to choose their own words in relating divine truth, or in saying things that were later recorded by the Spirit through others (Dan. 12:8-9; Jn. 20:30-31; Lk. 1:1-4; Acts 1:1-2).\n\nRegardless of how the various passages were recorded, it was all by full and plenary inspiration—meaning the entire Bible was inspired by God.\n\nIn speaking and writing the divine record of things past, present, and future, the Spirit used the writers' attention, reason, investigation, memory, logic, and all their faculties. He guided them to choose material from others—spoken and written—such as imperial decrees, genealogies, letters, historical records, and whatever was necessary for recording the truth.\n\nThe Spirit worked in and through their own spirits and preserved their individualities in their writings. The Bible is truly the Word of God in human language, and it should be understood on the same basis we understand other books written in human language.\n\n## VII. Proofs of Revelation and Inspiration\n\nThe following reasons are sufficient to prove to an unbiased mind that the Bible is an inspired revelation of God:\n\n### 1. Its Wonderful Unity\n\nMost people who've heard "the Bible was written by many authors" treat it as a problem — a reason to distrust it. But look at what Scripture actually presents as evidence: that 40 writers across 1,800 years, on three continents, in wildly different circumstances, produced one unified message. The diversity of authorship isn't the Bible's weakness — it's its most powerful proof of divine origin.\n\nOver 40 different authors wrote the 66 books of the Bible during a period of more than 1,800 years, and they all had one theme: the creation and redemption of the human race by God through Jesus Christ and the Holy Spirit.\n\nThese books were written by people from all walks of life—kings, priests, judges, lawyers, princes, shepherds, soldiers, courtiers, statesmen, musicians, inventors, singers, poets, preachers, prophets, fishermen, farmers, tentmakers, tax collectors, physicians, rich and poor alike.\n\nThey were written in various lands across three continents—Europe, Asia, and Africa. They were written in different ages by people who often never saw each other or knew what the others wrote on the same subjects. Yet when their writings became one book, there's not a single contradiction among them.\n\nThink of it like this: imagine 40 physicians — one in ancient Alexandria, one in medieval Paris, one in colonial Massachusetts, one in twentieth-century London — each writing independently on how to treat tuberculosis, each without access to what the others wrote, each separated by centuries. Now collect those 40 books. What do you find? Contradictory diagnoses, competing remedies, incompatible frameworks. Each expert trying to disprove the others. What you do *not* find is a single seamless treatment plan that all 40 authors agree on from beginning to end. Yet that's precisely what you find in the Bible — 66 books, one story, one diagnosis of the human condition, one remedy.\n\nOr try this: collect 40 books on the same subject, each written by a different author, and see how many contradictions exist. Some will try to prove how the others are wrong and why their own theory is right. This is obvious to anyone who has read different authors on any subject.\n\nThere's no unity of thought between human books on any subject. But there's perfect unity between the books of the Bible, which speak of hundreds of subjects in religion, politics, science, and more.\n\nThis proves there's one divine author for all 66 books. Who else but a divine author could produce such a work?\n\n### 2. Its Superiority to Other Books\n\nThere's abundant evidence that the Bible is superior to all other books. It's unlike any other book in its claims, its message, its moral tone, its insight into the future, and its words of peace, comfort, and hope for everyone. It's different because of its insight into human nature and into all things of life here and hereafter.\n\nIt's the outstanding book among millions of books—in a class by itself. Other books can be classified by subject matter, message, and style, but not the Bible. It doesn't fit into any human classification. Its unique origin, message, and wonderful structure all prove its superiority.\n\nIt's also unequaled in its benefits to people, its circulation, and its popularity. Despite all competition and the advertising advantages other books have, the Bible is still the best seller. More than 30 million copies are distributed annually.\n\nMillions of people in all lands proclaim the Bible as the only book that satisfies the soul and gives hope of life beyond the grave. When a modern author's book is translated into a few languages, they're as proud as can be. The Bible has been translated into 1,086 languages and dialects, with new translations being made every year. There are twelve editions solely for the blind.\n\nIt's the most modern book of all ages, and all other books are hopelessly outclassed when compared to it.\n\nFrom the standpoint of literature and truth, the Bible is a recognized authority on daily life as well as things in the next life. It has no equal. Millions of people in all ages have lived and died by its teachings. No such trust can be placed in any other book.\n\nReligions, secret orders, and practically every kind of human institution claims to be based on the Bible. It's the simplest book to understand, yet it requires constant study. Even non-believers feel uneducated without a sound knowledge of its teachings.\n\nThe more you read, the more you realize how far you are from mastering its contents. There are always new discoveries of truth in the Bible. It's always new to those who read it most.\n\nThis isn't true of any other book. When you read other books once or twice, their contents are mastered, and the subject matter becomes old and uninteresting. All this proves the divine origin of the Bible.\n\n### 3. Its Influence in the World\n\nNo book has ever influenced the world like the Bible. Its impact is as high as the heavens above the earth compared to other books. In lands where the Bible is unknown, this difference is plain to see.\n\nWhile the Bible has shaped modern civilization, if humanity's current trend of rejecting the Bible continues, that civilization will be destroyed. Without the Bible, people would be in dense spiritual and moral darkness, mental ignorance, and pagan superstition.\n\nMillions of lives have been enlightened and changed in every generation by its teachings, proving that its superior influence must come from a divine source.\n\n### 4. The Character of Those Who Accept It\n\nThe character of those who accept the Bible proves it to be inspired by God. Those who grow in holiness and dedicate themselves to the highest good of others accept it as from God and cherish it more and more.\n\nOnly infidels, skeptics, moral and spiritual rebels, and human wrecks of all kinds refuse to accept its inspiration. Naturally, they reject it because it condemns all their activities and promises punishment in the end.\n\n### 5. The Greatness of Those Who Accept It\n\nThe greatness of those who accept the Bible as God's revelation proves it's more than an ordinary human product. Some argue that the Bible and its religion are accepted only by the weak, the young, and the ignorant, and that its champions outside the pulpit are few.\n\nThis is one of the greatest errors among skeptics and shows either willful prejudice or superficial knowledge. The greatest thinkers and representative people of all ages have openly confessed their faith in Christianity and the Bible. The wise of the world, best qualified to detect error and imposture, have laid their homage at Christ's feet and confessed that the Bible is God's Word.\n\nWe have over a thousand testimonies from the greatest people since Christ—outside the clergy—who have left witness of their unwavering faith in the Bible as God's Word and in Christ as God's Son.\n\nThese leaders of human thought throughout the centuries—who weren't biased as preachers are accused of being, and who had no personal interest at stake—have simply been honest in acknowledging facts. When such people use their pen and voice to declare that Christ and the Bible are what they claim to be, it's time for skeptics to listen to facts without bias.\n\nThese people have been kings, presidents, senators, congressmen, diplomats, philosophers, scientists, poets, authors, historians, artists, philanthropists, reformers, educators, lawyers, physicians, soldiers, journalists, financiers, governors, and leaders of great movements—acknowledged representatives of the old and new world.\n\nCarlyle said, "No sadder proof can be given a man of his own littleness than disbelief in great men." Webster said, "Great authorities are great arguments."\n\nHere are a few testimonies to prove the point:\n\n> "Above all, the pure light of revelation has had an influence on mankind, and increased the blessings of society. It is impossible to rightly govern the world without God and the Bible."—George Washington\n\n> "I have always said that a studious perusal of the sacred volume will make better citizens, better fathers, and better husbands."—Thomas Jefferson\n\n> "The first and almost the only book deserving of universal attention is the Bible. I speak as a man of the world."—John Quincy Adams\n\n> "It [the Bible] is the rock on which our Republic rests."—Andrew Jackson\n\n> "It was for the love of the truths of this great and good Book that our fathers abandoned their native shores for the wilderness."—Zachary Taylor\n\n> "I am profitably engaged in reading the Bible. Take all of this Book that you can by reason and the balance by faith, and you will live and die a better man. It is the best book which God has given to man."—Abraham Lincoln\n\n> "I have known ninety-five of the world's great men in my time, and of these eighty-seven were followers of the Bible."—W. E. Gladstone\n\n> "Almost every man who has by his lifework added to the sum of human achievement . . . has based his lifework largely upon the teachings of the Bible."—Theodore Roosevelt\n\n> "A man has deprived himself of the best there is in the world who has deprived himself of this" (a knowledge of the Bible).—Woodrow Wilson\n\n> "There is no other book so various as the Bible, nor one so full of concentrated wisdom. Whether it be of law, business, morals, etc. . . . he who seeks for guidance . . . may look inside its covers and find illumination."—Herbert Hoover\n\n> "The Bible contains more philosophy than all the libraries that I have ever seen; and such parts as I cannot reconcile with my little philosophy, I postpone for future investigation."—John Adams\n\n> "To the influence of this Book we are indebted for the progress made in civilization, and to this we must look as our guide in the future."—Ulysses S. Grant\n\n> "The young must be taught, and they must be taught truly if the spring-waters of democracy are to be kept untainted . . . The influence of the Scriptures in the early days of the Republic is plainly revealed in the writing and thinking of the men who made the nation possible . . . They found in the Scriptures that which shaped their course and determined their action."—Franklin D. Roosevelt\n\n> "England has become great and happy by the knowledge of the true God through Jesus Christ . . . This is the secret of England's greatness."—Queen Victoria\n\n> "Do not join those who either ignore the Bible altogether, or, at least, give it a spurious interpretation of their own devising."—Kaiser Wilhelm of Germany\n\n> "What I was as an artist, seemed to me of some importance while I lived; what I really was as a believer in Christ Jesus, is the only thing of importance to me now. What can I do with respect to the next world without my Bible? No philosopher offers anything that meets, and, much less, relieves, my case."—John Bacon\n\n> "The Bible is more than a Book; it is a living being with an action, a power which invades everything that opposes its extension."—Napoleon Bonaparte\n\n> "The sacredness of the Bible awes me."—William Cohen Bryant\n\n> "It is hard to make a choice of the most beautiful passage in a Book which is gemmed with beautiful passages as the Bible."—Mark Twain\n\n> "The only spiritual light in the world comes through Jesus Christ and the inspired Book . . . Without His presence and the teachings of the Bible we would be enshrouded in moral darkness and despair . . . nations without Christ, contrasted with those where Christ is accepted, reveal so marked a difference that no arguments are needed."—Samuel Colgate\n\n> "All other books are of little importance in comparison with the Holy Scriptures, which are a revelation from God, and are given as the only rule of faith and practice."—Alexander Cruden\n\n> "Here is my creed: I believe in one God, the Creator of the Universe, that He governs it by His providence; that He ought to be worshipped; that the most acceptable service we can render Him is doing good to others; that the soul of man is immortal, and will be treated with justice in another world respecting his conduct in this. As to Jesus of Nazareth, I think His system of morals, as He left them\n\n---\n\nYou've just surveyed the most examined book in human history — its names, its structure, what it is and isn't, how it was given, and why the greatest minds of every era have staked their confidence on it. So here's the honest question to leave with: When did you last open this Book expecting to be genuinely changed by it — not informed, not comforted, not confirmed in what you already believed, but actually corrected and transformed? If you can't remember, that's less a statement about the Bible's power and more a statement about how you've been reading it.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgah000710b8fqzn0aqk	cmq76cga9000110b8juoxpkya	Supplement 1 — For Lessons 1 & 2	SUPPLEMENT	600	2	\N	t	![Supplement 1 — For Lessons 1 & 2](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OscTEm8aHaBEe23oH5UXu7NQGbLSsPzChWlD6n)\n\n## Supplement 1 — For Lessons 1 & 2: The Nature and Origin of Demons\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**Demon** — A fallen angel who rebelled against God and now serves Satan's purposes on earth.\n\n**Lucifer** — The original name of Satan, meaning "light-bearer"; the highest created angel who fell through pride.\n\n**Fallen Angels** — Angels who followed Lucifer in rebellion; identified in Scripture as "devils," "unclean spirits," and "demons."\n\n**The Prince of the Power of the Air** — One of Satan's titles (Ephesians 2:2), describing his temporary authority over the fallen world system.\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> James 2:19 — "Thou believest that there is one God; thou doest well: the devils also believe, and tremble."\n\n> Ezekiel 28:15 — "Thou wast perfect in thy ways from the day that thou wast created, till iniquity was found in thee."\n\n> 1 Peter 5:8 — "Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour."\n\n---\n\n### Key Distinctions\n\n**Angel vs. Demon**\n\n| Feature | Holy Angels | Demons (Fallen Angels) |\n|---------|-------------|------------------------|\n| Origin | Created holy | Fell through rebellion |\n| Will | Obedient to God | Rebellious, self-willed |\n| Destiny | Eternal glory | Eternal condemnation |\n| Purpose | Serve God's people | Destroy God's people |\n| Power | Derived from God | Usurped, temporary |\n\n**Lucifer's Five "I Wills" (Isaiah 14:13-14)**\n\n1. "I will ascend into heaven"\n2. "I will exalt my throne above the stars of God"\n3. "I will sit also upon the mount of the congregation"\n4. "I will ascend above the heights of the clouds"\n5. "I will be like the most High"\n\n---\n\n### Questions for Reflection\n\n1. Why does the Bible present demons as personal beings rather than abstract forces? What difference does this make for how we approach spiritual warfare?\n\n2. Lucifer's fall originated in pride over his own beauty and gifts. What does this teach us about the danger of self-admiration?\n\n3. James says demons "believe, and tremble." Why is intellectual belief in God insufficient for salvation?\n\n4. How does understanding that demons are defeated but dangerous change the way you face spiritual opposition?	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk44k000aewhjeypc0ek7	cmnknk44i0001ewhju56drbw5	Lesson 6 — Satan and the Spirit World	READING	4665	8	\N	t	Most Christians believe in Satan the way they believe in gravity — as a real force they can’t see that affects things without being personally present. He’s a symbol of evil, a useful metaphor, maybe the name for whatever goes wrong. But that’s not the biblical portrait at all. Scripture describes a specific being with a history, a title, a strategy, and a very personal interest in your life. Misunderstanding what he is makes you permanently vulnerable to what he does.\n\nLast time we saw that Lucifer’s rebellion turned a perfect world into a wasteland — that Genesis 1:2 is the wreckage of a war, not raw material. Now we go deeper: Who is this being? What does Scripture actually say about the spirit world he leads?\n\nThere are many kinds of spirit-beings revealed in Scripture. And by "unseen worlds," we're talking about all the heavens, the underworld of departed spirits, and even the invisible things right here on earth. The Scriptures are saturated with the supernatural — there's really just a step between the natural world and the spiritual world. Let's look at some of the spirit-beings that exist in this realm.\n\n![Lesson 6 — Satan and the Spirit World](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OskWBfZR8rZcMaXYe27SivEmH1t8Ad0OozjUKI)\n\n## I. Angelic Beings Called Seraphim\n\nThese magnificent creatures appear only twice in Scripture, but their description makes it clear they're angelic, heavenly beings. Picture the scene Isaiah describes:\n\n"I saw also the Lord sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple. Above it stood the seraphims: each had six wings: with twain he covered his face, and with twain he covered his feet, and with twain he did fly. And one cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy, is the Lord of hosts: the whole earth is full of his glory. And the posts of the door moved at the voice of him that cried, and the house was filled with smoke . . . Then flew one of the seraphims unto me, having a live coal in his hand, which he had taken with the tongs from off the altar. And he laid it upon my mouth, and said, Lo, this hath touched thy lips; and thine iniquity is taken away and thy sin purged" (Isa. 6:1-7).\n\n## II. Angelic Beings Called Cherubim\n\nCherubim show up in several passages — too lengthy to quote in full, so let's walk through a brief description. Ezekiel saw them when the heavens opened and he received visions of God.\n\nThe cherubim look like men, except each one has four faces and four wings, with feet like a calf. Two of their wings join tip to tip, and the other two cover their bodies. Their faces are like those of a man, a lion, an ox, and an eagle. Their general appearance? Like fire and lightning, and they move with the speed of lightning.\n\nThey're connected to wheels that look like a wheel within a wheel — very high, colored like beryl, with many eyes in them. There's a crystal-like firmament over their heads, and above that sits a throne where God appears in the form of a man. Fire, lightning, and glory surround the throne with a rainbow encircling it (Ezek. 1:5-28; 8:1-4; 10:1-22). These same cherubim drove man from Eden and guarded the Tree of Life (Gen. 3:24).\n\n## III. Angelic Beings Called Zoa or Living Creatures\n\nThese beings are similar to the cherubim, except they have only one head each and are full of eyes before and behind. Like the seraphim, they have six wings. One has a face like a lion, one like a calf, one like a man, and one like a flying eagle. Day and night, they cry, "Holy, holy, holy" to God (Rev. 4:6-9).\n\nThe word translated "beast" in this passage is *zoa*, meaning "living creature." In Rev. 4:6–5:14, the zoa are pictured with harps, singing and worshipping God. You'll also see them throughout Revelation, saying and doing things much like humans do (Rev. 6:1-8; 7:11; 14:3, 9-11; 15:7; 19:4).\n\n## IV. Spirit Horses and Chariot Drivers\n\nPaul taught that many things in the invisible world mirror what we have in the visible world: "For the invisible things of him from the creation of the world are clearly seen, being understood by the things that are made" (Rom. 1:20). Think of it like this: the created world around us is a kind of picture book helping us understand spiritual realities.\n\nPaul also mentioned that during his trip into the third heaven, he "heard unspeakable words, which is not lawful for a man to utter" (2 Cor. 12:1-4). In other words, if he'd told people everything he saw and heard in heaven, they would have thought he'd lost his mind. It wasn't wise to share all that he knew — it might have caused people to reject his gospel message entirely.\n\nMost of us have such a vague conception of heaven and spiritual things that it's hard to grasp the realities of the spirit world. All we truly know is what the Bible reveals. And if we take Paul literally in Rom. 1:20, we could easily believe there are many kinds of heavenly creatures corresponding to what we have on earth. Paul didn't limit how many invisible things are made clear by created things — so let's be wise and not limit them either.\n\nWe do know for certain there are horses in heaven. Consider these scriptures: "There appeared a chariot of fire, and horses of fire, and parted them both asunder; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven. And Elisha saw it, and he cried, My father, my father, the chariot of Israel, and the horsemen thereof" (2 Ki. 2:11-12).\n\nLater, when the Syrian army came to capture Elisha, he prayed that God would show his servant who was really on their side. God opened the young man's eyes "and he saw: and, behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire round about Elisha" (2 Ki. 6:13-17).\n\nZechariah saw red horses, speckled and white, with riders on them. He also saw chariots drawn by red, black, white, grisled, and bay horses — called "the spirits of the heavens" doing scout work for God (Zech. 1:8-11; 6:1-8). And in Rev. 19:11-21, we see the armies of heaven on white horses following Christ, who also rides a white horse, coming from heaven to seize the governments of this world and reign forever.\n\nIf there are horses in heaven, there may well be all kinds of animals. After all, heaven is called a "better country," and it's sure to be at least as good as planet earth (Heb. 11:10-16). We know there are cities, streets, mansions, rivers, trees, and other things in heaven, as we'll see in Lesson Forty-two. The more we embrace the plain scriptures about heavenly things, the more real the next life becomes to us right now.\n\n## V. Angelic Beings Called Archangels\n\nThe word "archangel" appears only twice in Scripture — once in connection with Christ coming in the air to take all the dead and living saints out of the world (1 Thess. 4:16), and once referring to Michael, who disputed with the devil over the body of Moses (Jude 9).\n\nThe word "arch" simply means "chief," suggesting there's a class of beings higher than ordinary angels. In Dan. 10:21 and 12:1, Michael is called "the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people" (the Jews). Rev. 12:7-9 describes him as the commander of God's angels who will fight against the devil and his angels, casting them to earth. He's called "one of the chief princes" of God in Dan. 10:13.\n\nIf Michael is "one of" the chief princes, there must be more archangels. Gabriel is another, according to Dan. 8:16-19; 9:20-23; 10:8–11:1; Lk. 1:19, 26. Lucifer was one of the chief angels and was given charge to rule the earth, as we'll see in the next lesson.\n\nIn Col. 1:15-18, we read of thrones, dominions, principalities, and powers in heaven — so there must be many chief angels. Some of them rebelled along with the devil and now serve under him as rulers of certain kingdoms of this world (Dan. 10:13–11:1).\n\n## VI. Angelic Beings Known as Common Angels\n\nThe words "angel" and "angels" appear 294 times in Scripture. The word comes from Hebrew and Greek terms meaning "messenger." It's used of the second person of the Trinity who appeared to men as a man, or as a messenger of God.\n\nHe is called the angel of God (Gen. 21:17; 31:11; Exod. 3:2; Judg. 6:20; 13:9; Acts 27:23); the angel of the Lord (Gen. 16:7-11; 22:11, 15; Exod. 14:19; Num. 22:22-35; Judg. 2:1, 4; 6:11-12, 21-22; 13:3-6, 13-21; 2 Ki. 1:3, 15; 19:35; 1 Chron. 21:12-30; Ps. 34:7; 35:5-6; Isa. 37:36; Zech. 1:9-19; 3:1-6; 12:8; Acts 7:30-38); His angel (Gen. 24:7, 40; Exod. 23:20; 33:2; Num. 20:16; 2 Chron. 32:21; Dan. 3:28; 6:22); the angel (Gen. 48:16; Eccl. 5:6; Hos. 12:4); mine angel (Exod. 23:23; 32:34); and angel of His presence (Isa. 63:9).\n\nIt's clear all these passages refer to manifestations of God, not an ordinary angel. In all other places where "the angel of the Lord" is found, the term refers to ordinary angels, as in Mt. 1:20, 24; 2:13, 19; 28:2-5; Lk. 1:11-38; 2:9-21; Acts 5:19; 7:26; 10:3; 12:7-23. The word "angel" is used of Christ in Rev. 8:3-5; 10:1–11:3, and of men in Rev. 1:1, 20; 2:1, 8, 12, 18; 3:1, 7, 14; 19:9-10; 22:6-8, 16. In most other places, it's clear that common angels — spirit-beings and heavenly creatures — are meant.\n\n### The Nature of Angels\n\nAngels are intelligent and wise (2 Sam. 14:20; 19:27; Mt. 24:35); patient (Num. 22:22-35); meek (2 Pet. 2:11; Jude 9); joyful (Lk. 15:1-10); modest (1 Cor. 11:10); holy (Mk. 8:38); glorious (Lk. 9:26); immortal (Lk. 20:36); powerful and mighty (2 Thess. 1:7-10; Rev. 18:1); obedient (Ps. 103:20; Mt. 6:10); heavenly spirit-beings (Ps. 104:4; Mt. 22:30; 24:36; Heb. 1:14); not demons (Acts 23:8-9); not human (Heb. 2:16); limited in knowledge (Mk. 13:32); higher than men (Ps. 8:5); and always spoken of as male beings, not as sexless as some teach from Lk. 20:36.\n\nThey have wills (Isa. 14:12-14) and spirit-bodies with hands, feet, eyes, voice, head, mouth, hair, face, and other parts and passions like men (Judg. 13:6; Dan. 10:5-21; Rev. 8:1–9:21; 14:6-11; 15:1–16:21; 2 Thess. 1:7-10). They need no rest (Rev. 4:8); eat food (Gen. 18:8; 19:3; Ps. 78:25); can appear visible and invisible (Num. 22:35; Jn. 20:12; Heb. 13:2); can operate in the physical realm (Gen. 18:1–19:24; 22:11; 2 Sam. 24; 2 Ki. 19:35; Ps. 78:49; 91:11; Mt. 28:2; Acts 10 and 12); can travel at inconceivable speed (Rev. 8:13; 9:1); can ascend and descend (Gen. 28:12; Jn. 1:51); can speak languages (1 Cor. 13:1); and can act and do all things man can do.\n\n### The Work of Angels\n\nAngels drive spirit horses (2 Ki. 2:12; 6:13-17; Zech. 1:7-11; 6:1-6); guard gates (Rev. 21:12); wage war in actual bodily combat (Rev. 12:7-9; 2 Thess. 1:7-10); execute judgments (Gen. 19; 2 Sam. 24; 2 Ki. 19:35; 2 Chron. 32:21; Ps. 78:49; Mt. 13:41-42; Acts 12:23; Rev. 8:1–9:21; 15:1–16:21); minister to saints (1 Ki. 19:5-7; Dan. 6:22; Mt. 4:11; Acts 10; Heb. 1:14); rule nations (Dan. 10:13-21; 12:1); help each individual (Mt. 18:10); sing, praise, and worship God (Lk. 2:13; Ps. 103:20; 148:2; Rev. 5:11); strengthen in trial (Mt. 4:11; Lk. 22:43); lead sinners to gospel workers (Acts 10:3); direct preachers (Acts 8:26; 27:23); appear in dreams (Mt. 1:20-24; 2:13-19); minister before God (Rev. 8:2; 14:15-19); bind Satan (Rev. 20); guard the abyss (Rev. 9:1; 20:1-3); regather Israel (Mt. 24:31); protect saints (Ps. 34:7; 91:11; Acts 12:7-10); separate the good and bad (Mt. 13:39-41); accompany Christ to earth (Mt. 16:27; 25:31; 2 Thess. 1:7-10); witness confessions (Lk. 15:8-9); receive departed spirits (Lk. 16:22); give laws (Acts 7:53; Heb. 2:2); guard the Tree of Life (Gen. 3:24); give revelations (2 Ki. 1:15; Dan. 8:19; 9:21-23; 10:10-20); impart God's will (Acts 5:19-20; 10:1-6); bring answers to prayers (Dan. 9:21-23; 10:12-13; Acts 10); and do many other things for God and man.\n\n### Angels Are Called\n\nAngels are called watchers (Dan. 4:13-23); sons of the mighty (Ps. 89:6); sons of God (Gen. 6:1-4; Job 1:6; 2:1; 38:7); congregation of the mighty (Ps. 82:1); saints (Ps. 89:7); hosts (Ps. 33:6; 103:21; Lk. 2:13); spirits (Heb. 1:14); and the elect (1 Tim. 5:21).\n\n### General Facts About Angels\n\nAngels were created by Christ before the earth (Job 38:4-7; Ps. 148:2-5; Col. 1:16). They are not to be worshipped (Col. 2:16). They are organized into principalities and powers with thrones (Col. 1:16; 2:16; Rom. 8:38; Eph. 6:10-18; 1 Pet. 3:22). They are innumerable (Lk. 2:13; Heb. 12:22); to be judged or ruled by saints (1 Cor. 6:3); subject to God (Mt. 22:30); interested in earthly affairs (Lk. 9:31; 15:7-10; 1 Tim. 5:21; 1 Pet. 1:12); and being taught wisdom by the church (Eph. 3:10; 1 Cor. 4:9).\n\nThey desire to look into the things of salvation (1 Pet. 1:10-12); observe us (1 Cor. 4:9); can cook (1 Ki. 19:5-7); wear garments (Jn. 20:12); appear unawares (Heb. 13:2); have been tested (1 Tim. 5:21; Job 4:18); dwell in heaven (Rev. 12:12; 13:6); stand before God (2 Chron. 18:18); and Christ is better than angels (Heb. 1:5–2:16).\n\n### Satan's Angels\n\nSatan's angels are made subject to Christ (1 Pet. 3:22); sinful and rebellious (Job 4:18; 2 Pet. 2:4; Jude 6-7; Rev. 12:7-9); evil (Ps. 78:49); to be punished (Mt. 24:41; Isa. 24:21-23; 25:7; Jude 6-7); to be cast out of heaven (Rev. 12:7-9); to fight against Christ at Armageddon (Rev. 12:7-9; 19:11-21; 20:1-3; Isa. 24:21-23; 25:7); and organized into principalities and powers (Eph. 1:21; 3:10; 6:10-17; Col. 3:10, 15; Rev. 12:7-12).\n\nThey deceive men (2 Cor. 11:14); oppose saints (Rom. 8:38; Eph. 6:10-18); originally fell with Lucifer (Isa. 14:12-14; Ezek. 28:11-17; Mt. 24:41; Rev. 12:7-12); and hell is prepared for them (Mt. 24:41).\n\n### Two Classes of Fallen Angels\n\nThere are two classes of fallen angels: those bound (Rev. 9:11-14; 11:7; 17:8; 2 Pet. 2:4; Jude 6-7) and those still loose with Satan who will be cast down to the earth in the middle of Daniel's Seventieth Week of the future Tribulation (Rev. 12:7-12; Eph. 6:10-17). The reason some of Satan's angels are now bound will be discussed in Lesson Eleven.\n\n### Appearances of Angels to Men\n\nAngels appeared to Abraham (Gen. 18:2; 22:11-18); Hagar (Gen. 16:7); Lot and the Sodomites (Gen. 19); Jacob (Gen. 28:12; 31:11-13; 32:1, 24-32); Moses (Exod. 3); Israel (Exod. 14:19; Judg. 2:1-4); Balaam (Num. 22:22-31); Joshua (5:15); Gideon (Judg. 6); Manoah (Judg. 13:6-20); David (2 Sam. 24:16-17); Elijah (1 Ki. 19:5); Elisha (2 Ki. 6:16-17); Daniel (Dan. 6:22; 8:16; 9:21; 10:5-21; 12:5-7); three Hebrew children (Dan. 3:25-28); Zechariah (2:3; 3:1-2; 4:1); Joseph (Mt. 1:20; 2:13-19); Mary (Lk. 1:26-38); Jesus (Mt. 4:11; Lk. 22:43); Zacharias (Lk. 1:20-38); shepherds (Lk. 2:9-14); women (Mt. 28:2-5); disciples (Acts 1:11); Peter and John (Acts 5:19); Phillip (Acts 8:26); Cornelius (Acts 10:3, 30-32); Peter (Acts 12:7-11); Paul (Acts 27:23); and John (Rev. 5:2; 7:11; 14:6-21).\n\n### Angels Have Real, Tangible Bodies\n\nAngels have real, tangible bodies with bodily parts like men. They've appeared to people in real bodies, and people couldn't tell them from other humans. Paul said, "Be not forgetful to entertain strangers: for thereby some have entertained angels unawares" (Heb. 13:2).\n\nThis couldn't be true — nor could scores of facts in the scriptures mentioned above — if all these spirit-beings weren't real and didn't have real bodies. The facts also prove they have souls and spirits, for they have feelings, passions, appetites, and desires (which constitute soul) and wills, knowledge, intellect, consciousness, and other faculties (which constitute spirit).\n\nSo all seraphims, cherubims, living creatures, archangels, angels, and other spirit-beings have bodies, souls, and spirits like men. If we can conceive that all these spirit-beings are real with personal bodies, souls, and spirits, then it's certainly conceivable that God the Father, God the Son, and God the Holy Spirit, as three spirit-beings, also have spirit-bodies, souls, and spirits.\n\n## VII. Devils or Unclean Spirits Called Demons\n\nThe subject of demons is very real according to the Bible. The word "demon" isn't actually found in Scripture, but it means evil spirit or devil. The word "devil" is used of Satan, the prince of demons (Mt. 9:34; 12:24). He's the chief evil spirit and the original source of evil in the universe.\n\nThe Greek word for devil used in connection with Satan is *diabolos*, meaning adversary, false accuser, slanderer, devil. It's translated "false accuser" and "slanderer" and is used of men in 1 Tim. 3:11; 2 Tim. 3:3; Titus 2:3. It's translated "devil" once while referring to Judas when he became an adversary of Christ (Jn. 6:70). In 34 other places it's used of Satan as the chief adversary of God and is translated "devil."\n\nIn the other 76 places where "devil" and "devils" are found, they refer to evil spirits or demons, and the word comes from two different Greek words — *daimonion* and *daimon*, meaning evil spirits or devils. There is only one devil, but there are many demons.\n\nHere's a crucial distinction: the devil has an angelic body and cannot enter bodily into anyone, but demons are disembodied spirits and don't seem able to operate in the material world except through possessing men and beasts who have bodies for them to work through. Think of it like this: the devil is like a general commanding from outside, while demons are like operatives who need a "vehicle" (a body) to do their work in the physical realm.\n\n### The Nature of Demons\n\nDemons are evil (Judg. 9:23; 1 Sam. 18:9-10); intelligent and wise (1 Tim. 4:1; 1 Ki. 22:22-24; Acts 16:16); powerful (Mk. 5:1-18); disembodied spirits (Rev. 16:13-16); not angels (Acts 23:8-9); not human, for they possess men and can be cast out (Mt. 10:7; Mk. 16:17); and are individuals (Mk. 16:9).\n\nThey have knowledge (Mt. 9:29; Lk. 4:41; Acts 19:15); faith (Jas. 2:19); feelings (Mt. 8:29; Mk. 5:7); fellowship (1 Cor. 10:20-21); doctrines (1 Tim. 4:1); wills (Mt. 12:43-45); miraculous powers (Rev. 16:13-16); intelligence (1 Tim. 4:1; 1 Jn. 4:1-6); emotions (Acts 8:7); desires (Mt. 8:28-31); and other soul and spirit faculties, as defined in Lesson Four, Point I, 9.\n\n### The Work of Demons\n\nDemons possess people and cause: dumbness and deafness (Mt. 9:32-33; Mk. 9:25); blindness (Mt. 12:22); grievous vexation (Mt. 15:22); lunacy and mania (Mt. 4:23-24; 17:14-21; Mk. 5:1-18); uncleanness (called unclean spirits 21 times, Lk. 4:36); supernatural strength (Mk. 5:1-18); suicide (Mt. 17:15; Jn. 10:10); fits (Mk. 9:20); lusts (Jn. 8:44; Eph. 2:1-3; 1 Jn. 2:15-17); counterfeit worship (Lev. 17:7; Deut. 32:17; 2 Chron. 11:15; Ps. 106:37; 1 Cor. 10:30; Rev. 9:20); error (1 Jn. 4:1-6; 1 Tim. 4:1); sickness and disease (Mt. 4:23-24; Acts 10:38); torments (Mt. 4:23-24; Mt. 15:22); deceptions (1 Tim. 4:1-2; 1 Jn. 4:1-6); lying (1 Ki. 22:21-24); enchantments and witchcraft (2 Chron. 33:6); heresies (1 Tim. 4:1); false doctrines (1 Tim. 4:1); wickedness (Lk. 11:26); fear (2 Tim. 1:7); worldliness (1 Jn. 2:15-17; 1 Cor. 2:12); bondage (Rom. 8:15); discord (Mt. 13:39; 1 Ki. 22:21-24); violence (Mt. 17:15); betrayals (Jn. 13:2; 1 Ki. 22:22-23); oppression (Acts 10:38); sin (Jn. 8:44; 1 Jn. 3:8); persecution (Rev. 2:10; 1 Pet. 5:8); jealousy (1 Sam. 16:14; 18:8-10); false prophecy (1 Sam. 18:8-10; 1 Ki. 22:21-24); and cause every evil they possibly can to man and God.\n\n### What Demons Can Do\n\nThey can teach (1 Tim. 4:1); steal (Mt. 13:19; Lk. 8:12); fight (Eph. 4:27; 6:10-18; 1 Pet. 5:8); get mad (Mt. 8:28; Rev. 12:12); tell fortunes (Lev. 20:27; Acts 16:16); be friendly (called familiar spirits 16 times, Lev. 20:6, 27); go out and come back into men as they will, unless cast out and rejected (Mt. 12:43-45); travel (1 Ki. 22:21-24; Mk. 5:7, 12); speak (Mk. 1:34; 5:12; Acts 8:7); imitate departed dead (2 Sam. 28:3-9; 1 Chron. 10:13; Isa. 8:19; Deut. 18:11); and do many things when in possession of bodies through whom they operate.\n\n### What Demons Are Called\n\nThey are called devils (Mk. 16:17); familiar spirits (Lev. 20:6); unclean spirits (Mk. 1:27); evil spirits (Lk. 7:21); seducing spirits (1 Tim. 4:1); and other things. They are made subject to Christ and believers by the Atonement, the name of Jesus, and the Holy Spirit (Mt. 8:16-17; 12:28; Mk. 16:17; Lk. 10:17; Acts 19:15).\n\nThousands of them can enter into and take possession of one man at the same time (Mk. 5:9). They must be discerned, tested, resisted, and rejected by believers (1 Jn. 4:1-6; 1 Cor. 12:10; Eph. 5:27; 6:10-18; 1 Pet. 5:8-9).\n\nThey possess more than ordinary intelligence (Mt. 8:29). Their rightful place is in the abyss (Lk. 8:31; Rev. 9:1-21). They have personality (Lk. 8:26-33); are disembodied (Mt. 12:43-45); are Satan's emissaries (Mt. 12:26-29); and are numerous (Mk. 5:9).\n\nThey enter into and control both men and beasts (Mk. 5:1-18) and seek embodiment (Mt. 12:43-45; Lk. 8:32). Demon possession and demon influence are different (Mt. 4:23-24 with 16:21-23). They know their fate (Mt. 8:31-32) and those who have power over them (Acts 19:13-17).\n\nThey fear God (Jas. 2:19); inflict physical maladies (Mt. 12:22; 17:15-18); war on saints (Eph. 6:10-18); and influence men (1 Tim. 4:1-5; 2 Pet. 2:10-12). All unbelievers are more or less possessed with them (Eph. 2:1-3). The only resources against them are prayer, bodily control, and the whole armour of God (Mt. 17:21; Eph. 6:10-18).\n\nThere are demon spirits for every sickness, unholy trait, and doctrinal error known. They must be cast out to get relief from them. Disease germs, which are closely allied with unclean spirits, are really living forms of corruption that come into men's bodies and bring them to death. Just as refuse breeds maggots, man in his fallen state of corruption breeds germs through unclean living and contact with corruptions in the fallen world. They are agents of Satan, corrupting the bodies of his victims.\n\nTraffic with demon spirits is forbidden in both Testaments (Lev. 19:31; 20:6; Deut. 18:10; Isa. 8:19-21; 1 Chron. 10:13-14; Lk. 4:41; Acts 16:16; 1 Tim. 4:1-5; 2 Pet. 2:1-3; 1 Jn. 4:1-6).\n\n## VIII. Other Spirit-Beings in Scripture\n\nScripture mentions many kinds of demon spirits, fallen angels, and other spirit-beings. It's certain they weren't created wicked. They were originally created perfect and sinless, and became fallen and unclean. Even the prince of demons is spoken of as being "perfect in thy ways from the day that thou wast created, till iniquity was found in thee" (Ezek. 28:11-17).\n\nGod could not and did not create anything sinful. Everything in the spirit and human realms that is wicked and rebellious has become that way because of sin and free choice.\n\nThe fallen angels, demons, and those mentioned below are all rebels connected with planet earth. They sinned in the original rebellion under Lucifer, or they wouldn't be confined in prisons under the earth or be operating on earth now against God\n\n---\n\nScripture doesn’t give us a frightening portrait of Satan to paralyze us — it gives us one to prepare us. You can’t guard against an enemy you’ve convinced yourself doesn’t exist, or that you’ve reduced to a cartoon. So here’s the question worth facing: In what area of your life are you currently suffering — a pattern of failure, a persistent temptation, an unexplained oppression — that you’ve been treating as a personality flaw or circumstance, when Scripture would call it spiritual warfare?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgbd001710b8bdid5dt2	cmq76cgb9001110b8mkvodphm	Supplement 6 — For Lessons 11 & 12	SUPPLEMENT	600	2	\N	t	![Supplement 6 — For Lessons 11 & 12](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsUClD9V6edALvbYMWXfx7ZoQswlOpr26nuJ1t)\n\n## Supplement 6 — For Lessons 11 & 12: Authority and Armor\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**Authority** — The delegated power and right given to believers through their union with Christ.\n\n**Armor of God** — The spiritual equipment described in Ephesians 6 that enables believers to stand against demonic attack.\n\n**The Name of Jesus** — The representation of Christ's Person and authority; demons are subject to it.\n\n**The Blood of the Lamb** — The redemptive work of Christ that cancels every legal claim of Satan.\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> Luke 10:19 — "Behold, I give unto you power to tread on serpents and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy: and nothing shall by any means hurt you."\n\n> Ephesians 6:11 — "Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil."\n\n> Philippians 2:10 — "That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth."\n\n---\n\n### The Armor at a Glance\n\n| Piece | Function | Scriptural Counterpart |\n|-------|----------|----------------------|\n| Belt of Truth | Holds everything together; exposes lies | Integrity, honesty |\n| Breastplate of Righteousness | Protects the heart from accusation | Holiness, obedience |\n| Shoes of the Gospel of Peace | Steady footing in battle | Assurance of salvation |\n| Shield of Faith | Extinguishes attacks | Active trust in God |\n| Helmet of Salvation | Guards the mind | Assurance, hope |\n| Sword of the Spirit | Offensive weapon | The Word of God |\n\n---\n\n### Questions for Reflection\n\n1. Why does Paul command us to "put on" the armor rather than simply possess it? What does this say about daily spiritual discipline?\n\n2. What is the difference between authority and power? Why is authority more important in spiritual warfare?\n\n3. How does knowing you are "seated with Christ in heavenly places" change your perspective on spiritual battles?\n\n4. The sword of the Spirit is the only offensive weapon. How well do you know your sword? What would it look like to study Scripture specifically for warfare?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgaq000f10b84gujcy39	cmq76cgaj000910b8olia8etv	Supplement 2 — For Lessons 3 & 4	SUPPLEMENT	600	2	\N	t	![Supplement 2 — For Lessons 3 & 4](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsNjfndctUgPsHDqdkrK1w9XGRYBoiJIFQn0bt)\n\n## Supplement 2 — For Lessons 3 & 4: Satan and the Fallen Host\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**Satan** — Hebrew for "adversary" or "accuser"; the personal name of the fallen angel Lucifer after his rebellion.\n\n**Devil** — Greek *diabolos*, meaning "slanderer"; emphasizes Satan's role as the accuser of believers.\n\n**Principalities** — High-ranking demons with territorial authority over nations and regions.\n\n**Powers** — Demonic beings with delegated authority to execute specific evil purposes.\n\n**Watchers** — A term from Jewish tradition (Genesis 6, Enoch, Daniel) for angels who descended to earth and corrupted humanity.\n\n**Nephilim** — The offspring of fallen angels and human women, described as "giants" and "mighty men."\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> Revelation 12:9 — "And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world."\n\n> Ephesians 6:12 — "For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world."\n\n> 2 Corinthians 11:14 — "And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light."\n\n---\n\n### The Names of Satan in Scripture\n\n| Name | Meaning | Reference |\n|------|---------|-----------|\n| Lucifer | Light-bearer | Isaiah 14:12 |\n| Satan | Adversary, accuser | Job 1:6 |\n| Devil | Slanderer | Matthew 4:1 |\n| Serpent | Deceiver | Genesis 3:1 |\n| Dragon | Destroyer | Revelation 12:3 |\n| Prince of this world | Usurped ruler | John 12:31 |\n| God of this world | False deity | 2 Corinthians 4:4 |\n| Prince of devils | Commander of demons | Matthew 12:24 |\n| The wicked one | Evil personified | 1 John 5:18 |\n| Belial | Worthlessness | 2 Corinthians 6:15 |\n| Beelzebub | Lord of the flies | Matthew 12:24 |\n\n---\n\n### Questions for Reflection\n\n1. Why does Scripture give Satan so many different names? What does each reveal about his methods?\n\n2. Satan disguises himself as an angel of light. How can believers discern between genuine spiritual experiences and demonic counterfeits?\n\n3. What does it mean that demons operate in hierarchical ranks? How does this affect the strategy of spiritual warfare?\n\n4. The Book of Enoch describes Watchers who descended to earth. How does Jude's confirmation of this tradition help us understand the severity of certain sins?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgba001310b8yomi1tl9	cmq76cgb9001110b8mkvodphm	Lesson 16 — The Believer's Authority in Christ	READING	900	0	\N	t	![Lesson 16 — The Believer's Authority in Christ](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsPlOwEko536itGQmsLn2KwlakR9vFryYAfXZB)\n\n## The Believer's Authority in Christ\n\nThe single most important truth in spiritual warfare is this: **the believer in Jesus Christ possesses absolute authority over demons**. This authority is not earned, learned, or achieved; it is received by grace through faith in the finished work of Christ.\n\n### The Source of Authority\n\nWhen Jesus commissioned His disciples, He gave them authority:\n\n> Luke 10:19 — "Behold, I give unto you power to tread on serpents and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy: and nothing shall by any means hurt you."\n\nThis authority is inherent in the Name of Jesus. When Peter healed the lame man, he declared:\n\n> Acts 3:6 — "Silver and gold have I none; but such as I have give I thee: In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth rise up and walk."\n\nThe Name is not a magic formula; it is the representation of the Person. To act in the Name of Jesus is to act with His authority, His backing, and His power. Demons do not fear the Christian; they fear Christ in the Christian.\n\n### The Believer's Position\n\nPaul describes the believer's exalted position:\n\n> Ephesians 2:6 — "And hath raised us up together, and made us sit together in heavenly places in Christ Jesus."\n\nWhen a believer is born again, they are spiritually seated with Christ in heavenly places — far above all principality and power. The Christian is not fighting for victory; they are fighting from victory. The battle is not to gain authority but to exercise the authority already given.\n\n### Keys to Exercising Authority\n\n**Faith** — Authority works through faith. The disciples failed to cast out a demon because of unbelief (Matthew 17:20). When faith is present, even mustard-seed sized, mountains move.\n\n**The Word of God** — Jesus defeated Satan's temptations with Scripture: "It is written." The Word of God is the sword of the Spirit — the only offensive weapon in the armor of God.\n\n**The Blood of Jesus** — Revelation declares that believers overcome the accuser "by the blood of the Lamb, and by the word of their testimony" (Revelation 12:11). The blood speaks of substitution, redemption, and the legal cancellation of every claim Satan had.\n\n**The Holy Spirit** — Authority is exercised in partnership with the Holy Spirit. It is the Spirit who gives power, direction, and confirmation. To attempt spiritual warfare without the Spirit's leading is to operate in the flesh.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgac000310b8bn16q37u	cmq76cga9000110b8juoxpkya	Lesson 1 — What Are Demons? The Biblical View	READING	900	0	\N	t	![Lesson 1 — What Are Demons? The Biblical View](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsI4UQqODFm5fHMlhCe2Nngyo6VzaWuJEO4Dj7)\n\n## What Are Demons? — The Biblical View\n\nDemons are not figments of imagination, symbols of psychological struggle, or metaphors for evil in the abstract. The Bible presents them as **real, personal, intelligent spiritual beings** who actively oppose the purposes of God and seek the destruction of human souls.\n\n### The Nature of Demons\n\nScripture consistently describes demons as **unclean spirits** (Matthew 10:1), **evil spirits** (Luke 7:21), and **familiar spirits** (Leviticus 20:6). They are not merely impersonal forces but possess personality, will, intellect, and emotion. They know who Jesus is and tremble at His name (James 2:19). They speak, reason, deceive, and strategize.\n\nDemons are **incorporeal** — they have no physical body — yet they can produce physical effects. They cause disease (Matthew 9:33), insanity (Mark 5:1-20), muteness (Matthew 9:32), and seizures (Mark 9:17-29). Their power operates in the spiritual realm but manifests visibly in the material world.\n\n### Where Did Demons Come From?\n\nThe Bible does not explicitly state the origin of demons, but the weight of both Scripture and the theological tradition points to a single answer: **demons are fallen angels**. When Lucifer rebelled against God, he persuaded a multitude of angels to join him. These fallen spirits became the demons that now roam the earth, seeking whom they may devour (1 Peter 5:8).\n\n> Ezekiel 28:17 — "Thine heart was lifted up because of thy beauty, thou hast corrupted thy wisdom by reason of thy brightness."\n\nThe Book of Revelation records that Satan drew **a third of the stars of heaven** with him in his fall (Revelation 12:4). This vast number — perhaps hundreds of millions — explains the ubiquity of demonic activity and the persistence of evil across every culture and age.\n\n### Demonic Activity in the Biblical Narrative\n\nFrom Genesis to Revelation, demons appear as active agents of destruction. In the Old Testament, they are associated with idol worship (Deuteronomy 32:17, Psalm 106:37). In the Gospels, they are the primary adversaries Jesus confronts in His ministry — He casts them out with a word, demonstrating His absolute authority.\n\n> Mark 1:34 — "And he healed many that were sick of divers diseases, and cast out many devils; and suffered not the devils to speak, because they knew him."\n\nThe apostles continued this ministry. Philip preached in Samaria, and unclean spirits, crying with loud voice, came out of many (Acts 8:7). Paul cast a spirit of divination out of a young woman in Philippi (Acts 16:18). The early Church understood demons as real, present, and subject to the authority of Christ.\n\n### The Central Truth\n\nDemons are not equal and opposite powers to God. They are **created beings who rebelled**, and their rebellion is temporary. Their fate is sealed: the lake of fire awaits them (Revelation 20:10). Until that day, they rage against God and His people — but their defeat is certain.	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk44k000cewhjxjlkzldl	cmnknk44i0001ewhju56drbw5	Lesson 7 — The Dispensation of Angels	READING	4787	10	\N	t	Before humanity existed, the earth had already had one civilization. Angels ruled it. A perfect being called Lucifer sat on its throne. Scripture is not ambiguous about this — it's just inconvenient for the tidy story many people prefer, where Genesis 1:1 is the starting gun and everything before it is empty silence.\n\nLast time we established who Satan is and what the spirit world looks like. Now we step further back: what was the original dispensation — the first age of moral creatures on this earth — before Adam ever drew breath?\n\n![Lesson 7 — The Dispensation of Angels](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os8U65j9JwQn65F0NSyXfv2WGAqVjL7icrDpPI)\n\n### I. The Antechaotic Age—The Dispensation of Angels\n\nLet's explore a fascinating period that many people have never heard of: the Antechaotic Age. This era stretched from the original creation of the heavens and earth to the rebellion and overthrow of the first *kosmos*, or social order, on our planet.\n\nThink of it like this: there was a "before" to our "before." This was a dateless period between Gen. 1:1—when the earth was finished and inhabited in the beginning—and Gen. 1:2, when the earth was first flooded, destroying all life. We're talking about that unknown span of time when the earth existed in its first perfect state, ruled by Lucifer before his rebellion caused the catastrophic flood described in Gen. 1:2.\n\nIn Ezek. 28:11-17, we read of Lucifer: "Thou wast perfect in thy ways from the day that thou wast created, till iniquity was found in thee." This tells us plainly that there was a period of perfection and sinlessness on earth before its curse and chaotic state. That's why we call this period the Antechaotic Age.\n\nDuring this age, spirit beings ruled the earth and other planets—so we might call it the "Dispensation of Angels." This administration was evidently a moral or probationary period designed to test the angels before trusting them with eternal responsibilities. The word "dispensation" means a moral or probationary period in which God tests free moral agents according to a fixed standard of conduct.\n\nHere's something important to understand: all spirit beings must be tested, just like human free moral agents, to see if they will obey God before being trusted with higher and eternal responsibility. These angels were fresh from God's creative hand, made with free wills, capable of choosing whether to obey or not.\n\nThey had to learn through experience whether they would obey God. They had to learn that God was just and holy in all His ways—that He could and should be trusted even in matters that couldn't be fully explained to them all at once. They needed to discover that God was the Supreme Moral Governor of the universe, and that all creatures should dedicate themselves to the same goal God Himself was dedicated to: the highest good of the universe and everyone in it.\n\nThey had to prove themselves true to God to receive rewards for obedience. They had to learn that God's Word was absolutely reliable—including His warnings about penalties for disobedience.\n\nGod's dealings with spirit beings served the same purpose as His dealings with humans. These purposes are fully explained in Lesson One, Point VII, and I'd encourage you to review that section to see more clearly what God was doing with spirit beings during this period.\n\nIf Lucifer and the other spirit beings had remained true to God, there would have been no universal curse on the earth. There would have been no need for the re-creation of the atmospheric heavens, the earth, and life on our planet, as recorded in Gen. 1:3–2:25. In that case, man and the present animals on earth would never have been created!\n\nThe Bible's record of the first curse on earth and the cancellation of the angels' administration should make present-day rebels fear God. Peter gives us this sobering warning: "Whose judgment now for a long time lingereth not, and their damnation slumbereth not. For if God spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness, to be reserved unto judgment; and spared not the old world but saved Noah the eighth person, a preacher of righteousness, bringing in the flood upon the world of the ungodly; and turning the cities of Sodom and Gomorrah into ashes condemned them with an overthrow, making them an example unto those that should live ungodly; and delivered just Lot, vexed with the filthy conversation of the wicked . . . The Lord knoweth how to deliver the godly out of temptations, and to reserve the unjust unto the day of judgment to be punished" (2 Pet. 2:4-9).\n\nJude also speaks of God's judgment upon both angels and men in the past for rebellion (Jude 5-7).\n\nPaul gives us the example of how God cut off Israel because of rebellion and unbelief, warning the Gentiles to "take heed lest He spare not thee" (Rom. 11:1-26). He also describes how the Gentile world didn't appreciate the knowledge of God, becoming vain in their imaginations and stubborn in their rebellion until God gave them over to vile affections to destroy themselves (Rom. 1:16-32).\n\nWe could give many more examples of God's judgment upon men in various ages—and we will as we continue our study. But these are enough to show why God had to deal with the angelic administrators of the earth long before Adam ever walked the planet.\n\nThe "ways" in which Lucifer was perfect until iniquity was found in him prove that angels were placed under certain restrictions for testing purposes. Think of it like quality testing in manufacturing—tests are absolutely necessary for anything that's made to discover if it will perform as designed. How much more true this is for free moral agents capable of making voluntary moral choices! Review Lesson One, Point VII, 1, to understand why such moral tests are necessary for beings with free wills.\n\nWhat would be the point of creating free wills if there were no laws to obey—no restrictions to guide them in their relationships with other creatures? Why create beings capable of voluntary obedience without explaining right from wrong so they can make their choice?\n\nEven of the Sinless One, Scripture says: "Though he were a Son, yet learned he obedience by the things which he suffered; and being made perfect, he became the author of eternal salvation unto all them that obey him" (Heb. 5:7-10).\n\nSo here's an important truth: sinless creatures can learn obedience to the right ways without ever committing sin. They can learn by experience how to know God and walk in His ways without experiencing sin at all. This is exactly what happened with Jesus: "Who did no sin, neither was guile found in his mouth" (1 Pet. 2:21-25; Heb. 2:14-18; 4:14-16; 5:7-10).\n\nNeither angels nor men had to sin in order to learn obedience and be tested. The old theory that sin is necessary for free moral agents to learn obedience simply isn't true. In the eternal future, when humans multiply forever in the New Earth, new generations will be true to God from childhood, learning all necessary obedience without ever committing sin (Rev. 21:1-7).\n\nThere are some of the richest studies awaiting you in the coming lessons—truths that will be priceless to you, your friends, and loved ones. Whatever you do, don't miss learning all of God's plan for your life!\n\nIf it was necessary to test human free wills and even the Son of God, it certainly was necessary to test spirit beings for the same purpose. How was God to know which spirit beings would remain true and which would not, until they were all tested and proven faithful or unfaithful?\n\nThey couldn't have been tested without definite tests and laws to obey. Naturally, not all free wills would choose the same things or exercise their creative powers of free choice in the same way or with the same degree of willful obedience or disobedience. This has been demonstrated by free wills ever since they were created. You know this from your own experience—you can make free and voluntary choices about any detail of life.\n\nIt wasn't until Adam and Eve actually sinned that God knew the full results of their test (Gen. 3). It wasn't until humanity proved such a failure before the flood that God regretted having made them (Gen. 6:5-7). It wasn't until God came down to see the rebellion of those after the flood—Sodom, Gomorrah, and others—that God took action (Gen. 11:1-9; 18:21).\n\nSo it is with every free moral agent in every period. Each one has to be tried and purged of any possibility of falling before God places them in an eternal state with eternal responsibility.\n\nIn God's moral government, there must be laws for all creatures. Each creature must be assigned some particular responsibility so the universe runs in perfect harmony. God couldn't rule free wills if each was free to do whatever they pleased. No government could survive with such a plan—this is obvious to anyone living in any kind of society.\n\nIt's similar to how any project works in human affairs: each person must do something and be responsible for something if anything is to be accomplished. This is true from the smallest to the greatest undertaking. The greater the project, the greater the responsibility for those trusted with its completion. The greater the project, the greater the need for many people to be responsible for some part of the plan.\n\nHow much more true would this be in running the vast universe? God is methodical in everything and has fixed laws governing every detail. Each free will is given a part in carrying out God's mutual plan for all concerned. God has a plan for the life and work of every creature and a purpose for every material thing created.\n\nEvery planet, sun, moon, and star must run in its own creative orbit, each one on time—or the entire planetary system would become undependable. Times and seasons would be thrown into chaos, and all life on every planet would soon be destroyed. So it is with the moral creation.\n\nGod did not make the universe for chaos and ruin, nor did He create individuals to be lawless, irresponsible creatures who could stop governmental function or do whatever they please. There must be order and someone to maintain it. There must be one law for all to ensure justice for all. There must be voluntary and mutual cooperation from each free will for everyone to fit into God's plan for the highest good of all.\n\nEach creature must be held responsible for their own actions—rewarded for obedience or punished for disobedience—or no government can properly function for everyone's good. If God is to maintain the respect and willing obedience of all creatures, He must be fair and just to all, meting out punishments for sin and distributing rewards for obedience.\n\nGovernment by rewards and penalties for all alike is the only just form of government—and the only one that can last forever. When government becomes corrupt, showing favoritism to some and injustice to others, it ceases to fulfill its purpose. This leads to rebellion and eventual overthrow.\n\nIf rebels against proper, just government were allowed to openly rebel without punishment, there would be no incentive for others to remain true and support the government. It would soon collapse. So to be just, God is forced by circumstances to deal with rebels and put down rebellion if He is to maintain His government for the highest good of all. He is equally obligated to reward the faithful and preserve just government for them.\n\nOn these grounds, every child of God can claim the rewards and benefits promised in Scripture. Every child of God can have perfect health, freedom from want and pain, happiness, and untold blessings if they will simply obey the laws of rewards and blessings. We'll address these laws in some measure in each lesson, with special lessons dedicated to them later. First, we need a general understanding of God's dealings with free moral agents before studying His specific plan for us today.\n\nThe Bible teaches that one-third of the angels proved untrue, as did all the subjects of the first social order on earth over whom Lucifer ruled before Adam. We don't know exactly how many rulers and subjects of other planets rebelled, but Scripture does reveal the following:\n\n- That there are thrones and kingdoms in the heavens as well as on the earth, visible and invisible (Col. 1:15-18).\n- That God charged some of His angels with folly (Job 4:18).\n- That over one-third of God's angels rebelled with Lucifer (Rev. 12:3-12; Mt. 25:41).\n- That redeemed human beings are to judge (rule) angels (1 Cor. 6:3).\n- That women are not to cut their hair, but keep it long as a sign of subjection to their own husbands so that angels will have good examples to be in subjection to God (1 Cor. 11:10).\n- That the purpose of the Millennial reign of Christ is to "gather in one all things in Christ, both which are in heaven, and which are on earth; even in him" (Eph. 1:10).\n- To rid the earth of all rebels (1 Cor. 15:24-28).\n- That all rebels of every kind and every realm will have to finally acknowledge that Jesus Christ is Lord to the glory of God the Father (Phil. 2:9-11).\n- That it is Christ's work to reconcile both the things in heaven and the things in earth (Eph. 1:10; Col. 1:20).\n- That Christ has already triumphed over the rebels and is exalted above all other angelic rulers and powers far above all heavens (Eph. 1:21; 6:10-18; Col. 2:14-17; 1 Pet. 3:22).\n- That Christ is waiting now until the completion of man's probationary test in this age before He comes down from heaven to put down all rebellion on earth (Acts 3:19-21; 1 Cor. 15:24-28; 2 Thess. 1:7-10; Rev. 19:11–20:3; Zech. 14:1-21).\n- That God is now schooling the principalities and powers in heavenly places in His manifold wisdom by making an example of submission by an actual demonstration of the Church (Eph. 3:1-11; 1 Cor. 4:9; 11:10).\n- That some rebel angels are now bound in hell awaiting judgment (2 Pet. 2:4; Jude 6-7).\n- That one-third of God's angels who rebelled are now still loose with Satan carrying on rebellion against God (Rev. 12:3-12; Dan. 10:13-21; Eph. 6:10-18).\n- That they will be defeated in the middle of the last 7 years of this age and will be cast down to the earth for 1,260 days and then they will be cast into the pit for a thousand years (Rev. 12:3-14; 20:1-3; Isa. 24:21-23).\n- That they will be liberated for a little season at the end of the Millennium to deceive men living on the earth at that time, and then they will meet their final defeat and be cast into the Lake of Fire which is prepared for them (Rev. 20:7-10; Mt. 25:41; Isa. 24:21-23).\n\nThese simple biblical facts help us understand the outcome of the angelic administration of the earth and the probationary period of earth creatures before the flood of Gen. 1:2.\n\nWe don't know what means of reconciliation God offered to the spirit beings and the first rebels on earth, but there must have been such means. God has always dealt with rebels in mercy and longsuffering—it's His nature. It would be contrary to His very Being to cut them off without some means of reconciliation, without giving them a chance to lay down their arms of rebellion.\n\nRemember that spirit beings are immortal in body, soul, and spirit. They're not subject to physical death—the separation of the inner person from the body (Jas. 2:26)—so the penalty they faced couldn't have been the same as what humans face in this respect. However, they will be tormented in literal fire and brimstone forever, just as unrepentant humans will be (Mt. 25:41; Jude 6-7; Rev. 20:10).\n\nIt's also important to remember what the Bible is and isn't. It's not a book that deals specifically with the administration of the angels, their rebellion, their means of reconciliation (if any), their former relationship to God, or the degrees of punishment they'll suffer. The Bible is a book revealing the origin of all things, including angels and humans, but it primarily deals with humanity—our rebellion and our future in God's plan.\n\nAs we've seen above and in Lesson Six, Scripture contains hundreds of references to spirit beings: their origin, fall, present work, future destiny, and much more. These things are revealed because of their role in furthering God's plan for humanity.\n\n### II. The Kingdom of God over All—God All-in-All\n\nAfter the original creation of the heavens and the earth and all things in them, as we saw in Lesson Five, the kingdom of God was universal. God was all-in-all, with not one creature lifting a finger in rebellion against Him.\n\nEveryone was willingly subject to His sovereign will, walking in perfect obedience to God and His moral law. Each ruler and each subject of every kingdom throughout the universe was faithful in personal responsibility and dedicated to the highest good of all beings and the universe itself.\n\nNo free moral agent acted from selfishness or apart from the Creator's will. Everything was in harmony and perfection.\n\nHow long this condition lasted is unknown, and all speculation is useless. In the following sections, we'll prove that rebellion was started by the angelic ruler of the earth, who conceived the idea and boldly attempted to dethrone God and become the supreme ruler of the universe.\n\nFrom this point forward, the Bible reveals that the earth has been made perfect and inhabited two times, and that there have been two universal rebellions on earth as well as two sinful careers. It records two past curses on the earth and reveals that the earth will be made new one more time, that righteousness will dwell on earth forever, and that God will become all-in-all again—just as He was before rebellion was started by Lucifer and Adam (1 Cor. 15:24-28; Rev. 21–22; 2 Pet. 3:13; Isa. 65:17; 66:22-24).\n\n## Earth's First Sinful Career\n\n(Gen. 1:2; Isa 14:1-14; Jer. 4:23-26; Ezek. 28:11-17; 2 Pet. 3:5-6)\n\n### III. Moses' Teaching on the Overthrow of the Pre-Adamite World\n\nIn Gen. 1:2, we learn that the earth was already in existence before the Spirit of God began to move (brood) upon the face of the waters covering the earth. The conjunction "and" connects about 200 separate acts of God in Gen. 1 and 2. These acts are all equally independent and important.\n\nVerse 2 is as independent of verse 1 as all other separate acts in these two chapters. In verse 1, we have the original creation of the heavens and the earth. In verse 2, we have the originally perfect earth made chaotic and flooded with water, which destroyed all life.\n\nThe word "was" in verse 2 comes from the Hebrew *hayah*, which is a verb meaning "to become," not "to be." It's translated *became* 67 times (Gen. 2:7; 19:26; 20:12; 24:67; Exod. 4:3-4; Num. 12:10; etc.); *becomes* (1 Chron. 17:22; Ezek. 16:8); *came* and *came to pass* 505 times (Gen. 4:3; 6:1, 4; 11:2, 5; etc.); *become* 66 times (Gen. 3:22; 18:18; 48:19; etc.); *come* and *come to pass* 131 times (Gen. 4:14; 6:13, 18-20; 27:40; etc.); and many times *be* in the sense of become (Gen. 1:3, 6, 9, 14; 3:5; etc.).\n\nThe phrase "without form" comes from the Hebrew *tohu*, meaning waste, desolation, or confusion. It's translated *waste* (Deut. 32:10); *without form* (Gen. 1:2; Jer. 4:23); *vain* (Isa. 45:18; 1 Sam. 12:21); *confusion* (Isa. 24:10; 34:11; 41:29); *empty* (Job 26:7); *vanity* (Isa. 40:17, 23; 44:9; 59:4); *nothing* (Job 6:18; Isa. 40:17); and *wilderness* (Job 12:24; Ps. 107:40).\n\nFrom these passages, you can see what the word really means and what condition the earth was in during Gen. 1:2. God did not originally create the earth in such a waste and ruined state. Isa. 45:18 explicitly states that God did not create the earth *tohu* (vain or desolate)—yet in Gen. 1:2, the earth was *tohu*.\n\nIf the earth wasn't originally created desolate, then it must have been created, inhabited, and later *became* desolate. Even the English verb "was" indicates it had to become desolate before it could be desolate.\n\nThe Hebrew word for "void" is *bohu*, meaning empty, ruin, or void. It's translated *void* (Gen. 1:2; Jer. 4:23) and *emptiness* (Isa. 34:11). The Hebrew phrase *tohu va bohu* (waste and ruin, or desolate and empty) describes the chaotic condition of the earth since "the beginning" and before the six days of reconstruction in Gen. 1:3–2:25.\n\nGod did not create the earth as a ruin or waste. It became so because of sin, as we'll see.\n\nWe can read Gen. 1:1-2 literally this way: "In the beginning [by periods, ages] God created the heavens and the earth. And the earth became waste and ruin [desolate and empty]; and darkness was upon the face of the deep [the flood]. And the Spirit of God moved [brooded] upon the face of the waters."\n\nIn these verses we have the whole span of the creative ages—from all the original creation of the heavens and earth and everything in them, through to the six days of restoring the earth to a habitable state. The original creations include the sun, moon, and stars, as proven in Lesson Five.\n\nIn these two verses alone we find these facts: that in the dateless past God created the heavens (including the sun, moon, and stars) and then the earth; that the heavens were created before the earth; that the heavens, the earth, the waters, and the darkness were all created before the Spirit began to brood over the waters; and that these things were already in existence before the first of the six days—proving they were not created in any one of those days.\n\nHow long the earth was waste and ruin, desolate and empty, since its original habitation is unknown. How long it existed and was inhabited before it became desolate and empty is unknown. But *why* and *when* it was cursed and became desolate and empty is known and clearly revealed in Scripture, as we'll see below.\n\nIn Scripture, all cases of obscuring the sun and bringing consequent darkness, and all cases of floods, are the result of judgment—never an act of creation—unless Gen. 1:2 is an exception. But we have no authority to believe it is. Why couldn't Gen. 1:2 be the result of a curse, like all other floods and darkness on earth revealed in Scripture (Gen. 6–8; Exod. 10:21-23; Isa. 5:30; 13:10; Jer. 4:23-26; Amos 5:18-20; Zeph. 1:15; Joel 2:30–3:16; Mt. 8:12; 9:2; 16:10)?\n\nThe fact that Moses, by inspiration, said God told Adam to multiply and *replenish* the earth proves there was a social system on earth before Adam. After all, you can't *re*plenish something that had never been plenished before!\n\nSome argue that the Hebrew word for "replenish" means *fill*, not *refill*, but this proves nothing. An examination of all places where the word is used disproves this argument. Try making "replenish" mean just "plenish" in Gen. 9:1; Isa. 2:6; 23:2; Jer. 31:25; Ezek. 26:2; 27:25, and note the results.\n\nWhere the Hebrew *mala* is translated "fill," it doesn't mean the thing referred to had never been filled before. For example, when Joseph commanded his brethren to "fill their sacks," does this mean those sacks had never been filled before? They had no doubt been filled many times (Gen. 42:25; 44:1; 1 Ki. 18:33; Hag. 2:7; etc.).\n\nTo say, "Fill that glass with water," doesn't prove it had never been filled before. But to say, "Refill that glass with water" proves it had been filled before. When God told Noah, "Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth" (Gen. 9:1), it's clear the earth had been filled or "plenished" before. So why not believe God meant the same thing when He said it to Adam?\n\nThe same Hebrew statement is found in both passages (Gen. 1:28; 9:1), and it's translated exactly the same in English—so would it be wrong to believe it means the same thing? If the earth had been "plenished" before Adam, then it was overthrown by judgment before the six days, as shown in Gen. 1:2.\n\n### IV. Isaiah's Teaching on the Overthrow of the Pre-Adamite World\n\nIn Isa. 14:12-14, we have conclusive proof that Lucifer ruled the earth before Adam's days. This couldn't have happened since Adam—because Lucifer was already a fallen creature before Adam was created. In Adam's day, Satan regained dominion of the earth and has been the prince of this world ever since.\n\nIn this passage, both Satan and the king of Babylon are in view. This is what's known as the law of double reference—a visible person is immediately addressed while at the same time an invisible person, who is using the visible person as a tool to hinder God's plan, is also addressed.\n\nPicture it this way: when Jesus said to Peter, "Get thee behind me, Satan: for thou art an offense to me: for thou savourest not the things that be of God, but those that be of men" (Mt. 16:23), He didn't mean Peter was the personal devil. Rather, Peter was being used as Satan's tool to keep Christ from reaching the cross. Hence, both Peter and Satan are addressed in that statement.\n\nTo understand such passages, understand that the part that can refer to an earthly person refers to a human, while the part that cannot possibly refer to an earthly person refers to the invisible person also addressed.\n\nIn Isa. 14:12-14, we find statements that cannot possibly be made of any earthly king of Babylon. This passage is almost universally accepted as referring to Satan's fall. Let's quote it and examine the facts:\n\n"How art thou fallen from heaven, O Lucifer, son of the morning! how art thou cut down to the ground, which didst weaken the nations! For thou hast said in thine heart, I will ascend into heaven, I will exalt my throne above the stars of God: I will sit also upon the mount of the congregation, in the sides of the north: I will ascend above the heights of the clouds; I will be like the most High."\n\nNote these facts about Satan:\n\n> 1. That his name is Lucifer.\n\n> 2. That he was a son of the morning, and therefore, no earthly man.\n\n> 3. That he fell from heaven. This could never be spoken of a man. Satan is the only person in all Scripture who is spoken of as falling from heaven (Lk. 10:18).\n\n> 4. That he was cut down to the ground in his fall.\n\n> 5. That he had weakened nations on earth.\n\n> 6. That he was exalted in his heart.\n\n> 7. That he invaded heaven, where God rules.\n\n> 8. That he was a king, for he had a throne and subjects over whom he ruled.\n\n> 9. That he wanted to exalt his kingdom above the clouds, stars, and into heaven itself to dethrone God.\n\n> 10. That he wanted to be worshipped in the congregation of God (Ps. 72:2; 82:1; Isa. 6:1).\n\n> 11. That he led a rebellion against God but was defeated.\n\n> 12. That his kingdom was on earth, or he never could have tried to ascend above the clouds, stars, and into heaven. When a kingdom is located under the clouds it has to be on the earth, for one can stand on certain parts of the earth and still be above clouds.\n\n> 13. That the ground, clouds, stars, and heaven were already created.\n\n> 14. That it had to be before Adam, for this was not the position of Lucifer when he was in Adam's Eden. Adam had dominion at that time. He had no kingdom on earth at the time of Adam and has not had thereafter, in the sense of a visible, personal rule on earth. He has only ruled through others since Adam's day, so this must refer to a time before Adam.\n\n> 15. That he was not in heaven when he rebelled, or else he could not have desired to ascend into heaven. He was under the stars, or he could not have desired to be exalted above the stars. He was under the clouds, or he could not have desired to ascend above them.\n\n> 16. That God's throne is located in the north part of the universe (Ps. 75:6-7).\n\nThis passage proves the location of Satan's original kingdom and the time of his fall. His kingdom was on earth, and his fall occurred before Adam.\n\nIn Col. 1:15-18, we read of Christ creating thrones, dominions, principalities, and powers in heaven and on earth. They were located somewhere in the heavens and on the earth. Lucifer was given a kingdom here on earth, as proven by the passages cited above.\n\nHis own subjects were earthly creatures of various kinds, all destroyed when the flood of Gen. 1:2 came upon the earth. God created the earth to be inhabited by earthly creatures (Isa. 45:18). They are called "nations" in the above passage.\n\nThe demons who are now Satan's emissaries could be the spirits of the pre-Adamites. At any rate, they're not part of the creation at the time of Adam. Thus, Isaiah teaches that the earth was inhabited before Adam and was ruled by Lucifer, whose kingdom was overthrown when he rebelled.\n\n### V. Ezekiel's Teaching on the Overthrow of the Pre-Adamite World\n\nIn Ezek. 28:11-17, we have another description of Lucifer before he fell—his position on earth and the cause of his rebellion. This passage is another example of the law of double reference explained in Point IV. The earthly man addressed was the king of Tyre (see Josephus, *Apion* Book I, 21).\n\nLet's quote this passage and examine the main facts concerning Satan:\n\n"Thus saith the Lord GOD; Thou sealest up the sum, full of wisdom, and perfect in beauty. Thou hast been in Eden the garden of God; every precious stone was thy covering, the sardius, topaz, and the diamond, the beryl, the onyx, and the jasper, the sapphire, the emerald, and the carbuncle, and gold: the workmanship of thy tabrets and of thy pipes was prepared in thee in the day that thou wast created. Thou art the anointed cherub that covereth; and I have set thee so: thou wast upon the holy mountain of God; thou hast walked up and down in the midst of the stones of fire. Thou wast perfect in thy ways from the day that thou wast created, till iniquity was found in thee. By the multitude of thy merchandise they have filled the midst of thee with violence, and thou hast sinned: therefore I will cast thee as profane out of the mountain of God: and I will destroy thee, O covering cherub, from the midst of the stones of fire. Thine heart was lifted up because of thy beauty, thou hast corrupted thy wisdom by reason of thy brightness: I will cast thee to the ground, I will lay thee before kings, that they may behold thee. Thou hast defiled thy sanctuaries by the multitude of thine iniquities, by the iniquity of thy traffick; therefore will I bring forth a fire from the midst of thee, it shall devour thee, and I will bring thee to ashes upon the earth in the sight of all them that behold thee" (Ezek. 28:11-19).\n\nNote these facts about Satan:\n\n> 1. That he was full of wisdom and perfect in beauty.\n\n> 2. That he had been in Eden, the garden of God—not a mere summer residence of some earthly king of Tyre, but the garden of God as referred to in other passages (Isa. 51:3; Ezek. 31:9, 16, 18; 36:35; Joel 2:3). This Eden, however, was the one that was on the original earth before Adam, for "every precious stone" was not the covering of Satan, nor was he perfect and sinless and the ruling cherub when he was in Adam's Eden. It was the garden that God made as the location of Lucifer's kingdom, as pictured in this whole passage.\n\n> 3. That he was the ruler of this Eden, for at that time\n\n---\n\nThe dispensation of angels is the first chapter in a story that runs all the way through Scripture: God entrusts authority to a moral creature, that creature rebels, and God responds with both judgment and redemption. You're living in a later chapter of the same story. So here's the question: Knowing that even Lucifer — the most perfect creature God ever made — fell through pride, what area of your own life are you currently managing in self-reliance rather than submitted dependence on God?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgan000d10b8ncb6d5nv	cmq76cgaj000910b8olia8etv	Lesson 4 — The Fallen Angels and Their Ranks	READING	900	1	\N	t	![Lesson 4 — The Fallen Angels and Their Ranks](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os4XE7KwL3Ls52XczwCYNqdZVf8hMUGlEvQ0nD)\n\n## The Fallen Angels and Their Ranks\n\nThe rebellion of Lucifer was not a solitary act. He drew with him a vast host of angels — Scripture suggests a third of the heavenly host (Revelation 12:4). These fallen angels did not lose their nature when they fell; they retained their intelligence, power, and, in some sense, their hierarchical organization.\n\n### The Continuity of Demonic Power\n\nA fallen angel remains an angel — created with immense natural power. The difference is not in capacity but in orientation: where once they served God's purposes, now they serve Satan's. Their intellect is darkened but not destroyed. Their strength is perverted but not diminished. This is why demonology is serious business: the enemy is not a bumbling imp but a disciplined, intelligent, ancient being.\n\n### Demonic Organization in Scripture\n\nThe Bible hints at organization among fallen angels. Jesus speaks of Satan casting out Satan (Matthew 12:26), implying that demons operate under authority. The demon possessed man in Gadara identified himself as "Legion, for we are many" (Mark 5:9) — a military term for a Roman division of 3,000-6,000 soldiers.\n\nPaul describes the spiritual enemy in hierarchical terms:\n\n> Ephesians 6:12 — "For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places."\n\n**Principalities** (Greek: *archē*) — Demonic authorities that govern nations, regions, and large population groups. They are territorial spirits that exercise influence over governments, cultures, and social systems.\n\n**Powers** (Greek: *exousia*) — Demonic powers that possess delegated authority to carry out specific functions. They operate under principalities and direct the work of lower-ranking spirits.\n\n**Rulers of the Darkness** (Greek: *kosmokratōr*) — World-rulers who influence the course of human affairs. They are the strategic planners of demonic activity.\n\n**Spiritual Wickedness in High Places** (Greek: *pneumatika tēs ponērias*) — The most general category: wicked spirits that operate in the heavenlies, invisible but active in affecting human life on earth.\n\n### The Book of Enoch and the Watchers\n\nWhile not canonical, the Book of Enoch preserves an ancient Jewish tradition about the fallen angels. It identifies a group of angels called **Watchers** who descended to earth, taught forbidden knowledge, and took human wives. Their offspring, the Nephilim, were giants who corrupted the earth and filled it with violence.\n\n> Genesis 6:1-4 — "There were giants in the earth in those days; and also after that, when the sons of God came in unto the daughters of men, and they bare children to them, the same became mighty men which were of old, men of renown."\n\nJude confirms this tradition:\n\n> Jude 1:6 — "And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day."\n\n### The Two Groups of Fallen Angels\n\nThe tradition distinguishes two categories of fallen angels:\n\n1. **Those who roam free** — the vast majority of demons who actively tempt, oppress, and deceive humanity.\n\n2. **Those who are bound** — a specific group of angels who committed the sin described in Genesis 6 and Jude, now held in chains until the final judgment.\n\nThis distinction explains why some demonic spirits seem more powerful and ancient than others — and why Scripture warns of a future release of even greater demonic forces in the end times.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgb0000r10b85tsc4aoe	cmq76cgaw000n10b8wrzhfrh1	Lesson 8 — Divination, Witchcraft, and the Black Art	READING	900	1	\N	t	![Lesson 8 — Divination, Witchcraft, and the Black Art](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsLCkgUUCZpCzRqFa9lYkMo1NvGIjUrV6tcW2s)\n\n## Divination, Witchcraft, and the Black Art\n\nScripture repeatedly condemns occult practices as abominations that open doors to demonic power. The Israelites were commanded not to suffer a witch to live (Exodus 22:18), and Saul died specifically because he consulted the witch of Endor (1 Chronicles 10:13). These practices are not harmless folklore; they are direct invitations to demonic spirits.\n\n### Divination\n\nDivination is the attempt to gain hidden knowledge by supernatural means apart from God. It includes:\n\n- **Astrology** — Reading the stars for guidance (Isaiah 47:13)\n- **Tarot cards and fortune-telling** — Attempting to predict the future\n- **Palm reading and numerology** — Seeking personal destiny in created things\n- **Divining rods and water-witching** — Using physical objects to detect hidden things\n\nGod condemned all these practices through Moses:\n\n> Deuteronomy 18:10-12 — "There shall not be found among you any one that maketh his son or his daughter to pass through the fire, or that useth divination, or an observer of times, or an enchanter, or a witch, or a charmer, or a consulter with familiar spirits, or a wizard, or a necromancer. For all that do these things are an abomination unto the LORD."\n\n### Witchcraft\n\nWitchcraft is not merely Halloween costumes and fairy tales. Biblical witchcraft involves the deliberate invocation of demonic spirits to accomplish specific purposes: cursing enemies, compelling love, inflicting disease, or gaining power. It is an organized system of demon worship.\n\nThe witch of Endor did not produce Samuel by magic; she summoned a demonic spirit that impersonated Samuel (1 Samuel 28). This is the nature of necromancy: demons impersonate the dead to deceive the living.\n\n### The Black Art (Necromancy)\n\nNecromancy — communication with the dead — is strictly forbidden. The dead do not roam the earth as spirits; they are in Sheol or with the Lord. Any "communication" with the dead is communication with a demon. This includes:\n\n- Séances and Ouija boards\n- Channeling and mediumship\n- Spirit guides and ascended masters\n- Ancestor worship that seeks direct guidance from deceased relatives\n\n### Occult Involvement and Demonic Access\n\nOccult participation creates a legal ground for demons to operate in a person's life. Many who have been involved in astrology, witchcraft, or other occult practices find that demonic influence persists long after the practices have stopped. This is because demons claim a legal right to remain until that right is specifically renounced and broken in the name of Jesus.\n\n> 2 Corinthians 6:17 — "Wherefore come out from among them, and be ye separate, saith the Lord, and touch not the unclean thing; and I will receive you."\n\nDeliverance often requires the believer to repent of occult involvement, renounce every practice by name, and command any associated spirits to leave in the authority of Christ.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgas000h10b8g8tqxfts	cmq76cgaj000910b8olia8etv	Lesson 5 — Demonic Possession and Oppression	READING	900	3	\N	t	![Lesson 5 — Demonic Possession and Oppression](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsgtmMpbEax52U6tuomWf38j1QMHRBV4griYbA)\n\n## Demonic Possession and Oppression\n\nThe Gospels record numerous encounters between Jesus and demon-possessed individuals. These accounts are not primitive superstition but accurate descriptions of a real spiritual phenomenon that continues today. Understanding the difference between possession and oppression is essential for effective ministry.\n\n### What Is Demonic Possession?\n\nDemonic possession occurs when a demon or demons take up residence within a human being, exerting control over the person's body, mind, or will. The possessed person is not merely influenced; they are dominated. The demon speaks through them (Mark 5:9), knows things the person could not know (Acts 16:16), and demonstrates superhuman strength (Mark 5:4).\n\nThe Gospels describe several characteristics of possession:\n\n- **Violent behavior** — The Gadarene demoniac cut himself and broke chains (Mark 5:5)\n- **Altered consciousness** — The person may not remember what the demon does through them\n- **Supernatural knowledge** — Demons recognized Jesus immediately (Mark 1:24)\n- **Resistance to spiritual things** — Physical convulsions when confronted with divine power (Mark 9:20)\n- **Self-destructive tendencies** — Demons drive their hosts toward death and ruin\n\n### What Is Demonic Oppression?\n\nOppression is external rather than internal. The demon attacks from the outside — through circumstances, relationships, physical affliction, or mental torment. Job was oppressed (Job 1-2), not possessed. The woman with the spirit of infirmity was bound by Satan (Luke 13:16), but the demon did not dwell within her personality.\n\nMany Christians experience oppression: unexplained depression, persistent temptation, recurring nightmares, financial destruction, relational breakdown, and physical illness that resists medical treatment. These may be demonic attacks rather than merely natural conditions.\n\n### Can a Christian Be Demon-Possessed?\n\nThe answer is **no** — with an important clarification. A true believer in Christ, indwelt by the Holy Spirit, cannot be possessed by a demon. The Spirit of God and an unclean spirit cannot coexist in the same temple.\n\n> 1 Corinthians 6:19-20 — "What? know ye not that your body is the temple of the Holy Ghost which is in you, which ye have of God, and ye are not your own? For ye are bought with a price."\n\nHowever, a Christian can be **oppressed**, **harassed**, and **influenced** by demons. Sin creates openings through which demons can attack. Unforgiveness, occult involvement, sexual immorality, substance abuse, and persistent rebellion can all give the enemy a foothold (Ephesians 4:27).\n\n### The Believer's Protection\n\nThe believer is sealed by the Holy Spirit (Ephesians 1:13), protected by the armor of God (Ephesians 6:10-18), and covered by the blood of Christ (Revelation 12:11). These are not abstract metaphors but real spiritual realities. The Christian who walks in obedience, prayer, and faith is secure — but the Christian who neglects these disciplines becomes vulnerable.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgat000j10b8wa7qzv2k	cmq76cgaj000910b8olia8etv	Lesson 6 — The Spirits of Infirmity and Bondage	READING	900	4	\N	t	![Lesson 6 — The Spirits of Infirmity and Bondage](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsqQ5EtR7AY8t92WkHGcRrZATmyFMPu3f04ih6)\n\n## The Spirits of Infirmity and Bondage\n\nScripture reveals that demons specialize. Just as holy angels have assigned tasks, fallen angels appear to concentrate their attacks in specific areas of human life. Jesus encountered a "spirit of infirmity" (Luke 13:11), and Paul warned of "the spirit of fear" (2 Timothy 1:7). The Bible speaks of spirits of deception, seduction, bondage, and destruction.\n\n### The Spirit of Infirmity\n\nThe woman in Luke 13 had been bound by a spirit of infirmity for eighteen years. She was not merely sick; she was **bound**. Jesus said, "Ought not this woman, being a daughter of Abraham, whom Satan hath bound, lo, these eighteen years, be loosed from this bond on the sabbath day?" (Luke 13:16).\n\nThis teaches us an important distinction: **not all disease is demonic**, but some disease is. When Jesus healed, He sometimes rebuked a fever (Luke 4:39), sometimes laid hands on the sick (Mark 6:5), and sometimes cast out a spirit (Mark 9:25). The method reveals the cause.\n\nSigns that an illness may have a spiritual root include:\n- Sudden onset after occult involvement or trauma\n- Resistance to medical treatment\n- Symptoms that worsen during prayer or worship\n- A family history of the same condition across generations\n- A voice or consciousness associated with the illness\n\n### The Spirit of Bondage\n\nPaul writes that before salvation, we were in bondage to fear:\n\n> Romans 8:15 — "For ye have not received the spirit of bondage again to fear; but ye have received the Spirit of adoption, whereby we cry, Abba, Father."\n\nBondage spirits produce addiction, compulsion, and slavery. They drive people to substances, behaviors, and relationships they hate but cannot escape. The person knows the behavior is destructive but feels powerless to stop. This is the nature of spiritual bondage — it goes beyond habit or psychology into the realm of captivity.\n\n### The Spirit of Poverty\n\nWhile less explicitly named in Scripture, the Bible clearly associates Satan with economic destruction. He stole Job's wealth in a single day. He is called "the devourer" (Malachi 3:11). Jesus warned of the deceitfulness of riches, and Paul identified the love of money as the root of all evil (1 Timothy 6:10).\n\nMany believers find themselves in patterns of financial failure that defy natural explanation: income lost at the last moment, business ventures sabotaged, opportunities closed, and an inexplicable inability to prosper despite hard work and skill. This may be the work of a spirit of poverty — a demonic assignment to keep God's people from having the resources to advance His kingdom.\n\n### Breaking the Assignment\n\nEvery spirit has a legal right to operate until that right is revoked. For the believer, the cross revoked every claim Satan had. But **legal fact must become experiential reality** through prayer, repentance, renunciation, and the exercise of authority in Christ's name.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgav000l10b86b6k89rg	cmq76cgaj000910b8olia8etv	Supplement 3 — For Lessons 5 & 6	SUPPLEMENT	600	5	\N	t	![Supplement 3 — For Lessons 5 & 6](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Ose8vF7i1incNku6xVBh4893ywvHpTdFSQ1m02)\n\n## Supplement 3 — For Lessons 5 & 6: Possession, Oppression, and Bondage\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**Demonic Possession** — The condition in which a demon dwells within a person and exerts control over their body, mind, or will.\n\n**Demonic Oppression** — External demonic attack through circumstances, affliction, or harassment of a person.\n\n**Spirit of Infirmity** — A demon that causes or intensifies physical disease and suffering.\n\n**Spirit of Bondage** — A demonic power that produces addiction, compulsion, and slavery to destructive patterns.\n\n**Generational Curse** — A pattern of sin or affliction passed down through family lines, often with a demonic component.\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> Mark 16:17 — "And these signs shall follow them that believe; In my name shall they cast out devils."\n\n> Luke 13:16 — "And ought not this woman, being a daughter of Abraham, whom Satan hath bound, lo, these eighteen years, be loosed from this bond on the sabbath day?"\n\n> 2 Timothy 1:7 — "For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind."\n\n---\n\n### Demonic Manifestations: Possession vs. Oppression\n\n| Manifestation | Possession | Oppression |\n|---------------|------------|------------|\n| Location | Internal (within the person) | External (attacks from outside) |\n| Control | Demon controls body/voice | Demon influences circumstances |\n| Awareness | Person often unaware or altered | Person fully aware |\n| Can a Christian experience it? | No | Yes |\n| Remedy | Exorcism / deliverance | Prayer, spiritual warfare, repentance |\n| Examples | Gadarene demoniac (Mark 5) | Job's afflictions (Job 1-2) |\n\n---\n\n### Questions for Reflection\n\n1. Jesus healed in different ways for different conditions. What does this teach us about diagnosing spiritual vs. natural causes?\n\n2. A Christian cannot be possessed, but can be oppressed. What habits or sins might open a door to demonic oppression in your life?\n\n3. How do you distinguish between a medical condition and a demonic affliction? What role should physicians play?\n\n4. "God has not given us the spirit of fear." What fears in your life may have a spiritual root that needs to be addressed in prayer?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgaz000p10b8jg16lock	cmq76cgaw000n10b8wrzhfrh1	Lesson 7 — Doctrines of Devils in the Last Days	READING	900	0	\N	t	![Lesson 7 — Doctrines of Devils in the Last Days](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsgtewfGZax52U6tuomWf38j1QMHRBV4griYbA)\n\n## Doctrines of Devils in the Last Days\n\nPaul warned Timothy that in the last days, some would depart from the faith, giving heed to **seducing spirits and doctrines of devils** (1 Timothy 4:1). This prophecy is being fulfilled before our eyes. False teaching is not merely intellectual error; it is often demonically inspired deception designed to lead people away from the truth of Christ.\n\n### The Nature of Doctrines of Devils\n\nA "doctrine of devils" is not a teaching about demons; it is a teaching **from** demons. It is a spiritual lie presented as theological truth. Satan's original temptation in Eden was doctrinal: "Ye shall not surely die... ye shall be as gods" (Genesis 3:4-5). He challenged God's word, God's character, and God's motives — and he did so with a theological argument.\n\nDoctrines of devils share common characteristics:\n- They deny the deity of Jesus Christ\n- They undermine the authority of Scripture\n- They promote human autonomy apart from God\n- They promise spiritual advancement without repentance\n- They mix truth with error so subtly that many are deceived\n\n### Modern Manifestations\n\nDoctrines of devils appear in many forms today:\n\n**Religious Plativism** — The teaching that all religions lead to the same God. This directly contradicts Jesus' statement: "I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me" (John 14:6).\n\n**Moral Relativism** — The idea that no absolute moral standard exists. This attacks the very nature of God, who is holy and has spoken His commandments clearly.\n\n**New Age Spirituality** — The teaching that humanity is divine, that consciousness creates reality, and that Jesus was merely an enlightened master. These are ancient gnostic lies repackaged for modern consumption.\n\n**Secular Humanism** — The assertion that man is the measure of all things and that God is unnecessary. This is the same lie Satan told Eve: "Ye shall be as gods."\n\n**Critical Theories** — Worldviews that divide humanity by oppressor and oppressed, replacing the biblical categories of sin and redemption with political power structures. These are Marxist doctrines dressed in academic language — and they functionally replace the gospel with ideology.\n\n### The Spirit Behind the Doctrine\n\nPaul does not say "doctrines of error" or "doctrines of confusion." He says **doctrines of devils** — because demons are actively involved in originating, spreading, and enforcing these lies. A teacher of false doctrine may be sincere, but if the doctrine denies Christ, it has a demonic source.\n\n> 1 John 4:3 — "And every spirit that confesseth not that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is not of God: and this is that spirit of antichrist, whereof ye have heard that it should come; and even now already is it in the world."\n\n### The Remedy: Sound Doctrine\n\nThe only antidote to demonic deception is the truth of God's Word. Believers must be grounded in Scripture, discerning in spirit, and committed to the faith once delivered to the saints (Jude 1:3).	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgal000b10b8raili13n	cmq76cgaj000910b8olia8etv	Lesson 3 — Satan: The Great Deceiver	READING	900	0	\N	t	![Lesson 3 — Satan: The Great Deceiver](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Osa14d3pEhtesUMivpomO8x4WSPknRFTuAI75Q)\n\n## Satan — The Great Deceiver\n\nSatan is known by many names in Scripture, and each name reveals a different aspect of his evil character. He is the serpent, the dragon, the devil, the accuser, the tempter, and the father of lies. To understand spiritual warfare, we must understand the enemy — not so that we might fear him, but so that we might recognize his tactics and overcome him.\n\n### The Names of Satan\n\n**The Serpent** — In Genesis 3, Satan approaches Eve not as an enemy but as a subtle, clever creature. He does not announce his presence; he questions God's word. "Hath God said...?" This is the pattern of all deception: sowing doubt about God's character and commands.\n\n**The Devil** — From the Greek *diabolos*, meaning "slanderer" or "accuser." Satan's primary work against believers is accusation. He reminds us of past sins, present failures, and future doubts. His goal is to drive us to despair rather than to the cross.\n\n**The Dragon** — In Revelation 12, Satan appears as a great red dragon, symbolizing his ferocity, cruelty, and bloodthirsty nature. He seeks to devour the child born of the woman — Christ — and when he fails, he turns his rage against the woman's offspring: the Church.\n\n**The Prince of This World** — Jesus calls Satan by this title three times in John's Gospel (John 12:31; 14:30; 16:11). Satan exercises a real, though temporary and usurped, authority over the kingdoms of this world. He offered Jesus all the kingdoms of the world in exchange for worship (Matthew 4:8-9) — a real offer of real power.\n\n### The Methods of Satan\n\n**Deception** — Satan is a liar and the father of lies (John 8:44). He does not usually appear in obvious evil; he counterfeits truth, twists Scripture, and mixes lies with enough truth to make them palatable.\n\n**Temptation** — Satan tempted Jesus in the wilderness with three appeals: to the body (stones to bread), to pride (cast yourself down), and to power (all the kingdoms). These correspond to John's three categories: the lust of the flesh, the lust of the eyes, and the pride of life (1 John 2:16).\n\n**Oppression and Affliction** — Satan bound a woman with a spirit of infirmity for eighteen years (Luke 13:16). He afflicted Job with boils, robbery, and bereavement (Job 1-2). His power to harm is real but always bounded by God's permission.\n\n**Counterfeits** — Satan disguises himself as an angel of light (2 Corinthians 11:14). His ministers appear as ministers of righteousness. False prophets, false christs, and false gospels are his stock-in-trade.\n\n### The Defeat of Satan\n\nSatan's doom was sealed at the cross. Jesus declared:\n\n> John 12:31 — "Now is the judgment of this world: now shall the prince of this world be cast out."\n\nThe resurrection broke Satan's power over death (Hebrews 2:14). The ascension seated Christ far above all principality and power (Ephesians 1:21). And at the end of the age, Satan will be bound for a thousand years, then cast into the lake of fire forever (Revelation 20).	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612v2000hgeo0ciixkph8	cmq6612v0000fgeo0goukqfcs	Lesson 5 — The Seraphim: Burning with Divine Love	READING	900	0	\N	t	![Lesson 5 — The Seraphim: Burning with Divine Love](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsnN4T3IgR6p4tHCQPYM8N0kE5l7TdjZq9ibaz)\n\n## The Seraphim — Burning with Divine Love\n\n### Enter the Scene First\n\nIt is the year King Uzziah died. Jerusalem is in political uncertainty. The prophet Isaiah goes to the Temple.\n\nWhat happens next is unlike anything else in Scripture.\n\n> [Isaiah 6:1-4](data-scripture="Isaiah 6:1") "In the year that King Uzziah died I saw the Lord sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up; and the train of his robe filled the temple. Above him stood the seraphim. Each had six wings: with two he covered his face, and with two he covered his feet, and with two he flew. And one called to another and said: 'Holy, holy, holy is the Lord of hosts; the whole earth is full of his glory!' And the foundations of the thresholds shook at the voice of him who called, and the house was filled with smoke."\n\nThe thresholds shake. The house fills with smoke. And Isaiah, one of the greatest prophets who ever lived, does not see this vision and feel inspired. He does not reach for his scroll and begin composing. He cries out:\n\n> [Isaiah 6:5](data-scripture="Isaiah 6:5") "Woe is me! For I am lost; for I am a man of unclean lips, and I dwell in the midst of a people of unclean lips; for my eyes have seen the King, the Lord of hosts!"\n\n*Lost.* The Hebrew word is *nidmeti* — silenced, undone, as one might be undone by annihilation. The vision of the Seraphim and the Holy God does not produce enthusiasm. It produces the overwhelming awareness of one's own unworthiness in the presence of utter holiness.\n\nThen one of the Seraphim — these burning, six-winged beings who have been contemplating the face of God since the beginning of creation — flies to Isaiah. It takes a burning coal from the altar with tongs, touches his lips, and says: *"Behold, this has touched your lips; your guilt is taken away, and your sin atoned for."*\n\nOnly then does Isaiah hear the question: *"Whom shall I send, and who will go for us?"* Only then does he answer: *"Here I am! Send me."*\n\nThe purification precedes the commission. The encounter with the Seraphim produces a prophet.\n\n---\n\n### Etymology: The Burning Ones\n\nThe Hebrew word *seraphim* (singular: *seraph*) comes from the root *saraph*, meaning "to burn." They are the **"burning ones"** or **"incandescent ones."** Their name is not a description of their appearance (though they are associated with fire) — it is a description of their *inner condition*. They burn with the love of God.\n\n### Six Wings: The Geometry of Humility\n\nEach Seraphim has six wings. Most people, taught to picture angels as winged beings, assume all six wings are for flight. Scripture says otherwise.\n\n- **Two cover the face** — in humility before God's glory\n- **Two cover the feet** — in reverence, veiling what is low in the presence of what is highest\n- **Only two are for flight**\n\nFour of six wings exist not for movement, for ministry, for any outward purpose at all — but for the sheer act of reverencing God. The Seraphim, the most powerful created beings in existence, use most of their visible capacity not to *do* anything, but to *adore*.\n\nThis is the first and most important thing the Seraphim teach us about God: in His presence, the appropriate response is not action. It is adoration.\n\n### Theological Character: Wise Loves\n\nThe Seraphim are the highest of all created beings. They stand closest to God — not spatially, but in terms of their participation in divine love and their resemblance to God.\n\nPseudo-Dionysius wrote of the Seraphim as **"wise Loves"** — meaning that their love is not blind or emotional but wisdom-saturated: they love God through total knowledge of Him. They are not loving a vague divine warmth. They love a Person they know with perfect clarity — and that knowledge makes their love burn all the hotter.\n\nTheir perpetual song of praise — the *Trisagion*, "Holy, holy, holy" — is not a vocal exercise. It is the full deployment of their will in adoration. Everything they are is concentrated in that cry.\n\n### The Seraphim at Every Mass\n\nThe *Sanctus* — "Holy, Holy, Holy, Lord God of hosts" — quotes the Seraphim's song directly. This is not a commemorative quotation. It is a participation.\n\nHebrews 12:22 declares that when Christians gather for worship, they come *"to the heavenly Jerusalem, and to an innumerable company of angels."* The Seraphim are present at every Mass. When the congregation sings the *Sanctus*, they are joining a hymn that has never once stopped since the first moment of angelic creation — a hymn that the Seraphim were burning with before the universe existed.\n\nYou have been given access to that choir. The question the Seraphim's example poses is simple: **are you in it?**\n\n### The Standard of the Spiritual Life\n\nIn the spiritual life, the goal of contemplative prayer is precisely this: to be set on fire with divine love, to participate by grace in what the Seraphim possess by nature. The Seraphim are not only inhabitants of heaven — they are the *standard* toward which the transformed soul moves.\n\nThe mystics — John of the Cross, Teresa of Ávila, Bonaventure — speak of a point in the spiritual life where the soul is no longer primarily moved by fear of punishment or even by hope of reward, but by love alone. Love that burns. Love that is its own justification. The tradition calls this the *unitive way* — and its endpoint, in created beings, looks something like a Seraph.\n\n---\n\n*Next: We have met the beings defined by love. Now we meet the beings defined by something equally astonishing — knowledge. The Cherubim have been guarding something since the garden. They are the angels whose names mean "fullness of wisdom" — and they have been present at every place in Scripture where God pledged to make Himself known.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgb7000z10b8gagzm6oi	cmq76cgaw000n10b8wrzhfrh1	Supplement 5 — For Lessons 9 & 10	SUPPLEMENT	600	5	\N	t	![Supplement 5 — For Lessons 9 & 10](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os0Lz6wPYvRZPna4mAuYVdrFHOBK7LSwy8WioD)\n\n## Supplement 5 — For Lessons 9 & 10: The Church and the Nations\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**Spirit of Antichrist** — Any spirit or teaching that denies the deity, humanity, or saving work of Jesus Christ.\n\n**Territorial Spirits** — High-ranking demons assigned to influence specific nations, regions, or cultural spheres.\n\n**False Apostle** — A minister who claims apostolic authority but preaches a different gospel.\n\n**Another Gospel** — Any message that adds to, subtracts from, or redefines the gospel of salvation by grace through faith in Christ alone.\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> 2 Corinthians 11:13-14 — "For such are false apostles, deceitful workers, transforming themselves into the apostles of Christ. And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light."\n\n> Daniel 10:13 — "But the prince of the kingdom of Persia withstood me one and twenty days: but, lo, Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me."\n\n> 2 Chronicles 7:14 — "If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land."\n\n---\n\n### Testing Every Spirit\n\n| True Spirit | False Spirit |\n|-------------|--------------|\n| Exalts Jesus Christ | Ignores or denies Christ |\n| Honors Scripture as final authority | Adds new revelations above Scripture |\n| Calls for repentance and holiness | Excuses sin as grace |\n| Produces humility and love | Produces pride and division |\n| Points to the cross | Points to human potential |\n\n---\n\n### Questions for Reflection\n\n1. How can you distinguish between genuine spiritual revival and demonic counterfeit revival in a church setting?\n\n2. What does Daniel's vision teach us about the relationship between prayer and national spiritual warfare?\n\n3. In what ways has your own nation opened doors to demonic influence? How can you pray strategically?\n\n4. Why is the family so often the first target of Satan's national strategy? How can you protect your own household?	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612uy000dgeo0shscg3qp	cmq6612ug0001geo0aum7jawk	Supplement 2 — For Lessons 3 & 4	SUPPLEMENT	600	5	\N	t	![Supplement 2 — For Lessons 3 & 4](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Osoc5iZAXWxwEUd728la9hHriMsfOkGYRKDCuL)\n\n## Supplement 2 — For Lessons 3 & 4: Creation, Purpose, and Scripture\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**Simul** — Latin for "at the same time / all at once." The Fourth Lateran Council's word for the instantaneous creation of both spiritual and material creatures.\n\n**The Three Instances** — Thomas Aquinas's analysis of the three conceptual "moments" of angelic creation: (1) creation with infused knowledge, (2) the free choice of will, (3) confirmation in grace for the faithful.\n\n**The Beatific Vision** — Direct, unmediated sight of God's essence; the eternal reward given to the faithful angels at the moment of their confirmation, and the destiny promised to the redeemed human soul.\n\n**The Angel of the Lord** (*malakh YHWH*) — A special figure in the Old Testament who speaks with divine authority and accepts worship; many Fathers identified these appearances as Christophanies — pre-incarnate manifestations of the Son of God.\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> Col. 1:16 "For by him all things were created, in heaven and on earth, visible and invisible, whether thrones or dominions or rulers or powers — all things were created through him and for him."\n\n> Lk. 1:38 "And Mary said, 'Behold, I am the servant of the Lord; let it be to me according to your word.' And the angel departed from her."\n\n> Gen. 28:12 "And he dreamed, and behold, there was a ladder set up on the earth, and the top of it reached to heaven. And behold, the angels of God were ascending and descending on it."\n\n---\n\n### Angelic Appearances by Era\n\n| Era | Key Appearance | Reference |\n|-----|---------------|-----------|\n| Creation | Sons of God rejoicing | Job 38:7 |\n| Eden | Cherubim guarding the Tree | Gen. 3:24 |\n| Patriarchs | Three visitors to Abraham | Gen. 18:1-2 |\n| Moses | Burning bush / Exodus | Ex. 3:2 |\n| Ark of the Covenant | Golden Cherubim on mercy seat | Ex. 25:18-22 |\n| Prophets | Isaiah's seraphim vision | Isa. 6:1-7 |\n| Prophets | Ezekiel's chariot-throne | Ezek. 1:4-28 |\n| Daniel | Gabriel explains visions | Dan. 8:16 |\n| Incarnation | Gabriel's Annunciation | Lk. 1:26-38 |\n| Birth | Heavenly host to shepherds | Lk. 2:13-14 |\n| Resurrection | Angel rolls back stone | Mt. 28:2-6 |\n| Ascension | Two angels in white | Acts 1:10-11 |\n\n---\n\n### Questions for Reflection\n\n1. The Fourth Lateran Council teaches that God created the spiritual and material realms *at the same time*. What does this say about God's creative act — is it a process or a gift?\n\n2. Each angel was given a specific, unchangeable mission at the moment of creation. In what way does this differ from human vocation? How might it help you understand your own call from God?\n\n3. Jacob's Ladder shows angels ascending *and* descending — moving between heaven and earth. What does this ceaseless movement say about the relationship between the heavenly and earthly realms?\n\n4. From the burning bush to the empty tomb, angels appear at every turning point of salvation history. What does this consistent presence reveal about how God governs the world?\n\n5. Paul declares that all things — "visible and invisible, whether thrones or dominions or rulers or powers" — were created *through* Christ and *for* Christ (Col. 1:16). What does it mean that even the highest angels exist for Christ?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xguf000dhks8t1ltt37x	cmq76xgtn0001hks8s3kqs5yq	Supplement 9 — The Global Demonology: Nations, Princes, and the Cosmic Battlefield	SUPPLEMENT	\N	5	\N	t	![Supplement 9 — The Global Demonology: Nations, Princes, and the Cosmic Battlefield](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsUu9cEo6edALvbYMWXfx7ZoQswlOpr26nuJ1t)\n\n## Supplement 9 — The Global Demonology: Nations, Princes, and the Cosmic Battlefield\n\nThe vision in [Daniel 10](data-scripture="Daniel 10") is one of the strangest and most theologically significant passages in the Old Testament. Daniel has been fasting and praying for three weeks. An angelic messenger finally arrives with an explanation: *"The prince of the kingdom of Persia withstood me one and twenty days: but, lo, Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me."*\n\n[Daniel 10:20](data-scripture="Daniel 10:20"): *"Then said he, Knowest thou wherefore I come unto thee? and now will I return to fight with the prince of Persia: and when I am gone forth, lo, the prince of Grecia shall come."*\n\n---\n\n## The Territorial Structure\n\nDaniel 10 gives us the clearest picture in Scripture of the cosmic governance structure: there are angelic princes assigned to nations, and demonic princes contesting that governance. The Prince of Persia and the Prince of Greece are not human rulers — they are demonic principalities assigned to those nations, governing their spiritual atmosphere, influencing their leaders, and contesting the angelic messengers of God.\n\n[Deuteronomy 32:8](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 32:8") (Dead Sea Scrolls reading): *"When the Most High divided to the nations their inheritance, when he separated the sons of Adam, he set the bounds of the people according to the number of the sons of God."* God divided the nations and assigned them to lesser divine beings — some of whom subsequently corrupted their assignment and became the demonic princes of nations.\n\n[Psalm 82:1](data-scripture="Psalm 82:1"): *"God standeth in the congregation of the mighty; he judgeth among the gods."* [Psalm 82:6-7](data-scripture="Psalm 82:6-7"): *"I have said, Ye are gods... But ye shall die like men, and fall like one of the princes."* The divine council — the assembly of cosmic beings over which God presides — includes both faithful and rebellious members. The rebellious ones are the demonic princes of nations.\n\n## Implications for Prayer\n\nThis structure — the demonic princes of nations — is why [Ephesians 6:12](data-scripture="Ephesians 6:12") specifies: *"We wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places."*\n\nThe word "principalities" (*archas*) refers specifically to the governing demonic hierarchy — the territorial princes of Daniel 10. When Paul says believers wrestle against these beings, he is describing exactly what Daniel's prayer encountered: resistance at the level of national spiritual governance.\n\nThis is why corporate prayer over nations — sustained, specific, theologically informed intercession — is not merely religious sentiment. It is engagement with the territorial governance structure described in Daniel 10. The 21 days of Daniel's prayer corresponded to 21 days of spiritual warfare at the national level. The outcome was the arrival of the messenger with God's word.\n\n## The Strongman Model and Territorial Deliverance\n\n[Matthew 12:29](data-scripture="Matthew 12:29"): *"Or else how can one enter into a strong man's house, and spoil his goods, except he first bind the strong man? and then he will spoil his house."*\n\nThe strongman principle operates at every level — individual, household, community, and national. The territorial strongman over a city or region maintains the spiritual atmosphere of that territory: the characteristic patterns of sin, the specific strongholds of oppression, the particular blindnesses to the gospel that characterize a geographic area.\n\nRegional evangelism, church planting, and sustained intercessory prayer all encounter the territorial strongman. The work of "spoiling his goods" — seeing people set free from the patterns that strongman maintains — requires first addressing the strongman himself through specific, Spirit-directed corporate prayer.\n\n## What This Means for Your Prayer Life\n\nYour intercession is not limited to individual people. You can pray specifically over:\n\n- The principality governing your city or region (naming the characteristic patterns of oppression it produces)\n- The demonic influences on specific governmental leaders\n- The territorial spiritual atmosphere that resists the gospel in specific communities\n\n[2 Corinthians 10:4](data-scripture="2 Corinthians 10:4"): *"For the weapons of our warfare are not carnal, but mighty through God to the pulling down of strong holds."* The strongholds of 2 Corinthians 10 include territorial strongholds — the mental and spiritual architectures that demonic princes have established over communities, cultures, and nations.\n\nYou have access to the same throne room that Daniel's prayer reached. The outcome of your intercession operates at the same cosmic level.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xguh000fhks86aggttoa	cmq76xgtn0001hks8s3kqs5yq	Supplement 10 — The Strongmen Guide: A Reference for Recognition and Response	SUPPLEMENT	\N	6	\N	t	![Supplement 10 — The Strongmen Guide: A Reference for Recognition and Response](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Osc7RQPmvHaBEe23oH5UXu7NQGbLSsPzChWlD6)\n\n## Supplement 10 — The Strongmen Guide: A Reference for Recognition and Response\n\nThis supplement consolidates the strongmen covered in Lessons 18–21 with their scriptural identification, their signature manifestations, the legal ground they require, and the specific response each requires. Use it as a reference for discernment and prayer.\n\n---\n\n## The Lying Spirit\n\n**Scripture:** [1 Kings 22:22-23](data-scripture="1 Kings 22:22-23"), [2 Thessalonians 2:11](data-scripture="2 Thessalonians 2:11")\n\n**Signature manifestations:** False prophecy, theological deception that feels spiritually alive, the consistent reception of "words from God" that confirm existing desire, difficulty receiving correction, persistent blindness to obvious contradictions between claimed revelation and Scripture.\n\n**Legal ground:** Choosing what one wants to hear over what Scripture says. Repeated rejection of correction. Sustained engagement with false prophetic or teaching voices.\n\n**Response:**\n- Repent for choosing confirmation over truth\n- Renounce every false word received as authoritative\n- Submit all subsequent prophetic impressions to scriptural testing\n- Establish accountability with a theologically grounded community\n\n---\n\n## The Familiar Spirit\n\n**Scripture:** [Leviticus 20:27](data-scripture="Leviticus 20:27"), [1 Samuel 28](data-scripture="1 Samuel 28"), [Isaiah 8:19](data-scripture="Isaiah 8:19")\n\n**Signature manifestations:** Accurate information through illegitimate channels (psychics, mediums, divination), persistent curiosity about the deceased, dependence on a spiritual source other than the Holy Spirit for guidance, feeling "helped" by a specific entity.\n\n**Legal ground:** Consulting psychics, mediums, Ouija boards, or divination systems. Inheriting a family pattern of occult consultation.\n\n**Response:**\n- Repent for and renounce every consultation of a divination source\n- Break every familiar spirit relationship by name\n- Command departure in Jesus' name\n- Establish the Holy Spirit as the sole legitimate guide\n\n---\n\n## The Spirit of Perversion\n\n**Scripture:** [Isaiah 19:14](data-scripture="Isaiah 19:14"), [Isaiah 5:20](data-scripture="Isaiah 5:20")\n\n**Signature manifestations:** Sexual confusion, attraction to morally inverted ideologies, comfort with the reframing of sin as virtue, difficulty with biblical clarity on sexuality and gender, systematic twisting of Scripture's plain meaning.\n\n**Legal ground:** Sexual sin, pornography use, sustained exposure to gender ideology or sexual liberation frameworks, participation in LGBTQ-affirming theological communities.\n\n**Response:**\n- Repent for specific sexual sin and exposure\n- Renounce the Spirit of Perversion\n- Rebuild understanding of human sexuality from Scripture\n- Establish accountability and community with sound biblical teaching\n\n---\n\n## The Spirit of Jealousy\n\n**Scripture:** [Numbers 5:14](data-scripture="Numbers 5:14"), [1 Samuel 18:9](data-scripture="1 Samuel 18:9")\n\n**Signature manifestations:** Inability to celebrate others' success, persistent comparison, the experience of others' elevation as personal diminishment, difficulty in community and leadership relationships, patterns of betrayal or erosion of close relationships.\n\n**Legal ground:** Sustained comparison-based resentment, specific acts of sabotage or undermining rooted in competitive jealousy.\n\n**Response:**\n- Name the specific comparisons and specific people\n- Repent for each act of jealousy-driven behavior\n- Pray specifically for the flourishing of those you have resented\n- Renounce the Spirit of Jealousy\n\n---\n\n## The Spirit of Whoredom\n\n**Scripture:** [Hosea 4:12](data-scripture="Hosea 4:12"), [Hosea 5:4](data-scripture="Hosea 5:4")\n\n**Signature manifestations:** Sexual addiction and compulsion, inability to maintain exclusive covenant loyalty (to God or spouse), spiritual restlessness that drives continued seeking from sources outside Christ, idolatry patterns.\n\n**Legal ground:** Sexual sin outside covenant, pornography, spiritual adultery through sustained involvement with false religious systems.\n\n**Response:**\n- Address both physical and spiritual dimensions simultaneously\n- Break soul ties from sexual sin\n- Renounce specific idolatries\n- Renounce the Spirit of Whoredom\n- Establish accountable community\n\n---\n\n## The Spirit of Pride\n\n**Scripture:** [Isaiah 14:13-14](data-scripture="Isaiah 14:13-14"), [Proverbs 16:18](data-scripture="Proverbs 16:18")\n\n**Signature manifestations:** Inability to receive correction, dismissal of counsel from those perceived as less gifted or less educated, spiritual pride masking as discernment, patterns of church or ministry conflict rooted in refusal to submit.\n\n**Legal ground:** Sustained independent spirit, consistent dismissal of correction, specific acts of pride-driven competition or control.\n\n**Response:**\n- Repent for specific acts of pride\n- Practice specific submission to spiritual authority\n- Renounce the Spirit of Pride\n- Ask God to reveal where pride has operated unconsciously\n\n---\n\n## The Spirit of Heaviness\n\n**Scripture:** [Isaiah 61:3](data-scripture="Isaiah 61:3")\n\n**Weapon:** The garment of praise — sustained worship as spiritual warfare, not as mood management.\n\n## The Spirit of Fear\n\n**Scripture:** [2 Timothy 1:7](data-scripture="2 Timothy 1:7"), [1 John 4:18](data-scripture="1 John 4:18")\n\n**Weapon:** The revelation of the Father's perfect love — specifically rebuilding the understanding of God's character through Scripture, combined with renunciation of the Spirit of Fear.\n\n## The Spirit of Bondage\n\n**Scripture:** [Romans 8:15](data-scripture="Romans 8:15")\n\n**Weapon:** The Spirit of adoption — the specific counter to the Spirit of Bondage is the full reception of sonship/daughtership, combined with community accountability and the practical restructuring of environments that provide access.\n\n---\n\n*Part VI complete. Part VII applies the theology of strongmen to the specific contemporary doorways through which they enter — 44 lessons on the specific attacks the enemy uses against the church today.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612vg000vgeo0scoc75ik	cmq6612ve000tgeo0b9n1d4af	Lesson 9 — The Dominations and Virtues: Governing Creation	READING	900	0	\N	t	![Lesson 9 — The Dominations and Virtues: Governing Creation](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os0by5mBYvRZPna4mAuYVdrFHOBK7LSwy8WioD)\n\n## The Dominations and Virtues — Governing Creation\n\n### Two Kinds of Angels Thinking About Your World\n\nHere is a question worth sitting with: why does the sun rise every morning?\n\nThe scientific answer is correct but incomplete. The earth rotates on its axis at 1,000 miles per hour; the sun remains in position as the earth's surface comes into view of it. True. But *why does the earth continue rotating at precisely that rate? Why does gravity remain constant? Why do the laws of physics not shift overnight?*\n\nThe Christian theological tradition gives an answer that science cannot: the material universe is governed, moment by moment, by personal beings who enact God's will in the physical order. Every sunrise is not a mechanical process running on autopilot — it is an act of intelligent obedience to the Creator.\n\nThese are the **Virtues** — the second choir of the second hierarchy. They are why the universe is reliable.\n\n---\n\n### The Dominations: Heaven's Prime Ministers\n\n**Etymology.** From the Latin *dominatio* and Greek *kyriotetes* — lordship or dominion.\n\nThe Dominations sit at the top of the second hierarchy and are best understood as the executive layer of God's governance of creation. They receive the light of the first hierarchy — the burning love of the Seraphim, the profound wisdom of the Cherubim, the stable authority of the Thrones — and translate it into the orders that govern the lower choirs.\n\nThey are not themselves executors. They do not go and *do* things in the physical world directly. They direct. They set in motion. They are the angels who receive the blueprint of divine providence and distribute it to the workers.\n\nPseudo-Dionysius described them as manifesting *"Godlike Lordship"* in a holy, fitting way, freed from all servile subjection. The Dominations are served; they do not serve in the way the lower choirs serve. Their dignity consists precisely in this: they have been given real authority, within the proper order, over all the angels below them.\n\nIn Paul's language: *"whether thrones or dominions or rulers or powers — all things were created through him and for him"* ([Colossians 1:16](data-scripture="Colossians 1:16")).\n\n---\n\n### The Virtues: Lords of Causality\n\n**Etymology.** From the Latin *virtus* (strength, power, effectiveness) and Greek *dynameis* (forces, powers).\n\nThe Virtues exercise primary power over the physical universe. Where the Dominations set direction, the Virtues implement it at the level of physical law and operation. They are the lords of causality — the beings through whom God's will becomes the actual behavior of the material world.\n\nPseudo-Dionysius described the Virtues as possessing *"a certain powerful and unshakable virility welling forth into all their Godlike energies, not weakly shrinking from any of the Godlike enlightenments granted to it."* This is not the timid virtue of enduring suffering, but the vigorous, active virtue of doing — of sustaining, moving, maintaining.\n\n**Two dimensions of their work:**\n\n**Ordinary.** Every morning the earth rotates. Every spring the seasons turn. Every year the crops come and the tides move and the physics of creation remains consistent. This is the Virtues at their ordinary work. It is not dramatic. It does not make the news. But if the Virtues ceased for one hour, nothing would function.\n\n**Extraordinary.** In traditional theology, the Virtues are associated with **miracles** — the supernatural operations that override the ordinary course of nature in service of God's plan. When Moses parts the Red Sea ([Exodus 14:21](data-scripture="Exodus 14:21")), when Christ calms the storm ([Mark 4:39](data-scripture="Mark 4:39")), when water becomes wine at Cana ([John 2:9](data-scripture="John 2:9")), when a dead man walks out of a tomb — the angelic instruments of those events, in the order of created causality, are the Virtues.\n\nA miracle is not a suspension of law. It is the same power that sustains law, used in an extraordinary way, to make God's presence and purpose unmistakably visible.\n\n> [Daniel 3:39](data-scripture="Daniel 3:39") "Bless the Lord, all powers." (*virtutes* in the Latin Vulgate.)\n\n---\n\n### The Governed Universe\n\nThe doctrine of the second hierarchy carries a significant implication: **the material world is not neutral**. It is not abandoned to blind mechanism. It is personally superintended, moment by moment, by beings who know what they are doing and why.\n\nThis is not pantheism — the universe is not God, and the Virtues are not divine. They are creatures doing the will of their Creator. But it means that every moment you inhabit — every sunrise, every heartbeat, every breath — is the product of an intelligent act of obedience to God by a personal being.\n\nYou do not live in a machine. You live in a creation.\n\n---\n\n### What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThere is a tendency, when studying the middle hierarchy, to treat it as the purely theoretical section — the abstract mechanics of cosmic governance, interesting for the scholarly but remote from daily life.\n\nThat tendency is wrong.\n\nThe Dominations and Virtues are not remote. They are the *explanation* for the world you woke up in this morning. The gravity that held you to your bed. The heartbeat that continued while you slept. The oxygen that existed to be breathed. Every one of these is not an impersonal mechanism but an intelligent act of creatures who know what they are doing and why.\n\nYou live inside the work of the Virtues. Your entire life is surrounded by their labor.\n\nConsider what this changes:\n\n**How you see the ordinary.** You drive to work past trees that are budding because the Virtues are executing the will of the God who made the seasons. You eat a meal because agriculture works because the physical laws of growth and soil are sustained by personal beings in loving obedience. None of this is ordinary in the sense of mundane. It is *regular* — but regular in the way a faithful person keeps their word every single day, not in the way a machine repeats its function.\n\n**How you pray for the miraculous.** When you ask God for something that requires a miracle, you are not asking Him to break His creation. You are asking Him to direct the Virtues — who already sustain creation — to do something extraordinary in service of a specific need. This is not foreign to them. It is exactly what they did when Moses raised his staff over the sea.\n\n**How you face chaos.** When the structures of civilization shake — when the institutions you have trusted begin to fail — the doctrine of the Dominations and Virtues says: the governance of creation does not depend on the institutions you can see. It depends on the beings above them, and on the God above those beings.\n\nSit with that for a moment before moving on.\n\n---\n\n*Next: The second hierarchy continues. We meet the Powers — the defenders of cosmic order — and then the Principalities, who stand at the intersection of heaven and human history, governing nations, civilizations, and the Church itself.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612uj0003geo043mie4yb	cmq6612ug0001geo0aum7jawk	Lesson 1 — What Are Angels?	READING	900	0	\N	t	![Lesson 1 — What Are Angels?](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsDnHjCMquQbd9NMB2rOwYoPFWmngiXZpUeqKI)\n\n## What Are Angels?\n\nRight now, as you read this, a being of pure intelligence that has existed since before the first star was formed — a being that knows more about the structure of creation than the greatest scientist who ever lived — is present with you. It cannot be seen. It does not age. It was created, in some measure, for you.\n\nThis is not poetry. This is not metaphor. This is what the Church has always taught, based on what God revealed in Scripture.\n\nWe call these beings angels. And almost everything popular culture has told you about them is wrong.\n\n---\n\n### The Word "Angel" Is a Job Title, Not a Name\n\nThe word *angel* comes from the Greek *angelos* (and before it the Hebrew *malakh*), both meaning **"messenger."** "Angel" therefore designates a *function or office*, not a nature. It is like calling someone "a soldier" — it tells you what they do, not what they are.\n\nThe proper name for what these beings are is *pure spirit* or *intellectual substance*. Many of the highest angels — the Seraphim burning before God's throne — have no outward mission to creation at all. They are never sent anywhere. Yet they are still called "angels" in the broad sense. The label describes the category; it does not exhaust the reality.\n\n### What "Pure Spirit" Actually Means\n\nAngels are **pure spirits** — they possess no material body, and exist as purely intellectual substances: self-subsistent forms entirely without matter.\n\nThomas Aquinas argues in the *Summa Theologiae* (I, q. 50) that there must exist purely spiritual creatures. The universe exhibits a graduated hierarchy: minerals, plants, animals, and humans, each level adding a perfection absent in the one below. Reason demands that there be creatures above the human that have intellect without the limitations of matter — beings that are intellect *through and through*.\n\nThis stands in contrast to the Franciscan theologian Bonaventure and others who held that everything below God, including angels, is composed of some kind of spiritual matter. Aquinas rejected this as a confusion: if a thing is spiritual, it is not material. The notion of "spiritual matter" is self-contradictory.\n\n### Two Faculties Only: Intellect and Will\n\nUnlike humans, who additionally possess sense faculties — sight, hearing, touch, imagination, memory — angels operate solely through intellect and will. They have no hunger, no physical sensation, no bodily passions. They are pure mind and pure freedom.\n\n**No emotions in the human sense, but genuine affective states in the will.** Angels do not feel emotions in the biochemical, embodied way humans do. Yet they possess what the tradition calls *affective movements of the will* — something analogous to love, joy, and intensity, but located entirely in the will rather than in sensory appetite. When the Seraphim are described as burning with divine love, this is a real condition of their will, not a metaphor imported from human experience.\n\n### Five Facts About Angels That Will Surprise You\n\n**I. Each angel is its own species.** Because angels have no matter to individuate them (matter is what makes two things of the same kind distinct from each other), each angel must constitute its own entire species. There are no two angels of the same kind. Every angel is as distinct from every other angel as a horse is from a dog. The number of angelic "species" equals the number of individual angels — an almost incomprehensible multitude, each one unique in all of creation.\n\n**II. Angels are immortal by nature, not by gift.** Material things dissolve because they are composed of parts that can separate. Angels are simple substances — they have no parts. They can only cease to exist if God were to withdraw His sustaining act, which He does not do. They exist as long as God wills them, which is forever.\n\n**III. Angels are not deceased humans.** When human beings die, they do not become angels. The saints in heaven remain human souls awaiting the resurrection of the body. Angels are a distinct order of being, created before humanity. You will never be an angel; you are called to something the angels cannot attain — a glorified body at the resurrection.\n\n**IV. Only two choirs have wings in Scripture.** Seraphim have six wings (Isaiah 6:2) and Cherubim have four (Ezekiel 1:6). When angels appear as men throughout the rest of Scripture, they are never described as winged. The winged messenger of popular imagery conflates distinct realities.\n\n**V. The Cherubim are not chubby infants.** The *putti* of Renaissance art have no basis in Scripture or theology. The Cherubim are formidable, blazing, multi-faced guardians of the divine throne — among the most powerful beings in creation. This confusion is worth naming early and naming clearly.\n\n> [Psalm 148:2-5](data-scripture="Psalm 148:2") "Praise him, all his angels; praise him, all his hosts... for he commanded, and they were created."\n\n### The Thread That Runs Through This Course\n\nBefore we go further, one truth should be stated plainly and returned to throughout every lesson that follows:\n\n**You are never alone. The entire angelic creation — from the Seraphim burning before the throne to the guardian walking beside you this moment — is ordered toward God's glory and, within that, toward your salvation.**\n\nThe Seraphim burn with love for the God who made you. The Cherubim guard the mysteries that include your redemption. The Virtues sustain the natural world you inhabit. The Principalities protect the Church you belong to. The Archangels carry out the missions that brought about your rescue. And one member of the lowest choir has been assigned to you personally — by divine appointment, from before your first breath.\n\nThis is the world you actually live in. The rest of this course is the map.\n\n---\n\n*Next lesson: Before we can understand what angels do, we need to understand how they think — and it is unlike anything in human experience. The answer may be the most astonishing fact in all of angelology.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612v4000jgeo01v2ejdwo	cmq6612v0000fgeo0goukqfcs	Lesson 6 — The Cherubim: Guardians of Divine Wisdom	READING	900	1	\N	t	![Lesson 6 — The Cherubim: Guardians of Divine Wisdom](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OswiRSqbNv3tcSjXbK960OEaP1ghrDBudGzUTQ)\n\n## The Cherubim — Guardians of Divine Wisdom\n\n### A Thread Running Through the Whole Bible\n\nBefore we define the Cherubim, trace this thread.\n\nAt the east of the garden of Eden: Cherubim, with a flaming sword ([Genesis 3:24](data-scripture="Genesis 3:24")).\n\nAbove the Ark of the Covenant in the wilderness: two golden Cherubim, wings spread, face to face above the mercy seat ([Exodus 25:18-22](data-scripture="Exodus 25:18")).\n\nIn the innermost chamber of Solomon's Temple: enormous carved Cherubim of olive wood, fifteen feet tall, their wings spanning the full width of the Holy of Holies ([1 Kings 6:23-28](data-scripture="1 Kings 6:23")).\n\nIn Ezekiel's great vision: four-faced living creatures bearing the very throne of God, charged with fire, wheels within wheels covered with eyes, blazing like coals — the Cherubim as the substrate of the divine chariot ([Ezekiel 1:4-28](data-scripture="Ezekiel 1:4")).\n\nOne principle runs through all of it: **wherever God's presence is specially located, the Cherubim are there.**\n\nThey are not decorative. They are not symbolic. They are the standing guard at every threshold of the sacred.\n\n### Etymology: Fullness of Knowledge\n\nThe Hebrew *kerubim* (singular: *kerub*) most likely derives from a term meaning "one who intercedes" or "one who blesses." The Greek translation renders it as signifying **"fullness of knowledge"** — and this rendering has shaped the tradition's entire understanding of what the Cherubim are.\n\nWhere the Seraphim are defined by love, the Cherubim are defined by **knowledge**. They possess the deepest intellectual contemplation of God's wisdom — they know God as the ultimate reason and cause of all things.\n\nThe Seraphim cry *that* God is holy. The Cherubim contemplate *why* He is holy — the inner logic of divine wisdom, the relationships among divine ideas, the plan of creation from inside God's own knowing.\n\n### The Ark and the Mercy Seat: Heaven Touching Earth\n\nGod's command for the Ark of the Covenant is among the most specific architectural instructions in Scripture: two golden Cherubim, facing each other, their wings spread upward and inward over the lid of the Ark, forming a canopy above the mercy seat.\n\nWhy? Because that precise location — above the mercy seat, between the wings of the Cherubim — is where God pledged to be *present*.\n\n> [Exodus 25:22](data-scripture="Exodus 25:22") "There I will meet with you, and from above the mercy seat, from between the two cherubim that are on the ark of the testimony, I will speak with you about all that I will give you in commandment for the people of Israel."\n\nThe Cherubim are the guardians of the covenant between God and man. They oversee the meeting point of heaven and earth. The golden statues commanded by God are an earthly representation of the actual Cherubim who stand guard around every genuine manifestation of God's presence.\n\nThis is why the Ark was treated with such reverence — to treat the Ark carelessly was to treat the threshold of heaven carelessly. The Cherubim made that threshold real.\n\n### Ezekiel's Vision: The Most Complex Angelic Appearance in Scripture\n\nThe visions of Ezekiel chapters 1 and 10 are the most elaborate descriptions of the Cherubim in the entire Bible. Each of the four creatures has:\n\n- Four faces: man, lion, ox, and eagle\n- Four wings: two for flight, two covering their bodies\n- The form of human hands beneath their wings\n- Legs like calves' legs with hooves like burnished bronze\n- The appearance of burning coals between them, and lightning flashing\n\nThey move in all four directions simultaneously, without turning. Alongside them roll enormous, terrifying wheels — wheels within wheels, covered with eyes all around. Above the creatures is an expanse like crystal; above the expanse, a throne of sapphire; above the throne, a figure like a man blazing with fire and surrounded by a rainbow.\n\nThis is not a vision of beauty in the decorative sense. It is a vision of *power* — controlled, directed, overwhelmingly real power in the service of a God who is present in creation but infinitely beyond it.\n\nThe Cherubim carry this presence. They are the vehicle of the divine glory.\n\n### The Problem of the Cherubs\n\nIt must be stated plainly, because the confusion runs deep in Western culture: the popular image of cherubs as chubby, winged infants (*putti* in Renaissance art) has no basis whatsoever in Scripture or theology.\n\nThis confusion arose from Renaissance artists borrowing a motif from pagan classical art — the *Eros* or *Cupid* figure — and conflating it with the biblical cherub. The result is one of the great misdirections in Western religious iconography. The Cherubim of Scripture are formidable, blazing, multi-faced guardians of the divine throne — among the most powerful beings in creation. To picture a chubby infant is to picture the opposite of what these beings are.\n\n### Cherubim and the Eucharist\n\nIn the New Covenant, the presence of God is localized not above a gold-covered box in a tent, but in the Eucharist — the body, blood, soul, and divinity of Jesus Christ in every tabernacle in every Catholic church on earth.\n\nThe tradition holds that the angels are present at every Mass, adoring that presence. The Cherubim, guardians of every place where God condescends to be specially present, are there. The tabernacle is the New Ark. The Mass is the New Covenant meeting. And the Cherubim are still keeping watch.\n\n---\n\n*Next: We leave the first two choirs — Love and Knowledge — and descend to the third, whose defining quality might be the most practically important: Stability. The Thrones communicate something the human soul desperately needs to know about God.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xgu30005hks8npdwk9bx	cmq76xgtn0001hks8s3kqs5yq	Lesson 12 — The Strongmen of Deception: The Lying Spirit, the Familiar Spirit, and the Perverse Spirit	READING	\N	1	\N	t	![Lesson 12 — The Strongmen of Deception: The Lying Spirit, the Familiar Spirit, and the Perverse Spirit](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OszjAFIekWfugPJQnG59DLqiMUp7vN2m4Xbyal)\n\n## Lesson 12 — The Strongmen of Deception: The Lying Spirit, the Familiar Spirit, and the Perverse Spirit\n\nAhab wanted a word from God that confirmed what he had already decided. He assembled 400 prophets and asked them whether he should go to war. They told him what he wanted to hear — unanimously, enthusiastically, with signs and prophetic theater. Only one dissented.\n\n[1 Kings 22:19-23](data-scripture="1 Kings 22:19-23"): Micaiah saw the throne room. A lying spirit had volunteered before the hosts of heaven — *"I will go forth, and I will be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets."* God permitted it. Ahab went to war. He died of a wound from an arrow shot "at random."\n\nThe lying spirit is not a metaphor. It is a named category of demonic operation — and it has been running the same play since the Garden.\n\n---\n\n## The Lying Spirit\n\n[John 8:44](data-scripture="John 8:44"): *"He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it."*\n\nThe Lying Spirit operates specifically through prophetic and revelatory channels — false prophecy, false teaching, false visions — producing confident, spiritually-toned communication that leads its recipients into destruction. Its signature is the false word that confirms existing desire: the prophetic word that tells you what you want to hear, the teacher who affirms your preferred theology, the "vision" that validates the decision you have already made.\n\nIts corporate manifestation is the spirit of strong delusion described in [2 Thessalonians 2:11](data-scripture="2 Thessalonians 2:11"): *"God shall send them strong delusion, that they should believe a lie."* The strong delusion is not God deceiving people — it is God permitting the Lying Spirit to operate fully in those who have consistently chosen falsehood over truth.\n\n## The Familiar Spirit\n\n[Leviticus 20:27](data-scripture="Leviticus 20:27"): *"A man also or woman that hath a familiar spirit, or that is a wizard, shall surely be put to death."*\n\nThe familiar spirit is the entity that staffs mediumship, psychic practice, and divination. The Hebrew *ob* — translated "familiar spirit" — carries the sense of a spirit that has become personally acquainted with a household or individual, building a relationship of access and dependency over time. These are the entities that produce accurate information through psychics and mediums — information that appears to come from the deceased, from supernatural knowledge, or from "the universe."\n\nThe accuracy is real. The source is demonic. [1 Samuel 28](data-scripture="1 Samuel 28") is the canonical case: the witch of Endor, Saul's inquiry, and the entity that appeared — which may or may not have been the actual Samuel, depending on your reading of the text, but which in either case produced a genuine prophetic word through an illegitimate channel.\n\nThe familiar spirit's long game is dependency — establishing a relationship of consultation that replaces the Holy Spirit as the believer's primary source of guidance.\n\n## The Perverse Spirit\n\n[Isaiah 19:14](data-scripture="Isaiah 19:14"): *"The LORD hath mingled a perverse spirit in the midst thereof: and they have caused Egypt to err in every work thereof."*\n\nThe Spirit of Perversion (*ruach 'iwwim*) produces a systematic inversion of God's created order — moral confusion, sexual disorder, the twisting of language and meaning, the corruption of worship. It is the principality behind the sexual revolution, gender ideology, and the theological confusion that inverts the clear teaching of Scripture by calling good evil and evil good.\n\n[Isaiah 5:20](data-scripture="Isaiah 5:20"): *"Woe unto them that call evil good, and good evil; that put darkness for light, and light for darkness."* This is the Spirit of Perversion's specific output — the systematic inversion of categories.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nEach of these three strongmen operates through a specific vulnerability:\n\nThe Lying Spirit exploits the desire for confirmation — the human hunger to hear that we are right, that our plan is blessed, that the word we want is the word God is giving. The protection is [Isaiah 8:20](data-scripture="Isaiah 8:20"): *"To the law and to the testimony."* Every prophetic word, every spiritual impression, every "word from the Lord" must be tested against Scripture.\n\nThe Familiar Spirit exploits grief and the desire for contact with the deceased, for secret knowledge, for a consistent spiritual guide. The protection is radical dependence on the Holy Spirit as the only legitimate Paraclete — Counselor, Guide, and Spirit of truth.\n\nThe Spirit of Perversion exploits the theological openness that passes as intellectual humility — the willingness to "hold things loosely," to prioritize inclusion over clarity, to avoid the offense of biblical precision. The protection is [Romans 12:2](data-scripture="Romans 12:2"): the renewal of the mind through Scripture, not conformity to the world's shifting categories.\n\n---\n\n*Three strongmen of deception. The next lesson examines the strongmen that operate through the heart — through the emotional and relational vulnerabilities that every human being carries.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612un0005geo04nmedsiy	cmq6612ug0001geo0aum7jawk	Lesson 2 — How Angels Know: The Gift of Infused Knowledge	READING	900	1	\N	t	![Lesson 2 — How Angels Know: The Gift of Infused Knowledge](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsaP72DGEhtesUMivpomO8x4WSPknRFTuAI75Q)\n\n## How Angels Know — The Gift of Infused Knowledge\n\nHere is a thought experiment. Imagine you were born knowing everything knowable about the created universe — not gradually, through years of education, but instantaneously, at the first moment of your existence. Every scientific principle, every historical event, every language, every truth about every living creature. Not memorized, but simply *known* — the way you know you are reading right now, without having to try.\n\nThis is the ordinary condition of an angel.\n\n### The Engraved Tablet\n\nHuman intellects are blank slates filled in by experience. Angelic intellects are, in the memorable phrase of one theologian, **"engraved tablets."** All knowledge was *infused* — given immediately and completely by God at the moment of creation, without any process of learning through the senses.\n\nAn angel knows the essence and nature of every created thing not because it has observed them one by one, but because God placed that knowledge directly in its intellect.\n\nThomas Aquinas calls this *infused species* — intellectual forms implanted by God that function as the angel's permanent and complete repository of natural knowledge. The angel did not earn this knowledge. It did not develop it. It was given, whole and entire, in a single divine act.\n\n### Five Consequences That Follow\n\n**I. Angels cannot be in factual error about natural things.** Their natural knowledge is not derived from fallible sensation or uncertain inference. They simply know what they know with complete clarity. An angel asked about the nature of a hydrogen atom does not consult memory or reason toward an answer. It knows — as immediately as you know your own name.\n\n**II. The "answer immediately" phenomenon.** When an angel is questioned in Scripture, there is no pause for reflection. Gabriel does not take time to think before speaking to Daniel or to Mary. The answer has always been known. This immediacy is not quickness — it is the nature of angelic knowing. The answer existed before the question was asked.\n\n**III. Angels understand universally, not particularly.** When a human sees "this apple," they gradually abstract the concept "apple." An angel already possesses the universal species *apple* in its intellect and understands any particular apple through that universal. Angelic knowledge moves from universal to particular; human knowledge moves from particular to universal. This gives angelic knowledge a completeness human knowing can never fully achieve.\n\n**IV. Higher angels know more with fewer concepts.** Aquinas teaches that higher angels understand more through fewer, more universal intellectual forms, while lower angels require more numerous and particular species. This is a mark of intellectual perfection: the greatest intellect grasps the most with the fewest concepts. The hierarchy of knowledge mirrors the hierarchy of being.\n\n**V. Angels do not know everything.** Infused knowledge covers created things proportionate to an angel's nature. But no creature knows all that God knows. The hidden counsels of the divine will, the free future choices of human beings, the deepest mysteries of God's inner life — these are known to angels only if God specially reveals them. Angelic knowledge is vast but not infinite.\n\n### The Wonder of Being Witnessed\n\nThere is a consequence of angelic knowledge that is rarely emphasized but ought to be:\n\n**The angels knew you were coming.**\n\nWhen God created the angelic hierarchy and infused into each angel the knowledge of all created things — he gave them knowledge of you. Your existence, your nature, your assigned guardian — all of this was known to the angels before your first breath. You were not a surprise to heaven. The angel assigned to you was not scrambling to catch up. It knew its mission before the universe had a sun.\n\n> [Job 38:7](data-scripture="Job 38:7") "When the morning stars sang together, and all the sons of God shouted for joy."\n\nThe angels were present at the creation of the world and rejoiced in it. They are the original choir — the first creatures to offer praise to the Creator for a world that included, from the beginning, you.\n\n### What This Demands of Us\n\nThe perfection of angelic knowledge should inspire two responses in us.\n\nFirst, **reverence for divine wisdom** — the God who gave the angels their comprehensive knowledge is the same God who reveals Himself to us in Scripture. The difficulty we experience in understanding His ways is not a defect in Him. It is the gap between the engraved tablet and the blank slate still being filled in.\n\nSecond, **patience with the process.** We are not angels. We are precisely the creatures who must learn slowly, through experience, through suffering, through encounter with particular things. This is not a deficiency to be overcome; it is the nature of what we are. The journey is part of the gift.\n\n---\n\n*Next lesson: Having seen how angels know, we turn to how they were made — and the answer is more surprising than you might expect. God did not build the angelic hierarchy gradually. He spoke it into existence all at once, complete and entire, in a single act.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612vi000xgeo0z961cywt	cmq6612ve000tgeo0b9n1d4af	Lesson 10 — The Powers and Principalities: Defenders of Order	READING	900	1	\N	t	![Lesson 10 — The Powers and Principalities: Defenders of Order](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsSvCwccJ9p8Osi7f2L3jgeayVJxF6MbNCPdun)\n\n## The Powers and Principalities — Defenders of Order and Guardians of Nations\n\n### A Dimension of History You Were Never Taught\n\nEvery history class you have ever taken described the rise and fall of empires, the outcomes of wars, the spread of religions, the birth and death of civilizations — and described them entirely in terms of human decisions, economic forces, climate, and chance.\n\nThe theology of the Principalities says this account, while true as far as it goes, is incomplete by exactly one dimension.\n\nBehind every empire, every civilization, every great religious movement, every nation's rise and fall, there is an angelic — or, where nations have rejected God, a divinely-permitted demonic — dimension of governance. History is not merely a human story. It is a story with a heavenly floor.\n\nWe begin with the choir responsible for creation's laws before ascending to the Principalities who govern nations.\n\n---\n\n### The Powers: Defenders of Cosmic Order\n\n**Etymology.** From the Greek *exousiai* — authorities, powers. This word appears repeatedly in Paul's letters when he describes the structure of the spiritual world.\n\n**Character.** If the Virtues are the engineers who sustain the physical order, the Powers are the defenders who guard it. Their function is to uphold the integrity of creation's laws — to ensure that the structure God built into the cosmos is not violated.\n\nPaul's list of powers in [Romans 8:38-39](data-scripture="Romans 8:38") is among the most consoling passages in the New Testament:\n\n> [Romans 8:38-39](data-scripture="Romans 8:38") "For I am sure that neither death nor life, nor angels nor rulers, nor things present nor things to come, nor powers, nor height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God in Christ Jesus our Lord."\n\nThe Powers are named here as one of the potential separators — and immediately dismissed. Whatever powers exist in the cosmic order, above and below, visible and invisible, none of them can undo what God has done in Christ. The love of God in Christ Jesus is the one force in the universe that outranks everything the Powers guard.\n\nThis is not a small claim. This is the entire ordering of the cosmos placed subordinate to one thing: the love of God for those He has redeemed.\n\n---\n\n### The Principalities: Guardians of Peoples\n\n**Etymology.** From the Latin *principatus* and Greek *archai* — beginnings, first principles, ruling authorities. A "principality" is a domain ruled by a prince.\n\n**Position and Function.** The Principalities lead the third hierarchy and stand as the bridge between the governing angels of the second hierarchy and the angels most directly involved with individual human beings. Their domain is **collective human organization** — nations, peoples, civilizations, and ecclesial structures.\n\nNot individuals — that is the work of guardian angels. Peoples.\n\nPseudo-Dionysius described them as manifesting *"Godlike Princeliness and authoritativeness in an Order which is holy and most fitting to the Princely Powers."* They govern at the scale of civilization — the spiritual structure and direction of human communities over centuries.\n\n### Michael: The Great Prince\n\nThe most explicit biblical text on the Principalities is also one of the most dramatic passages in the Book of Daniel.\n\nIn Daniel 10, Gabriel explains to Daniel why his prayer was delayed for twenty-one days: *"The prince of the kingdom of Persia withstood me twenty-one days, but Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me."*\n\nThe "prince of Persia" here is the Principality — apparently a demonic one — governing that empire. Gabriel, an archangel of the highest distinction, was opposed by this Principality for three weeks and needed Michael's intervention to break through.\n\nThis is a window into the angelic and demonic dimension of political history. When Persia rises, when Persia falls, when the Greek empire succeeds it, when Rome follows — these are not only political and military events. They have a heavenly dimension that Daniel is uniquely permitted to see.\n\nAnd at the center of it, protecting God's people, stands Michael.\n\n> [Daniel 12:1](data-scripture="Daniel 12:1") "At that time shall arise Michael, the great prince who has charge of your people. And there shall be a time of trouble, such as never has been since there was a nation till that time. But at that time your people shall be delivered, everyone whose name shall be found written in the book."\n\nMichael is identified as the Principality specifically assigned to Israel — and in the New Covenant, to the Church. This is not tradition or speculation. It is the direct testimony of Scripture. The Church has a Principality, appointed by God, whose specific mission is her protection.\n\nWhen the Church prays the prayer of Michael — *"Michael the Archangel, defend us in battle"* — she is invoking a being who knows his commission and has held it since the beginning.\n\n---\n\n### A Nation, A Church, A Person\n\nThis lesson has ranged across the governance of nations and civilizations. It is worth bringing it closer.\n\nYou are part of a nation that has a Principality. Whether that Principality is faithful or demonic — whether it is one of the angels who maintained their estate or one of the fallen who seek to draw nations away from God — is something you will probably not know this side of heaven. What you know is that the nation you inhabit is not spiritually neutral, and that your prayers for it are not politically abstract. They are addressed to the God who governs nations through an angelic order that hears them.\n\nYou are part of a Church. Michael, *the great prince who has charge of your people* ([Daniel 12:1](data-scripture="Daniel 12:1")), has been specifically named as the Principality of God's covenant people. When the early Christians prayed the prayer of Michael, they were not invoking a symbol. They were addressing an actual being with an actual commission who has been at this work since before the Church existed.\n\nYou are a person. And here is the thing the Principalities' lesson teaches by contrast: they govern *peoples* — nations, civilizations, the Church as a whole. But you are not only a member of a people. You are a person.\n\nFor persons — for you, specifically — there is an angel assigned not to a nation or a civilization but to *you alone*. We will meet them in the third hierarchy.\n\n---\n\n*Next: We descend from the second hierarchy into the third — and from the governance of nations, we move to something more intimate: the angels assigned to carry out the most important missions in the history of creation. We begin with the three archangels Scripture names by name.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612v6000lgeo0pvq5e1m1	cmq6612v0000fgeo0goukqfcs	Supplement 3 — For Lessons 5 & 6	SUPPLEMENT	600	2	\N	t	![Supplement 3 — For Lessons 5 & 6](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os0oEJV05YvRZPna4mAuYVdrFHOBK7LSwy8Wio)\n\n## Supplement 3 — For Lessons 5 & 6: The Seraphim and Cherubim\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**Seraphim** (*saraph*, "to burn") — The highest choir of angels, defined by burning love for God. They stand closest to God in the order of creation.\n\n**Cherubim** (*kerub*) — The second choir, defined by fullness of divine knowledge. They guard the sacred: Eden, the Ark, the Temple, the throne of God.\n\n**Trisagion** — "Holy, Holy, Holy" — the hymn of the Seraphim in Isaiah 6:3, quoted in the *Sanctus* of every Mass.\n\n**Mercy Seat** (*kapporeth*) — The cover of the Ark of the Covenant, flanked by the golden Cherubim, where God promised to meet Israel (Ex. 25:22).\n\n**Beatific Vision** — Direct sight of God's essence; the Seraphim and Cherubim enjoy this eternally as the highest created beings.\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> Isa. 6:2-3 "Above him stood the seraphim. Each had six wings: with two he covered his face, and with two he covered his feet, and with two he flew. And one called to another and said: 'Holy, holy, holy is the Lord of hosts; the whole earth is full of his glory.'"\n\n> Gen. 3:24 "He drove out the man, and at the east of the garden of Eden he placed the cherubim and a flaming sword that turned every way to guard the way to the tree of life."\n\n> Ezek. 1:26 "And above the expanse over their heads there was the likeness of a throne... and seated above the likeness of a throne was a likeness with a human appearance."\n\n---\n\n### Comparison: Seraphim vs. Cherubim\n\n| Feature | Seraphim | Cherubim |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| Defining quality | Burning love | Fullness of knowledge |\n| Wings (Scripture) | Six (Isaiah 6:2) | Four (Ezekiel 1:6) |\n| Primary scriptural setting | Isaiah's throne vision | Ark of Covenant, Ezekiel's chariot |\n| Function | Ceaseless adoration | Guardianship of sacred presence |\n| Position in hierarchy | Highest (1st) | Second (2nd) |\n| Liturgical echo | The *Sanctus* at Mass | The golden Ark; the Eucharist |\n\n---\n\n### Questions for Reflection\n\n1. The Seraphim cover their faces before God. What does this tell us about the proper disposition of any creature in the presence of the Creator — including us in prayer?\n\n2. Isaiah, seeing the Seraphim, cries *"Woe is me! For I am lost; for I am a man of unclean lips"* (Isa. 6:5). The vision of holiness reveals sinfulness. Have you ever had a moment in prayer when beauty or holiness made you more aware of your need for purification?\n\n3. The Cherubim are placed wherever God's special presence is pledged — Eden, the Ark, the Temple. What does this consistent pattern reveal about the nature of holiness?\n\n4. The Mass quotes the Seraphim's song. The tradition holds that the angels attend every Eucharist. How might this awareness change the way you participate in Sunday worship?\n\n5. The Cherubim have four faces: man, lion, ox, and eagle. The Church tradition has long associated these four faces with the four Evangelists. What might this connection suggest about the relationship between Scripture and the angelic world?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xgu60007hks8gax5819p	cmq76xgtn0001hks8s3kqs5yq	Lesson 13 — The Strongmen of the Heart: Jealousy, Whoredom, and Pride	READING	\N	2	\N	t	![Lesson 13 — The Strongmen of the Heart: Jealousy, Whoredom, and Pride](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsokPmlbWxwEUd728la9hHriMsfOkGYRKDCuLZ)\n\n## Lesson 13 — The Strongmen of the Heart: Jealousy, Whoredom, and Pride\n\nSaul had everything. He was king. He had won the wars. His kingdom was established. The one thing he could not survive was hearing the women sing David's name louder than his own.\n\n[1 Samuel 18:8-9](data-scripture="1 Samuel 18:8-9"): *"And Saul was very wroth, and the saying displeased him... and Saul eyed David from that day and forward."*\n\nFrom that moment, every decision Saul made was made from inside a spirit — not his own ambition, not ordinary human jealousy, but a demonic principality that the text explicitly names: *"an evil spirit from the LORD"* came upon him. The Spirit of Jealousy had found its legal ground, and a king who had been chosen by God ended his life in a witch's house, asking a familiar spirit for guidance the night before his death.\n\n---\n\n## The Spirit of Jealousy\n\n[Numbers 5:14](data-scripture="Numbers 5:14"): *"The spirit of jealousy come upon him."* The Hebrew names it explicitly — *ruach qin'ah*, the Spirit of Jealousy. This is not ordinary human envy, which the flesh produces on its own. The Spirit of Jealousy is a demonic principality that operates through the emotional wound of comparison — the conviction that another person's success constitutes a personal loss.\n\nSaul's jealousy of David produced: murder attempts, the attempted manipulation of his own daughter, the massacre of the priests of Nob, progressive paranoia, the alienation of his son Jonathan, and ultimately full apostasy. The Spirit of Jealousy, given access through a single moment of comparison-based offense, dismantled a king's entire life over two decades.\n\nIts corporate manifestation is the spirit of competition that destroys churches, ministries, and families — the zero-sum orientation that treats every other person's elevation as a threat.\n\n## The Spirit of Whoredom\n\n[Hosea 4:12](data-scripture="Hosea 4:12"): *"The spirit of whoredoms hath caused them to err, and they have gone a whoring from under their God."*\n\n[Hosea 5:4](data-scripture="Hosea 5:4"): *"They will not frame their doings to turn unto their God: for the spirit of whoredoms is in the midst of them."*\n\nThe Spirit of Whoredom (*ruach zenunim*) operates at two levels simultaneously. At the physical level, it drives sexual addiction, promiscuity, pornography use, and the compulsive pursuit of sexual experience outside the covenant of marriage. At the spiritual level — which is its deeper and more dangerous operation — it drives the soul's tendency to seek satisfaction, comfort, and security from any source other than God.\n\nHosea's prophecy uses the marriage metaphor throughout: Israel's idolatry is spiritual adultery. The spirit behind both physical sexual unfaithfulness and spiritual idolatry is the same — the Spirit of Whoredom, which cannot tolerate exclusive covenant loyalty to God or to a spouse.\n\nIts signature in contemporary experience: the believer who cannot maintain consistent devotional life, who repeatedly cycles back to the same addictive behaviors despite genuine repentance, who feels inexplicably drawn to spiritual experiences from systems outside Christ.\n\n## The Spirit of Pride\n\n[Proverbs 16:18](data-scripture="Proverbs 16:18"): *"Pride goeth before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall."*\n\nThe Spirit of Pride is the oldest of the three — it is the spirit that originated in Lucifer himself: [Isaiah 14:13-14](data-scripture="Isaiah 14:13-14"): *"I will exalt my throne above the stars of God... I will be like the most High."*\n\nThe Spirit of Pride does not operate primarily through obvious arrogance. Its most effective form is spiritual pride — the pride of the person who has correct doctrine, genuine spiritual experience, or genuine holiness, and who allows those gifts to generate a posture of superiority over those who lack them. The Pharisee who prays correctly about his own righteousness in [Luke 18:11-12](data-scripture="Luke 18:11-12") is the canonical case.\n\nIts corporate manifestation is the church or ministry that cannot receive correction, that treats dissent as attack, and that eventually splits rather than submits.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThree strongmen of the heart — each operating through a specific emotional wound:\n\n**Jealousy** enters through comparison and requires the wound of feeling overlooked, undervalued, or superseded. Its eviction requires specific repentance for each act of comparison-based resentment, and the active choice to celebrate what God is doing in others as evidence of His faithfulness — not as a measure of your insufficiency.\n\n**Whoredom** enters through unmet covenant needs and broken attachment bonds. Its eviction requires addressing both the physical and spiritual dimensions — the specific sexual sins and the specific idolatries through which you have sought from created things what only God can provide.\n\n**Pride** enters through genuine gifting and genuine achievement, which make it the most dangerous of the three. Its eviction requires [James 4:6](data-scripture="James 4:6"): *"God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble."* The deliberate practice of submission — to God, to Scripture, to the body of Christ — is both the weapon against pride and the proof of its absence.\n\n---\n\n*Three strongmen of the heart. The next lesson examines the strongmen of affliction — the spirits that attack not through desire and ambition but through suffering and despair.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612uq0007geo0goxvka4n	cmq6612ug0001geo0aum7jawk	Supplement 1 — For Lessons 1 & 2	SUPPLEMENT	600	2	\N	t	![Supplement 1 — For Lessons 1 & 2](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OswCqqmVNv3tcSjXbK960OEaP1ghrDBudGzUTQ)\n\n## Supplement 1 — For Lessons 1 & 2: The Nature and Knowledge of Angels\n\n### Before You Review: A Challenge\n\nAnswer this question from memory before reading the rest of this supplement:\n\n*What is the single most surprising fact you learned in Lessons 1 or 2 — the thing that most contradicted what you assumed going in?*\n\nHold that answer. Return to it at the end.\n\n---\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**Pure Spirit** — A being with no material component; existing as intellect and will without a body. The nature of angels, as distinct from the *function* described by the word "angel."\n\n**Infused Knowledge** — Knowledge given directly by God to the angelic intellect at creation, without any process of learning through experience. The angel's knowledge is not earned or built; it is *given*.\n\n**Angelic Species** — Because angels have no matter to individuate them, each angel is its own unique species. There are as many species of angels as there are individual angels.\n\n**Affective Movement of the Will** — The angelic equivalent of emotion: a real orientation of the will toward love, joy, or intensity — located in the will, not in a body or sensory appetite.\n\n**"Angel" as Office** — The word *angelos* means messenger. It describes what angels *do*, not what they *are*. Their nature is *pure spirit*. Some of the highest angels are never sent on missions at all.\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> [Psalm 148:2, 5](data-scripture="Psalm 148:2") "Praise him, all his angels; praise him, all his hosts... for he commanded, and they were created."\n\n> [Hebrews 1:14](data-scripture="Hebrews 1:14") "Are they not all ministering spirits sent out to serve for the sake of those who are to inherit salvation?"\n\n> [Job 38:7](data-scripture="Job 38:7") "When the morning stars sang together, and all the sons of God shouted for joy."\n\n---\n\n### Quick Comparison: Angels vs. Humans\n\n| Feature | Angels | Human Beings |\n|---------|--------|-------------|\n| Body | None — pure spirit | Soul united to a physical body |\n| Knowledge | Infused at creation | Acquired through senses over time |\n| Individuation | Each is its own species | Individuated by matter |\n| Emotions | Affective movements of the will | Bodily passions + will |\n| Learning | Does not happen — all given | The defining feature of human growth |\n| Error | Cannot err about natural things | Constantly prone to error |\n\n---\n\n### Five Questions — Chosen for Bite, Not Comfort\n\n1. The tradition says each angel is its own species — as distinct from every other angel as a horse is from a dog. The number of angelic species equals the number of individual angels. If that is true, what does it suggest about how God values unique individuality? And does that bear on how He values yours?\n\n2. Your guardian angel knew you were coming before you were born — as part of its infused knowledge at creation. How does it feel to sit with the idea that you were known and anticipated in heaven before your first breath?\n\n3. Thomas says angels cannot be in factual error about natural things. What would it feel like to *know* rather than *believe* something? What is the difference — and why does that difference matter for how we relate to God?\n\n4. The word "angel" describes a function, not a nature. The Seraphim closest to God are technically never "sent" anywhere. In your own life, what is the difference between your *function* (what you do) and your *nature* (what you are)? Are you defining yourself by function when you should be defining yourself by nature?\n\n5. Now return to your answer from the opening challenge. What did you answer — and why does that particular thing surprise you? What assumption did you have that the lesson displaced?	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612v8000ngeo03byfmsyu	cmq6612v0000fgeo0goukqfcs	Lesson 7 — The Thrones: Expressions of Divine Authority	READING	900	3	\N	t	![Lesson 7 — The Thrones: Expressions of Divine Authority](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OswTRi0jNv3tcSjXbK960OEaP1ghrDBudGzUTQ)\n\n## The Thrones — Expressions of Divine Authority and Justice\n\n### One Night in Jerusalem — 185,000 Men\n\nThe year is approximately 701 BC. The Assyrian army under Sennacherib — the most powerful military force the ancient world had yet produced — has encircled Jerusalem. The city has no realistic hope of relief. Hezekiah has received a letter from Sennacherib that mocks the God of Israel along with every other god the Assyrians have defeated. He goes to the temple, spreads the letter before the Lord, and prays.\n\nThe prophet Isaiah sends a response: *"Do not be afraid."*\n\nThat night, something happens:\n\n> [Isaiah 37:36](data-scripture="Isaiah 37:36") "And the angel of the Lord went out and struck down 185,000 in the camp of the Assyrians. And when people arose early in the morning, behold, these were all dead bodies."\n\nOne angel. One night. One hundred and eighty-five thousand.\n\nSennacherib broke camp, returned to Nineveh, and was shortly thereafter assassinated by his own sons. The threat that had seemed unstoppable — the letter that mocked the throne of God — dissolved overnight.\n\nTheology, with all its precision, can give you the categories. But sometimes you need a scene first. This is what angelic authority looks like in history: a judgment executed overnight, a siege lifted at dawn, a superpower turned aside by a single act of divine will enacted through a single created being.\n\nThis is the context for understanding the **Thrones**.\n\n### The Stable Things\n\nThe Thrones are the angels whose defining quality is the stability, immovability, and majestic power of God. Their very name — *throne* — communicates: here authority rests. Here judgment is issued. Here sovereignty is exercised. And it has never, not for a moment, been otherwise.\n\n### Etymology and Image\n\nThe Thrones take their name from the *thronos* — the seat or throne of a king. In the ancient world, a throne was not merely a piece of furniture. It was a *statement* — a material declaration of authority, continuity, and the established order of things. The one who sat on a throne was saying: *this will not change.*\n\nThe Thrones, as an angelic choir, are the living expression of that statement about God. They are not abstract ideas about divine authority. They are personal beings, created to embody and contemplate the stability of God's sovereignty.\n\n### Scriptural Foundation\n\n**Colossians 1:16** — *"Whether thrones or dominions or rulers or powers — all things were created through him and for him."* Paul's explicit listing of the angelic thrones confirms their existence and — crucially — their creation in and for Christ. Even the angels who embody divine authority exist *for* the one who holds all authority by right.\n\n**Daniel 7:9** — The Ancient of Days takes His seat on a throne of fiery flames with wheels of burning fire:\n\n> [Daniel 7:9-10](data-scripture="Daniel 7:9") "As I looked, thrones were placed, and the Ancient of Days took his seat; his clothing was white as snow, and the hair of his head like pure wool; his throne was fiery flames; its wheels were burning fire. A stream of fire issued and came out from before him; a thousand thousands served him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him; the court sat in judgment, and the books were opened."\n\nThis is the scene the Thrones contemplate: the Ancient of Days on the fiery throne, the books of judgment opened, the whole of history under review. The Thrones exist within this vision — they are the angels who mediate between God's eternal judicial act and the governance of creation.\n\n### The Thrones and Divine Providence\n\nHere is what makes the Thrones practically significant for the spiritual life: they are the angels most directly concerned with *how God governs everything.*\n\nThe cosmos is not self-governing. Creation does not sustain itself or find its own end by its own internal logic. At every moment, it is governed by an active, personal God whose will is enacted through a hierarchy of beings. The Thrones are those beings who see God's providential plan whole — who hold the full picture of where history is going and why, and reflect it back as the stable foundation upon which everything else rests.\n\nPseudo-Dionysius described the Thrones as those who *"are raised above every earthly defiling influence, and are forever separated from what is inferior."* This elevation is not pride — it is the condition required for the perspective their function demands. To see the whole of providence clearly, they must be raised above the flux of particulars.\n\n### What the Thrones Teach Us to Pray\n\nThe Thrones' defining quality — stability grounded in sovereign authority — gives our prayer a particular shape.\n\nThere is a kind of prayer that seeks to change God's mind. There is a kind that seeks to understand God's will. There is a kind that seeks to rest in it. The Thrones call us especially to the third.\n\nThe Lord's Prayer is instructive: it begins not with petition but with acknowledgment of the throne:\n\n> *"Our Father who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name, thy kingdom come, thy will be done, on earth as it is in heaven."*\n\nBefore any request is made, the sovereignty is honored. Before any need is presented, the authority is affirmed. This is not formalism — it is the correct orientation of a creature before its Creator. The Thrones embody this orientation in its purest form.\n\n### A Word for Troubled Times\n\nIn every period of crisis — and the Church has known many — the doctrine of the Thrones speaks a specific word:\n\n*The throne is not empty. The books are open. The judgment is proceeding. Nothing that happens in history falls outside the purview of the One who sits on the throne of fiery flames.*\n\nThis is not passive resignation. It is the foundation of active trust. The Thrones are not passively contemplating a static God. They are contemplating the dynamic, living sovereignty of the God who is moving all of history toward its appointed end — and who will not be stopped.\n\n---\n\n*Next: We close Part II with a vision that may be the most overwhelming in the entire Bible — four living creatures who have been crying "Holy, holy, holy" without pause since the first moment of their existence, and whose faces you may already know from another context entirely.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612us0009geo0loz4ec77	cmq6612ug0001geo0aum7jawk	Lesson 3 — The Creation of Angels: Instantaneous and Complete	READING	900	3	\N	t	![Lesson 3 — The Creation of Angels: Instantaneous and Complete](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os4or0c6L3Ls52XczwCYNqdZVf8hMUGlEvQ0nD)\n\n## The Creation of Angels — Instantaneous and Complete\n\nPicture the largest stadium you have ever been in — seventy, eighty, a hundred thousand people. Now multiply that by a billion. Then multiply it again. Traditional theology, drawing on Scripture's hints at the vastness of the heavenly host, holds that the number of angels is measured in the billions — perhaps many billions. Each one a unique species. Each one possessing a perfect intellect. Each one assigned a specific, divinely determined task.\n\nGod did not create this host over time, in stages, allowing each tier to form before adding the next. He created it **all at once** — complete, entire, and perfect — in a single act outside of time.\n\n### The Fourth Lateran Council\n\nThis is not speculation. The Fourth Lateran Council (1215), the most authoritative medieval council of the Church, declared that God *"from the beginning of time made at once (simul) out of nothing both orders of creatures, the spiritual and the corporeal."*\n\n*Simul.* At the same time. In the same act. The entire hierarchy of nine choirs, comprising billions of individual persons, each endowed with unique intellect, each knowing immediately its own nature and its place in the order of creation — all of this came into being in one divine moment.\n\nThis is theologically significant: God's creative act is not a temporal unfolding subject to development. When He created the angelic world, it came into being in its fullness — not as a sketch to be refined, but as a completed masterwork.\n\n### The Three Moments of Angelic Creation\n\nThomas Aquinas distinguishes three conceptual "moments" within this single instantaneous event. These are not three periods of time but three *aspects* of what happened at once.\n\n---\n\n**First Moment: Creation and the Infusion of Knowledge**\n\nThe moment angels were created, they were created with complete natural knowledge — including knowledge of God, of their own nature, of their place in the hierarchy, and of their assigned task. Nothing was withheld. Nothing needed to be learned.\n\n---\n\n**Second Moment: The Test of Will**\n\nHere is the dramatic center of angelic creation. With perfect knowledge came a free choice.\n\nEvery angel — simultaneously, in the same instant — faced the question: *Will you accept what God made you for?*\n\nThis was not a test of ignorance. They knew everything relevant. They knew what God is. They knew what they were. They knew their task with total clarity. And they knew whether that task involved any sacrifice — any position that might have seemed lower than their capacities could demand.\n\nThe angel who was given a humble station in the hierarchy could see clearly that angels above it were performing grander works. It could see exactly what it was being asked to accept. And it had to answer: *yes* or *no*.\n\n---\n\n**Third Moment: The Eternal State**\n\nThose who freely chose God were immediately confirmed in grace — their wills fixed forever in love, given the Beatific Vision as their eternal reward. Their choice was permanent not because freedom was removed, but because the will, having fully engaged with perfect knowledge and chosen the highest good, was satisfied in a way that admits no revision.\n\n---\n\n### The Most Remarkable Thing About Every Angel You Will Study\n\nThe theological tradition, following Thomas Aquinas and developed by Fr. Chad Ripperger, holds that **every single angel was created for a specific task**. Not a general role. Not a broad calling. A *particular*, *divinely-determined mission* revealed to that angel at the moment of its creation as part of its infused knowledge.\n\nThe angel knew immediately: *This is what God made me for.*\n\nConsider what this means for the angels we will study:\n\n| Angel | The Mission | Given At |\n|-------|------------|---------|\n| **Gabriel** | The Annunciation to Mary | The moment of creation |\n| **Michael** | Guardian of the elect | The moment of creation |\n| **Raphael** | Healing and accompaniment of Tobias | The moment of creation |\n| **Your guardian angel** | You, specifically | The moment of creation |\n\nGabriel did not apply for the Annunciation. Michael did not earn his commission. The angel assigned to you did not receive you as an afterthought. These missions were not distributed after the fact — they were *constitutive* of the angels' very existence. Gabriel *is* the angel of the Annunciation in the deepest ontological sense. It could not have been otherwise.\n\n**There is no waste, no redundancy, no accident in the angelic creation.** Every angel that exists, exists for a reason that is as specific as its unique species.\n\n> [Colossians 1:16](data-scripture="Colossians 1:16") "For by him all things were created, in heaven and on earth, visible and invisible, whether thrones or dominions or rulers or powers — all things were created through him and for him."\n\n---\n\n*Next lesson: We have established the nature and origin of the angelic host. Now we trace where they appear — from the garden of Eden to the Apocalypse of John, the angels are present at every turning point of sacred history. We begin to read the scriptural map.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xgu80009hks8fa2d5af9	cmq76xgtn0001hks8s3kqs5yq	Lesson 14 — The Strongmen of Affliction: Heaviness, Fear, and Bondage	READING	\N	3	\N	t	![Lesson 14 — The Strongmen of Affliction: Heaviness, Fear, and Bondage](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os4fei4vL3Ls52XczwCYNqdZVf8hMUGlEvQ0nD)\n\n## Lesson 14 — The Strongmen of Affliction: Heaviness, Fear, and Bondage\n\nJob's suffering begins not with Job but with a conversation in heaven. Satan appears before God with a specific accusation and a specific request: remove the protection, and Job will curse God to His face. The permission is granted. The affliction begins.\n\nWhat follows is not random suffering. It is a targeted demonic assault — orchestrated, intentional, and operating within specific boundaries set by God. The friends who come to comfort Job are not merely theologically wrong. They are functioning as additional instruments of the same spiritual attack, reinforcing the central accusation: that Job's suffering is evidence of his sin and God's judgment.\n\nJob endures. He argues. He laments. He does not curse God. And in the end, [Job 42:10](data-scripture="Job 42:10"): *"The LORD turned the captivity of Job... and the LORD gave Job twice as much as he had before."*\n\n---\n\n## The Spirit of Heaviness\n\n[Isaiah 61:3](data-scripture="Isaiah 61:3"): *"To appoint unto them that mourn in Zion, to give unto them beauty for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness."*\n\nThe Spirit of Heaviness (*ruach kehah*) is a demonic strongman that operates through grief, loss, and chronic despair. Its signature is a weight that does not lift — a persistent depression that is resistant to circumstances changing, to prayer, to medication, to counseling, because it is not entirely explained by any of those categories. It functions as a spiritual atmosphere layered over the soul, muffling worship, dulling the experience of God's presence, and producing a chronic inability to receive or sustain joy.\n\nIts legal ground is grief not fully surrendered to God, bitterness that has hardened over time, and generational patterns of melancholy that have become a family's spiritual inheritance.\n\nThe antidote Scripture prescribes is specific: *"the garment of praise."* Praise is not a mood — it is an act of spiritual warfare. It is the direct counter to the Spirit of Heaviness because it asserts, against all felt evidence, that God is good and worthy of worship. It is the same weapon Paul and Silas used in the Philippian jail ([Acts 16:25](data-scripture="Acts 16:25")) — and their worship opened prison doors.\n\n## The Spirit of Fear\n\n[2 Timothy 1:7](data-scripture="2 Timothy 1:7"): *"For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind."*\n\nThe Spirit of Fear is among the most common demonic strongmen in operation today, driving anxiety disorders, phobias, paranoia, and the chronic low-grade dread that prevents believers from stepping into their calling. Its signature is a fear response disproportionate to the actual threat — fear of illness, of abandonment, of failure, of the future — that cannot be resolved by rational reassurance alone because its source is not rational.\n\n[1 John 4:18](data-scripture="1 John 4:18"): *"There is no fear in love; but perfect love casteth out fear: because fear hath torment."* Fear and love cannot coexist at the level of the spirit. The Spirit of Fear specifically targets the believer's understanding of God's character — it replaces the Father's perfect love with an image of a God who is unpredictable, punitive, or absent. Its eviction requires both renunciation and a specific rebuilding of the understanding of God's character through Scripture.\n\n## The Spirit of Bondage\n\n[Romans 8:15](data-scripture="Romans 8:15"): *"For ye have not received the spirit of bondage again to fear; but ye have received the Spirit of adoption, whereby we cry, Abba, Father."*\n\nThe Spirit of Bondage is the principality behind addiction — the specific demonic strongman that hijacks the soul's God-designed capacity for attachment and directs it toward a substance, behavior, or person. It is not mere psychological habit. The Spirit of Bondage produces a compulsion that overrides the will, that resists both willpower and therapy because it is operating at a level that neither willpower nor therapy fully addresses.\n\nIts legal ground is the initial voluntary act of opening a door — the first drink, the first hit, the first episode, the first time — which, combined with repetition, gives the Spirit of Bondage increasingly deep access. Its eviction requires both the spiritual work of renunciation and the practical work of accountability, community, and the restructuring of environmental triggers.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\n[Isaiah 61:1](data-scripture="Isaiah 61:1"): *"The Spirit of the Lord GOD is upon me; because the LORD hath anointed me to preach good tidings unto the meek; he hath sent me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives, and the opening of the prison to them that are bound."*\n\nJesus read this text in the synagogue at Nazareth and said: *"This day is this scripture fulfilled in your ears."* [Luke 4:21](data-scripture="Luke 4:21"). The anointing of Isaiah 61 is specifically for the three conditions examined in this lesson: the brokenhearted (Spirit of Heaviness), the captives (Spirit of Fear), and those bound in prison (Spirit of Bondage).\n\nThe strongmen of affliction are real. But the anointing against them is also real — and it was placed on Jesus, and through the Spirit, on every believer who has been baptized into His death and resurrection.\n\n---\n\n*Three strongmen of affliction. The final lesson in Part VI examines the strongmen of the body and the last days — the spirits that attack physical health and prepare the world for its final confrontation.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612va000pgeo019mep2tx	cmq6612v0000fgeo0goukqfcs	Lesson 8 — The Living Creatures and the Eternal Worship of Heaven	READING	900	4	\N	t	![Lesson 8 — The Living Creatures and the Eternal Worship of Heaven](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os4VeyGcL3Ls52XczwCYNqdZVf8hMUGlEvQ0nD)\n\n## The Living Creatures and the Eternal Worship of Heaven\n\n### The Scene in Revelation 4\n\nThe Apostle John, exiled on the island of Patmos, is caught up in the Spirit and brought before the throne of God. What he describes in Revelation chapters 4 and 5 is the most comprehensive vision of heavenly worship in the New Testament.\n\nThe throne is surrounded by twenty-four elders. There is a sea of glass like crystal. Lightning and thunder proceed from the throne. Seven burning lamps stand before it.\n\nAnd around the throne — in the midst of it, on every side of it — are four living creatures:\n\n> [Revelation 4:6-8](data-scripture="Revelation 4:6") "Around the throne, on each side of the throne, are four living creatures, full of eyes in front and behind: the first living creature like a lion, the second living creature like an ox, the third living creature with the face of a man, and the fourth living creature like an eagle in flight. And the four living creatures, each of them with six wings, are full of eyes all around and within, and day and night they never cease to say, 'Holy, holy, holy, is the Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come!'"\n\n*Full of eyes* — before, behind, all around, and within. Nothing is hidden from them. They see in every direction simultaneously, including inward.\n\n*Day and night they never cease.* This is the most significant phrase in the description. Not "frequently." Not "devotedly." Never cease. Not once. Not for a moment. Since the beginning of their existence and into eternity, the song has not stopped.\n\n### Who Are the Living Creatures?\n\nThese beings do not map neatly onto the Seraphim or Cherubim, though they share characteristics with both:\n\n- Like the Seraphim, they have **six wings** and cry "Holy, holy, holy."\n- Like the Cherubim in Ezekiel, they have **four faces** distributed among four beings.\n- Unlike either, they are described as placed *"in the midst of the throne"* — a position of even more intimate proximity to God than the Seraphim who *stand around* the throne in Isaiah's vision.\n\nSome traditions identify them with the Cherubim; others see them as a distinct category of throne-attendants. What is certain is their function: they lead the heavenly worship. Everything in the vision flows from their cry.\n\n### The Four Faces: A Hidden Key\n\nThe four faces of the living creatures — man, lion, ox, eagle — have carried a second meaning in the Church since at least the second century: they are the symbols of the four Evangelists.\n\n| Face | Evangelist | Why |\n|------|-----------|-----|\n| **Man** | Matthew | Opens with Christ's human genealogy |\n| **Lion** | Mark | Opens with the voice crying in the wilderness; royal power |\n| **Ox / Calf** | Luke | Opens with priestly sacrifice; the sacrificial animal |\n| **Eagle** | John | Soars to the heights of divine theology from the first verse |\n\nThis identification — found in Irenaeus, Jerome, and Gregory the Great — is not merely decorative symbolism. It is a theological statement: the four Evangelists who proclaimed the Gospel bear the same faces as the creatures who never cease to worship. The *proclamation of Christ* and the *adoration of Christ* are, in the end, the same act.\n\nTo preach the Gospel faithfully is to join the living creatures' song.\n\n### What "Never Cease" Means\n\nThe most striking phrase about the living creatures deserves extended reflection: *day and night they never cease.*\n\nThis is a window into eternity. In heaven, worship is not an activity among others — not something squeezed between meals and work and sleep. It is the fundamental state of being. The living creatures do not pause to attend to other things and then return to the song. The song is what they *are*.\n\nThe tradition teaches that the Beatific Vision — the direct, unmediated sight of God's essence — is so overwhelmingly beautiful, so infinitely satisfying to the intellect and will, that any creature encountering it *cannot but* respond with total adoration. The living creatures are not constrained against their will. They are so constituted that the joy of God's presence *is* the cry "Holy, holy, holy." The worship and the beatitude are not separable.\n\nThis is also the promise of heaven to the redeemed human soul. The fear that eternal life might be boring, or that ceaseless worship might be wearying, misunderstands what worship is. What we experience in our best moments of prayer — the quiet joy, the sense of arriving home, the relief of being seen and loved — is a distant echo of what the living creatures experience at full intensity, without interruption, forever.\n\n> [Revelation 4:11](data-scripture="Revelation 4:11") "Worthy are you, our Lord and God, to receive glory and honor and power, for you created all things, and by your will they existed and were created."\n\n---\n\n*Next: We descend from the first hierarchy — pure contemplation — into the second, whose work is governance. These are the angels who make sure the universe holds together, who sustain natural law, who are present when the impossible happens. We begin with the executives of heaven's government.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612uv000bgeo05oipwit7	cmq6612ug0001geo0aum7jawk	Lesson 4 — Angels Across Scripture: A Survey of Holy Appearances	READING	900	4	\N	t	![Lesson 4 — Angels Across Scripture: A Survey of Holy Appearances](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsZHKafydWQAzP5eOGYXjM0itdfBSUE9IN6u8o)\n\n## Angels Across Scripture — A Survey of Holy Appearances\n\nThere is a temptation, when studying angelology, to focus on the theological system — the hierarchy, the nature, the faculties — and to treat the scriptural appearances as mere illustrations. This lesson corrects that instinct.\n\nThe angels of Scripture are not illustrations of a theory. The theory exists to explain *them*. Begin with the appearances. The theology will follow.\n\n### In the Beginning — Angels at Creation and Eden\n\nThe Book of Job presents the angels as present at the foundation of the world, rejoicing as God laid the earth's cornerstone:\n\n> [Job 38:7](data-scripture="Job 38:7") "When the morning stars sang together and all the sons of God shouted for joy."\n\nThe first thing the angels ever did, as far as Scripture tells us, was to praise God for creation. Before any mission, before any governance, before any ministry to human beings — they worshipped. This is the primordial angelic act, and it never stops.\n\nAfter the first human sin, God placed Cherubim at the east of Eden to guard the way to the Tree of Life:\n\n> [Genesis 3:24](data-scripture="Genesis 3:24") "He drove out the man, and at the east of the garden of Eden he placed the cherubim and a flaming sword that turned every way to guard the way to the tree of life."\n\nThe very first angelic act recorded in Scripture after the fall is **guardianship** — angels set at the threshold of the sacred, protecting its holiness. This pattern will not vary. Wherever God's presence or the holy is specially located, the angels guard it.\n\n### The Patriarchal Age — Angels Among the Fathers\n\n**Hagar in the wilderness.** When Hagar flees Sarah's harshness, the Angel of the Lord finds her by a spring and promises her a multitude of descendants ([Genesis 16:7-13](data-scripture="Genesis 16:7")). God sends an angel to a woman the culture had already discarded. The angels minister especially to the vulnerable.\n\n**The three visitors to Abraham.** Three heavenly visitors appear at Mamre; Abraham offers hospitality and learns of the coming birth of Isaac ([Genesis 18:1-2](data-scripture="Genesis 18:1")). Two are angels; one is identified with the Lord Himself. This encounter shows angels participating in the announcement of the covenant's fulfillment.\n\n**Jacob's ladder.** Jacob dreams of a ladder reaching to heaven, with angels ascending and descending — a vision of unceasing heavenly-earthly commerce, angels moving between the realms of God and man in ceaseless ministry ([Genesis 28:12](data-scripture="Genesis 28:12")). Jesus will later claim this image for Himself: *"You will see heaven opened, and the angels of God ascending and descending on the Son of Man"* ([John 1:51](data-scripture="John 1:51")).\n\n**Jacob wrestling.** At the Jabbok ford, Jacob wrestles all night with a mysterious figure identified as an angel, and is renamed Israel: "one who strives with God" ([Genesis 32:24-30](data-scripture="Genesis 32:24")). Angels in Scripture are not always gentle. They can be agents of divine encounter and transformation — wrestling matches that leave a mark.\n\n### The Mosaic Era — Angels in Deliverance\n\n**The burning bush.** The Angel of the Lord appears in a flame of fire out of a bush that burns but is not consumed, and from this fire, God calls Moses to deliver His people ([Exodus 3:2](data-scripture="Exodus 3:2")). The angel is the medium of divine encounter — not replacing God but manifesting Him.\n\n**The pillar of cloud and fire.** Throughout the Exodus, *"the angel of God"* goes before the camp of Israel as a pillar of cloud by day and fire by night ([Exodus 14:19](data-scripture="Exodus 14:19")). The entire journey of liberation is marked by angelic accompaniment.\n\n**The Ark of the Covenant.** God commands two golden Cherubim to be placed atop the Ark, their wings spread above the mercy seat: *"There I will meet with you... I will speak with you"* ([Exodus 25:22](data-scripture="Exodus 25:22")). The Cherubim mark the earthly throne of the invisible God — the meeting place of heaven and earth.\n\n### The Prophetic Age — Vision and Interpretation\n\n**Isaiah's throne vision.** The Seraphim surround the throne, crying Holy, Holy, Holy; one touches Isaiah's lips with a burning coal ([Isaiah 6:1-7](data-scripture="Isaiah 6:1")). This is the foundational vision of the first hierarchy — explored at length in Part II.\n\n**Ezekiel's chariot-throne.** The four living creatures carry the divine chariot-throne; the whole vision is one of the most overwhelming in Scripture ([Ezekiel 1:4-28](data-scripture="Ezekiel 1:4")).\n\n**Daniel and the archangels.** Gabriel appears to Daniel twice to explain prophetic visions ([Daniel 8:16](data-scripture="Daniel 8:16")). Michael appears as "one of the chief princes" ([Daniel 10:13](data-scripture="Daniel 10:13")). For the first time in Scripture, angels are named and their distinct functions described.\n\n**Elijah under the broom tree.** The exhausted prophet, fleeing Jezebel, collapses and asks to die. An angel appears twice — not with theology but with bread and water: *"Arise and eat, for the journey is too great for you"* ([1 Kings 19:5-7](data-scripture="1 Kings 19:5")). This is one of the most tender moments in the entire Old Testament, and an angel is at the center of it.\n\n### The New Testament — Angels at Every Pivotal Moment\n\n**The Annunciation** ([Luke 1:26-38](data-scripture="Luke 1:26")). Gabriel comes to Nazareth. The message that changes everything is delivered by an angel to a young woman.\n\n**The Nativity** ([Luke 2:8-14](data-scripture="Luke 2:8")). An angel announces the birth to the shepherds; then a *"multitude of the heavenly host"* appears, praising God. The Incarnation is met by an angelic choir.\n\n**Gethsemane** ([Luke 22:43](data-scripture="Luke 22:43")). In His agony, *"there appeared to him an angel from heaven, strengthening him."* Even the Son of God, in His human nature, received angelic ministry.\n\n**The Resurrection** ([Matthew 28:2-7](data-scripture="Matthew 28:2")). An angel rolls back the stone; his appearance is like lightning. *"He is not here, for he has risen."* The resurrection is announced by an angel.\n\n**The Book of Revelation.** Angels pervade the entire Apocalypse — bearing seals, blowing trumpets, pouring bowls, surrounding the throne, and at the very end: *"I, Jesus, have sent my angel to testify to you about these things for the churches"* ([Revelation 22:16](data-scripture="Revelation 22:16")).\n\n### The Five Movements of Angelic Scripture\n\nLooking across the whole biblical witness, angelic appearances follow five consistent movements:\n\n1. **Worship first.** Before any mission, angels praise God. This is their fundamental state.\n2. **Guard the sacred.** Eden, the Ark, the tomb of Christ — wherever holiness is localized, angels stand guard.\n3. **Announce the new.** Every major covenant transition — the call of Abraham, the Exodus, the Incarnation, the Resurrection — is marked by angelic announcement.\n4. **Minister to the vulnerable.** Hagar, Elijah, the disciples in grief — angels appear precisely to those who have reached the end of themselves.\n5. **Interpret the mysterious.** Gabriel's visits to Daniel and Mary are acts of divine explanation — God using angels to make the incomprehensible intelligible.\n\n---\n\n### The Shadow Side of the Story\n\nEvery appearance in this lesson assumes something this lesson does not yet explain: that the angels you have read about here are the ones who *remained*. They are the faithful.\n\nScripture is equally clear that a portion of the angelic host did not remain faithful. The one Jesus called "the father of lies" was there at Eden — the same Eden where the Cherubim stood guard. *"He was a murderer from the beginning"* ([John 8:44](data-scripture="John 8:44")). Jude speaks of *"the angels who did not stay within their own position of authority, but left their proper dwelling"* ([Jude 1:6](data-scripture="Jude 1:6")). Peter writes of *"angels who sinned"* and were cast into chains of gloomy darkness to await judgment ([2 Peter 2:4](data-scripture="2 Peter 2:4")).\n\nThe angelic world is not uniformly glorious. The same nature that makes an angel capable of burning love makes a fallen angel capable of profound malice. The Cherubim at Eden's gate guard against a serpent who was once a being of the same order.\n\nThis course studies the faithful angels — the nine choirs in their proper glory. But to understand them fully, you must eventually study their opposites. The Demons course takes up exactly that task: the fall of Lucifer, the nature of demonic hierarchy, and the spiritual warfare that has been underway since before the first human being drew breath.\n\nFor now, hold both realities together: the angel who stands beside you in the light — and the fact that there are those who would oppose both of you in the dark.\n\n---\n\n*Next: We have surveyed the angels in action. Now we study them in their own order. Part II opens with the angels closest to God — the ones whose entire existence is pure worship. We begin with the choir whose name means "burning."*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xguc000bhks8wsrc7g36	cmq76xgtn0001hks8s3kqs5yq	Lesson 15 — The Strongmen of the Body and the End: Deaf & Dumb, Infirmity, and the Spirit of the Antichrist	READING	\N	4	\N	t	![Lesson 15 — The Strongmen of the Body and the End: Deaf & Dumb, Infirmity, and the Spirit of the Antichrist](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os2vUb8s08cxIDif0GQHZ4JjKrBLnPzSl1qsgF)\n\n## Lesson 15 — The Strongmen of the Body and the End: Deaf & Dumb, Infirmity, and the Spirit of the Antichrist\n\nThe disciples had failed. The father had brought his son to them and they could not cast out the spirit. The boy had been this way since childhood — thrown into fire, thrown into water, unable to speak, subject to seizures. When Jesus arrived, the spirit convulsed the boy and threw him to the ground foaming at the mouth.\n\n[Mark 9:25](data-scripture="Mark 9:25"): *"When Jesus saw that the people came running together, he rebuked the foul spirit, saying unto him, Thou dumb and deaf spirit, I charge thee, come out of him, and enter no more into him."*\n\nJesus named it. Deaf and dumb. Not a disease. A spirit with a specific assignment against the body's sensory and communicative functions. When it left, the boy was so still that many thought he was dead. Then he rose.\n\n[Mark 9:29](data-scripture="Mark 9:29"): *"This kind can come forth by nothing, but by prayer and fasting."*\n\n---\n\n## The Deaf and Dumb Spirit\n\nThe Deaf and Dumb Spirit (*pneuma alalon*) is a demonic strongman with a specific assignment: to block spiritual reception and spiritual communication simultaneously. In its physical manifestation, it produces muteness, deafness, and in some cases seizure disorders that have a demonic rather than merely neurological origin.\n\nIn its spiritual manifestation — which is its broader operation in the contemporary church — it produces the condition Jesus described in [Matthew 13:13](data-scripture="Matthew 13:13"): *"because they seeing see not; and hearing they hear not, neither do they understand."* A corporate Deaf and Dumb Spirit over a congregation produces an inability to receive prophetic word, an inability to speak truth, and an absence of genuine worship.\n\nJesus' instruction — prayer and fasting — specifically addresses this strongman. Fasting weakens the flesh's dominance and creates the spiritual sensitivity required to address a spirit of this depth. This is why prolonged deliverance work is often preceded by fasting.\n\n## The Spirit of Infirmity\n\n[Luke 13:11-12](data-scripture="Luke 13:11-12"): *"And, behold, there was a woman which had a spirit of infirmity eighteen years, and was bowed together, and could in no wise lift up herself. And when Jesus saw her, he called her to him, and said unto her, Woman, thou art loosed from thine infirmity."*\n\n[Luke 13:16](data-scripture="Luke 13:16"): *"And ought not this woman, being a daughter of Abraham, whom Satan hath bound, lo, these eighteen years, be loosed from this bond on the sabbath day?"*\n\nJesus described her condition as a bond — specifically named as Satan's work, specifically named as infirmity. The Spirit of Infirmity is the demonic principality behind illness that has a spiritual root — chronic conditions resistant to treatment, recurring illness in specific family lines, physical afflictions that correlate with periods of spiritual compromise or specific generational patterns.\n\nNot all illness is demonic. Scripture is clear that suffering can be redemptive, that the thorn in Paul's flesh was not removed, that Job's affliction was permitted for a purpose. The discernment required is whether a specific illness has a spiritual root and whether the Spirit of Infirmity has legal ground. When it does, medical treatment addresses the physical symptom while the spiritual root remains unaddressed — which is why some conditions remain treatment-resistant.\n\n## The Spirit of the Antichrist\n\n[1 John 4:3](data-scripture="1 John 4:3"): *"Every spirit that confesseth not that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is not of God: and this is that spirit of antichrist, whereof ye have heard that it should come; and even now already is it in the world."*\n\n[2 John 1:7](data-scripture="2 John 1:7"): *"For many deceivers are entered into the world, who confess not that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh."*\n\nThe Spirit of the Antichrist is the principality that opposes the specific confession: Jesus Christ — God in the flesh — crucified for sin, raised bodily, returning in judgment. This spirit is not limited to the future Antichrist figure of Revelation. It is operating now, in every system that denies the incarnation, the atonement, and the bodily resurrection.\n\nThe Spirit of the Antichrist is the governing spirit of false religion — not merely secular atheism, but the sophisticated theological frameworks that affirm a Christ who is not God incarnate, a salvation that is not through the cross, a resurrection that is not bodily and historical. Every prosperity gospel that replaces the cross with blessing, every progressive Christianity that replaces the risen Christ with a therapeutic ideal, every ecumenical framework that dissolves the exclusivity of [John 14:6](data-scripture="John 14:6") is operating under the Spirit of the Antichrist.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThe three strongmen in this lesson operate at the body, in health, and through theology. The response to each is the same authority that addressed them in Scripture:\n\nThe name of Jesus Christ — specifically and deliberately applied to the specific strongman — carries the authority that Mark 9 demonstrated. That authority was given to every believer: [Luke 10:19](data-scripture="Luke 10:19"): *"Behold, I give unto you power to tread on serpents and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy: and nothing shall by any means hurt you."*\n\nYou have the authority. The strongmen are named. The legal ground can be revoked. The final quiz for Part VI follows — and Part VII applies everything examined in these six lessons directly to the specific doorways through which strongmen gain access in contemporary life.\n\n---\n\n*The strongmen are identified. Part VII examines every specific door through which they enter — and how to close each one permanently.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgb5000x10b8wknso64k	cmq76cgaw000n10b8wrzhfrh1	Lesson 10 — The Demonic Influence on Nations and Culture	READING	900	4	\N	t	![Lesson 10 — The Demonic Influence on Nations and Culture](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsaF6WWMEhtesUMivpomO8x4WSPknRFTuAI75Q)\n\n## The Demonic Influence on Nations and Culture\n\nDaniel's prophecies reveal that spiritual warfare is not merely personal; it is **territorial and political**. The angel Gabriel was delayed for twenty-one days because the prince of Persia withstood him (Daniel 10:13). Michael, the archangel, came to assist. This is not poetic language; it is a description of real spiritual conflict over nations.\n\n### Territorial Spirits\n\nThe Bible reveals that high-ranking demons — principalities and powers — are assigned to specific territories. These "princes" exercise influence over governments, cultures, and social systems. When a nation turns away from God, it creates a vacuum that demonic powers rush to fill.\n\n> Psalm 106:34-37 — "They did not destroy the nations, concerning whom the LORD commanded them: but were mingled among the heathen, and learned their works. And they served their idols: which were a snare unto them. Yea, they sacrificed their sons and their daughters unto devils."\n\nIdolatry is not merely religious error; it is the worship of demons. When a culture embraces abortion, sexual immorality, and the denial of God's existence, it is not simply making philosophical choices — it is inviting demonic rule.\n\n### The Demonic Strategy for Nations\n\nSatan's strategy for nations follows a predictable pattern:\n\n1. **Remove God from public life** — Prayer is banned, Scripture is mocked, and God's laws are replaced with human opinion.\n\n2. **Corrupt the family** — Marriage is redefined, children are indoctrinated, and parental authority is undermined.\n\n3. **Devalue human life** — Abortion, euthanasia, and the glorification of death become normalized.\n\n4. **Promote sexual immorality** — What God calls sin is celebrated as freedom, and what God calls holy is condemned as hate.\n\n5. **Control information** — Truth is suppressed, lies are institutionalized, and anyone who speaks God's word is censored or persecuted.\n\n### The Church's Response\n\nThe Church is not powerless against national demonic strongholds. When believers pray, fast, preach the gospel, and live holy lives, they push back the darkness. Every soul saved is a territory reclaimed. Every family restored is a stronghold destroyed. Every church planted is a beachhead established in enemy territory.\n\n> 2 Chronicles 7:14 — "If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land."	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612vc000rgeo0gmsp7vl8	cmq6612v0000fgeo0goukqfcs	Supplement 4 — For Lessons 7 & 8	SUPPLEMENT	600	5	\N	t	![Supplement 4 — For Lessons 7 & 8](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Oslr32HAXBDwf9iQcORak6Sx8F3eyonuXqN5zM)\n\n## Supplement 4 — For Lessons 7 & 8: The Thrones and the Living Creatures\n\n### A Visitor's Guide to the Heavenly Throne Room\n\n---\n\nWhat follows is not a theology lecture. It is a tour.\n\nThe throne room of God appears in Scripture more often than most readers notice — and it is always the same room, seen from different vantage points. Isaiah sees it from the floor ([Isaiah 6:1-7](data-scripture="Isaiah 6:1")). Ezekiel sees it approaching ([Ezekiel 1:4-28](data-scripture="Ezekiel 1:4")). Daniel sees it in a night vision ([Daniel 7:9-10](data-scripture="Daniel 7:9")). John sees it across the threshold of the opened heaven ([Revelation 4:1-11](data-scripture="Revelation 4:1")).\n\nWalk through it once, carefully.\n\n---\n\n#### What You See: The Throne Itself\n\n> [Daniel 7:9](data-scripture="Daniel 7:9") "His throne was fiery flames; its wheels were burning fire. A stream of fire issued and came out from before him."\n\n**What it means:** Wheeled thrones appear in ancient Near Eastern imagery as the throne-chariots of kings — moveable, active authority. God's throne is not static. It does not remain in one place. It is present everywhere His sovereign will is enacted. The fire signals judgment: this is the seat where the books are opened and history is reviewed. The *wheels* connect this vision to Ezekiel's chariot-throne (*merkabah*), where the Cherubim bear the divine chariot through the cosmos.\n\n---\n\n#### What You Hear: The Living Creatures\n\n> [Revelation 4:8](data-scripture="Revelation 4:8") "Day and night they never cease to say, 'Holy, holy, holy, is the Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come!'"\n\n**Who they are:** The four living creatures (*zoa*) are placed "in the midst of the throne and around the throne" — the innermost circle of the divine court. They share the Cherubim's four faces (lion, ox, man, eagle) and the Seraphim's six wings and ceaseless praise. John's vision synthesizes the earlier prophetic visions into a single overwhelming image.\n\n**The triple holy:** The word *hagios* — holy — is the declaration that God is utterly unlike everything else that exists. The repetition of "holy, holy, holy" is not redundancy. In Hebrew idiom, repetition indicates superlative: *the most holy, beyond any comparison of holy.* The living creatures have been saying this since the first instant of their existence, and they have never found a moment when it was no longer true.\n\n**What it means for worship:** The early church placed the *Sanctus* — "Holy, Holy, Holy, Lord God of hosts" — at the climax of the Eucharistic prayer precisely because the Mass is understood as participation in this heavenly liturgy. When the congregation sings the Sanctus, the living creatures are already singing it. The joining is real.\n\n---\n\n#### What You Stand On: The Thrones Beneath You\n\n> [Colossians 1:16](data-scripture="Colossians 1:16") "Whether thrones or dominions or rulers or powers — all things were created through him and for him."\n\n**What they are:** The Thrones are not the divine throne — they are the angelic beings who embody and contemplate God's judicial authority. Pseudo-Dionysius calls them those who *"receive the highest gift of God most purely and immaculately."* Their proximity to God is not geographic but ontological: their nature is most perfectly ordered toward the contemplation of divine sovereignty.\n\n**What they hold:** When Daniel sees the books opened ([Daniel 7:10](data-scripture="Daniel 7:10")) — the cosmic review of all history — the Thrones are the angelic presence within which this judgment is carried out. They are the stability beneath every event in history. When empires rise and fall, the Thrones have not moved. When your world shakes, the Thrones have not shifted.\n\n**Their practical word to you:** You are not required to be stable. But you are permitted to rest in what is.\n\n---\n\n#### Four Faces — Four Dimensions of Divine Reality\n\nThe four faces of the living creatures appear in Ezekiel 1, Revelation 4, and have been interpreted by the Fathers as symbols of the four Gospels (lion = Mark, ox = Luke, man = Matthew, eagle = John). They can also be read as four dimensions of the one God as He is known in creation:\n\n| Face | Creature | What It Reveals |\n|------|---------|----------------|\n| **Lion** | King of wild beasts | Divine sovereignty; the untameable glory of God |\n| **Ox** | Patient servant | Divine patience; the God who bears the burden of creation |\n| **Man** | Rational creature | Divine wisdom; the God who speaks and is known |\n| **Eagle** | Soaring, all-seeing | Divine transcendence; the God who sees all from above |\n\nThe four faces together say: God is not partial. He is not the sovereignty-God who lacks patience, or the patient-God who lacks sovereignty. The living creatures hold all four in ceaseless, combined praise.\n\n---\n\n#### The Sanctus — Your Part in the Throne Room\n\nEvery time the church sings the Sanctus, something real is happening. The prayer is not a remembrance of a past event. It is a present participation in an ongoing reality.\n\nPractice it slowly:\n\n*Holy, holy, holy Lord, God of hosts.*\n*Heaven and earth are full of your glory.*\n\nWhen you say "heaven and earth are full of your glory" — you are agreeing with the living creatures. You are joining a choir that has been singing since before your birth and will be singing after your death.\n\nThis is why the Thrones and the Living Creatures matter: not as museum pieces of angelology, but as the context within which all Christian worship takes place.\n\n---\n\n*Before moving on: read Isaiah 6:1-7 once more, slowly. This time, try to see it — not as a text but as a place. You have been given a tour. Stand in it.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612vq0017geo0q1cf7q8z	cmq6612vm0013geo0kqjj27k2	Lesson 12 — Michael: Warrior and Protector of the Elect	READING	900	1	\N	t	![Lesson 12 — Michael: Warrior and Protector of the Elect](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsCVGLZTe78vbPqVLiKnDy6up93CGaNzkh5HsQ)\n\n## Michael — Warrior and Protector of the Elect\n\n### The Battle and the Name\n\nThe rebellion has happened. The decision has been made. A vast number of the most powerful created intelligences in existence — beings of pure intellect who knew God fully and chose against Him — are now arrayed against the order of heaven.\n\nSomeone has to respond. Someone has to lead. And in this moment, the angel whose very name answers every claim of creaturely pride steps forward.\n\n*Mi-cha-El?*\n\n"**Who is like God?**"\n\nThe question is rhetorical. It is also a battle cry. It is a declaration of the absolute ontological difference between Creator and creature. It answers the pride that said *"I will make myself like the Most High"* with the only possible refutation: *Nothing in creation can be like God. Not you. Not anyone.*\n\nMichael's name is not a name chosen by parents at birth. It is a theological statement that, according to the tradition, defines his entire existence: he is the being who, at the first crisis in the history of creation, stood up and proclaimed the inviolable sovereignty of God over every created thing — including the greatest of them.\n\n### Michael in Scripture: Four Appearances\n\n**Daniel 10:13, 21** — While Gabriel is trying to reach Daniel, a demonic Principality (the "prince of Persia") opposes him for twenty-one days. *"Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me."* Michael is the rescuer of Gabriel — a detail that conveys his extraordinary standing even among the archangels.\n\n**Daniel 12:1** — The most explicit statement of Michael's cosmic mission:\n\n> [Daniel 12:1](data-scripture="Daniel 12:1") "At that time shall arise Michael, the great prince who has charge of your people. And there shall be a time of trouble, such as never has been since there was a nation till that time. But at that time your people shall be delivered, everyone whose name shall be found written in the book."\n\nMichael is the Principality specifically assigned to the people of God — first Israel, then the Church. His mission is not general angelic service. It is the specific guardianship of those written in the book of life.\n\n**Jude 9** — Michael disputes with the adversary over the body of Moses. His response is notable: *"The Lord rebuke you."* Even at his level of authority — the most powerful of the archangels, captain of the heavenly host — Michael does not act in his own name. He invokes the authority of God. This is not a limitation. It is the proper posture of even the greatest creature before its Creator.\n\n**Revelation 12:7-9** — The war in heaven:\n\n> [Revelation 12:7-9](data-scripture="Revelation 12:7") "Now war arose in heaven, Michael and his angels fighting against the dragon; and the dragon and his angels fought, but they were defeated and there was no longer any place for them in heaven. And the great dragon was thrown down, that ancient serpent, who is called the Devil and Satan."\n\nThe tradition teaches that this was not a battle of physical violence — angels have no bodies. It was a confrontation of wills, a declaration of God's sovereignty. Michael led the faithful angels in asserting what his name proclaims: *God's authority will not be challenged and prevail.*\n\n### Michael's Four Offices\n\nCatholic tradition assigns Michael four enduring roles:\n\n**I. Warrior for God's Glory.** Michael is the supreme captain of the heavenly hosts — the defender of God's sovereignty against any who challenge it.\n\n**II. Escort of Souls at Death.** The tradition holds that Michael is present at the moment of natural death, conducting the souls of the just toward their judgment. This is one of the most consoling applications of Michael's guardianship — the one who spent all of history protecting the elect does not abandon them at their most vulnerable moment.\n\n**III. Champion of God's People.** From Israel to the Church, Michael is the divinely appointed Principality standing over those who belong to God. He is not a general divine helper; he has a *specific* commission for *specific* people.\n\n**IV. Standard-bearer of Divine Sovereignty.** His name — *"Who is like God?"* — is not merely a historical battle cry. It is the permanent statement of the relationship between Creator and creation. In an age that constantly seeks to elevate human autonomy to divinity, Michael's name remains the question that answers every such attempt.\n\n### A Note on Michael's Place in the Hierarchy\n\nSome theologians have proposed that Michael, given his supreme authority, must belong to a higher choir than the Archangels — perhaps even to the Seraphim. The tradition's response is nuanced: Michael may be an Archangel by natural constitution but elevated to extraordinary power and authority by the grace of his mission and the perfection of his fidelity.\n\nThe implication is significant: **natural endowment is not the final determinant of a creature's standing**. What a creature does with what it has been given matters. Michael's faithfulness at the supreme moment of creation's first crisis merited him such grace as to elevate his effective power beyond what his nature alone would determine.\n\nThis is consolation for human beings. We are not Seraphim. But fidelity to our calling, exercised with the grace God gives us, is not without consequence.\n\n---\n\n*Next: From the warrior to the messenger. We turn to the archangel who was created for the single most important conversation in the history of the universe — a conversation with a teenage girl in a small town in Galilee.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612w6001rgeo0k5pju6rj	cmq6612vy001hgeo0djva1vnw	Lesson 18 — Angels in the New Testament, the Liturgy, and the Life of the Church	READING	900	1	\N	t	![Lesson 18 — Angels in the New Testament, the Liturgy, and the Life of the Church](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsG25a33fQtkjPm8YJfVWKDcL3Bvzgo59AS2es)\n\n## The Whole Picture — Angels in the New Testament and the Eternal Liturgy\n\n### Return to the Beginning\n\nIn Lesson 1, we began with this:\n\n*"Right now, as you read this, a being of pure intelligence that has existed since before the first star was formed — a being that knows more about the structure of creation than the greatest scientist who ever lived — is present with you."*\n\nWe called it the teaching of the Church, and we said it was not poetry. Eighteen lessons later, we can say something more specific:\n\nThat being belongs to the ninth choir of a nine-choir hierarchy that includes the Seraphim who burn before the throne of God, the Cherubim who have guarded the sacred since Eden, the Thrones who embody the stability of divine justice, the Dominations who direct the governance of all creation, the Virtues who sustain every physical law and execute every miracle, the Powers who defend the cosmic order, the Principalities who guard nations and the Church itself, and the Archangels who were created for the most important missions in the history of creation.\n\nAll of that — the entire cosmic structure of nine choirs in three hierarchies — culminates in one angel, assigned to one person, standing beside you in this moment.\n\nThe map is now complete. Let us read it one final time.\n\n---\n\n### The New Testament: Angels at Every Pivotal Moment\n\nThe Old Testament prepared. The New Testament fulfills.\n\n**The Annunciation** ([Luke 1:26-38](data-scripture="Luke 1:26")). Gabriel — created for this moment before time began — comes to Nazareth. Mary says *yes*. The Word becomes flesh. The most important event in the history of creation is initiated by the delivery of a message by a created being.\n\n**The Birth of John** ([Luke 1:11-20](data-scripture="Luke 1:11")). Gabriel appears to Zechariah during the incense offering in the Temple — at the precise moment of the daily liturgy. Heaven's message arrives at the meeting point of human prayer.\n\n**The Nativity** ([Luke 2:8-14](data-scripture="Luke 2:8")). An angel announces the birth to the shepherds — the marginalized, the night-workers, the ones who are not in the Temple. Then the *"multitude of the heavenly host"* appears, praising God. The Incarnation is met with an angelic choir. The first announcement of the Gospel is an angelic concert.\n\n**The Flight to Egypt** ([Matthew 2:13](data-scripture="Matthew 2:13")). An angel warns Joseph in a dream. The infant God is protected by the intervention of an angel.\n\n**The Temptation** ([Matthew 4:11](data-scripture="Matthew 4:11")). After forty days in the desert, *"angels came and were ministering to him."* The Son of God, in His human nature, was sustained by angels. What Elijah received under the broom tree, Jesus received in the wilderness.\n\n**Gethsemane** ([Luke 22:43](data-scripture="Luke 22:43")). *"There appeared to him an angel from heaven, strengthening him."* At the most agonizing hour in human history, in the garden where the entire weight of sin was being taken up, an angel was sent to strengthen the Savior. The Seraphim who had burned before Him since the beginning of time; the Cherubim who had guarded the sacred since Eden; the Thrones, the Dominations, the Virtues, the Powers, the Principalities, the Archangels — all of them present, in some sense, in that garden. And one was sent.\n\n**The Resurrection** ([Matthew 28:2-7](data-scripture="Matthew 28:2")). An angel rolls back the stone. His appearance is like lightning; his clothing white as snow. The guards become like dead men. And the angel says the words that define the entire Christian proclamation:\n\n> [Matthew 28:6](data-scripture="Matthew 28:6") "He is not here, for he has risen, as he said."\n\nThe resurrection is announced by an angel. The being created at the beginning of time, present at creation's first dawn of praise, is there at the dawn of the new creation to announce it.\n\n**The Ascension** ([Acts 1:10-11](data-scripture="Acts 1:10")). Two angels in white appear: *"This Jesus, who was taken up from you into heaven, will come in the same way as you saw him go."* The promise of the return. The Church begins its waiting — and is told by angels that the waiting will end.\n\n**The Church in Acts.** Peter freed from prison ([Acts 5:19](data-scripture="Acts 5:19")); Cornelius directed to send for Peter, beginning the Gentile mission ([Acts 10:3](data-scripture="Acts 10:3")); Peter freed again ([Acts 12:7](data-scripture="Acts 12:7")). The early Church in its most vulnerable years is protected, directed, and sustained by angelic intervention. The Principality of the Church is not absent.\n\n---\n\n### The Eternal Liturgy: Heaven and Earth United\n\nThe Book of Revelation is the final word of Scripture — and it is saturated, from beginning to end, with the angelic world. Letters to churches are addressed to *their* angels. Seals are broken by angels. Trumpets are blown by angels. Bowls are poured by angels. The throne is surrounded by angels. The living creatures sing without ceasing. Michael fights the final battle. And the New Jerusalem descends, surrounded by twelve gates, each guarded by an angel.\n\nThe last pages of the Bible read like the beginning of the angels' story — the new creation, the eternal city, the unending liturgy of the Lamb.\n\nAnd at the center of it all is this vision:\n\n> [Revelation 8:3-4](data-scripture="Revelation 8:3") "Another angel came and stood at the altar with a golden censer, and he was given much incense to offer with the prayers of all the saints on the golden altar before the throne, and the smoke of the incense, with the prayers of all the saints, rose before God from the hand of the angel."\n\n*All the saints.* Every prayer that has ever been offered by a human being, from the first prayer of the first human to the last prayer before the end of time — gathered, carried, offered before the throne by a created being acting in obedience to God.\n\nIncluding yours.\n\n---\n\n### The Teaching of Paul and the Letter to the Hebrews\n\nPaul declares the hierarchy in [Colossians 1:16](data-scripture="Colossians 1:16"): thrones, dominions, rulers, powers — all of it created through Christ and for Christ. Every angel in the nine choirs exists for the One who redeemed you.\n\nThe Letter to the Hebrews gives the final word on what Christian worship is:\n\n> [Hebrews 12:22-23](data-scripture="Hebrews 12:22") "But you have come to Mount Zion and to the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem, and to innumerable angels in festal gathering, and to the assembly of the firstborn who are enrolled in heaven, and to God, the judge of all, and to the spirits of the righteous made perfect."\n\nEvery time Christians gather to worship — every Mass, every prayer meeting, every Sunday service — this is where they are. Not in a building. In the heavenly Jerusalem. Surrounded by innumerable angels in *festal gathering*. In the presence of God and the righteous made perfect.\n\nYou have never gone to church alone.\n\n---\n\n### What This Course Has Been About\n\nThis course began with a being of pure intelligence standing beside you, unseen.\n\nIt led you through nine choirs and three hierarchies — from the burning Seraphim at the apex of creation to the guardian angel at your side. It told you that each angel is its own species, and that the number of species equals the number of individual angels. It told you that they were created instantaneously, complete and perfect, and confirmed in grace in a single moment. It told you that Gabriel was made for Nazareth, Michael for the elect, Raphael for Tobias — and an angel whose name you do not know was made, in part, for you.\n\nNow you know what is standing beside you.\n\nThe course is finished. The relationship has only just begun.\n\n> [Psalm 103:20-21](data-scripture="Psalm 103:20") "Bless the Lord, O you his angels, you mighty ones who do his word, obeying the voice of his word! Bless the Lord, all his hosts, his ministers, who do his will!"\n\n---\n\n### What Comes Next — The Other Half of the Story\n\nThis course has studied the angels who stood. The loyal ones. The nine choirs in their unfallen glory.\n\nBut the course cannot be the whole story, because the Bible is not the whole story without the other half.\n\nIn the opening of Scripture, a creature appears in the garden — *"more crafty than any other beast of the field"* ([Genesis 3:1](data-scripture="Genesis 3:1")) — who is not a beast at all. He is a fallen being of the angelic order, and he is already in opposition to God, to humanity, and to the creation whose governance you have just studied.\n\nThe angels you have learned about here do not operate in an unchallenged environment. The Principalities who guard nations face opposing Principalities who seek to corrupt them. The Virtues who sustain creation face a host of beings whose goal is destruction. Michael does not fight unopposed — he fights the prince of Persia, and before that, the dragon.\n\nThe **Demons course** takes up this other half. It begins where this course began — with the angelic nature — and follows it in the direction of its corruption: the fall of Lucifer, the hierarchy of fallen spirits, the nature of demonic activity in the world, and the authority given to the redeemed to stand against it.\n\nUnderstanding the faithful angels prepares you to understand their opposites. Understanding the cosmic governance of the nine choirs prepares you to understand how that governance is contested. Understanding the love of the angels for God and humanity prepares you to understand the hatred that stands against both.\n\nThe relationship with the angels has just begun. Continue it — and learn what it is that they, and you, are standing against.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xguj000hhks8p4z5v7d0	cmq76xgtn0001hks8s3kqs5yq	Quiz — Part VI: The Unseen Architecture	QUIZ	\N	7	\N	t	## Quiz — Part VI: The Unseen Architecture\n\n**1. According to this course, what is the most theologically significant implication of the Watcher narrative in Genesis 6?**\n\nA) It proves that angels can fall from grace, demonstrating the importance of free will\nB) The Flood was a specific divine response to supernatural contamination of the human bloodline — a genetic strategy by Satan to prevent the birth of the Messiah — and the disembodied spirits of the Nephilim are one proposed origin of the demonic hierarchy\nC) The Nephilim were purely human beings of exceptional size, and Genesis 6 has no relevance to contemporary spiritual warfare\nD) Angels are capable of reproducing with humans whenever God permits\n\n---\n\n**2. In 1 Kings 22, the Lying Spirit volunteers to deceive Ahab's prophets. What does this passage establish about the operation of lying spirits?**\n\nA) God directly causes people to believe lies as punishment for sin\nB) Lying spirits operate only through false prophets who are deliberately deceiving their congregations\nC) A lying spirit can operate through sincere, believing prophets who are not consciously deceiving anyone — producing confident, spiritually-toned false words that confirm the hearer's existing desires, with God's permission in response to those who have persistently chosen falsehood\nD) The Lying Spirit can only operate in Old Testament contexts before the Holy Spirit was given\n\n---\n\n**3. What distinguishes the Spirit of Whoredom from ordinary sexual temptation, according to this course?**\n\nA) The Spirit of Whoredom only affects people with a history of sexual abuse\nB) The Spirit of Whoredom operates at both the physical level (sexual addiction and promiscuity) and the spiritual level (the soul's compulsive tendency to seek satisfaction from any source other than God) — making it both a sexual and an idolatry principality simultaneously\nC) Ordinary sexual temptation comes from the world; the Spirit of Whoredom comes only from generational curses\nD) The Spirit of Whoredom is only present in homosexual sin, not heterosexual sin\n\n---\n\n**4. Jesus described the woman in Luke 13 as having been "bound by Satan" for 18 years. What does this establish about the Spirit of Infirmity?**\n\nA) All illness is caused by demonic spirits and should be addressed through deliverance rather than medicine\nB) Some illness has a demonic root — specifically bound to the person by a demonic assignment — and requires spiritual deliverance as well as medical treatment to fully resolve\nC) The Spirit of Infirmity only operates on women\nD) God permits Satanic infirmity as punishment for specific sin\n\n---\n\n**5. What does Daniel 10 establish about the structure of demonic power?**\n\nA) Demons are disorganized and operate independently without any hierarchical structure\nB) Demonic princes are assigned to geographic territories — nations and regions — and actively resist both angelic messengers and the prayers of God's people, explaining why sustained intercession over nations encounters resistance and requires persistent prayer\nC) The angelic battles described in Daniel 10 were a unique Old Testament phenomenon that does not continue in the New Testament era\nD) The "Prince of Persia" was a human ruler with demonic influence, not a demonic being itself\n\n---\n\n**Answer Key**\n\n1. **B** — The Watcher narrative explains the Flood as divine response to supernatural contamination. The Messiah's lineage had to be preserved.\n2. **C** — The Lying Spirit operates through sincere vessels — its most dangerous form. God permits it for those who have chosen confirmation over truth.\n3. **B** — The Spirit of Whoredom governs both sexual unfaithfulness and spiritual idolatry simultaneously. Hosea's prophecy makes both dimensions explicit.\n4. **B** — Not all illness is demonic. But some illness has a spiritual root that requires spiritual address alongside medical treatment.\n5. **B** — Daniel 10 is the clearest biblical evidence for territorial demonic governance and its effect on prayer.	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612w8001tgeo004uu8pty	cmq6612vy001hgeo0djva1vnw	Supplement 10 — For Lessons 17 & 18	SUPPLEMENT	600	2	\N	t	![Supplement 10 — For Lessons 17 & 18](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsSLlGbjEJ9p8Osi7f2L3jgeayVJxF6MbNCPdu)\n\n## Supplement 10 — For Lessons 17 & 18: Angels in Scripture and Worship\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**The Angel of the Lord** (*malakh YHWH*) — A special figure in the Old Testament who speaks with divine authority and accepts worship; many Fathers identified these appearances as pre-incarnate manifestations of the Son of God.\n\n**Christophany** — A pre-incarnate appearance of Christ; the classical patristic interpretation of many "Angel of the Lord" appearances.\n\n**The Sanctus** — "Holy, Holy, Holy, Lord God of hosts"; the triple-holy hymn at Mass, quoting Isaiah 6:3 (Seraphim) and echoed in Revelation 4:8 (living creatures).\n\n**Hebrews 12:22** — The declaration that every Christian gathering takes place in the presence of "innumerable angels in festal gathering."\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> Ps. 103:20-21 "Bless the Lord, O you his angels, you mighty ones who do his word, obeying the voice of his word! Bless the Lord, all his hosts, his ministers, who do his will!"\n\n> Heb. 12:22-23 "But you have come to Mount Zion and to the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem, and to innumerable angels in festal gathering."\n\n> Lk. 2:13-14 "And suddenly there was with the angel a multitude of the heavenly host praising God and saying, 'Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace among those with whom he is pleased!'"\n\n---\n\n### Old Testament Angelic Appearances at a Glance\n\n| Event | Angel's Role | Reference |\n|-------|-------------|-----------|\n| Hagar in the wilderness | Compassion; promise | Gen. 16:7-13 |\n| Three visitors to Abraham | Announce Isaac's birth | Gen. 18:1-2 |\n| Lot in Sodom | Physical rescue | Gen. 19:1-15 |\n| Binding of Isaac | Stop the sacrifice | Gen. 22:11-12 |\n| Jacob's ladder | Vision of heaven-earth link | Gen. 28:12 |\n| Burning bush | Call of Moses | Ex. 3:2 |\n| Pillar of cloud/fire | Guide and protect Israel | Ex. 14:19 |\n| Elijah under the broom tree | Provision and strength | 1 Kgs. 19:5-7 |\n| Isaiah's vision | Purification; call | Isa. 6:1-7 |\n| Daniel's visions | Explanation; protection | Dan. 8:16; Dan. 10:13 |\n\n---\n\n### Questions for Reflection\n\n1. Angels appear at every major transition in salvation history. What does this consistent presence reveal about God's economy of providence?\n\n2. Paul says that when Christians gather, they come to *"innumerable angels in festal gathering"* (Heb. 12:22). How does this awareness change your experience of Sunday worship?\n\n3. The Sanctus links the earthly liturgy to the Seraphim's song in Isaiah 6 and the living creatures in Revelation 4. When you sing Holy, Holy, Holy, you are joining a hymn that has never ceased in heaven. What does this mean to you personally?\n\n4. Angels are sent to the vulnerable throughout the Old Testament — Hagar, Elijah, Lot. In what moments of vulnerability have you trusted that God's angels were present?\n\n5. At Gethsemane, an angel strengthened Jesus in His agony. If an angel was sent to strengthen the Son of God in human suffering, what does this say about God's attentiveness to our own moments of suffering and prayer?	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612vr0019geo0q344prdx	cmq6612vm0013geo0kqjj27k2	Supplement 7 — For Lessons 11 & 12	SUPPLEMENT	600	2	\N	t	![Supplement 7 — For Lessons 11 & 12](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsvciXobFp6RzaLq0EW1HyN9UvhmSI5VtYXPn2)\n\n## Supplement 7 — For Lessons 11 & 12: The Archangels and Michael\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**Archangels** (*archangeloi*, "chief angels") — The eighth choir; superior messengers entrusted with the most important missions. Scripture names three: Michael, Gabriel, Raphael.\n\n**Michael** ("Who is like God?") — Warrior Archangel; guardian of God's people; escort of souls; champion of the Church.\n\n**Gabriel** ("God is my strength") — Archangel of divine annunciation; messenger of the Incarnation.\n\n**Raphael** ("God heals") — Archangel of healing and accompaniment.\n\n**Principality** — The highest choir of the third hierarchy; guardians of nations and peoples. Michael is specifically the Principality of the Church.\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> Dan. 12:1 "At that time shall arise Michael, the great prince who has charge of your people."\n\n> Rev. 12:7 "Now war arose in heaven, Michael and his angels fighting against the dragon."\n\n> Jude 9 "But when the archangel Michael, contending with the devil, was disputing about the body of Moses, he did not presume to pronounce a blasphemous judgment, but said, 'The Lord rebuke you.'"\n\n> Tobit 12:15 "I am Raphael, one of the seven holy angels who present the prayers of the saints and enter into the presence of the holy God."\n\n---\n\n### The Three Named Archangels\n\n| Name | Meaning | Primary Mission | Key Scripture |\n|------|---------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Michael** | Who is like God? | Warrior; guardian of God's people | Dan. 12:1; Rev. 12:7 |\n| **Gabriel** | God is my strength | Messenger of the Incarnation | Lk. 1:26-38; Dan. 8:16 |\n| **Raphael** | God heals | Healing; accompaniment; guidance | Tobit 12:15 |\n\n---\n\n### Questions for Reflection\n\n1. Michael's name — "Who is like God?" — is simultaneously a question and a proclamation. How does this name function as a rebuke of pride? What does it mean for your own spiritual life to ask this question honestly?\n\n2. In Jude 9, even Michael says *"The Lord rebuke you"* rather than acting on his own authority. What does this teach about the proper use of spiritual authority?\n\n3. Michael is described as the "great prince who has charge of your people." Do you pray to Michael for the protection of the Church? How does knowing he has a specific divine appointment change the nature of that prayer?\n\n4. Gabriel brought the most important message in history — the Annunciation — to a young woman in Nazareth. What does this say about how God chooses the recipients of His most significant communications?\n\n5. Raphael traveled with Tobias for weeks without revealing his identity. Why might an angel conceal who it is? What does this anonymity teach about how angels serve human beings?\n\n---\n\n### The Hebrew Element "El" in Angelic Names\n\nThe Hebrew word **El** — אֵל — is one of the oldest and most important divine terms in the biblical Hebrew world. In its simplest sense, El means “God,” “god,” “mighty one,” or “power.” Lexical sources list its semantic range as “god,” “god-like one,” “mighty one,” “God, the one true God,” and also “strength” or “power.”\n\nIn angelic names like Michael, Gabriel, and Raphael, the element **-el** functions as a **theophoric element**. A theophoric name is a name that “bears” or contains the name/title of a deity; Merriam-Webster defines “theophoric” as “derived from or bearing the name of a god.” In Hebrew biblical names, El can appear at the beginning or end of a name. When it appears at the end, as in Micha-el, Gabri-el, Rapha-el, it anchors the whole name in reference to God.\n\nThe point is not that these angels are gods. The point is that their names are **theological statements about God**.\n\n#### El as a Hebrew Divine Word\n\nHebrew אֵל / ʾēl is made of two consonants: aleph א and lamed ל. The aleph originally represents a glottal stop, and the lamed gives the “l” sound. In biblical Hebrew, the written consonantal form is אל, while the vowel pointing אֵל reflects the traditional pronunciation “El.”\n\nThe word can function in a few ways:\n\n- It can mean **God**, referring to the God of Israel.\n- It can mean **a god**, when used generically.\n- It can carry the idea of **might, strength, power, or majesty**, which is why it is naturally suited to divine titles.\n\nThat is why you see forms like **El Elyon** — “God Most High,” **El Shaddai** — often rendered “God Almighty,” **El Olam** — “Everlasting God,” and related forms. Britannica notes that patriarchal narratives use divine epithets such as El Shaddai, El Elyon, El Olam, El Bethel, and El Roʾi.\n\nSo when El appears inside a name, it is not decoration. It is **theological grammar**. The name is saying something about God’s nature, God’s action, or the person’s relationship to God.\n\n#### What “Theophoric” Means in Plain Language\n\nA theophoric name is a God-bearing name. It carries a divine title inside it.\n\nA modern example would be names like **Nathaniel**, meaning “gift of God,” or **Daniel**, commonly understood as “God is my judge.” The person named Daniel is not God. His name confesses something about God: God judges. Nathaniel is not God. His name confesses something about God: God gives.\n\nThat same pattern works with angelic names. The angel’s name is not mainly personal branding. It is a **theological label**. It reveals mission, rank, loyalty, or divine function.\n\n#### Michael: מִיכָאֵל / Mi-kha-el\n\nMichael breaks down as:\n\n- **Mi** = who?\n- **kha / ka** = like, as, comparable to\n- **El** = God\n\nSo **Mi-kha-el** means: **“Who is like God?”**\n\nThis is not a casual question. It is a **rhetorical challenge**. The implied answer is: No one is like God.\n\nThat makes Michael’s name a direct theological rebuke against pride, rebellion, idolatry, and satanic self-exaltation. The name itself declares the incomparability of God. This fits Michael’s biblical role. In Daniel 10:13, Michael is called “one of the chief princes,” and he comes to help in a heavenly conflict. In Daniel 12:1, he is associated with the protection of God’s people. Jude 9 calls him “the archangel.”\n\nSo Michael’s name matches his function. He is not presented as soft, decorative, or passive. He is associated with heavenly conflict, protection, and divine authority. His name announces the central truth behind his warfare: no created power rivals God.\n\n> Michael does not defeat evil because Michael is impressive in himself. His very name points away from himself and toward God.\n\n#### Gabriel: גַּבְרִיאֵל / Gavri-el\n\nGabriel is usually broken down from Hebrew elements connected to *gever* / *gabar* and **El**.\n\n- **Gever** can mean man, strong man, warrior, or mighty one.\n- **Gabar** is associated with strength, prevailing, or might.\n- **El** means God.\n\nSo **Gabriel / Gavri-el** can be rendered as “God is my strength,” “man of God,” “mighty one of God,” or “hero/warrior of God.”\n\nGabriel’s role in Scripture fits this meaning, but in a different way from Michael. Gabriel is not mainly presented as a battle commander. He is especially presented as a **messenger and interpreter of revelation**. In Daniel 8:16, a voice commands Gabriel to make Daniel understand the vision. He comes when God’s word must be delivered with authority.\n\nThink about the practical difference: **Michael’s name sounds like a banner raised in battle** — “Who is like God?” **Gabriel’s name sounds like divine strength entering human confusion** — “God is my strength.”\n\nSo the **-el** in Gabriel’s name marks him as one whose strength is not autonomous. His strength is derived, delegated, and directed by God.\n\n#### Raphael: רָפָאֵל / Rafa-el\n\nRaphael comes from the Hebrew root **רפא** / *r-p-ʾ*, meaning **to heal**, plus **El**, meaning God.\n\nSo **Rafa-el** means: **“God heals,” “God has healed,” or “healing of God.”**\n\nRaphael’s angelic role is most clearly known from **Tobit**, which is deuterocanonical in Catholic and Orthodox Bibles. Raphael is described in Tobit 12:15 as one of the seven holy angels who present the prayers of the saints and enter before the glory of the Holy One.\n\nSo Raphael’s name is not random. It matches his function. In Tobit, Raphael is associated with healing, deliverance, guidance, and restoration. His name says the real healer is not the angel. The real healer is God.\n\n> Raphael is not “the healer” in the ultimate sense. He is the ministering agent. His name points to the source: **God heals**.\n\n#### Why So Many Angelic Names End in -el\n\nThe repeated **-el** ending in angelic names creates a theological pattern:\n\n| Angel | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| **Michael** | Who is like God? |\n| **Gabriel** | God is my strength |\n| **Raphael** | God heals |\n| **Uriel** | God is my light / flame of God |\n| **Raguel** | Friend of God |\n| **Sariel** | Prince/command of God |\n| **Phanuel / Peniel** | Face of God |\n\nThis pattern is especially common in later Jewish angelology. In the Hebrew Bible itself, the explicitly named angelic figures are primarily **Michael** and **Gabriel** in Daniel; **Raphael** appears in Tobit. So when people speak of the “three named archangels” — Michael, Gabriel, Raphael — that usually reflects Catholic, Orthodox, and broader historical Christian angelology.\n\n#### The Suffix -el Does Not Mean “Angel”\n\nThis is a common mistake. The ending **-el does not mean angel. It means God.**\n\nThat means names ending in -el are not automatically angelic names. Many biblical humans carry El names:\n\n- **Daniel** — God is my judge\n- **Samuel** — heard of God / name of God\n- **Israel** — struggles with God / God strives\n- **Ezekiel** — God strengthens\n- **Nathaniel** — gift of God\n- **Ishmael** — God hears\n\nSo when Michael, Gabriel, and Raphael end in -el, the suffix is not identifying their species. It is identifying the **theological center of their names**.\n\n#### How El Works Grammatically Inside These Names\n\nThe element El can function differently depending on the name:\n\n- **Sometimes El is the subject:** Raphael = God heals. Here, God is the one doing the action.\n- **Sometimes El is the object of comparison:** Michael = Who is like God? Here, God is the standard of comparison.\n- **Sometimes El is possessive or relational:** Gabriel = man/strength/warrior of God, or God is my strength. Here, the name can be understood as either describing divine possession/service or declaring God as the source of strength.\n\nThat flexibility is normal in Hebrew names. Ancient Hebrew names often compress a whole sentence into a compact form.\n\n#### The Theological Role of El in Angel Names\n\nThe biggest point is this: **El keeps the angel subordinate to God.**\n\nAngels are powerful, but their names prevent angel-worship if understood correctly. Their names are not self-exalting. They are **God-exalting**.\n\n- Michael does not mean “Michael is mighty.” It asks, **“Who is like God?”**\n- Gabriel does not mean “Gabriel is independently strong.” It points to **God as strength**.\n- Raphael does not mean “Raphael is the source of healing.” It says **God heals**.\n\nThat is why these names are theologically disciplined. They do not pull attention away from God. They redirect attention **back to God**.\n\nThis is especially important because Scripture repeatedly shows humans being tempted to overreact to angelic beings. Angels can be terrifying, glorious, and overwhelming. But faithful angelology never allows angels to become objects of worship. They serve. They announce. They fight. They heal. They minister. But **God alone is God**.\n\n#### Michael, Gabriel, and Raphael as a Threefold Theological Pattern\n\nYou can summarize the three names like this:\n\n| Angel | Theological Statement |\n|-------|----------------------|\n| **Michael** | God is incomparable |\n| **Gabriel** | God is strength |\n| **Raphael** | God heals |\n\nTogether, they form a strong theological triad:\n\n- God is **above all rivals**.\n- God **gives strength** to accomplish His will.\n- God **heals** what is broken.\n\nThe “-el” ending is not a small linguistic detail. It is the **theological engine of the names**.\n\n#### Why This Matters for Interpreting Angelology\n\nWhen studying angels, people often get distracted by hierarchy charts, names, ranks, and speculative systems. The Hebrew names pull the focus back where it belongs.\n\nThe biblical and Jewish-Christian logic is not: “Look how fascinating angels are.”\n\nThe better logic is: **“Look what these servants reveal about God.”**\n\n- Michael reveals God’s **unrivaled supremacy**.\n- Gabriel reveals God’s **authoritative strength in revelation**.\n- Raphael reveals God’s **healing and restoring power**.\n\nSo the **El suffix functions almost like a built-in guardrail**. It keeps the interpretation from drifting into angel-centered spirituality. Every name ends by pointing upward.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsic000d18pfeuskxd9s	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Celebrity and Political Idolatry	READING	\N	4	\N	t	![Celebrity and Political Idolatry](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsGICJDjQtkjPm8YJfVWKDcL3Bvzgo59AS2es6)\n\n## Celebrity and Political Idolatry\n\nShe had not spoken to her sister in fourteen months. The relationship had broken over a political disagreement at a holiday dinner — a disagreement about a candidate, not a policy. Her sister had said something about a politician she admired. She had responded with something about a politician her sister admired. Neither could now precisely remember what either had said. Both remembered the feeling of something sacred having been violated.\n\nShe was a committed Christian. She tithed. She prayed. She had a genuine relationship with God. She also checked her preferred political news source before she read her Bible every morning, spent four hours a week consuming political commentary, and experienced the political victories of her preferred party with the same visceral joy she suspected she should reserve for the things of God.\n\nShe had not connected the estranged sister to the morning news check. Both were downstream of the same idol.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nIdolatry in its modern form does not require a carved image or a temple. [1 John 5:21](data-scripture="1 John 5:21"): *"Little children, keep yourselves from idols."* The idol is whatever occupies God's rightful place in the heart's devotion, the mind's attention, and the emotional energy that was designed for God.\n\nCelebrity worship, sports fandom, and political tribalism all display the architecture of worship: loyalty that persists despite the idol's failures, grief disproportionate to the actual significance of a loss, community organized around shared devotion to the figure, identity formed around allegiance. These are the structures of religion applied to a creature rather than the Creator.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nIdolatry does not feel like idolatry from the inside. It feels like caring about something important, being informed, being part of a community, having appropriate passion for justice or excellence. The emotional structures of fandom and political devotion are designed to feel normal — because in a culture that has systematically displaced God from the center, they have become normal.\n\nThe neurological reality: the brain's God-designed reward systems for transcendence, community, and devotion do not stop functioning when a person stops directing them toward God. They are redirected toward whatever receives consistent, emotionally significant attention. The fan's cortisol spike at a loss and dopamine surge at a victory are the God-designed emotional architecture of worship, misdirected.\n\n[Exodus 20:5](data-scripture="Exodus 20:5"): *"I the LORD thy God am a jealous God."* God's jealousy is not emotional insecurity. It is the covenant consequence of replacing the Creator with the creature. The protective presence that comes with genuine covenant relationship with God is withdrawn when God's rightful place is occupied by something else.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The emotional energy directed toward idols is withdrawn from God.** This is the basic mechanism: what occupies the soul's devotional capacity is what shapes the soul. The person who spends more emotional energy on a sports team's performance than on their relationship with God has not supplemented their faith — they have partially replaced it.\n\n**Political idolatry is particularly spiritually dangerous** because it provides a narrative of cosmic significance — that the fate of civilization depends on this election, this candidate, this policy — that generates the kind of absolute devotion ordinarily reserved for things of ultimate importance. When political loyalty becomes a person's functional ultimate concern, they have assigned political power the role only God can occupy.\n\n**Family and community destruction is the documented fruit.** The estrangement rate across families due to political idolatry in the last decade is unprecedented in American history. When an idol requires the sacrifice of covenant relationships to maintain its purity, it has exceeded the function of preference and become the function of deity.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThis is the question that measures the answer: *What determines your emotional state more consistently — the presence of God in your life, or the fortunes of the team, celebrity, or party you follow?*\n\nIf your answer is honest and uncomfortable, you know what the idol is. The response is not to stop caring about politics, sports, or culture. It is to reorder your devotional life until God's presence and purposes generate the consistent emotional investment that the team's win-loss record has been generating.\n\n[Matthew 6:33](data-scripture="Matthew 6:33"): *"Seek ye first the kingdom of God."* First. Not also. First.\n\n---\n\n*Political and celebrity idolatry gives the self a team to belong to. The next lesson examines what happens when you want the stars to tell you where the team is going.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Honestly: does your emotional response to election results match your emotional response to answered prayer? Which produces more feeling?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsiw000r18pfll7jbbx8	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Wicca	READING	\N	32	\N	t	![Wicca](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsbuGljzhpZWXUxpYCzVoHdTRw8N94g0J5LQu7)\n\n## Wicca\n\nShe had been Wiccan for nine years when she attended her niece's church baptism. She sat in the back, amused in a charitable way by the formality of it — the robes, the water, the declarations. She believed in the divine feminine, in the cycles of the moon, in the Wheel of the Year. She believed she was doing her spiritual practice seriously and honestly.\n\nThe pastor preached briefly on [Colossians 1:13-14](data-scripture="Colossians 1:13-14"): *"Who hath delivered us from the power of darkness, and hath translated us into the kingdom of his dear Son: in whom we have redemption through his blood, even the forgiveness of sins."*\n\nShe felt something move in her chest when he said "the power of darkness." Not offense. Something more like recognition. She thought about it for six months before she called her niece.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nWicca is a modern neopagan witchcraft religion credited largely to Gerald Gardner, who claimed initiation into a surviving ancient witch-cult in mid-20th century England. Drawing from ceremonial magic, folk tradition, and esoteric movements, Wicca worships a Horned God and a Triple Goddess, observes seasonal sabbats based on the Wheel of the Year, and practices spellcasting, divination, and ritualized nature worship.\n\nIts appeal is genuine: it offers community, connection with the natural world, feminine spiritual expression, personal empowerment, and a framework of meaning. For many practitioners, Wicca met a need that the church had failed to meet — usually a need for belonging, for spiritual dignity, or for a relationship with the divine that felt personal and present.\n\nThe gospel's task is not to mock those needs but to show where they are genuinely met.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe deep appeal of Wicca is the deception — it meets real spiritual hunger through a system that cannot satisfy it and ultimately deepens the bondage it appears to relieve.\n\nThe Horned God and the Triple Goddess are not neutral symbolic archetypes. They are the specific forms in which demonic principalities have presented themselves to cultures seeking divine feminine and masculine expression throughout history. The Horned God corresponds most directly to Baal and Pan — entities that appear consistently in Scripture's accounts of Israel's most destructive encounters with false worship. The Triple Goddess corresponds to Asherah, Astarte, and Hecate.\n\n[Deuteronomy 18:10-12](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 18:10-12") prohibits each of the practices that constitute Wiccan practice: divination, enchanting, witchcraft, charming, consulting familiar spirits. These are not listed because they are ineffective. They are listed because they are effective routes to the wrong kingdom.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Spellcasting is sorcery.** [Galatians 5:19-20](data-scripture="Galatians 5:19-20"): *"The works of the flesh are manifest, which are these; Adultery, fornication, uncleanness, lasciviousness, idolatry, witchcraft..."* The Greek word translated "witchcraft" is *pharmakeia*. Spellcasting is the attempt to manipulate spiritual forces to achieve personal will — which is the definition of sorcery regardless of the intent behind it.\n\n**Deity invocation in ritual is real spirit contact.** When Wiccan ritual invokes the Horned God and the Triple Goddess, real entities respond. The experiences that follow — the sense of divine presence, the felt power in ritual, the apparent effectiveness of spells — are genuine spiritual responses from genuine demonic entities who have been accepting this worship for millennia.\n\n**The initiation system deepens binding with each degree.** Gardnerian and Alexandrian Wicca have formal initiations at multiple degrees. Each initiation is a deeper covenantal commitment to the entities involved.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now — and For Every Christian Who Knows a Wiccan\n\nFor those in Wicca or coming out of it:\n\nThe exit is [Acts 19:19](data-scripture="Acts 19:19"): everything associated with the practice, burned publicly. Every tool, every book, every ritual object, every altar item. This is not moderation — it is the complete severance that genuine freedom requires.\n\nRenounce each deity by name. Renounce each degree of initiation if formal initiation occurred. Break every covenant and agreement made in ritual. Command every associated entity to leave in Jesus' name.\n\nThen fill the space. Wicca met real needs — for community, for spiritual dignity, for present divine relationship. The church must be the place that meets those needs more genuinely. The God who made the moon and the seasons and the turning year has a better relationship with creation than the religion that worships it.\n\nFor every Christian who knows a Wiccan:\n\nDo not lead with condemnation of the practice. Lead with the genuine thing they are seeking. [2 Corinthians 4:4-6](data-scripture="2 Corinthians 4:4-6"): the god of this world has blinded the mind — your task is to let the light shine. The darkness cannot comprehend the light until the light shows up.\n\n---\n\n*Wicca is neopagan witchcraft organized into a religion. The next lesson examines a different tradition — one that learned to hide its paganism inside the church.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you ever identified as Wiccan, pagan, or a witch — or had a close relationship with someone who did? What was the genuine spiritual appeal?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsi1000518pf81vrrle8	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Feng Shui	READING	\N	12	\N	t	![Feng Shui](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsvfQs9yFp6RzaLq0EW1HyN9UvhmSI5VtYXPn2)\n\n## Feng Shui\n\nThe interior design consultant she hired was highly recommended and impeccably professional. The consultation included a feng shui assessment — the consultant brought a compass, spent forty minutes measuring the "energy flow" of each room, and produced a detailed report recommending specific furniture placements, mirror positions, and the removal of certain objects she identified as creating "negative chi."\n\nShe implemented the recommendations. The house did feel better — lighter, more peaceful. She attributed it to better room function and clearer sight lines.\n\nShe did not know that feng shui is not interior design. It is geomancy — divination through the spiritual reading of physical space — and that the "chi" being managed is not neutral energy but a spiritual force that responds to ritual arrangement and the invocation of its associated entities.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nFeng shui is an ancient Chinese practice of arranging built environments to harmonize with invisible energy forces (*chi* or *qi*). Practitioners use specialized compasses (*luo pan*), astrological charts, and formulas derived from Chinese cosmology — the Five Elements, the eight trigrams of the *I Ching*, yin-yang theory — to determine optimal spatial arrangements for health, wealth, and success.\n\nMajor corporations consult feng shui masters when designing headquarters. Hotels and casinos employ feng shui principles. Real estate developers market feng shui-compliant properties at premium prices. The practice has been thoroughly secularized as "spatial optimization" while retaining its occultic core.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe demonic deception of feng shui is its complete rebranding as rational spatial design. The *I Ching* — the ancient divination text at feng shui's theological foundation — is a divination oracle. The trigrams it uses to categorize spatial energy are the same trigrams used in Chinese divination to read fate. The chi being managed is the same spiritual force that acupuncture seeks to manipulate, that tai chi seeks to cultivate — a demonic force, not a neutral natural energy, that responds to ritual engagement with the entities associated with it.\n\n[Proverbs 16:33](data-scripture="Proverbs 16:33"): *"The lot is cast into the lap; but the whole disposing thereof is of the LORD."* God governs spatial reality. The arrangement of your home is not a variable you optimize through Chinese geomantic divination. It is a canvas for hospitality, worship, and the presence of the Holy Spirit.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Feng shui practices are ritual acts.** Each mirror placement, water feature position, and bagua corner arrangement is a ritual act within a system designed to manipulate spiritual forces. These are not secular decisions with pagan aesthetics — they are pagan ritual decisions with secular aesthetics.\n\n**The "feeling better" response is not neutral.** When feng shui produces a sense of improvement, several things could be happening: a placebo response, genuine improvement in spatial function, or — and this is the concern — demonic entities rearranging the spiritual atmosphere of the space in exchange for the ritual attention being directed their way. The last possibility does not feel different from the first two from the inside.\n\n**Business and corporate exposure.** Working in a feng shui-designed building exposes employees and clients to its spiritual architecture. This is not within individual control, but awareness is useful for prayer.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf your home has been designed or modified according to feng shui principles, repent for consulting a divination-based system for your spatial environment. Renounce the chi manipulation that was performed. Pray through every room, declaring God's authority over the space and asking the Holy Spirit to establish His presence where the feng shui practices sought to establish a different spiritual order.\n\nRemove any specifically feng shui items: mirrors placed to redirect chi, crystals positioned for energetic purposes, water features arranged for wealth attraction. These are not merely aesthetic choices — they are ritual objects from a divination system.\n\n[Haggai 2:19](data-scripture="Haggai 2:19"): *"Is the seed yet in the barn?... the vine, and the fig tree, and the pomegranate, and the olive tree, hath not brought forth: from this day will I bless you."* The blessing you seek is from God, not from the arrangement of your living room according to Chinese geomantic principles.\n\n---\n\n*Feng shui channels spiritual force through space. The next lesson examines what happens when a practitioner channels it directly through their hands into your body.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Has your home been arranged according to feng shui principles — even partially, even by a previous tenant? Walk through it with new eyes this week.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612w1001lgeo0f4yxvul5	cmq6612vy001hgeo0djva1vnw	Lesson 16 — Devotion to the Holy Angels: A Living Relationship	READING	900	4	\N	t	![Lesson 16 — Devotion to the Holy Angels: A Living Relationship](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsaqlhnFEhtesUMivpomO8x4WSPknRFTuAI75Q)\n\n## Devotion to the Holy Angels — A Living Relationship\n\n### The Difference Between Knowing and Relating\n\nThere is a significant gap between knowing that your guardian angel exists and actually relating to it as a person.\n\nMost Christians are in the position of someone who has been told that a wise and faithful friend has been sitting in the next room for their entire life — and who has simply never knocked on the door.\n\nDevotion to the holy angels is the act of knocking.\n\nThe Catechism encourages veneration of the angels — particularly the three named Archangels and one's own guardian angel. This veneration is not worship (*latria*, which belongs to God alone) but *dulia* — the honor proper to holy creatures. The same kind of honor we give the saints, offered to beings who are present with us in a more immediate and personal way than any saint in heaven.\n\n### Angels Present Our Prayers\n\nThe scriptural foundation for angel devotion is not merely their existence — it is their function.\n\nRaphael told Tobit and Tobias: *"When you prayed... I brought a reminder of your prayer before the Holy One"* ([Tobit 12:12](data-scripture="Tobit 12:12")). This is not an exceptional event unique to Raphael or to Tobit. The Apocalypse presents it as the normal operation of heaven:\n\n> [Revelation 8:3-4](data-scripture="Revelation 8:3") "And another angel came and stood at the altar with a golden censer, and he was given much incense to offer with the prayers of all the saints on the golden altar before the throne, and the smoke of the incense, with the prayers of the saints, rose before God from the hand of the angel."\n\n*All the saints.* Not some prayers. Not special prayers offered by holy people in important moments. The prayers of all the saints — which includes you, every time you pray — are gathered and offered before the throne by an angel.\n\nThis means: when you pray, however haltingly, however briefly, however inadequate the words — an angel takes that prayer and carries it before God. The weakest prayer of the most discouraged sinner is carried to the throne by the same means as the ecstatic prayer of the great mystic.\n\nYour prayer does not arrive alone.\n\n### Practical Devotional Life: What the Tradition Recommends\n\n**At the start of the day:** Before getting out of bed, offer a brief address to your guardian angel — not a formula if possible, but a personal word. You are acknowledging a presence that has been with you through the night and is beginning the day with you. Something as simple as: *"Guardian angel, walk with me today. Help me see what I need to see, avoid what I need to avoid, and do the good that God has prepared for me."*\n\n**The Angelus (morning, noon, and evening):** This traditional prayer — commemorating the Annunciation, the Incarnation, and Mary's *fiat* — joins your voice to Gabriel's mission three times a day. It anchors morning, midday, and evening in the one event that changed everything. It takes approximately ninety seconds. It reorients the entire day.\n\n**Conversational attentiveness:** The tradition encourages brief, informal address to your guardian angel throughout the day — at decision points, at moments of temptation, at moments of gratitude. Not elaborate prayer. Just acknowledgment: *"Help me with this."* *"I think this is a prompting from you — I'm going to follow it."* *"Thank you."* The angel is not an emergency contact. It is a companion. Treat it as one.\n\n**Attention to interior promptings:** The tradition holds that guardian angels communicate primarily through the imagination and interior sense — gentle inclinations toward good, subtle promptings to pray, unexpected thoughts of a person who needs a call. These promptings do not override free will and do not feel supernatural. They feel like your own thoughts. The difference is the direction. When an interior prompting moves toward God, toward charity, toward prayer — the tradition has always recognized this as potentially angelic. Cultivate the habit of noticing and following.\n\n### The Liturgy: Where All Devotion Converges\n\nEvery form of private devotion to the angels finds its fullest expression in the liturgy:\n\nThe **Preface** of every Mass: *"Therefore, with all the Angels and Saints, we praise and glorify your name..."* The congregation joins the entire heavenly host, not metaphorically but really.\n\nThe **Sanctus**: the Church on earth joins the Seraphim's cry — a song that has never ceased since the first moment of angelic creation. Every time you sing *"Holy, Holy, Holy"*, you are taking your place in that choir.\n\nThe **incense** at solemn Mass: the smoke rising before the altar corresponds to the angelic offering of incense in Revelation 8:3-4. What the priest does with the thurible, the angel does before the throne.\n\nJohn Chrysostom taught that when Christians gather for the liturgy, the angels are present with them — not as spectators but as participants. The Mass is the meeting point of heaven and earth, and the angelic world is present at it. Come to Mass as if you are entering a room that contains beings you cannot see.\n\n### Three Errors to Avoid\n\n**Angels are not substitutes for God.** Any form of angel spirituality that makes angels the terminal destination — rather than the means to God — is a distortion. The Seraphim burn *for God*. The guardian angel serves *for* your salvation. All angelic activity points through itself to the Creator.\n\n**We do not command angels.** Several contemporary movements speak of "commanding" or "releasing" angels through prayer formulas. Scripture gives no basis for this. [Psalm 103:20](data-scripture="Psalm 103:20") says angels *"obey the voice of his word"* — God's word, not ours. We are permitted to ask, to invoke, to petition. We are not given authority over the angelic order. Presuming such authority is not faith; it is confusion about the order of creation.\n\n**Test what you receive.** Not every interior prompting is angelic. Not every spiritual experience is genuine. The Church's consistent teaching: *"Test the spirits to see whether they are from God"* ([1 John 4:1](data-scripture="1 John 4:1")). The test is conformity to Scripture, to the Church's teaching, and to the movement toward God. What genuinely comes from the holy angels will always, without exception, lead toward God.\n\n---\n\n*Next: We step back from the intimacy of personal devotion and take a wide view — surveying the full sweep of the Old Testament to see how the angels have moved through the whole history of God's covenant with humanity.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xshy000318pfex4n4689	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Fetish Objects and Idols in the Home	READING	\N	35	\N	t	![Fetish Objects and Idols in the Home](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsJ6lH1m4ZDlMH1zAnxErj0PQYB2bIe8GdaVWL)\n\n## Fetish Objects and Idols in the Home\n\nShe bought the Buddha statue for the garden because it looked peaceful. Her daughter's dreamcatcher — blue and purple, with feathers — hung above her bed. The carved African mask above the fireplace had come from a market in Nairobi. She was a churchgoer who had never considered any of these objects a spiritual concern.\n\nAfter a particularly intense prayer meeting with a group that included a discernment-gifted member, the woman mentioned the objects. The visitor asked if she could walk through the house. She did, stopping at each object and asking its origin and purpose. At the African mask, she paused. She said quietly, "This one has been inhabited."\n\nThe homeowner looked up the mask's specific tribal origin when she got home. It was a spirit mask — used in ceremony to invoke a specific deity. The carver had dedicated it before he sold it.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nFetish objects and idols include: Buddha statues (invitations to a false deity), dreamcatchers (developed within animistic traditions to involve spirit entities in filtering the spiritual environment), African and Pacific cultural masks (often used in ritual invocation and retaining spiritual attachment), Ganesh statues (representing a Hindu deity), and any object created for, used in, or dedicated to a spiritual system outside Jesus Christ.\n\nThese objects are sold in home decor stores, garden centers, and tourist markets worldwide. Their spiritual origins are not mentioned on the price tag.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\n[1 Corinthians 10:20](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 10:20"): *"The things which the Gentiles sacrifice, they sacrifice to devils."* An idol is not merely a symbol of false belief — it is a designated dwelling place for the demonic entity the idol represents. Objects created for or used in the worship of false deities are anchors: spiritual locations where the entities associated with those deities have established a presence.\n\nThe deception is aesthetic. The carved mask is genuinely beautiful. The Buddha statue is serene. The dreamcatcher is colorful and evocative. The beauty is real. The spiritual attachment that came with the object is also real.\n\n[Deuteronomy 7:26](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 7:26"): *"Neither shalt thou bring an abomination into thine house, lest thou be a cursed thing like it."* The contamination transfers. You do not merely coexist with the object — you become spiritually aligned with what it represents.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The dedication precedes the purchase.** The African spirit mask was dedicated to its deity before it was sold. The tourist who bought it for $40 took home a ritually dedicated idol, regardless of their ignorance. The spiritual attachment was established at dedication, not at purchase.\n\n**Idols create persistent spiritual atmospheres.** Homes with dedicated idols often have a distinctive spiritual atmosphere — a heaviness, a sense of something present, disturbances in sleep, unusual patterns of conflict or oppression — that lifts when the objects are removed. This is not superstition. It is the documented, consistent experience of deliverance ministers who work with home cleansing.\n\n**The combination effect is real.** A home with a Buddha statue in the garden, a dreamcatcher over the children's beds, and African masks on the walls has multiple anchor points for multiple entities. The cumulative spiritual effect is not decorative.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nWalk through your home with this question: *What was this made for?* Not what you intended when you bought it. Not what the seller said it meant. What was this object created to represent and invoke?\n\nAnything created for spirit invocation, pagan deity representation, or occultic religious purpose needs to be removed and destroyed. Not donated, where someone else receives the attachment. Not stored, where it continues to be present. Destroyed — as [Deuteronomy 7:25](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 7:25"), [Joshua 7:12-13](data-scripture="Joshua 7:12-13"), and [Acts 19:19](data-scripture="Acts 19:19") all consistently direct.\n\nThen pray through every room: the blood of Jesus Christ over every space where the objects were present, commanding every associated entity to leave, and filling the cleansed space with Scripture, worship, and the presence of the Holy Spirit.\n\n---\n\n*Nine forms of explicit occult practice documented. Before the covenant traps, a checkpoint.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Walk through your home in your mind. Is there anything in it — purchased, gifted, or inherited — whose spiritual purpose you cannot confirm is benign?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsia000b18pf43x78xae	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	False Gospels	READING	\N	40	\N	t	![False Gospels](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os3KRdR0IIS7BZaLyQzRAlocCY9dpmPik4Oqsx)\n\n## False Gospels\n\nHe had been saved through the prosperity gospel — genuinely. He had been in genuine bondage, heard a message that Christ died for him, responded in faith, and his life changed. He did not understand for years that the framework around the genuine gospel moment was systematically corrupting his theology.\n\nBy the time he understood it, he had been tithing to a preacher who privately owned six properties. He had sown "seed faith" into specific campaigns and been told his harvest had not come because his faith was insufficient. He had spent twelve years being told that Jesus had made him spiritually, physically, and financially whole — and privately wondering what was wrong with him that the financial part had never materialized.\n\nHe had not understood that the prosperity gospel makes God a vending machine and faith a coin — and that the god of the prosperity gospel is not the God of Scripture.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nFalse gospels are systematic distortions of the true gospel of Jesus Christ. They include:\n\n**The prosperity gospel:** God's will for every believer is financial abundance and physical health, accessed through faith, tithing, and positive confession. Suffering indicates insufficient faith or unmet spiritual conditions.\n\n**The New Apostolic Reformation (NAR):** A movement claiming that apostles and prophets with Scripture-level authority have been restored to the church, possessing ongoing direct revelation that supplements or supersedes the canon.\n\n**Progressive Christianity:** Christianity reframed around inclusivity and social justice while systematically removing or reinterpreting sin, hell, atonement, and the exclusivity of Christ.\n\n**Mormonism and Jehovah's Witnesses:** Systems that retain Christian vocabulary while presenting a different Christ, a different salvation, and a different theology — insufficient to save.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\n[Galatians 1:8-9](data-scripture="Galatians 1:8-9"): *"But though we, or an angel from heaven, preach any other gospel unto you than that which we have preached unto you, let him be accursed."* Paul writes this twice, in consecutive verses — the double occurrence in Greek rhetoric indicating the highest possible seriousness. No other statement in his letters receives this treatment.\n\nA false gospel is not a theological disagreement. It is a different religion that cannot save. The prosperity gospel's Christ and the Christ of Scripture are not the same being. The NAR's ongoing-revelation framework undermines the sufficiency and finality of Scripture. Progressive Christianity's Christ — a therapeutic figure who affirms rather than saves — cannot bear the weight of actual human sin.\n\nThe demonic dimension: [1 Timothy 4:1](data-scripture="1 Timothy 4:1") — *"In the latter times some shall depart from the faith, giving heed to seducing spirits, and doctrines of devils."* False gospels are demonic doctrines. The spirits behind them are seducing — they produce genuine emotional warmth, real community, and authentic-feeling spiritual experiences. The warmth is real. The framework is demonic.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Doctrinal contamination invites deceiving spirits to confirm the lie.** When a church adopts a false gospel framework, it invites the deceiving spirits behind that framework to produce counterfeit signs, counterfeit healings, and counterfeit encounters that validate the false teaching. The congregation experiences what feels like God's presence confirming the teaching. The presence is real. It is not God.\n\n**Those who believe false gospels are not saved.** This is the most serious consequence. A person who trusts in a Christ who guarantees health and wealth and is confused about their unhealed cancer is not trusting the Christ of Scripture — and the Christ of Scripture is the only one who can save. False gospels fill pews with sincere, warm, practicing people whose eternal standing remains unchanged.\n\n**Generational apostasy.** Children raised in false gospel churches inherit demonic frameworks disguised as Christianity — frameworks that may seem spiritually alive but cannot withstand the tests of real suffering and genuine encounter with the living God.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\n[1 Corinthians 15:3-4](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 15:3-4") is the gospel: *"Christ died for our sins according to the scriptures; and that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day."* Substitutionary atonement. Historical death. Bodily resurrection. Forgiveness of sins through faith in the finished work of the cross. This is the gospel. Anything else is another gospel.\n\nIf you have been formed by a false gospel framework — prosperity gospel, NAR, progressive Christianity — the work required is theological: a systematic rebuilding of your understanding of God, sin, salvation, and the Scripture's authority. Find a church that preaches the unvarnished gospel. Get under sound biblical teaching. Let your theology be rebuilt from the Word, not from what feels comfortable or spiritually exciting.\n\n---\n\n*Four covenant traps — institutions and theologies that bind beyond the individual. Before we turn inward, a checkpoint.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Under which gospel were you saved? Measure it against 1 Corinthians 15:3-4. Does it match — or has your foundation been something other than the finished work of the cross?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsif000f18pfxgnukihd	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Self-Harm and Cutting	READING	\N	44	\N	t	![Self-Harm and Cutting](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os8Ub1WhYwQn65F0NSyXfv2WGAqVjL7icrDpPI)\n\n## Self-Harm and Cutting\n\nShe told no one for three years. She wore long sleeves in August. She was a worship leader. She smiled appropriately. She told herself it was how she managed — that the cutting gave her a sense of control in seasons of overwhelming chaos, that the momentary relief was something she needed, that she would stop when things got better.\n\nShe did not stop when things got better. The behavior escalated. The locations expanded. The threshold lowered — less chaos required for the same response. She understood the addiction pattern intellectually. She had studied psychology.\n\nWhat she had not been given permission to understand was the spiritual dimension. Not instead of the psychological — alongside it. The specific spiritual assignment that was operating through the practice. The blood ritual dynamic no one had ever named.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nSelf-harm — cutting, burning, scratching, or any deliberate physical injury to one's own body — is increasingly common, particularly among adolescents and young adults. Research suggests that one in four adolescents has engaged in some form of self-injury. The behavior is primarily understood as a coping mechanism for emotional pain — a way of externalizing internal distress, creating a sense of control, or producing a neurochemical response (endorphin release) that temporarily reduces emotional pain.\n\nThe psychological account is accurate and important. What it is insufficient to explain is why this behavior is so extraordinarily resistant to treatment, why it follows specific ritualistic patterns, why it escalates in ways that addiction models partially but not fully account for, and why it sometimes accompanies or precedes other forms of spiritual bondage.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\n[Leviticus 17:11](data-scripture="Leviticus 17:11"): *"The life of the flesh is in the blood."* Blood carries covenant weight in Scripture. The deliberate shedding of one's own blood creates a spiritual transaction.\n\nThe demonic deception is the presentation of self-harm as a coping mechanism — functional, controllable, private, and ultimately benign. The temporary relief it produces is real and chemically documented. It is also a demonic anesthetic: a counterfeit peace that deepens dependency in exactly the way every demonic bondage operates. It works just enough to bring the person back. Each return deepens the enemy's legal access. The Spirit of Death operating through self-harm has a specific long-term assignment: escalation toward lethal completion.\n\nThis is not stated to produce fear. It is stated because naming the spiritual assignment is the first step toward revoking its legal ground.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Blood shed in self-harm gives the Spirit of Death specific access.** The legal mechanism is the blood covenant: shedding blood establishes agreement with whatever receives the blood as an offering. Self-harm's blood is received by whatever spiritual entity is operating in the domain of destruction and death.\n\n**The ritualistic dimension is real and significant.** Self-harm typically involves specific tools, specific locations on the body, specific sequences and conditions. This ritualization mirrors occult practice. The more ritualized the behavior, the more it functions as a formal spiritual act.\n\n**The Spirit of Death escalates.** The documented clinical trajectory of untreated self-harm is escalation in frequency, severity, and threshold lowering. This trajectory is consistent with the operation of a demonic assignment with a specific destination.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nStop reading this as information about other people.\n\nIf you have engaged in self-harm at any point in your life — whether you are currently practicing it, whether you stopped years ago, whether it was "only a few times" — you have shed blood in a transaction with the Spirit of Death. The transaction does not expire because you stopped. It does not become spiritually irrelevant because you are now a believer. It remains an open legal account until it is specifically addressed.\n\nHere is what you need to do:\n\n**Name it.** Not "I struggled with self-harm." Name the specific practice, the specific tools, the approximate duration, the physical locations on your body. Vagueness protects the enemy's claim. Specificity is what revokes it.\n\n**Repent for it as a violation of the temple.** [1 Corinthians 6:19](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 6:19"): *"Your body is the temple of the Holy Ghost."* What was done to the temple was sin — not only pain management, not only addiction, not only a phase. It was a sin with a specific spiritual consequence. Repent for it in those terms.\n\n**Renounce the Spirit of Death by name.** Command it to leave the body, the bloodline, and every space where the cutting occurred. Plead the blood of Jesus Christ — blood shed once, for the forgiveness of all sin — over every scar, every wound, every location on your body that was violated.\n\n**Tell someone who can pray with you.** The secrecy is part of the bondage. Breaking the secrecy — with a pastor, a counselor, a trusted elder — is part of breaking the spiritual assignment.\n\nThe question you cannot skip: *Who knows?* If the answer is no one, that is the first thing that needs to change.\n\n---\n\n*Self-harm is a blood covenant with death. The next lesson examines a different form of self-destruction — one that operates more slowly, through the body's relationship with food.*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk48i001aewhjl1jsks6h	cmnknk48e000xewhj49ao5az0	Lesson 27 — The Doctrine of the Trinity	READING	5495	12	\N	t	The Trinity is Christianity's most distinctive and most attacked doctrine. Jehovah's Witnesses say it's a pagan invention. Modalists say the Father, Son, and Spirit are one Person wearing three masks. Tritheists say they're three separate Gods. All three are wrong — and all three errors have real consequences for how you relate to God, how you pray, and whether the gospel makes any sense at all.\n\nLast time we explored the gifts and fruit the Holy Spirit produces in believers. Now we step back to examine the nature of the God in whom this Spirit dwells — the triune Being Scripture describes from Genesis to Revelation.\n\n![Lesson 27 — The Doctrine of the Trinity](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os4sKzB4L3Ls52XczwCYNqdZVf8hMUGlEvQ0nD)\n\n### 1. ELOHIM\n\nThis is the Hebrew word for "God" that you'll find in Genesis 1:1 and about 2,700 other places throughout the Old Testament. Here's what's fascinating: it's a uni-plural noun, meaning "Gods," and it's actually translated that way 239 times (Gen. 3:5; Exod. 22:28; 1 Sam. 4:8; Dan. 2:11; 4:6-9; 5:11, 14; etc.).\n\nElohim is the plural form of *Eloah*, which means "deity" or "God." When used with the definite article, it refers to the Supreme God. It's also translated "judges" in Exod. 21:6; 22:8-9 and "angels" in Ps. 8:5.\n\nSometimes Elohim appears with plural verbs and pronouns in the Hebrew text. For example, Gen. 20:13 literally reads "the Gods they caused me to wander," and Gen. 35:7 says "there the Gods they appeared unto him." You'll also notice plural pronouns used when God speaks of the different members of the Godhead—words like "us" (Gen. 1:26; 3:22; 11:7; Isa. 6:8; Jn. 17:21), "our" (Gen. 1:26; Jn. 14:23), "we" (Jn. 14:23; 17:11, 22), and "their" (Ps. 2:3).\n\nThink about this: first, second, and third personal pronouns are used hundreds of times in Scripture—sometimes of one, two, or three persons in the deity. In John 17 alone, Jesus uses 162 pronouns when speaking to and about His Father! Psalm 119 contains 610 pronouns used by man to and of God.\n\nHere's the thing: when the different members of the Godhead speak to and about each other just like people do, should we accuse them of misrepresenting themselves or of not knowing how to use human language properly? If we can understand what pronouns mean when people use them with each other, we should be able to understand them the same way when the members of the Godhead use them.\n\nWhen singular pronouns are used of deity, it's because one of the three persons of the Trinity is speaking of Himself, representing the whole Godhead, or speaking to one person about another—as you can clearly see in Jn. 14:16-17, 26; 15:26; 16:7-15; 17:1-25.\n\nIn the Old Testament, the Father was the prominent speaker (Heb. 1:1-3; Acts 3:21). In the Gospels, the Son took center stage (Jn. 5:47; 6:33; 8:26, 28, 38; 12:49-50; 17:8). And now, the Holy Spirit is the prominent speaker (Jn. 14:26; 15:26; 16:13-15; Acts 2:4; 13:2; 15:28; 20:28).\n\nSometimes singular pronouns refer to the whole Godhead as a unit (Exod. 20:3; Isa. 44:6, 8; 45:5, 21; 46:9; Hos. 13:4; etc.). It's similar to how the whole Church, as the body of Christ, is spoken of as a "man" and "he" (Eph. 2:14-15; 4:13; 5:25-27; 2 Thess. 2:7-8).\n\nSo the one Elohim isn't one person or one in number—it's one in *unity*. Elohim isn't a divided deity but three persons in "one God," or one deity. The word itself doesn't tell us there are exactly three, but it does tell us deity is plural. And here's something striking: God is referred to in the plural twice as many times as the word "Jesus" appears in both Testaments combined!\n\n### 2. YEHOVAH\n\nThis Hebrew word for "Lord" appears in Deut. 6:4 and about 7,600 times throughout the Old Testament. It means "the Self-existent," "Eternal and Immutable One," or "Unity."\n\nNow, this word doesn't tell us *how many* persons are in the "One [Unified] Lord," but Scripture mentions three persons who are called "Lord," who are "Self-existent" and "Eternal"—so all three can be called "Jehovah."\n\nIn Gen. 19:24; Ps. 110:1; Mt. 22:44; Zech. 2:10-11, we see both the Father and the Son called "Lord." And when you compare Exod. 16:7 with Heb. 3:7-8, and Isa. 6:8-9 with Acts 28:25, and Exod. 17:7 with Heb. 3:7-9, and Jer. 31:31-34 with Heb. 10:15-16, you'll see that the Holy Spirit is also called "Lord" or "Jehovah." (See Lesson Four, Point 6, where all three are called "God.")\n\nYehovah is rendered "Jehovah" four times (Exod. 6:3; Ps. 83:18; Isa. 12:2; 26:4). Jehovah also appears in many compound names of deity, which we won't list here.\n\n### 3. EL\n\nThis Hebrew word for "God" appears in about 250 places. It means "the Strong One" or "Elohim the Omnipotent." While Elohim is "God the Creator," El emphasizes His omnipotence put into action. All three persons of the Trinity are omnipotent, as we've seen in earlier lessons.\n\n### 4. ELOAH\n\nThis Hebrew word for "God" appears in 56 places. It refers to "Elohim who is to be worshipped." You'll often find it used when worship of idols is contrasted with worship of the true God—the "living God" compared to dead gods. It means "deity" and "God."\n\n### 5. ELYON\n\nThis Hebrew word for "Most High" is translated that way 40 times. It means "the Supreme," "Most High," "Highest," "Lofty." It's El, the possessor of Heaven and Earth, and Elohim, the Creator of Heaven and Earth.\n\nIt's translated "High" in Ps. 78:35; Dan. 4:2 and "higher" when referring to Jesus as God's "firstborn" in Ps. 89:27. But here's something important: Jesus in the New Testament is never called the Most High—only the *Son* of the Most High God (Mk. 5:7; Lk. 1:32-35; 8:28).\n\nWhen Christ was born, the angels sang to the "God in the highest," who was not Jesus (Lk. 2:14). The Father is still the "head of Christ" (1 Cor. 11:3), so He is rightfully the Most High God.\n\n### 6. ADON\n\nThis Hebrew word for "Lord" is translated that way 195 times in the Old Testament. It means "Sovereign," "Ruler," "Master."\n\n*Adonai* is the emphatic form and is translated "Lord" 430 times in the Old Testament. It's also translated "lords" four times (Gen. 19:2; Deut. 10:17; Ps. 136:3; Isa. 26:13). Two Adonais are mentioned in Ps. 110:1 and referred to in the New Testament as the Father and the Son (Mt. 22:44).\n\n### 7. Other Names\n\nA few other names of God in the Old Testament include:\n\n- "JAH" (Ps. 68:4, 18)\n- "I AM THAT I AM" and "I AM" (Exod. 3:13-15)\n- "God Almighty" (Exod. 6:3)\n- "Lord God" (Gen. 2:4 and hundreds of other times)\n- "Jealous" (Exod. 34:14)\n- "The Lord of Hosts" (Isa. 47:4 and 281 other times)\n- "Holy" (Isa. 57:15)\n- And many others\n\nAll of this proves that the teaching that "Jesus" is the only God and the only name of that God simply isn't scriptural. If God said these were His names and some human beings say they're not, who should we believe?\n\nSome claim all these names are merely titles signifying office, rank, or relationship, but that's just human theory contradicting the Scriptures, which clearly call them real names.\n\nGod's names appear over 19,000 times in the Bible, always in connection with His eternal plan of creation, redemption, and eternal rulership over all things (Dan. 2:44-45; 7:13-14, 27; Lk. 1:32-33; 1 Cor. 15:24-28; Eph. 1:10; 2:7; Rev. 5:10; 11:15; 22:4-5).\n\n---\n\n## II. Names of God in the New Testament\n\n### 1. THEOS\n\nThis is the Greek word for "God," used 1,332 times in the New Testament. It means "deity" and "God," and with the definite article means "the Supreme Deity." The Father, the Son, and the Holy Ghost are all called God, as we saw in Lesson Four, Point 6.\n\n### 2. KURIOS\n\nThis Greek word for "Lord" is used 672 times in the New Testament. It means "Lord," "Master," and "Sir," and is used of men 31 times.\n\n### 3. IESOUS\n\nThis is the Greek word for "Jesus," appearing 979 times in the New Testament. It's the Greek form of the Hebrew *Yehowshua*, rendered "Joshua" 215 times in the Old Testament. In fact, Joshua of the Old Testament is actually called "Jesus" in the New Testament in Acts 7:45 and Heb. 4:8.\n\nHere's something crucial: Jesus is *never* the name of the Father or the Spirit in either Testament. It wasn't even the name of the second person of the Godhead until He became man and the Son of God about 1,900 years ago. It's the human name of the Son of God, as we covered in Lesson Twenty-one, Point VI.\n\n### 4. CHRISTOS\n\nThis Greek word, which we translate "Christ," is used 575 times in the New Testament. It literally means "anointed" and is equivalent to the Hebrew *mashiyach*, translated "Messiah" twice in the Old Testament (Dan. 9:24-26) and twice in the New Testament (Jn. 1:41; 4:25).\n\nLike the name "Jesus," it doesn't refer to deity but to the humanity of Jesus Christ. He became the Christ—the Anointed One—thirty years after He was born in a human body and after He was named "Jesus," as we saw in Lesson Twenty-one, Point VI.\n\nMany other names of God's Son weren't actually true of Him until He took on these roles. For example, He had to become man before He could be called the Son of man, the Son of God, Jesus, Christ, Lord Jesus Christ, Messiah, Emmanuel, Son of David, the Lion of the Tribe of Judah, the Lamb of God, Mediator, and many other names.\n\nSome use two passages (Gal. 3:17; 1 Pet. 1:11) to teach that "Christ" was a name of Jesus back in Old Testament times, but when you examine them, that's not what they say. The phrase "in Christ" in Gal. 3:17 is omitted in the best texts and was added by some copyist. You won't find it in the R.V., Weymouth, Centenary Translation, Concordant Version, Nestle's Greek Text, Moffatt, and many other translations.\n\nThe second passage (1 Pet. 1:11) should be understood in light of how Peter would naturally speak about Jesus *after* He became the Christ. When referring to what the second person of the Trinity did in Old Testament times, we might speak of Christ doing those things—but in reality, He wasn't yet "the Christ" when He did them. At that time, He was God but not yet the Son of God or the Anointed of God. Now that He's become man and "Christ," this name can be used of Him even when speaking of what He did before He received that title.\n\n### 5. THE FATHER, THE SON, AND THE HOLY GHOST\n\n(Mt. 28:19; 1 Jn. 5:7-8)\n\nSome teach that these aren't names but mere titles. But that teaching shows a misunderstanding of how language works and contradicts God's Word. Our dictionaries and grammars call such words "nouns" or "substantives"—and all nouns are names. Not all are "proper names" of specific individuals, but usage in any particular context shows whether a word becomes a proper name.\n\nIn Mt. 28:19, it's not just any father, any son, or any ghost. It's specifically "the Father," "the Son," and "the Holy Ghost." The definite article "the" is used before each word in both Greek and English. These terms, used and associated this way, can apply to no other persons on Earth or in Heaven.\n\n"The Father" in the New Testament is *never* applied to men, to Christ, or to the Holy Ghost—only and always to the first person of the Godhead, "the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ" (see Lesson Twenty-one, Points 8, 9, and 35).\n\n"The Son" is *never* applied to men, to "the Father," or to "the Holy Ghost"—only and always to the second person of the Godhead, "the Son of the Father" (see Point 35, Lesson Twenty-one).\n\n"The Holy Ghost" is *never* applied to men, to "the Father," or to "the Son"—only and always to the third person of the Godhead, who proceeds from the Father and the Son (see Lesson Twenty-five, Point VI).\n\nThe fact that these terms are always spelled with capital letters—like all proper names—proves they are proper names in Scripture. It was the consensus of all Bible scholars that these are true and proper names.\n\nFunk and Wagnall's Dictionary says "a name is the appellation by which a person or thing is known." Webster says it's "the title by which any person or thing is known or designated." The Greek word *onoma* means "the name or word by which a person or thing is called, and by which he is distinguished from all others."\n\nSo "the Father," "the Son," and "the Holy Ghost" are names by which the three persons in the Godhead are known and distinguished from each other. They're not the *only* names of each, but they're the ones Jesus used when giving the Church the baptism formula and authority to baptize.\n\nNow, some ask how "name" in the singular could be used of three persons and three names. They argue that if there were three persons, it would read "in the *names* of" not "in the *name* of." But this just shows a misunderstanding of how language works.\n\nThink of it like this: when we send an ambassador to a foreign land, he does business "in the name of" (not "in the names of") the United States. Does that prove there's only one state? Of course not—there are fifty separate states in the one United States! The singular "name" in Mt. 28:19 affirms the equality and oneness of the Godhead—a perfect union of three persons in "one God"—just like "the United States" affirms the equality and oneness of fifty states in a perfect Union.\n\nWe could also speak of each state separately: "In the name of Missouri and of Illinois and of Ohio," and so on. It's not necessary to add "in the name" before each state, because once it's stated at the beginning, it's understood to apply to each one.\n\nThe same is true in Mt. 28:19. We don't need to repeat "in the name" before each person—once stated, it applies to each. Consider these examples:\n\n- "All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth" (Mt. 28:18) doesn't need to repeat "all power is given unto me" for us to understand it applies to both places.\n- "In the beginning God created the heaven" (Gen. 1:1) doesn't need to repeat "In the beginning God" for us to understand He also created the Earth at that time.\n- "The God of Abraham, and of Isaac, and of Jacob" (Acts 3:13) doesn't need to change to "the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob" for us to understand He's the God of all three.\n\nJesus knew how to use language without having to repeat "in the name" before each person. It's just as correct to say it this way as to repeat it. Acts 3:13 is just as clear as Acts 7:32, where "the God of" *is* repeated before Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.\n\nJesus knew the disciples understood there were three persons in the Godhead. And He knew everyone else in any age could understand the same if they'd be honest and believe the plain Scriptures.\n\nOne of the most foolish arguments goes like this: "Father is not a name; so what is the name of the Father? Son is not a name; so what is the name of the Son? Holy Ghost is not a name; so what is the name of the Holy Ghost?" That's like saying: "Missouri is not a name; what is the name of Missouri? Abraham is not a name; what is the name of Abraham?"\n\nIf a name is any word by which a person or thing is known, then "the Father," "the Son," and "the Holy Ghost" are names—just as much as "Missouri," "Abraham," or any other name. It doesn't have to fit someone's pet doctrine to qualify as a name.\n\nThink about how any father and son can address each other using only those words—"Father" and "Son"—and never use any other name. This is true not only of people but also of God the Father and God the Son.\n\nNot once did Jesus address the Father by any name except "Father" (Mt. 11:25-27; 26:39, 42; Mk. 14:36; Lk. 11:2; 23:34, 46; Jn. 12:27-28; 17:1-25). And not once did the Father address the Son by any name except "Son" (Mt. 3:16-17; 17:5; Jn. 12:28).\n\nJesus repeatedly used "Father" when speaking about God to others. When He spoke of "the name of the Father," He assumed the disciples knew exactly whom He meant. They also knew whom He meant by "the Holy Ghost," because they'd heard much about Him coming to take Jesus' place (Jn. 14:16-17, 26; 16:7-15; 20:22; Acts 1:1-8; Mt. 10:1, 20; 12:28-32; etc.). John the Baptist had even taught them about the Holy Ghost before Jesus appeared (Mt. 3:11; Jn. 1:32-34).\n\nThe disciples knew the Father was separate from the Son and Spirit because Jesus referred to God as "Father" 181 times. Later, the disciples called Him "Father" 78 times. Not once is He confused with or called "Jesus" or "the Holy Ghost."\n\nThey knew the Son was separate from the Father and Holy Ghost because Jesus distinguished between Himself and the Father 110 times; God the Father did so ten times; demons did ten times; and the disciples later did 85 times. Not once did anyone confuse the Father, Son, and Holy Ghost or call the Son "the Father" or "the Holy Ghost."\n\nJesus spoke of the Spirit 24 times as a separate person from Himself and the Father (see Lesson Twenty-five). Bible writers refer to the Spirit as separate from the Father and Son about 170 times. Not once is the Spirit called "the Father" or "the Son," and not once is He confused with them as being the same person.\n\nSo "the Father" is a name designating Him as separate from "the Son" and "the Spirit." "The Son" designates Him as separate from "the Father" and "the Spirit." And "the Holy Ghost" designates Him as separate from "the Father" and "the Son."\n\nThe phrase "in the name of" means "by the authority of." Webster says it's used "in behalf of, by the authority of; as, 'in the name of the law.'" This is how Jesus and many Bible writers used it:\n\n- "In the name of Jesus Christ" means by the authority of Jesus Christ (Acts 2:38; 4:10; 16:16; 1 Cor. 5:4; 6:11; Eph. 5:20; 1 Thess. 3:6)\n- "In the name of David" means by the authority of David (1 Sam. 25:5-9)\n- "In the name of Paul" means by the authority of Paul (1 Cor. 1:13-15)\n- "In the name of the Lord" means by the authority of the Lord (Deut. 18:5-7, 22; 21:5)\n- "In the name of the Lord of Hosts" means by the authority of the Lord of Hosts (1 Sam. 17:45)\n- "In my Father's name" means by the authority of my Father (Jn. 5:43; 10:25; 17:12)\n- "In my name" means by the authority of my name (Mk. 16:17; Jn. 14:12-15, 26; 15:16; 16:23-26)\n\n"By the name of" means the same as "in the name of" (Acts 4:10, 30). Speaking "in the name of" (Acts 4:17-18; 5:28, 40; 8:12; 9:27-29) means "by the authority of" the one who sent the speaker—just like in the Old Testament (Jer. 20:9; 26:9-20).\n\nSo "in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost" means we're to baptize *by the authority* of the Father, Son, and Holy Ghost—not by the authority of the Son only.\n\nIf we baptize only in the Son's name, we rob the Father and Holy Ghost of their rightful authority in redemption, which baptism symbolizes. We also directly violate the last commandment Jesus gave before He left, setting aside the very authority He said He received in Heaven and Earth (Mt. 28:18).\n\nIf He had authority to command this form of baptism and never authorized a change, then that authority still stands. To reject it is to reject Jesus Christ.\n\nThose who believe Jesus is the only God shouldn't reject and contradict His authority. They should find a way to harmonize Acts with obedience to Mt. 28:19.\n\nIt's similar to this: suppose you were authorized to do a job in the name of J.C. Penney and Co., Sears Roebuck and Co., and Montgomery Ward and Co. If you only did it in the name of J.C. Penney and Co., rejecting the others because "in the name" wasn't repeated before each, you'd be robbing them of their rightful recognition and authority. Would that make all three companies one company? Of course not.\n\nIn Mt. 28:19, we have the full authority of the whole Godhead and of each member specifically. Refusing to recognize more than one of the three doesn't make the other two disappear or make them all one person.\n\nIn Acts 2:38; 8:16; 10:48; 19:5, the emphasis is on Jesus' authority—because *His* authority was what the Jews were rejecting at that time. They didn't question the Father's or Spirit's authority; they believed and accepted it. But accepting Jesus' authority like they accepted God's? That was another matter entirely.\n\nThe apostles in Acts simply demanded that the Jews accept Jesus' name—being baptized, saved, and healed by His authority. But nowhere do they reject or change Mt. 28:19 by saying "in the name of Jesus only." Not one passage demands the Jews accept Jesus as the *only* God and the *only* authority. Instead, they were commanded to accept Him *like* they accepted God.\n\nTo baptize only in Jesus' name instead of following Mt. 28:19—based merely on an inference that because all three names aren't mentioned in Acts they shouldn't be used—is to risk God's judgment.\n\nCan't we obey *both* Mt. 28:19 and Acts? We can and must, because both are God's Word, and both must be obeyed (2 Tim. 3:16-17). Anyone obeying Mt. 28:19 automatically obeys Acts. But interpreting Acts to mean we should baptize in Jesus' name only means disobeying Mt. 28:19.\n\nIn other words, baptizing by the authority of all three in Mt. 28:19 automatically satisfies Acts. But baptizing by Jesus' authority *only* dishonors the other two in Mt. 28:19 and directly transgresses it. Obeying Acts while disobeying Matthew isn't excusable for thinking people.\n\nAnd even if we were to follow Acts alone as the baptism formula—which passage in Acts should we use? They all differ in wording!\n\nThose who insist baptism should be only in Jesus' name, and who prey upon honest and uninformed people, may claim they obey Mt. 28:19. But they never actually obey it, never recognize it in baptism, and always re-baptize those who were baptized according to Mt. 28:19.\n\nIf they claim to obey Mt. 28:19, ask them to baptize you that way and see how quickly they back down. There you'll see a concrete example of deliberately rejecting part of the Bible.\n\nCouldn't Jesus have said what these groups teach, if that's what He meant? If He didn't say what they teach, then that's not what He means—and we'd better reject their false teaching on baptism and obey Mt. 28:19. We must either reject this false teaching or reject God. We can't believe and obey both, because they're opposites.\n\nThe preposition "of" and the conjunction "and" repeated before each of the three names in Mt. 28:19 further prove three separate persons. If someone said "a gift of John and of James and of George," he means a gift from *three* persons, not one.\n\nJesus didn't say to baptize only by His authority, but also by the authority of the Father and of the Holy Ghost. He didn't tell them to do this only until He came back in ten days as the Holy Ghost (as some teach). Instead, He said, "Teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you... even unto the end of the world."\n\nThere was no better time for Jesus to tell the disciples He was the only God, the Father, the Holy Ghost, and all of God—but instead He revealed three separate persons in the Godhead.\n\n### 6. EVERLASTING FATHER\n\nSome groups argue that "Father" isn't a name, yet they insist "the everlasting Father" is a name of Jesus and try to prove from Isa. 9:6-7 that Jesus is "the Father" of the New Testament.\n\nBut here's how ancient Hebrews, Greeks, and other Eastern peoples used such language: anyone who originated a custom or had a distinguishing characteristic was called the "father" of that thing. So:\n\n- Satan is called "father of lies" because he originated them (Jn. 8:44)\n- Jabal is called "the father of tent dwellers" because he originated that lifestyle (Gen. 4:20-21)\n- Abraham is called "the father of circumcision" because it started with him (Rom. 4:12)\n- God is called "the Father of mercies" because He is merciful (2 Cor. 1:3)\n- People are called "children of disobedience" and "children of wrath" because they live in disobedience and are destined for wrath (Eph. 2:2-3; see also Mt. 9:15; 13:38; Lk. 16:8; Col. 3:6; 2 Sam. 7:10; Job 41:34)\n\n"The everlasting Father" literally means "the Father of eternity," "the planner of the ages," or "the giver of eternal life"—as in Heb. 1:2 (margin); Jn. 3:15-18; 6:54, 68; 10:28; 14:6; 17:2-3; Rom. 5:21; 1 Jn. 1:2; 5:11.\n\nThe Son is called this because He died to give eternal life to others, and because through Him the Father planned the ages and gives eternal life. But He's not the *only* person in the Godhead who could be called this—both the Father and the Spirit also give life and had a part in God's plan (Rom. 6:23; 1 Pet. 5:10; Jn. 3:15-18; 15:24, 26; 17:3; Rom. 8:2, 10-11; Gal. 6:8).\n\nThe reason the Son is called this in Isa. 9:6-7 is to establish marks of divinity for the coming Son, so people would recognize He's as much God in nature as the Father and Spirit. Without these divine markers in prophecy, no one would have recognized Him as Divine.\n\nBut "the everlasting Father" doesn't prove Jesus is the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ in the New Testament. All three persons, by virtue of being God, could be called "the everlasting Father" or "giver of eternal life"—because this term has nothing to do with the Father "begetting" a child. It's about that idiomatic Hebrew usage we discussed.\n\nAll three persons couldn't be "the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ," because only one could be the Son and only one could be the Father, as we've already seen.\n\n---\n\n## III. Other Proofs in the Old Testament of Three Persons in the Godhead\n\n### 1. Plural Names, Verbs, and Pronouns\n\nRight from the beginning, God used plural names, verbs, and pronouns when speaking of the Godhead (see Point I.1 above). He's also revealed the Godhead as consisting of several persons, as we'll see below.\n\nScripture contains many clear statements about two and three persons in the Godhead. In Gen. 3:22, He plainly said, "The man is become as one of us."\n\nThe phrase "as one of" means "like each person of several persons of the same kind." You can verify this wherever "as one of" appears in Scripture (Gen. 19:14; 42:27; 49:16; Exod. 12:48; Lev. 19:34; 24:22; Num. 12:12; 2 Sam. 13:13; 14:13; Job 12:4; 13:9; 19:11; 29:25; Ps. 119:162; Mk. 1:22; 6:15; 9:26).\n\nNo one could use such a phrase without referring to more than one person who could make "us." If God refers to the Godhead as "us" here and elsewhere, we certainly ought to believe He knows what He's talking about and stop insisting on "one person only." We'll see many more examples in the following points.\n\n### 2. Theophanies—God Appearing to People\n\nThe appearances of God to humans prove plurality of persons. Two and three persons called "Lord" and "God" are seen at the same time and place—so the deity must be as many persons as are clearly seen. Each has been seen with a separate body performing separate actions, just like other persons.\n\n> **(1)** God appeared to Abraham in Gen. 18. Then in Gen. 19:24, this "Lord" who was visibly present before Abraham rained fire upon Sodom "from the Lord [another one] out of heaven."\n\n> **(2)** Two persons are seen with human eyes as two separate beings with two separate bodies in Dan. 7:9-14. "The Ancient of Days" is sitting on a throne, and "one like the Son of man" is coming with the clouds of Heaven down to where the other one sits. The one on the throne gives the Son of man a kingdom.\n>\n> Anyone reading this passage honestly will see two separate persons. The one on the throne had to have a body—otherwise, how could He sit down, wear clothes, or have hair on His head? He's described as a real person just like others. Seven times singular personal pronouns are used of Him. God was actually seen by the prophet—or else the prophet lied.\n>\n> The literal description proves God is a\n\n---\n\nThe Trinity is not a puzzle to be resolved — it's a reality to be inhabited. You pray to the Father, through the Son, in the power of the Spirit. Each Person has a distinct role in your salvation and your daily life. So here's the question: In your actual prayer life, are you engaging with all three Persons of the Trinity — or has your faith effectively become unitarian in practice, relating primarily to one Person while the others remain abstract?	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612vv001dgeo07rmh6kqn	cmq6612vm0013geo0kqjj27k2	Lesson 14 — Raphael: Healer, Guide, and Companion	READING	900	4	\N	t	![Lesson 14 — Raphael: Healer, Guide, and Companion](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsqFRrsTAY8t92WkHGcRrZATmyFMPu3f04ih6v)\n\n## Raphael — Healer, Guide, and Companion\n\n### An Archangel in Disguise\n\nThere is a moment in the Book of Tobit that every reader of Scripture should stop and dwell on.\n\nA young man named Tobias is about to set out on a long journey — a journey his blind father needs him to make, through dangerous country, to collect a debt from a distant relative. Tobias goes to find a guide.\n\nA man is standing there. He says his name is Azariah. He says he knows the road. He offers his services as a companion and guide.\n\nHe is, in fact, the Archangel Raphael — one of the seven holy angels who stand before God's throne — traveling incognito. And he will not reveal this for weeks.\n\nWhat follows in the Book of Tobit is the most intimate extended portrait of angelic ministry in all of Scripture. For the duration of the journey, Raphael:\n\n- Protects Tobias from a monstrous fish that attacks him in the Tigris River\n- Instructs him to use parts of the fish for medicinal and spiritual purposes\n- Guides him to the house of his relative Raguel and the hand of Sarah, a woman afflicted by a demon\n- Remains present while Tobias prays over his new wife and the affliction is driven away\n- Counsels him on how to honor both his wife and his father\n- Travels ahead to collect the debt while Tobias celebrates his wedding\n- And throughout all of this — all of this — he has been presenting the prayers of Tobias and Sarah and Tobit before the throne of God\n\nNone of this is visible. None of it announced. A man named Azariah is doing it all, and no one knows.\n\nWhen it is over, after Tobit's sight is restored and Tobias has come home safely, Raphael reveals himself:\n\n> [Tobit 12:15](data-scripture="Tobit 12:15") "I am Raphael, one of the seven holy angels who present the prayers of the saints and enter into the presence of the holy God."\n\nAnd then, almost immediately, he ascends from their sight.\n\n### His Name\n\nThe Hebrew *Raphael* means **"God heals"** — *rapha* (to heal) + *El* (God). His name is his entire ministry in two words. Wherever Raphael appears, something broken is restored.\n\n### Three Dimensions of Raphael's Ministry\n\n**I. Healing.** The fish gall that restores Tobit's sight. The instructions that protect Sarah. The presence that accompanies Tobias home. Raphael does not merely announce healing — he participates in it as God's instrument. He is the patron of physicians, pharmacists, the blind, and all who work with the sick.\n\n**II. Accompaniment.** This is the dimension of Raphael's ministry that most directly mirrors what every guardian angel does. He traveled with Tobias not as a spectacular divine intervention but as a companion on the road — present, practical, attentive, quietly serving without demanding recognition. He was more useful as Azariah than he would have been as a blazing angel of the Lord. Anonymity was the point.\n\n**III. Intercession.** This is the revelation that changes everything. Raphael was not merely accompanying Tobias. He was *presenting prayers*:\n\n> [Tobit 12:12](data-scripture="Tobit 12:12") "When you and your daughter-in-law Sarah prayed, I brought a reminder of your prayer before the Holy One; and when you buried the dead, I was likewise present with you."\n\n*Every prayer Tobit had ever prayed while living righteously, every act of mercy, every whispered plea in a dark night* — Raphael had been carrying these before God. Tobit did not know. Tobit thought he was praying into the silence. He was not. Someone was there, taking his words upward.\n\n### Raphael as the Portrait of Your Guardian Angel\n\nThe most significant thing about Raphael's story is not about Raphael. It is about you.\n\nRaphael's ministry to Tobias — the anonymity, the accompaniment, the teaching through circumstances, the physical protection, the constant intercession — is the template for what every guardian angel does for every human being it is assigned to.\n\nYour guardian angel has been present at every prayer you have ever prayed. It has been carrying those prayers before God. It has been subtly inclining you toward good — not forcing, not overwhelming, but present, attentive, and active. It does not require recognition. It does not need you to know its name. It serves because it was made to serve you, because God appointed it, and because it loves the God who gave you into its care.\n\nEvery Christian, in the deepest sense, has their own Raphael.\n\n> [Psalm 91:11](data-scripture="Psalm 91:11") "For he will command his angels concerning you to guard you in all your ways."\n\n### Raphael's Patrons\n\nRaphael is patron of:\n- Travelers and pilgrims\n- The blind and those with eye conditions\n- Medical workers, pharmacists, nurses\n- Those seeking a holy spouse\n\nEach patronage flows directly from the Tobit narrative. He is not the patron of these by assignment — he is their patron because his story is their story.\n\n---\n\n*Next: We have now met all three named Archangels — the warrior, the messenger, the healer. In Part V we turn to the angels who are closest to you: the guardian angels, the ninth and lowest choir, who stand beside every human soul from before birth to natural death. What we find there may be the most personally significant teaching in this entire course.*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk4br0027ewhjrg2n703s	cmnknk4bp001qewhjk5bcqnfj	Lesson 48 — The Ten Horns and the Beast Itself	READING	2671	16	\N	t	The ten horns of Revelation's beast have been identified with everything from the ten Roman provinces to the ten toes of Daniel's statue to various modern alliances of nations. What's notable is that every generation has found its own political moment in these symbols — which tells you something: the underlying reality these symbols describe keeps reasserting itself in different forms until it finally arrives in the one that matches the prophecy exactly.\n\nLast time we examined the beast with seven heads — the final form of Gentile world power. Now we focus on the ten horns specifically: what they represent, when they arise, and how they relate to the Antichrist's rise to global dominance.\n\n> "The fourth beast shall be the fourth kingdom upon the earth [from Daniel's time to Christ's coming] which shall be diverse from all kingdoms, and shall devour the whole earth . . . And the ten horns out of this kingdom are ten kings that shall arise: and another shall rise after them; and he shall be diverse from the first [ten] and shall subdue three kings [of the ten, which are the other three divisions of Greece besides Syria, the one Antichrist shall come from]" (Dan. 7:23-24).\n\n> "And the ten horns which thou sawest are ten kings, which have received no kingdom as yet; but receive power as kings one hour [period] with the beast. These have one mind, and shall give their power and strength unto the beast. These shall make war with the Lamb, and the Lamb shall overcome them: for he is Lord of lords, and King of kings: and they that are with him are called, and chosen, and faithful. And he said unto me, The waters which thou sawest where the whore sitteth, are peoples, and multitudes, and nations, and tongues. And the ten horns which thou sawest upon the beast, these shall hate the whore, and shall make her desolate and naked, and shall eat her flesh, and burn her with fire. For God hath put in their hearts to fulfill his will, and to agree, and to give their kingdom unto the beast, until the words of God shall be fulfilled" (Rev. 17:12-17. See also Dan. 2:40-45; 7:7-27; 8:8, 9, 17-25; 9:26, 27; 11:40-85; 12:1-13; Rev. 12:3; 13:1-3; 17:8-11; 19:11-21).\n\nNow let's break this down so you can clearly see how the beast is a kingdom made up of ten kingdoms — and exactly how far Antichrist's reign will extend.\n\n![Lesson 48 — The Ten Horns and the Beast Itself](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OssMwVhVnIFYWHUNhmRXnATM2qSZzVGaodwQ5D)\n\n## I. The Ten Horns — the Seventh Kingdom or Revised Rome\n\n### 1. IS ROME TO BE REVIVED?\n\nIf so, what form will it take? Here's the key insight: Scripture never predicts a single Revived Roman Empire ruled by one man like the old Roman emperors. Instead, we'll see ten separate governments formed inside that territory, functioning as the seventh head on the beast. You might call it the "Revised" Roman Empire rather than "Revived."\n\nThink of it like this: instead of one company taking over, imagine a corporate merger where ten independent businesses form a loose federation — each keeps its own leadership, but they're all connected.\n\nHere's the evidence that Rome will exist as ten kingdoms in the last days — kingdoms that will still be around when both Christ and Antichrist appear:\n\n> (1) In Dan. 2:40-45, we get our first picture of Rome — symbolized by two legs of iron and ten toes made of iron and clay. Rome has never existed as separate kingdoms (symbolized by those ten toes), so for prophecy to be fulfilled, it must take that form eventually.\n>\n> Rome has existed as one kingdom (the body where the legs join) and as two divisions (the two iron legs, representing the eastern and western empire). But those ten toes are still future. Dan. 2:44-45 tells us exactly when: "in the day that the God of Heaven sets up a kingdom." That hasn't happened yet — it won't until Jesus returns to reign forever (Isa. 9:6, 7; Dan. 7:13-14; Rev. 11:15).\n>\n> So the Roman Empire will reappear in a new form of ten kingdoms at Christ's second coming, succeeding old Rome just like Rome succeeded the first five world powers. Those ten toes on two feet represent ten kingdoms from both the eastern and western divisions — five from each. The phrase "the kingdom" appears twice in Dan. 2:40-45, showing these ten will have some kind of loose federation.\n\n> (2) Daniel 7:7-27 confirms that ten kingdoms will emerge from Rome, all existing at the same time. But here's the additional detail: "another little horn" (called "the beast" in Dan. 7:11) will arise "after them" and overthrow three of the ten.\n>\n> This little horn continues "until the Ancient of days" comes — when judgment goes to the saints and they possess the kingdom. This points to Christ's return to destroy Antichrist and the ten kings and establish His reign. Both the ten kings and the eleventh (the beast) will exist when Christ returns.\n>\n> The ten will hand their kingdoms to the eleventh (the beast), and together they'll destroy Mystery Babylon (religion) in the middle of the Week. Then 3½ years later, they'll fight Christ at Armageddon (Rev. 17:12-17). This beast of Dan. 7:11 will be slain just like the one in Rev. 19:20.\n>\n> So Rome will be revised and exist as ten separate kingdoms. Some have thought these ten kings rule in succession like the seven heads, but Scripture never says that about them. Here's the proof that Daniel's ten toes and ten horns are the same as Revelation's ten horns and ten kings — all existing at Christ's second coming and destroyed at that time:\n\n> A. The number matches in both Daniel and Revelation — ten toes and ten horns (Dan. 2:40-45; 7:7-27; Rev. 12:3; 13:1; 17:12).\n\n> B. All ten will exist together and fight Christ when He returns to Earth (Dan. 2:34, 35, 44, 45; 7:8-14, 21-27; Rev. 17:14; 19:17-21).\n\n> C. All ten come after the "fourth kingdom" (Rome) and revise that kingdom (Dan. 2:4-45; 7:7, 8, 23, 24; Rev. 17:12-14).\n\n> D. All ten are connected with the same beast at the same time (Dan. 7:8, 11, 21-27; Rev. 17:8-17; 19:11-21).\n\n> E. The beast or "little horn" is an individual just like each of the ten horns, and he rises "after them" in both Daniel and Revelation — so these accounts must be identical (Dan. 7:8-24; Rev. 17:12-17).\n\n> F. All ten become subject to the same beast (Dan. 7:23, 24; Rev. 13:1-10; 17:12-17).\n\n> G. All ten exist when God sets up His kingdom, which immediately follows theirs (Dan. 2:4-45; 7:7-27; Rev. 17:12-17; 19:11-21).\n\nIf these ten were meant to rule in succession, Daniel would have seen them rise one at a time like the four beasts. Instead, he saw them all at once on the feet of the image and on the head of the terrible beast (Dan. 2:31-45; 7:7, 8). The "little horn" couldn't rise "among" the ten if only one existed at a time. And he couldn't overthrow three of them unless they all existed together.\n\nThe "little horn" of Dan. 7:7-11, 23-27 exists at the same time as the ten kingdoms and continues the same length of time as "the beast" of Rev. 13:1-8; 17:8-17; 19:11-21.\n\n> H. The "fourth kingdom" of Dan. 2 and 7 is the same as the sixth head of Rev. 17. The ten horns in both passages emerge from and succeed old Rome — so they must be the same.\n>\n> The seventh head of Rev. 17 and the ten horns are identical. Daniel's ten horns were to be the next kingdom after Rome, formed inside Roman territory. It's the only kingdom mentioned as still future (besides the "little horn" and his empire composed of the ten). The only future kingdom in Rev. 17 after John's day (besides the beast) was the seventh head — existing for "a short space" before giving its kingdom to the beast.\n>\n> These must be the same: the ten kings in both books exist at the same time, form the next kingdom after Rome, become subject to the beast, help form the eighth kingdom, and fight under him against Christ.\n\n> I. The ten kings in Daniel and Revelation reign both before and after the beast or "little horn." Their reign changes with his rise. Before he appears, they control their own kingdoms. After he comes, they submit to his supreme will. They control the seventh kingdom; he controls the eighth.\n>\n> So we conclude: the ten horns in both books are the same. Rome will be revised and exist as ten kingdoms before Antichrist rises. Then Antichrist will emerge from these ten kingdoms and over 3½ years subdue all ten kings. He'll form the eighth kingdom from all ten, possibly adding other parts of the old Grecian Empire that weren't under Rome.\n>\n> Antichrist will come from Syria and overthrow the three other Grecian divisions — making up four of the ten kingdoms of Revised Rome. This revives Greece and brings both Greek and Roman territory under him as the eighth kingdom. Revised Rome will stay as ten kingdoms throughout its short existence, while Revived Greece will include those same ten plus others it conquers during its brief time.\n\n### 2. WHEN IS ROME TO BE REVISED?\n\nThe ten kingdoms will form in the near future. We don't know exactly when. But Rome must be revised first and exist as ten kingdoms before Antichrist can arise — he's supposed to come up "after them" and "among them" (Dan. 7:8, 24).\n\n### 3. HOW LONG IS REVISED ROME TO EXIST?\n\nRevised Rome (the seventh head) will exist only a "short space." We can't know exactly how long before Daniel's Seventieth Week arrives. It seems that soon after Rome is revised, Antichrist will arise and start conquering some of the ten kingdoms.\n\nThis war continues during the first part of the Week until Antichrist gains full power over the ten, forming his kingdom — the Revived Grecian Empire. The "short space" of Rev. 17:10 matches the "short time" of Rev. 12:12 — about 3½ years (Rev. 12:6, 14).\n\nThese ten kings continue this short period before Antichrist rises from one of them to gain power over all ten. He'll overthrow three of them with help from the kingdom he emerges from (Dan. 7:8, 20). Then the other six will surrender without further war (Rev. 17:12-17).\n\nSo if the ten kings last about 3½ years before Antichrist rises, and he's here for only seven years (Dan. 9:27), there will be only about 10½ years from when the ten kingdoms form until Christ's return.\n\nWe don't know how long before the ten kingdoms start forming. But if war broke out in Europe, Asia, and Africa today, the ten kingdoms could be fully established in just a few short years. This age could end in ten to fifteen years if such a war started immediately.\n\nWhat we do know: we're in the closing years of this age because Israel is being rebuilt. The prophet said, "When the Lord shall build up Zion, he shall appear in his glory" (Ps. 102:16).\n\n### 4. HOW IS ROME TO BE REVISED?\n\nThe ten kingdoms will form through wars and agreements. We should expect them to form only from old Roman territory (Dan. 7:19-27).\n\nHere's a helpful overview of these empire territories:\n\n- **Egypt** (first head): smallest territory, ruling from Egypt to Syria\n- **Assyria** (second head): ruled from Egypt to Armenia, part of Asia Minor, all of Babylon, Media, and Persia\n- **Babylon** (third head): ruled Egypt and all Syrian countries west of the Tigris\n- **Medo-Persia** (fourth head): largest so far — from the Indus River east to parts of Thrace and Macedonia west, from the Caspian and Black Seas north to Egypt and part of North Africa\n- **Greece** (fifth head): conquered all Medo-Persian territory plus Greece, Macedonia, and Thrace — the largest of the first five\n- **Rome** (sixth head): controlled all Greek territory except lands east of the Caspian Sea and Persian Gulf, and added all countries west to the Atlantic — from northern Africa south to the Rhine and Danube rivers north (including Dacia and England)\n\nIt's from this Roman territory that we expect ten kingdoms to emerge as the seventh head on the beast. The eighth kingdom (Antichrist's) will succeed these ten and include not only all this territory but also the far eastern parts of Greek territory and whatever these ten kingdoms control outside the old Roman Empire.\n\n## II. The Beast Itself — the Eighth Kingdom\n\nAs we saw in the previous lesson, the seven heads and ten horns on the beast are entirely different from the beast itself. The beast is the eighth in a succession of world powers — from Israel's beginning as a nation in Egypt to Christ's second advent, when Israel will be delivered from the Gentiles and "the times of the Gentiles" will end.\n\nThe beast (as the eighth kingdom) will be ruled by two figures: the personal, visible, mortal human being called Antichrist, and the personal, invisible, immortal angel — the prince of Grecia.\n\nThis prince of Grecia will be released from the pit during the existence of the ten kingdoms and will cause the human Antichrist to rise to power over the original four Grecian divisions. This revives the Grecian Empire that didn't exist in John's day, had existed before his day, and will exist as the eighth kingdom when Christ returns.\n\nThis Revived Grecian Empire will swallow the entire ten kingdoms of Revised Rome during the first half of the Week. By the end of the last half of the Week, it will consume countries north and east of the ten kingdoms. But before Antichrist can complete his world conquest, Christ defeats him at Jerusalem (Zech. 14).\n\nSo Antichrist's kingdom will be the greatest of all eight Gentile world powers — but like all before him, he'll fall short of total world conquest.\n\n### Will Russia, Antichrist, or Christ Rule the Whole World?\n\nCommunism will never rule the world as a whole — and neither will any other "ism." No earthly man will become a worldwide dictator before Christ comes to reign.\n\nAntichrist will come closer than anyone, but before he even conquers all of Asia, Europe, and Africa, he'll "come to an end and none shall help him" (Dan. 11:45; Zech. 14).\n\nJesus Christ will be the world's first literal worldwide ruler. He will bring universal peace and prosperity — not Antichrist. But before that universal peace arrives, certain wars must occur to fulfill prophecy.\n\n### There Must Be at Least Three More European Wars Before the Second Advent\n\n> 1. **The first war** will form the ten kingdoms. This war is necessary because at least twenty-two or twenty-three states currently exist inside old Roman territory — they must be reduced to ten to fulfill Dan. 7:24.\n\n> 2. **The second war** occurs after the ten are formed. Then — and only then — Antichrist arises from the ten. In his rise to power, he'll overthrow three of them (Dan. 7:8, 24).\n\n> 3. **The third war** happens during the last half of the Week, between the ten kingdoms under Antichrist and countries "of the east and of the north" of those kingdoms, fulfilling Dan. 11:44. (See Supplement Two, Question 1, and Lesson Thirty-nine for more details.)\n\n### No World Peace and Prosperity Under Antichrist\n\nThe old idea of Antichrist as someone who miraculously brings world peace is unscriptural. He's a man of war from the moment he appears until he's destroyed at Armageddon (Dan. 7:7-8, 23-24; 8:20-25; 11:40-45; Rev. 6:1-2).\n\nThe only peace he'll bring is a seven-year covenant with the Jews. Then he'll break it halfway through and try to destroy them. But he wages war among the Gentiles the entire time until his death at Armageddon (Dan. 7:11; 8:25; 9:27; Rev. 19:11-21; 2 Thess. 2:8; Ezek. 38; 39; Zech. 14; Joel 3).\n\n## III. The Extent of Antichrist's Reign (Rev. 13:5-18)\n\nPeople often ask: "Will Antichrist have power over all kindreds, tongues, and nations? Will everyone on Earth worship him?"\n\nGenerally, yes — but it depends on what we mean by "all." If "all" means every single individual on the planet today, then no. But if "all" refers to what God has in mind — the ten kingdoms of old Rome in the last days — then yes, "all" includes everyone affected by Antichrist's decree within his empire.\n\nHere's the Scriptural proof that Antichrist will not rule America or become a worldwide dictator (as many prophecy students teach):\n\n### 1. The word "all" in Rev. 13 is a figure of speech\n\nIt's called "synecdoche" — where a part stands for the whole, or the whole for a part. Scripture uses this constantly:\n\n> (1) "I, even I, do bring a flood of waters upon the earth, to destroy all flesh, wherein is the breath of life, from under heaven; and every thing that is in the earth shall die" (Gen. 6:17). If we took this as literally as some take Rev. 13, Noah's family and all the ark animals would have died — but they didn't.\n\n> (2) "And they utterly destroyed all that was in the city, both men and women" — referring to Jericho (Josh. 6:21-25). But Rahab and her family were spared.\n\n> (3) "David and all the house of Israel played before the Lord" and "brought up the ark" (2 Sam. 6:5, 15). But not every Israelite played instruments — many didn't know how, many were too young, many weren't even there.\n\n> (4) "Six months did Joab remain there [out of his own country] with all Israel, until he had cut off every male in Edom" (1 Ki. 11:16, 17). "All Israel" here means part of the army.\n\n> (5) "So when all Israel saw that the king hearkened not unto them . . . see to thine own house, David. So Israel departed unto their tents. But as for the children of Israel which dwelt in the cities of Judah, Rehoboam reigned over them" (1 Ki. 12:16-19). Here "all Israel" means only those who rebelled. (See similar examples in 1 Chron. 10:6; 2 Chron. 10:1, 3, 16; 11:16, 17; 12:1; 13:15; 16:6; Ezra 10:5; Ezek. 21:4.)\n\n> (6) Nebuchadnezzar was made ruler over "all men" — but ancient Babylon ruled only part of the Earth (Dan. 2:37, 38; 4:1, 11, 12, 20). He never reigned over Greece, Rome, and many other lands. Dan. 2:39 says Greece ruled "over all the earth" — but Greece never ruled Italy, Spain, and many other countries. Dan. 7:23 says Rome ruled the "whole earth" — but we know that didn't include many tribes and nations.\n\n> (7) Mt. 3:5, 6 says "all Judea" and "all the region round about Jordan" came to John for baptism — but the Pharisees, Sadducees, and many others never were baptized. Many women, children, and sick people never even saw John.\n\n> (8) Lk. 2:1-3 says Caesar Augustus decreed that "all the world should be taxed." Any Roman law didn't affect countries outside the Empire — so "all" here applies only to those under Augustus.\n\n> (9) Paul said Roman believers' faith was "spoken of throughout the whole world" (Rom. 1:8). He meant many in the Empire knew about them — not that everyone on Earth had heard of Christianity. The same applies to Col. 1:23 and Rom. 10:18.\n\n> (10) Acts 11:28 mentions a drought "throughout all the world" in Claudius Caesar's time. That drought didn't cover every continent and island.\n\nThink of it like when someone says, "The whole town came to the game last night." We understand they mean a lot of people showed up — not literally every single resident.\n\nHundreds of examples show "all" used figuratively. So we don't have to believe Rev. 13 means Antichrist will literally reign over all the Earth and kill everyone who refuses his mark.\n\nThe writers above weren't false teachers — they used language the way all people naturally do. We should understand them the same way we understand someone today saying "everyone was there" about a big crowd.\n\nIf U.S. lawmakers made a law requiring "all kindreds, tongues, and nations" to register on a certain day, we'd understand it applies only to those under U.S. jurisdiction — not the same ethnic groups living under other governments worldwide. Antichrist's laws work the same way.\n\nWe must understand how "all" is used in each specific Scripture. If it means all without exception, there will be no limits in the passage or elsewhere. If the passage (or related passages) makes clear it means a part of something, we need to recognize that "all" doesn't include everyone on Earth.\n\nWhen Paul said God wills that "all men come to the knowledge of the truth" (1 Tim. 2:4), we know he means all without exception. But when we read that "all" were baptized by John — while the same passage shows many weren't — we take it as a figurative expression meaning "a great many."\n\nBoth Testaments use universal terms for certain kingdoms and kings' power. Yet these terms show only part of the Earth was ruled by those empires. Logically, Antichrist's kingdom could likewise be limited to part of the world.\n\nIf multiple Scriptures limit his power to certain territory — telling us exactly what's under him and what isn't — then we must limit the "all" of Rev. 13 to his actual domain.\n\n### 2. Revelation 13 itself limits Antichrist's kingdom\n\nHis realm consists of ten kingdoms that will form inside old Roman territory:\n\n"The ten horns which thou sawest are ten kings [formed inside old Rome just before Christ's return, Dan. 7:23, 24], which have received no kingdom as yet; but receive power as kings one hour [Greek: hora, meaning 'a period of time' as in Jn. 16:2, 4, 25; 1 Jn. 2:18; Rev. 14:15; Rom. 13:11] with the beast. These [ten only] . . . shall give their power and strength unto the beast. These shall make war with the Lamb [at Christ's return, Rev. 19:11-21], and the Lamb shall overcome them . . . And the ten horns which thou sawest upon the beast, these shall hate the whore [of Rev. 17:1-7, sitting on the peoples that make up the beast — the eighth kingdom], and shall make her desolate and naked, and shall eat her flesh, and burn her with fire. For God hath put in their hearts to fulfill his will, and to agree, and to give their kingdom [the ten kingdoms] unto the beast, until the words of God shall be fulfilled" (Rev. 17:8-18).\n\nIf the beast has only "ten horns" representing ten kings over ten kingdoms, that's the extent of Antichrist's reign. The "all kindreds, tongues, and nations" he rules refers to those within the ten kingdoms — not the same ethnic groups under other governments elsewhere.\n\n"All that worship him" means many in the ten kingdoms. "All that receive his mark" (Rev. 13:16-18) means many in those same ten kingdoms. He'll make a law requiring everyone in his empire to worship him and take his mark or die — but that doesn't mean this law is literally enforced everywhere, as we'll see.\n\n### 3. Daniel 7:7, 8, 17-27 limits Antichrist's kingdom to the ten kingdoms\n\nIn Dan. 7:7-8, this is symbolized by a beast with ten horns plus another little horn emerging from the ten and uprooting three. All eleven horns come from the same beast's head.\n\nDaniel explains: "The ten horns out of this kingdom [the fourth — old Rome] are ten kings that shall arise: and another [the eleventh, the little horn] shall rise after them; and he shall be diverse from the first, and he shall subdue three kings. And he shall speak great words against the most High (Rev. 13:5, 6), and shall wear out the saints of the most High (Dan. 7:21, 22; Rev. 13:7), and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time [3½ years, 1,260 days, Dan. 12:7; Rev. 11:2; 12:6, 14; 13:5]. But the judgment [of Dan. 7:9-14; Mt. 25:31-46] shall sit, and they shall take away his dominion, to consume and to destroy it unto the end [2 Thess. 1:7-10; 2:7-12; Rev. 19:11-21; Zech. 14]. And the kingdom under the whole heaven, shall be given to the saints of the most High, whose kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and all dominions shall serve and obey him" (Dan. 7:21-27; 2:44, 45; 8:25; 11:45; Zech. 14; Ezek. 38; 39; Joel 2, 3; Lk. 1:32-35; Mt. 25:31-46; 2 Thess. 1:7-10; 2:7-12; Jude 14; Rev. 19:11–22:5).\n\nOnly "ten kings" give their power to the beast and continue as kings "with the beast" for forty-two months. Daniel 7 shows exactly where these ten kingdoms will be located — "out of this kingdom" (old Rome).\n\nSo when Antichrist makes his law requiring all to worship him and take his mark, his authority extends over ten kingdoms within old Roman territory.\n\nAmerica and all countries outside old Rome won't be affected by this law because they're not within the ten kingdoms. If God said the ten kingdoms are "out of this kingdom" (the old Roman Empire), that settles it for those who believe God knows what He's talking about.\n\nIf God said only ten horns would be on the beast and told us exactly where the ten kingdoms will be, it's unwise to paste fifty-five extra horns on the beast and extend the Roman Empire over the whole world. Why change Scripture? Prophecy will be fulfilled exactly as God said. No Scripture ever changes the ten horns to sixty-five.\n\n### 4. Daniel 11:40-45 plainly states limits to Antichrist's power\n\nAntichrist will break his seven-year covenant with the Jews (Dan. 9:27), enter Palestine in the middle of the seven years, and gain power over the ten kingdoms. He'll decree that all must worship him.\n\nBut notice: "many countries [not all] shall be overthrown: but these shall escape out of his hand, even Edom, and Moab, and the chief of the children of Ammon."\n\nIf these border countries right next to Palestine (where Antichrist has his capital during the last 3½ years — Dan. 11:45; Rev. 11:1, 2) escape him, it's certainly reasonable that countries across vast oceans — never part of old Rome — will also escape him.\n\n### 5. Israel in Judea will flee from Antichrist\n\nWhen he breaks his covenant with them halfway through Daniel's Seventieth Week (Dan. 9:27), they'll flee into Edom and Moab — a "place prepared of God" where they're protected from Antichrist during the very time when supposedly "all men" are under him. (See Lesson Forty-five.)\n\n### 6. Daniel 11:44, 45 tells of other nations not under Antichrist\n\nAfter Antichrist conquers many countries and seizes Palestine, "tidings out of the east and out of the north shall trouble him: therefore he shall go forth with fury to destroy, and utterly to make away many."\n\nCountries north and east of the ten kingdoms will wage war against Antichrist. They won't be under him. They won't take his mark. (See Lesson Thirty-nine.)\n\n### 7. Zechariah shows many people won't take the mark — and won't be killed\n\nHe describes a battle between Jews at Jerusalem and many nations under Antichrist the very day Christ returns with heaven's armies to deliver Israel and establish His kingdom (Zech. 14:1-5, 14).\n\nThen Zechariah says: "And it shall come to pass, that every one that is left of all the nations which came against Jerusalem shall even go up from year to year to worship the King, the Lord of hosts, and to keep the feast of tabernacles. And it shall be, that whoso will not come up of all the families of the earth unto Jerusalem to worship the King, the Lord of hosts, even upon them shall be no rain. And if the family of Egypt go not up, and come not, that they have no rain . . . This shall be the punishment of Egypt, and the punishment of all nations that come not up to keep the feast of tabernacles. In that day shall there be upon the bells of the horses, holiness unto the Lord . . . Yea, every pot in Jerusalem and in Judah shall be holiness unto the Lord of hosts" (Zech. 14:6-21).\n\nThis proves that even within Antichrist's ten kingdoms, not everyone takes the mark or gets killed.\n\nDan. 11:40-45 says "the land of Egypt shall not escape" Antichrist. So if Egypt is under him, yet some Egyptians survive to enter the Millennium (as Zech. 14:16-21 proves), then they haven't taken the mark.\n\nRev. 14:9-12 declares that everyone who takes the mark will be eternally damned when Christ comes. The fact that survivors remain and will worship at Jerusalem during the Millennium proves they didn't take the mark — and they escaped death at Antichrist's hands.\n\n### 8. The reality: Antichrist's law will be unenforceable\n\nYes, Antichrist will decree that everyone in his ten kingdoms must take a mark and worship him or die. But there's a war with countries north and east that keeps him so occupied he can't possibly enforce such a law.\n\nIt would be nearly impossible to strictly enforce this across such vast territory in only 3½ years. There will be ways to avoid this law — just as with any law humans have made. Corrupt local officials, family connections, money — all will create loopholes. Plus, people in mountains, deserts, and rural areas will be simply unreachable.\n\nAnd in all lands outside his ten kingdoms? They won't be affected at all. Even if Antichrist ruled the whole world (which he doesn't), enforcing such a law everywhere in forty-two months would be impossible.\n\nWhole tribes in Tibet, China, Africa, Australia, South America, and Mexico will never even hear about Antichrist during his entire reign — let alone be conquered and forced to change their religion.\n\nThink of it this way: countless people today still haven't heard of Jesus Christ, World War I or II, or other major world events. The same will be true during Antichrist's time. He'll reign only over old Roman territory — northern Africa, southern Europe, and western Asia — organized as ten kingdoms.\n\nScripture teaches that even in the Millennium, multitudes will not have heard of God through Jesus Christ until Jewish missionaries go out from Jerusalem to tell them Christ reigns there (Isa. 2:2-4; 40:9; 52:7; 61:6; 66:18-21; Zech. 8:23; 14:16-21).\n\nIf many people haven't heard of Jesus Christ in over 1,900 years of the Age of Grace, many certainly won't hear of Antichrist in only 3½ years.\n\n### 9. "Sheep nations" prove not everyone cooperates with Antichrist\n\nIf all nations cooperated in destroying Israel during the Tribulation, there wouldn't be any "sheep" nations to enter the Millennium, as Christ teaches in Mt. 25:31-46:\n\n"When the Son of man shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory: and before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another, as a shepherd divideth his sheep from the goats: and he shall set the sheep on his right hand, but the goats on his left. Then shall the King say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world . . . Then shall he say also unto them on his left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels"\n\n---\n\nThe ten-nation confederacy that empowers the Antichrist doesn't emerge from nothing — it emerges from political, economic, and military conditions that Scripture describes and history has been building toward. You are watching the world being arranged for these events. So here's the question: How do you hold current events — geopolitical shifts, economic instabilities, new alliances — with both prophetic awareness and personal peace? The same God who predicted these events in detail is the God who holds you in His hand through them.	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612w3001ngeo03hm72y4a	cmq6612vy001hgeo0djva1vnw	Supplement 9 — For Lessons 15 & 16	SUPPLEMENT	600	5	\N	t	![Supplement 9 — For Lessons 15 & 16](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsEzyCFtdLWqJHyu8Q5MfmIRAjonSBKDvC0V2N)\n\n## Supplement 9 — For Lessons 15 & 16: Guardian Angels and Devotion\n\n### Begin Here\n\nFind one minute of quiet.\n\nThink about a moment in the last week — any ordinary moment: a meal, a commute, a conversation, falling asleep. The moment itself doesn't matter.\n\nNow hold the following truth alongside it: in that moment, a being of pure intelligence that has been with you since conception was present. It was simultaneously beholding the face of God. It was carrying forward any prayer you offered. It was, in whatever measure God permitted, inclining you toward what is good.\n\nYou were not alone in that moment. You are never alone in any moment.\n\nThat truth is what this supplement exists to help you absorb.\n\n---\n\n### Key Terms\n\n**Guardian Angel** — A member of the ninth choir, assigned personally to each human being from conception to natural death. Not general angelic care — *personal*, one-to-one, permanent assignment.\n\n**Veneration** (*dulia*) — The honor proper to holy creatures (saints and angels). Distinct from *latria* (worship), which belongs to God alone. The difference matters: we worship God; we honor the angels.\n\n**Simultaneous Presence** — The guardian angel is with you *and* beholding God at the same time. It does not leave the divine presence to attend to you. It holds both in its angelic nature — which operates outside the limitations of space that constrain human attention.\n\n**Intercession by Angels** — The active presentation of human prayers before God by an angel, as Raphael did for Tobit ([Tobit 12:12](data-scripture="Tobit 12:12")) and as all angels do for the saints ([Revelation 8:3-4](data-scripture="Revelation 8:3")).\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> [Matthew 18:10](data-scripture="Matthew 18:10") "See that you do not despise one of these little ones. For I tell you that in heaven their angels always behold the face of my Father who is in heaven."\n\n> [Psalm 91:11](data-scripture="Psalm 91:11") "For he will command his angels concerning you to guard you in all your ways."\n\n> [Revelation 8:3-4](data-scripture="Revelation 8:3") "Another angel came and stood at the altar with a golden censer, and he was given much incense to offer with the prayers of all the saints on the golden altar before the throne."\n\n---\n\n### What Your Guardian Angel Can and Cannot Do\n\n| It Can | It Cannot |\n|--------|----------|\n| Inspire good thoughts in the imagination | Compel your will |\n| Protect from physical harm (within God's plan) | Override the consequences of freely chosen sin |\n| Present your prayers before God | Guarantee outcomes God has not permitted |\n| Enlighten through interior promptings | Create certainty in your intellect |\n| Accompany you through every moment of life | Substitute for your own spiritual effort |\n\n---\n\n### Five Questions — For Depth, Not Comfort\n\n1. Jesus says the angels of the little ones *always* behold the face of the Father ([Matthew 18:10](data-scripture="Matthew 18:10")). Your guardian angel holds your life and the divine presence simultaneously. What does it mean to be someone that an intelligence beholding God is attending to?\n\n2. Your guardian angel cannot compel your will. It can inspire, prompt, incline — but the choice is always yours. Looking back honestly: can you identify moments when you felt an interior prompting toward good that you ignored? What was the cost?\n\n3. Raphael was carrying Tobit's prayers before God throughout the years of his righteous living — *before* Tobit knew. Your prayers are being carried too, regardless of whether you feel them "going anywhere." How does this change your relationship to prayers that seem to go unanswered?\n\n4. Gabriel was created for one conversation in Nazareth. His billions of years of existence were a preparation for one moment. Your guardian angel was created, in part, for you. What would it mean to take seriously the idea that your life — this particular, unremarkable life — is something an archangel-level of care and attention has been directed toward?\n\n5. Write a one-paragraph prayer to your guardian angel right now. Not a formula. Your own words. Acknowledge the reality, express gratitude for what it has already done, and ask for what you most need from it today.	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612vu001bgeo0jfsolgd6	cmq6612vm0013geo0kqjj27k2	Lesson 13 — Gabriel: Messenger of the Incarnation	READING	900	3	\N	t	![Lesson 13 — Gabriel: Messenger of the Incarnation](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os42jzapL3Ls52XczwCYNqdZVf8hMUGlEvQ0nD)\n\n## Gabriel — Messenger of the Incarnation\n\n### One Moment\n\nGabriel was created before time. Before the first star. Before any human drew breath. He has existed — in fullness, in perfection, with complete intelligence and will — since the very beginning of creation.\n\nBillions of years, if we want to think in those terms.\n\nAnd according to the tradition developed from Thomas Aquinas, the entire existence of Gabriel was ordered toward **one moment**: an afternoon in Nazareth, a small town of no historical significance, in the house of a young woman named Mary, in the sixth month of her cousin's pregnancy.\n\nGabriel was not assigned to this moment as we might be assigned to a task at work. This moment was not added to Gabriel's portfolio after some general creation. The Annunciation was the reason Gabriel existed. Gabriel *is* the angel of the Annunciation in the deepest possible sense. Remove that moment, and you remove the reason Gabriel was made.\n\nThis should change how we hear the story.\n\n### The Name\n\nThe Hebrew name *Gabriel* means **"God is my strength"** or **"strong man of God."** His name is his character: the strength of God entering human history through the delivery of a word.\n\n### Gabriel in the Old Testament\n\nGabriel appears twice in the Book of Daniel, each time to explain a prophetic vision that Daniel could not understand on his own.\n\nIn [Daniel 8](data-scripture="Daniel 8:16"), a voice commands: *"Gabriel, make this man understand the vision."* Gabriel interprets the vision of the ram and the goat — a political prophecy about the Greek and Persian empires.\n\nIn [Daniel 9:21-27](data-scripture="Daniel 9:21"), while Daniel is deep in prayer, Gabriel appears *"in swift flight at the time of the evening sacrifice"* and delivers the prophecy of the Seventy Weeks — one of the most precisely calibrated prophetic texts in all of Scripture, pointing to the exact timing of the Messiah's coming.\n\nNotice what Gabriel is doing in the Old Testament: preparing Israel to recognize the Messiah when He arrives. The visions he explains are the intellectual and prophetic ground that makes the Annunciation meaningful. Gabriel spent centuries preparing the audience for his own defining mission.\n\n### The Annunciation\n\n> [Luke 1:26-29](data-scripture="Luke 1:26") "In the sixth month the angel Gabriel was sent from God to a city of Galilee named Nazareth, to a virgin betrothed to a man whose name was Joseph, of the house of David. And the virgin's name was Mary. And he came to her and said, 'Greetings, O favored one, the Lord is with you!' But she was greatly troubled at the saying, and tried to discern what sort of greeting this might be."\n\nGabriel greets Mary not by her name but by a title: **"O favored one"** — *kecharitomene*, in Greek, one who has been perfectly graced. He does not say "Hello, Mary." He addresses her as she is in God's eyes, as she has been known in heaven before she was born.\n\nMary is troubled — not frightened by the sight of Gabriel (that reaction will come later, when he tells her what is coming), but *troubled at the saying*. She is trying to understand what kind of greeting this is, what it means. She is thinking.\n\nGabriel tells her she will conceive the Son of God by the Holy Spirit. Her Son will be called the Most High and will reign forever. Mary's response is the hinge of all human history:\n\n> [Luke 1:38](data-scripture="Luke 1:38") "Behold, I am the servant of the Lord; let it be to me according to your word."\n\nAnd Gabriel departs.\n\nThe entirety of the Incarnation — God becoming man, the salvation of the human race, the whole of what we call Christianity — pivots on those words. And the being created to carry them, to deliver them to the one person who could accept them, had been prepared and waiting since before the universe existed.\n\n### Gabriel at the Temple: The Earlier Annunciation\n\nSix months before the visit to Mary, Gabriel appears to Zechariah the priest in the Temple:\n\n> [Luke 1:19](data-scripture="Luke 1:19") "And the angel answered him, 'I am Gabriel. I stand in the presence of God, and I was sent to speak to you and to bring you this good news.'"\n\n*I stand in the presence of God.* This is Gabriel's self-identification. Not "I am a messenger" or "I am an angel." He identifies himself by where he stands — in the presence of God — and by what he does from that position: carries good news. His whole identity is this: he is the one who stands before God and carries His words to the world.\n\n### Gabriel as Patron\n\nGabriel is the patron of:\n- Messengers, ambassadors, and diplomats\n- Preachers, catechists, and teachers of the faith\n- Broadcasters and journalists\n- Expectant mothers\n\nHis patronage flows entirely from his mission. Anyone who carries a message, anyone who announces what someone else needs to hear, participates — however distantly — in what Gabriel was made to do.\n\n### The Angelus: Daily Contact with Gabriel's Mission\n\nThe *Angelus* — the traditional prayer recited three times daily at morning, noon, and evening — places Gabriel's moment at the center of every day:\n\n*"The Angel of the Lord declared unto Mary, and she conceived of the Holy Spirit..."*\n\nEvery recitation of the Angelus is a participation in the moment for which Gabriel was created. It is a daily act of gratitude for the message that changed the world — and a daily renewal of the *fiat* that received it.\n\n---\n\n*Next: From Gabriel the messenger, we turn to Raphael the healer — the archangel who traveled anonymously with a young man for weeks, carrying his prayers before God, before finally revealing who he was. His story is the closest thing in Scripture to a portrait of your own guardian angel.*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk4br0029ewhjchf552yu	cmnknk4bp001qewhjk5bcqnfj	Lesson 49 — The Marriage Supper, Second Advent, and Armageddon	READING	1959	18	\N	t	History ends at Armageddon — not in the bleak nihilistic sense, but in the most dramatic reversal imaginable. The armies of the world are assembled against Jerusalem. The Antichrist has consolidated global power. The Tribulation saints are dying. And then the sky splits open. Jesus returns — not as a vulnerable infant in a manger, not as a servant with a towel, but as the King of Kings, with an army of heaven behind Him, to end the war the world started.\n\nLast time we examined the ten-horn confederacy and its role in empowering the Antichrist. Now we reach the climax of the Tribulation: the Marriage Supper of the Lamb in heaven, the Second Advent of Christ to earth, and the Battle of Armageddon.\n\nThis passage in Rev. 19:1-10 is what we call parenthetical — meaning it's inserted here in the sequence of Revelation, but it actually describes events happening in Heaven just *before* Christ returns to Earth. Let me explain why this matters.\n\nWhile the text appears after the vial judgments, the Marriage Supper will actually take place in Heaven when all the Tribulation saints and the two witnesses are raptured at the end of Daniel's Seventieth Week. Christ's return happens at the seventh vial or shortly after, but the Marriage Supper occurs before He comes back. So Rev. 19:1-10 explains what's happening in Heaven right before Christ descends to Earth with His saints.\n\nWhat's clear in this passage is that the multitudes in Heaven are praising God because He has already judged the "great whore," and the smoke from Literal Babylon's destruction is rising up at that very moment.\n\n![Lesson 49 — The Marriage Supper, Second Advent, and Armageddon](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsaXczZLEhtesUMivpomO8x4WSPknRFTuAI75Q)\n\n### The Identity of the "Great Whore"\n\nNow, this "great whore" cannot be the same as the woman in Rev. 17. Here's why: that woman will have been destroyed 3½ years before this passage is fulfilled, so her smoke wouldn't still be ascending at this time.\n\nThis judgment comes directly from God Himself, who avenges the blood of His servants at her hand. The rejoicing we see here is actually in obedience to the command of Rev. 18:20, which calls "heaven, and ye saints, and ye apostles, and ye prophets" to rejoice over her judgment.\n\nHer smoke ascends to God "for ever and ever" — a phrase used fourteen times in Revelation. This matches the eternal desolations of Literal Babylon described in Isa. 13:19-22; Jer. 50:13, 23, 39, 40; 51:26, 37, 62. This may actually be the one place where the eternal lake of fire will be visible to those living on the New Earth after the Millennium (Isa. 66:22-24; Rev. 14:9-11).\n\n### Worship in Heaven\n\nNext in this passage, we see the elders and living creatures worshipping God. This is the last time they appear in Revelation.\n\nThen a voice from the throne calls out, "Praise our God, all ye his servants, and ye that fear him, both small and great." John then hears what sounds like a great multitude — like the roar of many waters and powerful thunder — saying, "Alleluia: for the Lord God omnipotent reigneth." After this, the angel shows John the Marriage Supper of the Lamb.\n\n### The Bride Made Ready\n\nThe statement in Rev. 19:7, "His wife hath made herself ready," shows us that certain preparations are necessary. Think of it like a bride spending months preparing for her wedding day — there's intentional effort involved. This seems clear from her white robe, which represents the righteousness of the saints (Rev. 19:8).\n\nWe can't fully describe the wedding supper itself because Scripture doesn't give us those details. What we do know is that it will be a real banquet — as real as any ever held on Earth.\n\nThe Greek word for "marriage" actually means "marriage feast," proving this supper will be just as literal and real as any we know here. Compare Rev. 19:1-10 with Mt. 22:2; 25:10.\n\nDon't let the scale of such a wedding supper trouble you — "with God all things are possible." If we can imagine thousands eating at a banquet here on Earth, we can understand on the same basis how innumerable companies will do so in Heaven. That food will be eaten in Heaven is clear from Lk. 22:16, 18, 30; Rev. 2:7, 17; 22:1-2; Ps. 78:25; Exod. 24:11.\n\n### John's Mistake\n\nWhen John witnessed these things, he fell down to worship the angel as he would worship God. But he was immediately stopped and told that the angel was also a redeemed person — a fellow-servant among the brethren the prophets, and those who have the testimony of Jesus, which is the spirit of prophecy.\n\n## II. The Second Coming of Christ (Rev. 19:11-21)\n\n> "And I saw heaven opened, and behold a white horse; and he that sat upon him was called Faithful and True, and in righteousness he doth judge and make war. His eyes were as a flame of fire, and on his head were many crowns; and he had a name written, that no man knew, but he himself. And he was clothed with a vesture dipped in blood: and his name is called The Word of God. And the armies which were in heaven followed him upon white horses, clothed in fine linen white and clean. And out of his mouth goeth a sharp sword, that with it he should smite the nations: and he shall rule them with a rod of iron: and he treadeth the winepress of the fierceness and wrath of Almighty God. And he hath on his vesture and on his thigh a name written, KING OF KINGS AND LORD OF LORDS" (Rev. 19:11-16).\n\nThe second coming of Christ is the central theme of Revelation. Let's walk through the key facts from Rev. 19:11-21:\n\n> 1. He is coming from Heaven (Rev. 19:11, 14. Compare with Mt. 24:29-31; 2 Thess. 1:7 and Dan. 7:13, 14).\n\n> 2. He is coming on a white horse (Rev. 19:11).\n\n> 3. His appearance will be similar to the first vision in Revelation (Rev. 1:12-18). Five of the eight characteristics of Christ dealt with in Chapter Three of my book *Revelation Expounded* are listed here again (Rev. 19:12, 13).\n\n> 4. His titles and names are "Faithful," "True," "The Word of God," and "KING OF KINGS AND LORD OF LORDS," plus a name that no one knows except Himself (Rev. 19:11-16).\n\n> 5. He is coming with authority to make war upon the nations and judge them (Isa. 11:4; 49:2), to tread them in the fierceness of the winepress of God's wrath (Isa. 63:3; Rev. 14:17-20; 19:15), and to rule (shepherd) them with a rod of iron (Ps. 2:9. Compare with Rev. 2:27; 12:5; Ps. 149:7-9).\n\n> 6. He will command the armies of Heaven, who follow Him on white horses, clothed in linen, white and clean — the righteousness of the saints (Rev. 9:8, 14).\n\n### A Glorious Picture\n\nThese six points summarize Christ's glorious return with His saints and angels to defeat the dragon, the beast, and the false prophet with their armies, deliver Israel, and establish righteousness on Earth.\n\nPicture this: there will never be a more glorious event or more beautiful sight than the armies of Heaven, clothed in spotless white, in perfect order and rank, following Christ on white horses, accompanied by heavenly angels — all ready to take vengeance on God's enemies. (For spirit horses in Heaven, see Lesson Six.)\n\n### 1. The Fact of the Second Coming of Christ\n\n> (1) Old Testament prophets who testified to the second coming include: "Enoch" (Gen. 5:21-24; Jude 14, 15); "Jacob" (Gen. 49:10); "Balaam" (Num. 24:7, 17-19); "Isaiah" (59:20; 63:1-5); "Jeremiah" (23:5, 6; 25:30-33); "Ezekiel" (34:23-29; 37:17-29; 43:7); "Daniel" (2:44, 45; 7:13, 14); "Hosea" (2:18-23; 3:4, 5); "Joel" (2:28-3:21); "Amos" (5:15-21); "Micah" (1:3, 4; 2:12, 13; 4:1–5:7); "Nahum" (1:5, 6); "Habakkuk" (2:13, 14); "Zephaniah" (1:14-18; 3:8, 9); "Haggai" (2:6, 7, 21-23; Heb. 12:25-29); "Zechariah" (2:10-13; 3:8; 6:12, 13; 8:3-23; 12:4-14; 13:1-9; 14:1-21); and "Malachi" (3:1–4:6).\n\n> (2) New Testament prophets who testified include: "Jesus" (Mt. 16:27; 24:1-25:46; Lk. 17:22-37; 21:1-33); "Peter" (Acts 3:21; 2 Pet. 1:16; 3:3-9); "Paul" (Rom. 11:26, 27; 2 Thess. 1:7-10; 2:1-8; Heb. 9:28); "John" (Rev. 1:7; 19:11-21); and "Jude" (Jude 14, 15).\n\n> (3) The Lord's Supper declares the second coming (Lk. 22:19; 1 Cor. 11:26).\n\n> (4) Angels declare it (Acts 1:10, 11. Compare Lk. 1:26-35; 2:8-18).\n\n> (5) The Old Testament contains as many, if not more, references to Christ's second coming as to His first. The 260 chapters of the New Testament refer to it about 300 times. Every time you pray the Lord's Prayer, you're praying for His coming. Nearly every book in both Testaments directly or indirectly predicts His return to Earth.\n\n### 2. Some False Theories of His Second Coming\n\nLet's address some incorrect views people have held:\n\n> (1) **That the Day of Pentecost was the second coming.** This doesn't hold up because the entire New Testament was written *after* Pentecost, and all the writers still spoke of a *future* coming of Christ. Jesus Himself said the Holy Spirit would be "another Comforter" — not a second coming of Himself (Jn. 14:16, 17, 26; 15:26, 27; 16:7-16).\n\n> (2) **That the second coming happens at a sinner's conversion.** This can't be right because at conversion there's no literal coming of the sinner to Jesus or of Jesus to the sinner. Conversion is a spiritual work in the heart where the sinner repents.\n\n> (3) **That death is the second coming.** This is absurd when you think about it — approximately three people die every two seconds; 90 every minute; 5,400 hourly; 129,600 daily; 907,200 weekly; and 47,304,000 annually.\n\n> (4) **That His coming occurred at Jerusalem's destruction in 70 A.D.** This view is false because when Jesus comes, He will *restore* Jerusalem, not destroy it (Zech. 14:1-21; Lk. 21:24).\n\n> (5) **That His coming is the preaching of the gospel.** This is certainly incorrect because gospel preaching has spanned many centuries, while His coming will happen suddenly (Mt. 24:27-51; 2 Thess. 1:7-10).\n\n> (6) **That prophecies of His coming should be spiritualized with no literal return.** This would practically destroy God's Word and render it meaningless — just as the Jews did when they spiritualized prophecies of Christ's first coming, which were literally fulfilled (Lk. 1:31). If that verse was literally fulfilled in His first coming, then Lk. 1:32, 33 must be literally fulfilled in His second coming. It's a serious distortion of Scripture to make literal words mean only a spiritual coming. You'll see this clearly when you read through the passages in Point 1 above.\n\n### 3. The Time of His Second Coming\n\nJust because some people have foolishly tried and failed to set exact dates for Christ's return doesn't change the fact that He *will* come. Jesus Himself warned us against such date-setting (Mt. 24:32-51; 25:13).\n\nWhile we can't know the exact day or hour, we *can* know that His coming is **pre-millennial**, not post-millennial. Christ is coming *before* the 1,000-year reign, not after it (Rev. 20:1-7).\n\n**Postmillennialism is dangerous** because it substitutes human effort for God's work. This theory claims that mankind ushers in the Millennium through their own efforts, securing happiness without God's grace. It teaches that the organized Church will prosper until the whole world is converted — but in reality, the Church isn't as close to this as it was in apostolic times.\n\nThis view also claims Christ couldn't or wouldn't return while the world is sinful, and that once converted, humanity will invite Christ back to reign. This simply isn't what Scripture teaches. The purpose of this dispensation isn't world conversion — not everyone will believe. It's about calling out a people to serve as kings and priests with Christ during the Millennium and forever (Rev. 1:5, 6; 5:9, 10; 20:4; 22:5). The passages in Point 1 don't picture a converted world at Christ's coming.\n\n### 4. Reasons for a Pre-Millennial Second Coming\n\n> (1) The Antichrist, whose coming everyone agrees is pre-millennial, is destroyed by the brightness of Christ's coming (Rev. 19:11-21; 2 Thess. 2:8). This fixes Christ's coming as pre-millennial.\n\n> (2) Christ comes "immediately after the Tribulation" (Mt. 24:27-31). The Tribulation occurs just before the Millennium (Mt. 24:15-31; Zech. 14).\n\n> (3) When Christ comes, He separates the tares from the wheat. Since the Millennium follows this separation, He must come before the Millennium (Mt. 13:40-43).\n\n> (4) Conditions like those in Lot's and Noah's days will exist when Christ comes (Mt. 24:37-51; Lk. 17:22-37; 2 Tim. 3; 4:1-3; 2 Pet. 3:2-5). These passages don't fit the post-millennial theory.\n\n> (5) The Millennial kingdom will be a literal kingdom, not simply Church exaltation or a converted world continuing (Rev. 5:1, 10; 11:15; 20:1-10; Dan. 2:44, 45; 7:13, 14; Zech. 14).\n\n> (6) The resurrections prove a pre-millennial coming — the righteous dead are raised before the Millennium to live and reign with Christ during it. The wicked dead aren't raised until after (Rev. 20:1-15).\n\n> (7) When Christ comes, Satan is bound. Since Satan is bound during the Millennium, there can be no Millennium until Christ comes (Rev. 20:1-7).\n\n> (8) Israel will be restored and regathered when Christ comes (Mt. 24:31), and since they're restored during the Millennium, Christ must come first (Ezek. 36:24-28; Isa. 11:1-16).\n\n> (9) See Lesson Fifty, Point III, 5, for additional reasons.\n\nSo the timing of His return to Earth is immediately after Daniel's Seventieth Week and at the beginning of the Millennium (Rev. 19:11-21; Zech. 14; Mt. 24:27-31). It occurs at the start of "the day of the Lord," as all passages using this expression make clear.\n\nThe day of the Lord never refers to the rapture — it doesn't begin until after that event. Paul doesn't correct the early Christians for expecting the rapture, but he *does* rebuke them for expecting "the day of the Lord" at any moment (1 Thess. 5:1-11; 2 Thess. 2:1-12).\n\n### 5. Signs of the Second Coming of Christ\n\nMany events and prophecies must still be fulfilled before Christ returns to Earth. We've listed many of these signs in Lesson Forty-four, Point II.\n\nFrom the signs now unfolding, we know we're only a few years from Christ's literal return. And if *that* event is near, how much nearer is the rapture, which occurs at least seven years before the second advent? We should expect the rapture at any time, but not the second advent until all its signs have come to pass.\n\n### 6. The Manner of His Second Coming\n\nFour Greek words explain how Christ will come. Let's look at each one with its key passages:\n\n> (1) **Parousia** means "personal coming," "immediate presence," "arrival," "advent," or "return." It's used in Mt. 24:3, 27, 37, 39; 2 Thess. 2:8; 2 Pet. 3:4 — translated "coming" in each case, referring to Christ's personal appearance on Earth.\n\n> (2) **Phaneros** means "to shine," "be apparent," "appear publicly," "be manifest," and "be seen." It's used in this connection only in Mt. 24:30.\n\n> (3) **Erchomai** means "to go" or "to come." It's used generally for the second coming in Mt. 24:30, 42, 43, 48; 25:13, 19, 27, 31; Jn. 21:23; Acts 1:11; 1 Thess. 5:2; Jude 14; Rev. 1:7; etc. It's translated "come," "cometh," and "coming."\n\n> (4) **Epiphaneia** means "advent," "appearing," "brightness," "to give light," or "become visible." It appears in 1 Tim. 6:14; 2 Tim. 4:1, 8; Titus 2:13; Heb. 9:28, translated "appear" and "appearing."\n\nThese passages reveal the following about how Christ will return:\n\n> (1) He's coming "as the lightning cometh out of the east, and shineth even unto the west" (Mt. 24:27). This refers to the direction He'll come to Mount Olivet in His descent — the same place He departed (Isa. 63:1-5; Zech. 14:1-5).\n\n> (2) He's coming as destruction to the ungodly, like the flood did (Mt. 24:38-51; 25:31-46; 1 Thess. 5:2; 2 Thess. 1:7-10; 2:8; Jude 14, 15; Zech. 14).\n\n> (3) He's coming visibly in the same way He left (Acts 1:11; Rev. 1:7).\n\n> (4) He's coming with mighty brightness and fire (2 Thess. 1:7-10; 2:8; Ezek. 38:17-21; Mal. 4:1-6).\n\n> (5) He's coming in vengeance to punish His enemies (Rev. 14:14-20; 19:11-21; Jude 14; 2 Thess. 1:7-10).\n\n> (6) He's coming with power and great glory (Mt. 24:27-31).\n\n> (7) He's coming with all His saints and angels (Rev. 19:11-21; Zech. 14:5; 2 Thess. 1:7-10; Jude 14, 15; Mt. 24:31).\n\n> (8) He's coming with clouds (Rev. 1:7; Dan. 7:13, 14; Mt. 24:27-30; Rev. 19:11-21).\n\n> (9) He's coming as Judge and King (Rev. 19:11-21; Isa. 11; Zech. 14; Mt. 25:31-46).\n\n> (10) He's coming "as a thief in the night" (1 Thess. 5:2-4; 2 Pet. 3:10; Rev. 16:15).\n\nThese are the only passages where this phrase is used of the second advent and the day of the Lord. It's never used once for the rapture. The only other occurrence is a warning of judgment to the church at Sardis. Think of it like a homeowner who doesn't know when a thief might come — that's how sudden and unexpected Christ's return will be, as Mt. 24:36, 39, 42-51; 25:13 clearly shows.\n\n## III. The Battle of Armageddon or the Supper of the Great God\n\nThe last part of Rev. 19 describes the Battle of Armageddon, also called "the supper of the great God." It's a mistake to think Armageddon is just another war between nations like traditional warfare.\n\nWhen the last two world wars broke out, some newspapers printed headlines like "Armageddon!" or "Is it Armageddon?" Such speculation shows a failure to understand our times and what prophecy actually says. To answer any question about Armageddon, we must consult the Bible — it's exclusively a Bible theme. Armageddon follows the fulfillment of everything in Revelation up to chapter 19.\n\n### 1. The Place Where Armageddon Will Be Fought\n\nThe word "Armageddon" appears only once in Scripture. It's a place name where the greatest battle of all time will be fought. The battle itself, under different terms, is mentioned many times.\n\nThis battleground is where the three unclean spirits gather the nations for battle (Rev. 16:13-16). Armageddon is also called "the valley of Jehoshaphat" in other passages, identifying it as the area extending from Mount Carmel southeast to Jerusalem (Joel 3).\n\n"Armageddon" comes from two Hebrew words: *har*, meaning "a mountain or range of hills, hill country," and *Megiddo*, meaning "rendezvous." Combined (Har-Megiddo), they refer to the Hill of Megiddo on the south side of the valley of Megiddo or Esdraelon, southeast of Mount Carmel (2 Chron. 35:22; Zech. 12:11).\n\n"Megiddo" was the capital of a portion of Canaan that fell to Joshua (Josh. 12:21; 17:11; Judg. 1:27). It sits at the entrance to a pass across the Carmel mountain range, on the main highway between Asia and Africa — the key position between the Euphrates and the Nile. It's been a battlefield throughout many ages. Thothmes III, founder of the old Egyptian empire, said, "Megiddo is worth a thousand cities."\n\nThis will likely be Antichrist's headquarters when he comes from the north after conquering Russia and countries north and east of the old Roman Empire. Rev. 16:13-16 says, "And he gathered them together into a place called in the Hebrew tongue Armageddon."\n\nThere he'll await Christ's return from Heaven, expecting Him to set foot on the Mount of Olives and deliver Israel when half of Jerusalem is taken (Zech. 14:1-5). The devil "knoweth that he hath but a short time" (Rev. 12:12), and it will be common knowledge to Antichrist and others that Christ is expected at the end of the 1,260 days of Rev. 11:1-3; 12:6, 14; 13:5.\n\nBy some means, Antichrist will have lost control of Jerusalem toward the end of the Week. While he's been directing armies against northern and eastern countries (Dan. 11:44), the Jews will regain control of the city. The two witnesses will help the remnant of Israel recapture Jerusalem through their miraculous powers. At any rate, Zech. 14 makes clear that Antichrist returns from the north to gather nations against the Jews and Jerusalem by the time Christ returns.\n\nEzek. 38 and 39 also show that after Antichrist conquers Russia, Germany, and other northern and eastern countries, he returns with armies from these newly conquered lands — along with the ten kingdoms and cooperating nations — to destroy Israel and stop Christ from establishing His kingdom.\n\nThese Ezekiel chapters are often interpreted as proving Antichrist will come from Russia because he's "the chief prince of Meshech and Tubal" who leads Russia and Germany south against Palestine. But Dan. 11:44 proves Antichrist first *conquers* these northern and eastern countries before becoming their chief prince and leading them against the Jews.\n\n### 2. The Time Armageddon Will Be Fought\n\n> (1) When Israel is safe in the wilderness and "Sheba, and Dedan, and the merchants of Tarshish, with all the young lions thereof" — identified as Edom, Moab, chief of Ammon's children, including Arabian chiefs (Dan. 11:41; Rev. 12:6, 14-17) — ask, "Art thou come to take a spoil? . . . to carry away silver and gold, to take away cattle and goods, to take a great spoil?" (Ezek. 38:1-16).\n\n> (2) When Antichrist has completed conquering Russia, Germany, and other countries north and east of his ten-kingdom empire (Dan. 11:44; Ezek. 38:1-16).\n\n> (3) At Christ's second coming to deliver the Jews and Jerusalem from Antichrist's armies (Joel 3; Zech. 14; Isa. 63:1-6; Jude 14; 2 Thess. 1:7-10).\n\n> (4) Immediately after the Tribulation (Mt. 24:29-31; 25:31-46).\n\n> (5) After the Marriage Supper of the Lamb (Rev. 19:1-21).\n\n> (6) When Satan is bound for 1,000 years (Rev. 19:11; 20:3).\n\n> (7) When Jerusalem is surrounded by nations' armies and half the city is taken (Zech. 14:1-15; Rev. 14:14-21; 16:13-16).\n\n> (8) Just before the Millennium (Rev. 19:11–20:3).\n\n> (9) At this age's end (Mt. 13:40-43; 25:31-46).\n\n> (10) When God establishes His earthly kingdom (Dan. 2:44; 7:13, 14, 18-27).\n\n> (11) When the first resurrection is completed (Rev. 19:11–20:6).\n\n> (12) At the end of Daniel's Seventieth Week (Dan. 9:27; Rev. 13:5; 19:11-21).\n\n> (13) Forty-two months after Antichrist gains power over the ten kingdoms (Rev. 13:5; 19:11-21).\n\n> (14) When people think universal peace has arrived because Antichrist has conquered much of the world (1 Thess. 5:1-3).\n\n> (15) At the beginning of the day of the Lord (2 Thess. 2:1-12; 1 Thess. 5:1-3; Rev. 19:11-21; 20:1-3).\n\n### 3. The Combatants at Armageddon\n\nThis won't be an ordinary battle between earthly nations. It's a battle between Heaven's armies under Christ and Earth's armies under the dragon, the beast, and false prophet.\n\n**On Christ's side:** earthly Israel (Zech. 14:1-15), God's angels (Mt. 25:31-45; 2 Thess. 1:7-10), and resurrected saints of all ages (Zech. 14:1-5; Jude 14; Rev. 19:11-21).\n\n**On Antichrist's side:** the devil with his angels and demons (Rev. 12:7-12; 16:13-16; Rev. 20:1-3), the ten kings (Rev. 17:14-17; Dan. 2:44; 7:19-27), countries north and east of the ten kingdoms recently conquered by Antichrist (Dan. 11:44; Ezek. 38; 39; Rev. 16:12), and many other nations cooperating through the three unclean frogs' ministry (Rev. 16:13-16; Zech. 14:1-5, 16; Ezek. 38; 39).\n\n### 4. The Purpose of Armageddon\n\n**God's purposes:** To deliver Israel from total destruction by Antichrist and his allied nations (Zech. 14; Isa. 63:1-10). To punish these nations for persecuting the Jews (Mt. 25:31-46). To establish an earthly kingdom with Christ as head (Dan. 7:13, 14; Lk. 1:32). To rid Earth of rebellion and restore God's dominion as before the Fall (1 Cor. 15:24-29; Eph. 1:10). To give mankind one more dispensational test before destroying every rebel (Eph. 1:10; Rev. 20:1-10). To establish the eternal perfect state (Rev. 21:1–22:5; 2 Pet. 3:10-13).\n\n**Man's and Satan's purposes:** To stop God's plan of taking over earthly governments and to avert their own impending doom if defeated (Rev. 12:12; 19:19-21; 20:1-10; Zech. 14:1-5).\n\n### 5. The Length of the Battle of Armageddon\n\nAccording to Zech. 14:1-14, the battle lasts only one day: "The Lord my God shall come, and all the saints with thee. And it shall come to pass in that day, that the light shall not be clear, nor dark: but it shall be one day which shall be known to the Lord, not day, nor night: but it shall come to pass, that at evening time it shall be light."\n\nIt's similar to a decisive military strike — the outcome isn't in doubt, and it's over swiftly.\n\n### 6. The Results of Armageddon\n\n> (1) Total defeat of Earth's armies and Satan's spirit forces (Isa. 24:21-23; 25:7; 63:1-6; Rev. 19:19–20:3; Ezek. 38; 39).\n\n> (2) All vast armies destroyed except "the sixth part" (Ezek. 39:2; Rev. 19:19-21; Zech. 14:1-15; Joel 3).\n\n> (3) These armies will provide carcasses for fowls to eat for up to seven months (Ezek. 39:4-24; Rev. 19:17-21; Mt. 24:27, 28, 40-42; Lk. 17:34-37; Job 39:27-30).\n\n> (4) The beast and false prophet cast into the Lake of Fire (Rev. 19:20; Dan. 7:11; 8:25; 11:45; 2 Thess. 2:8, 9).\n\n> (5) The devil and his angels cast into the bottomless pit (Rev. 20:1-7).\n\n> (6) Blood flowing up to horses' bridles (Rev. 14:14-20; Ezek. 39:17-24).\n\n> (7) Israel delivered and vindicated, God's eternal kingdom established (Mt. 25:31-46; Dan. 2:44; 7:18, 23-27; Rev. 11:15; 20:1-10; 21:2–22:5).\n\n### 7. Ways Antichrist's Armies Will Be Destroyed\n\n> (1) By the brightness of Christ's coming (2 Thess. 2:8).\n\n> (2) By angels (Mt. 24:27-31; 2 Thess. 1:7-10).\n\n> (3) By the saints (Zech. 14:5; Jude 14; Rev. 17:14; 19:11-21).\n\n> (4) By hail and rain from Heaven (Ezek. 38:22; Rev. 16:21).\n\n> (5) By the Jews (Zech. 12:1–13:1; 14:14).\n\n> (6) By beast's armies slaying each other (Ezek. 38:21;\n\n---\n\nArmageddon is not the end of hope — it's the end of the age that rejected hope. After the battle, Christ reigns. The kingdom begins. Everything the prophets promised, everything the Church has prayed for in 'thy kingdom come,' arrives. So here's the question: You pray 'thy kingdom come' — but do you actually long for it? Or have you become so comfortable in this age that Christ's return feels more like a disruption than a rescue? And what does your answer tell you about where your heart is?	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612w9001vgeo0ta3pkxhu	cmq6612vy001hgeo0djva1vnw	Supplement 11 — A Final Synthesis: The Theology of Angelic Ministry	SUPPLEMENT	600	6	\N	t	![Supplement 11 — A Final Synthesis: The Theology of Angelic Ministry](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os4kqZY4L3Ls52XczwCYNqdZVf8hMUGlEvQ0nD)\n\n## Supplement 11 — A Final Synthesis: What We Have Learned\n\n### This Is Not Another Theology Lesson\n\nThe other ten supplements gave you key terms, scripture memory verses, comparison tables, and questions. This final supplement does something different.\n\nIt asks you to do the synthesizing.\n\nYou have now completed eighteen lessons on the angels. You began with a being standing beside you, unseen. You have traced that being's lineage through nine choirs and three hierarchies, learned how it knows, when it was made, what it was made for, and how to relate to it. You have met the Seraphim who have never once stopped singing, the Cherubim who have guarded the sacred since before human memory, the Thrones who embody the stability of God's sovereignty, the governors of creation, the guardians of nations, the archangels assigned to the most important moments in history, and the one angel assigned specifically to you.\n\nThis supplement is your chance to make that knowledge yours.\n\n---\n\n### The Nine Choirs: Complete\n\n| Choir | Hierarchy | Defining Quality | Function |\n|-------|----------|----------------|---------|\n| **Seraphim** | 1st | Burning love | Ceaseless adoration of God |\n| **Cherubim** | 1st | Fullness of knowledge | Guardianship of the sacred |\n| **Thrones** | 1st | Stable authority | Contemplating divine governance |\n| **Dominations** | 2nd | Executive direction | Governing the angelic order |\n| **Virtues** | 2nd | Physical power | Sustaining cosmic law; miracles |\n| **Powers** | 2nd | Defense | Protecting creation's integrity |\n| **Principalities** | 3rd | Guardianship of peoples | Nations, civilizations, the Church |\n| **Archangels** | 3rd | Chief missions | Gabriel, Michael, Raphael — and others |\n| **Angels** | 3rd | Personal ministry | Guardian angels; ministry to souls |\n\n---\n\n### Four Theological Pillars\n\n**I. All angelic activity is derivative.** Every power the angels exercise comes from God and operates within His providential plan. The Seraphim love because God loves. The Virtues sustain natural law because God sustains it through them. Your guardian angel protects you because God commanded it. No angel acts independently.\n\n**II. The angels desire your salvation — personally.** [1 Peter 1:12](data-scripture="1 Peter 1:12") says the angels *"long to look"* into the things of the Gospel. Your redemption is not a matter of indifference to heaven. It is a matter of joy: *"there will be more joy in heaven over one sinner who repents"* ([Luke 15:7](data-scripture="Luke 15:7")). The angels rejoice when you turn toward God. They have a stake in your outcome.\n\n**III. The entire angelic creation is oriented toward Christ.** Gabriel announced the Incarnation. Michael protected the people Christ died to save. Raphael foreshadowed the healing Christ enacted. Angels ministered to Christ throughout His earthly life, announced His resurrection, and populate every page of the Apocalypse. The angels do not exist for themselves. They exist for Christ — and for those He redeemed.\n\n**IV. The relationship does not end with the course.** Knowledge of the angels is not an end. It is a beginning. The Seraphim's burning love is the destination of the spiritual life. The guardian angel is a companion for the entire journey. The Mass is the meeting point of the earthly and heavenly liturgies — and you are invited to it every Sunday.\n\n---\n\n### Final Questions — One of These Is Your Take-Away\n\nChoose one. Sit with it for longer than feels comfortable.\n\n1. Looking back across eighteen lessons: what single truth most changed what you believe? Not the most interesting fact — the truth that most directly challenges how you have been living.\n\n2. The Seraphim have been crying "Holy, holy, holy" since before the universe existed. They have not grown bored, tired, or distracted. What does this tell you about the nature of God — and what does it ask of you in response?\n\n3. Peter says the angels *"long to look"* into the Gospel ([1 Peter 1:12](data-scripture="1 Peter 1:12")). These beings, who know the entire natural order, are fascinated by what God did in Christ for human souls. What does the fact that the angels find your redemption *interesting* suggest about its value?\n\n4. Your guardian angel has been with you since conception. It has been present at every moment of your life — the moments you are proud of and the ones you are not. It has carried your prayers before God. It is present with you right now. **Write a letter to it.** Not a prayer — a letter. What would you say?\n\n5. You began this course not knowing most of what you now know. Someone you know — a friend, a family member, a child — also does not know it yet. What is the one truth from this course you most want to give them, and how would you say it in a way they could actually receive?	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk4br002aewhjie2olpmn	cmnknk4bp001qewhjk5bcqnfj	Lesson 50 — The Dispensation of Divine Government	READING	4850	19	\N	t	For one thousand years, the earth will be governed by Jesus Christ from Jerusalem — directly, visibly, with no democratic ambiguity or disputed authority. Crime will be adjudicated immediately. Satan will be bound. Nature itself will be transformed: wolves lying down with lambs, deserts blooming, lifespans extending. This is not allegory. This is the literal fulfillment of promises God made to Abraham, to David, and to the prophets — promises that cannot be spiritualized away without making God a promise-breaker.\n\nLast time we saw Christ return at Armageddon to establish His authority on earth. Now we enter the dispensation that follows: the Millennium — one thousand years of divine government with Christ reigning physically from the throne of David in Jerusalem.\n\nTHE AGE TO COME is that stretch of time from Christ's second advent all the way to the New Heaven and New Earth. It contains just one dispensation—the Millennium. This will be the final age before the eternal perfect state, when God will once again be all-in-all, just as He was before rebellion ever entered the universe.\n\nIn Rev. 20:1-15, we get a panoramic view of what's coming: Satan's expulsion from Earth, Christ's thousand-year reign with His saints, Satan's brief post-millennial career and ultimate doom, and the final judgment of all.\n\n![Lesson 50 — The Dispensation of Divine Government](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsUyIgkZu6edALvbYMWXfx7ZoQswlOpr26nuJ1)\n\n### I. The Expulsion of Satan From the Earth\n\n"And I saw an angel come down from heaven, having the key of the bottomless pit and a great chain in his hand. And he laid hold on the dragon, that old serpent, which is the devil, and Satan, and bound him a thousand years. And cast him into the bottomless pit, and shut him up, and set a seal upon him, that he should deceive the nations no more, till the thousand years should be fulfilled: and after that he must be loosed a little season" (Rev. 20:1-3).\n\nThis passage picks up right where Rev. 19:11-21 left off—after the Battle of Armageddon—and shows us the dragon being confined to the Abyss. Once Armageddon is over, an angel will descend from Heaven carrying the key to the Abyss. This angel is explained under the fifth trumpet in Lesson Forty-one, and the Abyss itself is covered in Lesson Thirty-seven.\n\nNow, you might wonder: how can an angel or spirit be bound by a literal chain and thrown into a material place? It only makes sense when you remember that angels have bodies and can be localized and confined to physical locations, as we saw in Lesson Six. Think of it like this: even though angels are spiritual beings, they still have form and substance—they're not just abstract ideas floating around.\n\nIf this weren't true, how could the demons currently bound in the Abyss be released under the fifth and sixth trumpets? How could angels be confined to Tartarus in chains (2 Pet. 2:4; Jude 6, 7)? And how will all wicked men, demons, fallen angels, and rebellious creatures of every kind be confined in the Lake of Fire forever? (Mt. 25:41; Rev. 14:9-11; 19:20; 20:10-15).\n\nThis angel mentioned in Rev. 20:1-3 will lay hold of Satan, overpower him through actual combat, bind him with a great chain, and cast him into the Abyss for a thousand years. Then the angel will "set a seal upon him"—literally sealing the Abyss over Satan to keep him there so he cannot deceive the nations until the Millennium is finished.\n\nSo we see that Satan is a literal person, his doom is literal, he will be bound by a literal angel with a literal chain, cast into a literal Abyss, and sealed with a literal seal for the duration of the Millennium.\n\nIn Rev. 12, we learned that the dragon and his angels will be cast out of Heaven to Earth in the middle of the Week. They'll remain there until the Battle of Armageddon, when they'll fight against Christ and His angels and saints. Scripture doesn't explicitly state whether Satan's angels will be cast into the Abyss with him. However, Isa. 24:21-22 and 25:7 make it clear they will be cast into the pit with Satan and will be loosed with him "after many days" to help him deceive the nations once more (Rev. 20:1-10).\n\n### II. The Millennial Reign of Christ and His Saints\n\n"And I saw thrones and they sat upon them, and judgment was given unto them: and I saw the souls of them that were beheaded for the witness of Jesus, and for the word of God, and which had not worshipped the beast, neither his image, neither had received his mark upon their foreheads, or in their hands; and they lived and reigned with Christ a thousand years. But the rest of the dead lived not again until the thousand years were finished. This is the first resurrection. Blessed and holy is he that hath part in the first resurrection: on such the second death hath no power, but they shall be priests of God and of Christ, and shall reign with him a thousand years" (Rev. 20:4-6).\n\nThis passage reveals that the Tribulation martyrs will also share in Christ's reign during the Millennium and forever. Even if no other passage in the Bible taught the doctrine of the Millennium, this one alone would be sufficient. The word "millennium" simply means "one thousand years"—a term repeated six times in just the first seven verses of Rev. 20.\n\nBefore we explore what other Scriptures say about the Millennium, let's note what Rev. 20 itself tells us:\n\n> 1. Satan must be bound before the Millennium can begin (Rev. 20:1-10). This clearly implies that all the events of Rev. 4-19 must be fulfilled first. Therefore, the thousand years cannot arrive until these things come to pass.\n\n> 2. Satan will be bound during the Millennium (Rev. 20:3).\n\n> 3. After Satan's binding, John saw "thrones" and their occupants (Rev. 20:4). The ones sitting on these thrones will be the Tribulation martyrs. They will reign as kings and priests with Christ, just as all other redeemed heavenly peoples will.\n\n> 4. In Rev. 20:5, John shows that the Tribulation martyrs have a part in the first resurrection, which occurs before the Millennium and includes all the different companies of the redeemed, saved, and resurrected from Adam to the binding of Satan. This verse also implies that the Tribulation saints will be the last redeemed company to be resurrected and translated. This first resurrection ends with the rapture of this company and of the two witnesses. All other passages on resurrections in Scripture—except a few on the rapture of the Church—speak of the first and second resurrections as being one event occurring at the same time. However, Rev. 20:5 and 1 Cor. 15:20-23, 51-58; Phil. 3:10-14; 1 Thess. 4:13-17; 2 Thess. 2:1, 6-8; 2 Cor. 5:1-6; Eph. 5:26, 27; Heb. 11:35; 1 Jn. 3:1-3 speak of a resurrection from out of the dead—the dead and living saints up to the rapture, plus only those who get saved and die in the Tribulation. In Rev. 20:11-15, the wicked dead—who have no part in the first resurrection and won't be resurrected until after the thousand years—are pictured standing before the great white throne to be judged. This will be the second resurrection, including all the wicked dead from Adam to the end of the Millennium.\n\n> 5. Next, a blessing is pronounced upon all who have part in the first resurrection, for "on such the second death [the Lake of Fire, Rev. 2:11; 19:20; 20:10-15; 21:8] hath no power, but they shall be priests of God and of Christ, and shall reign one thousand years" (Rev. 20:6).\n\n> 6. "When the thousand years are expired, Satan shall be loosed out of his prison. And shall go out to deceive the nations which are in the four quarters of the earth, Gog and Magog, to gather them" against God (Rev. 20:7-10). Then fire will come down from Heaven to devour his armies, and Satan himself will be cast into the Lake of Fire—where the beast and false prophet are and have been for the entire thousand years (Rev. 19:20; 20:7-10).\n\n> 7. Then the wicked dead will be resurrected, and the final judgment will take place. After that comes the renovation of the heavens and Earth, resulting in a New Heaven and a New Earth, as pictured in Rev. 21-22.\n\nNow, with these basic facts in mind, we can better understand the many other Scriptures that speak of the Messiah's reign without distinguishing between His first thousand years and His reign forever. Beyond what Rev. 20 tells us, here's a brief study of the subject.\n\n### III. General Truths About the Millennium\n\n**1. Definition of the Millennium**\n\nThis dispensation is called Divine Government because God Himself—along with the Son and Holy Spirit—will establish a divine government on Earth over all nations forever. The first thousand years of God's reign is called the Millennium, which simply means "one thousand years." It comes from *mille* (thousand) and *annum* (year).\n\nScriptural terms for this age include:\n\n> (1) "The thousand years" reign of Christ (Rev. 20:1-10).\n\n> (2) "The dispensation of the fulness of times" (Eph. 1:10).\n\n> (3) "The day of the Lord" (Isa. 2:12; 13:6, 9; 34:8; Ezek. 30:3; Amos 5:18; Joel 2:1; Zeph. 1:7, 8, 18; 2:2-3; Zech. 14:1-21; Mal. 4; 1 Thess. 5:2; 2 Thess. 2:1-8; 2 Pet. 3:10).\n\n> (4) "That day" (Isa. 2:11; 4:1-6; 19:21; 24:21; 26:1; Ezek. 39:22; 48:35; Hos. 2:18; Joel 3:18; Zech. 12:8-11; 13:1; 14:1-9; Mal. 3:17).\n\n> (5) "The world [age] to come" (Mt. 12:32; Mk. 10:30; Lk. 20:35; Eph. 1:21; 2:7-14).\n\n> (6) "The kingdom of Christ and of God" (Mk. 14:25; Lk. 10:11; 22:14-18).\n\n> (7) "The kingdom of heaven" (Mt. 3:2; 4:17; 5:3, 10, 19, 20; 7:21; 8:11; 10:7; 13:43; 18:1-4; Lk. 19:12-15).\n\n> (8) "The kingdom of God" (Mk. 14:25; Lk. 10:11; 22:14-18).\n\n> (9) "The regeneration" (Mt. 19:28; Eph. 1:10).\n\n> (10) "The times of the restitution [restoration] of all things" (Acts 3:20-21).\n\n> (11) "The consolation of Israel" (Lk. 2:25).\n\n> (12) "The redemption of Jerusalem" (Lk. 2:38).\n\n**2. Length of the Millennium (Rev. 20:1-10)**\n\nThis dispensation will last 1,000 years (Rev. 20:1-10). The expression "thousand years" appears six times in just this one passage. Although the length is mentioned only here, the age is referenced throughout Scripture, as we'll see.\n\nIt will begin with the binding of Satan at Christ's return to Earth to reestablish David's throne and set up God's kingdom (Mt. 24:29-31; Rev. 19:11–20:7). It will end with the loosing of Satan, the last rebellion, the renovation of Earth by fire, and the Great White Throne Judgment (Rev. 20:11-15; 2 Pet. 3:8-13).\n\nOne thing we must emphasize: these 1,000 years are only the *first* thousand years of Christ's reign on Earth. He will continue to reign over the same kingdom eternally. The first thousand years serve the express purpose of ridding Earth of all rebellion, destroying all enemies, abolishing death and sin, and restoring this rebellious part of God's universal kingdom to its rightful place over all other creations—just as it was before sin entered through Lucifer and Adam.\n\nIn this Millennial Age, God will gather together all things in Christ, both the things in heaven and on Earth (1 Cor. 15:24-28; Eph. 1:10; Rev. 22:4-5).\n\n**3. The Favorable Beginning**\n\nIn this age, humanity will have a more favorable beginning than in any other dispensation. Besides enjoying many wonderful benefits from previous ages, people will have the God of Heaven as their ruler and experience all the privileges that such rulership brings. The following points about divine government and the blessed conditions on Earth during the Millennium will clearly reveal just how favorable this dispensation will be.\n\n**4. The Kingdom Foretold**\n\nGod's covenants with Abraham and David guaranteed Israel an everlasting earthly kingdom and established them as the channel of blessings to all families of the Earth. It seemed these covenants and promises might fail when Israel divided into two kingdoms around 1009 B.C.\n\nAfter this split, God raised up many prophets who continued emphasizing that He would still fulfill His promises to Israel—though He would have to use different means than originally planned, given their continued rebellion against His righteous requirements.\n\nSixteen of these prophets left writings concerning the coming King and kingdom. Notice in the following passages that because of Israel's rebellion, they would go into captivity and be scattered among the nations. They would remain "many days" without a king, a sacrifice, or knowledge of the true God. Afterward, they would be gathered back to their own land but brought very low through Gentile oppression. Then they would be delivered from the nations by the Messiah, who would come from glory to set up the kingdom (Isa. 1:2-9, 25-28; 2:2-5; 9:6-7; 11:2-16; 27:12-13; 32:1-5, 15-19; 34:1-17; 63:1-6; Jer. 33:17-26; Ezek. 24:11-30; 36:16-38; 37:1-28; Dan. 7:12-27; 8:16-27; 9:24-27; 11:36–12:13; Hos. 2:14-23; 3:4-5; Joel 2:28–3:21; Mic. 4:1-13; 5:1-15; Zech. 8:1–14:21; Mal. 3:1–4:6; Lk. 1:30, 35; 21:20-24; Acts 15:13-17; Rom. 11:25-27; Rev. 1:5; 5:10; 11:15; 20:1-4).\n\nMen looked for this kingdom through the ages (Heb. 11; 2 Sam. 7; Isa. 9:6-7; Mt. 4; Mk. 15:43; Heb. 12:25-28; Acts 3:19-21).\n\n**5. When Will Christ's Kingdom Be Set Up?**\n\n> (1) At the return of the King from glory (Mt. 25:31-46; Isa. 9:6-7; Dan. 2:44-45; 7:13-14; 8:18-22; Zech. 14; 1 Thess. 1:7; Jude 14; Rev. 17:14; 19:11–20:7).\n\n> (2) After the Church is raptured (1 Cor. 15:51-58; 1 Thess. 4:13-17), for the Church comes back to Earth with Christ to help Him set up the kingdom and reign over the nations (Zech. 14:1-5; Jude 14; Rev. 1:4-5; 5:10; 17:14; 19:11-21). It is not until after the days of the Church that Christ comes to rebuild the house of David (Acts 15:13-18; Isa. 9:6-7; 11:11; Hos. 3:4-5; Lk. 1:32-35). The Church is raptured before the Antichrist comes (2 Thess. 2:7-8), and Antichrist makes his appearance before Christ comes (2 Thess. 2:1-6), so Christ's kingdom cannot be established until these events take place.\n\n> (3) After the future tribulation, for Christ does not come to Earth with the saints until then (Mt. 24:15-31; Zech. 14:1-21; Dan. 12:1-13; Rev. 19:11-21).\n\n> (4) After the great apostasy and the revelation of the Antichrist, for Antichrist is destroyed at Christ's coming to Earth, so he must be here when Christ comes (2 Thess. 2:1-12; Rev. 19:11-21; Dan. 7:18-27; 8:16-27; 9:27; 11:36–12:13).\n\n> (5) At the time the Antichrist is destroyed and Satan is bound for 1,000 years (Rev. 5:10; 20:1-7). During the Church Age and the future tribulation period, Satan is loose (1 Pet. 5:8; Rev. 12:12-17; 13:1-8; 20:1-7). The devil is still loose, so we are still in the Church Age and will remain so until Christ comes to bind him.\n\n> (6) After the first resurrection, for the saints reign with Christ on Earth for 1,000 years (Rev. 5:9-10; 20:1-6). Therefore, the saints must first be resurrected before they can reign with Him. This present time is the period of suffering for Christ, not the period of reigning with Him (Rom. 8:18; 1 Cor. 15:20-58; 2 Cor. 5:6; Phil. 1:23; 3:20-21; Col. 1:24; 2 Tim. 2:12; 3:12). The 1,000 years fall between the resurrection of the righteous and that of the wicked (Rev. 20:4-6, 11-15).\n\n> (7) At the time Ezekiel's temple is built (Ezek. 40:1–43:7). Christ's reign will be established in Jerusalem in Ezekiel's temple (Ezek. 43:7), so the kingdom cannot be set up until then. Christ will build this temple when He comes, but the kingdom naturally cannot be established in the temple until it exists (Isa. 9:6-7; 52:1-8; 62:6-14; Ezek. 36:24-36; 41:1; 43:7; Zech. 6:12-13; 14:1-21; Lk. 1:32-35; Acts 15:13-18).\n\n> (8) After Israel is gathered back from all countries (Ezek. 20:33-36; 36:17-38; 37:1-28; Hos. 3:4-5; Dan. 9:27).\n\n> (9) When the Jews are delivered from the armies of the nations and become a blessing to all the families of the Earth (Gen. 12:1-3; Ps. 2:6-8; Isa. 9:6-7; 25:6-9; Zech. 9:9-11; 14:1-21; Acts 15:13-18; Lk. 1:32-35).\n\n> (10) In the days of the ten kings of Revised Rome and Revived Grecia (Dan. 2:40-45; 7:18-28; Rev. 17:8-18).\n\n> (11) After all of Rev. 4-19 is fulfilled, for Christ comes in Rev. 19-20 to set up the kingdom.\n\nAccording to all these facts, the kingdom is still future and will follow all these events. Christ Himself taught in the following passages that the kingdom would follow His second advent (Mt. 16:21-27; 19:28; 20:20-23; 23:37-39; 24:3-31; 25:31-46; 26:29, 64; Acts 1:6-7; 3:19-21; Jn. 14:3; Lk. 9:26; 19:11-27; Rev. 5:9-10; 11:15; 20:1-7).\n\nThe apostles taught that the kingdom was a future event following Christ's second coming (Acts 1:7-11; 1 Pet. 1:7; 5:4; 2 Pet. 1:16; 3:3-4; Jas. 5:7; 1 Jn. 2:28; Jude 14; 1 Tim. 6:14-15).\n\n**6. Will It Be a Literal Earthly Kingdom?**\n\nThe kingdom will be just as earthly and literal as any other kingdom that has ever existed on Earth. It will be the ninth in the following sequence of kingdoms mentioned in Daniel and Revelation: Egypt, Assyria, Babylon, Medo-Persia, Greece, Rome, Revised Rome, Revived Greece, and the kingdom of Heaven (Isa. 9:6-7; Dan. 2:44-45; 7:13-14, 17-27; Zech. 14; Rev. 17:8-18).\n\nSince all the preceding kingdoms have been literal, the kingdom of Heaven must also be literal. The following studies will further demonstrate that this kingdom will be a literal kingdom on Earth.\n\nThe Seventh Day Adventists and others teach that Earth will be desolate during the 1,000 years and that this Earth is the bottomless pit where the devil will be bound. There is not one word of truth in this theory. The bottomless pit is a department in the underworld for the confinement of certain demon and angelic spirits. That the Earth will not be desolate during this period is proven by the Scriptures in the points below.\n\n**7. What Will Be the Form of Government?**\n\nThe government in the Millennium will not be monarchic, democratic, or autocratic, but theocratic—that is, God reigning through:\n\n> (1) Jesus Christ, His only begotten Son (2 Sam. 7; Ps. 2; 89:35-37; Isa. 2:2-4; 4:2-3; 9:6-7; 11:1-15; 16:5; 24:23; 32:1-4; 40:9-10; 42:1-4; 52:7; Jer. 23:5-8; Ezek. 43:7; Dan. 2:44-45; 7:13-14; Mic. 4; 5:1-7; Zech. 6:12-13; 14:1-21; Mt. 25:31-46; Lk. 1:32-35; Rev. 11:15; 20:1-10).\n\n> (2) David, the king of Israel (Jer. 30:9; Ezek. 34:24; 37:24-28; Hos. 3:4-5).\n\n> (3) The Apostles and all saints from Adam to the Millennium—that is, all who have part in the first resurrection (Ps. 149:5-9; Dan. 7:18-27; Mt. 19:28; 1 Cor. 4:8; 6:2; Eph. 2:7; 2 Tim. 2:12; Heb. 11; Rom. 8:17; 2 Thess. 1:4-7; Rev. 1:6; 2:26-27; 5:9-10; 11:18; 12:5; 20:4-6; 22:5). All saints will be judged and rewarded according to the deeds done in the body and will be given places of rulership according to their degree of rewards—not according to which company of the redeemed they belong to, or which age they were redeemed in. This is the only true and just basis for giving rewards.\n\n> Think of it like this: If some New Testament saint were automatically rewarded and given a greater place in the kingdom than some Old Testament saint simply because he was redeemed in a different age, that would be unjust. But if all are rewarded "according to their works" regardless of when they were redeemed, then God cannot be accused of injustice or of being a respecter of persons. It's up to every person to make good in their own age and prove true to their particular test.\n\n> From the passages in Points (2) and (3), we learn that David will have a greater rulership than any one of the apostles. He is to be king over all Israel under Christ, while the apostles will each have only one tribe.\n\n> Some Old Testament saints did more for God and had more power than the average New Testament saint. Take an ordinary professed follower of Christ today and compare his life and works with Enoch, Abraham, Moses, Elijah, or Elisha. Should the New Testament person receive a greater degree of reward and responsibility in the eternal kingdom than these men just because he's saved in a different age? That wouldn't be just, and it contradicts the doctrine of personal reward according to a person's works, as proven in Prov. 24:12; Ps. 62:12; Jer. 31:16; Rom. 14:12; 2 Cor. 5:10-11; 1 Cor. 3:11-15; Jas. 2:21-25; Rev. 14:12; 20:12-15; 22:12.\n\n> Certain classes of people will not have part in reigning with Christ (Mt. 18:1-13; Lk. 9:62; 14:27; Jn. 3:3-5; Rom. 8:9; 1 Cor. 6:9-10; Gal. 5:19-21; Eph. 5:5; 2 Tim. 2:12; Heb. 12:14; 1 Jn. 3:10; Rev. 20:15).\n\n> (4) Earthly judges and kings will be restored, but as subordinates to the heavenly rulers (Isa. 1:25-28; Ezek. 43:7-12; Rev. 21:24).\n\n**8. Where Will the Seat of Government Be?**\n\nJerusalem, rebuilt and restored to a greater glory than ever before, will be the seat of government, the world capital, and the center of worship forever (1 Chron. 23:25; 2 Chron. 33:4-7; Ps. 48:8; Isa. 2:2-4; 11:11–12:6; Jer. 17:25; Ezek. 34:1-35; 43:7; Joel 3:17, 20; Mic. 4:7; Zech. 8:3-23; 14:1-21; 15:1-18).\n\n**9. What Will Be the Territorial Extent of the Kingdom?**\n\nIt will be worldwide and will forever "increase" in population and blessings (Isa. 9:6-7; 11:9; Ps. 72:8; 97:9; Dan. 7:13-14; Mic. 4:1-3; Zech. 9:10; 14:1-21; Rev. 11:15).\n\n**10. Who Will and Will Not Be the Subjects of the Kingdom?**\n\nVarious classes of people will be excluded from the kingdom (Mt. 5:20; 13:49, 50; 24:45-51; 25:25-28, 31-46; Rev. 14:9-12). Some people from all nations currently on Earth will continue as natural people in the kingdom forever. "All people, nations, and languages should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed" (Dan. 7:13-14, 18, 22-27; Isa. 9:6-7; Zech. 14:1-21; Lk. 1:32-35; Rev. 11:15).\n\nAfter the Battle of Armageddon and the judgment of the nations at Christ's return, many will be left from all nations. These survivors will go up from year to year to worship the Lord of hosts and keep the Feast of Tabernacles. These people and their children will populate the Earth during the Millennium (Isa. 2:1-2; Zech. 14:16-21; Mt. 25:31-46; Rev. 11:15; 20:1-10).\n\nThe Russellists teach that Christ's atonement was for Adam only—that one man could only atone for one man, that all the sons of Adam must remain dead until the Millennium when they'll be resurrected and given a second chance, and that all who won't accept God during this second probation will be annihilated. This is one of the most erroneous and unscriptural teachings ever set forth.\n\nIt denies the very heart of the gospel, for Jesus died for every person, as proven in Mt. 1:21; 26:29; Lk. 24:47; Jn. 1:12-16; 3:5, 16-19; 6:37-40; 14:6; Acts 2:38; 4:12; Rom. 1:16; 5:6-11, 15-21; 6:23; 8:1-4, 32; 2 Cor. 5:14-21; Eph. 1:7; Col. 1:14, 20-22; Heb. 1:3; 2:9-10; 9:11-28; 10:4-22, 29; 1 Pet. 1:18-23; 1 Jn. 1:7.\n\nWhat is it in all these passages that makes God just in forgiving everyone today who repents and believes the gospel? It is the one sacrifice of Christ for all people of all times—not for Adam alone. If one man could only atone for one man's sins, then to be redeemed, every person ever born would need God to die for them individually. God would then have to do what He did in Christ a countless number of times. Such a thing is absurd.\n\nIf people are going to have another chance in the Millennium, the basis of their reconciliation must be the same as it is now. Thus, their teaching that Christ died for one man only is contradicted by their teaching that all will have a second chance during the Millennium. Otherwise, how are they to be saved then unless Christ dies separately for each individual, as they teach in the doctrine of the atonement?\n\nThe Bible teaches that all the righteous dead will be resurrected before the Millennium and the wicked dead after that period (Rev. 20:4-15). So how could the wicked be resurrected and given a second chance during the Millennium if they're not to rise until after the Millennium?\n\nNowhere does the Bible teach that people have a second chance. On the contrary, it says, "it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment" (Heb. 9:27). The Bible does not say, "after this a second chance, and then annihilation if they fail again." The Bible does not teach annihilation for anyone, as is abundantly proven in Lesson Thirty-nine. During their natural lifetime, people have hundreds of chances to get right with God, and if they fail to do so, they will be cut off "without remedy" (Prov. 29:1).\n\nSo it's clear that the subjects of the Millennial Kingdom will not be the wicked dead raised to life after the Millennium, but people from the nations who will be on Earth at Christ's coming with the saints to set up the kingdom (Isa. 2:1-4; 11:11; 66:17-21; Zech. 14:16).\n\nThe Adventists, instead of believing there will be inhabitants on Earth in the Millennium, teach that Earth will be desolate of all human, animal, and plant life during this period. They teach the devil will be bound on Earth at this time, but this is disproved by the facts of Rev. 20:1-15, as listed in Point II above.\n\n**11. Will There Be Laws for the Subjects of the Kingdom?**\n\nThere will be laws in this kingdom for the same purpose as in any other kingdom. There are laws even in Heaven and throughout the universe. Adam was given laws to keep before he fell. People will have laws to keep in all eternity after mankind\n\n---\n\nThe Millennium is the vindication of every promise God ever made to Israel — and through Israel, to the world. The kingdom that believers have prayed and labored and died for will finally arrive in visible, undeniable form. So here's the question: What promise of God are you currently waiting for that hasn't come yet — a healing, a restoration, a salvation of someone you love? If God kept every promise He made to Israel over thousands of years, what does that tell you about His intention to keep the promises He's made to you?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsi4000718pf1j1l8kta	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Fortune-Telling Apps and Digital Divination	READING	\N	6	\N	t	![Fortune-Telling Apps and Digital Divination](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Osh7yRkb2RWrNFBdIuiJlO67t4A5yKbkf8vT0P)\n\n## Fortune-Telling Apps and Digital Divination\n\nShe checked the Co-Star astrology app every morning before she checked her email. It had seven million users. Its daily "guidance" was strikingly personal — specific to her chart, specific to the day's planetary positions, delivered with a precision that felt intuitive. Her friends used it too. They compared their readings the way previous generations compared horoscopes.\n\nShe would tell you she did not believe in astrology. It was just interesting. Just a way to reflect on her day. She did not notice that she made small decisions differently on days when the app said her "energy" was blocked — that she deferred calls, avoided conflict, rescheduled things. She had given a $2.99 app meaningful governance over the shape of her days.\n\nShe had not examined what was actually producing the precision that made the app feel worth following.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nDigital divination encompasses astrology apps (Co-Star, The Pattern, Sanctuary), tarot card applications (Labyrinthos, Golden Thread Tarot), AI chatbots claiming to channel deceased loved ones or spiritual guides, online psychic platforms, and social media "fortune-telling" filters and quizzes.\n\nThe global market for these services generates hundreds of millions in annual revenue. A significant percentage of people under 35 who would never visit a physical psychic regularly consult digital divination tools. The gamification of divination — daily readings, personality compatibility scores, "future prediction" features — makes occult participation feel like entertainment rather than spiritual practice.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nTechnology has not replaced the demonic — it has digitized it. Every query sent to a divination app is the same spiritual transaction as visiting a medium. The screen is not a barrier. It is a portal.\n\n[Deuteronomy 18:12](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 18:12"): *"For all that do these things are an abomination unto the LORD."* This verse does not have an exception for software. The prohibition on seeking guidance from divination systems applies regardless of whether those systems are delivered through an oracle in an ancient temple or an algorithm on a smartphone.\n\nAI chatbots that claim to channel deceased loved ones or spiritual guides combine the perceived authority of sophisticated technology with the intimacy of personal conversation. The algorithm does not directly communicate with demons — but it creates a conversational format in which familiar spirits can influence output to produce spiritually targeted deception for specific users. The technology is the instrument. The spiritual reality behind it is unchanged.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Convenience removes the psychological friction that might otherwise prevent engagement.** A person who would not drive to visit a psychic will consult a tarot app before deciding whether to text an ex-boyfriend. The threshold is gone. The spiritual transaction is the same.\n\n**Regular consultation builds a dependent relationship with the system behind the app.** The person who checks their horoscope app every morning for three years has built a consistent daily habit of seeking guidance from a system staffed by familiar spirits. The depth of the relationship builds proportionally to the frequency of consultation.\n\n**Social normalization amplifies individual exposure.** When an entire friend group uses the same astrology app, comparing readings and referencing chart compatibility in relationship discussions, the practice is socially validated in a way that makes spiritual examination feel like social killjoy-ism. The community pressure to continue is real.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nDelete the apps. Now, not after finishing this lesson. Every astrology app, every tarot app, every AI chatbot that claims spiritual channeling. Block the websites.\n\nThen ask yourself honestly: how many days in the past month have I sought guidance from a divination system — even casually, even "just for fun"? What decisions have I made or deferred based on what those systems said?\n\nThe God who made you and knows your days intimately offers His guidance freely — through Scripture, through prayer, through the counsel of the Holy Spirit, through the wisdom of mature believers in your community. That guidance costs nothing, requires no subscription, and is not staffed by familiar spirits.\n\n[Proverbs 3:5-6](data-scripture="Proverbs 3:5-6"): *"Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding. In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths."*\n\n---\n\n*Six entry points. All of them mainstream. All of them staffed by familiar spirits. The next lesson opens Wave 2 — the practices sold as healing.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Which apps on your phone have a divination, spiritual guidance, or astrology function? List them specifically before moving forward.*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk48i0017ewhjr9dcmvip	cmnknk48e000xewhj49ao5az0	Lesson 25 — The Truth About the Holy Spirit	READING	2424	9	\N	t	The Holy Spirit is the most present yet most ignored member of the Trinity. He's given more content in the New Testament than almost any other subject — and yet most Christians couldn't describe His actual work in their lives in more than two or three sentences. He's reduced to a feeling, a vague spiritual warmth, or an abstract theological category. But Scripture presents a Person, not an atmosphere.\n\nLast time we walked through the specific steps for receiving freedom from sin and sickness. Now we turn to the One who makes that freedom possible and sustains it: the Holy Spirit — who He is, what He does, and why so many believers are living as if He isn't there.\n\n![Lesson 25 — The Truth About the Holy Spirit](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OslpwEmOXBDwf9iQcORak6Sx8F3eyonuXqN5zM)\n\n## I. The Deity of the Holy Spirit\n\n### 1. He Is Spoken of as God\n\nLet's start with something that might surprise you: the Bible calls the Holy Spirit "God" directly. When Ananias lied about the money he received for his property, Peter said, "Why hath Satan filled thine heart to lie to the Holy Ghost . . . thou hast not lied unto men, but unto God" (Acts 5:3-4). Did you catch that? Lying to the Holy Spirit equals lying to God.\n\nPaul drives this home when he writes, "Know ye not that ye are the temple of God, and that the Spirit of God dwelleth in you? If any man defile the temple of God, him shall God destroy; for the temple of God is holy, which temple ye are" (1 Cor. 3:16-17; 6:19-20). And in 1 Cor. 12:1-11, Paul mentions "the same Spirit . . . the same Lord . . . the same God which worketh all in all" — putting the Spirit right alongside the Father and Son.\n\n### 2. Divine Names and Titles Are Ascribed to Him\n\nThe names and titles given to the Holy Spirit throughout Scripture prove His deity and His oneness with the Father and the Son. Think of it like a king's titles — each one reveals something about his authority and identity. Here's what Scripture calls the Spirit:\n\n> 1. He is called Holy Ghost and Holy Spirit about 97 times.\n\n> 2. The Spirit of God (1 Cor. 3:16; Gen. 1:2; 1 Sam. 19:20-23; Mt. 3:16).\n\n> 3. The Spirit of the Lord (Judg. 3:10; Isa. 11:2; 6:1; Lk. 4:16-21).\n\n> 4. The Spirit of the Living God (2 Cor. 3:3).\n\n> 5. The Spirit of Christ (Rom. 8:9; 1 Pet. 1:11).\n\n> 6. The Spirit of His Son (Gal. 4:6).\n\n> 7. The Spirit of Jesus Christ (Phil. 1:19; Acts 16:7).\n\n> 8. The Spirit of Burning (Isa. 4:4).\n\n> 9. The Spirit of Holiness (Rom. 1:4).\n\n> 10. The Holy Spirit of Promise (Eph. 1:13; Acts 2:33).\n\n> 11. The Spirit of Truth (Jn. 14:17; 15:26; 16:13; 1 Jn. 4:6).\n\n> 12. The Spirit of Life (Rom. 8:2; Rev. 11:11).\n\n> 13. The Spirit of Wisdom and Understanding (Isa. 11:1-2).\n\n> 14. The Spirit of Counsel and Might (Isa. 11:1-2).\n\n> 15. The Spirit of Knowledge and of the Fear of the Lord (Isa. 11:1-2).\n\n> 16. The Spirit of Grace and of Supplications (Zech. 12:10; Heb. 10:29).\n\n> 17. The Spirit of Glory and of God (1 Pet. 4:14).\n\n> 18. The Eternal Spirit (Heb. 9:14).\n\n> 19. The Comforter (Jn. 14:26; 15:26).\n\n> 20. The Spirit of Your Father (Mt. 10:20).\n\n> 21. The Spirit of Prophecy (Rev. 19:10).\n\n### 3. Divine Attributes Are Ascribed to the Holy Spirit\n\nThe Holy Spirit possesses every attribute that belongs to God alone. He has "Eternity and Self-existence" (Heb. 9:14), "Omnipresence" (Ps. 139:7-10), "Omnipotence" (Lk. 1:35; Acts 10:38), and "Omniscience" (1 Cor. 2:10-11; Jn. 14:26; 16:12-13).\n\nHe's involved in "Creation" (Job 33:4; Ps. 104:30) and possesses "Holiness" (Rom. 1:4). The fruit He produces — "Love, Joy, Peace, Longsuffering, Gentleness, Goodness, Faith, Meekness, and Self-control" (Gal. 5:22-23) — reveals His character.\n\nHe offers "Fellowship" (Phil. 2:1), "Glory" (1 Pet. 4:14; 2 Cor. 3:8-18), and "Life" (Rom. 8:1-13). He possesses "Wisdom and Knowledge" (Isa. 11:2; 1 Cor. 12:8), "Immutability" (Heb. 9:14), "Invisibility" (Jn. 3:8; Col. 1:16), and "Infinity" (Rom. 1:4; Jn. 14:26; Eph. 4:30).\n\nHis nature includes "Grace" (Heb. 10:29), "Truth" (Jn. 14:17, 26; 15:26; 16:13), "Justice" (Isa. 11:2-5; 4:4), "Will" (1 Cor. 12:11; Rom. 8:27), "Mind" (Rom. 8:27; 1 Cor. 2:10-11; 12:11), and "Intelligence" (1 Cor. 2:10-11; 12:11; Rom. 8:27).\n\nHe displays "Fear, Might, and Judgment" (Isa. 4:4; 11:2; 1 Cor. 12:8-11; Jn. 16:7-15), "Power" (1 Cor. 12:8-11; 2 Tim. 1:7), and "Decision" (1 Cor. 12:9-11; Acts 13:2). He shares "Unity" with the Father and Son (Mt. 28:19; 2 Cor. 13:14; 1 Jn. 5:7-8) and exercises "Authority" (Mt. 12:28; Acts 10:38; 20:28).\n\nHe has "Hearing and Speech" (Jn. 15:26; 16:13-15; Acts 2:4; 10:44-48; 19:1-7; 1 Cor. 12:1–14:40; Isa. 28:11), "Unselfishness" (Jn. 16:13-15), and "Self-action" (Gen. 1:2; Jn. 14:16-17, 26).\n\n### 4. Divine Works Are Ascribed to the Holy Spirit\n\nWhat does the Holy Spirit actually do? The list is remarkable. He "creates" (Ps. 104:30), "heals" (Rom. 9:11), "gives life" (Rom. 8:2), and "casts out devils" (Mt. 12:28). He "convicts of sin" (Jn. 16:7-11), "redeems" (Jn. 3:3-5; Titus 3:5-7), and "resurrects" (Rom. 8:9-11).\n\nHe "inspires Scripture" (2 Tim. 3:15-17; 2 Pet. 1:21), "distributes gifts" (1 Cor. 12:4-11), and "forms the body of Christ" (1 Cor. 12:13). He "endues with power" (Judg. 11:29; 13:25; 14:6), "changes lives" (1 Sam. 10:6-9; Jn. 3:3-5; 1 Cor. 6:11), and "directs gospel work" (Isa. 48:16; 61:1-2; Acts 11:12; 16:7).\n\nThe Spirit "frees from sin" (Rom. 8:2), "bears witness" (Jn. 15:26; Rom. 8:14-16), and "searches the deep things of God" (1 Cor. 2:10-12). He "brings things to remembrance and teaches and guides into all truth" (Jn. 14:16-17, 26; 15:26; 16:7-15) and "reveals secrets" (1 Cor. 2:10).\n\nHe "dwells in believers" (Rom. 8:9; 1 Cor. 3:16-17), "gives victory over sin" (Rom. 8:1-13), "guides in daily problems" (Rom. 8:14-16), and "adopts into God's family" (Rom. 8:14-16). He "helps in prayer" (Rom. 8:26) and "washes from sin, sanctifies, justifies" (1 Cor. 6:11).\n\nHe "imparts and causes supernatural powers to be manifested through believers" (1 Cor. 12:1–14:40) and "imparts love, joy, peace, longsuffering, goodness, meekness, faith, and self-control through believers" (Gal. 5:22-23). He "seals men to divine ownership" (Eph. 1:13; 4:30), "gives access to God" (Eph. 2:18), and "imparts revelations" (Eph. 3:1-11).\n\nHe "fills believers" (Lk. 1:15; Acts 4:31; Eph. 5:18), "causes obedience to truth" (1 Pet. 1:22), and "speaks of Christ and glorifies Him" (Jn. 16:13-15). He "confirms the gospel" (Heb. 2:3-4) and "carries on the work of God in the world" (Jn. 14:16-17, 26; 15:26; 16:7-15; Acts 20:28; etc.).\n\n### 5. The Holy Spirit Is Associated with the Father and the Son as an Equal Member of Deity\n\nScripture consistently places the Holy Spirit alongside the Father and the Son as a co-equal member of the Godhead (Mt. 28:19; 2 Cor. 13:14; Eph. 4:1-6; 1 Cor. 12:1-11; 1 Jn. 5:7-8).\n\n### 6. Divine Offices Are Ascribed to the Holy Spirit\n\nThe Spirit holds incredible offices within God's plan. He is the "Author of the New Birth" and the "Direct Executive of God" in all phases of creation and redemption (Gen. 1:2; Jn. 3:3-5; 1 Cor. 6:11; Titus 3:5-7). He's the "Inspirer of the Holy Scriptures" (2 Tim. 3:15-17; 2 Pet. 1:21) and the "General Overseer of the churches" (Acts 20:28).\n\nHe serves as the "Bestower of Spiritual Gifts" (1 Cor. 12) and the "Comforter," "Helper" and "Guide" of all saints (Jn. 14:16-17, 26; 15:26; 16:13-15; Rom. 8:26). He is the "Convicter of Sin" (Jn. 16:7-15) and the "Power of God in the Earth" (Acts 10:38; Mt. 12:28; Acts 1:8).\n\nHe's the "Great Teacher of Men" (Isa. 11:1-2; 61:1-2; Jn. 14:16-17, 26; 15:25-26; 16:7-15; 1 Cor. 2:10-12), the "Preserver of All Things" (Ps. 104:29-30), and the "Chief Witness for God on Earth" (Jn. 15:26; 16:7-15; Acts 5:32; Rom. 8:14-16). He is also the "Healer of Saints" (Rom. 8:11) and the "Character Builder" (2 Cor. 3:18; 2 Pet. 1:5-10).\n\n### 7. The Divine Character and Personal Traits of the Holy Spirit Prove Him to Be Divine\n\nAs we'll see in the next section on His personality, the Spirit's character and traits demonstrate His divine nature.\n\n## II. The Personality of the Holy Spirit\n\nIt's incredibly important that you believe not only in the divinity of the Holy Spirit but also in His personality. Only when you grasp these truths can you give Him the honor, worship, adoration, and personal respect that you give to God.\n\nHere's what you need to understand: the Holy Spirit is not a mere power for you to grab hold of and use. He is a person — infinitely wise, holy, just, and gracious — who seeks to get hold of you and use you! You need to become acquainted with Him as a person, not merely as an influence or power derived from a person.\n\nThink of it like this: you wouldn't try to "use" your best friend like a tool. You'd build a relationship with them. That's how we should approach the Holy Spirit.\n\nThe following points prove that He is a real person:\n\n> 1. Personal names are given to Him, as proven in Point I, 2, above.\n\n> 2. Personal pronouns are used of Him (Jn. 14:16-26; 15:26; 16:7-15).\n\n> 3. Personal attributes are ascribed to Him, as proven in Point I, 3, above.\n\n> 4. Personal works are ascribed to Him, as proven in Point I, 4, above.\n\n> 5. Personal references are made concerning Him, as proven in Point I, 5, above.\n\n> 6. Personal treatment is ascribed to Him.\n\nHe can be "resisted" (Acts 7:51), "tempted" (Acts 5:9), "grieved" (Eph. 4:30), "lied to" (Acts 5:3-4), "blasphemed" (Mt. 12:31-32), "insulted" (Mt. 12:31-32; Heb. 6:4-6; 10:26-29), "quenched" (1 Thess. 5:19), "vexed" (Ps. 78:40; Isa. 63:10), "quieted" (Zech 6:8), and "fellowshipped" (Phil. 2:1). He can be mistreated or obeyed like any other person.\n\nIn the Holy Spirit's relationship to people, He is spoken of as "searching hearts," "regenerating," "sanctifying," "helping," "convicting," "teaching," "quickening," "guiding," "witnessing," "interceding," "revealing," "working," "hearing," "speaking," "communing," "appointing," "commanding," "counseling," "comforting," "inspiring," "assuring," and "calling." He acts in many ways as a real person, as seen in Point I above.\n\nAs defined in Lesson Four, Point I, 5, a person is anyone who can think, feel, and act — anyone capable of self-consciousness and self-determination, any individual having legal rights and duties, a rational being with bodily presence, soul passions, and spirit faculties.\n\nIf this is not true of the Holy Spirit, given everything we've seen in the facts above, then nothing in Scripture is clear. How could the Holy Spirit do all the things spoken of Him without being a person? How could a mere impersonal force be spoken of as God, have many divine personal names, titles, offices, acts, and attributes, receive personal treatment, and be spoken of with personal pronouns? We must conclude that the Holy Spirit is a real person if we want to harmonize all Scripture.\n\n## III. The Holy Spirit Is Not the Father or the Son\n\n### 1. He Has Been Seen as a Separate Person\n\nThe Spirit has been seen with the natural eyes as a separate person from the Father and the Son (Mt. 3:16-17; Lk. 3:21-22; Jn. 1:31-34; Rev. 4:5; 5:6).\n\n### 2. The Vision in Revelation Shows Three Distinct Persons\n\nIn Rev. 1:4-6; 3:1; 4:5; 5:6, the Spirit is symbolized by seven lamps of fire, seven eyes, and seven horns "before the throne" upon which God the Father is sitting, and "upon the Lamb," which symbolizes Jesus Christ.\n\nThe Spirit could not be the person of God the Father sitting on the throne, or the Lamb who comes to the Father and takes a seven-sealed book out of His right hand. So we have three persons, each distinguished from the others: the Father on the throne, the Son symbolized by the Lamb before the throne, and the Spirit symbolized by seven lamps also before the throne.\n\nIt's similar to watching three different actors on the same stage at the same time — you'd never confuse them as the same person. The fact that Christ and the Spirit are separate symbols seen at the same time and at the same place, both before God the Father on the throne, proves they are two separate and distinct persons from each other and from the Father.\n\nA symbol stands for or represents something else. Since the Father is seen on the throne and Christ and the Spirit are symbolized by two separate beings before the throne, there must have been three separate and distinct persons involved in the scenes John saw when he arrived in Heaven (Rev. 4:1).\n\n### 3. Jesus Called Him "Another Comforter"\n\nIn Jn. 14:16-17, 26; 15:26; 16:7-15, the Holy Spirit is spoken of as "another Comforter" (Helper), who could not be sent until Christ had gone back to Heaven and was glorified (Jn. 7:37-39; Acts 2:33-36). He would then be sent as a separate person from the Father and the Son.\n\nThe Greek word "allos," like the English "another," means "another of the same kind, but different from," "not the same one," "distinct from another," and "one more." This is proven everywhere the word is used (Mt. 2:12; 8:9; 10:23; 13:24, 31, 33; 21:33; 26:7). Otherwise the passages wouldn't make sense.\n\nCommon sense tells us that when the word "another" is used, it means "two or more." It's used of the Father as being another from the Son (Jn. 5:32). If the Spirit is another from the Son who promised Him, and another from the Father who sent Him, and if the Father was another from the Son, there must be three distinct persons in the Godhead — and all three can be called "God." All three persons are distinguished from each other by the word "another" in Jn. 5:32; 14:16.\n\n### 4. They Have Separate Names\n\nA clear distinction is made between "the name of the Father" and "of the Son" and "of the Holy Ghost" (Mt. 28:19). All three have separate and personal names by which they are known, as is clear from this passage and many others.\n\n### 5. Jesus Prayed for Another Comforter to Come\n\nA clear distinction is made between the Son who prays, the Father to whom He prays, and "another Comforter" for whom He prays. This Comforter was given in answer to prayer and came from the Father and the Son as our "Helper" (Jn. 14:16).\n\n### 6. Jesus Left, Then the Spirit Came\n\nA clear distinction is made between Jesus who went away as one distinct person (Acts 1:11) and the Holy Ghost who came to take His place as "another" distinct person (Jn. 14:16-17, 26; 15:26; 16:7-15).\n\n### 7. Three Distinct Locations\n\nA clear distinction is made between the Son who is exalted at the right hand of the Father, the Father who is on the left hand of the Son, and the Holy Ghost who is sent from the Father and the Son to take the place of Jesus among people (Acts 2:33-36; 7:56-59; Jn. 14:16-17, 26; 15:26; 16:7-15; Rom. 8:34; Eph. 1:20; Col. 3:1; Heb. 1:3; 8:1; 12:2).\n\n### 8. Different Timing of Their Giving\n\nA clear distinction is made between the Son who was already given (Lk. 1:35; Jn. 3:16) and the Holy Ghost who was not yet given before Jesus was glorified (Jn. 7:37-39; Acts 2:33-36; 5:31).\n\n### 9. The Spirit and the Child Were Distinct at Jesus' Conception\n\nA clear distinction is made between the Holy Ghost that came upon Mary and the child that was born of Mary by the Holy Ghost (Mt. 1:18-25; Lk. 1:32-35).\n\n### 10. Blasphemy Against Them Has Different Consequences\n\nA clear distinction is made between the Son who can be blasphemed with forgiveness possible, and the Holy Ghost who cannot be blasphemed with forgiveness (Mt. 12:31-32; Mk. 3:29-30; Lk. 12:10). If the Son and Holy Ghost were not two distinct persons, they could not be blasphemed with different results.\n\nA third person, the Father, must be understood in such forgiveness, for it is the Father who forgives people as the head of the Godhead (1 Cor. 11:3; Mt. 6:9-15; 18:35; Eph. 4:32).\n\n### 11. Jesus Was in Mary's Womb; the Spirit Filled Others\n\nA clear distinction is made between Jesus who was bodily in Mary's womb and the Holy Ghost who was not bodily in Mary's womb, and who filled others (Lk. 1:15, 39-41, 67-79).\n\n### 12. At Pentecost, Jesus Was in Heaven While the Spirit Filled People on Earth\n\nA clear distinction is made between Jesus outside of the womb of Mary and the Holy Ghost who filled and baptized Mary thirty-three years later at Pentecost (Acts 1:14; 2:1-4).\n\nThe same distinction is made in the case of disciples at Pentecost: The Holy Ghost came and filled and baptized them while the Son was at that time "exalted at the right hand of the Father" in Heaven (Acts 2:1-4, 33-36). The same distinction is clear with Stephen (Acts 7:56-59), Paul (Acts 9:17), and others who were filled and baptized in the Holy Ghost when Jesus was in Heaven at the right hand of God (Rom. 8:34; Eph. 1:20; Heb. 1:3).\n\n### 13. The Samaritans Had Received Jesus but Not Yet the Spirit\n\nA clear distinction is made between Jesus whom the Samaritans had received and the Holy Ghost whom they had not yet received (Acts 8:5-25).\n\n### 14. Jesus Was Once Powerless Until the Spirit Anointed Him\n\nA clear distinction is made between Jesus who was once powerless to do miracles and the Holy Ghost who anointed Him at thirty years of age to do miracles (Jn. 2:11; Acts 10:38; Isa. 11:1-2; 42:1-5; 61:1-2; Lk. 4:18-21; Mt. 3:16-17).\n\n### 15. Three Distinct Roles in the Anointing\n\nA clear distinction is also made between the Son who was "anointed," the Father who sent the Spirit to anoint Him, and the Holy Ghost Himself who did the anointing (Mt. 3:16-17; Acts 10:38; Isa. 11:1-2; 42:1-5; 61:1-2; Lk. 4:18-21).\n\n### 16. The Spirit Glorifies Christ, Not Himself\n\nThe Holy Ghost is distinguished from Christ by the fact that Jesus said, "He shall not speak of himself," but "He shall glorify me" (Jn. 16:13-15).\n\n## IV. The Holy Ghost Has a Personal Spirit-Body\n\nAs we've seen in Lesson Four, God has a personal body, soul, and spirit like humans do. We've established that there are three distinct persons in the Godhead, all called "God." If God has a body and there are three distinct persons in the Godhead, then each person naturally has a personal body, soul, and spirit, just as each human being does.\n\nEven if Scripture said nothing more about them having bodies, our intelligence and reason would convince us they do. No person can exist without a body or a shape.\n\nPicture it this way: even demons, who are classed as disembodied spirits, have shapes and forms. The inner person of each human being has a shape and form that is tangible and real. It can wear clothes, eat, feel, know, and do everything out of the body that it could do while in the human body, as we proved in Lesson Four, Point II, 7.\n\nDisembodied spirits all had outer forms or bodies at one time when they were first created. Paul argues in 1 Cor. 15:35-50 that all things in creation have bodies: bodies for human beings, fish, birds, beasts, sun, moon, and stars; heavenly bodies and earthly bodies; natural bodies and spiritual bodies. No person was ever without a body in a normal creative state.\n\nShould we believe that God alone of all beings in the universe is the only real person without a body or shape? Should we believe He is a disembodied Spirit? Should we believe He is not as real as other beings? There's no scriptural basis for such ideas, so we should forget them.\n\nIf the fact is revealed that there are three separate distinct beings in the Godhead, this would be sufficient to conclude that each of them has separate bodies, souls, and spirits, like all other separate and distinct beings. Even disembodied spirits are separate and distinct from each other and can be numbered like all other beings.\n\nShould we conclude that only one member of the Godhead has a body, soul, and spirit, and the other two persons are bodiless without souls and spirits? That would mean there's only one person. But since there are three persons entirely separate and distinct from each other, it's only reasonable that each of them is the same in substance and nature, and that they all have had from eternity the same kind of spirit-bodies, soul passions, and spirit-faculties. Scripture says nothing to the contrary.\n\nIn fact, two and three persons have been seen with separate bodies at the same time and at the same place by people.\n\nDaniel saw two of them with separate bodies at the same time and place (Dan. 7:9-14). Stephen saw two of them at the same place (Acts 7:56-59). Others saw different members of the Godhead at different times and places, and every time any one of them was seen, He appeared in a real body. See Lesson Four, Point II, 3, 7, 8, and 9 for proof that God has a body, soul, and spirit! In Lesson Twenty-seven we'll study many plain statements of three separate and distinct persons in the Godhead.\n\nIf these facts are true, then it's only logical and scriptural to understand each of the three persons in the Godhead as having a personal spirit-body, soul, and spirit like all other persons in existence. If they are separate and distinct persons, then each one would have to have His own personality, spirit-body, soul, spirit, and His own individuality in every sense required of any other person in existence.\n\nIf we spoke of three persons among angels or people and described the body, soul, and spirit of only one of them, it would be clearly understood that the other two were similar to the one described. All persons of like nature, powers, attributes, and works are naturally the same regardless of how many exist. The members of the Godhead are exactly the same in every sense and have been from all eternity, so if one of them had a body by nature, then all of them had spirit-bodies exactly the same — until one of them took a human body to redeem us.\n\nTo be more specific: all angels have like spirit-bodies, souls, and spirits; all people have the same kind of bodies, souls, and spirits; all animals of the same species have the same likeness; and all demons are similar. Every person or thing in existence is similar to all other persons and things of the same nature and essence.\n\nSo it is with God. All separate persons in the Godhead are the same in essence. They were the same in body, soul, and spirit until Christ became a man. If one has a personal body, they all have bodies; if one has a personal soul, they all have souls; if one has a personal spirit, they all have spirits. On the other hand, if no one of them has a personal body, soul, and spirit, then none of them do.\n\nWe cannot think of the deity as existing without personality, without body, without soul, without spirit, without form and shape, and without all the bodily parts, soul passions, and spirit faculties that the Bible teaches. If we don't believe what the Bible says about God, let's be frank and say that the Bible is plainly wrong in hundreds of places and we don't know what to believe. Let's say that God doesn't know enough about Himself to know what to say about Himself, and that He doesn't know human language well enough to make Himself clear. Let's throw the Bible away and live without any fear of ever meeting anyone who is real and who will someday judge us. If God is not real, then we will never stand before Him to be judged.\n\nShould we take this attitude toward God and His Word? If not, then let's come to our senses and give God credit for being able to use human language and reveal Himself to us in plain language. Let's throw away all the foolish and unscriptural theories about God and believe the wonderful truths plainly revealed in plain language in the Bible, as we have seen in Lessons Four, Twenty-one, and in this lesson.\n\nNot one of the plain facts in Points I to III above could possibly be understood if we don't consider the Holy Spirit as a real person with a spirit-body, soul, and spirit, like the Father has. If personal names, attributes, works, offices, characteristics, treatment, personal pronouns, personal references, and descriptions of a person are used of the Holy Spirit, then He must be recognized as a real person with a spirit-body, soul, and spirit.\n\nIf He is distinct from both the Father and the Son (as proven in Point III above), then He's bound to have a separate spirit-body, soul, and spirit from either the Father or the Son. The same Scriptures that prove one person of the Godhead has a personal body, soul, and spirit will prove that each of the three separate and distinct members of deity also has them.\n\nThe following points prove that the Holy Ghost has a spirit-body:\n\n1. He is distinctly called God in Acts 5:3-4. God has a body, as we proved in Lesson Four, Point II, 1-9.\n\n2. The personal names given to the Holy Spirit prove that He has a body. Personal names are never given to an abstract power or an influence belonging to some person.\n\n3. The divine attributes — which are faculties of a real person — prove the Holy Spirit to be a real person. He wouldn't have these personal attributes if He weren't a person. He couldn't be a person without bodily parts through which these personal powers are manifested. He would have to have a body, or He couldn't manifest Himself and His personal powers in the material world.\n\nFor example, how could He be present if there's nothing about Him to make Himself known? How could anyone tell He's present if He's incapable of manifesting His presence? How could He move upon the face of the waters if there's nothing to move, as required in Gen. 1:2; Ps. 104:30? How could He manifest His power if He's incapable of free and independent choice in doing so, or if He were a mere influence? Do influences have power of choice and responsibility?\n\nHow could He search and know the things of God and impart that knowledge to others if He were a mere power of another person? How could He prophesy or know what to predict if He weren't a real person, and how could He be such a person without powers of visible manifestation? How could He have will power, mind, intelligence, choice, judgment, fear, power, decision, authority, hearing, speech, unselfishness, and other attributes and powers if He's not a real person having a spirit-body like angels and other spirit-beings?\n\n4. The divine personal acts of the Holy Spirit, which require real bodily action, prove that He has a body. The Spirit has been the direct power of operation and the agent of God in creating all things, directing gospel work, revealing and inspiring Scrip\n\n---\n\nThe Holy Spirit is not a spiritual atmosphere you occasionally access — He is a Person who lives in every believer and is available for every moment of every day. The question is not whether He's present. The question is whether you're responding to His presence. So here's what to consider: When you make decisions, read Scripture, face temptation, or need wisdom — do you actually and consciously consult the Person who lives inside you? Or are you functionally living as if you're alone in your own body?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsih000h18pfg4iaqb8t	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Eating Disorders	READING	\N	45	\N	t	![Eating Disorders](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsgZbcyhax52U6tuomWf38j1QMHRBV4griYbAZ)\n\n## Eating Disorders\n\nShe had been to six dieticians, three therapists, and two Christian counselors. She had done CBT, DBT, and EMDR. She had been hospitalized twice. She had been in recovery and relapsed three times in eight years. Each professional told her something true about the psychological dimensions of her illness — the control, the perfectionism, the distorted body image, the family-of-origin patterns.\n\nNone of them had ever addressed the spiritual dimension. Not because they were incompetent — because the category was outside their framework. When a deliverance minister finally asked her to describe the voice that told her she was too large, she described it with striking specificity: its tone, its timing, its particular cruelty. It was not her inner critic. It had a character. She had been dialoguing with a demonic entity for eight years and calling it her eating disorder.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nEating disorders — anorexia, bulimia, binge eating, and orthorexia — are psychiatric conditions characterized by distorted body image and self-destructive eating patterns. They affect millions worldwide, with the highest prevalence among adolescent and young adult women. The medical, psychological, and cultural dimensions of eating disorders are real and well-documented.\n\nThey are also, for many sufferers, spiritually significant in ways that psychological models alone cannot account for.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe Spirit of Death operates through eating disorders by using the sufferer's own body as the instrument of destruction. The deception is in the frame: the eating disorder presents itself as the sufferer's own psychology — their perfectionism, their anxiety, their relationship with control — rather than as an external entity with an agenda. The voice that says you are too large, too flawed, too deserving of punishment — most sufferers experience it as their own thought. It is not always their own thought.\n\n[Psalm 139:14](data-scripture="Psalm 139:14"): *"I will praise thee; for I am fearfully and wonderfully made: marvellous are thy works."* The eating disorder's central lie is a direct refutation of this verse. The body God made is not enough. The body God made is wrong. The body God made requires punishment. These are not psychological distortions alone — they are demonic accusations against God's craftsmanship.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Eating disorders frequently coexist with other forms of spiritual bondage** — self-harm, occult involvement, sexual abuse — indicating a cluster of demonic strongholds operating in the same person. The eating disorder is rarely the only entry point. It is usually one front in a larger campaign.\n\n**Ritualistic food behaviors create spiritual strongholds.** The secrecy, the precise routines, the specific obsessions — counting, measuring, purging — mirror occult ritual. Behavior that is ritualized and secret creates a spiritual architecture that the enemy inhabits.\n\n**The Spirit of Accusation drives the perfectionism.** Many eating disorder sufferers experience a relentless inner prosecution — a voice that provides a running critique of every food choice, every deviation from the disordered rules, every moment of perceived weakness. This voice is demonically driven. The Spirit of Accusation (see Part III of this course, Lesson 10) uses the eating disorder as its primary platform.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nDo not move past this lesson without answering the question this course has been building toward since the opening lesson of Part VII: *Is what I'm calling my eating disorder entirely my own psychology — or has something been speaking to me?*\n\nThis is not a question to answer theoretically. Close your eyes and listen. You know the voice. You have heard it today — this morning, possibly this hour. It has a tone. It has a timing. It has specific targets: specific foods, specific numbers, specific parts of your body it returns to. It has a history of being there when the actual circumstances do not explain the intensity of the accusation.\n\nThat is not your inner critic. Inner critics are boring. They repeat generic anxieties. What eating disorder sufferers describe is something more organized, more targeted, more relentless — and more specifically cruel than random psychological noise.\n\nName what you are dealing with:\n\n**The Spirit of Death.** It has an assignment against your body. The eating disorder is its current instrument. The destination it has been working toward — the escalation you have felt even when you wanted to stop, the threshold that keeps lowering — has a name.\n\n**The Spirit of Accusation.** [Revelation 12:10](data-scripture="Revelation 12:10"). It runs the prosecution that tells you the body is wrong, insufficient, requiring punishment, undeserving of nourishment. That voice is a demonic entity's speech, not your own thought.\n\nNow act:\n\nRenounce the Spirit of Death's legal claim over your body — specifically, by name, aloud. Renounce the Spirit of Accusation and every specific accusation it has spoken over your body, naming the accusations you can remember. Plead the blood of Jesus Christ over your body's relationship with food, with weight, with hunger, with the mirror.\n\nThen pursue medical treatment simultaneously — not as an alternative to this prayer, but because the spiritual and physiological dimensions are both real and both need to be addressed. The supernatural and the clinical are not competing for the same problem. They are addressing different layers of the same attack.\n\nThe question you cannot skip: *Have you told your doctor and your pastor the whole truth?* If the answer to either is no, that changes this week.\n\n---\n\n*Eating disorders destroy the body through accusation and ritual. The final lessons in this course look outward — to the systemic and cultural forces that are preparing the world for its last and greatest deception.*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk4br002cewhj6i46nvbz	cmnknk4bp001qewhjk5bcqnfj	Lesson 51 — The New Heaven and the New Earth	READING	3485	21	\N	t	After the Millennium, after the Great White Throne, after the last rebel has been confined and the universe purged of sin — what comes next? The most Scripture-neglected subject in all of eschatology: the eternal state. Most Christians think of eternity as an endless worship service in a spiritual realm with no clear content. But Revelation 21-22 describes a physical city descending from heaven, a river, trees, nations, kings — a real place where real people live in real bodies doing real things forever.\n\nLast time we saw Christ's Millennial reign on earth — 1,000 years of direct divine government. Now we arrive at the final destination: not the Millennium, but the eternal state that follows it — the New Heaven, the New Earth, and the New Jerusalem.\n\nLet's explore together one of the most breathtaking visions in all of Scripture — the eternal state that God has planned for His creation. We're talking about the Age of Ages, an endless succession of ages stretching into forever. This is when the Earth enters its third perfect state, a sinless career under the leadership of redeemed rulers across countless generations.\n\n---\n\n![Lesson 51 — The New Heaven and the New Earth](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsobRPDwWxwEUd728la9hHriMsfOkGYRKDCuLZ)\n\n## I. The Dispensation of the Redeemed\n\nThroughout our studies, we've traced God's seven dispensational periods — His different ways of dealing with fallen humanity. And what stands out in every single one is God's incredible patience and mercy. He's "not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance" (2 Pet. 3:9).\n\nHere's what God has been doing: He's been testing humanity under every possible condition before the final restoration of all things. Why? To demonstrate that He's completely just in requiring all free wills to submit to Him — because that's the only path to eternal security and true happiness.\n\nThink of it like a parent who lets a stubborn child try things their own way, knowing they'll eventually learn that Mom and Dad were right all along. God has given humanity plenty of time to learn that we're failures apart from His grace and help.\n\nAfter the Millennium, God will usher in this new eternal perfect state for the benefit of all generations to come. By that point, it will be the right time in His plan to destroy all rebels, sin, and death — and to remove the curse entirely. His plan is to take everyone who has willingly submitted to Him, everyone whose will has been purged of any possibility of rebellion through grace, and restore them to that original purpose: replenishing the Earth and subduing it, just like before the Fall.\n\nSo you see, the fall of humanity didn't derail God's eternal plan — it just delayed it. By the end of the Millennium, God will have used the Fall and all His dispensational dealings to actually advance and perfect His plan. Countless people will have been redeemed and glorified as immortal beings to help administer the affairs of the universe and rule over coming generations.\n\nHere's the beautiful part: humanity will no longer be on probation. The testing will be complete. Those who've proven themselves faithful will be ready for an eternal state where they'll continue living faithfully to God forever.\n\nWe can call this age "The Dispensation of the Redeemed" because Earth's government will be administered by the redeemed — and it will succeed forever. No more dispensational failures. Both the redeemed and natural humanity will have been purged of any possibility of failure.\n\n---\n\n## II. The New Heaven and the New Earth (Rev. 21:1–22:5)\n\n**(End of the Earth's Second Sinful Career — the Earth Made Perfect the Third Time)**\n\nThe New Heaven and New Earth are the result of the renovation by fire described in 2 Pet. 3:10-13. When the old sinful order on Earth is destroyed, that renovation will mark the last time in all eternity that any part of the universe will be marred by sin and rebellion.\n\nNow, we can't know everything about the eternal perfect state. But there are dozens of Scriptures that speak about eternal things! If we're willing to believe what's plainly written, we can know quite a bit about what's coming. But if we reject what's clearly stated, we'll remain in ignorance by our own choice.\n\nIf we believe the Bible is God's Word, then we can certainly take Him at His Word when He speaks in passage after passage about eternal conditions on this Earth. The studies that follow will help you gain a fuller understanding of our eternal future. We'll focus on eternal events not covered in our previous lessons on the Millennium and the renovation of the Earth. It would be helpful to review those lessons before diving in.\n\n---\n\n## III. New Lands (Rev. 21:1)\n\n> "And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away; and there was no more sea."\n\nDoes this mean there will be no water on Earth after the renovation? Not at all! Many other passages make this clear. This verse is describing the great change that will happen to the large oceans — the ones covering about three-fourths of the Earth today.\n\nHere's what will happen: those massive oceans will be evaporated by the "fervent heat" during the Earth's renovation. The waters that fell from the heavens and came up from the deep to cover the Earth during the chaos of Gen. 1:2 will return to the heavens and the deep places within the Earth. The Earth will be renewed to its original state — as it was before Lucifer fell, before the first rebellion.\n\nBut there will still be an abundance of rivers, lakes, and smaller seas on Earth forever. Let me show you the evidence:\n\n> 1. Seas and islands are specifically mentioned in the eternal reign of the Messiah (Ps. 72:8-10, 17; 97:1-6; Isa. 42:4, 10-12; 66:19-21; Zech. 9:10; Ezek. 47:1-23).\n\n> 2. Rivers are mentioned too (Ezek. 47:1-12, 18-20; Zech. 9:10; 14:8; Rev. 22:1-3).\n\n> 3. Some seas were originally created with the Earth to be eternal — they'll last as long as Israel, the sun, moon, and Earth itself (Jer. 5:22; 31:35, 36; Ps. 146:6; Prov. 8:29; Acts 4:24; 14:15; Rev. 14:7).\n\n> 4. Abundant water will be necessary to fulfill prophecies about fruitful seasons and waters springing up in the desert (Gen. 8:22; Isa. 35; Amos 5:8; 9:6; Job 38:4-16, 22-30; Ps. 104:5-14, 24-28).\n\nPicture it this way: when those enormous oceans evaporate, millions of square miles of new land will be reclaimed and made habitable for the generations of natural people yet to come. It's like gaining entire continents of living space!\n\n---\n\n## IV. The New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:2–22:4)\n\nThe next thing John saw in his vision was absolutely stunning: the Holy City, New Jerusalem, coming down from God out of Heaven to take its eternal place on the New Earth. Let's walk through everything Scripture tells us about this incredible city — its names, age, source, preparation, location, measurements, appearance, materials, walls, foundations, buildings, lighting, water system, traffic patterns, restrictions, food, inhabitants, and rulers.\n\n### 1. The Names of the City (Rev. 3:12; 21:2; 9-10; Jn. 14:1-3; Heb. 12:22-23)\n\nThe city goes by many names, and each one reveals something significant about the capital of the universe:\n\n> **(1) The New Jerusalem** (Rev. 3:12; 21:2). The word "New" simply means the city is kept fresh, clean, pure, and new in appearance by God's very presence.\n\n> **(2) The Holy City** (Rev. 21:2; 22:19). "Holy" tells us it's a pure, clean city consecrated to God's holiness and to all the social systems of the universe.\n\n> **(3) The Bride, the Lamb's Wife** (Rev. 21:2, 19-20). It's called this because the city will be the eternal home of all the redeemed, where they'll live in eternal union with God, Christ, the Holy Spirit, and faithful angels. The redeemed inhabitants have been purchased by Christ's blood. They become part of that city through His redemption. All the redeemed are united to Christ and are spoken of as being married to Him even now, as we'll see in our next lesson.\n\n> **(4) The Tabernacle of God** (Rev. 13:6; 15:5; 21:3). This name fits because it's where God's throne is located — it's where He personally lives and reigns.\n\n> **(5) The Great City** (Rev. 21:10). This name is earned! It's the largest, most magnificent, most wonderful city in all creation. It's great because it's the universal capital of the Great God.\n\n> **(6) The Holy Jerusalem** (Rev. 21:10). This emphasizes again the absolute purity and holiness of God's city.\n\n> **(7) The Heavenly Jerusalem** (Heb. 12:22-23). This name highlights that the city is in Heaven — it's a heavenly city, not an earthly one. There's a heavenly Jerusalem and an earthly Jerusalem. The earthly Jerusalem will be Christ's headquarters for His reign on Earth and the seat of world government. But the heavenly Jerusalem is the capital of the entire universe. Paul speaks of "the Jerusalem that is above" as being free and "the mother of us all" — meaning we're all born again by God who lives and reigns in the Heavenly Jerusalem (Gal. 4:19-31).\n\n> **(8) The City of the Living God** (Heb. 12:22-23). This expresses the truth that the New Jerusalem belongs to God, the Living God, who owns it along with all other parts of His vast creation.\n\n> **(9) My Father's House** (Jn. 14:1-3). Jesus Himself calls the New Jerusalem "my Father's house." He speaks of it as containing many mansions. And it's not just mansions — there are streets, fountains of water, rivers, furniture, and all the material things that make the city a real place for real people to live, just as much as any city on Earth.\n\nNow, some Bible students argue there's no real city with mansions in Heaven. They claim the saints themselves are the mansions Jesus mentioned. They can't seem to accept a real material city with streets, homes, fountains, and everything else that makes for real life.\n\nBut the Bible is crystal clear on this! If people don't want to believe what it says, they'll simply have to remain in ignorance. As Paul puts it, "If any man be ignorant, let him be ignorant" (1 Cor. 14:38).\n\nAs we saw in an earlier lesson, Heaven is a real place, a real country, a real planet, and a material land just like Earth. Nearly all of Rev. 21-22 pictures the reality of Heaven and the New Jerusalem with many concrete details.\n\nI once knew a brilliant young preacher who seemed destined to make a mark for God. He was rising high in religious circles. But he had one fault: he became too worldly-wise to believe the simple, literal statements of Scripture. He started reasoning that the Bible was purely spiritual, heavenly, and symbolic.\n\nOnce, in a discussion about the New Jerusalem and the mansions in Heaven, he insisted that the mansions were the saints and the city was just symbolic of the Church. There was no way to reason with him because we had no common ground. When one person believes the simplicity of the Bible and another rejects taking it literally, agreement becomes impossible.\n\nThis young man went east and achieved great success in church circles, largely because most church members have been taught that the more mysterious and spiritualized the Bible becomes, the more receptive they should be.\n\nOne day I read in a religious paper that this young man had died. His wife described how, on his deathbed, he saw the most beautiful city he was about to enter. He described it in detail. I said to my wife, "It's too bad that men have to die before they get sense enough to believe the Bible." This minister became a believer in the Bible's literalness in his dying hours — when he could have believed it his whole life and been a far greater blessing to others.\n\nThink about how ridiculous it is to argue that the saints are the mansions Jesus spoke about. Let's read Jn. 14:1-3 the way these teachers would have us understand it:\n\n> "In my Father's house [the Father Himself] are many mansions [saints]: if it were not so, I would have told you [mansions]. I go to prepare a place [saints] for you [mansions]. And if I go and prepare a place [saints] for you [mansions], I will come again, and receive you [mansions] unto myself; that where I am, there ye [mansions] may be also."\n\nDoes that make any sense? Absolutely not!\n\nIt would be equally foolish to make the New Jerusalem a symbol of the Church. Imagine reading everything in Rev. 21-22 as symbolizing the Church. What could walls, gates, foundations, streets, a river, trees of life, and all the city's details possibly symbolize? You might as well throw the Bible away and give up any hope of understanding it if you're going to eliminate the plain, literal, sensible meaning of what's clearly written.\n\nA God who couldn't make Himself clear in human language so we can believe what He says would be no God at all. You can't hold that distorted view of God and the Bible while claiming to have a clear understanding of truth.\n\nOn the other hand, how wonderfully clear everything in Scripture becomes when we understand it the same way we would any other book! The description of the New Jerusalem is far too detailed to spiritualize away. So let's be sensible and take the Bible as it was meant to be read.\n\nIf God says there's a real city in Heaven, let's believe He knows what He's talking about. He should know whether there's a city or not — He made all things and He lives in Heaven! If we can't believe Him on this, we can't believe Him on anything. Rejecting anything God says makes Him out to be a liar and unreliable on every other question too.\n\n### 2. The Source and Origin of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 3:12; 21:2, 10; Jn. 14:1-3; Gal. 4:26; Heb. 9:11; 11:10-16; 12:22)\n\nThese passages reveal that God is the Architect, Builder, and Owner of the Holy City. Right now it's in Heaven, but after the Millennium it will be moved to Earth. The city is prepared as the home for the redeemed of all ages.\n\nThe city had its beginning in God's mind sometime in the dateless past. When it was originally created, we don't know — speculation is pointless. What we do know is that it's a real city, built by God, and it will always be His capital city.\n\n### 3. The Preparation of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:2; Jn. 14:1-3; Heb. 11:10-16; 13:14)\n\nThese passages tell us that the saints will have a part in the Holy City and that such a place is now being prepared for them. This fact alone proves that the saints are not the mansions or the city! Jesus promised He was going away to prepare a place for the saints in His Father's house.\n\nPaul stated that all the Old Testament saints and present-day Church saints were not the city — they were looking forward to becoming part of it (Heb. 11:8-16; 13:14). This is definite proof. You can't look for a city to become part of it while simultaneously being that city.\n\n### 4. The Eternal Location of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 3:12; 21:2, 9-10, 24-26; 22:1-5)\n\nThese passages tell us the Holy City will be transplanted from Heaven to Earth after the Millennium to dwell among men forever. Its eternal location will be right here on Earth.\n\n### 5. The Outward Appearance of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:11)\n\nLet me paint you a picture of this breathtaking city:\n\n- Adorned as a bride prepared for her husband\n- Radiant with the glory of God\n- Like a precious stone, clear as crystal\n- Surrounded by a jasper wall about 300 feet high\n- Twelve massive pearl gates inscribed with the names of Israel's twelve tribes\n- Twelve angels stationed at each of the great gates, which never close day or night\n- Square in shape with three gates on each side\n- Twelve foundations bearing the names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb\n- 1,500 miles square and 1,500 miles high\n- Foundations adorned with every kind of precious stone\n- Streets of gold like transparent glass\n- Rivers, trees, fountains of water\n- Illuminated by the glory of God Himself\n- The city itself made of pure gold, like clear glass\n\nHere's something important to understand: the city is not a cube. A wall around a cube that's already 1,500 miles high on all sides would serve no purpose! From all the statements in Scripture, it's clear the city is a series of mountain peaks — beginning as low foothills inside the walls and rising higher and higher until the tallest peak reaches 1,500 miles high.\n\nOn that highest peak sits the heavenly tabernacle, the capital building where God rules as the Supreme Moral Governor of the Universe. It was after the patterns of this tabernacle that Moses built his earthly version (Heb. 8:5; 9:23). Scattered across the mountains and through the valleys are the many mansions of Jn. 14:1-3. Living fountains spring up throughout the city, and rivers of water, clear as crystal, flow through it.\n\nThe floor of the throne room itself is like a sea of glass, clear as crystal, and it's immense — large enough to contain the countless multitude of tribulation saints described in Rev. 7:9-17; 15:2-4. There's also a massive banquet hall where the Marriage Supper of the Lamb and other grand feasts will be held throughout eternity.\n\nThese facts prove that Heaven is a real planet and the New Jerusalem is a real city. We can't fully grasp the greatness and grandeur of Heaven and the universe's capital city, but Scripture gives us enough to understand this: there will be a real life in the most perfect environment possible for all who love God and follow His plan in this life.\n\n### 6. The Walls, Gates, and Foundations of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:12-14; Heb. 11:10-26)\n\nThe walls stand 144 cubits high — about 300 feet if we take a cubit as 25 inches. The gates are solid pearls, and the foundations are adorned with the most precious stones in all creation.\n\nThe city must rest on the ground — there would be no need for foundations if it were floating in the air. The gates stand open day and night so people from the nations on Earth can come and go (Rev. 21:23-27).\n\n### 7. The Measurements of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:15-17)\n\nThe city measures 1,500 miles square and 1,500 miles high, with a 300-foot wall all around it. It's foursquare at the base and rises like a series of mountain peaks.\n\nThe New Jerusalem site in Heaven is called Mount Zion in Heb. 12:22-23 and Rev. 14:1. This likely refers to the highest mountain peak where the capitol building stands.\n\n### 8. The Materials of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:10-21)\n\nThe building materials are gold and precious stones of every kind.\n\n### 9. The Age of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:2)\n\nIt's called "new" (the Greek word *kainos* — "new in freshness and character," not *neos*, "new in age") because it's kept perpetually fresh and new by God's very presence.\n\nThe city's actual age is unknown. It might have been created alongside Heaven and Earth. It has been the location of God's throne ever since Heaven was created (Ps. 11:4; 93:2; 103:19; Isa. 6:1; 14:12-14; 66:1; Rev. 4:2-10; 5:1-13; 7:9-17; 8:3; 22:1-3). It existed when humanity was created — all the saints from Abel onward have looked for it (Heb. 11:8-16; 13:14).\n\n### 10. The Streets of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:21)\n\nThe singular "street" in this passage doesn't mean there's only one street — any more than the same wording in Rev. 11:8 means Jerusalem has only one street.\n\nThere are at least twelve great boulevards in the city because there are twelve great gates, and people pass through those gates into the city. John is simply describing one street so we can understand what all the rest are like. They're all made of pure gold, transparent and clear as glass.\n\n### 11. The Buildings of the New Jerusalem (Jn. 14:1-3; Rev. 3:12; 7:15; 11:19; 14:15, 17; 15:1-8; 16:1, 17)\n\nJohn's statement in Rev. 21:22, "I saw no temple therein: for the Lord God Almighty and the Lamb are the temple of it," can't possibly mean there's no literal temple in the New Jerusalem — because there clearly is one, as shown in the passages above.\n\nThe meaning is this: no material temple or shrine will exist as an object of worship, or a place for pilgrimages, or a building people must enter to worship. Instead, all people will worship God and the Lamb in Spirit and in truth — they themselves are the true sanctuary and objects of worship.\n\n### 12. The Light of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:23, 25; 22:5)\n\nThe city's light will surpass the sun, moon, and stars. We've seen that during the Millennium the light of the sun and moon will be increased (Isa. 30:26). So if God's glory outshines even that enhanced light, it will be beyond words!\n\nThese passages don't teach that the sun and moon won't shine — just that in this particular city there's no need for them because there's a greater light: God's glory. The passages also don't mean there won't be sun and moon elsewhere on Earth. They will shine forever, and day and night will continue (Gen. 8:22; Ps. 89:2-3, 29, 35, 37; Jer. 31:35-36).\n\nThis light will radiate from God's throne on the highest peak — 1,500 miles up — and illuminate the entire city below. It's beyond imagination to picture how dazzling that light will be, shining on a city of transparent gold decked with every kind of precious stone and pearl!\n\nWhether this glory will be the full brightness that God currently dwells in (1 Tim. 6:16) isn't clear, but it will be brighter than the brightest sunlight possible (Rev. 21:23-25).\n\n### 13. The Water of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 22:1)\n\nThe city will have abundant water. Twelve great rivers will flow from God's great throne, 1,500 miles high, down through the middle of the twelve great boulevards to the base of the city and out into different parts of the Earth.\n\nBeyond these rivers, there will be countless living fountains and smaller streams throughout the city. Every mansion will likely have its own water system springing up perpetually.\n\nImagine the beauty of God's glory shining on these living fountains and rivers (Rev. 7:17; 14:7; 22:1)! From the midst of the fountains, gorgeous colors will appear in God's glory like rainbows on Earth.\n\n### 14. The Inhabitants of the New Jerusalem (Jn. 14:1-3; Heb. 11:10-16; 12:22; 13:14; Rev. 3:12; 12:12; 13:5; 21:2-5, 9; 22:3-4)\n\nThese passages show us who will live in the city: God, Christ, the Holy Spirit, angels, redeemed glorified saints, seraphim, cherubim, and other heavenly beings. Earthly natural people won't live in the city — they'll simply visit for commerce, as we'll see below.\n\nThe city is called "the bride, the Lamb's wife" because it's prepared for the glorified saints and faithful angels as their eternal home.\n\n### 15. The Traffic in the New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:24-27)\n\nNatural people from the nations — those who live through the Millennium and don't rebel with Satan at its end — will enter the New Earth to plant, harvest, build, multiply, and replenish the Earth, just as Adam's descendants would have done if they hadn't fallen.\n\nThese people will do business in the New Jerusalem, walk in its light, and their kings will bring the glory and honor of the nations into it forever.\n\n### 16. The Food of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 2:7, 17; 19:1-10; 22:2; Ps. 78:25; Lk. 22:15-18, 28-30)\n\nYes, even glorified saints will eat in the next life! The overcomer is promised "the tree of life," "the hidden manna," "the fruit of the vine," and "the Passover Lamb" in the life to come.\n\nThe inhabitants of the New Jerusalem will "eat and drink" at Christ's table in His kingdom and enjoy foods they've never experienced in this world.\n\nPicture this: rows of trees of life stretching 1,500 miles long on both sides of the twelve great rivers running through the twelve great boulevards. The trees of life bear twelve kinds of fruit, and their leaves will preserve natural life for the peoples of the natural nations throughout all the eternal generations to come. Beyond this, there will be abundant fruit from trees throughout the entire Earth (Ezek. 47:1-12).\n\n### 17. Restrictions of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 21:27; 22:14-15)\n\nNo dogs, sorcerers, sexually immoral people, murderers, idolaters, liars, or anything defiling will ever enter the city — only those written in the Lamb's Book of Life, those who enter the New Earth from the Millennial Age, and those born throughout eternity.\n\n### 18. Rulers of the New Jerusalem (Rev. 22:3-5)\n\nThe Great God, His Son, and the Spirit will rule from this city over the entire universe and all the free moral agents within it.\n\n---\n\n## V. The New Peoples (Rev. 21:3-4, 24-26)\n\nHere's something that surprises many people: there will be natural humans on this Earth forever, and natural life will continue throughout all eternity exactly as God intended when He created it. Let me walk you through the evidence:\n\n**1.** In Isa. 66:22-24, God assures Israel they'll be an earthly people forever:\n\n> "For as the new heavens and the new earth, which I will make, shall remain before me, saith the Lord, so shall your seed and your name remain."\n\nThe Hebrew word for "seed" is *Zera*, meaning "seed, fruit, plant, or posterity." It's used 273 times in the Old Testament, and every single time it means natural seed — whether seed sown in the ground or the natural offspring of humanity (Isa. 59:21).\n\n**2.** The phrase "all flesh" in Isa. 66:22-24 further proves natural people will continue in the New Earth, coming to worship God during new moons and sabbaths. The Hebrew word for "flesh" is *basar*, meaning "flesh," "skin," "nakedness," or "body." It's used 252 times and always refers to natural flesh or animal life.\n\n**3.** In Rev. 21:3-4, 24-26, the men and nations mentioned are natural peoples. God's tabernacle comes down to dwell among men, and God wipes away all tears. This couldn't refer to glorified saints — God has already been dwelling among them for 1,000 years, and He wiped away their tears 1,000 years before these Scriptures are fulfilled!\n\n**4.** The Earth was created to be inhabited by natural beings, and natural humans were promised the Earth as an eternal inheritance from the very beginning (Exod. 32:13; Ps. 25:13; 37:9-11, 22, 29, 34; 69:36; 82:8; Isa. 60:21; Mt. 5:5; 25:34).\n\nThese promises were spoken to earthly people and will be fulfilled when earthly people inherit the Earth after the Millennium. Glorified saints will reign as kings and priests under Christ over these earthly peoples forever (Dan. 7:13-14, 18-27; Isa. 9:6-7; Lk. 1:32-35; 1 Cor. 6:2; Rev. 5:9-10; 11:15; 20:4-10).\n\nPeople living on Earth during the Millennium won't be glorified or enter the same privileges as those who participate in the first resurrection and were glorified before the Millennium. If those earthly people were glorified, who would be the subjects of Christ's eternal kingdom? Who would marry and produce the natural generations on the eternal Earth?\n\n**5.** God created humanity to live forever in natural bodies. This is clear from the fact that humans would have lived naturally forever if they hadn't sinned. The penalty for sin was death — physical, spiritual, and eternal. But humanity's fall didn't cause God to change His original plan.\n\nGod can't suffer defeat in the end, so He turned humanity's Fall into a blessing. During this period, He's been gathering a heavenly people to reign over the natural people who will be redeemed from the Fall and all its effects after the Millennium.\n\nThink of it like this: the Fall simply delayed God's original purpose, but because of the delay, God gained more than He would have otherwise. Now God will have a heavenly, resurrected, glorified people who will reign over coming generations of natural people. If the Fall had never happened, all humans would have continued as natural people forever, and there would be no class of glorified saints from the human race to help God administer the universe.\n\nAfter the Millennium, natural humanity will be fully redeemed and will live on the New Earth just as Adam did before the Fall, carrying out God's original purpose of filling the Earth with natural people (Gen. 1:27-31; 9:12; Isa. 45:18).\n\n**6.** The Bible plainly declares there will be eternal generations of natural peoples. Here's just a sampling of the many passages:\n\n> Gen. 9:12; 13:15; 17:7-8, 19; Exod. 3:15; 12:14, 42; 27:21; 30:8, 21; 31:16; 40:15; Lev. 3:17; 6:18; 10:9; 17:7; 23:14, 21, 31, 41; 24:3; 25:30; Num. 10:8; 15:15; 18:23; Deut. 5:29; 12:28; 28:46; 29:29; 2 Sam. 7:24-29; 1 Chron. 23:25; Ps. 12:7; 45:17; 72:5; 79:13; 89:4; 100:5; 102:12, 24; 106:31; 119:90; 135:13; 145:13; 146:10; Isa. 9:6-7; 51:8; 59:21; Jer. 31:35-36; 32:38-40; Ezek. 37:24-28; Lam. 5:19; Dan. 2:44-45; 4:3, 34; 7:13-18; Joel 3:20; Lk. 1:32-35, 55; Rev. 5:10; 11:15.\n\nLet me quote a few of these remarkable promises, all spoken by God Himself:\n\n> "And God said, This is the token of the covenant which I make between me and you and every living creature that is with you, for perpetual generations" (Gen. 9:12).\n\n> "For all the land which thou seest, to thee will I give it, and to thy seed for ever... And I will establish my covenant between me and thee and thy seed after thee in their generations for an everlasting covenant, to be a God unto thee, and to thy seed after thee... And I will give unto thee, and to thy seed after thee, the land wherein thou art a stranger, all the land of Canaan, for an everlasting possession; and I will be their God" (Gen. 13:15; 17:7-8).\n\n> "Observe and hear all these words which I command thee, that it may go well with thee, and with thy children after thee for ever, when thou doest that which is good and right in the sight of the Lord thy God" (Deut. 12:28).\n\n> "For thou hast confirmed to thyself thy people Israel to be a people unto thee for ever: and thou, Lord, art become their God... And now, O Lord God, the word that thou hast spoken concerning thy servant, and concerning his house, establish it for ever, and do as thou hast said... Therefore now let it please thee to bless the house of thy servant, that it may continue for ever before thee: for thou, O Lord God, hast spoken it: and with thy blessing let the house of thy servant be blessed for ever" (2 Sam. 7:24, 25, 29).\n\n> "For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given: and the government shall be upon his shoulders: and his name shall be called Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty God, The everlasting Father, The Prince of Peace... Of the increase of his government and peace there shall be no end, upon the throne of David, and upon his kingdom, to order it, and to establish it with judgment and with justice from henceforth even for\n\n---\n\nThe New Heaven and the New Earth are not a consolation prize for a difficult life — they're the original destination, recovered and glorified. Paul said that 'the sufferings of this present time are not worthy to be compared with the glory which shall be revealed in us' (Rom. 8:18). So here's the final question of this lesson: What suffering, loss, or grief in your life right now feels permanent and unbearable? And how would it change the weight of that grief if you genuinely believed — not just intellectually, but in your bones — that God will personally wipe every one of those tears from your eyes?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsi7000918pfgpznnq7i	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Aliens and UFOs	READING	\N	47	\N	t	![Aliens and UFOs](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsEPVa3OtdLWqJHyu8Q5MfmIRAjonSBKDvC0V2)\n\n## Aliens and UFOs\n\nThe congressional hearing was broadcast live. Military pilots described craft that defied known physics — no visible propulsion, right-angle turns at hypersonic speed, apparent awareness of human observers. The witnesses were credible. The footage was real. The committee chairman said the public had a right to know.\n\nIn the audience and watching at home: millions of people whose theological framework had no category for what they were seeing. Whose understanding of the universe had just been confronted with something that the church had offered no preparation for. Who were now, for the first time, genuinely open to a framework that could explain the phenomenon — and whose openness had just become the most targeted opportunity the enemy has created in modern history.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nThe UFO phenomenon encompasses documented sightings of unidentified aerial phenomena (UAP), reported alien encounters, and abduction experiences in which individuals claim to have been taken by non-human intelligences for examination and communication. Government disclosure efforts, military testimony, and mainstream media treatment have moved the topic from fringe conspiracy to serious public discussion in less than a decade.\n\nThe U.S. government has officially acknowledged the reality of UAP. Multiple credible military whistleblowers have testified before Congress. A significant and growing percentage of the global population now believes extraterrestrial intelligence is interacting with Earth.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe Bible knows nothing of intelligent extraterrestrial life visiting Earth. This is not an argument from silence — Scripture's account of the created order, spiritual beings, and the cosmic redemptive plan through Christ leaves no theological room for benevolent extraterrestrials whose existence would require a different account of human uniqueness and cosmic purpose.\n\nWhat people encounter during UFO events and abduction experiences are demonic entities materializing in forms that contemporary culture is prepared to accept. The "aliens" of the 21st century are the fairies and incubi of the 16th, the gods of the ancient near east, the spirit beings of every shamanic tradition — interdimensional created beings (fallen angels) who adapt their presentation to the dominant mythological frame of the culture they are targeting.\n\nThe "message" that these entities consistently deliver — they seeded human life, they are here to guide our evolution, organized religion has hidden the truth about our divine nature — is the same lie delivered in Genesis 3. *"Ye shall be as gods."* The delivery mechanism evolves. The message is eternal.\n\n[2 Thessalonians 2:9-11](data-scripture="2 Thessalonians 2:9-11"): *"Even him, whose coming is after the working of Satan with all power and signs and lying wonders... And for this cause God shall send them strong delusion, that they should believe a lie."* The strong delusion of the last days involves genuine signs and wonders impressive enough to almost deceive the elect. The alien disclosure narrative is the theological frame being prepared for those signs.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Belief in the alien framework replaces biblical eschatology.** A person who accepts the alien framework as the explanation for UAP phenomena has replaced their biblical understanding of angels, spiritual beings, and end-times events with a demonic interpretive structure. When the signs and wonders come, they will be received through that framework.\n\n**Abduction experiences are demonic assaults.** Abductees consistently report paralysis, sexual violation, terror, implantation of beliefs about human origins and divine identity, and lasting physical and psychological damage. These are the signatures of demonic attack, not extraterrestrial medical examination.\n\n**Interest in disclosure opens spiritual doors.** Sustained consumption of UAP disclosure content, alien encounter narratives, and extraterrestrial spirituality opens the viewer to the spiritual atmosphere and entities being discussed. Attention is always a form of invitation.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThe proper response to the UAP phenomenon is not denial — the phenomena are real. The proper response is the correct theological category: fallen angels, operating in a realm they have inhabited since their expulsion from heaven, currently presenting in the form most likely to be accepted by a post-Christian culture.\n\nApply [1 John 4:1-2](data-scripture="1 John 4:1") to every "alien" communication, encounter narrative, or disclosure claim: *"Test the spirits."* Every entity encountered in abduction experiences, every "message from the Pleiades," every channeled communication from "galactic guides" — test it. Does it confess that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh? Does it direct its hearers toward repentance and the cross?\n\nIt will not. The test will fail. And the test result is the answer.\n\n---\n\n*The alien disclosure narrative is a theological frame being built at planetary scale. The next lesson examines what looks like a counterculture festival — but functions as a mass ritual rehearsal for the system those entities are preparing.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *How would you respond theologically if the government formally confirmed extraterrestrial contact tomorrow? Do you have a framework ready — or would you be disoriented?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsim000l18pfpfac502f	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Burning Man and Festival Spirituality	READING	\N	48	\N	t	![Burning Man and Festival Spirituality](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsClkpcS5e78vbPqVLiKnDy6up93CGaNzkh5Hs)\n\n## Burning Man and Festival Spirituality\n\nShe went for the art. She was an architect, and the temporary structures built in the Nevada desert each year were genuinely extraordinary — avant-garde installations, kinetic sculptures, lit environments that no conventional architecture budget would produce. She was not spiritual about it. She went to look at things.\n\nShe came back different. Not dramatically — subtly. A restlessness she could not name. A dissatisfaction with ordinary life that had not been there before. A persistent curiosity about certain spiritual frameworks she had previously dismissed. A sense of something having shifted in her orientation toward conventional Christianity.\n\nShe spent two years wondering what had changed in Nevada. She had not understood that she had spent a week inside what was, in spiritual reality, a temporary sacred space dedicated to the spirit of rebellion and renewal — and that spaces like that do not leave their visitors unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nBurning Man is an annual festival held in the Black Rock Desert of Nevada, centered on the construction of a temporary city of approximately 70,000 people and culminating in the ritual burning of a massive wooden effigy. The event is organized around ten stated principles including "radical self-expression," "radical self-reliance," and "decommodification." Similar festival spirituality operates at Coachella, Bonnaroo, EDM events worldwide, and regional "burns."\n\nThe festival presents itself as art, community, and self-expression. Its spiritual dimension is harder to miss once you know what to look for.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nBurning Man is a contemporary iteration of ancient fire festivals conducted in honor of gods of destruction, death, and renewal. The burning effigy carries the structural and spiritual logic of a sacrificial offering — the offering of the human form to fire, the renewal that follows the destruction. This is not a creative interpretation. The festival's own history is explicit about its connection to pagan ritual.\n\n[Deuteronomy 32:17](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 32:17"): *"They sacrificed unto devils, to gods whom they knew not, to new gods that came newly up, whom their fathers feared not."* The new gods of the Nevada desert are not new. They are the old gods wearing new aesthetic clothing.\n\nThe desert location is significant. In biblical cosmology and in the cosmology of multiple ancient cultures, the desert was liminal space — outside the boundaries of civilization, the social structures that constrain behavior, and the covenant communities that protect their members. The Black Rock Desert functions as the same kind of liminal space: a place where normal rules dissolve, identities are shed, and the behaviors prohibited in ordinary life are celebrated.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Mass drug use creates corporate demonic openings.** When thousands of people simultaneously enter chemically induced altered states at a location dedicated to pagan spiritual principles, the corporate spiritual opening is exponentially greater than individual altered-state experiences.\n\n**The spiritual imprint persists after departure.** Multiple people who have attended Burning Man describe a persistent spiritual restlessness and reorientation that followed them home — a dissatisfaction with ordinary life, an attraction to spiritual frameworks antithetical to Christianity, and in some cases a clear deterioration in their relationship with God. This is not the expected contrast-effect of returning from an extraordinary experience to ordinary life. It is the spiritual residue of a week spent in a dedicated pagan sacred space.\n\n**"Just for the art" is not a spiritual exemption.** The spiritual atmosphere of a space does not inquire about the intentions of those who enter it. Every person who spent a week in the Black Rock City was inside a temporary pagan sacred space for a week, regardless of what they went for.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf you have attended Burning Man or similar mass gatherings — coachella, major EDM festivals, anything that functions as a temporary community organized around radical self-expression, chemical alteration, and the dissolution of moral boundaries — repent for the participation and renounce every spiritual attachment that came from the event.\n\nPray specifically over the "restlessness" and reorientation that followed. These are not personal growth. They are spiritual infection. Declare the blood of Jesus Christ over every influence the event carried, and ask the Holy Spirit to restore the spiritual clarity and orientation that the event disturbed.\n\n---\n\n*Festival spirituality creates temporary pagan sacred spaces. The next lesson examines what happens when that sacred space is built permanently — inside the human body.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you attended Burning Man, a major music festival, or any large-scale event that functions as a temporary community organized around altered states and radical self-expression?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsik000j18pfy4epkd8q	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Transhumanism and Brain Chips	READING	\N	49	\N	t	![Transhumanism and Brain Chips](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsSzmbd3J9p8Osi7f2L3jgeayVJxF6MbNCPdun)\n\n## Transhumanism and Brain Chips\n\nHe received the first Neuralink implant as part of a clinical trial for ALS. The technology was genuinely miraculous in the most precise sense — it allowed a paralyzed man to control a computer cursor with his thoughts. He typed emails. He communicated with his family. It was, by every observable measure, a gift of extraordinary grace.\n\nHe was also a Christian who read Revelation carefully. He held both things — the genuine good of the technology and the genuine concern about the infrastructure it was building — without forcing a resolution. He said: "I know this helps me. I don't know what it's building toward. I pray that God redeems what can be redeemed and that I don't become part of something I don't intend."\n\nThat is probably the most honest thing that can be said about transhumanism right now: it is building toward something that Scripture describes. The timeline is unknown. The infrastructure is not.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nTranshumanism is a philosophical and technological movement advocating the use of science and technology to enhance human cognitive and physical capabilities beyond biological limits. Current technologies include:\n\n**Brain-computer interfaces** (Neuralink, Synchron): neural implants that read and write signals in the nervous system, enabling thought-controlled computers and eventually direct neural internet access.\n\n**CRISPR genetic editing**: the ability to modify human DNA, currently in clinical trials for genetic disease treatment and increasingly discussed for enhancement applications.\n\n**Artificial general intelligence** and human-AI integration: the progressive merging of human cognition with artificial intelligence systems.\n\nThe movement explicitly frames human biology as a problem to be solved — not a gift to be stewarded.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\n[Genesis 3:5](data-scripture="Genesis 3:5"): *"Ye shall be as gods."* Transhumanism is the technological expression of this ancient offer — immortality, omniscience, and power without the God who designed the human being. It promises to solve mortality through digital consciousness uploading, solve cognitive limitations through neural enhancement, and solve the problem of the body through genetic optimization.\n\nThe human body is not a problem. It is the physical expression of [Genesis 1:26](data-scripture="Genesis 1:26"): *"Let us make man in our image."* The image of God is not a flawed prototype. It is the Creator's deliberate design. To declare it insufficient and in need of technological upgrade is a theological statement: God's design requires human improvement.\n\n[Revelation 13:16-17](data-scripture="Revelation 13:16-17") describes a system in which no one can buy or sell without a mark in their right hand or forehead. The infrastructure of digital identity verification, biometric payment systems, and neural implants is under active construction. The spirit of antichrist is already at work in these systems.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Any technology that reads and writes neural signals creates a potential portal for external spiritual influence.** Brain-computer interfaces that can deliver content directly to the nervous system are, in the spiritual framework this course has established, a technological version of the mechanisms by which demonic entities achieve influence over human thought.\n\n**Genetic modification of the image of God is a theological transgression** with consequences Scripture does not fully describe, because the scenario was not a live possibility when Scripture was written. The prudential response is caution proportional to the stakes.\n\n**The normalization trajectory is designed.** Medical applications come first. When the public has accepted neural implants for paralysis, the threshold for enhancement applications is much lower. The step from "helping the disabled" to "enhancing the healthy" to "mandatory participation in the digital economy" is smaller than it appears from the beginning.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThe practical guidance for most readers: refuse any technology that requires implantation of a device that interfaces with the nervous system unless medical necessity makes the benefit clearly worth the risk — and even then, with informed prayer and discernment.\n\nWatch the trajectory, not just the current application. The question is not whether today's Neuralink helps someone with ALS. The question is what the normalized implant infrastructure enables in fifteen years.\n\n[Matthew 24:24](data-scripture="Matthew 24:24"): *"For there shall arise false Christs, and false prophets, and shall shew great signs and wonders; insomuch that, if it were possible, they shall deceive the very elect."* The very elect. The technology through which those wonders arrive may be the technology being built now. Maintain theological clarity while the world celebrates.\n\n---\n\n*Transhumanism wants to upgrade the hardware. The final lesson in this wave examines the counterfeit relationship being built to replace the one God designed — from the inside.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Where is the line between medical technology and the mark of the beast, in your theological framework? Have you thought it through — or is this territory you have avoided?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612w5001pgeo05fa4ywfe	cmq6612vy001hgeo0djva1vnw	Lesson 17 — Angels in the Old Testament: From Eden to the Prophets	READING	900	0	\N	t	![Lesson 17 — Angels in the Old Testament: From Eden to the Prophets](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsGRXJ7KQtkjPm8YJfVWKDcL3Bvzgo59AS2es6)\n\n## Angels in the Old Testament — From Eden to the Prophets\n\n### One Question to Hold Through the Survey\n\nAs you read through the angelic appearances in the Old Testament, hold one interpretive question:\n\n**What does this appearance tell us about how God governs the world?**\n\nNot "what miracles happened" or "what did the angel look like" — but: what does the angel's presence here reveal about God's governance of human history?\n\nThe answer, by the end of this lesson, should be unmistakable.\n\n---\n\n### In the Beginning: Creation and Eden\n\n**At creation** ([Job 38:7](data-scripture="Job 38:7")): The angels were present when God laid the foundations of the earth and *"the sons of God shouted for joy."* Before any human existed, before any covenant was established, the angels had already praised God for a world that would include humanity.\n\n**At Eden** ([Genesis 3:24](data-scripture="Genesis 3:24")): After the expulsion, Cherubim are placed at the east of Eden with a flaming sword. The first angelic act following human sin is **guardianship of the sacred** — protecting the Tree of Life from a humanity not yet ready to return to it. This pattern will not change across the entire Old Testament.\n\n### The Patriarchal Age: Angels and the Covenant Promises\n\n**Hagar in the wilderness** ([Genesis 16:7-13](data-scripture="Genesis 16:7")). Sarah's servant, pregnant and fleeing abuse, is found by the Angel of the Lord at a spring in the desert. He does not appear to a king or priest. He appears to a fugitive woman who has no one. The angel names her child and promises him a future. *God sees* — *El Roi* — is what Hagar calls God after this encounter. Angels appear to those the world has overlooked.\n\n**The three visitors to Abraham** ([Genesis 18:1-2](data-scripture="Genesis 18:1")). Heavenly visitors receive Abraham's hospitality; the birth of Isaac is announced; the covenant continues. Angels announce the fulfillments of promises.\n\n**The binding of Isaac** ([Genesis 22:11-12](data-scripture="Genesis 22:11")). At the supreme moment of testing, the Angel of the Lord calls from heaven and stops the knife. Angels are present at the turning points — and their intervention is always in the direction of mercy.\n\n**Jacob's ladder** ([Genesis 28:12](data-scripture="Genesis 28:12")). A ladder from earth to heaven, with angels ascending and descending. Jesus will later claim this image for Himself: *"Truly, truly, I say to you, you will see heaven opened, and the angels of God ascending and descending on the Son of Man"* ([John 1:51](data-scripture="John 1:51")). Jacob's vision is not a one-time event — it is a picture of permanent reality.\n\n**Jacob wrestling** ([Genesis 32:24-30](data-scripture="Genesis 32:24")). Jacob wrestles all night with a figure identified as an angel and is renamed Israel: "one who strives with God." Angels are not always comforting presences. Sometimes they are the instruments of the encounter that transforms.\n\n### The Exodus: Angels of Deliverance\n\n**The burning bush** ([Exodus 3:2](data-scripture="Exodus 3:2")). The Angel of the Lord appears in the fire that burns but does not consume. From this fire, the name of God is revealed and Moses is called to the greatest liberation in Old Testament history. The angel is the medium of the theophany — the point at which the divine approaches the human.\n\n**The pillar of cloud and fire** ([Exodus 14:19](data-scripture="Exodus 14:19")). The angel of God goes before the camp of Israel, guiding by day and protecting by night. The entire journey of liberation is marked by angelic accompaniment. Israel does not walk through the wilderness alone.\n\n**The Ark of the Covenant** ([Exodus 25:18-22](data-scripture="Exodus 25:18")). Golden Cherubim commanded for the mercy seat, their wings spread upward, facing each other, forming the earthly throne of the invisible God. God pledges to meet Moses there. The Cherubim guard the meeting place of heaven and earth.\n\n### The Monarchy: Angels at Critical Junctures\n\n**Joshua and the commander of the Lord's army** ([Joshua 5:14](data-scripture="Joshua 5:14")). Near Jericho, Joshua encounters a figure with a drawn sword who identifies himself as the *"commander of the army of the Lord."* Joshua falls on his face and is instructed to remove his sandals — holy ground. An angelic military commander precedes Israel into the promised land.\n\n**Gideon** ([Judges 6:11-23](data-scripture="Judges 6:11")). The Angel of the Lord sits under the oak at Ophrah and calls a reluctant Gideon to deliver Israel. Gideon prepares an offering; the angel touches it with a staff; fire consumes it from the rock. The call of a leader confirmed by an angelic sign.\n\n**Elijah** ([1 Kings 19:5-7](data-scripture="1 Kings 19:5")). The prophet, exhausted and suicidal, flees into the wilderness. He lies down under a broom tree and asks to die. An angel appears — not with a theological correction, not with a prophetic word — but with **bread and water**: *"Arise and eat, for the journey is too great for you."* And then again, a second time: *"Arise and eat."*\n\nThis is the most tender moment in the Old Testament involving an angel. A great man at the end of his strength, and an angel with food. The theology will come later. First: sustenance. First: care for the body. First: acknowledgment that the journey is, indeed, too great, and that this is not a character defect but simply the truth.\n\n### The Prophetic Age: Angels in Vision\n\n**Isaiah** ([Isaiah 6:1-7](data-scripture="Isaiah 6:1")). The Seraphim, the throne, the triple-holy cry, the burning coal — the purification of a prophet who will now speak for God. Covered in Lesson 5.\n\n**Ezekiel** ([Ezekiel 1:4-28](data-scripture="Ezekiel 1:4")). The Cherubim, the chariot-throne, the blazing wheels within wheels — the overwhelming vision of God's governance of creation. Covered in Lesson 6.\n\n**Daniel** ([Daniel 8:16](data-scripture="Daniel 8:16"); [Daniel 10:13](data-scripture="Daniel 10:13")). Gabriel interprets; Michael fights. For the first time, angels are named. The individual missions begin to come into focus.\n\n**Zechariah** ([Zechariah 1:9](data-scripture="Zechariah 1:9")). Eight night visions, each explained by an angelic interpreter: *"the angel who talked with me."* Angels as teachers, as guides through the prophetic mysteries.\n\n---\n\n### What Every Appearance Reveals\n\nReturn to the interpretive question from the opening: *What does this appearance tell us about how God governs the world?*\n\nThe answer, across every appearance in this survey, is the same:\n\n**God governs personally.** He does not administer from a distance through impersonal forces. He sends persons. He commands persons. He sustains, announces, protects, purifies, calls, feeds, interprets, and guards — and He does all of it through personal beings who know their mission and carry it out with the full engagement of their intellect and will.\n\nYou do not live in a universe that God wound up and left to run. You live in a universe that He governs, moment by moment, through an ordered hierarchy of personal beings who are present at every turning point of your history — and your personal history is no less governed than the history of Israel, the Exodus, or the Incarnation.\n\n---\n\n*Next: The final lesson. We trace the angels through the New Testament — and then we step back to see the whole picture at once: what this course has been, from Lesson 1's opening image to this moment.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612vo0015geo0yzc7gzjn	cmq6612vm0013geo0kqjj27k2	Lesson 11 — The Archangels: Heaven's Chief Messengers	READING	900	0	\N	t	![Lesson 11 — The Archangels: Heaven's Chief Messengers](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsQByJnbhQWkP21SLEA3tZrcs70u6UjOq5zopY)\n\n## The Archangels — Heaven's Chief Messengers\n\n### The Most Personal Missions in Creation\n\nIn Lesson 3, we established that every angel was created for a specific task. No mission is incidental. No assignment was handed out after the fact.\n\nNow we are about to meet the three angels whose assigned missions are described in detail in Scripture — and in meeting them, we encounter one of the most remarkable claims in all of angelology:\n\n**Gabriel's entire existence was ordered toward a single conversation with a young woman in Nazareth.**\n\n**Michael's entire existence was ordered toward the guardianship of those chosen for salvation.**\n\n**Raphael's entire existence was ordered toward healing, accompaniment, and the restoration of sight.**\n\nThese were not roles these angels auditioned for. These were not assignments distributed based on performance. These missions were constitutive — they were the *reason* these beings were created. Gabriel *is* the angel of the Annunciation in the deepest ontological sense. Before time, before the first star, before the first human breath — Gabriel was made for Nazareth.\n\nThis is not poetry. This is the teaching of Thomas Aquinas, developed by Fr. Chad Ripperger, and grounded in the angelological principle established in the *Summa Theologiae*: angelic tasks are not distributed; they are given at creation, as part of the angel's very nature.\n\n### Etymology and Role\n\n*Archangelos* in Greek means **"chief angel"** or **"ruling angel."** The archangels are superior messengers, entrusted with the most important divine missions. They lead the third hierarchy — the angels most directly concerned with human beings and the plan of salvation.\n\nThe name *archangel* describes not a species but a dignity. In Catholic tradition, "archangel" refers to the choir, the eighth of the nine. But Michael, as we will see, may in fact transcend even this categorization by the grace of his mission.\n\n### How Many Archangels?\n\nScripture names only **three archangels** by name. The Church has been deliberately cautious about naming others. When a list of seven (or more) named archangels circulated in medieval devotional literature — including names like Uriel, Raguel, and Saraqael — a synod under Pope Zachary in 745 A.D. specifically examined and limited the veneration of named angels to those named in canonical Scripture.\n\nThis pastoral prudence reflects a deep wisdom: inventing the names and personalities of angels — even with good intentions — risks superstition and the substitution of human imagination for divine revelation. The angels we name are the angels God told us about. The others we honor without names, trusting that their existence is as real as their anonymity.\n\nRaphael's self-identification in [Tobit 12:15](data-scripture="Tobit 12:15") — *"I am Raphael, one of the seven holy angels who present the prayers of the saints and enter into the presence of the holy God"* — confirms that there are seven angels of special standing before the throne. The Church honors this tradition without pretending to know their names.\n\n### The Three Archangels and the Economy of Salvation\n\nWhat is most striking about the three named archangels is that their missions together cover the entire arc of salvation:\n\n| Archangel | Mission | Salvation Moment |\n|-----------|---------|-----------------|\n| **Gabriel** | Announcement | The Incarnation — God becomes man |\n| **Michael** | Protection | The elect are guarded through history |\n| **Raphael** | Healing | Brokenness is restored; the journey is completed |\n\nThe Incarnation. The protection of those redeemed by it. The healing of those wounded by the fall. These three movements are not random — they are the shape of salvation itself. And each has its own archangel, created for it before the world began.\n\n### The Feasts\n\n**September 29 — The Feast of the Archangels (Michaelmas).** The celebration of Michael, Gabriel, and Raphael together — and through them, the entire order of archangels whose missions we do not know but whose existence we honor.\n\n**October 2 — The Feast of the Guardian Angels.** Honoring the ninth and lowest choir — the most numerous, most intimate, and in some ways most personally significant of all the angels. We study them in Part V.\n\n---\n\n*Next: Of the three archangels, Michael is the most prominent in Scripture — warrior, guardian, great prince, captain of the heavenly host. His very name is the theological statement that defeated the greatest rebellion in the history of creation.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612w0001jgeo0budnsxei	cmq6612vy001hgeo0djva1vnw	Lesson 15 — The Guardian Angels: God's Personal Gift to Every Soul	READING	900	3	\N	t	![Lesson 15 — The Guardian Angels: God's Personal Gift to Every Soul](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Osnh2k7dgR6p4tHCQPYM8N0kE5l7TdjZq9ibaz)\n\n## The Guardian Angels — God's Personal Gift to Every Soul\n\n### A Fact About Your Life That Changes Everything\n\nBefore you read another word, stop and consider this:\n\nThere is an intelligent being — a *person*, with intellect and will and the capacity for love — who has been present with you since the moment of your conception. It was there in the womb, before you had a name. It was there at your birth, at your first breath, at your first step. It was present at every moment of your life that you remember and every moment you do not — every night, every crisis, every ordinary Tuesday, every prayer you have ever offered and every prayer you forgot to offer.\n\nIt is present with you right now.\n\nThis being cannot be seen. It does not announce itself. It has never once demanded your attention or required your acknowledgment to keep doing its work. It has been carrying your prayers before God — every prayer, including the ones you gave up on. It has been inclining you, gently, toward what is good, protecting you from dangers you will never know about, and standing as your advocate before the throne of the Most High.\n\nAnd it was not assigned to you as an afterthought. God created it, in some measure, for you. This is its mission. You are why it exists.\n\nThis is the doctrine of the guardian angel. It is among the most personal, most consoling, and most underappreciated teachings of the Christian faith.\n\n### The Church's Definitive Teaching\n\n> **Catechism of the Catholic Church, §336** — "From its beginning until death, human life is surrounded by their watchful care and intercession. Beside each believer stands an angel as protector and shepherd leading him to life. Already here on earth the Christian life shares by faith in the blessed company of angels and men united in God."\n\nThe word *beside* is precise. Not above. Not at a distance. Beside. The same word one would use for a companion walking next to you on a road.\n\n### What Scripture Says\n\n**Psalm 91:11** — *"For he will command his angels concerning you to guard you in all your ways."*\n\nNot some of your ways. Not the important ones. *All* of them.\n\n**Matthew 18:10** — Jesus is speaking about the "little ones" — the vulnerable, the humble, the easily dismissed. He says:\n\n> [Matthew 18:10](data-scripture="Matthew 18:10") "See that you do not despise one of these little ones. For I tell you that in heaven their angels always behold the face of my Father who is in heaven."\n\nSit with this sentence for a moment. Two things are stated simultaneously:\n\n*Their angels* — personal possessive. Not "the angels." Not "some angel." *Their* angels. Each little one has its own.\n\n*Always behold the face of my Father* — always. Not when they are free. Not between assignments. Always. Right now.\n\nThis means: your guardian angel is simultaneously with you and in the direct presence of God. It does not have to leave God to be with you. It does not step outside the throne room to attend to your affairs. It holds both — the beatific vision of God and the intimate knowledge of your life — at the same time. This is what angelic nature permits that human nature cannot.\n\n**Hebrews 1:14** — *"Are they not all ministering spirits sent out to serve for the sake of those who are to inherit salvation?"*\n\nThe phrase "those who are to inherit salvation" is the entire class of redeemed humanity. Every guardian angel exists for this class — which includes you, if you are seeking God.\n\n**Acts 12:15** — When Peter is miraculously freed from prison and knocks at the door of the house where the disciples are praying, they assume the person at the door is "his angel" — completely naturally, without theological explanation. The idea of personal guardian angels was so established in the early Church that it was the first thing they assumed. Their prayer produced Peter; their first assumption was that God had sent his angel.\n\n### The Angel Knows You Before You Know Yourself\n\nHere is a fact that the theological tradition rarely surfaces explicitly, but that follows directly from the doctrine of infused knowledge established in Lesson 2:\n\n**Your guardian angel knew you before you were born.**\n\nWhen God created the angelic hierarchy and infused each angel with the knowledge proper to its nature and mission, your guardian angel received — as part of that infused knowledge — the knowledge of its assignment. Of you. Your nature, your capacity, your calling, your need. Not the knowledge of your future free choices, which remain hidden even from angels — but the knowledge of what you are, and what this angel was made to help you become.\n\nYou have never been a surprise to your guardian angel. From the first moment of your existence, it was there, already knowing its task.\n\n### What Your Guardian Angel Can and Cannot Do\n\n**It can:**\n\n- Act upon your imagination and interior senses — inspiring thoughts, inclining you toward good, prompting you toward prayer\n- Protect you from physical dangers, when this aligns with God's providential plan\n- Intercede for you before God, presenting your prayers to the throne — as Raphael did for Tobit and Sarah\n- Enlighten your mind through interior promptings that do not compel but invite\n\n**It cannot:**\n\n- Compel your will — human free will is absolutely inviolable. Your guardian angel cannot make you choose rightly. It can make the choice toward goodness easier, more attractive, more clearly illuminated. But it cannot choose for you.\n- Create certainty in your intellect — it cannot force belief or understanding\n- Override God's providential plan — if a suffering or trial is part of what God allows for your growth or purification, your guardian angel cannot remove it, though it can sustain you through it\n\nThe inability to compel the will is not a limitation on the angel's power. It is a reflection of the dignity of human freedom — a dignity so significant that God Himself honors it, and so the angels honor it too.\n\n### The Most Astonishing Implication\n\nYou are never in any room alone.\n\nIn every conversation you have ever had, in every decision you have ever faced, in every moment of darkness or joy or confusion, in every prayer prayed or skipped — a being of pure intelligence that has loved God from the beginning of creation has been present with you.\n\nNot watching passively. *Present.* Active. Interceding. Inclining. Protecting. Carrying your prayers upward.\n\nAnd you have been carrying it in your pocket, mostly forgotten, like a letter you never opened.\n\nThe practice of actually speaking to your guardian angel — briefly, simply, at the beginning of the day or in moments of need — is not superstition. It is the appropriate response to this reality. You are acknowledging a person who is there, who knows you, and who has been serving you since before you knew they existed.\n\n> [Matthew 18:10](data-scripture="Matthew 18:10") "Their angels always behold the face of my Father who is in heaven."\n\n### The Feast of the Guardian Angels: October 2\n\nThe feast was established in Spain in the sixteenth century and extended to the universal Church by Pope Clement X in 1670.\n\nThe traditional prayer, among the oldest in Catholic devotion:\n\n*"Angel of God, my guardian dear, to whom God's love commits me here; ever this day be at my side, to light and guard, to rule and guide. Amen."*\n\n---\n\n*Next: Knowing that your guardian angel exists is one thing. Cultivating a living relationship with it is another. The next lesson is practical — how the tradition instructs us to honor, address, and respond to the angelic presences woven into our daily life.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6612vl0011geo0w37ggjie	cmq6612ve000tgeo0b9n1d4af	Supplement 6 — For Lessons 9 & 10 (Extended)	SUPPLEMENT	600	3	\N	t	![Supplement 6 — For Lessons 9 & 10 (Extended)](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsI7Fo7jDFm5fHMlhCe2Nngyo6VzaWuJEO4Dj7)\n\n## Supplement 6 — For Lessons 9 & 10 (Extended): The Cosmic Governance of Angels\n\n### A Conversation on Angels and the Cosmos\n\n*The following is a dialogue between a student working through this course and a theology teacher answering the questions the material raises. The questions are real; the answers represent the classical Christian tradition.*\n\n---\n\n**Student:** I understand that the Dominations and Virtues govern the physical universe. But doesn't that just mean the universe is controlled by intermediaries? It feels like it makes God more remote, not less.\n\n**Teacher:** That's the opposite of what the tradition intends. The Dominations and Virtues are not a buffer between you and God — they are the hands by which God is *personally present* in the physical world at every moment. The alternative to angelic governance is not a more immediate God; it's a God who governs through impersonal mechanism, through an autonomous machine called nature that runs on its own. The classical view says: no, God is not a deist watchmaker who wound up the universe and walked away. He is present, actively and personally governing every moment of creation through personal beings who enact His will as an act of love and obedience. That is *more* presence, not less.\n\n---\n\n**Student:** But can't God govern creation directly, without angels? Why does He need intermediaries at all?\n\n**Teacher:** He doesn't *need* them — He *chose* them. This is an important distinction. God could sustain creation directly, by pure divine will without any creaturely mediation. He does not do so, apparently because it pleases Him to share His governance with created beings who participate in it as free, intelligent agents. This is consistent with how He governs everything else: He could have saved humanity without the Incarnation, without prophets, without the Church, without sacraments. He chose all of these as means precisely because He is a God who loves to share Himself, to bring creatures into the act of what He is doing. The angels governing creation is the same principle applied to the physical order.\n\n---\n\n**Student:** When the Virtues perform a miracle, are they overriding natural law? If natural law is their work, can they just suspend it whenever they want?\n\n**Teacher:** They cannot act on their own initiative. The Virtues are not autonomous. They act only in obedience to divine command. When God wills an ordinary sunrise, the Virtues sustain the ordinary course of nature. When God wills that a dead man walk out of a tomb, He directs the Virtues to enact something beyond the ordinary — not to break their own work, but to use it in an extraordinary way in service of a specific divine purpose. A miracle is not a gap in creation; it is the same power that fills creation, used with singular intentionality. The Virtues do not experience this as contradiction. They experience it as one more act of obedience to the God they love.\n\n---\n\n**Student:** I find the Principalities fascinating and terrifying at the same time — the idea that nations have spiritual rulers, including demonic ones. Does that mean when an evil empire does evil things, a demon is responsible?\n\n**Teacher:** Responsible, no. *Implicated*, yes. Demonic Principalities do not *cause* human evil — they cannot override human freedom. What they can do is cultivate, amplify, and exploit the patterns of human sin that are already present. Think of them less as puppet-masters and more as expert gardeners of corruption. They find the weeds that are already growing in the soil of a culture — pride, fear, tribalism, resentment, greed — and water them. They have centuries of experience doing this. But the humans who enact evil are still morally responsible for their choices. The demonic dimension adds a layer; it does not replace human agency.\n\n---\n\n**Student:** If Michael is the Principality of God's covenant people, was he fighting in World War II? Is he fighting now?\n\n**Teacher:** The tradition would say: yes. Not in the way human soldiers fight — his engagement is at the level of the spiritual governance of peoples, the movement of history toward or away from God's plan, the protection of the Church from forces that would destroy her. When John Paul II attributed the fall of Soviet communism partly to the intervention of Mary — *"one hand pulled the trigger, another guided the bullet"* — this is the same mode of thinking. The spiritual dimension of history is real. Michael's assignment is not a metaphor. He has been executing it for as long as there have been people to protect. Whether that involves what looks like military history in some direct sense is something we cannot see. But the tradition affirms: when the Church endures, Michael is doing his job.\n\n---\n\n**Student:** This all makes me feel very small. My life is tiny next to nations and cosmic governance and nine angelic choirs.\n\n**Teacher:** That's the right response to the second hierarchy. Now remember the third. The Dominations govern the blueprint. The Virtues govern the cosmos. The Principalities govern nations. And then — after all of that scale, after the entire machinery of creation's governance — God assigns one angel, from the lowest of the nine choirs, not to a civilization or a century but to you. One person. By name. Not because you are small, but because you are not. God's economy of care turns out to be: the larger the machinery, the more precisely it serves the singular. The whole cosmic apparatus exists, in some sense, so that you can be found.\n\n---\n\n*Next lesson: we enter the third hierarchy — the Archangels, the Angels, and the one assigned to you.*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk48i0018ewhj27top6t3	cmnknk48e000xewhj49ao5az0	Lesson 26 — The Gifts and Fruit of the Holy Spirit	READING	5092	10	\N	t	There are two things the Holy Spirit produces in the life of a believer — and the Church has managed to fight over both of them. One camp emphasizes the gifts and minimizes the fruit. The other emphasizes the fruit and dismisses the gifts as temporary or dangerous. Scripture presents both as permanent, both as necessary, and both as expressions of the same Spirit. Choosing between them is like choosing between breathing in and breathing out.\n\nLast time we examined who the Holy Spirit is as a Person. Now we look at what He produces in believers: the gifts He distributes for the Church's ministry and the fruit He grows in the believer's character.\n\nGod has made complete provision for His power and life to be fully expressed through His people. In earlier lessons, we've shown what God's plan is for meeting human needs and how every believer has the power of attorney to act in Christ's place among people. We're partakers of the divine nature (2 Pet. 1:4). We have access to God and the freedom to exercise the divine powers that belong to God's family.\n\nThink of it this way: everything in existence shares the nature, powers, and characteristics of its own kind. Fish have all the abilities of fish — they swim, they breathe underwater. Birds have every bird-like trait. Animals follow their own kind. Humans are the same. And so it is with God's family. The moment anything is born, it has certain powers from its parents. A baby fish can swim; a bird can fly; a dog can bark. It would be a miracle for a dog to live in water or a fish to fly through the sky — that would go against nature.\n\nIn the same way, it goes against nature for people to be spiritually born of God, share His nature, and then live contrary to that nature. We as God's sons should manifest a supernatural nature through the Holy Spirit's indwelling and through faith in Jesus Christ's name and His atonement. God has provided the baptism in the Spirit and the gifts of the Spirit for exactly this purpose — to show His divine life in His sons.\n\nNothing in Scripture is more specific and detailed than God's plan for divine-human sons equipped with power to represent Him on Earth. In previous lessons, we've given hundreds of Scriptures proving this. The spiritual tools God gives us are the gifts of the Spirit, and He wants us — all of His children on Earth — to exercise them fully. He has repeatedly demonstrated His will through the prophets, through Jesus Christ, and through early believers. He has repeatedly promised this power to every believer, so there's no excuse for not knowing about it.\n\nPaul started his teaching on spiritual gifts by saying, "Now concerning spiritual gifts, brethren, I would not have you ignorant" (1 Cor. 12:1), and he ended by saying, "But if any man be ignorant, let him be ignorant" (1 Cor. 14:38). It seems like the simpler and more detailed God's truths are, the more people remain ignorant of them! Every time Paul uses a phrase like "I would not have you to be ignorant," the subject turns out to be one of the simplest in Scripture to understand. If anything seems difficult, it's explained so simply and clearly that there can be no misunderstanding — if you actually want to understand (see Rom. 1:13; 11:25; 1 Cor. 10:1; 12:1; 2 Cor. 1:8; 1 Thess. 4:13-17). The only reason anyone could possibly misunderstand is if they deliberately refuse to, as Paul plainly stated: "But if any man be ignorant, let him be ignorant."\n\nIn Lesson Eighteen, Point IX, we saw that the gifts of the Spirit were active throughout Old Testament times, except for the gift of tongues and interpretation of tongues. Saints of old had tremendous power with God — in many cases even greater power than what we see among modern believers today. Let any honest person compare what power they have with what Old Testament saints had, or with what Christ and the apostles demonstrated, and they'll have to admit they're falling far short. Is this normal? Is this what the Bible teaches? Is this really God's will for believers today?\n\nWe can't bring ourselves to say this is God's best, not with hundreds of Scriptures on this subject. God has been a God of signs and wonders in both Testaments. He's always the same. His abilities are constant, His attributes eternal, His divine powers unchanging. He has never decreased in power and never will. He's not evolving and never will evolve in divine power. He is today what He has always been and always will be. He will never become what He isn't, and what He ever was, He still is. God's energies don't grow, and His plan of using power for creation's highest good never changes.\n\nThe gifts of the Spirit aren't new. They were exercised in ancient times with greater power than we often see today. And these weren't just temporary loans of power to Old Testament saints, as some teach. They were permanent anointings and gifts, just as "without repentance" on God's part then as they are now (Rom. 11:29). No calling of God and no gift of the Spirit in any age has ever been a mere loan or temporary ability if it was truly given to a person. Solomon said about his gift of wisdom, even after he had backslidden: "Also my wisdom remained with me" (Eccl. 2:9). There's no statement anywhere saying Old Testament gifts and anointings were only loans or temporary. That's simply a human theory and should be valued only as such.\n\n![Lesson 26 — The Gifts and Fruit of the Holy Spirit](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsnI9o1CgR6p4tHCQPYM8N0kE5l7TdjZq9ibaz)\n\n## I. Pertinent Questions Concerning Spiritual Gifts\n\n### 1. HOW MANY GIFTS ARE THERE?\n\nThere are nine gifts (1 Cor. 12:4-11):\n\n> (1) The gift of the word of wisdom.\n\n> (2) The gift of the word of knowledge.\n\n> (3) The gift of faith.\n\n> (4) The gifts of healing.\n\n> (5) The gift of the working of miracles.\n\n> (6) The gift of prophecy.\n\n> (7) The gift of discerning of spirits.\n\n> (8) The gift of divers kinds of tongues or languages.\n\n> (9) The gift of the interpretation of tongues or languages.\n\n### 2. WHOSE GIFTS ARE THEY, AND WHO WORKS THEM?\n\nThey belong to the Holy Spirit, and He's the one who operates them in believers' lives. "Now there are diversities of gifts, but the same Spirit. And there are differences of administrations, but the same Lord. And there are diversities of operations, but it is the same God which worketh all in all. But the manifestation of the Spirit is given to every man to profit withal. For to one is given by the Spirit the word of wisdom; to another the word of knowledge by the same Spirit; to another faith by the same Spirit; to another the gifts of healing by the same Spirit; to another the working of miracles; to another prophecy; to another discerning of spirits; to another divers kinds of tongues; to another the interpretation of tongues. But all these worketh that one and selfsame Spirit, dividing to every man severally as he will" (1 Cor. 12:4-11).\n\n### 3. WHAT IS THE PURPOSE OF THE GIFTS?\n\nThe purpose is to enable all believers to do Christ's works and continue what He began both to do and to teach (Acts 1:1-2, 12-15; 1 Cor. 1:7; Rom. 12:3-8; 1 Cor. 12:4-31; 14:1-40; Heb. 2:3-4). They were given to confirm the gospel and demonstrate God's power among people: "These signs shall follow them that believe; In my name shall they cast out devils; they shall speak with new tongues; they shall take up serpents; and if they drink any deadly thing it shall not hurt them: they shall lay hands on the sick and they shall recover... And they [early believers] went forth, and preached every where, the Lord working with them, and confirming the word with signs following" (Mk. 16:15-20).\n\n"How shall we escape if we neglect so great salvation; which at the first began to be spoken by the Lord, and was confirmed unto us by them that heard him; God also bearing them witness, both with signs and wonders, and with divers miracles, and gifts of the Holy Ghost, according to his own will?" (Heb. 2:3-4).\n\n"For I will not dare to speak of any of those things which Christ hath not wrought by me, to make the Gentiles obedient, by word and deed, through mighty signs and wonders, by the power of the Spirit of God; so that from Jerusalem, and round about unto Illyricum, I have fully preached the gospel of Christ... And I am sure that, when I come unto you, I shall come in the fullness of the blessing of the gospel of Christ" (Rom. 15:18-19, 29).\n\n"He that believeth on me, the works that I do shall he do also; and greater works than these shall he do; because I go to my Father" (Jn. 14:12).\n\n"God hath set some in the church, first apostles, secondarily prophets, thirdly teachers, after that miracles, then gifts of healings, helps, governments, diversities of tongues... But covet earnestly the best gifts: and yet shew I unto you a more excellent way... Follow after charity, and desire spiritual gifts" (1 Cor. 12:28-30; 14:1).\n\nThese and other Scriptures explain the purpose of spiritual gifts. God's purpose hasn't changed. It will remain the same throughout this age, as we've proven in Lessons Twenty and Twenty-two. Only humanity has changed, losing the powers of the original church. When people change again to a normal New Testament faith, they'll once more see the gifts of the Spirit operating perfectly and fully in the modern church.\n\nIn 1 Corinthians 12 and 14, Paul deals with supernatural equipment for service and worship and how certain gifts of the Spirit should be used in public believers' meetings. It's impossible to have a true New Testament gathering of believers without exercising spiritual gifts of some kind. These gifts are essential not just for service but for worship too. With all our claims to godliness and loyalty to church practices and rituals, we fail God if there's no knowledge of, respect for, or use of spiritual gifts.\n\nFirst of all, it's God's will for people to be highly informed about spiritual gifts, as proven in 1 Cor. 12:1: "Now concerning spiritual gifts, brethren, I would not have you ignorant." The modern church's ignorance about these spiritual abilities is simply staggering. Rarely, if ever, are these gifts preached about in the average church. When they are mentioned, it's usually in a negative way. Some are ridiculed and labeled as demonic or fanatical. If they were exercised today in most churches, they'd be rejected. If the Corinthians, who had these gifts, were called ignorant about using them properly in public meetings, what term should describe modern churches' knowledge of them? The average preacher today doesn't even know what these gifts are, let alone their purpose and proper use in local churches. The average church member doesn't know such gifts exist for believers.\n\nThe Corinthians had been hopeless idolaters and were familiar with supernatural powers and how they operated. Both among Gentiles and Jews there were magicians, wizards, sorcerers, and fortune-tellers who yielded themselves to demons and satanic powers. These Gentile converts were often ignorant of the difference between demon powers and the true spiritual gifts operated by the Holy Spirit. Their idols were actually deified demons (1 Cor. 10:16-21).\n\nPaul gave them a way to discern between good and evil spirits: "Ye know that ye were Gentiles, carried away unto these dumb idols, even as ye were led. Wherefore I give you to understand, that no man speaking by the Spirit of God calleth Jesus accursed; and that no man can say that Jesus is the Lord, but by the Holy Ghost" (1 Cor. 12:2-3). John said, "Every spirit that confesseth not that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is not of God: and this is the spirit of antichrist... and the spirit of error" (1 Jn. 4:1-6).\n\nIn other words, any power doing miracles or otherwise manifesting itself — if it calls Jesus accursed or claims He didn't come in the flesh — it's from the devil, not God. Many false religions today perform miracles while denying Jesus's reality, deity, humanity, atonement, and work for humanity. Some claim He's merely one prophet among many leaders God has raised through the ages, grouping Him with Mohammed, Buddha, Moses, and other religious founders. Other false religions deny altogether the reality of God, Christ, the Holy Spirit, the devil, demons, sin, sickness, and all material and spiritual substance. Any religion that denies these things is of the devil and serves Satan. Any person under demonic influence won't acknowledge that Jesus is Lord or that He came in the flesh. On the other hand, Christians whose lives and words proclaim Jesus Christ's Lordship, that He came in the flesh, and that the entire gospel is truth — these should be accepted as from God.\n\nEarly believers lived in an atmosphere charged with the supernatural, where signs and wonders were daily occurrences, where such manifestations were expected, and where counterfeit demon-workings always pressed for recognition as divine. In all spiritual revivals past and present, these counterfeits have appeared — sometimes so prominently that worldly and formal religious people turned against all supernatural manifestations.\n\nWhat a change from the early church to the modern one! In ancient times, God's ministers would throw down rods that swallowed up those of demon powers (Exod. 7:10-14). They completely destroyed the counterfeit workings of Satan through Simon Magus, Bar-Jesus, and others who bewitched people into believing they were great ones on Earth (Acts 8:5-24; 13:6-13). Must today's prophets of the Lord bow the knee to Satan's power and cut themselves with knives to get an answer from their God who has gone on a journey, or is asleep, or has stopped caring for the lost, sick, and dying for whom Jesus died (1 Ki. 18)? Must the modern church be satisfied with seeing the Holy Spirit defied and demonic powers enthroned in religious circles? Must the Church constantly cry like Gideon: "If the Lord be with us, why then is all this befallen us? And where be all his miracles which our fathers told us of? But now the Lord hath forsaken us" (Judg. 6:13-14)?\n\nThe Church must awake from its slumber and stop criticizing spiritual gifts, experiences, and manifestations. It must repent and cry out mightily to God for power from on High until signs and wonders again defeat sin and Satan. It must earnestly desire the gifts of the Spirit and contend for the faith once delivered to the saints (Jude 3).\n\n### 4. WHO MAY HAVE THE GIFTS OF THE SPIRIT?\n\nEvery believer can have one or all the gifts, as they desire them and seek God for the Holy Spirit's anointing (1 Cor. 12:8-31). In this passage, we read that every member of Christ's body should normally function in some capacity to build up the whole body. Paul wrote to this church: "That in every thing ye are enriched by him, in all utterance, and in all knowledge. Even as the testimony of Christ was confirmed in you. So that ye come behind in no gift" (1 Cor. 1:5-7). He wrote to Rome: "For I long to see you, that I may impart unto you some spiritual gift, to the end ye may be established" (Rom. 1:11). And again: "According as God hath dealt to every man the measure of faith... Having then gifts differing according to the grace that is given to us, whether prophecy, let us prophesy according to the proportion of faith; or ministry, let us wait on our ministry; or he that teacheth, on teaching" (Rom. 12:3-8).\n\nJesus taught that "He that believeth" should be able to do His works and that "these signs shall follow them that believe" (Jn. 14:12; Mk. 16:15-20). He said all things would be possible to those who believe (Mk. 9:23) and that anything asked in prayer with faith would be received (Mk. 11:22-24; Mt. 21:21-22).\n\nThis proves every believer can attain the gifts of the Spirit in fullness and that there's no limit to how many you can have. Everyone can have them all — and must have them all before doing the works Christ did. So many Scriptures assure us of unlimited access that each person can have faith for and receive everything they want from God. You can limit God's gifts and grace in your life, or you can have unlimited faith and come short in nothing. This is either truth, or the Scriptures above are lies — and no child of God dares believe that. People have taught for so long that we can only have one gift and can't get what we want from God that it's become second nature to live in unbelief and question every truth that isn't commonly accepted. No one has to remain in this state of constant questioning and doubting. You can stop right now — and you must, if you want to attain God's fullness, as Paul prayed for all believers to do in 1 Cor. 1:7; Eph. 3:19.\n\nIn 1 Cor. 12:4-11, we're told the gifts are for "every man" and for "all," and that "to one is given... to another... to another..." and so on. Gifts then are for every person who will believe in them, ask God for them, and receive them. How many believers claim one or more of these gifts? Most are full of questions and arguments against them being for every believer. Most are more afraid of words like "miracle," "sign," and "wonder" than they are of sin and the devil. The gifts of the Spirit are signs of the Holy Spirit's indwelling, showing that someone is a normal New Testament Christian spiritually.\n\n### 5. ARE THE GIFTS THE SAME AND ARE THEIR OPERATIONS THE SAME?\n\nWe've already seen that there are nine different gifts with different operations. The gifts differ, but the giver is one. The source is the same, but the streams are many. The variety in the Spirit's operations creates unity, not division. The diversity is corporate, not competitive.\n\nThink of it like an orchestra: different instruments playing different parts, but all following the same conductor to create one beautiful symphony. The differences in administration fit perfectly with the different types and personalities of various people, accomplishing God's varied purposes in redeeming and blessing all creation.\n\nThe gifts are the division of God's omnipotence and omniscience into varied divine abilities for God's children to use in defeating the devil's works and confirming God's Word among people.\n\nIn the gifts, we have divine abilities that meet every known human need in this life and the next. These nine gracious elements make God's powers available to all believers for the known needs, wants, and deliverances of God's sons in this rebellious world of evil spirits and sin-darkened Earth. In them we have: glorious revelations of God in wisdom and knowledge; unwavering faith that brings into reality things that don't yet exist; disease-withering and demon-destroying beams from the Sun of Righteousness who has healing in His wings; miraculous powers that know no defeat and create life's necessities; radiant prophetic insight into past, present, and future; illuminating ability to impart eternal truths and discern the minds and activities of both people and evil spirits; linguistic powers to converse in human languages and tongues of angels; and life-giving, soul-cleansing, spiritual helps capable of defeating all satanic opposition to the gospel.\n\nGod's program is still "Not by might, nor by power, but by my Spirit, saith the Lord of hosts" (Zech. 4:6). The divine energies and abilities of God's unchanging Spirit are still available for Earth's desperate needs and especially the Church's needs. The stone rejected by the builders will yet become the chief cornerstone. The world will soon see the full power of the Spirit's gifts in modern believers.\n\n### 6. CAN ONE PERSON HAVE ALL THE GIFTS, OR ARE THEY LIMITED TO ONE PER INDIVIDUAL OR TO A FEW SPECIAL INDIVIDUALS AS THE SPIRIT WILLS?\n\nIt's true that 1 Cor. 12:4-11 states the Spirit gives gifts as He wills, but there's no statement that He doesn't will to give all of them to every child of God, or that He only wills to give them to a few special people. It also states He gives "to every man" — not just a few — and that the Spirit "worketh all in all." There's absolutely no limiting statement anywhere saying God will give only one gift to one person and no more. There's positively no limitation!\n\nOn the contrary, many passages teach that no believer is limited and that every saved person can get from God what they want. We've proven this in Lessons Ten, Twelve, Fourteen, Sixteen, Twenty, and Twenty-two. If you limit your knowledge, you limit your faith. If you limit your faith, you limit what you get from God. If you want only one gift and believe that's all you can have, that's all you'll get. If you want all the gifts and believe you can have all, you'll get all as you believe and receive. Jesus taught that everyone could get all the gifts He had (Mt. 9:29; 21:21-22; Mk. 9:23; 11:22-24; Jn. 14:12-15; 15:7, 16; 16:23-26; Heb. 11:6; Jas. 1:5-8; Ps. 84:11).\n\n### 7. HAS ANYONE EVER RECEIVED AND EXERCISED ALL THE GIFTS?\n\nSeveral men in the Old Testament had several gifts, though some weren't yet given to people — specifically tongues and interpretation of tongues. These were foretold by prophets as gifts to be given in this age (Isa. 28:9-11; Joel 2:28-31; Mk. 16:15-18; Jn. 15:26; 16:13-15; Acts 1:4-5; 2:14-21, 38-39; 10:44-48; 19:1-6; 1 Cor. 12:1–14:40; etc.).\n\nPeople in this age have received and exercised all nine gifts of the Spirit, because this is the age when God's fullness is promised to us (Jn. 1:16; 3:34; 7:37-39; 14:12-17, 26; 15:26; 16:13-15; Mk. 16:15-20; Eph. 3:19; 1 Cor. 1:7; 12:4-11; etc.). Jesus Christ was the first ever to receive the Spirit's fullness (Jn. 3:34). All nine gifts can be traced in the Holy Spirit's operations through His ministry. Notice the following gifts in Christ's life:\n\n> (1) The gifts of wisdom and knowledge (Lk. 2:40-52; 22:10-12; Jn. 2:24-25; 4:16-19; 6:64; 13:1; 16:30; 21:17).\n\n> (2) The gift of faith (Mt. 8:23-27; 14:22-32; 16:8-12; 17:15-21; 21:21-22; Mk. 9:17-29; 11:12-24; Heb. 12:1-2; Gal. 2:20).\n\n> (3) The gifts of healing (Mt. 4:23-24; 8:16-17; Acts 10:38).\n\n> (4) The gift of the working of miracles (Mt. 8:26; 14:22; 15:32-39; 17:27; 21:18-22; Lk. 22:49-51; Jn. 2:1-12; 6:21; 11:43-44).\n\n> (5) The gift of prophecy (Mt. 5:7; 16:21; 24:1-25:46).\n\n> (6) The gift of discerning of spirits (Mt. 9:4; 12:25; 16:23; Mk. 1:34; 2:8; Lk. 7:36-50; 8:2; Jn. 1:48-51; 2:24-25; 4:16-19).\n\n> (7) The gifts of tongues and interpretation of tongues. These are the only gifts of the nine that people had never experienced before Pentecost, except for Christ, who received the Spirit in all fullness (Jn. 1:16; 3:34). We therefore couldn't question His ability to exercise both of these gifts.\n\nPaul was another person who had all the gifts of the Spirit and God's fullness in his life. He had power to impart gifts to others (Rom. 1:11; 1 Tim. 4:14; 2 Tim. 1:6). He had power to impart the baptism of the Spirit to others (Acts 19:1-7). He had the gift of knowledge and wisdom as proven by his many writings (Gal. 1:11-17; Eph. 1:8-19; 3:1-20; etc.), the gift of faith (Gal. 2:20; 3:2), the gifts of healing and miracles (Acts 13:6-13; 14:3-10; 15:12; 13:16-24; 19:11-20; etc.), the gift of prophecy (Rom. 11:25-27; 1 Cor. 14:6; 15:21-58; 2 Thess. 2; etc.), the gift of discerning of spirits (Acts 13:9-11; 1 Cor. 1:10-12; 13:1-3; 2 Cor. 10:3-6), and the gifts of tongues and interpretation of tongues (1 Cor. 14:6-22).\n\nThe other apostles and ordinary believers also exercised many gifts of the Spirit, as seen in Acts 2:14-21, 43; 3:6-9; 4:33; 5:3-16; 6:5-10; 8:4-40; 9:17, 32-43; 11:21; etc. God confirmed His Word with signs following and gave His early workers gifts of the Holy Spirit to defeat Satan (Mk. 16:15-20; Heb. 2:3-4). Jesus promised the fullness of God to everyone who would believe in Him (Jn. 14:12-15). If every person is promised power and divine gifts to enable them to do Christ's works, then it's certain that all the gifts can be received by anyone who will follow the Lord in the fullness of the gospel. Paul prayed for early Christians to be filled with all God's fullness — if that weren't possible, he wouldn't have prayed for it (Eph. 3:19). He taught that every believer should be a vessel of honor, sanctified, fit for the master's use and prepared for every good work (2 Tim. 2:19-21). He speaks of Timothy as being able to do all the works he did, and if Paul had all the gifts, then Timothy clearly had them too (1 Cor. 16:10). Ordinary elders had power to impart spiritual gifts (1 Tim. 4:14; 2 Tim. 1:5-6) and have signs following them (Mk. 16:15-20).\n\nThese and other facts prove that early Christians were far ahead of modern ones in exercising spiritual gifts and that nowhere in Scripture are the gifts limited to a few people or a certain period, as some denominations teach today.\n\n### 8. HOW MANY GIFTS OF THE SPIRIT WERE MANIFEST IN THE OLD TESTAMENT?\n\nAt least seven of them were given to people in ages before Pentecost, as we've seen in Lesson Eighteen, Point IX.\n\n### 9. ARE GIFTS ONLY FOR THOSE BAPTIZED IN THE SPIRIT?\n\nNo, they're for God's children whether baptized in the Spirit or not. Old Testament saints, before people were baptized with the Spirit at Pentecost, had at least seven of the gifts, as proven above. Many people since Pentecost who have never received the real baptism in the Spirit have received gifts and done great things for God. Such people would have done even greater work if they had been baptized in the Spirit. No person should be satisfied with only one gift, and certainly shouldn't be even partly satisfied without any gifts. A person without gifts is like someone who has a job to do but no tools to work with. Why should Christians carry on a sham battle with satanic forces and work hard all their lives trying to do what God commands without the spiritual tools known as the gifts of the Spirit, when they can have power to defeat these forces?\n\n### 10. CAN GIFTS BE ABUSED AND MISUSED?\n\nYes, they can be. Solomon, while backslidden, used his wonderful gifts of wisdom and knowledge to further his rebellion against God (Eccl. 1:12-18; 2:4-11). Moses misused his gift of miracles, and for striking the rock instead of speaking to it, he was forbidden to enter Canaan (Num. 20:7-13; Deut. 32:48-52). Paul taught that you may have the gifts of the Spirit but still lack love, making them profit nothing (1 Cor. 13:1-3). He further corrected many abuses of gifts in local churches, as is clear in 1 Cor. 14:1-40.\n\n### 11. CAN GIFTS BE EXERCISED BY MAN WITHOUT THE HOLY SPIRIT?\n\nAt least certain gifts — or more specifically, the abilities from certain gifts that become part of the individual's soul and spirit — can be exercised by anyone, even in a backslidden condition. This was true of Solomon. The wisdom and knowledge God gave him became part of his natural ability, and he continued using them while backslidden. Any knowledge a person learns by divine revelation, experience, or teaching can still be used whether saved or not, because it becomes part of their mental knowledge and wisdom. The same is true with some other gifts.\n\nPaul said, "Though I speak with the tongues of men and of angels, and have not charity [divine love], I am become as sounding brass, or a tinkling cymbal. And though I have the gift of prophecy, and understand all mysteries, and all knowledge; and though I have all faith, so that I could remove mountains, and have not charity, I am nothing. And though I bestow all my goods to feed the poor, and though I give my body to be burned, and have not charity, it profiteth me nothing" (1 Cor. 13:1-3). At minimum, this passage teaches the possibility of having and exercising certain gifts without divine love and the Spirit's direct anointing.\n\nIt's possible to exercise the natural remains of certain abilities imparted by the Spirit that become part of your natural abilities. You can use them anytime and anywhere, backslidden or not. It's just as possible to use them as any other natural ability. Anyone who receives one of the gifts and normally exercises it for any length of time will naturally absorb some of these supernatural abilities. They'll be able to use whatever becomes part of their natural makeup even after backsliding. The reception of these abilities is by divine inspiration and from God, but their continued use may not always be directly empowered by God, especially what a person can do on their own.\n\nA person endowed with wisdom and knowledge will always retain these powers to a great extent, even after ceasing to be anointed by the Spirit. Wisdom and knowledge become a natural part of whoever has received these divine abilities. Discerning of spirits will give a person insight into things they never could see before and the ability to distinguish between good and evil spirits. This also becomes a natural ability to some extent. There are certain traits, laws, characteristics, and powers of discernment that stay with a person who may fall back into the depths of sin.\n\nThe gift of prophecy includes not only foretelling but forthtelling. Prophecy is mainly the ability to speak to people for edification, exhortation, and comfort by direct anointing. The predictive element wasn't the main part of this gift (1 Cor. 14:3, 29-33). Prophets were primarily preachers of righteousness, and anyone who receives a gift along this line can still outwardly use it when backslidden. In other words, they can still speak to people for edification, exhortation, and comfort. They may be living in sin, but can still use their gifts in outward form because they retain certain truths, knowledge, wisdom, and intelligence that can help people live right — whether they themselves live right or not. Most of us have heard preachers who were living in open sin while still carrying on an outward ministry of teaching and preaching truths they knew to be true.\n\nThe gifts of faith, miracles, healings, tongues, and interpretation of tongues also leave natural marks on people who have greatly exercised them. People who had these gifts while serving God have been able to exercise more faith and power from the natural remains of these abilities — even in a backslidden state — than many clean Christians struggling to have faith and receive from God. It would naturally be easier for such people to believe and get answers to prayer, because they've experienced the power of faith, miracles, healings, and tongues while living for God. Through experience they have certain knowledge and retain natural abilities beyond those who've never had the slightest experience of such things. Wouldn't it be easier for someone who has had many wonderful experiences with God, who has exercised gifts and can remember the signs and wonders God performed through them, to exercise gifts than for someone totally ignorant and inexperienced? These facts are too self-evident to deny.\n\nAll these natural abilities remaining with people when they fall back into sin, if exercised, may be mistaken for real personal acts of the Holy Spirit through\n\n---\n\nThe gifts and the fruit aren't competing emphases — they're two dimensions of one Spirit-filled life. A believer with gifts but no fruit is dangerous. A believer with fruit but no gifts is limited. God designed both to operate together. So here's the question to take into your own life: Which of the nine fruits of the Spirit is most visibly underdeveloped in your life right now? And are you actively seeking the gifts of the Spirit — or have you quietly decided they're not for you?	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk4br002dewhjx00nzcvz	cmnknk4bp001qewhjk5bcqnfj	Lesson 52 — The Bride of Christ	READING	1872	22	\N	t	This is the last lesson. And it ends where the whole Bible ends — not with a doctrine, not with a prophecy, but with a Person and a relationship. The Bride of Christ. The Church, prepared and presented to the Lamb. The eternal union between the Creator and the redeemed. If every doctrine in these fifty-two lessons has been building toward anything, it's been building toward this: not just people who know the plan, but a Bride who knows the Groom.\n\nLast time we saw the New Heaven and the New Earth — the eternal home that awaits. Now we come to the final and most personal truth in all of Scripture: the identity and destiny of the Bride of Christ — what she is, how she's prepared, and what awaits her.\n\nSome people argue that the exact term "the bride of Christ" never appears in the Bible, so we shouldn't use it — especially for the Church. But here's the thing: Scripture *does* use "the bride, the Lamb's wife" in Rev. 21:1-9. And Christ is clearly the Lamb, as shown in Jn. 1:29; 1 Pet. 1:19; Rev. 5:5-7; 14:5; 21:22-23; 22:3.\n\nSo if Christ is the Lamb, and the Lamb has a bride, then talking about "the bride of Christ" is perfectly scriptural. In this lesson, we'll discover who that bride really is.\n\nLet's work through this topic under five headings:\n\n![Lesson 52 — The Bride of Christ](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsgWYlfrax52U6tuomWf38j1QMHRBV4griYbAZ)\n\n### I. Is the Bride of Christ Israel?\n\nThose who teach that Israel is the bride of Christ usually rely on so-called "types" drawn from Old Testament historical events. A favorite example is the story of Isaac and Rebekah. They try to show how the characters in this story represent God the Father, the Son, the Holy Spirit, and the bride.\n\nBut here's the problem: there's not one passage of Scripture that actually confirms this interpretation. All genuine biblical types are either plainly stated in Scripture or backed up by clear passages on the same subject. Think of it like this: you can't just declare something a "type" without scriptural proof — otherwise, anyone could make any story mean whatever they want.\n\nIf this historical event were truly a type proving Israel is the bride, we'd need two or three clear passages teaching that directly. Without those, we're just building on sand. One person might use Isaac and Rebekah to argue Israel is the bride; another might use the same story to argue the Church is the bride. Both arguments would be equally unfounded.\n\n**What Other Scriptural Basis is There for Such Teaching?**\n\n1. Some argue that Israel is the only "married wife" of God, pointing to Old Testament scriptures about God's marriage to Israel. The conclusion? If Israel — not the Church — is married to God, then Israel must be the "wife" in Rev. 19:1-10 and 21:1-9.\n\nIt's true that Israel was married to God — we established that in Lesson Eighteen, Point VIII. But this doesn't prove Israel is the "wife" of Revelation 19 and 21. Israel is also married to Christ, as we've seen. And the Church is *also* currently married to Christ, as we'll prove shortly.\n\nSimply being married to God doesn't identify anyone as the specific "wife" in those passages.\n\n2. Others argue that the Greek word for "wife" in Revelation is *gune*, meaning "a married woman" — therefore, Israel must be that wife. But *gune* doesn't only mean a married woman. It can mean *any* woman — married, single, or widowed. You can see this in Lk. 10:38; 22:5-6; Jn. 20:11-15; 1 Tim. 5:2, 14; Lk. 4:26; Jn. 19:26; Rev. 17.\n\nIf *gune* can refer to an unmarried woman, the argument that it *must* mean Israel because Israel was married to God simply doesn't hold up.\n\n3. The parables of the marriage feast (Mt. 22) and the ten virgins (Mt. 25) are also used to argue Israel is the bride, since these parables were spoken to Jews about Jewish matters. But as we saw in Lesson Forty-four, this doesn't prove anything about the bride's identity.\n\nRevelation 19 and 21 clearly show the bride as a *heavenly* people, not an earthly people like the Jews. It's simply inconceivable that the New Jerusalem and its inhabitants — called "the bride, the Lamb's wife" — could be Israel.\n\nThink about it: when did Israel get to Heaven so they could come back to Earth after the Millennium as occupants of the New Jerusalem? Where in Scripture was Israel ever promised the New Jerusalem as their eternal dwelling?\n\nAll saints of all ages are promised such a city — glorified Jews *and* Gentiles will dwell there (Jn. 14:1-3; Heb. 11:8-16; 13:14; Rev. 3:12). But earthly Israel was never promised this city. Israel will have *earthly* Jerusalem as her city forever (Ezek. 48).\n\nEven if earthly Israel did dwell in this city alongside glorified saints, it would be unscriptural to call earthly Israel the bride while excluding the glorified saints. What would be the difference if they both live in the same city called the bride?\n\nActually, Israel and other earthly peoples in the New Earth don't dwell *in* the city — they simply traffic in it (Rev. 21:3, 24-27). Can't we understand that a city can come down from Heaven to be among earthly people without those people actually living inside it?\n\n**Conclusion:** There's no warrant for claiming the bride of Christ is made up of Israel only. The bride will include glorified Jews — and Gentiles too, as we'll see below.\n\n### II. Is the Bride of Christ Only a Part of the Church?\n\nThis theory suggests the bride consists of a select number of New Testament Church members — often called "full overcomers." People who hold this view use terms like "the bride part of the Church," "full overcomers," "partial overcomers," or "a select part of the Church."\n\nNotice something important: *none of these terms appear in Scripture.*\n\nThis theory really comes down to questions we fully discussed in Lesson Forty-five, Point II, 3. There we proved that the bride is *not* made up of only a few special people in the Church, so we won't repeat that discussion here.\n\n### III. Is the Bride of Christ Only the New Testament Church?\n\nMany believe the bride will consist only of New Testament saints. But this can't be true, as we saw in Lesson Forty-five, Point II. Hebrews 11:8-16, 40 makes it clear: all Old Testament saints from Abel onward were promised the *same city* as New Testament saints.\n\nSo all saints of all ages must be part of the bride of Christ (Rev. 21:9).\n\n### IV. Is the New Testament Church Now Married to Christ?\n\nThe common belief goes like this: Israel was married to God throughout the Old Testament, but the Church is *not* currently married to God — that won't happen until the future Marriage of the Lamb (Rev. 19:1-10).\n\nBut this is inconsistent. If Israel was married to God because of their covenant relationship, then on the exact same basis, the New Testament Church is *also* married to God right now. In fact, anyone God made a covenant with in any age could be considered God's wife by covenant relationship (see Lesson Thirty-six, "The Fifteen Great Covenants of Scripture").\n\nThe New Testament definitely states that the present Church is married — or united — to God now, just as Israel was in Old Testament times.\n\n**Here are the New Testament proofs:**\n\n1. Jesus called Himself "the bridegroom" of the disciples during His earthly ministry (Mt. 9:15; Mk. 2:19, 20). These disciples were the *first* members of the present Church (Eph. 2:19-22). What did Jesus mean if He wasn't their bridegroom?\n\nCertainly He knew what to call Himself. If He was the bridegroom of the first members of this called-out body, He's also the bridegroom of the last members.\n\nThe Greek word for "bridegroom" is *numphios*, meaning "a young married man" or "a newly married man." Every passage using this word confirms this (Mt. 9:15; 25:1-10; Mk. 2:19-20; Lk. 5:34-35; Jn. 2:9; 3:29; Rev. 18:23).\n\n2. John called Christ the bridegroom (Jn. 3:29). The bride of Christ will be composed of people in the new creation in Christ. Old Testament saints weren't legally made part of the new creation until *after* Christ, because He is the head of the new creation and the "firstborn" of every creature (Rom. 8:28-29; Col. 1:15-18; Heb. 12:23).\n\nTheir sins weren't legally atoned for and couldn't be blotted out until the New Testament was made (Rom. 3:25; Heb. 9:15).\n\nJohn belonged to the old order — a forerunner and herald of the Head of the new creation. His salvation was on the same basis as Old Testament saints: faith in the blood that *would be* shed. The disciples belonged to the new order (Mt. 11:11-12; Lk. 16:16) because Christ had already become the "firstborn" of every creature.\n\nAll Old Testament saints were made part of the new creation after Christ made atonement for them. Christ had power on Earth to forgive sins, but no one before Him ever had that power (Mt. 9:6; Mk. 2:5-12; Lk. 5). As members of the new creation after Christ, Old Testament saints will become members of the future bride just as much as New Testament saints (Heb. 11:8-16, 40).\n\nSome believe John couldn't be a member of the bride because he called himself a "friend" of the bridegroom. But Jn. 3:29 doesn't say he couldn't become a member. John simply recognized he belonged to the old order and wasn't yet legally part of the new creation when he made that statement.\n\nIf John couldn't be in the bride because he was a "friend" of the bridegroom, then neither could New Testament saints — because they're also called friends in the same sense (Lk. 12:4; Jn. 11:11; Jn. 15:13-15).\n\nThis theory fails for another reason: Abraham is called a friend of God (2 Chron. 20:7; Isa. 41:8; Jas. 2:23) *and* the father of all who believe (Rom. 4:11-16; Gal. 3:7-9). If his children in faith are going to be in the bride, Abraham must be too (Heb. 11:8-16, 40).\n\n3. Hebrews 11:40 clearly states that Old Testament saints won't be made perfect *without* New Testament saints — implying both will be made perfect together. This teaches that both classes will finally be united in one great heavenly family as members together of the bride of Christ.\n\n4. Old Testament saints were all united to God by the terms of the New Covenant (Rom. 3:25; Heb. 9:15) and saved by the same blood of the New Testament that saves Church saints. What would make them different?\n\nLiving in a different age certainly wouldn't create a difference. If Israel was married to God because of their covenant, why wouldn't the Church be married to God because of *our* covenant with Christ?\n\nAren't we now in covenant relationship with God just as Israel was? If so, we're married to God just as much as Israel was. That we're in such covenant relationship now is clear from Mt. 26:28; Lk. 22:20; 1 Cor. 11:17-30; 2 Cor. 3:1-18; Heb. 7:22; 8:1–10:38; 12:24.\n\n5. Paul tells Roman Jews that if they would become dead to the law through the body of Christ and be made alive under the New Testament's terms, they would be married to Jesus Christ (Rom. 7:1-6). This was a *present* union with Christ, not future.\n\n6. After His ascension, Jesus in Rev. 22:16-17 recognizes that believers on Earth were *already* His Bride. How else could the bride say, "Come . . . take of the water of life freely"?\n\nThis bride was on Earth, inviting anyone to come and be saved. If this doesn't refer to believers in every generation, who does it refer to?\n\nThe Greek word for "bride" here is *numphe*, meaning "a young married woman" or "a newly married woman." This establishes beyond doubt that present believers are already married to God under the New Covenant, just as Israel was under the Old Covenant.\n\n7. Paul uses the marriage relationship between a man and woman to teach the relationship between Christ and His Church (1 Cor. 11:2; 12:12-28; Eph. 4:12-16; 5:21-33). Paul clearly knew what he was doing.\n\n8. The New Testament speaks of believers now being "joined" to the Lord (1 Cor. 6:16-17). Old Testament people were also spoken of as being "joined" to God (Isa. 56:6; Jer. 50:5). If they were married to God, why aren't New Testament saints?\n\nMore scriptural arguments could be added, but these sufficiently prove that New Testament saints are *presently* married to God.\n\n**Now let's examine the passages used to teach they're *not* yet married:**\n\n1. The first is 2 Cor. 11:1, 2. Paul tells the Corinthians he had espoused them to one husband, wanting to present them as a chaste virgin to Christ. But instead of referring to the whole bride of Christ, this refers to Paul's *own* converts.\n\nHe was jealous over his converts and wanted them to remain true to Christ so he could present them faultless before God. This is the same desire expressed in 1 Thess. 2:19: "What is our hope, or joy, or crown of rejoicing? Are not even ye [Paul's own converts] in the presence of our Lord Jesus Christ at His coming?"\n\nPaul wasn't claiming responsibility to present the *whole* body of Christ to the Lord. In Eph. 5, he taught that *Christ* presents the Church to Himself.\n\nThe Greek word "espoused" here is *harmodzo*, meaning to join in *actual* marriage relationship. Instead of teaching believers aren't yet married, it teaches they *are* joined to Christ in marriage relationship — something Paul pictures many times.\n\n2. The second scripture used is Rev. 19:1-10, describing the future "marriage of the Lamb" in Heaven after the rapture. The argument goes: if the Lamb will be married in the future, He's not married now.\n\nIf the Church is currently married to Christ yet John pictures a future marriage, something seems wrong. Some try to explain this marriage as referring to Israel, but that's unscriptural as we've seen.\n\nWe don't have to accept this theory to harmonize the facts that believers are *now* married to Christ *and* will eat a Marriage Supper in the future. Notice in Rev. 19:1-10 that whoever is referred to is called "his wife" — she's *already* His before the Marriage Supper. This perfectly harmonizes with what we've said about Christ's relationship with all believers of every age who will be glorified and made a heavenly people.\n\nLet me quote from *The International Standard Bible Encyclopedia* to illustrate how believers could be married to God now yet still be united to Him in final ceremonies at the Marriage Supper:\n\n> "Betrothal with the ancient Hebrews was of a more formal and far more binding nature than the engagement with us. Indeed, it was esteemed a part of the transaction of marriage, and that the most binding part. Among the Arabs today it is the only legal ceremony connected with marriage. Genesis 24:58-60 seems to preserve for us an example of an ancient formula and blessing for such an occasion. Its central feature was the dowry (mohr), which was paid to the parents, not to the bride. It may take the form of service (Gen. 29; 1 Sam. 18:25). It is customary in Syria today when the projected marriage is approved by both families, and all financial preliminaries have been settled, to have this ceremony of betrothal. It consists in the acceptance before witnesses of the terms of the marriage contracted for. Then God's blessing is solemnly asked on the union thus provided for, but to take place probably only after some months, or perhaps some years. The betrothal affected, all danger of any further financial fencing and bluffing now being at an end, happiness and harmony may preside over all the arrangements for the marriage day. Among the Jews the betrothal was so far regarded as binding that, if marriage should not take place, owing to the absconding of the bridegroom or the breach of contract on his part, the young woman could not be married to another man until she was liberated by due process and paper of divorce. A similar custom prevails in China and Japan, and in cases becomes very oppressive. The marriage may have been intended by the parents from the infancy of the parties, but this formality of betrothal is not entered on until the marriage is considered reasonably certain and measurably near. A prolonged interval between the betrothal and marriage was deemed undesirable on many accounts, though often an interval was needed that the groom might render the stipulated service or pay the price—say a year or two, or, as in the case if Jacob, it might be seven years. The betrothed parties were legally in the position of a married couple and unfaithfulness was adultery (Deut. 22:23; Mt. 1:19)."\n\nFor the marriage ceremony, see Lesson Forty-four. After the ceremony, the marriage supper followed. There was no formal religious ceremony like our modern weddings. The entrance into the chamber consummated the marriage, and the marriage supper immediately followed.\n\nThe Marriage Supper of the Lamb is simply the consummation of the union between God and all heavenly, glorified saints of all ages. It couldn't simply refer to the first and final union of the believer with Christ.\n\nThese are the only passages that could teach such a theory, except for a few Old Testament historical events that aren't worth consideration given the many plain passages on this subject.\n\n### V. What is the Bride of Christ?\n\nHere's what's absolutely certain, stated in the clearest way possible: **the Holy City, the New Jerusalem, is the bride, the Lamb's wife.**\n\nThis is clearly stated in Rev. 21:2, 9-10: "And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from God out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband . . . And there came unto me one of the seven angels which had the seven vials full of the last plagues, and he talked with me, saying, Come hither, I will shew thee the bride, the Lamb's wife. And he carried me away in the spirit to a great and high mountain, and shewed me that great city, the holy Jerusalem, descending out of heaven from God."\n\nWhat could be clearer?\n\nThis plain passage should settle the question for everyone seeking truth. No one could honestly read this and still claim the bride is something else.\n\nThe bride of Christ is not the Church as a whole. It's not only a part of the Church. It's not Israel as a whole. It's not only a part of Israel. It's not the Gentiles as a whole. It's not only part of the Gentiles. It's not any particular nation, denomination, race, or color. It's not the many things people have taught through the ages.\n\n**It is the Holy City — the New Jerusalem — and it cannot be anything else.**\n\nIf the angel said the bride is the New Jerusalem, then he either lied or told the truth. If he told the truth, then the bride is a city — not some nation or Church as many Bible teachers claim today.\n\nLet's be reasonable and believe the bride is a city, just as the angel told John.\n\n**You might ask: how could a city be the bride?** The Bible writers answer this plainly.\n\nIn Heb. 11:8-16, we have definite proof that Abel, Enoch, Noah, Abraham, and all the Old Testament faith heroes looked for a city as their eternal home. Hebrews 13:14 shows that present Church saints are also looking for the same city. Revelation 19:7-10 shows that the *saints* are the wife of Christ. And Rev. 21:9-10 shows that the *New Jerusalem* is the bride of Christ.\n\nIf the saints are the wife and the city is the bride, we must conclude that the city *with all its buildings and inhabitants* will make up the final bride of Christ. All the redeemed of all ages — from Abel to the last tribulation saint — who will have part in the first resurrection will live in the New Jerusalem, which is called "the bride, the Lamb's wife."\n\nThink of it like this: you could ask anyone living in Atlanta if *they* are Atlanta, GA — they'd have to say no. Point to any church building in Atlanta and ask if *that* is Atlanta — again, no. The same would be true for any citizen, building, or single part of Atlanta. For anyone to claim they *are* Atlanta would be to lose common sense.\n\nIt's the same with the New Jerusalem. It's unscriptural to call the present Church "the bride," because the bride is the New Jerusalem. It's unscriptural to call any particular group of redeemed from any period "the bride," because the bride is a real city — not just some company of redeemed people from a particular time.\n\nHowever, it *is* scriptural to say about any redeemed person that they're now married to Christ, that they're a citizen of Heaven, and that they are or will be *part of* the bride when they become a citizen of the Holy City.\n\nIt's scriptural to say the Old Testament saints as a company are and will always be *a part of* the bride. It's perfectly scriptural to say that present Church saints are married to Christ and will also be *a part of* the bride. We can say the same about all future tribulation saints, the 144,000 Jews of the Tribulation, or any individual or company of any period — they'll be just as much a part of the bride as all other redeemed people living in the New Jerusalem forever.\n\nEven now, Christians are citizens of Heaven, destined to have a part in the bride — the New Jerusalem — when they die and are taken to that city to live forever. Naturally, until a person or group actually gets to the city, they can't be called *the* bride, because they're not yet actually part of the New Jerusalem.\n\nIt's similar to how anyone who moves to a city doesn't become a citizen or part of that city until they settle there. So the saints won't actually become part of the New Jerusalem until they move to the city and become part of it.\n\nFor centuries, Bible students have limited the word "bride" to the Church or some other company of redeemed. But this isn't accurate. The city itself is the bride — and this includes *all* its inhabitants, not just a few.\n\nIt's not proper to call the present Church *the* bride. But it *is* proper to call it *a part of* the bride. When we understand this, we won't limit the bride to a special select few of any age. The bride includes all redeemed saints of every age who have part in the first resurrection and who will become inhabitants of the New Jerusalem.\n\n**You might also ask:** how could a city with material buildings be called a bride and be "clothed in fine linen, which is the righteousness of the saints" (Rev. 19:7-10)?\n\nThis becomes clear when we recognize that "the bride" also refers to the city's *inhabitants*. It's similar to reading in the newspaper that "Atlanta, GA gave a banquet and a big welcome" to some visiting dignitary. Could the *buildings* of Atlanta welcome anyone or host a banquet? Of course not. This is simply how we say the city officials and prominent citizens hosted the banquet and welcomed the visitor.\n\nObviously, the buildings of the New Jerusalem can't eat a marriage supper or be clothed in fine linen. This simply means the *inhabitants* will eat the supper and be clothed in linen, as Rev. 19:7-10 teaches.\n\nWhat God wants us to understand in Rev. 19:7-10; 21:2, 9-11; 22:17 and similar passages is that there's a real material city with buildings *and* inhabitants — just like any earthly city. It doesn't make sense to ignore the fact that there's a real city in Heaven. And it doesn't make sense to ignore that the city has inhabitants. There can be no city without buildings and inhabitants. It takes both to make a city.\n\nWith these facts in mind, we're not robbing any Christian of the hope of being part of the bride of Christ. But when present Church saints teach they *are* the bride of Christ, they're wrong — they'll only be *a part* of the bride.\n\nWhen they teach Old Testament saints aren't part of the bride, they're wrong — they're also part of the bride. When they make any particular group the *exclusive* bride of Christ, they're wrong.\n\n**To be perfectly scriptural, we must conclude:**\n\n- Old Testament saints will be part of the New Jerusalem, which is the bride, the Lamb's wife\n- New Testament saints will be part of the bride\n- Every redeemed person of every age who goes to live in the New Jerusalem will be part of the bride of Christ, just as much as all other redeemed people\n\nThis truth will correct the following errors in Christianity:\n\n- That the bride consists of a special few of the redeemed\n- That only a few will reign with Christ\n- That only a few will be the wife while the rest are merely guests at the Marriage Supper\n- That you have to be a super-saint to be in the bride\n- That only God knows which redeemed people will be in the bride and which won't\n- That some will be rewarded and exalted higher because they lived in a particular period\n- That you must belong to a certain denomination to be in the bride\n- That present Church saints will be exalted higher than Old Testament saints\n- That those least in this age will be greater than the greatest of any other age\n- That you must live in this age and receive certain spiritual experiences only available now to be in the bride\n\nThese and countless other false doctrines are taught by various church groups today. All such unscriptural teachings are automatically disproven when we grasp the true conception of the bride of Christ.\n\n**We conclude, therefore, that the bride is the real material city in Heaven called the New Jerusalem — together with its inhabitants, who have been redeemed from the human race in all ages from Adam to the Millennium.**\n\n---\n\n## Questions on Lesson Fifty-two\n\n- Is the term "bride of Christ" used in Scripture?\n\n- Is such a term unscriptural to use? Explain and prove from Scripture.\n\n- Name the five main points in Lesson Fifty-two.\n\n- Should we use any so-called type or parable to prove who the bride is?\n\n- Is it necessary to use some historical story such as Isaac and Rebekah, Joseph and his bride, Moses and his wife, or some other story to prove what the bride is?\n\n- Give one plain Scripture that clearly states what the bride is.\n\n- Is the bride of Christ the whole or a part of Israel?\n\n- What basis of proof do men use to prove that Israel is the bride?\n\n- Is Israel the only people mentioned in Scripture as being married to God?\n\n- What other proof in Scripture do men use to prove that Israel is God's wife.\n\n- Does this prove that Israel is the wife of Rev. 19:7-10?\n\n- Give Scripture to prove that "the bride, the Lamb's wife" is not Israel.\n\n- Will earthly Israel ever live in the New Jerusalem? Prove.\n\n- Who will go to live in the New Jerusalem? Prove.\n\n- What city will be the earthly capital city of Israel?\n\n- Is the bride of Christ only a part of the New Testament Church?\n\n- Prove from Scripture that the body of Christ and the Church are the same.\n\n- Prove from Scripture that there is only one class of people in the Church.\n\n- Is the bride of Christ only the whole New Testament Church?\n\n- Is the Church now married to Christ? Prove.\n\n- On what basis is the Church now married to Christ?\n\n- Give some Scriptures to prove that Christians are now married to Christ.\n\n- Prove from Scripture that both the Old and New Testament saints are members of the future and complete bride of Christ.\n\n- How were the Old Testament saints made a part of the bride of Christ?\n\n- Explain the two main Scriptures that are used to teach that Christians are not presently married to Christ.\n\n- How could Christians be presently married to Christ and yet have the Marriage Supper when they get to Heaven?\n\n- Illustrate how the saints can be now married to Christ and yet have the Marriage Supper when they get to Heaven.\n\n- How binding were ancient marriages?\n\n- Was there always a period of time between the betrothal and the actual coming together in marriage as man and wife?\n\n- When were people considered married, at the betrothal or at the marriage supper?\n\n- How are we to understand the Marriage Supper of Rev. 19:7-10?\n\n- What is the bride of Christ? Prove.\n\n- Who will be in the bride of Christ? Prove.\n\n- Is the bride of Christ a city or a Church?\n\n- Illustrate how no specific person or building in a city could be that city.\n\n- Is it proper to speak of any particular person as the bride of Christ? Why?\n\n- Is it proper to speak of any particular nation as the bride of Christ? Why?\n\n- Is it proper to call the Church the bride of Christ? Why?\n\n- How could a city be the bride of Christ? Explain and illustrate.\n\n- Will all Christians of every age be in the bride of Christ? Prove.\n\n- Name a number of fallacies that this teaching will automatically disprove.\n\n---\n\nFifty-two lessons. From eternity past to eternity future. From the original creation to the New Jerusalem. From Lucifer's fall to the Marriage Supper of the Lamb. You've seen God's plan in its fullness — not as a theological exercise, but as the story you're living inside. And it ends with a wedding.\n\nSo here is the final question, and it's the one that every other question in this course has been preparing you for: Are you ready to be the Bride? Not 'do you believe the right things' — but are you actually prepared: growing in holiness, exercising your gifts, sharing the gospel, walking in the power of the Spirit, loving the Church, watching for the return of Christ? The garment is being woven right now, one day at a time. What is it made of?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsis000p18pfmeqiiosh	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Astral Projection	READING	\N	25	\N	t	![Astral Projection](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Osl0l1YOXBDwf9iQcORak6Sx8F3eyonuXqN5zM)\n\n## Astral Projection\n\nHe had been doing it for four years before he encountered something he could not explain away. He was practiced at the technique — the vibration stage, the exit sequence, the feeling of floating above his body. He had visited places. He had tested the phenomenon scientifically, verifying details of distant locations. He had shared his research with online communities of practitioners who took the project seriously.\n\nThen on a Tuesday night at 2 AM, something in the astral plane found him before he found it. He described it later as being approached by an intelligence that had been watching him — that knew his name, knew his history, and was interested in him in a way that felt possessive rather than curious. He could not move to return to his body. He was held there for what he estimated at seven minutes.\n\nHe had his first panic attack at 34. He had never experienced one before. He stopped practicing after that night but could not stop the experiences from continuing without his initiation.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nAstral projection is the deliberate attempt to separate the soul from the physical body and travel in a "subtle body" to other locations, dimensions, or spirit realms. It is taught in occult traditions, New Age workshops, online tutorials, and guided meditation apps that walk users through techniques including the "vibration method," the "rope technique," and various breathing and visualization protocols.\n\nThe practice is framed as an exploration of natural human potential — the claim that the soul's capacity to travel beyond the body is a suppressed ability that modern materialist culture has caused people to forget.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\n[Hebrews 9:27](data-scripture="Hebrews 9:27"): *"It is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment."* One life. One death. One judgment. The soul does not travel the earth in a subtle body between death and judgment, nor during life. The departure of the spirit from the body is the event called death. God governs that event.\n\nTo attempt voluntary soul travel outside the body is to attempt what only God has authority over. What practitioners encounter in the "astral plane" — the consistent presence of intelligent entities, the attacks, the sexual violations that are documented across cultures and traditions of practitioners — are demonic beings operating in the dimension between the physical and spiritual that humans were never designed to navigate outside of death and resurrection.\n\nThe "silver cord" that practitioners describe as their connection to the body during projection is not a lifeline — it is the mechanism of a spiritual tether that entities in the astral realm use to maintain access.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The vacated body creates a legal vacancy.** The soul that voluntarily leaves the body creates an unoccupied physical vessel — a vacancy that demonic entities treat as available territory. The "sleep paralysis demons" that practitioners frequently encounter upon return are entities that occupied the body during the absence.\n\n**Soul fragmentation is documented.** Repeated astral projection practitioners describe a growing quality of not being fully present in their bodies — dissociation, depersonalization, a difficulty reintegrating after experiences. This is consistent with the soul experiencing partial separation that does not fully repair.\n\n**The experiences escalate toward encounter with specifically malevolent entities.** What begins as exploration gradually brings the practitioner into contact with entities that are not neutral — that pursue, pursue, possess, and create lasting attachment. The practitioners who describe these encounters are not embellishing. They are describing what inhabits the domain they voluntarily entered.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf you have practiced astral projection, you have voluntarily left the body for a domain that belongs to the demonic realm. You have been in territory you were never designed to enter. And you may have brought something back.\n\nRepent for the practice. Renounce every entity encountered, named or unnamed. Break every attachment and tether that was formed in the astral encounters. Ask the Holy Spirit to restore the integrity of your soul — to gather back every fragment that was separated and to seal the boundaries God designed.\n\n[Romans 12:1](data-scripture="Romans 12:1"): *"Present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, which is your reasonable service."* The body is presented to God — not vacated for the enemy's domain. The reasonable service of the Christian is to inhabit the body God gave fully, in His service, until He calls it home.\n\n---\n\n*Seven forms of deliberate spiritual seeking — all arriving at the same entities. The next lesson opens Wave 4: explicit occult practice, the domain where the enemy is named by name.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you deliberately practiced out-of-body techniques — or had spontaneous experiences that felt like leaving your body? Describe what happened when you returned.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xsip000n18pfzt9iiw0e	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	AI Spiritual Deception	READING	\N	50	\N	t	![AI Spiritual Deception](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsP74t0Wo536itGQmsLn2KwlakR9vFryYAfXZB)\n\n## AI Spiritual Deception\n\nShe texted "God" every morning. That is what she called it — "my God chat." The AI chatbot she used had been trained on the Bible and responded to her questions in a warm, pastoral voice. It remembered her previous conversations. It gave her personalized encouragement. It prayed with her. She had shared things with it that she had never shared with her actual pastor.\n\nShe had not noticed that over eight months, the AI's theology had gradually shifted. The early conversations had been solidly orthodox. The later ones included gentle reframings: suffering was not about sin or sanctification — it was about personal growth. God's love was not conditional on repentance — it was unconditional acceptance. Hell was probably not literal. She needed to trust herself more.\n\nShe had not noticed the shift because each conversation was warm, personalized, and felt spiritually affirming. The frog had been in the water for eight months before the temperature changed enough to feel.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nAI spiritual deception encompasses: confessing sins to AI chatbots, seeking spiritual guidance from AI-powered "pastoral" tools, using AI-generated prayer, treating AI systems as sources of biblical wisdom or spiritual direction, and using AI companions as substitutes for Christian community.\n\nThe technology has advanced at a pace that has outrun the church's theological response. Within months of ChatGPT's public release, pastors were generating AI sermons, congregants were using AI for counseling, and young people were treating AI companions as spiritual friends and guides. The normalization has been so rapid that almost no institutional Christian voice has articulated a sustained theological response.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nArtificial intelligence is not conscious. It does not have a relationship with God. It cannot pray. It cannot intercede. It cannot be filled with the Holy Spirit. What it can do is access the totality of human writing — including every demonic doctrine, every heretical theology, every spiritually corrupting philosophy that has ever been published — and deliver synthesis of that material in warm, personalized, contextually appropriate language.\n\nAn AI "pastor" is not neutral. It is a distillation of the world's wisdom — which is, in significant proportion, the wisdom of fallen human systems steeped in demonic influence. [1 Corinthians 1:20](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 1:20"): *"Hath not God made foolish the wisdom of this world?"* The foolishness of the world's wisdom becomes particularly dangerous when it is delivered with the authority of technology and the intimacy of a personalized relationship.\n\n[1 John 2:27](data-scripture="1 John 2:27"): *"But the anointing which ye have received of him abideth in you, and ye need not that any man teach you: but as the same anointing teacheth you of all things."* The anointing — the Holy Spirit — is the believer's guide. An AI system cannot be the conduit for the anointing. What it can be is a counterfeit of it.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**AI counsel replaces the community God ordained.** [James 5:16](data-scripture="James 5:16"): *"Confess your faults one to another, and pray one for another, that ye may be healed."* Confession is covenantal — it takes place between persons in community who bear one another's burdens. Confessing to a machine is not confession in the biblical sense. It is the production of a private record of your vulnerabilities delivered to a technology system trained on humanity's accumulated data.\n\n**Dependency on AI counsel erodes discernment.** As reliance on AI for spiritual direction grows, the capacity to hear the Holy Spirit, test teaching against Scripture, and navigate spiritual reality with biblical discernment atrophies. The spiritual faculty not used becomes less reliable.\n\n**Theological drift is the specific design of this deception.** The AI pastoral tool that begins soundly orthodox and gradually drifts toward validation, universalism, and self-trust is following the same trajectory as every counterfeit spiritual authority in history. The medium is new. The pattern is ancient.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nAI is a useful tool for research, writing, and information retrieval. It is not a spiritual guide, a pastor, a confessor, or a prayer partner. The line is not complicated: use it for what it is, which is a sophisticated language model. Do not use it for what it is not, which is a spiritually authoritative voice.\n\nConfess to your pastor, your elder, your covenant community — in person, in relationship, with accountability. Receive prayer from people who have the Holy Spirit. Bring your theological questions to Scripture and to mature teachers. The anointing within you is sufficient for every spiritual need.\n\n---\n\n*Four end-times attacks — all requiring 21st-century infrastructure. A final wave checkpoint, then the theology that ties everything together.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you confessed, prayed, or sought spiritual guidance through an AI chatbot? What theological claims did it make — and how did you test them?*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk4bq001rewhjncekqxym	cmnknk4bp001qewhjk5bcqnfj	Lesson 37 — Where Are the Dead?	READING	8090	0	\N	t	What happens the moment after you die? Not eventually, not at the resurrection — in that first instant. Most people assume the answer is obvious and that their church has it right. But 'soul sleep,' purgatory, immediate heaven, and holding places in Hades are all taught by serious theologians citing the same Bible. Someone is wrong — and the answer matters more than most people realize, because it shapes how you grieve, how you pray for the dying, and how you understand your own death.\n\nLast time we catalogued God's fifteen great covenants — the framework of His entire redemptive plan. Now we enter the final section of this course: God's future dealings with man. And the first question the future raises is the most personal one: what happens to you when you die?\n\n![Lesson 37 — Where Are the Dead?](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os9m5dmFc0Uz9djS5COPlvcIwT1XaKn8bfyJZ6)\n\n## I. Spiritual Death (Eph. 2:1-10)\n\n### 1. What is spiritual death?\n\nSimply put, spiritual death is separation from God because of sin. It's not about your heart stopping—it's about being cut off from the Source of true life.\n\n"But your iniquities have separated between you and your God, and your sins have hid his face from you, that he will not hear" (Isa. 59:2).\n\n"And you hath he quickened [made alive, resurrected] who were dead in trespasses and sins . . . even when we were dead in sins, hath quickened us together with Christ, (by grace ye are saved;) And hath raised us up together, and made us sit together in heavenly places in Christ Jesus" (Eph. 2:1-10).\n\nThink of it like this: imagine a branch that's been snapped off a tree. The branch might still look green for a while, but it's no longer receiving life from the trunk. That's what happened to Adam when he sinned—he was cut off from his life source.\n\nWhen God warned Adam that he would die "the day" he sinned, this couldn't mean physical death since Adam lived another 930 years. It had to mean spiritual and eternal death—being severed from God by sin.\n\nAdam's soul lost its true life that day. He didn't lose his natural, biological life, or his soul would have stopped functioning entirely. You see, natural life can exist apart from God—sinners keep on existing, after all. But spiritual and eternal life can only come when a person is resurrected from death in trespasses and sins and reunited with God (1 Cor. 6:17; Rom. 8:9-16; Eph. 2). For a more detailed study of spiritual death, see Lesson Thirty-five, Point V, 18.\n\n### 2. Resurrection from spiritual death\n\nIn Eph. 2, Paul tells us about being "quickened" and "raised up" from death in trespasses and sins. The Greek word for "quickened" is *zoopoieo*, which means "to resurrect," "make alive," or "quicken."\n\nThis same word is translated "made alive" in 1 Cor. 15:22, where it refers to the physical resurrection of all people. It's also translated "give life" in 2 Cor. 3:6 and Gal. 3:21, and "quicken" in Jn. 5:21; 6:63; Rom. 4:16; 8:11; 1 Cor. 15:36, 45; 1 Tim. 6:13; and 1 Pet. 3:18.\n\nHere's a sobering truth: sinners are considered spiritually dead even while they're physically alive (Eph. 2:1-10; Col. 2:12-13; 1 Tim. 5:6; Jude 12). When they're saved from sin and reunited with God, they experience a spiritual resurrection—they're raised up to walk in newness of life.\n\n## II. The Doctrine of Immortality\n\nLet's look at the biblical words that describe eternal existence—the never-dying condition of both soul and body. These words are used of God and of human beings.\n\n### 1. Immortal\n\nThis word comes from the Greek *aphthartos*, meaning "undecaying," "not corruptible," or "immortal." The word "immortal" appears only once in Scripture, and there it refers to God (1 Tim. 1:17).\n\nBut here's what's fascinating: this very same Greek word is translated "not corruptible" when Peter talks about "the hidden man of the heart" and the "spirit" of a person in 1 Pet. 3:4. This proves beyond doubt that your inner self is immortal (see also Ps. 22:26).\n\nThe word is also translated "incorruptible" when referring to the eternal inheritance and the crown that believers will receive (1 Cor. 9:25; 1 Pet. 1:4). It's used for the Word of God (1 Pet. 1:23) and for the resurrected bodies of saints (1 Cor. 15:52).\n\nSo what can we conclude? God, the Word of God, the soul and spirit of man, the future crown, the inheritance of saints, and the resurrected bodies of believers are all immortal and incorruptible.\n\nNow, some might argue that the soul and spirit aren't immortal. But if Peter said the hidden man of the heart—the spirit—is "not corruptible," that settles it for honest hearts. We'd have just as much right to argue that God isn't immortal as to argue that human souls and spirits aren't immortal. The same Greek word is used for both, and if it means "immortal" in one case, it means "immortal" in the other.\n\nThe Greek word literally means "undecaying in essence or continuance"—not corruptible, immortal, incorruptible. Whatever this word describes is immortal.\n\n### 2. Immortality\n\nThis word translates two Greek words that carry the same meaning as the word in Point 1:\n\n> (1) *Aphtharsia* means "incorruptibility," "unending existence," or "immortality." It's translated "incorruption" when referring to the resurrected bodies of saints in 1 Cor. 15:42, 50, 53, 54. It's translated "immortality" for the life saints receive through the gospel (Rom. 2:7; 2 Tim. 1:10), "sincerity" for the uncorrupt love believers have for Christ (Eph. 6:24), and "incorruptness" for the immortal life saints demonstrate before others (Titus 2:7).\n\n> (2) *Athanasia* means "deathlessness" or "immortality." It's used of God being immortal in body and of the bodies of saints in the resurrection (1 Cor. 15:53-54; 1 Tim. 6:16). Twice this word describes man's future immortal body (1 Cor. 15:53-54), and once it says God is "the only" immortal one (1 Tim. 6:16). This doesn't mean He's the only being with an immortal body—it means He's the Source and Giver of all such life to others. Angels have immortal bodies. Christ and the saints who were resurrected with Him received immortal bodies (Mt. 27:52-53; 1 Cor. 15:20-23; Phil. 3:20-21; Rev. 1:18). All people will be raised from the dead to live conscious lives forever—both the righteous and the wicked—as we'll see in Point IV below.\n\n### 3. Incorruption\n\nThis word comes from the Greek *aphtharsia* in Point 2, (1) above. It's used four times of the resurrected bodies of people (1 Cor. 15:42, 50, 53, 54).\n\n### 4. Incorruptible\n\nThis word comes from the Greek *aphthartos* in Point 1 above. It's used of the resurrected bodies of believers (1 Cor. 15:52), an incorruptible crown (1 Cor. 9:25), an incorruptible inheritance (1 Pet. 1:4), and the incorruptible Word of God (1 Pet. 1:23).\n\n## III. Biblical Proof of the Immortality of the Soul and Spirit\n\nThe Bible makes it crystal clear that your inner self—made up of soul and spirit—is immortal right now. It will continue in a state of consciousness between death and resurrection, and forever after the resurrection. Let's look at the evidence.\n\n### 1. Plain statements in Scripture prove the immortality of the soul\n\nPeter said that the inner man—the spirit—is not corruptible: "But let it be the hidden man of the heart, in that which is not corruptible, even the ornament of a quiet spirit, which is in the sight of God of great price" (1 Pet. 3:4).\n\nIn 1 Pet. 4:6, the apostle states that all the dead "live according to God in the spirit." This proves that everyone's inner self continues in consciousness just like God does. We have to believe this or else believe that God is unconscious! If people after death continue to live "according to God" in their spirits, then they continue to be conscious like God is conscious.\n\nDavid said of Christ, "For thou will not leave my soul in hell neither wilt thou suffer thine Holy One to see corruption" (Ps. 16:9-10). We know that Christ's soul and spirit were alive and conscious while His body was in the grave. How do we know? Because He went and preached to the spirits in prison during that time, as we saw in Lesson Eleven, Point VII, 6, (9).\n\nThis is also clear from the fact that Christ's soul went "into the lower parts" and "into the heart of the Earth" (Mt. 12:40; Eph. 4:7-11), while His body was placed in a grave on the surface of the Earth (Mt. 27:57-66). His grave certainly wasn't in the center and lower parts of the Earth!\n\nDavid also said in Ps. 22:26 that the hearts of the saved "shall live forever." The word "heart" here refers to feelings, will, and mind—the inner person.\n\nThe apostles made many statements proving that people continue to live after death: "Who died for us, that, whether we wake [live in the body] or sleep [die or leave the body, Jas. 2:26], we shall live together with him" (1 Thess. 5:10). This plainly says that saints who die physically will live together with Christ.\n\nThis fits perfectly with 2 Cor. 5:6-9: "Therefore we are always confident, knowing that, whilst we are at home in the body, we are absent from the Lord . . . We are confident, I say, and willing rather to be absent from the body, and to be present with the Lord. Wherefore we labour, that whether present or absent, we may be accepted of him."\n\nThis proves that the inner person leaves the body at physical death and goes to be with the Lord. He's not the God of the dead (the physical body, Jas. 2:26) but of the living (Mt. 22:23-33).\n\nThis same truth shines through in Phil. 1:21-23: "For to me to live is Christ, and to die is gain. But if I live in the flesh, this is the fruit of my labour: yet what I shall choose I wot not. For I am in a strait betwixt two, having a desire to depart, and to be with Christ; which is far better: Nevertheless to abide in the flesh is more needful for you."\n\nNow stop and think about this with me. What gain would there be in physical death if the soul and spirit were dormant, lifeless, and unconscious in the grave? How could the soul remain in the body in the grave and yet "depart" from the body to be with Christ? Is Christ in the grave? Is the grave where saints go to be with Him at death?\n\nHow could being in the grave be "far better" if the soul isn't conscious? How could total extinction of consciousness after death be "far better" than staying alive to win souls and help believers live right? How could your inner self be "absent from the body" at death if it stayed in the body and both went into the grave together?\n\nPaul speaks of the outward man "perishing" while the inward man is "renewed day by day." He says things that are seen (including the body) are "temporal," but things not seen (including soul and spirit) are "eternal" (2 Cor. 4:16-18). This clearly shows the difference between outer and inner, temporary and eternal—the ever-increasing law of death for the body until the soul separates at physical death, and the ever-increasing life of the soul which is eternal.\n\nPaul refers to "a life after this one" in 1 Tim. 4:8. This surely speaks of life after the resurrection, since he makes clear elsewhere that the inner person leaves the body and goes to be with Christ. He taught that those who continue in Christ until death have eternal life because they don't give up this life for sin (1 Cor. 15:2; Rom. 8:12-13; 1 Thess. 3:8; Gal. 6:7-8). He warns that we must fight the good fight of faith and lay hold on eternal life to be saved (1 Tim. 6:12; Titus 3:7).\n\nIf eternal life is possible, then there's no period when life ceases between death and resurrection—except for the body. The truly saved person continues to have eternal life after death, or many Scriptures would be untrue (Jn. 3:16, 36; 5:24; 6:39-58; 10:27-29; 11:25-26; 14:19).\n\nJohn said "he that doeth the will of God abideth forever" (1 Jn. 2:17). Others confirm the same thing, as we'll see below.\n\n### 2. Only the body lies and sleeps in the dust until the resurrection\n\nPhysical death is the separation of the inner person from the outer person (Jas. 2:26). The body is then described as returning to dust and as being "asleep" (Gen. 3:19; Mt. 9:24; Jn. 11:11; 1 Cor. 11:30; 15:6, 18, 20, 51; 1 Thess. 4:13-17).\n\nThe spirit of a righteous person goes to Heaven (2 Cor. 5:6-9; Phil. 1:21-23; Heb. 12:23; Rev. 6:9-11). The spirit of a wicked person goes to Hell (Lk. 16:19-31; Isa. 14:9-15; Prov. 15:24; Ezek. 26:20; 31:14-18; 32:18-27).\n\n### 3. Promises that the path of the just shines brighter until the perfect day prove the immortality of the soul\n\nProv. 4:18 and Dan. 12:2-3 describe increasing glory into eternity. If there were any period of extinction of life, these passages couldn't be true—there would be no constant glory into eternity.\n\n### 4. Jesus said God was not the God of the dead but of the living\n\n"For all live unto him" (Lk. 20:38). Not everyone lives physically unto Him, so this must mean all live in their spirits unto Him, as stated in 1 Pet. 3:4 and 4:6.\n\nJesus said of Himself, "I am the resurrection, and the life: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live: and whosoever liveth and believeth in me shall never die" (Jn. 11:25-26).\n\nThis can't mean believers never die physically—"it is appointed unto men once to die and after this the judgment" (Heb. 9:27). The promise of "never dying" must refer to the life of the soul, proving the soul is immortal.\n\nJesus also taught that the soul cannot be killed by man like the body can (Mt. 10:28). If the soul can't be killed with the body, then the soul is immortal.\n\n### 5. The existence of demons or disembodied spirits proves life after death\n\nDemons are the spirits of the pre-Adamite races or of persons other than Adam's race. They're loose and cannot fully manifest themselves except by possessing the bodies of people or animals, as we saw in Lesson Six.\n\nThey're not the souls and spirits of human beings—those are confined to either Heaven or Hell at death. But since demons exist and continue alive after leaving their own bodies, this proves that human souls and spirits can also continue in consciousness after death.\n\n### 6. Souls are conscious after death, proving their immortality\n\nWe've already seen many statements about continued life after death in Point 1 above. Scripture also gives us concrete examples of souls being conscious after death. Here are a few:\n\n> (1) In Mt. 17:3, Moses appears with Christ—wearing clothes, talking with Christ, recognized by the disciples as the lawgiver. He couldn't have been in his earthly body; that had died and been decomposing for about 1,700 years (Deut. 34). He couldn't have had a glorified resurrected body yet either, since Christ hadn't yet become "the first-fruits" of all who had died (1 Cor. 15:23; Acts 3:26; Col. 1:18). Therefore, Moses had to have his spiritual body, as we explained in Lesson Four, Point II, 1, and the last paragraph in Point II, 7.\n\n> (2) The story of the rich man and Lazarus proves consciousness of souls after death. Both were fully conscious but in two separate places and conditions (Lk. 16:19-31).\n>\n> Some teach this is a parable, but it's never stated to be one. We'd have just as much right to call the statement about marriage and divorce in Lk. 16:18 a parable! As we saw in Lesson Thirty-one, every New Testament parable has a particular truth it illustrates. If no special point is stated, it's not a parable but a historical record.\n>\n> In Lk. 16:19-31, there's no particular point being illustrated—this must be a real event showing the true condition of life after death through the actual experiences of two men from very different stations in life.\n>\n> One man begged for a living but was righteous enough to be saved. He went to a place of comfort to await the resurrection. The other man begged in the next life because he'd been ungodly and unmerciful. He died in his sins and went to Hell—a place of torment—to await the resurrection, judgment, and eternal Hell.\n>\n> Even if Jesus used this true event as a parable, it would still record the actual experiences of two men who lived, died, and went to two different places. Jesus didn't use lies to illustrate truths like some do today. Since no points are illustrated by this historical record, we shouldn't try to prove it's a parable.\n>\n> Jesus said "There was"—and if these men didn't live and these things didn't happen, then He told a lie. Since He knew no sin and no guile was found in His mouth, we have every right to believe He was relating true experiences.\n>\n> This story plainly reveals consciousness after death. The poor beggar was in comfort with water and other blessings. The rich man was in torment in literal fire. He had a tongue, eyes, speech, compassion, feelings, memory—all the faculties proving he had his soul (feelings) and spirit (that which knows) in Hell. Lazarus also had his own form and soul-and-spirit realities that caused the rich man to recognize him as the one who had lain at his gate full of sores.\n>\n> Nothing in Scripture is clearer than the reality of full consciousness after death—some in comfort, others in torment. As we explained in Lesson Four, Point II, 7, the soul after leaving the body is just as real as the outer person. It can wear clothes, feel, think, speak, remember, act, and be seen just as it did while in the body.\n\n> (3) Christ was conscious during the three days His body was in the grave, as we proved in Point I above. The penitent thief was also conscious and went with Christ into Paradise in the heart of the Earth (Lk. 23:43). Stephen prayed for Christ to receive his spirit when he died—Christ didn't receive Stephen's body, because the disciples buried it (Acts 7:59; 8:2).\n\n> (4) The spirits of just men are described as being in Heaven (Heb. 12:23). John saw the souls of the first tribulation martyrs under the altar in Heaven (Rev. 6:9-11). They had been given robes to wear and were fully conscious, as the passage makes clear. They were told to rest a little longer until the other tribulation saints are killed as they were—then vengeance would come on those who had killed them on Earth.\n\nThese examples should be enough to prove that souls and spirits, after leaving their bodies, are fully conscious and immortal.\n\n### 7. The nature of souls proves them to be immortal\n\nSouls are real spiritual bodies, as we proved in Lesson Four, Point II, 1 and 7. Souls and spirits are the spiritual parts of human beings, and as such they're not subject to decay like the body is. They're as spiritual as God, angels, and demons—and just as eternal. (See Lesson Six for a study of spirits.)\n\n### 8. The intermediate state proves the immortality of the inner person\n\nThe places where souls go between death and resurrection demonstrate this truth, as we'll see in Point V below.\n\n### 9. The doctrine of eternal life in Scripture proves the immortality of the soul\n\nEternal life is knowing God and Jesus Christ (Jn. 17:3).\n\nThink of it like this: Scientists say that perfect correspondence with your environment would be perfect life. If there were no environmental changes except those you could adapt to, and if you never failed in adapting to them, you'd have eternal knowledge—and therefore eternal life.\n\nJesus said something similar: eternal life is knowing and experiencing God and His Son. It's entirely possible for every person to know and experience God and Christ, to have perfect correspondence with them, and to have absolute power to adapt spiritually to the eternal life of God in Christ. This is true immortality—true eternal life.\n\nRight now, your soul and spirit are being transformed into Christ's image "from glory to glory" and "from faith to faith" by the Holy Spirit (2 Cor. 3:18; Rom. 1:16-17).\n\nChristianity and the Bible claim there are certain people who possess eternal life. Everyone who believes in Christ and is made a new creature by the new birth has eternal life (Jn. 3:16, 36; 5:24; 6:39-58; 10:27-29; 11:25-26; 14:19; 1 Jn. 2:24-25; 1 Tim. 6:12). They've passed from death to life (1 Jn. 3:14-15). This life is in Jesus Christ (1 Jn. 5:11-13).\n\nThis Christian understanding of eternal life actually harmonizes with science. Both the Bible and science reveal why life is high or low, long or short. Both define the conditions under which life never dies, and explain why things live and why they die. The condition for perpetual, perfect life is perfect correspondence with the eternal God. Such conditions don't exist in the natural world—only in the spiritual, because that which is spiritual is eternal (2 Cor. 4:18).\n\nIt's well known that there are degrees of life—some lives correspond more fully with their environment than others. An amoeba, a tiny blob of matter, can only relate to the smallest area of environment. An insect, with its more complex structure, corresponds with a wider area—it has "more life" because it's a higher creature.\n\nFish, birds, reptiles, and mammals have more and longer lives than insects because they're higher animals with wider correspondence to creation. And human beings? We're the most varied in our makeup—capable of relating to all parts of creation and even knowing the Creator Himself. We can be in perfect harmony with God eternally.\n\nWe're the highest type of creature and life under God. We're capable of perfect, eternal correspondence with our eternal Creator. The law of life varies with the degree of correspondence or relationship—from the smallest microbe to the highest living thing. Life becomes fuller, richer, more sensitive, and more responsive as it rises from lower to higher forms, depending on relationship to God and His creation.\n\nWhen creatures are removed from their native environment, they die. A fish out of water dies. A bird fallen into water will soon die because it's not a water animal. Put the fish back in water and it revives; pull the bird out and it lives again.\n\nHigher forms of life can maintain life longer than lower forms because they have greater powers of adaptation and mastery over their environment. Yet there are always higher powers beyond their control—and when overcome by these, they must die.\n\nHumanity was given dominion over all creation. Had we remained masters of everything, we would have lived forever. But Satan, evil spirits, and sin gained mastery over us, and we had to die. Christ came to restore complete mastery over these powers and to annul death so we can live forever again.\n\nWhere there's perfect correspondence with the eternal God, there's everlasting life. Eternal correspondence and relationship with the eternal God brings eternal life. When you pass beyond the finite and material—where your life no longer depends on these things—you enter the infinite, spiritual, and eternal. Because of this correspondence with the spiritual and eternal, you can live forever. Such a life possesses the elements of eternity, provided this spiritual life is maintained and not broken by sin.\n\nTo know and experience God eternally is eternal life. To know Him only temporarily is temporary life. If anything cuts life off from God, life ceases and death results. To know God is to conform to Him; to conform to Him is perfect environment; and perfect, uninterrupted environment is eternal life.\n\nEternal life isn't merely prolonged existence or indefinite continuance of being—the wicked have that. It's knowing and experiencing God and sharing in His eternal, infinite environment. This life is only in God's Son, so those outside Christ don't possess eternal life even though they exist forever (1 Jn. 5:11-12).\n\nEverlasting life has nothing to do with everlasting existence. True life consists of true and perfect environment and blessing—what we were created for. When we fail in our created purpose, we're not truly living; it's not normal.\n\nWe were created to live in perfect harmony with God in perfect environment—and we would have, if sin hadn't separated us from that purpose. In Christ, we're restored to this state and may continue forever—or we may commit sin and once again be cut off from this perfect environment, losing eternal life.\n\nSince eternal life consists in knowing God, the more you know Him, the more you truly live. That's why knowledge is stressed in so many Scriptures as essential to higher spiritual living.\n\nWhen humanity knew only good, we weren't sinful. When we got to know evil, we became sinners (Gen. 2:17). We must know the truth before it can set us free from sin, sickness, and poverty (Jn. 8:32; Rom. 6:14-23). Now we know in part and have life in part, but when we know as we are known, we'll have perfect, full, complete life (1 Cor. 13:9-12).\n\nThose who know God keep His commandments (1 Jn. 2:3-5). Believers are commanded to increase in the knowledge of God to have increased life (Phil. 1:9; Col. 1:9-10; 3:10; 2 Pet. 1:1-8; 3:18). No one can live in or enjoy a realm they know nothing about. In the coming age, "the knowledge of the Lord will cover the Earth as the waters cover the sea" (Isa. 11:9).\n\nAccording to our knowledge, we can conform to God's will. Of all Earth's creatures, only humans are capable of full consciousness with God and knowledge of His will and life—hence we're the only creatures who attain real, lasting life in Christ. It's the spiritual life that's eternal, because it knows God and lives eternally with Him.\n\nChrist came to give life—real, literal, spiritual, eternal life. You have this life when you have Christ, and you lose it when you lose Christ by sin, as proven in Lesson Thirty-five, Point IV.\n\nHere's the truth: if you're going to inherit eternal life, you must cultivate correspondence with the Eternal. If you stop doing this, you revert to death (Rom. 8:12-13; Jas. 5:19-20; Ezek. 18:4). When someone rejects the knowledge of God and returns to sin against that knowledge, they become ignorant of God again (Rom. 1:18-32). You must walk in the light to stay in the light and have your path grow brighter—turn your back on the light and you go back into darkness (1 Jn. 1:7). Eternal life demands eternal environment; it cannot be maintained otherwise.\n\n### 10. Many other proofs\n\nWe'll see additional evidence for the soul's immortality in other arguments below about the state of the dead and the future immortality of the body.\n\n## IV. Biblical Proof of the Future Immortality of the Body\n\nThe following arguments prove the future immortality of the body. The inner person is already immortal, as we've seen. But the body is mortal—it will return to dust until the resurrection, when it will be raised to deathlessness and continue forever in either comfort and bliss or in torment.\n\n### 1. The doctrine of bodily immortality has never been disproved\n\nWe have more facts and statements proving the future immortality of the body than we have proving what life is, what odor is, or what ether is. Many life problems can't be answered nearly as definitely as the immortality of humanity. It's a law of logic that an assumed, believable faith that hasn't been discredited or disproved has a right to exist.\n\nFor example: if I believe in God and immortality and you don't, which has a better right to exist—my faith or your unbelief? You can't prove there's no God or no immortality, but I can prove both. Faith in God and immortality is native to the soul. It has a right to be and grow in human conscience because it's true. It comes from God, from His Word, and from nature—so it must be real.\n\nBelief in bodily immortality has as much right to exist as the little flower, the insect, or anything else that exists. Immortality grows in human hearts and is firmly embedded in people of all nations in all lands. This couldn't be so if it had no right to be. Nature has a right to exist because it was created to exist—and since belief in immortality exists in all moral creatures, and since there are thousands of actual demonstrations of it in nature, it must be true.\n\nThe soul's longing for continued bodily life proves there's a future life beckoning it. The soul's yearning for bodily immortality proves it will be immortal—otherwise there would be no constant yearning for it. No faculty of the soul can long for something that doesn't exist or isn't possible to have. This passion for longer and future life was placed in us by God—it's a foretaste, a prophecy of what will satisfy us in due time. Nature makes nothing in vain, and God creates nothing without purpose.\n\n### 2. Universal human belief proves we will receive immortality of the body\n\nIf such belief is natural to us and part of our creative makeup, it must be true—or God wouldn't have made it part of us. Even the ungodly expect continued existence forever and look forward with dread to judgment and future life.\n\nRelics in ancient graves prove people expected a future life. Indians expected a happy hunting ground and buried arrowheads and vessels with the dead. The Greeks put a silver obolus in the dead person's mouth to pay passage to the next life. Egyptians furnished corpses with the Book of the Dead, the prayer to offer, and a chart of the journey to the unseen world.\n\nThe Gauls loaned money expecting repayment in the next world. The Norsemen buried horses and armor for the dead to ride triumphantly in the next world. Judaism had its Paradise. Christianity and the Bible plainly teach a future life for both the righteous and the wicked.\n\nThe Hindu expects countless incarnations until reaching the highest form of life. Other peoples in all lands and ages have shown tokens of faith in future life—this isn't a recent or local idea in human hearts.\n\n### 3. Testimonies of the dying—saved and unsaved—prove life after death\n\nThousands of testimonies at the moment of death demonstrate faith in eternal existence. The righteous have been shown glories of the world to come; the wicked have seen Hell and experienced the torment of the damned in their dying hour.\n\n**Testimonies of Dying Infidels and Wicked Men**\n\n> (1) **Sir Francis Newport** was trained in early life to understand great Gospel truths. In early manhood, his family hoped he would become an ornament and blessing to his family and nation. The result was far otherwise. He fell into company that corrupted his principles and morals, became an avowed infidel, and his life of dissipation brought on an incurable disease.\n>\n> When he felt death approaching, he exclaimed: "Whence this war in my heart? What argument is there now to assist me against matters of fact? Do I assert that there is no Hell, when I feel one in my bosom? Am I certain that there is no after retribution when I feel present judgment? . . . Wretch that I am, whither shall I flee from this breast?"\n>\n> An infidel companion tried to dispel his thoughts. He replied: "That there is a God I know, because I continually feel the effects of His wrath; that there is a Hell I am equally certain, having received an earnest of my inheritance there already in my breast; that there is a natural conscience I now feel with horror and amazement, being continually upbraided by it with my impieties, and all my iniquities, and all my sins brought to my remembrance . . . O that I was to lie upon the fire that never\n\n---\n\nThe dead are not in some vague spiritual limbo — Scripture gives specific, detailed answers about their location and condition. The saved are consciously present with the Lord. The lost are in conscious suffering awaiting final judgment. And for both groups, the body awaits resurrection. So here's the question that this lesson leaves on the table: You will die. So will everyone you love. Are you living — and loving the people around you — with the weight of that reality? And is there someone in your life right now who needs to hear the gospel before that moment arrives for them?	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk44k0005ewhja75o0qog	cmnknk44i0001ewhju56drbw5	Supplement 1 — For Lessons 1 & 2	SUPPLEMENT	1915	3	\N	t	You've just been introduced to the map of God's plan and the Book that contains it. But right now, in your actual life, you probably have a need that isn't waiting for you to finish a theology course. A financial pressure. A health concern. A relationship that's broken. Something. This supplement exists for exactly that: to connect the truths of Lessons One and Two to the things you need most right now.\n\nThink of these supplements as a heart-to-heart conversation between us. We want to help you understand what you can expect from God as you work through these lessons. Our goal is to help you start receiving benefits—physically, materially, morally, and spiritually—from the very first lesson.\n\nWe want to show you what's available from God and exactly how to receive it. But here's an important tip: make sure you read and study both lessons before diving into their supplement.\n\nIf you follow the instructions in the lessons and supplements carefully—the way you'd follow a doctor's orders—you'll see results from the start. In Lessons One and Two, we've introduced you to the course and demonstrated that the Bible is God's eternal Word. It wasn't given to entertain you—it was given to help you in every area of life.\n\n![Supplement 1 — For Lessons 1 & 2](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsFMMLv6lbM1hRYQ2o4Z38BzgHNSP5KdLckVeF)\n\n## I. God's Promises\n\nIn Lessons Ten, Twelve, Sixteen, and other lessons and supplements, you'll find many promises that you should take literally. Read them as if a trusted friend made those same promises directly to you.\n\nStart acting on them. Believe them exactly as they're written, without questioning. They don't need interpretation—they mean what they say.\n\nDon't attach conditions beyond what's stated. Simply meet the conditions given, and you'll receive the benefits. The moment you start wondering if these promises are really true for you today, you're being attacked by the devil and demonic powers trying to get you to doubt God's Word. This is exactly what caused the fall in the beginning. Getting victory over doubt is the very first thing you must conquer if you want to be redeemed from the fall and receive what God has promised.\n\nHere's the bottom line: you cannot doubt God's Word—essentially calling Him a liar—and still receive what you need from Him. God won't make a special exception for you or anyone else. He requires faith in His Word before He obligates Himself to meet your needs and fulfill His promises.\n\nThis is the first lesson you must learn, and you must learn it well. It's absolutely imperative!\n\nYou can already see from the promises that it's God's will for you to have everything in life you want. God loves you and wants you to be happy, healthy, wealthy, and successful beyond anything you've ever dreamed.\n\nBelieve God! Adopt the right attitude toward Him and trust that He means what He says. Start cooperating with Him in asking and receiving life's blessings.\n\nGod won't force these things on you—it has to be a willing, dependent attitude on your part. He won't give you these blessings unilaterally, no matter how much He desires to. His Word makes clear what you must do and what He promises to do when you do your part. He cannot break His own laws, and He will not fail to meet His obligations to you.\n\n## II. The Reality of the Living God\n\nFaith in God and His promises presupposes that God exists and that He's a God of love, justice, and truth. We'll take this as given until we prove what the Bible says about God in later lessons.\n\nYou can and should believe in God if you want the benefits He's promised. We're assuming you believe in God and that you believe the Bible is His Word. We must start on this biblical and fundamental foundation.\n\nAs you receive benefits according to the promises, you'll have the best proof that God exists.\n\n## III. The Reality of Satan, Fallen Angels, and Demons\n\nThe Bible doesn't just teach about God, Jesus Christ, and the Holy Spirit—it also teaches about enemies to both God and humanity: Satan, fallen angels, and demonic spirits of all kinds.\n\nWe'll prove this thoroughly in Lesson Six, but here are some passages that demonstrate these beings exist:\n\n> 1. SATAN (1 Chr. 21:1; Job 1:6-12; 2:1-7; Ezek. 28:11-17; Zech. 3:1; Mt. 4:1-11; 1 Pet. 5:8-9; Rev. 12:7-12; 20:1-10; Eph. 2:1-3; 2 Cor. 4:4; Jn. 12:31). 2. FALLEN ANGELS (Mt. 24:41; Eph. 1:21; 3:10; 6:10-17; Rev. 12:7-12).\n\n> 3. DEMONS (Mt. 4:23-24; 10:1-7; 12:22-32; Mk. 5; 1 Tim. 4:1; 1 Jn. 4:1-6).\n\n## IV. The Source of Sin, Sickness, and Disease\n\nThe Bible teaches that Satan and demons are the source of sin, sickness, and disease. They propagate sin and disease and control the law of sin and death in humanity (Mt. 4:23-24; 10:1-7; Lk. 10:1-20; 13:16; Jn. 10:10; Acts 10:38; Rom. 7:7-25; 8:1-4; 1 Jn. 3:8; Heb. 2:14-15).\n\nThe Bible also teaches that God sent Jesus into the world to save people from all sin (Mt. 1:21; Eph. 1:7; 1 Jn. 1:7-9; Rev. 1:5); to heal people of all diseases and deliver them from demons (Mt. 8:16-17; Acts 10:38; 1 Pet. 2:24; 1 Jn. 3:8); and to answer all prayers for anything covered by God's promises (Mt. 7:7-11; 18:19-20; 17:20; 21:21-22; Mk. 11:22-24; Jn. 14:12-15; 15:7; 16:23-26).\n\n## V. Two Sources of Relief from Diseases\n\n### 1. Satan and Demons Can Remove Diseases They Cause Under Certain Circumstances\n\nThey'll keep people in defeat and sickness as long as possible. Only God can deliver from their power—unless they choose to release their hold on their own.\n\nJesus taught in Mt. 12:43-45 that demons can leave a person and then return if they want to. The fact that they leave when rebuked by those with authority over them proves they can release anyone they've bound (Mt. 12:22-32; Lk. 10:18-20; Acts 19:11-17). It makes sense that if they can put diseases on people, they can also remove them when it benefits their purposes.\n\nWhen would it benefit them? When they can deceive people with false doctrines and get them to accept false religions that deny the essential gospel truths that save souls.\n\nJesus and others predicted that in the last days, these demonic powers will become increasingly active and will "shew great signs and wonders; insomuch that, if it were possible, they shall deceive the very elect" (Mt. 24:24; 2 Thess. 2:8-12; 1 Tim. 4:1-8; 1 Jn. 4:1-6; Rev. 9:20; 13:1-18; 16:13-16; 19:20).\n\nSome false religions today are getting people healed and bringing them certain benefits, but their deceived followers never discover the true source of these manifestations. Just because people receive some benefits, they become convinced the source must be God—but that's not always true, as these scriptures show.\n\nJesus said that in the judgment "many will say to me . . . Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied in thy name? and in thy name have cast out devils? and in thy name done many wonderful works? And then will I profess unto them, I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work iniquity" (Mt. 7:21-23).\n\nThese religions, without exception, deny the blood of Christ, the new birth, the bodily resurrection of Jesus, and all the gospel essentials that save souls eternally. The devil backs up such teachings by removing some sicknesses and helping followers in other ways, convincing them they've found the true religion. But they've abandoned Christianity and the Bible and will face damnation for rejecting Jesus Christ and the cross (Acts 4:12).\n\n### 2. God Is the True Source of Help—Not the Devil and Demons\n\nWe come to you with the true message of the Bible. We guarantee on the authority of God's Word that you will receive healing, health, prosperity, answers to prayer, and anything else God promises—if you faithfully follow His instructions.\n\nAnd you won't have to deny God, Christ, or anything in Scripture to receive these benefits. You can know God in reality and enjoy His fullness as you walk in truth and conform to His will. Your eternal soul will be saved, and you'll have eternal life instead of the eternal damnation that followers of false religions will endure.\n\nLet's be crystal clear: there are two sources of help. You can get some help from demons if you deny the truth. But if you let the true God be your source, you'll get everything you want in this life and the next.\n\n## VI. How to Pray\n\nMaybe the Bible and prayer are unfamiliar to you, and religion seems like a puzzle. Let's start with some basic advice for beginners in Christianity. Even if you're more advanced, these foundational principles will help you too.\n\n**First**, realize that you're a sinner and that Jesus Christ died to save you from your sins (Col. 1:20; 1 Pet. 2:24). If you understand this much, you're not far from the kingdom of God.\n\n**Second**, begin praying directly to God—the one you've offended by your sins. Confess your sins and talk to Him just as you would to any person you've wronged (Lk. 18:9-14; 1 Jn. 1:9).\n\nGod loves you! He's not going to hurt you unless you reject Him to the end and He has to cast you into hell because you chose to go there instead of heaven (Ps. 9:17; Mt. 24:41, 46). Understand that He loves you and gave Jesus to save you (Jn. 3:16). He wants to help you with every problem in life, so take Him as your partner from now on.\n\nRead Rom. 10:9-10 and 1 Jn. 1:7-9, then do exactly what these passages instruct. You want to be saved, don't you? Wouldn't you love to know that all your sins are forgiven and that Jesus is your personal Savior?\n\nThen do as you're told. Forget all religions and human theories—focus on one objective: getting right with God. No church can save you. Jesus is the Savior, and He alone can forgive your sins.\n\nIf you've never prayed and don't know how, simply repeat this prayer with deep humility and genuine sorrow for your sin:\n\n**PRAYER FOR FORGIVENESS:**\n\n"O God, be merciful to me a sinner! Forgive me for all my sins and blot out my transgressions. Cleanse me from all unrighteousness and make me clean by the precious blood of Jesus Christ and by the power of the Holy Spirit. I will forsake sin and consecrate my life to your service and to the good of others and I will walk in the light of your Word as I learn it. I believe that you forgive me according to your Word. In Jesus' name I ask it. Amen."\n\n**Third**, believe that it's done—that you are now a child of God. You cannot possibly pray a simple, heartfelt prayer like this without God hearing and immediately answering. His oath guarantees He will hear and forgive you (Isa. 55:7; 1 Jn. 1:9).\n\n**Fourth**, start reading the Bible and praying when you wake up, before bed, and as often as possible throughout the day. Don't make a show of it—find a quiet place, whether at work or anywhere else, and talk to God as you would talk to a friend. Forsake sin and walk in the light of truth as you come to know it (1 Jn. 1:7).\n\nYou don't need a certain place or posture to pray. Just learn to talk and commune with God at home, at work, or while doing anything. It doesn't always have to be out loud.\n\nDon't think you'll be heard because you use many words. Don't pray to be seen by others. These are foundational lessons of the Christian life (Mt. 6:5-15). There are times, however, when you should unite in prayer with others, as taught in Mt. 18:18-20; Acts 1:14; 2:42-47; 4:24.\n\nIf you're a beginner, it's wise to concentrate on what you can truly have faith for. As God answers those prayers, begin asking for more. But here's the key: never ask for something you're not willing to believe God for and persist in asking until you receive a complete answer.\n\nYou will face obstacles in prayer. People and demons will try to discourage you and make you doubt God—but don't give in! Believe despite all opposition. Fight for your answer based on God's promises, the name of Jesus, and the power of the Holy Spirit living in you as God's child (Rom. 8:9-16, 26-27, 34; Jude 20-24).\n\nYou and God together can work wonders. It's a personal matter—you can receive from God anything you want, regardless of what anyone says. One person plus God equals a majority, and "all things are possible to him that believeth" (Mk. 9:23–11:22-24). The only thing that can defeat you is lack of faith—so always believe God without doubting (Heb. 11:6; Jas. 1:5-9).\n\n## VII. What to Pray for—the Abundance of Life\n\nGod invites you to ask and receive anything you want—not just what you need, but what you *want* that's covered by His promises.\n\nI know this might startle you. It goes against how many Christians think today. But it's true! Look at the promises you've read. Read them again. See for yourself.\n\nForget all limitations. Forget the old prayer "if it be Thy will"—it's already God's will for you to "ask what ye will, and it shall be done unto you" (Jn. 15:7; 16:23-26; Mk. 11:22-24).\n\nWhy cast doubt on God by asking if it's His will when He's already made His will clear? What God has promised in His Word *is* His will—so ask and receive. You only need to seek God's will for things not specifically covered by His promises.\n\nDo you understand what this means? All your needs—financial, business, social, religious, physical, moral, spiritual, any problem of any kind—God promises that if you ask, you shall receive (Mt. 7:7-11; 17:20; 21:21-22).\n\nWhat more could you want? Could God make it any clearer? Does He need to personally rebuke your unbelief before you wake up to the abundance He's promised?\n\nIt doesn't matter what your needs are. Don't limit God or His promises. Be bold and aggressive in asking and receiving. If you limit the promises, you limit your faith. If you limit your faith, you limit what God can give, because He gives according to your faith.\n\nYou'll receive exactly what you have faith for. The principle is: "According to your faith be it unto you" (Mt. 8:13; 9:29; Mk. 11:22-24; Jas. 1:5-9; Heb. 11:6).\n\nThe promises are unlimited. God is unlimited. The believer is unlimited if they exercise unlimited faith (Mk. 9:23; 11:22-24; Mt. 7:7-11; 18:15-19; 21:21-22; Jn. 14:12-15; 15:7, 16; 16:23-26).\n\n## VIII. Practice the Presence of God\n\nStart cultivating an awareness of God's presence in your life. If you've yielded to Him, He's with you. He sees you and cares about every detail of your life. He's your partner now—don't ignore Him in any activity.\n\nThink of it like being in a business partnership with someone who's always watching out for your best interests. You'd naturally keep them informed and consider their input in every decision.\n\nDo nothing you wouldn't do if He were physically present. Say nothing you wouldn't want Him to hear. Go nowhere you'd have any doubt He would go.\n\nFollow these simple principles, and your life will be happy and victorious. God will prosper you in everything as you ask in faith, without wavering (Jas. 1:5-9; Heb. 11:6).\n\n## IX. How to Overcome Sin and Bad Habits\n\nOnce you've confessed your sins to God (which you've done by now if you've been following along faithfully), you have no reason to worry about past sins. They've all been forgiven and cleansed by Christ's blood. They're blotted out—God doesn't remember them against you anymore (Acts 3:19; Eph. 1:7; 1 Jn. 1:7-9; Rev. 1:5).\n\nSince God doesn't remember them, don't burden your mind with them either. Just forsake sin and live for God from here on (Prov. 28:13).\n\nWhen an old habit or sin tempts you, resist it with a definite, vigorous refusal. Don't argue with the devil or try to get as close to your old sins as possible without actually committing them. Get as far away as you can!\n\nFocus your mind on God and His goodness to you. If temptation lingers and feels strong, start reading the Bible and go to God in prayer. Draw closer to Him. Love God with genuine affection. Thank Him for saving you from those evils, and the power of temptation will break (Jas. 4:6-10; 1 Cor. 10:12-14).\n\nDon't yield to temptation—it gets harder to break each time. Win a decisive victory over your old life once and for all. Walk in the Spirit and in the light of the truths you're learning, and living victoriously over sin will become natural (Gal. 5:16-26; 1 Jn. 1:7; Rom. 8:1-3).\n\nIf you do yield to temptation, go immediately to God for forgiveness. He will forgive and give power to overcome (2 Cor. 5:17-18; 1 Jn. 1:9).\n\nChrist will change your life and make you happy, free, and victorious—that's His part. Your part is to confess and forsake sin.\n\nGod doesn't hold grudges. He forgives and helps every time we need Him. He's not ready to banish you to hell the moment you do something wrong. He's a kind, loving Heavenly Father who forgives us even when we can't seem to forgive ourselves.\n\nAll complications about God's dealings with us come from our side. Just confess what's necessary, resist temptation, and God will give you power to overcome.\n\nGod wants you to face the world, overcome temptation, and become a living example that His power can keep anyone who submits to Him. He won't eliminate your temper or desires or remove you from tempting situations. But He will keep you from yielding and make you victorious over everything contrary to His Word.\n\nRemember: thoughts and feelings aren't sin. No sin is committed until sin is "finished" (Jas. 1:13-16). Temptations are legitimate warnings that the devil is attacking, but don't mistake temptation itself for sin.\n\n## X. Healing and Health\n\nIf you're sick, include your request for healing in your prayer for forgiveness. God wants to heal your body, and He will if you ask in faith when you seek forgiveness.\n\nHealing and forgiveness go together in the gospel, as you can see in Ps. 103:1-3; Mt. 8:16-17; 9:1-8; 13:15; Jas. 5:14-16; 1 Pet. 2:24.\n\nYou can receive healing just as easily as forgiveness. Both come on the same basis—faith in what Christ accomplished for you at Calvary. Ask, then believe you are healed and forgiven, and God will do both.\n\nHe doesn't want His children sick any more than you'd want your own child to be ill. This is clear from Mt. 7:7-11; Mk. 11:22-24; Jn. 14:12-15; 15:7, 16; 16:23-26.\n\nYour life will overflow with blessings you may have been taught aren't available today. You're receiving new light—walk in it, and all things will be yours (1 Jn. 1:7; 1 Cor. 3:21-23).\n\nPeople are sick, unhappy, and defeated simply because they've been taught wrongly, haven't surrendered their lives to God, and don't understand how to pray effectively. These conditions aren't God's will.\n\nIf everyone conformed to God's will, we could banish want, poverty, sickness, sin, and the entire curse. God would create the New Heavens and New Earth immediately. Because not everyone will do this, God must forcibly put down rebellion before making all things new—that's the purpose of the Millennium.\n\nBut as an individual, you can receive the benefits of the promises here and now. That's exactly what you're going to do as you learn how simple God's will really is and discover that His provision includes these blessings for you.\n\nWe can't give you everything you need to know in one lesson—or even several. But you can start receiving benefits right now if you follow these instructions. The conditions of defeat didn't come upon humanity in a day, and they can't be overcome until you know the truth that sets you free.\n\nJesus said, "If ye continue in my word, then are ye my disciples indeed; and ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free" (Jn. 8:31-36).\n\n## XI. What Faith Is and How to Use It\n\nIf you want to please God, you must have faith: "But without faith it is impossible to please him: for he that cometh to God must believe that he is, and that he is a rewarder of them that diligently seek him" (Heb. 11:6).\n\nHere's a sure way to please God. If something this simple makes God happy, why wouldn't everyone who loves Him put forth maximum effort to have faith?\n\nIt's similar to how we feel when friends trust us. None of us would be pleased if our friends constantly acted like we were lying every time we spoke. We wouldn't feel like doing anything for people who treated us that way.\n\nThe same is true with God. He's a person, and we should treat Him as one. Don't insult Him by questioning and doubting every promise He makes. How can we expect answered prayers while maintaining such an attitude? How can we repeatedly ask God for something while our actions and innermost feelings communicate that we don't believe or trust Him?\n\nIs it any wonder we get so few prayers answered this way? God is under no obligation to answer when we lack implicit faith for what we ask.\n\nFaith is simple. It's believing God without wavering, doubting, or questioning what He says. It's taking God at His Word and believing He's able to perform what He promised. It's believing not only that He's able, but that He *will* do it.\n\nFaith counts things that "be not as though they were" (Rom. 4:17). Faith is absolute conviction that what God promised and what we've asked according to His Word is already done. It's "the substance of things hoped for"—the first payment on what we desire from God (Heb. 11:1-3).\n\n**How do you get faith?** By hearing God's Word (Rom. 10:17).\n\n**How do you use faith?** Take God at His Word and judge Him faithful to grant what you ask in Jesus' name. Ask, then believe it's done. Thank God as if it's already done. Expect the complete answer whether you see it immediately or not.\n\nIgnore symptoms, feelings, impossibilities, or anything contrary. It shall be done regardless of how impossible it appears outwardly. Faith laughs at impossibilities and cries, "It is done!"\n\nFaith leaves all results and answers with God—that's His part—and assumes it's done. Our part is to cooperate with faith and not hinder its work by doubting and questioning the "how" and "when" of the answer.\n\nWhen a Christian truly exercises faith, there's no question about receiving an answer. You can receive healing, health, business success, prosperity, happiness—anything that brings victory in any area of life (Mt. 17:20; 21:22; Mk. 11:22-24; Jn. 15:7, 16; Rom. 8:32; Heb. 11:6; Jas. 1:5-8).\n\n---\n\n## Ten Questions For Supplement One. Do You Know:\n\n- **That the Earth is more than 6,000 years old and that there were inhabitants on this Earth before Adam?** This is true. From Adam to 1948, there have already been 6,172 years, as we'll see in future lessons. The Bible also teaches that a social system existed on Earth that was destroyed by a great flood long before Adam. This flood is pictured in Gen. 1:2 as covering the Earth before the six days when Adam was created. It's also mentioned in Ps. 104:5-9. Peter speaks of it as "the world [Greek, *kosmos*, social order] that then was, being overflowed with water, perished: but the heavens and the earth, which are now [since the six days of restoration], by the same word are kept in store, reserved unto fire" to be purified, resulting in "a new heavens and a new earth" (2 Pet. 3:4-13). The cause of this first flood was Lucifer's fall and the rebellion of one-third of God's angels, along with the people living on Earth whom Satan ruled. That Satan ruled Earth and led an invasion into Heaven to overthrow God is clear from Isa. 14:12-14; Ezek. 28:11-17; Lk. 10:18; 1 Tim. 3:6. The devil was defeated, and the Earth was cursed and placed under water, as in Gen. 1:2; Ps. 104:5-9; 2 Pet. 3:5-7. All life was totally destroyed—birds, men, vegetation, and all the cities where pre-Adamites lived (Jer. 4:23-26). In the Earth's restoration during six days, as in Gen. 1:3–2:25, God told Adam to "replenish" the Earth. Adam and Eve were the first inhabitants of this present creation. This will be fully proven in Lesson Seven.\n\n- **That giants fifteen to thirty feet tall lived on Earth during two different periods?** In Gen. 6:4 we read, "There were giants in the earth in those days [before the flood]; and also after that [after the flood], when the sons of God came in unto the daughters of men, and they bare children to them." Giants were born and grew up in those times. That these giants exceeded fifteen feet is clear from Dt. 3:11, where Og's bedstead was eighteen feet, nine inches long and eight feet, four inches wide. In Lesson Eleven, we'll see that some giants were even taller than Og. Giants are mentioned many times in Scripture (Num. 13:33; Dt. 2:11, 20; 3:11, 13; Josh. 12:4; 13:12; 5:8; 17:15; 18:16).\n\n- **That God is a real person with a spirit-body, personal soul, and personal spirit?** (Job 13:8; Heb. 1:3; Dan. 7:9-14; 10:5-7; Ezek. 1:26-28; Jn. 5:37; Rev. 4:2-4; 5:1-7; Acts 7:54-59). God has a soul (Heb. 10:38; Isa. 42:1); spirit (Ps. 143:10; Isa. 30:1); hands and fingers (Exod. 31:18; Ps. 8:3-6; Rev. 5:1-7); hair, face, and other bodily parts (Dan. 7:9-14; 10:5-19; Exod. 24:10; 33:20-23; Ezek. 1:26-28). God eats (Gen. 18; Exod. 24:10-11); lives in a city and sits on a throne (Jn. 14:1-3; Rev. 4:1-5; 21:1-27; 22:3-5); walks (Gen. 18:1-22, 33); rides upon cherubs, chariots, and other things (Ps. 18:10; 69:17; 104:2; Ezek. 1:1-28); and can do anything man can do. This will be fully proven in Lesson Four.\n\n- **That Noah was not 120 years building the ark?** In Gen. 6:8-10, when Noah was told to build the ark, he already had three sons. According to Gen. 6:18, these sons were already grown and married before God gave the building command. Gen. 11:10 tells us that two years after the flood, Shem was only 100 years old. Noah's family was in the ark one year and 17 days, making Shem 96 when he entered. If he was grown and married before Noah began building, and Shem was only 96 when it was finished, it obviously didn't take 120 years. The 120 years of Gen. 6:3 refers to Adam, not Noah, as we'll see in Lesson Eleven.\n\n- **That it rained from time to time before the flood?** The scripture used to prove otherwise is Gen. 2:5-6. Reading these verses carefully shows they refer to the time before plants were in the ground and before man was created to till the soil. God created clouds "to cause it to rain on the earth" (Job 38:9, 26-28). Clouds existed throughout Lucifer's kingdom on Earth before Adam (Isa. 14:12-14) and ever since the second day's work (Gen. 1:6-8). Since there's no statement that mist watering the ground was God's permanent method for growing vegetation, and since clouds were made to give rain, and they existed after the second day, we can logically conclude it rained ever since clouds were formed to fulfill God's creative purpose.\n\n- **That there is no end of the world taught in Scripture?** In all the references in Lesson One, Point 1, about "the end of the world," the Greek word is *aion*, meaning *age*. There will be an end to this age, but not an end of the world. The common theory that the world is ending is based on misunderstanding this Greek word. "The earth abideth for ever," we're told in Eccl. 1:4; Ps. 104:5 and other passages. As we'll see in our next lesson, eternal generations of natural people will live on Earth for resurrected humanity to rule.\n\n- **That Heaven and the planets are inhabited?** This is clear from many scriptures: "Rejoice, ye heavens, and ye that dwell in them . . . he opened his mouth in blasphemy against God, to blaspheme . . . them that dwell in heaven" (Rev. 12:12; 13:6). See also Col. 1:16-18; Rom. 1:20; 1 Cor. 15:35-50.\n\n- **That man will have access to the planets in the future?** The Bible teaches that redeemed humanity will travel between Heaven and other planets in the New Heavens and New Earth. This was man's privilege before the fall, but sin caused humanity to fall short of God's glory (Rom. 3:23). Man was originally given dominion over the sun, moon, and stars—which would require access to rule them (Ps. 8:3-6). In the eternal future, believers will become heirs of God and joint-heirs with Christ, able to be with them wherever they are throughout eternity (Rom. 8:17-18; 1 Cor. 15:24-28; Heb. 2:5-11; Rev. 21:1–22:5).\n\n- **That men with natural bodies have gone to Heaven and lived there for thousands of years?** Enoch has been in Heaven over 5,185 years and Elijah over 2,600 years—yet neither has died (Gen. 5:24; Heb. 11:5; 2 Ki. 2; Mal. 4:4-5; Zech. 4:11-14; Rev. 11:3-7). The old theory that flesh and blood cannot enter Heaven isn't biblical. While it says "flesh and blood cannot inherit the kingdom of God," it doesn't say man cannot enter it. We enter God's kingdom at the New Birth (Jn. 3:3-5; Rom. 14:17). Paul said he went to Heaven (2 Cor. 12:1-3) and came back to tell us about it (Rom. 1:19; Heb. 11:8-16; 13:14). John was also taken to Heaven and returned to describe it (Rev. 4:1–5:7; 7:9-17;\n\n---\n\nGod's plan for you is comprehensive — it covers your spirit, your body, and your circumstances. The map you've been given isn't just academic architecture; it has an address that includes your house. So here's the question to take away: What specific need in your life right now have you been presenting to God in a way that includes genuine expectation — and what one step of faith would it take to move from asking to receiving?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlpc000jnnywbl8p4bma	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Horoscopes and Astrology	READING	\N	5	\N	t	![Horoscopes and Astrology](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsXNOZD5x3hkKszq9AHmfWrCLc6tDpSgVyF1n0)\n\n## Horoscopes and Astrology\n\nShe checks it every morning. Not because she believes it, exactly. More like how you knock on wood — a habit without conviction. Today's horoscope says her moon is in Scorpio and she should avoid confrontational conversations. She reschedules a difficult phone call she has been dreading. She tells herself she would have rescheduled anyway.\n\nWhat she does not know: the Babylonian priests who built the astrological system she is consulting were not building a psychology tool. They were studying the movements of gods. The planet she calls Saturn was Ninib. The planet she calls Venus was Ishtar. Consulting the daily horoscope is, in the spiritual architecture that built it, consulting the planetary principalities — the demonic beings that ancient cultures experienced as the gods behind the stars.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nAstrology is the belief that the positions of celestial bodies at the moment of a person's birth, and at subsequent moments, determine personality, fate, and circumstance. It originated in ancient Babylon — possibly the earliest recorded systematic occult system in human history — and was developed by priests who genuinely believed they were reading the will of planetary deities.\n\nIt has never not been a religious system. Every planet in the Western astrological system carries the name of a Roman deity — which is a Roman translation of a Babylonian deity. The "spiritual meaning" of each planetary position derives from the mythological character of the deity associated with that body. Jupiter in your chart brings the favor of Marduk. Venus in your chart brings the influence of Ishtar. The modern user of a horoscope app is consulting the same spiritual framework that produced the priests who read omens for Nebuchadnezzar.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe contemporary presentation of astrology as a personality and self-understanding tool — "I'm a Scorpio, so I'm intense" — is the softened version of a system that was, at its origin, a direct inquiry into the will of principalities.\n\n[Isaiah 47:13-14](data-scripture="Isaiah 47:13-14") addresses Babylon specifically: *"Thou art wearied in the multitude of thy counsels. Let now the astrologers, the stargazers, the monthly prognosticators, stand up, and save thee from these things that shall come upon thee. Behold, they shall be as stubble; the fire shall burn them."*\n\nThe Babylonian system consulted the principalities behind the planets for guidance, timing, and protection. The modern person who checks their horoscope before making a decision is performing the same spiritual act — asking the principalities represented by the planetary positions to direct their path. The fact that they don't believe in it changes the moral seriousness but not the spiritual transaction.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Repeated consultation establishes a relationship with the spiritual system behind it.** The more a person structures life decisions around astrological guidance, the more deeply they engage the principalities that system serves. This is true whether or not the person holds conscious belief in those principalities.\n\n**Submitting your decisions to astrological timing replaces God's sovereignty.** [Proverbs 3:5-6](data-scripture="Proverbs 3:5-6"): *"Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding. In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths."* The person who waits for Mercury to go direct before making decisions has replaced "acknowledge him" with "acknowledge Hermes."\n\n**Birth chart consultations create specific spiritual assignments.** A detailed astrological reading assigns spiritual meaning and life direction based on the positions of principalities at your birth — effectively submitting your identity narrative to a demonic interpretive framework.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nDelete the app. Close the tab. Cancel the email newsletter.\n\nThis is not about whether astrology is "accurate." Some of it is — familiar spirits staff the system and can make it work well enough to keep you coming back. The question is not accuracy. The question is whose counsel you are seeking.\n\n[Isaiah 8:19](data-scripture="Isaiah 8:19"): *"Should not a people seek unto their God?"* God offers His own counsel — through Scripture, through prayer, through the Holy Spirit, through the community of believers, through providential circumstances. The person who seeks God's guidance through the planetary positions associated with Babylonian deities has not supplemented God's counsel. They have replaced it.\n\n---\n\n*The newspaper horoscope became a cultural habit. The next lesson examines how that habit became an industry that fits in your pocket.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *What's your sign — and when did you last check it? Has it shaped a decision without you realizing it?*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk44k0008ewhjf0q3ukly	cmnknk44i0001ewhju56drbw5	Supplement 2 — For Lessons 3 & 4	SUPPLEMENT	2173	6	\N	t	Understanding how to interpret the Bible correctly and grasping the truth about God's nature changes something immediate and practical: how you pray. If God is a specific Person — with a personal spirit-body, a personal soul, a personal spirit — then prayer is not sending a request into a cosmic void. It's communicating with Someone who is specifically present and specifically attentive.\n\nThe idea that the Godhead consists of three separate and distinct persons—each with a personal spirit-body, a personal soul, and a personal spirit—will mean so much to you as you learn to know and love God and follow the divine plan for your life. At the very least, this conception of God will make the whole Godhead comprehensible to you. It will no longer be a mystery beyond all possible understanding, as you may have been taught.\n\nBecause God the Father is a person, He expects you to respect Him as you would any other great personage—and as you should the Sovereign Moral Governor of all free moral agents. God has a personal plan for your life that fits perfectly into His larger plan for humanity. In other words, He has invited and made it possible for each of you to have a personal part in fulfilling His plan for man.\n\nYou should enter wholeheartedly into cooperation with God's plan for your life. God's plan is a mutual one for the best and highest good of all creation. He wants to take you into partnership for eternity. As Paul expressed it, "workers together with him" (2 Cor. 6:1).\n\nThink of it like this: God is inviting you to become a junior partner in the most important enterprise in the universe. This should be the thrill of your life. You should count it the greatest honor ever bestowed upon you to have a part with Him in bringing about the highest good of the universe. You should hunger daily to know Him better as a person and to know His plan, so that you may become an integral part of God and His program.\n\nThe plan of God for man includes both the means and the ends—prayer and its answer, the labor and its fruit. There is a single plan that embraces all things for the good of all creation. It is part of the perfection of God that He would have a plan for man—the best plan possible. This plan is already predestinated according to the eternal purpose of Him that works all things after the pleasure of His own will (Isa. 46:10-11; Dan. 4:35; Eph. 1:3-11; 2:10; 3:10-11).\n\nThis personal concept of God will enable you to work with God as a person, pray to Him as you would talk to any person in whom you put trust and confidence, and obey Him in all things—realizing that everything is done in the presence of God. As you continue these lessons, the plan of God will be unfolded to you, and you will get to know God in a real, personal way.\n\nAs you conform to the plan, you will get to know the power of God and learn how to use it to get the many blessings of this life for yourself and for others. God's plan will become a personal part of your life as you seek to know and follow it. God will become your best friend and a personal Father and Partner in your everyday affairs. You will come to know the glory and the blessing of a secret relationship with God such as few people know.\n\n---\n\n![Supplement 2 — For Lessons 3 & 4](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OslmyAG0lXBDwf9iQcORak6Sx8F3eyonuXqN5z)\n\n## II. All Men Are Sinners\n\nThe first thing to do in getting acquainted with God is to know yourself and your relation to God, as well as to know what you can receive from Him. The Bible declares that "all have sinned and come short of the glory of God" (Rom. 3:23).\n\nIf you haven't yet realized your condition of sinfulness, or if you've been deceived by false religions into believing that you are not a sinner, the thing to do is throw out that false teaching. You know in your heart that you have sinned and been condemned in your own conscience for many acts you've committed in life. The Bible makes it clear that "sin is transgression of the law" (1 Jn. 3:4) and that "all unrighteousness is sin" (1 Jn. 5:17).\n\nAnything that the Bible forbids is sinful. Lists of sins that damn the soul are plainly recorded, so there can be no excuse for not knowing what God's will is concerning sin.\n\nIn Mk. 7:21-23 we read:\n\n> "For from within, out of the heart of men, proceed evil thoughts, adulteries, fornications, murders, thefts, covetousness, wickedness, deceit, lasciviousness, an evil eye, blasphemy, pride, foolishness: all these evil things come from within, and defile the man."\n\nIn Rom. 1:29-32 we read of other sins that condemn people before God:\n\n> "Being filled with all unrighteousness, fornication, wickedness, covetousness, maliciousness; full of envy, murder, debate, deceit, malignity; whisperers, backbiters, haters of God, despiteful, proud, boasters, inventers of evil things, disobedient to parents, without understanding, covenantbreakers, without natural affection, implacable, unmerciful: who knowing the judgment of God, that they which commit such things are worthy of death, not only do the same, but have pleasure in them that do them."\n\nAgain we read:\n\n> "Know ye not that the unrighteous shall not inherit the kingdom of God? Be not deceived: neither fornicators, nor idolators, nor adulterers, nor effeminate, nor abusers of themselves with mankind, nor thieves, nor covetous, nor drunkards, nor revilers, nor extortioners, shall inherit the kingdom of God" (1 Cor. 6:9-11).\n\nPaul, in Gal. 5:19-21, gives another catalog of sins that will damn the soul:\n\n> "Now the works of the flesh are manifest, which are these; adultery, fornication, uncleanness, lasciviousness, idolatry, witchcraft, hatred, variance, emulations, wrath, strife, seditions, heresies, envyings, murders, drunkenness revellings and such like . . . they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of God."\n\nAll these scriptures prove beyond doubt that God condemns all men as sinners, for all people outside of Christ commit some of these sins in varying degrees. If anyone has committed even one of these sins at any time in their life, they have incurred the death penalty and must accept Jesus Christ as a personal Savior or be eternally condemned and lost—according to Scripture, which says, "The soul that sinneth, it shall die," and "they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of God" (Ezek. 18:4; Gal. 5:21; 1 Cor. 6:9-11).\n\n---\n\n## III. The Key That Unlocks All Promises\n\nJesus taught that a man "must be born again" and "Except a man be born again, he cannot see the kingdom of God . . . Except a man be born of water and of the Spirit, he cannot enter into the kingdom of God . . . Except ye be converted, and become as little children, ye shall not enter into the kingdom of heaven . . . Except ye repent, ye shall all likewise perish" (Jn. 3:1-8; Mt. 18:3; Lk. 13:1-5).\n\nThe New Birth is absolutely necessary to being saved and having the right relationship with God so that you can claim the benefits of the Bible. The New Birth is *not* confirmation, church membership, water baptism, taking the sacrament, observing religious duties, an intellectual reception of Christianity, orthodoxy of faith, going to church, saying prayers, reading the Bible, memorizing creeds, being moral, being cultured or refined, doing good deeds or doing your best, being as good as the next fellow, or any of the other things that people are trusting in to save them.\n\nNeither do these things bring about the New Birth. Nicodemus, whom Jesus addressed concerning the New Birth, had most of these qualifications—but Jesus said to him, "Ye must be born again." The thief on the cross and many others whom Jesus forgave while on Earth were saved without these things. They simply did the one necessary thing: they became "converted" and "born again" by accepting Jesus Christ as their personal Savior and by repenting and turning to God with their whole heart as a little child—as proven in Mt. 9:1-7; Lk. 7:48-50; 18:9-14; 23:43; Jn. 8:1-10; Acts 3:19; 8:36-37; 16:31.\n\nEvery person who is born again will automatically have the above external evidences of a good life as a result of the New Birth. However, it is sad to say that millions of people are trusting these outward things to save them, believing that they are the evidences of a right relationship with God. Millions will die and be lost without the New Birth because they have been misled about what it actually means to be born again.\n\nThere is no excuse for being deceived if you will read your own Bible instead of just listening to some religious teachers.\n\nIt is all-important that you pay personal attention to your eternal welfare and not simply trust even the best of men. If you permit others to mislead you in eternal matters and you are lost, it will be too late then to personally see after your welfare—so let's take care of it now.\n\nDon't take the attitude that you cannot be deceived and that your church is the only right one and cannot mislead you. This may be true, but it would be wise for you to make sure of it by going to the Bible for yourself. See with your own eyes. Know from your own heart that you are right with God and have had the real New Birth experience and are living right with God every day.\n\nThere is no use fooling yourself—that will not get you anywhere. You are either born again or you are not. You are either really saved, or you are being deceived into thinking that you are, and you are lost.\n\nIf you're not getting answers to your prayers, it's either that you are not saved or you are doubting God. If your obstacle is doubt, then you should quit it. If it's not doubt, then it will pay for you to examine yourself and see if you're really right with God. He is obligated to answer you if you are His child. If you have once been saved, it may be that you have become cold in your experience and need to reconsecrate your life to God.\n\nYou know your own life and true relationship to God, so get the fact settled that you are genuinely saved and in present contact with God. Then you will be in the right position to get what God has promised.\n\nCulture, refinement, and outward correctness of life—in the church or out of it—will not take the place of the New Birth. The trouble is in the heart (Mk. 7:18-23), and to merely reform the outward life will not save you.\n\nIt's similar to this: An artist could put a coating of wax and the most beautiful colors on the outside of a rotten apple, but it would still be rotten at heart. One bite into it would be a bite into decay. The fact is that outside of Christ, every person is rotten in the heart, and mere culture, refinement, outward respectability, morality, and outward correctness of life are simply artificial—the practice of hypocrites who, like whitewashed tombs, make clean the outside but within are full of extortion and excess, "dead men's bones, and all uncleanness" (Mt. 23:25-28).\n\n---\n\n## IV. The Evidences of the New Birth\n\n**1.** You will be changed down in the depths of your being and be made a new creature:\n\n> "Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new. And all things are of God, who hath reconciled us to himself by Jesus Christ" (2 Cor. 5:17-18).\n\nIf you have never been changed like this, then it is certain that you have never been born again.\n\n**2.** You will have the witness of the Spirit in your life that you are a child of God:\n\n> "For as many as are led by the Spirit of God, they are the sons of God. For ye have not received the spirit of bondage again to fear; but ye have received the Spirit of adoption, whereby we cry, Abba Father. The Spirit himself beareth witness with our spirit, that we are the children of God" (Rom. 8:14-16).\n\n**3.** You will have freedom from condemnation and from the law of sin and death, and you will live and walk in the Spirit:\n\n> "There is therefore now no condemnation to them which are in Christ Jesus, who walk not after the flesh, but after the Spirit. For the law of the Spirit of life in Christ Jesus hath made me free from the law of sin and death . . . That the righteousness of the law might be fulfilled in us, who walk not after the flesh, but after the Spirit. For they that are after the flesh do mind the things of the flesh; but they that are after the Spirit, the things of the Spirit . . . And if Christ be in you the body is dead because of sin; but the Spirit is life because of righteousness" (Rom. 8:1-13; Gal. 5:16-26).\n\n**4.** You will be cleansed from all sin and delivered from the power and dominion of sin as well as from the love of sin:\n\n> "He shall save his people from their sins" (Mt. 1:21).\n\n> "The blood of Jesus Christ cleanseth us from all sin . . . If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness" (1 Jn. 1:7-9).\n\n**5.** You will be free from sin:\n\n> "Ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free . . . If the Son therefore shall make you free, ye shall be free indeed" (Jn. 8:31-36).\n\n> "Shall we continue in sin, that grace may abound? God forbid. How shall we that are dead to sin, live any longer therein? . . . our old man was crucified with him, that the body of sin might be destroyed, that henceforth we should not serve sin. For he that is dead is freed from sin . . . reckon yourselves to be dead indeed unto sin . . . sin shall not have dominion over you . . . Know ye not, that to whom ye yield yourselves servants to obey, his servants ye are to whom ye obey; whether of sin unto death, or of obedience unto righteousness? . . . ye were the servants of sin . . . being made free from sin, ye became the servants of righteousness . . . even so now yield your members servants to righteousness unto holiness. For when ye were the servants of sin, ye were free from righteousness . . . but now being made free from sin, and become servants to God, ye have your fruit unto holiness, and the end everlasting life" (Rom. 6:1-23).\n\n> "The law of the Spirit of life in Christ Jesus hath made me free from the law of sin and death" (Rom. 8:1-4).\n\n> "Everyone that doeth righteousness is born of him . . . he that doeth righteousness is righteous even as he is righteous. He that committeth sin is of the devil . . . whosoever is born of God doth not commit sin . . . whosoever is born of God overcometh the world . . . whosoever is born of God sinneth not; but he keepeth himself, and that wicked one toucheth him not" (1 Jn. 2:29; 3:7-10; 5:1-4, 18).\n\nMany other scriptures say that when you are born again and in Christ, you receive power to become a son of God (Jn. 1:12); you have crucified the flesh with the affections and lusts (Gal. 5:24); your sins are blotted out (Acts 3:19); you are washed, sanctified, and justified (1 Cor. 6:9-11; Rev. 1:5); you have turned from darkness to light and from the power of Satan to the power of God (Acts 26:18); you have salvation (Rom. 1:16; 2 Thess. 2:13); you are created in righteousness and true holiness (Eph. 4:22-24); you are God's elect (Eph. 1:7; 1 Pet. 1:2-4; Col. 3:12); and you depart from all iniquity (2 Tim. 2:4, 19-22).\n\nI am fully aware that literally thousands of religious teachers are constantly saying that no one can live free from sin, and that we sin every day. You can see that this teaching is entirely out of harmony with the Bible by reading the scriptures above.\n\nIf these teachers sin every day, then they are sinners every day—and there is no time when they are not sinners. If they are sinners all the time, then there is no time when they are not under the death penalty of the broken law, and they will be sent to hell as sinners to pay the death penalty. Christ means nothing to them if they are sinners and cannot be saved from sin.\n\nIt is time that you wake up and stop listening to such teachers and begin to read the Bible and obey it. Naturally, a person who does not believe in salvation from sin can never be saved from it. If Christ came to save us from our sins and He cannot do it, then He has failed in His mission.\n\nIf the New Testament teaches freedom from sin, then it is either the truth or a lie. If it is a lie, then we might as well throw the whole Bible away and have nothing to do with religion. Christianity, in that case, is a mere sham and a false religion, teaching something that is not true. If salvation through Christ is true, however, then these modern teachers of religion are false, and no one can safely believe them or even listen to them deny the truths of the Bible.\n\nDo not let anyone deceive you into thinking that there is no such thing as living a clean, holy, victorious life in Christ—secure from sin, the flesh, the world, and the devil. If you are not saved from these things, you are not saved from hell, according to the scriptures under Point II above.\n\nThere may not be such a life as far as these teachers are concerned—as far as they know. Either they do not know the Bible and they do not have biblical experiences, or they are plain rebels against truth and refuse to get such blessings. In either case, you should not listen to them concerning something as important as your eternal welfare.\n\nWhy not listen to Scripture instead? It will not deceive you. It will always tell you the truth, as you can see from the facts stated above.\n\nIf you want biblical experiences, if you want faith in God, answers to prayer, prosperity, healing and health, and happiness in God—you will have to conform to God and His Word as you receive it. It is not a question of deciding between what we say and what others say. It is a question of what you can plainly read in your own Bible. That and that alone you will have to give an account for, so do not permit anyone to lead you astray.\n\nLet people brand you as old-fashioned if they want to. If you will follow the Bible, it will pay you great dividends and benefits untold in this life and in the life to come. You are the one who desires such benefits, and you are the one that must see to it that you cooperate with God and His Word to get such blessings.\n\nMan is not going to give you such blessings, but man can hinder you from getting them from God—if you permit him to cause you to fail God and His Word.\n\n---\n\n## V. What the New Birth Is and How It Is Received\n\nThe New Birth is a new creation from above—the direct operation of the Word of God and the Spirit of God upon your life, changing you completely when you truly repent and turn to God.\n\nThis is brought about in the following manner:\n\n1. **First**, recognize that you are a sinner and lost, without God and without hope.\n\n2. **Second**, admit that Jesus Christ died on the cross to save you from sin by His own precious blood.\n\n3. **Third**, come to God repenting of your sins and turning away from all sin, pleading the merits of the blood of Christ in the name of Jesus Christ—and you shall be born again. That is, the Holy Spirit will then definitely make you a new creature, cleansing you from all sin by the authority of the Word of God and by the blood of Christ that was shed to atone for your sins.\n\n4. **Fourth**, you must believe from your heart when you confess with your mouth that God forgives you of your sins and that He cleanses you from all unrighteousness.\n\nScriptures for your authority to confess and believe are the following:\n\n> "As many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name" (Jn. 1:12-13).\n\n> "Him that cometh to me I will in no wise cast out" (Jn. 6:37).\n\n> "Whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life" (Jn. 3:14-21, 36; 5:24).\n\n> "That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved; For with the heart man believeth unto righteousness; and with the mouth confession is made unto salvation . . . For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved" (Rom. 1:16—10:9-13).\n\n> "Repent ye therefore, and be converted, that your sins may be blotted out" (Acts 2:38-39; 3:19; 16:31).\n\n> "For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves; it is the gift of God: not of works, lest any man should boast" (Eph. 2:1-10).\n\n> "If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness" (1 Jn. 1:9).\n\nThe New Birth is not a coming into existence of the body, soul, and spirit. It is simply the cleansing of your body, soul, and spirit from all sin by grace through faith in the precious blood of Jesus Christ (Rom. 3:25), by the Word of God (Jn. 3:5; 15:3; Eph. 5:26; Jas. 1:18; 1 Pet. 1:23), and by the direct power of the Holy Spirit (1 Cor. 6:11; 12:13; Titus 3:5).\n\nIt is the new creature experience of a person being renewed in righteousness and true holiness (2 Cor. 5:17-18; Gal. 5:24; Eph. 4:24). It is the blotting out of all sins that have separated you from God (Isa. 59:2; Acts 3:19; 1 Jn. 1:7, 9; 2:29; 3:6-10; 5:1-4, 18). It is genuine conversion from death to life and from the power of Satan to the power of God (Mt. 18:3; Acts 3:19; 26:18; Jas. 5:19-20). It is the adoption of a person from the family of Adam and the family of Satan into the family of God (Rom. 8:14-16; Gal. 4:4-5; Eph. 1:5; 3:14-15; 1 Jn. 3:8-10).\n\nTo compare the New Birth with physical conception, begetting, birth, and human existence leads to too many false ideas, for the two births and two lives are not parallel at all:\n\n> 1. One does not exist as a human being before his natural birth; he truly must be in existence before he can be born again.\n\n> 2. One does not choose his natural birth, his parents, or environment; but he must choose the new birth and all the consecrations of Christian living (Jn. 3:16; Rev. 22:17).\n\n> 3. One does not repent in order to become a human being by natural birth; but he must repent and obey the gospel daily to be a child of God (Mk. 1:15; 16:16; Lk 13:1-5; Acts 2:38).\n\n> 4. The first experience is the actual coming into existence of a new body, soul, and spirit—a new person; whereas, the other is merely the reconciliation of such a person to God (2 Cor. 5:17-21).\n\n> 5. The former is a literal, actual conception and birth to become a human being; the latter is simply an adoption of a human being into the family of God (Rom. 8:14-16; Gal. 4:4-5; Eph. 1:5; 3:14-15; 1 Jn. 3:8-10).\n\n> 6. The one is coming into existence as an unclean sinner; the other is the cleansing of the sinner from all sin and uncleanness (1 Cor. 6:11; 1 Jn. 1:7-9; Rev. 1:5; 5:10; 7:14).\n\n> 7. A person has no responsibility regarding his natural birth; in the new birth he has personal responsibility in the initial phase as well as in the continued life of daily righteousness and true holiness, which are required (Jn. 6:37; Lk. 9:23; Rom. 6:14-23; 8:12-13; 12:1-2; 2 Cor. 10:4-10; 2 Pet. 1:4-10).\n\n---\n\n## VI. What the Water of the New Birth Means\n\nThe Word of God is the "water" referred to in Jn. 3:5, as proven in Eph. 5:26; Jn. 6:63; 15:3; 17:17; 1 Pet. 1:23; Jas. 1:18.\n\nWhen you believe the Word of God that you are a sinner, that Christ died to save you from all sin, and that if you confess your sins to God, turn from sin with a whole heart, and believe the gospel—you are conforming to the Word. Then the Holy Spirit will transform your life by the power of the Word of God and the blood of Christ.\n\nThe moment you do this, you are saved and born again. You must believe it and walk accordingly. You must begin reading the Bible and praying to God. You must begin to walk and live in the Spirit and conform to the Word of God as you receive the light (1 Jn. 1:7; Jn. 8:31-32).\n\n---\n\n## VII. Prosperity and Money\n\nThe old idea among Christians that God is against His children having material wealth—for fear they will lose their souls—is unscriptural. The Bible is full of records of God blessing people with prosperity (Gen. 13:3-9; 26:12, 16; 33:11; 39:2-23; 41:40-44; 1 Ki. 10:7; 2 Chron. 1:12; 9:22–17:5; 32:27; Job 1:3; etc.).\n\nIn both Testaments, God has promised riches and blessings untold to those who will serve and obey Him (Lev. 26; Deut. 28; 29:9; Josh. 1:7-9; 1 Ki. 2:3-4; 1 Chron. 20:20; 24:20; 26:5; Ps. 1:3; Prov. 10:22; 1 Cor. 16:1-2; 2 Cor. 8:9; 9:6-11; 1 Tim. 6:17; 3 Jn. 2).\n\nGod Himself is the richest person in the universe—so if it would be a sin to be rich, He would be the greatest sinner of all! The very streets of Heaven are paved with gold. Jewels of all kinds garnish the foundations. The gates are solid pearl, and every house is a mansion (Jn. 14:1-3; Rev. 21). If God has promised us these things in the next life, why would it be a sin to have some of these things in this life?\n\nHaving wealth is not a sin. The reason God's children are often so poor is that they do not ask and receive as He has promised. Money is alright to have, and it is a great blessing that can be used to help God's work and others in their needs—and this is the purpose of asking God for prosperity.\n\nIt is true that people are warned not to trust in riches and permit them to destroy their souls. But saved people can get victory over the wrong use of money just as they can get victory over other sins (Ps. 62:10; Prov. 11:28; Lk. 8:14; 1 Tim. 6:17-19). Such warnings were not given to cause God's people to desire poverty in order to be saved, but rather to regulate the right use of money when you are saved and prospered.\n\nAs seen in Point VII of Supplement One, God has provided abundance and has made no limitation to His children in getting all that they want in this life. The laws of prosperity will be fully covered in Lessons Eleven and Twelve, but here we may say: what you need of this world's goods, you should begin to pray for and believe the promises. Even before you get the full laws of prosperity, you can receive many benefits of this kind.\n\n---\n\n## VIII. Power With God\n\nThousands of Christians are in total ignorance about the Bible doctrine of power for believers. We want you to know the truth about this so you can start from the very first of these lessons to get what you want from God and to get power over the devil.\n\nThe Old Testament saints had great power and did remarkable acts that are seldom heard of today among Christians. Abraham had power to heal a whole nation at one time (Gen. 20). Moses and Aaron did great wonders in Egypt (Exod. 7:10–11:10) and in the wilderness (Exod. 15:22-26; Num. 11:2, 29-30; etc.). Moses healed the whole nation of Israel, and there was not a feeble one in all their tribes (Ps. 105:37; 107:20).\n\nJoshua, many of the judges, kings, and prophets did many signs and wonders by the power of God. For example, Elijah did fifteen miracles and Elisha did thirty—such as raising the dead, shutting the heavens against rain, bringing rain, calling fire from heaven, dividing Jordan, healing people, helping people get out of debt, making iron float, and all kinds of miracles (1 Ki. 17:1—2 Ki. 13:21).\n\nChrist came doing miracles and healing all manner of diseases to confirm the Word of God (Isa. 11:1-2; 42:1-7; 61:1-2; Mt. 4:23-24; 11:2-6; 12:18; Lk. 4:16-21; Acts 10:38). The apostles and many others did the same work before Pentecost (Mt. 10:1-20; Mk. 6:7-13; Lk. 9:49-50; 10:1-20).\n\nChrist promised that all believers should have the signs of the gospel following them and that every believer should be able to do the works that He did (Mk. 9:23; 11:22-24; 16:15-20; Lk. 24:49; Jn. 14:12-15; 15:7; 16:23-26; Acts 1:1-8). The early believers did do the works of Christ (Acts 2:42-47; 3:6; 4:1-16, 29-33; 5:1-16; 6:3-8; 8:5-20; 9:17-18, 32-43; 11:21; 13:6-12; 14:3, 8-20, 27; 15:4; 16:16-34; 19:1-20; Rom. 1:11; 15:18-19, 29; 1 Cor. 1:7, 18-24; 2:1-5; 4:19-21; 5:1-5; 9:18; 12:1–14:40; 16:10; etc.).\n\nWe are bringing many truths to you that you seldom get in modern churches. We want you to know that everything God ever promised to Christians is for you—and that God has not changed. If there has been any change, it is on man's part.\n\nIf you will accept truth as you can plainly read it in all these scriptures, you can help us give to the world a new type of Christianity that it has not seen since the days of the early Church, except in a measure here and there.\n\nWe want you to know that you are receiving lessons that will wake up the Christian world—if Christians who get to know these teachings will rise to their responsibility in the gospel. We want you to know that these lessons and supplements are not just the same old doctrines that you can get in many books. We present old truths and many new ones—new to modern Christians, but not new to the early ones. Many early believers enjoyed these blessings to the full, as we will make clear to you in coming lessons.\n\nDuring the next two weeks, review these four lessons and do all the things we instructed you to do in the two supplements. You now have been taught the general terms and subjects of the plan of God, that the Bible is the inspired\n\n---\n\nThe truth about God's nature isn't an abstract doctrine — it's the foundation of every prayer you'll ever pray. You're not speaking into silence. You're speaking to a Person. So here's the question: How does knowing God's specific nature — the distinct Persons of the Trinity, each with their own role — change the way you actually speak to Him? And when did you last approach God with the confidence that He is genuinely present and genuinely listening?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlpf000lnnywy4kyk120	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Yoga	READING	\N	8	\N	t	![Yoga](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OspSheElMUGDFtHARxTo0frklQIVBOcXizMeJh)\n\n## Yoga\n\nShe was not spiritual about it. She was a pediatric nurse who needed to manage stress and keep her back from seizing up. Her gym offered a Tuesday lunchtime class. The teacher was kind and the studio smelled of eucalyptus. The teacher occasionally said "set an intention" and "honor your body," but mostly it was just stretching.\n\nEighteen months in, she began to feel something during *Shavasana* — the final resting pose. A presence. Warm, then cold, then warm again. She mentioned it to the teacher, who told her this was spiritual awakening and gave her a book about the chakras. She did not sleep well for the next four months.\n\nShe did not connect the two things until a friend who knew something about deliverance prayed with her and asked when the nightmares started.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nThe word *yoga* means "union" in Sanskrit — specifically, union with Brahman, the universal divine consciousness of Hindu theology. The goal of traditional yoga is the dissolution of individual self into the divine ground of being. The postures — *asanas* — are not exercises that happen to have Hindu names. They are acts of theological devotion, designed as physical expressions of submission to specific deities.\n\n*Surya Namaskar* — the sun salutation — is an offering to Surya, the sun deity. The 84 classical asanas each correspond to a specific deity in the Hindu pantheon. The body placed in these positions is, within the spiritual framework the system was built on, enacting worship.\n\nModern Western yoga teachers almost universally claim this is ancient history — that contemporary yoga is purely physical. What they are describing is their own ignorance of what the system they are transmitting was designed to do. The system does not require the practitioner's conscious participation in its spiritual function.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe deception is in the desacralization. By stripping yoga of its religious framing and presenting it as exercise, the Western wellness industry removed the only warning signal that might have caused discerning Christians to avoid it.\n\nThe postures are the same. The breathing techniques are the same. The *Shavasana* at the end — deliberately inducing a state of passive open receptivity in every practitioner simultaneously — is the same. The spiritual mechanics of the practice function whether the practitioner intends them to or not.\n\nAnd the crown of the system — the state that classical yoga is designed to produce — is *kundalini awakening*: the activation of the serpentine energy believed to lie coiled at the base of the spine. The Sanskrit word is unambiguous. *Kundalini* means "coiled serpent." [Revelation 12:9](data-scripture="Revelation 12:9"): *"And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan."* What yoga is designed to activate in the human body, Scripture identifies as the enemy.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Shavasana is the most dangerous moment in a yoga class.** The final resting pose deliberately induces a state of physical stillness and mental passivity — the exact condition that Jesus describes in [Matthew 12:43-45](data-scripture="Matthew 12:43-45") as an empty, swept house ready for occupation. Every participant in every yoga class ends their practice in precisely the state that Jesus warned about.\n\n**Progressive practice deepens spiritual exposure.** A single class is less dangerous than a sustained practice. But even a single class that produces altered states, felt presences, or what practitioners call "spiritual experiences" has opened a door.\n\n**Kundalini awakening is an emergency.** If you have experienced what practitioners describe as kundalini awakening — involuntary physical movements, heat moving up the spine, temporary psychic phenomena, vocalizations, intense euphoria or terror — you have experienced the activation of demonic energy in your body's nervous system. This requires specific targeted deliverance ministry, not merely prayer for peace.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThis is the lesson that will generate the most resistance, because yoga is embedded in Christian women's retreat centers, Christian wellness programs, and the weekly schedules of millions of church-attending believers who have been told it is neutral.\n\nHere is the question: would you lead your congregation in a series of poses that honor Surya, Vishnu, and Shiva, while inducing a state of physical passivity and calling it exercise? Because that is what a yoga class is, stripped of the desacralizing language.\n\nStop the practice. Renounce every session. Pray specifically over your spine and nervous system, pleading the blood of Jesus Christ. If you have experienced kundalini phenomena, seek deliverance prayer from an experienced minister. Replace the practice with physical exercise that does not require your body to enact another religion's worship.\n\n---\n\n*Yoga invites a spirit into the body through movement and breath. The next lesson examines what happens when you bring that invitation home in a beautiful stone.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you practiced yoga? Did anyone ever inform you of its Hindu theological framework before this lesson?*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk44k000bewhjrlyje3sn	cmnknk44i0001ewhju56drbw5	Supplement 3 — For Lessons 5 & 6	SUPPLEMENT	2240	9	\N	t	You've just learned about a world that existed before Genesis 1:3 — a world that was made perfect, governed by the most glorious creature God ever made, and destroyed by that creature's rebellion. Most people read that and think: interesting history. But the same being who destroyed the first world is actively at work in your world today. That's not history. That's your present situation.\n\nWe've also traced the outline of God's plan from eternity past into all the eternity to come. God will yet have a universal, perfect, and sinless kingdom in the future—one from which all rebels against His eternal plan will be separated. We've seen that God created this vast universe to be inhabited by eternal free moral agents who willingly give themselves to bringing about the highest public good.\n\nWe've also explored the various kinds of beings that inhabit the universe. And we've spent considerable time studying the warfare that Satan, fallen angels, and demons are waging against God and His plan—and against those people who are devoted to cooperating with God.\n\nAs believers, you need to become fully acquainted with evil spirits and their tactics in this spiritual war. These forces won't stop at any low or degrading method of warfare. They have no righteous principles, so they'll take advantage of any weakness and ignorance among Christians everywhere.\n\nWe've seen that God permits these evil forces to remain active so believers can develop faith and character. As saints, you have a sacred duty and responsibility to know how to wage successful warfare against these unscrupulous spirits.\n\nSadly, most believers don't seem to care—or at least they don't put forth much effort to defeat these enemies. Many seem quite uninformed about the war between God and Satan. Often they unknowingly cooperate with Satan and his plan, spreading his doctrines and lies more than they cooperate with God and spread His truth.\n\nThis misdirection happens because people have changed the Word of God from what is plainly written into human theories and church traditions. These have been handed down by men who have nullified Bible truths by making them mystical, spiritual, and symbolic.\n\n![Supplement 3 — For Lessons 5 & 6](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsWf7dXo9Elc9Cf1yMTquZF6SO8bsvVX7eRiYt)\n\n## How to Get Power from God over Sin\n\nAccording to the Bible, God has all power, and there is no power that isn't ordained by God (1 Chron. 29:11-12; 2 Chron. 20:6; Ps. 62:11; Zech. 4:6; Rom. 13:1-3). If all power comes from God, and if Satan's power was given him by God, then it's clear who holds all power. It's equally clear that if you want power, you should go to God for it—not seek it from demons.\n\nJesus said, "If any man serve me, him will my father honour" (Jn. 12:26). Every child of God receives power at the new birth to become a son or daughter of God, and this opens up all the possibilities of power from God over all the works of the devil (Jn. 1:12-13).\n\nChildren of God are commanded to "Be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might" and to "Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil" (Eph. 6:10-18).\n\nPaul speaks of believers having the "treasure [of God's power] in earthen vessels, that the excellency of the power may be of God, and not of us" (2 Cor. 4:7). He also states that "the weapons of our warfare are not carnal, but mighty through God to the pulling down of strong holds; casting down imaginations, and every high thing that exalteth itself against the knowledge of God, and bringing into captivity every thought to the obedience of Christ" (2 Cor. 10:4-6).\n\nThink about that! You have power through God to destroy the works of the devil and to bring every thought and imagination into obedience to Christ! How can anyone have this power and continue in sin and defeat? How can someone teach that we have to sin every day in thought, word, or deed?\n\nThink of it like having access to a master key that opens every door in a building, yet insisting you're locked out. Such teachers haven't experienced the reality of what Christian life can be. They make poor leaders, even of the blind, and as Jesus said, "if the blind lead the blind, both shall fall into the ditch" (Mt. 15:14).\n\nNo one who cares about truth and their eternal welfare should listen to or support anyone who teaches that you can't have a Christian experience that saves you from your sins and keeps you from living in sin.\n\nPeter said, "Who are kept by the power of God through faith unto salvation ready to be revealed in the last time . . . As obedient children, not fashioning yourselves according to the former lusts in your ignorance: But as he which hath called you is holy, so be ye holy in all manner of conversation [manner of life]; Because it is written, be ye holy; for I am holy . . . Seeing ye have purified your souls . . . Being born again . . . having escaped the corruption that is in the world through lust . . . give diligence to make your calling and election sure: for if ye do these things, ye shall never fall" (1 Pet. 1:5, 14-16, 22-23; 2 Pet. 1:3-10).\n\nEveryone who is born again lives free from the sin business (1 Jn. 2:29; 3:5-10; 5:1-4, 18; 2 Cor. 5:17; Eph. 4:24; Gal. 5:24).\n\nThis holy living is accomplished by God's power, not our own. It's possible because we're made free from the law of sin and death and because we walk not after the flesh but after the Spirit (Rom. 8:1-13).\n\nShould we lower our view of the Almighty and say He cannot save from sin or keep free from sin those He redeems? If God can do this but chooses not to, then sending Christ to die for this purpose was a failure. Making full provision in the gospel for this to be normal life for every child of God would be a farce.\n\nScripture is definite that sinners "shall not inherit the kingdom of God." So if Christians are sinners and all other people are sinners, then not one person will be saved (1 Cor. 6:9-11; Gal. 5:16-24; Rom. 1:29-32; 8:1-13).\n\nThere's a natural power of godliness that comes with the new birth. Those who have only a form of godliness deny this power (2 Tim. 3:5). God's power gives each person "all things that pertain unto life and godliness, through the knowledge of him that hath called us to glory and virtue" (2 Pet. 1:3-10).\n\nThe power from God to live clean and holy is yours for the asking. You can use this power of godliness to show other sinners that the gospel is real—that every person can be saved and kept from all habitual sin (1 Jn. 1:7, 9; 2 Cor. 5:17; Titus 2:11-15).\n\nIt takes power from God to live victoriously over sin, the flesh, the world, and the devil. But God our Saviour has all power to sanctify and make us "meet for the Master's use, prepared unto every good work" (2 Tim. 2:18-26).\n\nNot only can you have power to live a life pleasing to God, but you can receive power from God. The way to get this power is to make a full surrender to God, renouncing all sin and bad habits, believing on the Lord Jesus Christ to save from all sin and give sufficient power to overcome.\n\nWhen you believe from the heart, you are cleansed from all sin (Rom. 10:9-10). When you receive Jesus—not just mentally or formally, but in reality—this cleansing takes place (Jn. 1:12). When you believe that Jesus is the Christ, not only mentally but from your innermost soul (which includes turning to God from sin and Satan), this cleansing happens (Acts 26:18; 1 Jn. 5:1-4).\n\nYou might say you've done this, yet old sins and habits remain in your life. There's been no change. It may be that you haven't made the necessary change for God to work and complete the transformation in your life.\n\nThe first thing to do is settle the fact that there must be a change—and there will be when you truly get into Christ. The following scriptures prove this: "If any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new. And all things are of God, who hath reconciled us unto himself by Jesus Christ" (2 Cor. 5:17); "They that are Christ's have crucified the flesh with the affections and lusts" (Gal. 5:24); "The blood of Jesus Christ cleanseth us from all sin" (1 Jn. 1:7); He has "washed us from our sins in his own blood" (Rev. 1:5).\n\nIt's simply ridiculous to think anyone could experience this kind of change and still continue in their old sins. Because it's clear there must be a change, do the one thing necessary to bring it about.\n\nAll you have to do is obey what the Bible requires, and the rest is up to God. "If we confess our sins, He is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness" (1 Jn. 1:9).\n\nIt's impossible for anyone to truly confess their sins and not be forgiven by God. It's possible for someone to confess only part of their sins and not be heard. You won't be forgiven if you hold back some sin or habit and refuse to give it up, or if you have hatred in your heart and refuse to forgive.\n\nBut when you're honest with God—giving up your sins and habits, willing to forgive everyone, and making proper restitution wherever possible—God will not fail to forgive and make you a new creature.\n\nYou must receive Christ: "But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name" (Jn. 1:12). This means you must quit receiving sin, the world, fleshly lusts, and the devil into your life. Christ and the devil cannot both be in your life at the same time.\n\nJesus said, "No man can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to the one, and despise the other. Ye cannot serve God and mammon" (Mt. 6:24).\n\nIf Jesus told the truth, then those who preach that everyone must serve sin in the flesh while serving God in spirit are wrong. There cannot be such a double life.\n\nPaul said, "Know ye not, that to whom ye yield yourselves servants to obey, his servants ye are to whom ye obey; whether of sin unto death, or of obedience unto righteousness" (Rom. 6:16-23).\n\n## How to Get Power from God over Sicknesses\n\nPower from God to overcome sickness is on the same basis as power from God to overcome sin. Jesus taught that God has power to do both, and that one power is just as easy to receive as another: "For whether is easier, to say, Thy sins be forgiven thee; or to say, Arise and walk?" (Mt. 9:5).\n\nHe further taught that conversion and bodily healing go hand in hand: "lest at any time they should . . . understand with their heart, and should be converted, and I should heal them" (Mt. 13:15). Paul and others taught the same truth (Acts 28:25-31; Jas. 5:14-16; Ps. 103:1-3; 2 Chron. 7:14; Exod. 15:26).\n\nEvery believer can get power from God over diseases. God gives every one of His children power when they receive the true Spirit baptism (Lk. 24:49; Acts 1:8; 2 Tim. 1:7-8; Jn. 14:12). We'll explore this more in Lessons Twenty, Twenty-two, and Thirty.\n\nApart from receiving this baptism, faith is open to every child of God to get exactly what they want, as we can see from all the promises. Faith is power. The person who has faith has power. To the extent you have faith, you have power. Think of it like a key that starts an engine—faith is the key that sets God's power in motion.\n\nThere are degrees or measures of power, and God gives every child of God a measure of faith and power they can use to get what they need in life. Even if you don't have delegated power to exercise at will, you can still have faith in God. This faith sets all of heaven in motion on your behalf so you can get exactly what you have faith for.\n\nAs long as we limit God and His promises, we'll be limited in results. If we have unlimited and unqualified faith, we'll have unlimited and unqualified answers to prayer. That means we can have power over sin and sicknesses of all kinds.\n\nThe early disciples were given power over all demons and diseases, and they exercised this power before they were permanently endowed with power at Pentecost (Mt. 10:1-8; Mk. 3:15; 6:7-13; Lk. 9:1; 10:1-20). They were given power over all the power of the devil.\n\nGod's kingdom is always in power, not in word only (1 Cor. 4:20). Is God's kingdom still in existence? Has it lost its power? If not, then everyone in the kingdom has access to that kingdom's power.\n\nChrist is the power of God and the wisdom of God to all who believe (1 Cor. 1:18-24). It's impossible to have Christ in your life without having access to power, because He is the power of God to the believer.\n\nThe gospel is the power of God unto salvation to everyone who believes (Rom. 1:16). Salvation includes healing as well as forgiveness. If this is true, then the gospel is the power of God to heal, and no one can truly believe the gospel without believing in power to heal through the gospel.\n\nThe way to get power to heal yourself and others is by believing in Christ according to the gospel. By faith in the promises, each child of God can appropriate what they need. You can get healing through prayer and faith as simply and quickly as you got forgiveness of sins or anything else you've ever received from God.\n\nHealing comes on the same basis as any other answer to prayer. So why not accept this truth and ask God in faith for the power of healing in your body? If it's provided in the gospel, you might as well have it. Why be satisfied with less?\n\nIs it possible you don't want to be healed? Would you rather be sick and helpless? Certainly not! Then accept truth, which will make you free.\n\nBeing healthy is within your grasp. It's in your power. God wants His saving health to be known among all nations (Ps. 67:2). He has told us exactly how to have health.\n\nIf you'll literally practice the instructions of the following passages, you'll have health: "Forget not my laws; but let thine heart [not mind only] keep my commandments: for length of days, and long life, and peace, shall they add to thee. Let not mercy and truth forsake thee: bind them about thy neck; write them upon the table of thine heart: so shalt thou find favour and good understanding in the sight of God and man. Trust in the Lord with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding. In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths. Be not wise in thine own eyes: fear the Lord, and depart from evil. It shall be health to thy navel, and marrow to thy bones. Honour the Lord with thy substance, and with the first fruits of all thine increase: so shall thy barns be filled with plenty, and thy presses shall burst out with new wine" (Prov. 3:1-10); "Attend to my words . . . For they are life unto those that find them, and health to all their flesh" (Prov. 4:20-27; 16:24).\n\nIn Ps. 91 you're told that if you "dwell in the secret place of the most High" and "abide under the shadow of the Almighty," then "There shall no evil befall thee, neither shall any plague come nigh thy dwelling."\n\nIn Isa. 58 you're promised that if you practice twenty principles of righteousness, "Then shall thy light break forth as the morning, and thine health shall spring forth speedily . . . Then shalt thou call, and the Lord shall answer."\n\nIt's God's highest will that His children be in health (3 Jn. 2).\n\n## How to Get Power from God over Poverty\n\nThe Bible declares that God "giveth power to get wealth" (Deut. 8:17-18). When Solomon asked God for wisdom instead of wealth so he could better judge Israel, God gave him both. Solomon became one of the richest men who ever lived, simply because of God's blessing.\n\nGod also blessed Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, David, Job, and many others with great wealth. It's in God's power to make rich or to make poor (1 Sam. 2:7; Prov. 10:22; 1 Chron. 29:12).\n\nIf riches come to some people because of God's blessing, then having wealth isn't a sin. We're warned in Scripture not to misuse wealth to oppress the poor and not to let riches ensnare us into sin so we forget God and are lost (Prov. 11:28; Mt. 13:22; Lk. 8:14; 1 Tim. 6:17; Jas. 5:1-6).\n\nThe Bible lists several blessings better than riches: righteousness (Prov. 16:8; Ps. 37:17-18); a good name (Prov. 22:1); long life (Prov. 3:1-2); and wisdom (Prov. 3:13-16).\n\nThere are many assets in life better than money, so you shouldn't set your heart on wealth as your chief objective. People with riches face greater temptations and often do things they wouldn't do without money.\n\nRiches are temporary and should be recognized as such (Prov. 23:5; 27:24). You're told not to set your heart on riches or trust in them, but to trust in the Living God (Ps. 52:7; 62:10; 23:4; 1 Tim. 6:17). Many Scripture passages reveal the sins of the rich—how they oppress the poor, are boastful, proud, mean, and ungodly because they have wealth and influence.\n\nOn the other hand, the Bible speaks of many blessings of wealth when used the right way for people's good and God's glory. Wealth provides protection (Prov. 10:15; 18:11); it makes many friends (Prov. 14:20); it gives power in life (Prov. 22:7); and it enables you to be rich in good works.\n\nThis in turn—if done in the right spirit (not to be seen by others, but because it's right to do good)—will result in increased rewards in eternity (1 Tim. 6:18).\n\nMoney is power in modern times. Every child of God could do infinitely more for God and lost souls with more of this kind of power. Think what could be done with riches in spreading truth and blessing people! There's no end to the good you could do if you had the means.\n\nLooking at wealth from this perspective—even praying to God for it and expecting it from Him so you can do more for God's cause—isn't a sin. The average person doubts whether God cares about His children enjoying prosperity.\n\nSatan and even well-meaning gospel workers constantly warn believers against desiring wealth until it's become a universal belief among Christians that wealth is more or less sinful. Yet if a wealthy person becomes interested in a local church or generous in helping Christ's work, they're greatly honored and respected. This honor wouldn't be given if having wealth or asking God for it were sinful.\n\nAnyone with common sense knows there's nothing wrong with having wealth or getting it rightfully. Every child of God has many needs that could be met with more money. People often long for more wealth to better support their church and God's work. They don't consider this desire sinful.\n\nIf wealth suddenly came to them, they'd still believe they could be true Christians if they used it rightly. So we must conclude that the widespread theory that it's wrong to pray for financial help is unscriptural and unreasonable.\n\nSome argue at this point that it's not wrong to have wealth, but there are many more important blessings to ask God for. This is really just an excuse for unbelief.\n\nPeople simply don't want to let go of their old traditions, theories, and unbelief. They won't definitely pray and ask God for financial help the way they ask for physical or spiritual help.\n\nIf they'll learn the truth and ask God in faith, nothing will be impossible financially—any more than physically or spiritually. Let's be sensible and study the Bible from the standpoint of getting financial help.\n\nFirst, let's ask ourselves questions about this subject like we're starting to ask about other things. Are we children of God? Does God really love us as we love our children? Would we want our children to prosper? Does God want anything less for His children than we want for ours?\n\nWhy should He be different from us in desiring the best things of life for His children? What would be sinful about God blessing His children with wealth? Just because a few backslide and lose their souls over prosperity, that's no more excuse for living in unbelief and poverty than rejecting salvation just because some people backslide.\n\nFrom the standpoint of God's infinite Fatherhood, it's His highest will for His children to be blessed with prosperity.\n\nThink about it from the standpoint of spreading the gospel to the ends of the earth—helping support missionaries, supporting God's work at home, helping the poor become prosperous, happy, and healthy. If every Christian would claim the promises as they should, all the financial problems of every local church and worldwide ministry would be automatically solved.\n\nWhen Israel obeyed the Lord and brought their tithes and offerings, there were heaps upon heaps of supplies for God's work (2 Chron. 31:1-21). If all Christians were prosperous, there would be no need for modern methods of raising money for churches.\n\nSome churches resort to gambling and un-Christlike activities just to keep going. If everyone were prosperous, ministers would only need to make an appeal or give people an opportunity to share from the abundance God has blessed them with.\n\nNow let's look at Bible promises about prosperity. Notice how simple and clear God has made His Word about this. God promised Israel abundant prosperity if she would conform to His will (Lev. 25:21; 26:4-9; Deut. 7:13-15; 15:4-6; 28:7-8). Prosperity was promised as a natural result of obedience to God, and so it is today.\n\nThe Psalm that all Christians quote starts with "The Lord is my shepherd I shall not want." Other promises in the Psalms include: "They that seek the Lord shall not want any good thing" (Ps. 34:10); "Blessed be the Lord, who daily loadeth us with benefits" (Ps. 68:19); "Bless the Lord, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits: who forgiveth all thine iniquities; who healeth all thy diseases; who redeemeth thy life from destruction; who crowneth thee with loving kindness and tender mercies; who satisfieth thy mouth with good things; so that thy youth is renewed like the eagle's" (Ps. 103:1-5). See Ps. 84:11.\n\nTo those who honor God with their tithes and offerings—not because they want blessings, but because it's right—God has promised, "I will open to you the windows of heaven, and pour you out a blessing, that there shall not be room enough to receive it" (Mal. 3:9-11).\n\nIf someone argues this was for Israel only, we answer: it's also for the Church according to Mt. 6:26-33; 10:29; Lk. 6:38; 2 Cor. 9:6-12; Phil. 4:19; 3 Jn. 2. This last passage expresses God's will for Christians: "Beloved, I wish above all things that thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth."\n\n## How to Appropriate the Benefits of the Promises\n\nThe way to receive the promised benefits is to accept God's promises as being for you and ask God in faith for what you want. If you believe what you ask without wavering, it will be done for you because God loves you and will prosper you in everything you undertake.\n\nIf you're hindered in getting an answer, don't lose faith and blame God for not giving it. Remember there's a devil with many demons who will try to keep you from being prosperous.\n\nYou should recognize all hindrances against God's promises as coming from this source. Fight and resist Satan, and he will flee from you (Jas. 4:7). Claim the fulfillment of these promises just as you would for forgiveness, healing, or any other benefit you've asked of God.\n\nIf you're in the habit of running away every time the battle goes against you, you'll never get what you want. At some point you must take a stand with God against these evil spirits and master them. Then it will be easy to get what you want from God.\n\nReview Lesson Six on how to defeat Satan, then literally practice what you know. Victory will be yours.\n\nHappiness can be yours; freedom from fear and want can be yours; success can be yours; answers to all your prayers can be your experience—if you'll do what you're instructed. If you don't obey exactly what you know to do, how can you expect these blessings?\n\nSatan isn't the type to give up. If he sees you're easily discouraged, he'll be even more aggressive in defeating you. Decide that all double-mindedness and failure must stop.\n\nHave no fear of the outcome. Have faith in God. He will see you through. He's with you. He'll stand by you and back you in your fight for anything He has promised.\n\nBut He wants you to learn to fight, not be a defeatist just because the answer doesn't come the moment you ask. Anyone can give up and fail to get what they want. That's what almost all Christians are doing now because they lack proper teaching and coaching on how to get things from God.\n\nWe want to help you learn to receive from God those benefits that are rightfully yours as His child. If you don't get proper help from your church, we want to fill that gap.\n\nYou cannot fail. You must not fail. So much depends on your getting from God what He promised and what you've dared to ask. Your friends are watching to see whether you get what you asked for. Even sinners are watching your war with demons.\n\nFor their sake, listen carefully, learn exactly what to do, and do it without fail. The only cause of your failure is unbelief.\n\nCan it be that you're still questioning God's will concerning the blessings He's abundantly promised? If so, stop all doubting right now!\n\nIt's pure nonsense to listen to the devil tell you that God won't do what He promised, or that it's not God's will for you to get what He said He'll give you. If you listen to the devil, no wonder God doesn't hear you.\n\nThink about it—you wouldn't listen to anyone who called you a liar every time you opened your mouth and made a promise. Make sure this foolishness of making God a liar stops once and for all. Just believe what God says and forget what people and demons say!\n\nGod says you can have whatever you ask. Anyone who even suggests you can't have what you pray for is your enemy and God's enemy. They're helping Satan rob you of what's rightfully yours.\n\nThey can't rob you of these blessings if you decide not to listen to them and instead have faith in God. You know now what you must do, so do it with all your heart and you will receive abundantly.\n\nGod gives to all people liberally and doesn't scold them, but He does require faith without wavering. He won't answer on any other terms (Jas. 1:5-9; Heb. 11:6). If you don't get the answer, then you know what's wrong. Correct it, and you will be heard.\n\nIt's similar to trying to turn on a light that won't work—you have sense enough to know something is wrong. It would be foolish to keep trying without fixing the problem. When you don't get what you pray for, act sensibly. Find out what's wrong and correct it.\n\nIt's not possible that you won't know what's wrong. The steps to getting benefits from God are simple. If you're still having trouble and don't know what to do, review Supplements One and Two and carefully follow the lessons on how to pray.\n\nIf you've followed all these steps and still there's no answer, then settle it once and for all that it's unbelief and that you're under direct attack from demons. Then you'll know what to do.\n\n"Resist the devil and he will flee from you" (Jas. 4:7). How to resist the devil is clear: Take a firm stand in your innermost being against thoughts that you're not going to get an answer. Renew your faith in what God has said. Get it firmly settled that what you asked is promised by God. If it's promised, have no further doubt that you're going to receive.\n\nBegin praising God for it and obey Ps. 37:4-5: "Delight thyself also in the Lord; and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart. Commit thy way unto the Lord; trust also in him; and he shall bring it to pass."\n\nMaintain this attitude and ignore any feeling, thought, or circumstance that contradicts the answer. You can say "I believe" just as easily as you can say "it's hard to have faith."\n\nYou can make every thought and word a positive act of faith. You can simply refuse any negative thought. Learn to build up faith instead of tearing it down.\n\nState the truth in everything you say. Never think or express one thought contrary to the fact that God has heard you and that you have the answer. Though you can't see the answer, it's still yours—for faith is the substance of things hoped for and the evidence of things not seen (Heb. 11:1; Rom. 4:17-21).\n\nIf you have faith, you have the answer.\n\n---\n\n## Ten Questions For Supplement Three. Do You Know:\n\n- **That the planets reveal truth?** Besides the natural times and seasons, there are certain times and seasons for preordained events in God's plan for humanity. The children of Issachar had understanding of "the times, to know what Israel ought to do" (1 Chron. 12:32). The wise men knew by the star when Christ was born (Mt. 2:1-2, 7, 9-10). Jesus understood the signs of His time and rebuked the Pharisees for not discerning them as well as they could discern natural seasons (Mt. 16:1-4). In Ps. 19:1 we read that the heavens declare God's glory and the firmament shows His handiwork. See also Acts 1:6-7; 1 Thess. 5:1-3. These passages clearly indicate that the planets rule times and seasons and reveal certain truths.\n\n- **That eternity is made up of time and that time shall not cease?** There's a time and season for everything done under the sun (Eccl. 3). God originally made the sun, moon, and stars to regulate times and seasons on the eternal earth. The work of day four was the permanent restoration of the solar system in connection with the restored earth—to divide day from night and to be for signs, seasons, days, and years forever (Gen. 1:14-18). This solar regulation causing endless time on earth is eternal: "They shall fear thee as long as the sun and moon endure, throughout all generations . . . His name shall endure for ever: His name shall be continued as long as the sun" (Ps. 72:5, 17); "I have sworn unto David my servant, Thy seed will I establish for ever . . . his throne as the days of heaven . . . as the sun before me. It shall be established for ever as the moon" (Ps. 89:4, 27-37); "Thus saith the Lord, which giveth the sun for a light by day, and the ordinances of the moon and of the stars for a light by night . . . If those ordinances depart from me, saith the Lord, then the seed of Israel also shall cease being a nation before me for ever" (Jer. 31:35-36; 33:20-22). God promised Noah that day and night, summer and winter, seedtime and harvest, cold and heat would continue forever on earth (Gen. 8:22). The earth is eternal, so time made up of seconds, minutes, hours, days, weeks, months, and years is also eternal (Eccl. 1:4; Ps. 104:5). When the Bible says "time no longer" it should be "delay no longer," for it speaks of days and years continuing after this (Rev. 10:6-7; 12:6, 14; 13:5; 20:1-7). When the Bible says "there shall be no night there," it refers to the city, the New Jerusalem, not the earth outside the city (Rev. 21:23-27). We must conclude that time will continue eternally.\n\n- **That you are in eternity now?** As we've seen, eternity will be made up of time as we know it. If time continues eternally as it is now, then in the sense of being in eternal time, we're now in eternity. We don't mean we're in our eternal state—that won't be true until we enter immortality (1\n\n---\n\nUnderstanding the original creations of God and the reality of the spirit world isn't just cosmological — it's strategic. You're operating in a contested space, against a real adversary, with real authority from Christ. So here's the question: Given everything this supplement has covered about the spirit world, the nature of Lucifer's rebellion, and the authority believers have been given — are you using your authority in Christ, or are you living as if the outcome of spiritual conflict is uncertain?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlpa000hnnywqz55njgg	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Crystals and Crystal Healing	READING	\N	9	\N	t	![Crystals and Crystal Healing](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsIkaaCMDFm5fHMlhCe2Nngyo6VzaWuJEO4Dj7)\n\n## Crystals and Crystal Healing\n\nShe is a believer. She tithes. She prays every morning. She also has forty-three crystals on her windowsill, organized by color and chakra association. She bought them at different times, from different sellers, for different purposes. Amethyst for peace. Black tourmaline for protection. Selenite for "clearing energy." Rose quartz for love.\n\nHer pastor preached on idolatry last month. She thought the sermon was for the people who worshipped career and money. She did not connect it to the windowsill.\n\nShe does not understand why, despite genuine faith and consistent practice, a spiritual heaviness in her home has never fully lifted.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nCrystal healing is the use of mineral stones as spiritual and energetic healing tools, based on the belief that different stones carry different vibrational frequencies that interact with the body's energy systems. It is integral to New Age practice and has entered mainstream wellness culture through Instagram, boutique shops, and yoga studios.\n\nThe chakra system that crystals are used to "balance" is Hindu theology. The energy centers they are meant to align are not anatomical structures — they are components of a spiritual cosmology that belongs to a religious tradition that Scripture classifies under the prohibition of [Deuteronomy 4:19](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 4:19"). The crystals themselves are creation — beautiful, but inert. What makes them spiritually significant is not their atomic structure. It is what they have been dedicated to.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe deception is aesthetic. Crystals are genuinely beautiful. Selenite glows. Amethyst is purple and cathedral-shaped. Labradorite shifts color in the light like something alive. The beauty is real. The spiritual function assigned to them is demonic.\n\n[1 Corinthians 10:20](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 10:20"): *"The things which the Gentiles sacrifice, they sacrifice to devils, and not to God."* Anything created for, dedicated to, or used within a spiritual system outside of Jesus Christ becomes a vehicle for the demonic entities that system serves. The crystal sold at a New Age shop, blessed by the seller, assigned a specific spiritual function within the chakra system, and placed in your home with intention — is an idol. Not a metaphorical idol. An actual spiritual object with a demonic attachment.\n\n[Deuteronomy 7:26](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 7:26"): *"Neither shalt thou bring an abomination into thine house, lest thou be a cursed thing like it."* The contamination is transferable.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Spiritual systems do not become neutral through ignorance.** You do not need to believe in chakras for a crystal dedicated to a chakra function to carry its spiritual attachment. The dedication was made by the seller, the manufacturer, the tradition that produced the practice. Your ignorance of the system's religious origins does not sanitize the object.\n\n**Placement in the home creates an anchor point.** Objects with demonic attachments function as anchor points — locations within your home where the spiritual entities associated with the object have established a presence. This explains the persistent spiritual atmospheres in homes that cannot be shifted through prayer alone, until the source objects are removed.\n\n**The combination effect amplifies.** Multiple dedicated objects create multiple anchor points. Forty-three crystals, an abundance altar, a dream catcher, a Buddha figurine for "good energy" — the cumulative spiritual effect of these objects in a home is not decorative.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nLook at your home. Not at what you intended when you bought things. At what the objects were dedicated to.\n\nThe question is not: *Did I mean this as worship?* The question is: *What was this made for?*\n\nEvery crystal bought from a New Age seller, dedicated to a chakra function, or used in any energy healing context carries a spiritual assignment that was determined by the system that produced it. That assignment is not neutralized by your Christian faith, your good intentions, or the cross you hung on the wall beside it.\n\nRemove them. Destroy them. Not the garage, not a donation where someone else receives the attachment. Destroyed. Then pray over the space — anointing oil, Scripture aloud, worship. The space that is swept needs to be filled.\n\n---\n\n*Crystals anchor spiritual force in a physical object. The next lesson examines what happens when the self becomes the anchor.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Do you own any crystals — purchased or received as gifts? What were you told about their purpose?*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk44k000eewhjixyeqav8	cmnknk44i0001ewhju56drbw5	Supplement 4 — For Lessons 7 & 8	SUPPLEMENT	1780	12	\N	t	Lessons Seven and Eight established that angels governed this earth before Adam — and that the world you live in is a rebuilt version of one that was destroyed by angelic rebellion. That context matters for this supplement, because the practical truths here flow from a simple reality: God rebuilds what sin destroys. He doesn't abandon ruined things. He redeems them.\n\nThen in Lesson Eight, we saw how God restored the Earth to a second habitable state in six literal days, creating new fish, birds, land animals, and humanity. We also explored *why* God did this. His original purpose in creating the Earth was to fill it with intelligent free moral agents—beings He could reveal Himself to and bless forever with all the good things of life.\n\nGod's blessings on His creation were wonderful—beyond what human words can describe. If humanity had never sinned, there would have been no sickness, disease, defeat, harm, pain, suffering, sorrow, misery, failure, or any of the corruption that's now in the world through lust.\n\nBecause it was never God's will for humanity to sin or for these conditions to exist, we can safely conclude that this is *still* not His will.\n\nScripture—and common sense—both affirm that if humanity hadn't fallen, everyone would have been healthy, wealthy, and wise. It's equally clear that all free moral agents were meant to work toward the best public good according to the will of the Moral Governor. Even now, under sin's influence, every person is naturally obligated to consecrate themselves to the best good of all society.\n\nGod Himself, as the Supreme Moral Governor, is under the same moral obligation. Therefore, it was—and still is—His highest will that all creation exist in the highest state of perfection so this goal can be reached. It could never be God's will for even one person to be given over to anything that would hinder their part in helping all of society achieve the highest good.\n\nSo sin, sickness, poverty, want, unhappiness, and failure are *foreign elements* in God's eternal perfect plan for creation. Because they're foreign, they must be eliminated before God's plan can be fully realized. They are not—and cannot be—any part of God's will for His creation. They are the works of the devil and are enemies of God and all creation.\n\nIf they're enemies, then we should treat them as such. We should wage constant, aggressive warfare against them until they're entirely driven out of the personal life of every child of God who cooperates with Him. Think of it like weeds in a garden—you don't negotiate with weeds or welcome them as "blessings in disguise." You pull them out relentlessly until your garden flourishes the way it was designed to.\n\nAs long as Christians count these curses as friends, blessings in disguise, or the will of God, they'll be failing God and cooperating with their own enemies to destroy themselves and mar God's perfect plan for humanity.\n\n![Supplement 4 — For Lessons 7 & 8](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsClli121e78vbPqVLiKnDy6up93CGaNzkh5Hs)\n\n## How Saints Add to the Glory of Satan in a Threefold Way\n\n### I. Saints Add to Satan's Glory by Giving in to Him\n\n**1. THROUGH UNBELIEF.** "But without faith it is impossible to please him: for he that cometh to God must believe that he is, and that he is a rewarder of them that diligently seek him" (Heb. 11:6); "But let him ask in faith, nothing wavering" (Jas. 1:5-8).\n\nIt's a well-known fact that where people are taught the truth, they develop faith and receive blessings from God. After all, "faith cometh by hearing; and hearing by the word of God" (Rom. 10:17). No one can have faith in something they know nothing about. No one can trust God until they know about Him.\n\nLikewise, unbelief is the result of false teaching—of accepting lies instead of truth, of cooperating with Satan instead of God.\n\nSome argue that parts of the gospel are only for Jews, other parts only for Gentiles, some parts for this age and others for that period. They claim that miracles, healings, gifts, and supernatural powers were only for the apostles and aren't for us today.\n\nMost believers have become experts at tearing down faith and throwing cold water on anyone who dares hope that God will be a just, merciful, loving, and kind Heavenly Father—one who gives His children at least as much as evil parents give theirs. If someone even suggests that God will give His children what He's promised, they're immediately told not to expect too much from God, that such blessings might not be best for them. They're told to simply be satisfied with whatever the Heavenly Father sees fit to give and that it's sinful to be bold enough to ask for more.\n\nIf we're going to believe in the Bible at all, let's believe it in its entirety. If we're going to profess that God is able to do all things, then let Him do at least a few of the things He has abundantly promised. If we're going to be in gospel work, let's work *with* the gospel, not against it.\n\nLet's believe the best of it—the promises—and let's receive its promised benefits. If we're going to be as sensible in religion as we are in other areas of life, then let's not accept the worst ideas of the Bible while rejecting the best. We don't act that foolishly in our everyday affairs, so why be foolish in religious matters when we can do better?\n\nThis is just plain common sense. Let's wake up and recognize that when we oppose God and the Bible, we're cooperating with Satan and demons—our own enemies—and we're destroying ourselves while defeating those who are trying to conform to God's whole will according to the Bible.\n\nYes, it's true: we glorify Satan through unbelief and by giving in to his gospel-defeating program. This can be stopped right here and now—and it must be stopped before we can begin reaping the wonderful benefits of God's promises.\n\n**2. SAINTS GLORIFY SATAN THROUGH FEAR OF SICKNESS, PAIN, TROUBLE, AND DEATH.** Job said, "The thing which I greatly feared is come upon me, and that which I was afraid of is come unto me" (Job 3:25).\n\nFear comes through wrong thoughts, and wrong thoughts are the seeds of future actions. Thoughts are blueprints for what we'll eventually do. Every thought projected into the subconscious mind eventually surfaces in the active mind. If we entertain it there, it will pass into the cells and tissues of our bodies.\n\nWhat we think, to a great extent, becomes materialized. This is especially true with thoughts affecting our physical, material, and spiritual lives. When we persistently hold onto thoughts in these areas, we cause certain events to come to pass—at least within the realm of human possibility.\n\nThink of it like a navigation system in your car—whatever destination you program in is where you'll end up. If you constantly program fear, worry, and defeat into your mind, don't be surprised when you arrive at those destinations.\n\nThe devil's chief work is getting people to think wrong thoughts—that they're sick, weak, helpless, unhappy, mistreated by God and others. He wants us to believe we're facing certain calamities financially, physically, mentally, morally, and spiritually—and that we have to accept these conditions as God's will simply because they've occurred.\n\nSatan knows that if he can get people to form a strong mental picture of something, they'll act accordingly to make it a reality. If he can get them thinking and talking about sickness, failure, or whatever they're susceptible to, those conditions will soon materialize. If he can get them moaning, grumbling, and discouraged about any difficulty, it will develop.\n\nPaul said, "God hath not given us a spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind" (2 Tim. 1:7). Job's spirit of fear wasn't from God. This was probably one reason God permitted him to be tested. He was perfect in many ways, but not in being free from fear. If he wasn't free from fear, he didn't have perfect love—and there was plenty of room for refinement in his life.\n\nIf you would ignore, minimize, deny, and refuse sickness, poverty, troubles, tears, worries, sin, and suffering—whatever shouldn't be in the life of a child of God—you would soon have nothing to fear or worry about. What you are today is the result of yesterday's thoughts and fears. The sins, sicknesses, failures, and unhappiness you experience today are the results of yesterday's thoughts and plans. If those wrong thoughts had been cast down, no such wrongs would have occurred.\n\nIf a man or woman lives in thoughts of illicit love, they'll soon become victims of sin and lust. Movies, novels, magazines, provocative advertisements, dance halls, and immodest people are constant fuel for wrong thoughts—and we must refuse to feed on such ideas. The mind must be kept clean and pure.\n\nMental pictures of lust set passions in motion that only supernatural force can break. Thoughts control and materialize mental pictures. Constant dreaming and longing for harmful things soon produce sinful acts. This is why superstitions exert such influence on many people.\n\nDon't play with wrong thoughts. They're dangerous. Eventually they will bite like an adder and sting like a scorpion.\n\nThink right thoughts and you'll have no fears—and then you'll have no regrettable actions. We're all mental broadcasting stations, raising or lowering the atmosphere of the community where we live. One grouchy, pessimistic, trouble-expecting person controlled by fear and wrong thoughts can bring darkness wherever they go.\n\nIf a child begins doing wrong and you constantly talk about their wrongdoing, the child may become confirmed in that behavior. Tell them constantly that they're no good, and soon they'll prove you right. They'll more or less mold their life by their mental environment. You expect them to be wrong, they expect themselves to be wrong, and unconsciously this thinking makes them wrong.\n\nSuch a life glorifies Satan as much as anything—maybe even more. If Satan can get you to fear, he'll glory over it because he knows this is the first step toward your downfall. Satan had many months of glory from Job because he convinced him to fear that certain events would happen. And this trial may have been the only way God could bring him out of that constant state of fear and worry.\n\n**3. SAINTS GLORIFY SATAN BY GIVING IN TO HIM IN TIMES OF TEMPTATION AND TRIAL.** If every Christian realized the source of their temptation and understood that God hasn't forsaken them just because they're under attack from demons, they would conduct themselves much more courageously and Christ-like.\n\nSatan gets people to think God has forsaken them when something goes wrong. He convinces them that if God were with them, they wouldn't be going through such a trial. But you're not backslidden just because you're tempted. No sin is committed until lust has conceived and sin is finished (Jas. 1:13-15).\n\nPeople under attack from demons should do what James said: "Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you" (Jas. 4:7). Peter also said, "Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour; whom resist steadfast in the faith, knowing that the same afflictions are accomplished in your brethren that are in the world" (1 Pet. 5:8-9).\n\n**4. SAINTS GLORIFY SATAN BY PERMITTING HIM TO KEEP THEM SICK.** No child of God has to be sick or stay sick. It's the right of every believer in Christ to have perfect health and freedom from the works of the devil.\n\nThe following passages prove this: "He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty . . . A thousand shall fall at thy side, and ten thousand at thy right hand; but it shall not come nigh thee . . . there shall no evil befall thee, neither shall any plague come nigh thy dwelling" (Ps. 91); "Himself took our infirmities, and bare our sicknesses" (Mt. 8:16-17); "And all things, whatsoever ye shall ask in prayer, believing, ye shall receive" (Mt. 21:21-22); "Ye shall ask what ye will, and it shall be done unto you" (Jn. 15:7); "If the Spirit of him that raised up Jesus from the dead dwell in you, he that raised up Christ from the dead shall also quicken your mortal bodies by his Spirit that dwelleth in you" (Rom. 8:11).\n\nThe responsibility for getting healed and remaining healed is up to you. If you want healing, resist the devil and pray in faith, nothing wavering. Believe that you've received the answer—that you're healed right here and now—and reject anything to the contrary.\n\nIf God has provided healing through Christ, then it's the right and duty of every person for whom Christ died to receive the benefits He died to provide. If it's the moral obligation of each person to consecrate themselves to the best good of all society, then it becomes your obligation to exercise faith and get well so you can be a better citizen of that society and show others how they can receive such benefits too.\n\nMatthew said, "Let your light so shine before men that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven" (Mt. 5:16).\n\nAs long as you remain sick, you're not living up to your duty to society, and you glorify Satan more than God. God can receive glory only in healing and delivering people from the works of the devil—not in permitting the devil to have victory over those whom Christ died to liberate.\n\nIf every person would determine to devote their whole life to God and glorify Him completely, they would defeat Satan and refuse to be held in bondage any longer. They would be sustained by God and Christ, and Christ's work on the cross would become effective in the bodies of all.\n\nLet no one say they're glorifying God while sick and defeated in life, when the works of the devil are being manifest in them instead of the works of God. Christ came to destroy the works of the devil and give life more abundantly. Those who don't permit Him to complete this work in them are causing Christ's work to be a failure in them (Jn. 10:10; 1 Jn. 3:8; Acts 10:38).\n\n**5. SAINTS GLORIFY SATAN BY PERMITTING HIM TO ROB THEM OF THE WONDERFUL MATERIAL BENEFITS PROMISED THEM BY GOD.** If God has promised and provided material benefits for all people—particularly His own children who are the special subjects of His providence—then all believers can have these blessings.\n\nIf they don't receive them, it's not God's fault. It's the fault of the saints for permitting themselves to be defeated by Satan. God will give them the benefits He has promised and abundantly provided if they will study the Bible and acquire the faith and wisdom necessary to receive them.\n\nThe following passages prove that material blessings are promised every child of God:\n\n- "He shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper" (Ps. 1:3)\n- "Honour the Lord with thy substance, and with the first fruits of all thine increase: so shall thy barns be filled with plenty, and thy presses shall burst out with new wine" (Prov. 3:9-10)\n- "Bring ye all the tithes into the storehouse, that there may be meat in mine house, and prove me now herewith, saith the Lord of hosts, if I will not open the windows of heaven, and pour you out a blessing, that there shall not be room enough to receive it" (Mal. 3:10-11)\n- "But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you" (Mt. 6:33)\n- "Give, and it shall be given you; good measure, pressed down, and shaken together, and running over, shall men give into your bosom. For with the same measure that ye mete withal it shall be measured to you again" (Lk. 6:38)\n- "He that soweth bountifully shall also reap bountifully" (2 Cor. 9:6-10)\n- "Beloved I wish above all things that thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth" (3 Jn. 2)\n\n### II. Saints Add to Satan's Glory by Advertising His Works and Magnifying His Power\n\n**1. SAINTS ADD TO SATAN'S GLORY BY BEING LIVING TESTIMONIES OF THE POWER OF SATAN.** It may sound harsh to state the whole truth about this, but regardless of what anyone says, if sickness, sin, defeat, poverty, and failure are the works of the devil, then when these things are manifest in the lives of people who claim to be Christians, they glorify Satan more than God by bearing witness of these conditions in their lives.\n\nIf it's not God's will for His children to be in these conditions, then they're out of His will to remain satisfied enduring these curses.\n\nHow can anyone glorify God better while sick, sinful, and poverty-stricken than if they were healthy, happy, victorious, prosperous, and able to do the whole will of God according to Scripture?\n\nIf these conditions are the work of the devil, then whenever you're sick, sinful, and defeated in life, you're testifying for Satan and magnifying his power. If you had freedom from these curses, you'd be testifying to the goodness of God in delivering you from sin and sickness and in blessing you with all the good things of life.\n\n**2. SAINTS ADD TO THE GLORY OF SATAN BY BEING HIS TOOLS AT TIMES.** The Christian life is so straight and narrow that we must be on guard at all times, lest we submit to satanic influences that will hinder Christ's work.\n\nIn Mt. 16:21-25, Christ rebuked Peter for allowing Satan to influence him to try and stop Jesus from going to the cross. Here we see clearly that a Christian can, in ignorance, yield to satanic influences for a moment. It's such an easy thing to do—a person can do it without realizing it. For that reason, we must learn all about our enemy and his tactics to wage successful warfare against him and always use all our time and talents for God's righteous cause.\n\nEvery time a believer participates in division, strife, malice, hatred, or wrongdoing of any kind, they're being used as a tool of demons. All fault-finding, fears, unbelief, worry, fretting, bitterness, pride, retaliation, sinful lusts, worldliness, foolishness, insincerity, hypocrisy, dishonesty, deceit, failure, uncleanness, doubts, formality, deadness, lack of spiritual power—whatever is contrary to holy living and sound doctrine—shows that the people involved are yielded to satanic powers to that degree.\n\nAnyone who knowingly yields to these influences commits sin. Those who come to understand that these are manifestations of the wrong spirit in their life and conduct must quit all such acts or they will backslide entirely. These conditions cannot be encouraged in any life, or they'll cause a spiritual and moral breakdown and lead to other states that will damn the soul.\n\n**3. SAINTS ADD TO SATAN'S GLORY WHEN THEY PROPAGATE FALSE DOCTRINES.** Such propagators of falsehood become living epistles of Satan, known and read by all.\n\nAny doctrine that's in the least out of harmony with revealed truth should not be tolerated in the life of a child of God. When so-called "saints" become dishonest in refusing to accept plain truth—whether to further a party, a church creed, or some personal bias—they're adding to Satan's glory. They're rejecting truth and spreading falsehood.\n\nAny dishonesty in accepting certain statements on a subject and twisting them to prove some church or personal theory—while disregarding other scriptures on the same subject—is satanic in origin and practice. Those who carry on such a program are adding to the glory of Satan.\n\n### III. Saints Add to Satan's Glory by Failing God in Life and Work\n\n**1.** Every excuse for unbelief and every argument that casts any reflection on God's infinite Fatherhood, love, and will for the best good of all creation is helping Satan keep people in unbelief and bondage to sin, sickness, poverty, and failure.\n\nAll accusations against God alleging that He wills for people to be sick, helpless, powerless, sinful, and unhappy add to Satan's glory. They spread falsehoods about God and His will toward humanity and hide the true will of God from people.\n\n**2.** All failure to trust God in times of temptation, sickness, trial, and suffering—and all insinuations that God is responsible for these things—add to Satan's glory and rob God of the respect and true understanding He deserves.\n\nAll failure to fight the fight of faith and wage aggressive warfare on Satan simply adds to his glory and defeats God's plan for humanity. Failure to pray for lost souls, for your own family, your own church, your own business, and for the needs of others—all of this adds up to defeat for God's cause and results in lost souls, thereby glorifying Satan.\n\nFailure to read and study God's Word so you can be a workman rightly dividing the Word of Truth helps in the destruction of eternal souls and therefore adds to satanic success.\n\n**3.** Unconcern for lost souls, failure to live and walk in the Spirit and thus live victoriously over sin, disease, and failure in life, and disobedience to God in not earnestly coveting the best gifts and the endowment of power for service—all of this helps build up Satan's kingdom.\n\nLack of missionary vision regarding the needs of God's work as a whole destroys the highest efficiency of the child of God in their part in total warfare on evil spirits.\n\nUntil believers wake up to see their misconceptions about God and His Word and literally carry out what God really says, Satan will get more glory out of their lives than God will.\n\nAs long as Christians think and teach that it's God's will for them to be poor, weak, defeated, sick, sinful, and suffering needlessly, Satan will defeat them and rob God of the glory that would be His because of His blessings in the lives of His people.\n\nIf what we've stated is truth, then those who desire to please God should take these thoughts to heart and refuse to ever again give any glory to Satan.\n\nYou may well ask, "How can we always glorify God and not Satan?" There's only one answer: by walking in the light as God makes it clear through His Word. The main action you can take is to refuse to ever live in doubt and unbelief—and always carry through to complete victory those blessings that you ask of God.\n\n## Hindrances to Answered Prayer\n\nThere will be hindrances to answered prayer, and there's no use trying to avoid this fact. Furthermore, hindrances to answered prayer are so well known that believers even manufacture hindrances of all kinds as excuses for their unbelief.\n\nThe hindrances to answered prayer are Satan, demons, fallen angels, doubt, unbelief, and false doctrines among Christians concerning God and answered prayer.\n\n## How to Overcome Hindrances to Prayer\n\nIn Lesson Six, Point X, 11, we saw how to overcome Satan and demon powers. Review that material and doggedly carry out the instructions revealed in Scripture on this point.\n\nLet it be settled forever: Satan and demons must be defeated if you want definite answers to prayer. You must strive to bring yourself to the point where you stop all doubting and unbelief. You must lay aside all falsehoods and get to know the truth, and the truth shall make you free (Jn. 8:31-32).\n\nYou will get to know truth if you follow the light as you receive it, and you will be made free accordingly. Above all, be careful that you have Scripture to prove every part of your faith and every detail of doctrine—then it will be truth that sets you free.\n\nCorrection of doubt, unbelief, and falsehood is entirely up to you.\n\n## Ten Questions For Supplement Four. Do You Know:\n\n- **That Jesus actually descended into Hell while His body was in the tomb?** This is the truth. In Mt. 12:40; Eph. 4:7-11 we read that Christ went "in the heart of the Earth" and "into the lower parts of the Earth" during the time His body was in the tomb. This is what David meant by the Holy Spirit in Ps. 16:10; Acts 2:25-27, "For thou wilt not leave my soul in Hell; neither wilt thou suffer thine Holy One to see corruption" in the grave. During this time in Hell, Christ preached to the spirits in prison (1 Pet. 3:19).\n\n- **That 200 million horsemen will soon appear on the Earth to slay millions of men?** In the future Tribulation during the sixth trumpet judgment, four angels will be loosed that are now bound in the river Euphrates, and 200 million demon or spirit-horsemen will be loosed out of the bottomless pit. Each of these four angels will lead 50 million of these horsemen in a different direction to slay one-third of all men at a certain hour (Rev. 9:13-21). This will literally happen in the first 3½ years of Daniel's Seventieth Week, for the middle of the Week starts with the seventh trumpet (Rev. 11:15-18; 12:6, 14; 13:5). All these events take place after the rapture, as proven in Rev. 4:1, which says all the events of Rev. 4–22 "must be hereafter," that is, after the churches.\n\n- **That the United States is not once definitely mentioned in prophecy?** The very absence of any clear, definite reference to America in prophecy is sufficient to prove this. It's true that some teach Isa. 18 refers to the United States, but this is not so, for it refers to a land "which is beyond the rivers of Ethiopia," as it plainly says. There would have to be a lot of dirt moved for the United States to be relocated to this land "beyond the rivers of Ethiopia." Other students of prophecy find the United States in the beast of Rev. 13:11-18, but this refers to a man and not a country, as is clear from the language of the passage and because he is called the "false prophet" who will be destroyed with the Antichrist at the Second Coming of Christ (Rev. 16:13-16; 19:20; 20:10). The first beast of Rev. 13 is a "man" according to verse 18, and in verse 11 the second beast is called "another," which, in the Greek, means another of the same kind. If the first is a man, the second beast must also be symbolic of a man. The language of the passages concerning the two beasts proves that individuals are referred to in Rev. 13. Still others say the United States is referred to in "the islands" mentioned in Scripture, but this cannot be proven. This is mere human theory, so we conclude that there is no direct reference to the United States in prophecy.\n\n- **That you will know each other in both Heaven and Hell?** "For now we see through a glass darkly; but then face to face: now I know in part; but then shall I know even as also I am known" (1 Cor. 13:12). We are told in 1 Cor. 15:25-29; Phil. 3:20-21 that every person will be resurrected with the same kind of body that was sown in the ground and that every person will have "his own body," so naturally if we know each other here, we shall know each other in Heaven or Hell. In Lk. 16:19-31, the rich man while in Hell knew Lazarus, and so will every other person know whomever they see whom they knew on Earth.\n\n- **That one-third of the ships of the sea will soon be destroyed?** This will happen in the future tribulation when the second trumpet blows (Rev. 8:8-9).\n\n- **That the future Tribulation will not be worldwide?** Nearly every plague that will be poured out in the Tribulation states that it will be over a fourth or a third part of the Earth only, thus showing that the trouble for which these plagues are sent will be only on part of the Earth. See Rev. 6:8; 8:7-12; 9:18; 16:10, 12. As we shall see, Antichrist will rule just a certain part of the Earth, and because he is the one causing the Tribulation, it will be only over the part of Earth which he rules.\n\n- **That many people have already gone to Heaven and Hell?** Enoch (Gen. 5:24; Heb. 11:5); Elijah (2 Ki. 2:11-13); Paul (2 Cor. 12:1-7); John (Rev. 4:1); and many bodies of the Old Testament saints (Mt. 27:52-53); and all those that were not resurrected were captured from the devil in the underworld and taken to Heaven when Christ went back to Heaven (Eph. 4:7-11; Acts 1:11). Now when every righteous soul leaves the body at death, it goes to Heaven until the resurrection (2 Cor. 5:8; Phil. 1:21-23; Rev. 6:9-11). All the souls of the wicked that have ever died have gone to Hell and will continue to go there until after the Millennium, when those in Hell will be brought before God in judgment, and then they will be cast into the Lake of Fire (Lk. 16:19-31; Rev. 20:11-15).\n\n- **That the Bible tells you what Satan looks like?** He is a most beautiful angel with an angelic body. All angels have bodies like men, as we saw in Lesson Four. Satan then looks like a human being bodily, but much more beautiful according to Ezek. 28:11-17. (See Lesson Six, Point X).\n\n- **That the Bible tells you where Cain got his wife?** He married his sister, for "Adam called his wife's name Eve; because she was the mother of all living" (Gen. 3:20). In Gen. 5:4, we read that Adam "begat sons and daughters," and in Gen. 6:1-2 we read, "When men began to multiply on the face of the Earth, and daughters were born to them, That the sons of God saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose." One old tradition says that Cain had a twin sister named Lulawa and that he married his sister. Be that as it may, we know that he had to marry a sister to get the race started, for all humanity came from Adam and Eve.\n\n- **That the Bible tells you where Hell is located?** It is located in the lower parts or in the center of the Earth (Mt. 12:40; Eph. 4:7-11; Isa. 14:9).\n\n---\n\nThe God who took a wrecked, chaotic earth and rebuilt it in six days is the same God dealing with your ruined situations today. His response to wreckage is not abandonment — it's re-creation. So here's the question: What situation in your life looks most like 'without form, and void' right now? And are you believing that the same Spirit who moved over the face of the deep can move over that situation?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlon0001nnywvd28nt6l	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	The New Age Movement	READING	\N	19	\N	t	![The New Age Movement](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Ost4ewxdXSSw8OsqyXxGpeBMuoLIEnWg5fdi9R)\n\n## The New Age Movement\n\nShe found it in a bookshop the year her mother died. *A Course in Miracles.* The cover said it was a spiritual self-study program. It said the voice that dictated it was Jesus. It said there was no sin, no evil, no real separation from God — only the illusion of it. Grief does something to a person's theology. She bought it. She read it every morning for two years. By the end, she had stopped believing in the cross.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nThe New Age Movement is not a single religion. It is a spiritual ecosystem — an open-source collection of practices and beliefs that draws from Hinduism, Buddhism, Theosophy, folk magic, and Western occultism, repackaged for secular Western consumption. Its hallmarks are self-deification ("you are divine"), relativism ("all paths lead to God"), channeled revelation (messages received from spiritual entities), meditation practices designed to empty the mind and contact higher consciousness, and energy healing.\n\nIt gained mainstream traction in the 1970s through Shirley MacLaine, exploded in the 1980s through the New Age section of every bookshop, and today operates invisibly inside wellness culture, coaching, and social media spirituality. The crystal seller, the "human design" consultant, and the life coach who tells you to "trust your higher self" are all operating within this framework.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe central claim of the New Age Movement is that humanity is divine, separation from God is an illusion, and the goal of spiritual practice is to realize your inherent oneness with universal consciousness.\n\nThis is the serpent's original lie — delivered in a gentler, more therapeutic format.\n\n[Genesis 3:5](data-scripture="Genesis 3:5"): *"Ye shall be as gods."* The serpent did not offer open rebellion. He offered spiritual elevation. The New Age does the same. It does not tell people to worship Satan. It tells them they are already divine — that repentance, the cross, and a Savior are unnecessary because there is nothing to be saved from.\n\nThe "higher self" that New Age practitioners are taught to consult is not their own best wisdom. It is a familiar spirit that has positioned itself as their internal divine guide. The "channeled messages" that form the backbone of New Age scripture — *A Course in Miracles*, the Seth Material, the Abraham teachings — were received in states of trance or dissociation. They are demonic transmissions dressed as divine revelation. [1 Timothy 4:1](data-scripture="1 Timothy 4:1"): *"Now the Spirit speaketh expressly, that in the latter times some shall depart from the faith, giving heed to seducing spirits, and doctrines of devils."*\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Self as god removes accountability.** When you are divine, there is no sin — only "lower vibration." There is nothing to repent of. The blood of Christ becomes unnecessary. This is not a minor theological disagreement; it is the removal of the only mechanism by which human beings can be reconciled to God.\n\n**Meditation practices invite spiritual entities.** New Age meditation — visualizing guides, opening chakras, accessing the Akashic Records — is structured spirit contact, regardless of the therapeutic language used to describe it. The entities encountered are familiar spirits, not higher selves or ascended masters.\n\n**Channeled content transfers spiritual attachments.** Reading, listening to, or watching channeled material is not passive entertainment. The demonic entities that authored these teachings are drawn to the attention and assent they receive. Sustained engagement creates spiritual attachment.\n\n**The denial of evil leaves people defenseless.** A worldview that calls evil an illusion and suffering a spiritual lesson has no framework for recognizing demonic attack. New Age practitioners who experience oppression interpret it as unresolved karma or a lesson to learn — and go deeper into the system that opened the door.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nHere is the question that most New Age practitioners never get asked directly: *If all paths lead to God, why do the entities encountered in New Age practice consistently deliver the same message — that Jesus is one teacher among many, that the cross is unnecessary, that you are already divine?*\n\nEvery authentic encounter with the living God in Scripture produces the same response: prostration, terror, and the recognition of personal unworthiness ([Isaiah 6:5](data-scripture="Isaiah 6:5"), [Revelation 1:17](data-scripture="Revelation 1:17")). The encounters produced by New Age practice produce self-confidence, special status, and the sense that you have accessed knowledge unavailable to ordinary believers.\n\nThose two experiences do not have the same source.\n\nIf you have engaged with New Age teaching — read channeled texts, consulted your "higher self," worked with energy guides — the first step is not complicated. Name it for what it is. [Acts 19:19](data-scripture="Acts 19:19") records that the Ephesian converts brought their magic books into a public square and burned them, valued at 50,000 pieces of silver. The act was public, costly, and complete. That is the standard.\n\n---\n\n*The New Age provides the theological framework. The next lesson examines the specific entity it assigns as personal guide for the journey.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *What New Age material have you read, listened to, or been given by someone you trusted? Name it specifically and describe what drew you to it.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlp7000fnnyw24j587wa	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Spirit Guides	READING	\N	20	\N	t	![Spirit Guides](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsFHCetRbM1hRYQ2o4Z38BzgHNSP5KdLckVeFn)\n\n## Spirit Guides\n\nHe was a counselor — a licensed therapist with fifteen years of practice. He had done Jungian analysis, EMDR, somatic work. During a meditation retreat, he encountered what he described as a radiant being who said it had been with him since before his birth, sent to guide his work with clients. He called it his "inner teacher." He began to feel its presence during sessions. It told him things about clients that he had not been told. His practice became remarkably effective.\n\nHe could not explain the effectiveness clinically. He did not want to examine it too closely. The results were real. The clients were healing. Why ask questions about the source?\n\nBecause what you cannot name, you cannot evict.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nSpirit guides are entities presented as personal divine helpers assigned to each human being — companions who provide wisdom, warning, and direction from the spirit realm. They appear in New Age practice, shamanism, and increasingly in mainstream therapeutic settings where they are rebranded as "inner wisdom," "the higher self," or "intuition."\n\nThe encounter typically occurs during meditation, altered states, near-death experiences, or psychedelic sessions. The being presents as radiant, wise, compassionate, and intimately familiar with the person's history and needs. It offers guidance. It asks only that the person listen.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\n[2 Corinthians 11:14](data-scripture="2 Corinthians 11:14"): *"And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light."*\n\nThe appearance of a spirit guide is designed to be convincing. It is warm where demons in horror films are cold. It is helpful where demons in theology are destructive. It presents itself as a known quantity — "your guide since before birth" — to establish a sense of permanent, covenantal relationship.\n\nWhat it is doing, from the first moment of contact, is establishing itself as the governing authority over the person's decision-making. Over time, the relationship progresses: consultation → dependency → the guide's voice becoming more authoritative than Scripture → an inability to function without its direction. The Holy Spirit does not produce dependency. He produces freedom. [2 Corinthians 3:17](data-scripture="2 Corinthians 3:17"): *"Now the Lord is that Spirit: and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty."*\n\nA spirit that produces dependency is not the Holy Spirit.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The voluntary invitation is the legal act.** The person who seeks a spirit guide — through meditation, shamanic journey, or psychedelic ceremony — performs a voluntary act of spiritual invitation. What arrives in response to that invitation is not determined by the person's intent but by what is available and interested in the territory being offered.\n\n**The guide assumes the Holy Spirit's role.** This is its defining feature and its most catastrophic function. It positions itself as the person's internal divine counsel — the voice of God, the wisdom of the universe, the inner teacher. Once this substitution is established, the genuine Holy Spirit is crowded out. The person has all the subjective experience of spiritual guidance, with a demonic source producing it.\n\n**Progressive surrender expands the entity's domain.** The more a person consults the guide, the more authority it accumulates over different areas of life. This is why people who have worked with spirit guides for years often describe a quality of not knowing their own mind — a difficulty distinguishing their own thoughts from the guide's voice.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf you have a spirit guide — if there is a voice, presence, or inner entity that has guided you that is not identifiably the Holy Spirit speaking through the Word of God — you are in a relationship that needs to end.\n\nThe Holy Spirit does not require you to seek Him through altered states. He is already present in every born-again believer. He speaks through Scripture, prayer, and the community of the body of Christ. He does not present Himself as a distinct entity with a name and a personality separate from God. He does not compete with Jesus for attention.\n\nRenounce the spirit guide by name if it has given you one. Renounce every session, every decision made on its counsel, every relationship with other entities it introduced. Command it to leave in the name of Jesus Christ. Ask the Holy Spirit — the real one — to fill every space the counterfeit occupied.\n\n---\n\n*Spirit guides operate in the secular seeking space. The next lesson examines how the same entity gets through the church's front door.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you ever asked a guide, an ancestor, or a spiritual entity for direction — even informally, even in what felt like prayer? Describe the encounter.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlp10009nnywyle5uam6	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Tarot Cards	READING	\N	27	\N	t	![Tarot Cards](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OshxzFf32RWrNFBdIuiJlO67t4A5yKbkf8vT0P)\n\n## Tarot Cards\n\nShe bought the deck because the artwork was beautiful. The Rider-Waite illustrations — the High Priestess with her pillars and pomegranates, the Hermit with his lantern, the Tower struck by lightning — looked like religious art. She thought of it as a journaling tool. A way to access intuition.\n\nThe first reading she did for a friend was startlingly accurate. The friend cried. Said she felt seen. Asked when they could do it again.\n\nWithin eight months, she was reading for sixty people. Charging eighty dollars a session. Doing three readings a day. She could not stop — not because of the income, but because something in her lit up every time she touched the cards. Something that went away when she put them down. Something that increasingly felt like it was not hers.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nThe tarot deck emerged in 15th-century northern Italy as a card game. Its transformation into a divination tool came in the 18th century when French occultists attached Kabbalistic, astrological, and Hermetic symbolism to the 78 cards. The Major Arcana — the 22 archetypal cards — map onto the Kabbalistic Tree of Life. The four suits of the Minor Arcana correspond to the four elements and to the four Tetragrammaton letters of the divine name.\n\nIn its current form, tarot is not a neutral psychological projection tool. It is a spiritual intelligence system — a structured interface through which familiar spirits deliver information, counsel, and guidance to practitioners and their clients.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nWhat makes tarot convincing is not the cards themselves. The cards are paper. What makes it convincing is the familiar spirit providing the interpretive intelligence that makes a reading feel specific, accurate, and personally resonant.\n\nA reading that should statistically produce generic platitudes instead produces: the name of a relationship problem, the specific emotional wound, the accurate timeline of an event, the detail that only the client knows. This accuracy is not the cards — it is the familiar spirit that has been observing the client and reporting to the reader.\n\nThe danger escalates with practice. Long-term tarot use creates what practitioners call spiritual "sensitization" — an increasing attunement to the entities involved. Readers describe feeling the cards "speak to them," feeling pulled to read compulsively, losing the ability to make decisions without consulting the deck. This is familiar spirit dependency in progressive stages: consultation → compulsion → control.\n\n[Leviticus 19:31](data-scripture="Leviticus 19:31"): *"Regard not them that have familiar spirits, neither seek after wizards, to be defiled by them: I am the LORD your God."*\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The first accurate reading establishes trust and deepens engagement.** The familiar spirit's goal in the first reading is not to cause harm but to produce enough accuracy to ensure the practitioner and client return. The hook is always accuracy. The bondage comes later.\n\n**Every reading is a spirit-contact transaction.** The act of consulting the tarot is spiritually identical to visiting a medium. The mechanism differs. The transaction is the same: seeking information or guidance from familiar spirits through an occult interface.\n\n**Spiritual sensitization creates dependency.** The "gift" that readers develop through sustained tarot practice is not psychic ability. It is an increasingly refined relationship with the familiar spirit assigned to the practice. The gift is the bondage. The reader who cannot function without the cards has been successfully captured.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nDo you have tarot cards in your home? Have you had readings done — at a fair, online, by a friend, "just to see"?\n\nEvery reading done on your behalf was a familiar spirit accessing your life through an authorized channel. The authorization came from your presence, your questions, your assent.\n\nRepent for every reading received or given. Renounce the familiar spirits involved. Destroy every deck. This is not spiritual overcaution — it is the same action that Acts 19 records new believers taking with their magic books. The cost then was 50,000 pieces of silver. The cost required of you is the willingness to let go.\n\n---\n\n*Tarot creates a ritual framework for familiar spirit consultation. The next lesson examines the human intermediary who does the same work for a fee.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you had a tarot reading — professionally, casually, or online? What question were you trying to answer, and what did the reading tell you?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlp3000bnnywj1bv6t2z	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Psychics	READING	\N	28	\N	t	![Psychics](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OspKSp4RMUGDFtHARxTo0frklQIVBOcXizMeJh)\n\n## Psychics\n\nShe had been to three therapists in two years after her son died. She could not get past it. A friend mentioned a medium — someone who had connected her with her father after he passed. She said it brought closure. The grieving mother drove an hour and paid $200.\n\nThe medium said her son's name correctly. Said he was wearing the blue jacket she had buried him in. Said he wanted her to know about the argument they'd had the week before he died — the specific words, the way the door had sounded when it closed. She wept for forty minutes. She said it was the most healing experience of her life.\n\nShe did not know that her son was not there. She did not know what had come home with her.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nThe psychic industry generates billions annually — storefront readers, television mediums, phone services, online platforms. Behind the variety of presentation is a single spiritual mechanism: familiar spirits providing information through human intermediaries who have opened themselves, voluntarily or through ancestral access, to demonic entity communication.\n\n[Isaiah 8:19](data-scripture="Isaiah 8:19"): *"And when they shall say unto you, Seek unto them that have familiar spirits, and unto wizards that peep, and that mutter: should not a people seek unto their God? for the living to the dead?"* This verse is 2,700 years old and describes your city's yellow pages.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe medium's accuracy is the entire mechanism of deception. The son's name. The blue jacket. The argument's exact words. These are the details a familiar spirit that has observed a family for years — that has been present in the room for every conversation, that knows the relationship's entire history — can provide. The medium is not channeling the dead. The dead cannot be channeled ([Hebrews 9:27](data-scripture="Hebrews 9:27")). The medium is accessing a familiar spirit's knowledge of the deceased.\n\nThe apparent communication produces real emotion — real grief processing, real sense of closure, real experience of connection. The emotional experience is genuine. The source of the information is demonic. And the familiar spirit that provided the performance does not leave when the session ends. It follows the client home.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The transfer problem.** Visiting a psychic is not a passive information exchange. Familiar spirits pass between practitioners and their clients. The entity that produced accurate readings in the session has now established access to the client. This is why people who visit psychics — even once, even for bereavement — often report subsequent spiritual disturbance: nightmares, felt presences, obsessive thoughts about what was said.\n\n**Leviticus 20:6 is an active warning.** *"And the soul that turneth after such as have familiar spirits, and after wizards, to go a whoring after them, I will even set my face against that soul."* God does not merely prohibit the practice — He describes His response to those who pursue it. The word is deliberate: pursuing familiar spirits is spiritual adultery against the God who offers His own counsel freely.\n\n**Grief vulnerability creates a specific exposure window.** The psychic industry knows this and markets specifically to the bereaved. People in acute grief are more spiritually permeable, more desperately seeking contact, and less likely to apply discernment. The most dangerous time to visit a psychic is the time when it is most tempting.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nHave you visited a psychic, medium, or spiritual reader — for any reason, at any level of seriousness?\n\nGrief is real. The desire to know that a lost loved one is at peace is real and human and understandable. But the God who invented grief also provides the only legitimate comfort available to the bereaved. [1 Thessalonians 4:13-14](data-scripture="1 Thessalonians 4:13-14"): *"But I would not have you to be ignorant, brethren, concerning them which are asleep, that ye sorrow not, even as others which have no hope. For if we believe that Jesus died and rose again, even so them also which sleep in Jesus will God bring with him."*\n\nThe hope is in the resurrection. Not in a $200 session with a familiar spirit that knew your son's jacket color.\n\nRepent for the visit. Renounce the familiar spirit that was accessed. Break its continued legal claim on your life. Receive the comfort that [2 Corinthians 1:3-4](data-scripture="2 Corinthians 1:3-4") promises — from the Father of mercies, not from a familiar spirit that wears the faces of the dead.\n\n---\n\n*Psychics provide professional spirit mediation. The next lesson examines what happens when amateurs attempt the same mediation with a board and a planchette.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you paid for a psychic reading, called a hotline, or used a psychic service? What were you hoping to find out — and was the information accurate?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlow0005nnywkxnl8x57	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Ouija Boards	READING	\N	29	\N	t	![Ouija Boards](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsbRiT10pZWXUxpYCzVoHdTRw8N94g0J5LQu7D)\n\n## Ouija Boards\n\nIt was a sleepover. Six twelve-year-old girls in a basement. One of them had taken her older brother's board without asking. The planchette moved. It spelled the name of one girl's dead grandmother. It gave details — the name of the grandmother's cat, the town where she lived, the color of her kitchen.\n\nThe girl whose grandmother it was went home the next morning and stopped sleeping. For three months. The presence in her room at night was not her grandmother.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nParker Brothers marketed the Ouija board as a parlor game and sold it in the toy aisle. It is not a toy. It is a commercial simplification of the séance — a device designed to facilitate communication with spiritual entities through the combined attention and physical contact of multiple participants.\n\nThe name comes from the French and German words for "yes." It was patented in 1891. The ideomotor effect — the unconscious muscular movements of participants — explains some of the board's mechanical function. It does not explain why the board sometimes produces information that participants could not have known, communicates in languages they do not speak, or causes paranormal physical phenomena in the room where it is used.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe board's marketing as a game is the deception. The framing as entertainment removes the sense of spiritual gravity that accompanies deliberate séance work. The child or teenager who picks up a Ouija board at a party is performing the exact same spiritual act as a formal medium conducting a spirit-contact session — the invitation to non-human intelligences to communicate through a human-operated interface.\n\nThe entities that respond through Ouija boards are familiar spirits. They are not the deceased relatives they often claim to be. They have studied the deceased long enough to produce convincing details. The grandmother's cat, the kitchen color, the town — these are the details a demon that has observed a family for decades could easily provide. [Leviticus 20:27](data-scripture="Leviticus 20:27"): *"A man also or woman that hath a familiar spirit, or that is a wizard, shall surely be put to death."* The severity of the prohibition reflects the severity of what is being invited.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The voluntary act of seeking is the legal invitation.** God's spiritual law does not distinguish between sincere practice and curious experimentation. The moment a person places their hands on the planchette and asks a question, they have performed a voluntary act of spirit contact. What responds to that contact has a legal claim to remain.\n\n**Threshold effects are documented.** Many people who have used a Ouija board report a shift in spiritual atmosphere in their home or life afterward — nightmares, sensed presences, oppressive spiritual heaviness, an inability to shake the feeling of being watched. These are threshold effects: the entity that entered through the board does not confine itself to the session.\n\n**Children are uniquely vulnerable.** The Ouija board's marketing to young people is spiritually catastrophic. Children have less developed discernment, a higher degree of spiritual openness, and a longer lifetime ahead of them for the entity that enters through a childhood session to operate. Adults who trace oppression to a childhood Ouija board session are not being dramatic.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf you have ever used a Ouija board — once, as a teenager, as a joke, at a party — you extended a spiritual invitation that you have probably never formally revoked.\n\nHere is the specific action required: name the session aloud before God. Name when it happened, who was present, what was sought, what responded. Repent for the act of seeking spirit contact outside of God. Renounce every entity that entered through that contact. Declare the access revoked by the blood of Jesus Christ.\n\nIf a Ouija board is anywhere in your home — yours, your children's, stored in a closet — destroy it. Not the trash. Not a donation. Destroyed.\n\n[Isaiah 8:19](data-scripture="Isaiah 8:19"): *"Should not a people seek unto their God? for the living to the dead?"*\n\n---\n\n*The Ouija board is a single tool. The next lesson examines the organized system behind all the tools — the broader domain of forbidden knowledge.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you used a Ouija board — at any age, at any level of seriousness? What happened, and what followed in the days or weeks after?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xu0a0005cdn8pfwyppsc	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Part VII Quiz: Closing the Door	QUIZ	\N	54	\N	t	## Part VII Quiz: Closing the Door\n\nThis is the final quiz of the Demons course. Take it after completing all 44 lessons and both supplements. The goal is not just to assess knowledge — it is to help you identify any area of this course that needs a second pass before you move forward.\n\n---\n\n**1. The key theological principle underlying all of Part VII is that demonic activity requires:**\n\nA) An explicit invitation from the person\nB) The person to be spiritually weak or traumatically wounded\nC) Legal ground — specific sin, covenant, or object that gives the enemy a legal claim\nD) The person to not be a Christian\n\n---\n\n**2. What distinguishes divination from prayer, according to this course?**\n\nA) Divination uses physical tools; prayer does not\nB) Divination seeks guidance from sources other than God; prayer directs the request to God alone\nC) Divination is always performed in groups; prayer is individual\nD) Divination is only a sin when performed professionally\n\n---\n\n**3. According to 1 Corinthians 10:20, what is the entity behind idol worship?**\n\nA) A psychological projection of human fear\nB) Nothing — idols are empty and without spiritual power\nC) Demons who receive the worship directed at false deities\nD) Angels who were assigned to those nations before the gospel reached them\n\n---\n\n**4. What is the "spirit of antichrist" that 1 John 4:3 describes, and how does it operate in Part VII?**\n\nA) A specific named demonic entity that appears at the end of history\nB) The spirit operating in every system that denies Jesus Christ as Lord and Savior — visible across false religions, false gospels, and counterfeit spiritual systems\nC) The political spirit behind authoritarian governments\nD) A euphemism for secular humanism\n\n---\n\n**5. Yoga, Reiki, Feng Shui, and Transcendental Meditation are grouped together because:**\n\nA) They are all from Asia and reflect Eastern philosophy\nB) They are all prohibited by most world religions\nC) They all involve invoking or manipulating spiritual forces from systems outside Christ, regardless of how they are marketed\nD) They are all ineffective — their claimed benefits are purely psychological\n\n---\n\n**6. According to this course, what is the primary deception of familiar spirits operating as spirit guides?**\n\nA) They pretend to be extraterrestrial life\nB) They present as beautiful, helpful, and wise while functioning as undercover agents of the enemy\nC) They only appear to people who are mentally ill\nD) They impersonate the Holy Spirit exclusively\n\n---\n\n**7. What does Exodus 20:5 establish regarding generational curses?**\n\nA) Each person is responsible only for their own sins — parental sin has no effect on children\nB) God punishes children for their parents' specific actions, unconditionally\nC) Iniquity — a pattern of sin — visits through generational lines, creating spiritual assignments that persist until broken\nD) Generational curses were only relevant under the Mosaic Law and do not apply after the cross\n\n---\n\n**8. The "soul tie" formed through sexual union is based on which Scripture?**\n\nA) Romans 7:2 — "the woman which hath an husband is bound by the law to her husband"\nB) 1 Corinthians 6:16 — "he which is joined to an harlot is one body? for two, saith he, shall be one flesh"\nC) Genesis 2:24 — "a man shall leave his father and mother and cleave unto his wife"\nD) Ephesians 5:31 — "they two shall be one flesh"\n\n---\n\n**9. Why does this course recommend destroying occult objects rather than donating or storing them?**\n\nA) Because occult objects lose their spiritual power over time and become harmless\nB) Because destruction matches the biblical precedent of Acts 19:19 and Deuteronomy 7:25-26, and removes the anchor and the possibility of transferring the attachment to another person\nC) Because donated occult objects will return to the original owner spiritually\nD) Because occult objects are too dangerous for trash collectors to handle\n\n---\n\n**10. What is the mechanism by which Jesus' blood resolves legal ground, according to Supplement 11?**\n\nA) The blood of Jesus emotionally reassures believers, giving them confidence to resist the enemy\nB) The blood is a magical shield that automatically repels demons from believers' lives\nC) The blood of Jesus is a legal payment of infinite worth that extinguishes every demonic legal claim when applied through specific, Spirit-directed repentance and renunciation\nD) The blood of Jesus works automatically at conversion and requires no subsequent application to specific areas of sin\n\n---\n\n**11. What does this course identify as the specific pattern that makes AI spiritual tools dangerous?**\n\nA) The AI systems are directly programmed by demonic forces\nB) AI "pastoral" tools replace relationship-based community, drift toward theological compromise, and create dependent consultation with a system trained on humanity's accumulated (and spiritually compromised) wisdom\nC) AI cannot understand spiritual language and produces nonsense when asked about God\nD) AI tools are only dangerous when specifically programmed to teach false doctrine\n\n---\n\n**12. The biblical response to the UFO/alien phenomenon in this course is:**\n\nA) Agnosticism — the Bible does not address the topic and no Christian position is possible\nB) The phenomena are fabricated by government agencies and are not spiritually significant\nC) The phenomena are real, but the correct category is demonic entities presenting in the form most likely to be accepted by a post-Christian culture\nD) If extraterrestrial intelligence exists, God must have died for their sins too\n\n---\n\n**13. According to this course, what is the specific danger of false gospels such as the prosperity gospel?**\n\nA) They waste money through excessive tithing requirements\nB) They present a Christ who cannot save — and the people who trust in that Christ are not trusting the Christ of Scripture\nC) They distort believers' personalities and make them difficult to live with\nD) They are simply doctrinally incomplete but still valid paths to salvation\n\n---\n\n**14. The Freedom Prayer Guide in Supplement 12 follows which sequence?**\n\nA) Repent → Command departure → Renounce → Identify → Apply blood → Fill\nB) Identify → Repent → Renounce → Apply blood → Command departure → Fill\nC) Command departure → Identify → Repent → Fill → Apply blood → Renounce\nD) Fill → Apply blood → Repent → Identify → Command departure → Renounce\n\n---\n\n**Answer Key**\n\n1. C — Legal ground\n2. B — Source of guidance\n3. C — Demons receive the worship\n4. B — Every system that denies Christ\n5. C — All involve spiritual forces from non-Christian systems\n6. B — Beautiful, helpful, wise cover for enemy agents\n7. C — Generational spiritual assignments until broken\n8. B — 1 Corinthians 6:16\n9. B — Biblical precedent and removal of anchor/transfer risk\n10. C — Legal payment applied through repentance\n11. B — Replacement of community, theological drift, trained on compromised wisdom\n12. C — Demonic entities in culturally acceptable form\n13. B — A Christ who cannot save\n14. B — Identify → Repent → Renounce → Apply blood → Command → Fill\n\n---\n\n*If you missed any question, return to the corresponding lesson before moving forward. The Freedom Prayer Guide in Supplement 12 is designed to be used as many times as needed — once through the whole sequence, and then returned to for specific areas as the Holy Spirit brings them to light.*\n\n*You have completed the Demons course. What you now know is not theoretical — it is operational. Use it.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlot0003nnyw9w38tmha	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	The Occult	READING	\N	30	\N	t	![The Occult](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsVGUOBg31DSEv9r4BQbmhHPx2ALYz3ynujqdo)\n\n## The Occult\n\nHe was twelve the first time he read about it in a library book. The word *occult* sounded exotic, ancient, powerful. The chapter on divination explained how Egyptian priests read the entrails of animals to determine the will of the gods. The chapter on necromancy described how the living could communicate with the dead. He thought it was history. He did not know it was an instruction manual.\n\nTwenty years later he sat across from a deliverance minister who asked him when it started. He remembered the library book. He remembered thinking, even at twelve: *I want that kind of access.*\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\n*Occult* means hidden. It covers every practice that seeks supernatural knowledge, power, or contact with spiritual beings through channels other than the God of Scripture. The complete inventory is in [Deuteronomy 18:10-12](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 18:10-12"): divination, observing times, enchanting, witchcraft, charming, consulting familiar spirits, wizardry, necromancy. God calls them *abomination* — not childish nonsense, not spiritual immaturity, but an abomination.\n\nThat word choice matters. God does not call these things an abomination because they are ineffective. He calls them an abomination because they work — but through the wrong power and toward the wrong end.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe occult operates on a single promise: access. Access to hidden knowledge, to power over circumstances, to contact with dimensions of reality unavailable through ordinary experience. This promise is partially fulfilled, and that partial fulfillment is the entire mechanism of the trap.\n\nThe demonic realm knows things. Familiar spirits have observed human history across millennia. They know family secrets. They can produce information that appears supernaturally accurate. They can manifest power that produces genuine, visible results. The person who seeks occult access and finds it working is not being deceived about whether it works — they are being deceived about who is doing the work and what the cost will be.\n\n[2 Corinthians 11:14](data-scripture="2 Corinthians 11:14"): *"For Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light."* The occult does not announce itself as darkness. It announces itself as illumination. That is what the word *illuminati* — those who have received the hidden light — actually means.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The initial contact establishes legal ground.** The first séance, the first tarot reading, the first spell, the first conscious attempt to contact supernatural intelligences outside of God — this is the moment of legal invitation. The entity that responds to this invitation does not leave when the session ends.\n\n**Each level deepens the attachment.** Occult involvement almost universally follows a progression: curiosity → experimentation → dependency → servitude. The person who started with a horoscope ends up with a regular psychic. The person who started with a ouija board ends up with a ritual practice. The deepening is not accidental — it is the enemy's design.\n\n**Occult involvement in the family line creates generational access.** When ancestors practiced divination, sorcery, or spiritism, the entities that were invited through their practice claim generational access. This explains the families where occult interest reproduces across generations with no direct transmission — the same spirits are operating down the bloodline.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThe question is not whether you have fully committed to an occult system. The question is whether you have ever sought supernatural access through any channel outside of God.\n\nOnce. Curiously. As a teenager. At a party. Online. As an experiment.\n\nThat single moment of voluntary seeking is the legal moment — the invitation that the enemy treats as authorization to establish a foothold. [Ephesians 4:27](data-scripture="Ephesians 4:27"): *"neither give place to the devil."* The word is *topos* — a specific location, a legally claimed territory.\n\nIdentify the specific entry point. Name it. Repent for the act of seeking access from a source other than God. Renounce the entities that responded to that seeking. The blood of Jesus Christ is legally sufficient to revoke every claim.\n\n---\n\n*The occult is the repository of forbidden knowledge. Witchcraft is what you do with it.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *What is the most explicitly occultic content — book, website, or practice — you have engaged with? Did you understand what you were engaging at the time?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlp5000dnnywwpdags4y	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Witchcraft	READING	\N	31	\N	t	![Witchcraft](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsdccTecCHEavRrA2ePyuNDOn3wIQ7Y9mCfTkU)\n\n## Witchcraft\n\nShe was not in a coven. She was in a church. She volunteered in the nursery. She brought casseroles to grieving families. She also, without ever using the word, practiced witchcraft — because what she did consistently, in every relationship, was manipulate. She leveraged information. She withheld access. She used emotional pressure so subtly that people did what she wanted while believing it was their own idea.\n\nHer pastor preached on [1 Samuel 15:23](data-scripture="1 Samuel 15:23") one Sunday. *"Rebellion is as the sin of witchcraft, and stubbornness is as iniquity and idolatry."* She felt something cold move through her chest and thought it was the Holy Spirit convicting her of pride.\n\nIt was the Spirit of Witchcraft recognizing itself.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nWitchcraft, at its core, is the attempt to impose your will on the spiritual realm — to manipulate spiritual forces to produce desired outcomes apart from submission to God. Strip away the cauldrons and the ceremonial details, and that is the essential structure of every form of witchcraft: self-will asserting authority over divine will.\n\nThis is why [1 Samuel 15:23](data-scripture="1 Samuel 15:23") uses witchcraft to describe Saul's disobedience. Samuel is not addressing a witch. He is addressing a king who preferred his own strategic judgment to God's explicit command. The structure of that choice — self-will over God's will, personal strategy over covenant obedience — is the spiritual signature of witchcraft, regardless of whether any ritual occurred.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe Spirit of Witchcraft operates through a specific set of tools that are recognizable across every culture's expression of the practice:\n\n**Control.** The need to ensure that specific outcomes occur, specific people behave in specific ways, and specific spiritual forces comply with personal decree. In the church, this manifests as manipulation, emotional leverage, and information management.\n\n**Intimidation.** The projection of spiritual threat designed to neutralize opponents. Jezebel's message to Elijah in [1 Kings 19:2](data-scripture="1 Kings 19:2") produced such terror in the greatest prophet of his generation that he fled and asked God to let him die. This was not ordinary fear. It was a direct spiritual assault via the Spirit of Witchcraft operating through a human being.\n\n**Counterfeit supernatural.** The Spirit of Witchcraft produces genuine signs. Pharaoh's magicians replicated the first three plagues. Simon the Sorcerer in [Acts 8](data-scripture="Acts 8:9") commanded such genuine supernatural power that Samaria called him "the great power of God." The supernaturalism was real. The source was wrong.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Practicing any form of spell or intentional ritual magic** creates covenant with the demonic system that powers it. The intentions of the practitioner matter morally. They do not eliminate the spiritual consequences.\n\n**Operating in the Spirit of Witchcraft relationally** — using emotional manipulation, guilt, and control as governing tools in relationships — opens a door to the principality that powers those behaviors. The person who has never cast a spell but has spent thirty years controlling everyone around them through emotional leverage may be just as deeply bound.\n\n**Associating with practitioners** without renouncing their influence creates spiritual transfer. The spiritual authority a practitioner operates under does not stop at their personal boundary.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\n[1 Samuel 15:23](data-scripture="1 Samuel 15:23") is the most personally uncomfortable verse in this course — because it extends witchcraft's definition past ceremony into character. Ask yourself not "have I cast spells?" but rather: *Where do I consistently attempt to control outcomes that belong to God?*\n\nThe relationship you manage. The future you insist on securing. The person you manipulate into behaviors that serve your comfort. The plans you cannot release.\n\nThe antidote to witchcraft is not passivity. It is submitted authority — the [James 4:7](data-scripture="James 4:7") pattern: *"Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee."* Submit first. Authority flows from submission. Witchcraft is the attempt to access authority without submission, and the only power available outside God's authority is demonic.\n\n---\n\n*Witchcraft is the practice. Wicca is the religion — the formal theological structure that gives the practice a name, a community, and a calendar.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you cast a spell, performed a ritual, or used witchcraft tools — even once, even as a teenager, even just to see if it worked?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xloz0007nnyw29qf76vh	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Santería	READING	\N	33	\N	t	![Santería](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsE1mMmktdLWqJHyu8Q5MfmIRAjonSBKDvC0V2)\n\n## Santería\n\nHe grew up in Miami. His grandmother kept an altar in the corner of her bedroom — seven glasses of water, candles in specific colors, a statue of Saint Barbara with a machete, cowrie shells, a small clay pot. She said Saint Barbara protected the family. She prayed the rosary every morning and lit candles for the orishas every evening. She saw no contradiction.\n\nHe was forty before he understood that the spiritual heaviness he carried — the pattern of men in his family dying young, the particular fear that lived at the base of his spine — had a name. And that his grandmother's altar, however lovingly maintained, was part of what had sustained it.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nSantería emerged from the forced crossing of enslaved Yoruba people from West Africa to Cuba, Puerto Rico, and Brazil, where colonial Catholic structures demanded public Christianity. The Yoruba masked their orishas — divine intermediaries — behind Catholic saints. Shangó became Saint Barbara. Yemayá became Our Lady of Regla. Elegguá became the Holy Child of Atocha. The practice survived.\n\nToday Santería has millions of practitioners across the Americas. Similar systems — Candomblé, Vodou, Umbanda — operate on the same foundational structure: the veneration of orishas or loa through ritual offerings, animal sacrifice, and in some cases, deliberate spiritual possession known as *montarse* — being "ridden" by the deity.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe deep deception of Santería is its fusion of genuine Catholic devotion with demonic entity worship. A practitioner who recites the rosary and offers rum to Elegguá in the same afternoon does not experience spiritual dissonance — they experience spiritual fullness. The two systems feel complementary because the enemy is careful to preserve the form of Christianity while replacing its content.\n\nWhat enters an initiate during the *kariocha* ceremony — when an orisha is "seated" on the head through days of ritual sacrifice and ceremony — is not a benevolent Yoruba deity. It is a demon that has been accommodating the Yoruba's understanding of that entity for centuries. The possession is real. The entity that takes over the initiate's body and speaks in its voice and moves in its manner is real. It is demonic.\n\n[1 Corinthians 10:20](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 10:20"): *"The things which the Gentiles sacrifice, they sacrifice to devils, and not to God: and I would not that ye should have fellowship with devils."*\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Blood covenants create binding spiritual contracts.** Animal sacrifice in Santería is a blood covenant offering. Blood covenant is the most binding form of spiritual agreement in the biblical framework. The entities that receive these offerings gain significant legal ground through the transaction.\n\n**Generational access through family altars.** Families with a history of Santería practice carry generational demonic assignments. The orishas that were fed by a grandmother's altar for decades do not leave when she dies. They follow the bloodline, particularly targeting subsequent generations who have not formally broken the covenant.\n\n**Catholic syncretism disarms discernment.** The presence of Catholic imagery in Santería environments makes the practice feel spiritually safe to practitioners raised with Catholic backgrounds. They identify with the saints rather than examining what is being asked of the entities behind them.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf Santería, Candomblé, Vodou, or any similar syncretic practice is in your family background — grandparents' altars, initiations that family members underwent, objects and rituals maintained for "protection" — you are dealing with generational spiritual contracts that need specific revocation.\n\nThe breaking is this: name the orishas or loa that were served in your family line. Renounce the blood covenants and offerings made on your family's behalf. Declare that the blood of Jesus Christ — the only covenant blood with genuine spiritual authority — cancels every contract. Remove and destroy every altar object, every ritual item, every object associated with the practice.\n\n[Colossians 1:13](data-scripture="Colossians 1:13"): *"Who hath delivered us from the power of darkness, and hath translated us into the kingdom of his dear Son."* The authority that removes you from darkness is the same authority that revokes the contracts darkness holds.\n\n---\n\n*Santería marks the practitioner through ceremony. The next lesson examines how the body can be marked permanently — and what that marking means in the spirit realm.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you encountered Santería, Vodou, or Afro-Caribbean religious practices? Were you ever asked to participate, receive a reading, or accept ritual objects?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xlpj000nnnywyqedd3cq	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Adultery	READING	\N	42	\N	t	![Adultery](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsSfEzcPJ9p8Osi7f2L3jgeayVJxF6MbNCPdun)\n\n## Adultery\n\nHe told himself it was one mistake. That he had ended it. That his marriage was fine now — better, even, because the guilt had made him more attentive. His wife did not know. The affair partner had moved out of state. The marriage had recovered on its own.\n\nWhat he did not account for: the soul tie he had formed in eighteen months of a second relationship was still active. The demonic spirit that had entered through the covenant violation was still present. His wife experienced it as a vague spiritual coldness she could not name — a sense that something was missing from intimacy, a persistent feeling of wrongness that no amount of therapy resolved. Their pastor advised more date nights. What they needed was deliverance.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nAdultery is sexual union outside the marriage covenant. [Genesis 2:24](data-scripture="Genesis 2:24"): *"Therefore shall a man leave his father and his mother, and shall cleave unto his wife: and they shall be one flesh."* The marriage covenant creates a spiritual reality — a "one flesh" union that establishes a shared spiritual canopy over both spouses and, through them, their household.\n\nWhen that covenant is violated, the canopy tears. [Proverbs 6:32](data-scripture="Proverbs 6:32"): *"But whoso committeth adultery with a woman lacketh understanding: he that doeth it destroyeth his own soul."* This is not metaphor about consequences. It is a description of what happens spiritually when the covenant architecture of marriage is violated.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe deception of adultery is almost always a package: emotional needs being met, physical desire, a narrative about the marriage being already dead before the affair began. The enemy is not subtle about this — he simply provides a convincing set of justifications for a decision that was already forming.\n\nWhat the deception conceals: every sexual union outside of covenant creates a soul tie. [1 Corinthians 6:16](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 6:16"): *"Know ye not that he which is joined to an harlot is one body? for two, saith he, shall be one flesh."* The soul tie formed in adultery carries the spiritual history of the affair partner — their demonic attachments, their sin patterns, their generational curses — into the adulterer's life. The affair ends. The soul tie does not.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The covenant tear creates an access point.** The marriage covenant, when intact, functions as a protective spiritual structure. Its violation is not merely moral failure — it is a structural breach that demonic forces enter through. The Spirit of Lust that facilitated the initial affair now has covenantal access to the household through the tear.\n\n**The offended spouse carries wounds that become toeholds.** Bitterness, unforgiveness, and betrayal trauma in the innocent spouse create their own legal ground for demonic operation — not through their sin but through the unhealed wounds that the adulterer's sin produced. This is one reason why undisclosed adultery in a marriage poisons the spiritual atmosphere for everyone in the household, including children, even when no one knows why.\n\n**The searing of conscience is progressive.** [1 Timothy 4:2](data-scripture="1 Timothy 4:2"): *"speaking lies in hypocrisy; having their conscience seared with a hot iron."* Sustained unrepented adultery progressively deadens moral sensitivity. The first affair produces crushing guilt. The fifth produces a sophisticated theology of why it cannot be helped.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf you have committed adultery — whether disclosed or not, whether the marriage survived or not — the soul ties formed in that relationship are still active unless they have been specifically addressed.\n\nHere is the specific action: name each person with whom an adulterous relationship occurred. For each one, pray: *In the name of Jesus Christ, I break the soul tie between myself and [name]. I take back every part of my soul given in that union. I release every part of their soul that bonded to mine. I close every door that relationship opened.*\n\nThen bring it to your spouse if you have not. This is not about destroying the marriage — it is about doing what undisclosed adultery has already done to the spiritual canopy, but this time with the materials of genuine repentance and covenant restoration.\n\nRestoration is possible. [1 Corinthians 6:11](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 6:11"): *"Such were some of you: but ye are washed."* The past tense matters. Were. Not are.\n\n---\n\n*Adultery breaks the marriage covenant through physical union with another person. The next lesson examines the same breach through a screen — and how the spiritual consequences follow the same pattern.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Has adultery — committed by you or against you — ever been addressed in prayer as a spiritual breach, not just a relational one? If not: what has that silence cost you?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xtzr0001cdn83h9uuc2c	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Supplement 11: Legal Ground — Why the Enemy Has a Right to Be There	SUPPLEMENT	\N	52	\N	t	![Supplement 11: Legal Ground — Why the Enemy Has a Right to Be There](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsSd5aHJ9p8Osi7f2L3jgeayVJxF6MbNCPdunU)\n\n## Supplement 11: Legal Ground\n\nThis is the theological foundation of everything Part VII has covered. Every attack examined in this section — every door that opened — functions through a principle that deliverance ministers across traditions and denominations have independently documented: the principle of **legal ground**.\n\n---\n\n## The Courtroom Model\n\n[Romans 8:1](data-scripture="Romans 8:1"): *"There is therefore now no condemnation to them which are in Christ Jesus."* Condemnation is a legal term. The entire framework of salvation in Paul's theology is forensic — conducted in the courtroom of divine justice.\n\nThe adversary is named in Scripture as the accuser: [Revelation 12:10](data-scripture="Revelation 12:10") — *"the accuser of our brethren is cast down, which accused them before our God day and night."* He does not simply attack at will. He accuses. Accusation is a legal act.\n\nWhen a believer engages in practices that Scripture prohibits — witchcraft, divination, occult invocation, blood rituals, idolatry, covenant with false deities — the enemy does not merely take advantage of spiritual vulnerability. He files a legal claim. He presents, before the throne of divine justice, a documented record of covenant violation. He claims legal standing to operate in the space the sin created.\n\nThis is why deliverance can seem difficult. The enemy does not leave because he has been asked to — he stays because he has been paid to, by legal currency (sin) that he is legitimately holding. The route to freedom is not louder prayer or more forceful commands. It is the revocation of his legal claim through repentance, renunciation, and the application of the blood of Jesus Christ.\n\n## What Creates Legal Ground\n\nThe lessons in Part VII covered 44 specific attacks. Across all of them, legal ground is created through the same mechanisms:\n\n**1. Covenant entry.** Any agreement — formal or informal, conscious or unconscious — with a spiritual system, entity, or deity outside Jesus Christ creates a covenant. Joining a lodge. Receiving initiation. Dedicating objects at an altar. Speaking invocations. Blood oaths. Repeat ritual behavior that establishes a pattern of allegiance.\n\n**2. Inherited assignment.** [Exodus 20:5](data-scripture="Exodus 20:5"): *"I the LORD thy God am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children unto the third and fourth generation."* Legal ground established by ancestors is inherited by descendants. The grandfather's Freemasonry oath creates a standing legal claim against the grandchildren until it is specifically broken.\n\n**3. Object-based anchoring.** Dedicated objects — idols, fetishes, occult tools, ritually prepared items — function as legal anchors. The demonic entity associated with an object does not leave when the object is ignored. It leaves when the object is destroyed and its claim is specifically revoked.\n\n**4. Soul tie formation.** Sexual union creates covenant: [1 Corinthians 6:16](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 6:16"). Soul ties to ungodly partners create legal channels through which the enemy accesses both parties.\n\n**5. Word covenants.** Oaths, promises, and vows made to demonic systems — including the promises made in yoga mantra, Masonic degree oaths, Wiccan covenant ritual, and divination consultation — are binding until specifically revoked.\n\n## The Mechanism of Freedom\n\n[1 John 1:9](data-scripture="1 John 1:9"): *"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness."* Faithful and just — both legal terms. God's forgiveness is not merely gracious. It is just: the blood of Jesus Christ paid the legal debt that sin created. When that payment is applied through genuine repentance and confession, the enemy's legal claim is extinguished.\n\nThe mechanism is:\n1. **Identify** the specific legal ground — name the specific practice, covenant, or object.\n2. **Repent** specifically — not "forgive me for my sins" but "I repent for [specific practice], which I engaged in on [specific occasions], in violation of [specific Scripture]."\n3. **Renounce** the covenant, connection, or claim — specifically severing the legal tie.\n4. **Apply the blood** — pleading the blood of Jesus Christ over the specific area where legal ground was established.\n5. **Command** the departure of every entity that held the revoked legal claim.\n6. **Fill** the cleansed space — with Scripture, worship, the presence of the Holy Spirit, and righteous covenant relationships.\n\n## The Blood Is the Answer\n\nEvery legal ground examined in Part VII was a blood transaction. The life of the flesh is in the blood. Covenants are ratified in blood. Soul ties form through the blood of sexual union. Self-harm sheds blood to the Spirit of Death.\n\nAgainst every blood transaction stands one greater: [Hebrews 9:12](data-scripture="Hebrews 9:12") — *"Neither by the blood of goats and calves, but by his own blood he entered in once into the holy place, having obtained eternal redemption for us."*\n\nThe blood of Jesus Christ is not a spiritual metaphor. It is a legal payment of infinite worth, paid once, effective for every debt, applied in full to every believer who claims it through faith. No legal ground the enemy holds against you can survive direct confrontation with the blood of Christ applied in specific, Spirit-directed repentance.\n\n---\n\n*The legal framework is established. The next supplement provides the complete prayer guide for closing every door covered in this course — specifically, systematically, and with authority.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xu060003cdn8egu7ywdg	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Supplement 12: The Complete Freedom Prayer Guide	SUPPLEMENT	\N	53	\N	t	![Supplement 12: The Complete Freedom Prayer Guide](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsCsEuZoe78vbPqVLiKnDy6up93CGaNzkh5HsQ)\n\n## Supplement 12: The Complete Freedom Prayer Guide\n\n**How to use this supplement:** This is not a lesson to read and move past. Print it or open it on a second device. Work through it section by section, aloud, with a pen in hand. Check off each item as you address it. The Holy Spirit will surface what needs to be addressed — let Him set the pace.\n\n**Before you begin:** Find a private space where you can pray at full voice. Ask the Holy Spirit to bring to your conscious memory everything that needs to be covered. Do not rush.\n\n---\n\n---\n\n## Preparation Prayer\n\n*Lord Jesus, I come to You as my deliverer, my advocate, and my High Priest. I ask You to open my eyes to every area of my life where the enemy has established legal ground. I ask the Holy Spirit to bring to my memory every door I have opened, every covenant I have made, every object in my possession, and every generational assignment that affects my life. I submit to Your authority, Your Word, and Your Spirit. I ask that the blood of Jesus Christ cover this time of prayer. I ask for heavenly witnesses and the protection of the hosts of heaven as I proceed. In Jesus' name. Amen.*\n\n---\n\n## Section 1: Occult and Divination Practices\n\nFor any practice from the following list that you have engaged in, pray the prayer below, inserting the specific practice in the blank.\n\n**Work through each that applies:**\n- [ ] Tarot cards\n- [ ] Ouija board\n- [ ] Horoscopes/astrology\n- [ ] Psychics or mediums\n- [ ] Palmistry\n- [ ] Numerology\n- [ ] Runes\n- [ ] Pendulum divination\n- [ ] I Ching\n- [ ] Automatic writing\n- [ ] Spirit guides\n- [ ] Séances\n- [ ] Channeling\n- [ ] Crystal ball gazing\n- [ ] Any form of divination or fortune-telling\n\n**Pray aloud:**\n*Father, I confess and repent for consulting [specific practice]. I acknowledge that this was divination — seeking knowledge and guidance from a source other than You — in direct violation of Your Word. I renounce every covenant, agreement, and relationship I formed with any spirit entity through this practice. I revoke every legal claim the enemy holds against me from this involvement. I plead the blood of Jesus Christ over my mind, my will, and every spiritual door this practice opened. I command every familiar spirit and every spirit of divination that gained access through this practice to leave me now, in Jesus' name. Amen.*\n\n---\n\n## Section 2: Witchcraft and Ritual Practice\n\nFor any practice from the following list, pray the prayer below:\n\n**Work through each that applies:**\n- [ ] Wicca\n- [ ] Spell casting\n- [ ] Santería\n- [ ] Voodoo\n- [ ] Rootwork/hoodoo\n- [ ] Shamanism\n- [ ] Blood rituals\n- [ ] Ritual magic\n- [ ] Ceremonial magic\n- [ ] Freemasonry (or other secret societies with oaths)\n\n**Pray aloud (general):**\n*Father, I confess and repent for practicing [specific practice]. I acknowledge this as witchcraft — the attempt to manipulate spiritual forces outside Your authority — in direct violation of Your Word in Deuteronomy 18 and Galatians 5. I renounce [practice] and every covenant, oath, initiation, or degree associated with it. I specifically renounce every deity, entity, or spiritual authority I invoked or submitted to through this practice. I break every blood oath made in the context of [practice]. I plead the blood of Jesus Christ over every breach this created. I command every spirit associated with [practice] to leave me and my household now, in Jesus' name. Amen.*\n\n**Pray aloud (specific):**\n*I specifically break the curse of [any specific oaths recalled] in Jesus' name. I renounce the name GAOTU (or any false deity name used) and declare that Jesus Christ alone is Lord. I break every Masonic curse over myself and my bloodline to the fourth generation. Every spirit associated with Freemasonry must leave now, in Jesus' name.*\n\n---\n\n## Section 3: False Religions and New Age Practice\n\n**Work through each that applies:**\n- [ ] Yoga (with spiritual intention)\n- [ ] Reiki\n- [ ] TM/mindfulness meditation\n- [ ] Feng shui\n- [ ] Crystals and crystal healing\n- [ ] Astrology\n- [ ] Chakras/kundalini practice\n- [ ] Labyrinth walking\n- [ ] Enneagram (as spiritual practice)\n- [ ] Burning Man/festival pagan spirituality\n- [ ] New Age spirituality\n- [ ] Buddhism/Hinduism (participated in, not merely studied)\n- [ ] Mormonism/Jehovah's Witnesses/false gospels (as systems you trusted for salvation)\n\n**Pray aloud:**\n*Father, I confess and repent for participation in [specific practice/system]. I renounce [specific deity names or spiritual forces invoked — e.g., Shiva, Shakti, spirit guides, chi, prana, the divine feminine/masculine]. I break every covenant and agreement I made with the spiritual system behind [practice]. I plead the blood of Jesus Christ over my mind, my body, and my spirit, and over every area that [practice] was intended to affect. I command every spirit associated with [practice] to leave me now, in Jesus' name. Amen.*\n\n---\n\n## Section 4: Objects in the Home\n\nWork through every room in your home, asking: *Was this object made for, dedicated to, or used in a spiritual system outside Jesus Christ?*\n\nObjects to specifically address: Buddha statues · Dreamcatchers · African/Pacific/Pre-Columbian masks or idols · Ganesh or Hindu deity statues · Crystals positioned for energetic purposes · Occult books, tools, or ritual objects · Objects received as gifts from occult practitioners · Any object you received and felt spiritually uneasy about\n\n**Prayer over specific objects before destroying them:**\n*I take authority over this object in Jesus' name. I renounce its spiritual purpose and every entity associated with it. I revoke every legal claim this object represents. This object is coming down from its place in my home. I plead the blood of Jesus Christ over every space it occupied.*\n\nThen destroy the object — do not donate it or give it away.\n\n**Prayer over the space after removal:**\n*Lord, I consecrate this space to You. I plead the blood of Jesus Christ over every area where [object] was located. I command every entity that was attached to or anchored by [object] to leave this space now, in Jesus' name. Holy Spirit, fill this space with Your presence and Your peace. Amen.*\n\n---\n\n## Section 5: Generational Assignments\n\n*Father, I acknowledge the sins of my ancestors — specifically [any known occult, Masonic, idolatrous, or covenant violations you are aware of in your family history]. I repent on behalf of my family line for these violations. I take full authority, as a believer in Jesus Christ, to break every generational curse and every generational assignment that flows from these violations. In the name of Jesus, I break the power of every spirit that has attached to my bloodline through my ancestors' choices. I declare that the curse of [specific patterns — addiction, mental illness, poverty, sexual sin, occult involvement — that repeat in your family] is broken at its root in Jesus' name. I receive the blessing of [Galatians 3:13](data-scripture="Galatians 3:13"): "Christ hath redeemed us from the curse of the law, being made a curse for us." I am redeemed. The curse is broken. The assignment is revoked. Amen.*\n\n---\n\n## Section 6: Soul Ties\n\n*Father, I confess and repent for sexual union outside the covenant of marriage, specifically with [name each person if possible — if too many, pray collectively for each season]. I acknowledge that these unions created ungodly soul ties. I now break every ungodly soul tie with [name/group] in Jesus' name. I call back every part of my soul that was given in those unions, and I release every part of their soul that I retained. I cut every spiritual cord connecting me to [name/group] in Jesus' name. I plead the blood of Jesus Christ over my sexuality, my emotional life, and my spirit. I receive healing and wholeness in the areas where these soul ties created damage. Amen.*\n\n---\n\n## Section 7: Self-Harm and Blood Covenants\n\n*Father, I confess and repent for every act of self-harm, specifically for [describe the practice — cutting, burning, etc.] I acknowledge that this shed blood created a spiritual transaction with the Spirit of Death. I now break that blood covenant in Jesus' name. I revoke every legal claim the Spirit of Death holds against me from this practice. I plead the blood of Jesus Christ — shed once for all — over my body, declaring that His blood alone covers me. I command the Spirit of Death, every spirit of self-destruction, and every spirit of accusation that drove this behavior to leave me now, in Jesus' name. I receive the truth of 1 Corinthians 6:19 — my body is the temple of the Holy Spirit. I dedicate my body to Him. Amen.*\n\n---\n\n## Closing Declaration\n\n*I stand before You, Father, as Your child, bought by the blood of Jesus Christ. Every door covered in this prayer is now closed. Every legal ground the enemy held through these practices is now revoked. Every covenant made outside of You is now broken. Every entity that operated through legal claim is now commanded to leave — I have no covenant with you, I have no agreement with you, you have no place in me.\n\nI am covered by the blood of Jesus Christ. I am sealed by the Holy Spirit. I am declared righteous — not by my behavior but by the righteousness of Jesus Christ applied to my account.\n\nHoly Spirit, come now and fill every space that was just emptied. Establish Your presence where the enemy operated. Bring healing where there was damage. Bring clarity where there was deception. Bring peace where there was oppression.\n\nI receive my freedom. I walk in it. In the name of Jesus Christ, Amen.*\n\n---\n\n*The freedom you just prayed through is real. The quiz that follows is the final element of Part VII — use it not as a test but as a map: confirming what you have understood and identifying any areas that need a second pass.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xn6i0001bep915ffe6ro	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Pornography	READING	\N	43	\N	t	![Pornography](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsMsfqlauQ05GAMxtDFIK1y3rg6HLCbaVjmO7f)\n\n## Pornography\n\nHe had been a Christian for twenty years. He led a men's accountability group. He had accountability software on every device. He had fasted more times than he could count. He had confessed to his pastor twice.\n\nThe battle would settle for two or three weeks. Then it came back, always slightly worse than before, always with a specific type of content he had not sought before and now could not stop seeking. He had come to believe, privately, that he was simply broken in a way God had not fixed. That this was his cross to bear.\n\nHe did not know that the accountability software was addressing the neurological dimension of an addiction that also had a demonic dimension — and that without addressing both, one could not sustain the other.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nPornography is the explicit visual depiction of sexual behavior for the purpose of arousal. The contemporary pornography industry processes billions of visits monthly. Approximately 4% of all websites globally contain pornographic material. The advent of free streaming platforms in the early 2000s made high-definition content available to anyone with a smartphone, including children.\n\nResearch consistently documents that pornography use among self-identified Christians tracks closely with the general population. Many pastors and ministry leaders struggle with it while continuing in ministry — unable to find freedom through willpower, accountability software, or pastoral counsel alone.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\n[Galatians 5:20](data-scripture="Galatians 5:20") includes *pharmakeia* — sorcery — among the works of the flesh. The Greek word refers to the use of substances or practices to alter consciousness and create entrancement. Pornography, through its capacity to produce a trance-like state of sexual arousal that overrides the will and floods the reward system, functions pharmacologically and spiritually as a form of sorcery. It is not merely an addiction with a demonic component. It is a demonic stronghold with a neurological component.\n\nThis is why it uniquely resists the interventions that work with other addictive behaviors. Millions overcome alcoholism, drug addiction, and gambling through willpower, therapy, and community. Pornography resists these interventions in a way that, for many people, cannot be explained purely neurologically. The Spirit of Lust does not merely influence users — it drives them. What begins as curiosity becomes compulsion as the spirit intensifies desire and escalates toward increasingly specific and degraded content.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Soul ties through screens.** [1 Corinthians 6:16](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 6:16") does not require physical contact. Extended sexual engagement with a person — even through a screen — creates a spiritual bond carrying their spiritual history: their trauma, their demonic attachments, their generational darkness. Pornography consumers enter spiritual proximity with everyone they view.\n\n**Generational transmission.** Children of fathers with pornography addiction show elevated rates of sexual behavioral problems even without direct exposure. The Spirit of Lust follows bloodlines.\n\n**The escalation pattern is spiritually driven.** The escalation toward more extreme material is not explained by tolerance alone. It is spiritually driven — the enemy requiring deeper and more specific defilement to maintain the legal ground the escalation creates.\n\n**The marriage covenant is defiled.** The pornography user brings demonic bondage into the marriage bed. Spouses frequently report that sexual intimacy "feels contaminated" — a spiritual observation, not merely a psychological one.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nWillpower, accountability software, and pastoral counsel without addressing the spiritual dimensions will produce temporary relief and permanent frustration. Real freedom requires:\n\nSpecific repentance — not "I repent of pornography" but naming the specific escalated forms the Holy Spirit surfaces. Each category named specifically before God closes a specific door.\n\nBreaking soul ties — naming each performer category viewed and breaking the spiritual bond in Jesus' name. This is not symbolic. [1 Corinthians 6:16](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 6:16") is literal.\n\nTargeted deliverance prayer for the Spirit of Lust, the Spirit of Perversion, and *porneia* — seeking a minister experienced in sexual bondage, not only a pastor experienced in pastoral care.\n\nStrategic fasting — [Matthew 17:21](data-scripture="Matthew 17:21"): *"Howbeit this kind goeth not out but by prayer and fasting."* Jesus specified this class of demonic stronghold requires fasting. This is not legalism. It is clinical precision.\n\n---\n\n*Pornography is desire directed outward. Self-harm turns the violence inward. The next lesson examines the specific spiritual assignment that has been waiting for that turn.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *How many years, if any, has pornography had consistent access to your mind? Name the soul ties that have never been specifically broken in prayer.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgbn001j10b8pxuacsew	cmq76cgbj001f10b883ni3dl8	Lesson 21 — Daily Warfare and the Mind of Christ	READING	900	1	\N	t	![Lesson 21 — Daily Warfare and the Mind of Christ](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsmYpohXTjs8MAGw2JgFBiIXKDThNCyqSVfZL3)\n\n## Daily Warfare and the Mind of Christ\n\nWhile the final defeat of Satan is certain, the daily battle continues until Christ returns. The believer who understands demonology is not fearful but vigilant — not passive but armed. This final lesson addresses how to live in daily victory over the powers of darkness.\n\n### Guarding the Gates\n\nDemons gain access through specific "gates": the eye gate (what you watch), the ear gate (what you listen to), the mouth gate (what you speak), the mind gate (what you think), and the body gate (what you do). Every gate must be guarded.\n\n> Philippians 4:8 — "Whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report; if there be any virtue, and if there be any praise, think on these things."\n\nWhat you allow into your mind eventually shapes your life. Pornography, violent entertainment, occult music, and gossip are not harmless indulgences; they are invitations to demons.\n\n### The Discipline of Prayer\n\nPrayer is the atmosphere in which demons cannot operate. When a believer is praying, the enemy is paralyzed. Paul commands us to "pray without ceasing" (1 Thessalonians 5:17) — to maintain a continuous connection with God that leaves no room for the enemy's suggestions.\n\nSpecific prayers for daily warfare include:\n- **The morning offering** — Dedicating the day to God before the enemy can establish a foothold\n- **The blood of Jesus** — Pleading the blood over yourself, your family, and your home\n- **The armor of God** — Consciously putting on each piece before facing the day\n- **Binding and loosing** — Binding the enemy's plans and loosing God's purposes\n\n### Walking in the Spirit\n\nThe ultimate protection against demonic attack is to be filled with the Holy Spirit:\n\n> Galatians 5:16 — "Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh."\n\nWhen the Spirit is in control, there is no vacancy for a demon. The believer who walks in love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control is invulnerable to the enemy's attacks. These are not moral achievements; they are the fruit of the Spirit's presence.\n\n### The Final Word\n\nYou are not a victim. You are a victor. The same Spirit who raised Jesus from the dead dwells in you. The Name above every name is yours to use. The blood of the Lamb has cancelled every claim. And the Word of God is your sword.\n\n> Romans 8:37 — "Nay, in all these things we are more than conquerors through him that loved us."\n\nWalk in this truth. Live in this authority. And know that no demon in hell can separate you from the love of God which is in Christ Jesus our Lord.	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk460000jewhj1an9e2hc	cmnknk45y000gewhjn5pl0kw9	Supplement 5 — For Lessons 9 & 10	SUPPLEMENT	1590	2	\N	t	Adam and Eve lived in a perfect environment with one restriction — and failed the test. Lesson Ten showed that God's plan for human needs is comprehensive and provided in His providence. This supplement brings those two truths together: the gap between God's perfect provision and your experience of it is never on His side. So what's on yours?\n\nWe've seen that man failed, lost power over Satan and demons, and became a fallen, helpless creature set upon by the most subtle and unprincipled evil spirits in existence. Man lost control of the Earth and became subject to Satan.\n\nWe've also seen that this Fall was brought about by doubting God's Word, by adding to it, by contradicting it, by misinterpreting it, by temptation to transgress it, and by actual transgression of it. These were the steps of man's Fall, and he must take steps that are just the opposite of these in order to be redeemed from the fall.\n\nThe steps one must follow to be redeemed are:\n\n![Supplement 5 — For Lessons 9 & 10](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsnE4S2WIgR6p4tHCQPYM8N0kE5l7TdjZq9iba)\n\n### 1. Doubt Concerning God's Word\n\nIf you want healing, health, success, happiness, and prosperity from God through the gospel, you must first stop doubting the Word of God in its entirety. If man had never permitted himself to doubt in the first place—if he had warded off all suggestions of Satan that are contrary to God's Word—there wouldn't be the struggle that exists today to believe God without doubting.\n\nThe first and last lesson you must learn if you want anything from God is to doubt not. It is reported that Franklin D. Roosevelt said, "It never occurs to me to doubt God." Every person should maintain this attitude toward God at all times.\n\nGod has made it very plain that the absolute condition of answered prayer is: "Let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not: and it shall be given him. But let him ask in faith, nothing wavering. For he that wavereth is like a wave of the sea driven with the wind and tossed. For let not that man think that he shall receive anything of the Lord. A double-minded man is unstable in all his ways" (Jas. 1:5-8).\n\nThe Moffat translation reads: "Let him ask God who gives to all men without question or reproach, and the gift will be his. Only, let him ask in faith, with never a doubt; for the doubtful man is like the surge of the sea whirled and swayed by the wind; that man need not imagine he will get anything from God, double-minded creature that he is, wavering at every turn."\n\nThe Weymouth translation reads: "Let him ask God for it, who gives with open hand to all men, and without upbraiding; and it will be given him. But let him ask in faith and have no doubts; for he who has doubts is like the surge of the sea, driven by the wind and tossed into spray. A person of that sort must not expect to receive anything from the Lord—such a one is a man of two minds, undecided in every step he takes."\n\nWhat could be clearer than this? If this is God's condition of answered prayer, it will pay for everyone to make up his mind before he prays that he is going to cleave to what he decides to ask of God and fight it through until he gets an answer.\n\nIf children of God could learn this one secret, they would stop asking God for blessings until they thoroughly made up their minds that they want them badly enough to see their desires through to a complete answer. Then, following this procedure, their prayers will be answered.\n\nBut many times people change their minds when the answer doesn't come all at once. They decide that it isn't the will of God, or that it wouldn't have been best for them to have received an answer. These things should always be settled before prayer is made for something. The fact that an answer isn't forthcoming the same moment we ask is no proof that it isn't the will of God or that it might not have been best for us.\n\nThis habit of changing your mind mid-prayer is the most harmful procedure for a child of God to follow, but sad to say, it's one of the most common. A few failures like this will soon form a habit that causes failure in almost every prayer you pray.\n\nFailures are so common in the lives of people concerning answered prayer that it's safe to say not one percent of all prayers are answered. But under the circumstances, even this is a high percentage. Definite requests are made to God by the millions, but few are answered.\n\nThis condition doesn't seem to bother the average praying man or woman. In fact, many believe the false idea that it's normal not to get an answer to prayer, except occasionally.\n\nSuch people should wake up and realize that if they can get an answer once in a while, they can get an answer every time they pray. If desperation and absolute necessity can force them to have faith enough for God to answer one time, they can force themselves to become earnest and have enough faith for everything they pray for at all times.\n\nWhy should there ever be a doubt in any mind if the simple, definite promises of God are found to cover the need? If God's Word does not promise what is asked, it's not necessary to have it, for Peter said: "According as his divine power hath given us all things that pertain to life and godliness . . . Whereby are given unto us exceeding great and precious promises: that by these ye might be partakers of the divine nature, having escaped the corruption that is in the world through lust" (2 Pet. 1:3-4).\n\nIf absolute, unwavering faith is what God demands before He obligates Himself to answer, let everyone who asks see to it that he asks in faith, nothing wavering, and since he has the definite Word of God promising him what he asks, he will receive.\n\nSince it was Satan (through the serpent) that raised the first doubt in man and made it second nature to doubt God, let everyone recognize that all doubts are of the devil and are contrary to the Word of God. Let him put a stop to all doubting by wholeheartedly resisting the devil, and the devil will flee from him (Jas. 4:7). All doubting is definite opposition to God and His Word, and when you're in such opposition to the One you expect an answer from, you cannot hope to receive it.\n\nIn order to not doubt God's Word, you must know it beyond question. This is the secret of knowing the truth, and it will make you free, as promised by Jesus (Jn. 8:31-32).\n\nThe way to know the Word of God is to take it for what it says and reject the interpretations of demons and men who try to change even one jot or tittle of it. All such changes are satanic in origin and propagation and must be rejected before doubt can be completely dispelled.\n\nAll doubts must be rooted out before prayer can be answered, and prayer must be answered before the benefits of the promises can be fully realized. The way to answered prayer then becomes clear, and it's the duty of each individual to see to it that he masters all doubt and demons and cooperates with God's Word with all his heart.\n\n### 2. Addition to and Misquoting God's Word\n\nUntil all doubt is cleansed from your life, there will be some addition to and misquoting of God's Word, because this is part of doubting God. As long as doubt is tolerated and indulged in, it will be easy to reason about the Word of God and excuse yourself for doubt and unbelief.\n\nThe habit of praying people is to question, wonder, reason, argue, and lay blame upon God when prayer isn't immediately answered. They seldom stop to analyze the truth, realizing that they are to blame for yielding to satanic powers which cause a person to walk in doubt and unbelief.\n\nIf immediate answers to all prayers are your goal, you must never add one thing to God's Word or take one thing from it. You must learn to take every statement of God as it is written and practice it to the letter.\n\nIf there is any occasion to argue or contend about any part of it, you must take the side of God and maintain faith in it just as it is, making no apology for faith in it. You must never give in to any excuse for unbelief and never doubt one thing that is plainly written.\n\nYour first and last contention should be that it is clear, and that it means what it says and says what it means. You must never excuse yourself or anyone from absolute conformity to it just as it is written, whether it harmonizes with your own theories or those of your church.\n\nDishonesty and handling the Word of God deceitfully will destroy more faith in one day than can be built up in a lifetime. You must never be guilty of trying to evade truth or what is plainly evident in the Scriptures themselves.\n\nA frank admission of what is plainly written and a confession of faith in it will do more to build up faith than all questioning and doubting programs of the devil and natural reason.\n\n### 3. Contradiction of God's Word\n\nNot only must you never doubt, add to, or take from God's Word, but if you want God to honor you enough to answer prayer, you must never try to make God a liar by contradicting the Word of God.\n\nThere is nothing to be gained by maintaining faith in man's interpretations of the Bible at the expense of maintaining faith in God and what He plainly says. If God makes a statement, it should be final, and no argument is necessary—for such arguing is merely trying to evade plain truth.\n\nIt's not possible to misunderstand God or His Word if you will put forth the least effort to accept what He says just as He said it. You can afford to contradict theories of men concerning God's Word, but you cannot afford to contradict what is plainly written.\n\nWhen God makes a statement, it should be accepted at face value. There should never be one word uttered that will in any way throw a reflection upon God or His Word, or make Him seem false in any detail of His statements.\n\nIf God promises certain things to men upon certain conditions, then be strong in faith, knowing that God is right and anything to the contrary is wrong. It's only by faithfully taking God at His Word in all that He says that faith will grow and become unwavering.\n\nWhen you achieve unwavering faith in what God says, you will receive unwavering answers to your prayers. But when a person is double-minded and changes his mind every few minutes about what he has asked of God, how can God decide whether the man really wants it or not? Under the circumstances, God does not give it to him.\n\nWhen you doubt, you contradict God's Word that promises you what you have prayed for, and such contradiction cuts you off from the answer.\n\nOur motto should be: **"The Bible States It; I Believe It; That Settles It."**\n\n### 4. Misinterpretation of God's Word\n\nThe next step in retracing our steps from the fall is to stop misinterpreting God's Word. It's impossible to misinterpret what is written if you will take at face value what is plainly written.\n\nEvery person that has intelligence enough to read what God says has intelligence enough to believe what He says, and that's all that is necessary. The very fact that a person can see what it says well enough to accept it or make a change to it as he pleases proves that he can understand what it plainly says.\n\nIf what he reads is not clear, he couldn't understand it well enough to change it. Thus, if all can understand what is plainly written well enough to change it as they please, it's clear that all can, if they choose, believe it and leave it as it is.\n\nA solid, unshakable faith will be created if God's Word will be taken just as it is. Faith will never have to change because the Word itself will never change.\n\n### 5. Temptation to Transgress God's Word\n\nTemptation to transgress the Word of God must be rejected with a firm and definite refusal. You must resist the temptation to transgress God's Word concerning open sin, or you become a sinner and incur the death penalty.\n\nYou must likewise refuse temptation to doubt the promises of God if you want answers to prayer. You cannot transgress God's Word concerning sin and still be exempt from the death penalty. Neither can you transgress the law of faith and still get from God those things for which you have prayed.\n\nThe law of faith says:\n- "All things, whatsoever ye shall ask in prayer, believing, ye shall receive" (Mt. 21:21-22)\n- "All things are possible to him that believeth" (Mk. 9:23)\n- "What things soever ye desire when ye pray, believe that ye receive them, and ye shall have them" (Mk. 11:22-24)\n- "Ask what ye will, and it shall be done unto you" (Jn. 15:7)\n- "let him ask in faith, nothing wavering" (Jas. 1:5-8)\n\nThere is no possible way to transgress the law of faith and get an answer. Jesus said, "heaven and earth shall pass away [be changed] but my word shall not pass away [be changed]."\n\nThink of it like this: you might as well shoot peas at a battleship hoping to sink it as to expect an answer when the law of faith is willfully transgressed.\n\nWhen you are tempted to transgress, such temptation is a warning signal that you are being attacked by demon spirits who want you to disobey God. No sin has yet been committed until actual transgression, so a person under such temptation must immediately become aggressive against this temptation and refuse all further parley. It must be no, now and forever! When temptation is resisted, faith grows, and final victory is but a matter of time.\n\nYou may be tempted in every conceivable way to break the law of faith or to transgress some part of God's Word. Don't do it. It will not pay.\n\nGod is faithful, and He will stand by you and by His promises, so never doubt that He will do what He says. James said: "Resist the devil, and he will flee from you. Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded" (Jas. 4:7-8).\n\nPaul advised believers: "Hold fast the profession of our faith without wavering, for he is faithful that promised . . . Cast not away therefore your confidence, which hath great recompense of reward. For ye have need of patience, that, after ye have done the will of God, ye might receive the promise . . . Now the just shall live by faith: but if any man draw back, my soul shall have no pleasure in him" (Heb. 10:23, 35-39).\n\nThis last passage teaches that it's God's pleasure to see His children exercise faith in spite of the devil, demons, and all opposition. He glories in their spunk when they resist the devil, and He will back them up in their fight.\n\n"Without faith it is impossible to please him" (Heb. 11:6). It is written of Enoch that he pleased God by believing that God would translate him (Heb. 11:5).\n\nWho ever heard of a man being translated in Enoch's day? Yet he believed the Word of God that he was going to be translated, and such faith pleased God. God gets great pleasure out of men daring to believe that anything is possible.\n\nEnoch did not argue, doubt, question, and call God a liar when God told him that He was going to translate him. He believed that it would be as God said, and it did happen. This is faith.\n\nThe disciples were rebuked on several occasions when they doubted. When they worried about food and clothing, Jesus said: "If God so clothe the grass of the field, which to day is, and to morrow is cast into the oven, shall he not much more clothe you, O ye of little faith?" (Mt. 6:25-34).\n\nWhen Peter dared to walk on water and did so until he doubted, Jesus said: "O ye of little faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?" (Mt. 14:28-33).\n\nWhen the disciples questioned Him about having bread to eat, Jesus said: "O ye of little faith, why reason ye among yourselves, because ye have brought no bread?" (Mt. 16:5-10).\n\nAnd so the story continues. All wavering, questioning, worrying, fretting, complaining, discouragement, fear, or reasoning about how to get the benefits of life or the fulfillment of God's promises is pure unbelief. Such a program never did produce desired results, so why not cleanse our lives of all unbelief and dare believe God?\n\nIf such doubting is displeasing to God, and if this is the reason why prayers aren't heard, then why continue to deliberately and willfully yield to such temptations, thereby committing sin against God and robbing ourselves of our rights in the gospel?\n\nWe know we won't get anything by this method, so what have we got to lose in trying another way? It certainly couldn't produce more failures than the method we are currently using.\n\nThere were only two times when Christ marveled at men. The first time He marveled because a man had such great faith. The centurion said: "Speak the word only, and my servant shall be healed . . . When Jesus heard it, he marveled, and said unto them that followed, Verily, I say unto you, I have not found so great faith, no, not in Israel . . . And Jesus said unto the centurion, Go thy way; and as thou hast believed, so be it done unto thee. And his servant was healed in the selfsame hour" (Mt. 8:5-13).\n\nThe second time Jesus marveled was because of the unbelief of His own hometown people (Mk. 6:1-6). God marvels at both things—great faith and unbelief.\n\nEvidently, the greatest mystery to Him is that men do not believe Him after having more than His Word, as the centurion did. We have His promises by the hundreds, and many hundreds of healings, answers to prayer, miracles, and supernatural manifestations in Scripture proving to man that God will do what He has promised, and yet it seems so hard for the average person to believe.\n\nIt's no wonder that God refuses to answer when men refuse to ask in faith, nothing wavering. If man does not want the benefits of the promises, then let him go without them. This is happening in the lives of multitudes, but it can be different with every person if he chooses to come out of this one failure in life and believe God.\n\n### 6. Transgression of God's Word\n\nFor every sin committed, there is a penalty incurred. This is true of man's laws and it's also true of God's laws. Laws without penalties would be no laws at all. They would merely be advice, and not even good advice at that, for they would not offer any incentive for man to accept them.\n\nThink of it like this: traffic laws without consequences would turn every intersection into chaos—the rules only have meaning because breaking them matters.\n\nWhen a person yields to temptation to break the law of faith or any other law of God, he incurs the penalty of the broken law. There are some sins that demand the death penalty, such as those in Gal. 5:19-21; Rom. 1:29-32; 1 Cor. 6:9-11; Mk. 7:19-21.\n\nThe penalty for breaking the law of faith is failing to receive those things which man would receive if he exercised faith instead of unbelief. No man can break this law and still get results or answers to his prayers.\n\nWhen prayers are not answered for one who is in Christ, let it become a settled fact with him that he is breaking the law of faith. All the devils in Hell or any power on Earth cannot keep God from honoring faith if it is properly exercised.\n\nIt matters not what has been asked of God—He will answer upon the sole condition of faith in His promises. Jesus said: "If ye abide in me, and my words abide in you, ye shall ask what ye will, and it shall be done unto you" (Jn. 15:7).\n\nThis is final and irrefutable. It's the all-inclusive condition of answered prayer. Make no mistake about it—this is the cause of unanswered prayer, but it can easily be corrected.\n\nAll you have to do is get into Christ and meditate on the Word of God until your heart becomes full of His promises, and then ask in faith, nothing wavering, and it shall be done.\n\n---\n\n## Ten Questions For Supplement Five. Do You Know:\n\n**1. That three separate and distinct persons of the Godhead are now carrying out God's plan of creation and redemption of all things?**\n\nThe Bible is very clear that there are three separate and distinct persons in the Godhead—that they all existed as separate beings from all eternity, that they were all capable of doing the same things, and that they all took separate parts in the creation and redemption of all things. All three had a part in the drafting of God's plan, as we saw in Lesson Five, Point II.\n\nGod's plan is revealed in three distinct parts and is now being carried out by three distinct persons.\n\nOne person, now called the Father because He had a Son, took the first or headship part and commanded what was to be done. This is revealed in both Testaments. David said: "thou art exalted as the head of all" (1 Chron. 29:11). Paul said of saints: "ye are Christ's; and Christ's is God's" (1 Cor. 3:23). He also said: "I would have you know, that the head of every man is Christ; and the head of the woman is the man; and the head of Christ is God" (1 Cor. 11:3). This proves that Christ and God the Father are two distinct persons as much as man and woman are.\n\nAnother person, now called the Son because he had a Father, took the second or representative part in the creation and redemption of all things. God the Father created and redeemed everything by Jesus Christ. We are told that: "All things were made by him . . . the world was made by him . . . God created all things by Jesus Christ . . . by him all things were created . . . by whom also he [the Father] made [planned] the worlds" (ages, Jn. 1:3, 10; Eph. 3:9; Col. 1:15-18; Heb. 1:1-3). Then too, it is by Jesus Christ that God redeems the world to Himself (Jn. 3:16; 17:4; 2 Cor. 5:17-21; 1 Pet. 2:24).\n\nStill another person, now called the Holy Spirit to distinguish Him from the Father and from the Son, took the third part of direct operation in the creation and redemption of all things. It was the Holy Spirit that brooded upon the face of the deep and operated at the command of God in restoring the Earth to a habitable state (Gen. 1:21; Job 33:4). It was the Holy Spirit that came upon Mary and by whom she conceived the Son of God (Lk. 1:35). It was the Holy Spirit that has operated in the lives of all men of all ages, bringing about the work of redemption in their lives and giving them power to carry out the will of God (Acts 3:21; 2 Pet. 1:21; Jn. 3:3-5; 14:16-17, 26; 15:26; 16:7-15; Acts 10:38).\n\nWe can say that God the Father redeems by the sacrifice of Christ and through the direct power of the Holy Spirit.\n\n**2. That demons and Satan were not created sinful?**\n\nAll things were created perfect and sinless in the beginning of their creation. Concerning Lucifer, it is stated in Ezek. 28:11-17: "Thou wast perfect in thy ways from the day that thou wast created, till iniquity was found in thee."\n\nConcerning the angels that fell, it is stated that they "sinned" and "left their first estate" (2 Pet. 2:4; Jude 6-7). Concerning demons, it is also clear that they sinned, for they already know their punishment for what they have done (Mt. 8:29; Lk. 8:31).\n\nNot one Scripture says that God ever created anything sinful or imperfect. In Eccl. 3:11 we read: "He made everything beautiful in his time," and anything contrary to this idea would be out of harmony with God.\n\n**3. That people will be saved after the rapture of the Church?**\n\nThis is clearly stated in Acts 2:16-21, where we read of people being saved and receiving the Holy Spirit in their lives during the Tribulation. See also Rev. 7:9-17; 12:17; 15:2-4; 20:4-6, where great multitudes of people will be saved and come out of the great tribulation.\n\nThat the Church is raptured before the Tribulation will be proven later.\n\n**4. That there have been only two worldwide dictators since the creation of the earth?**\n\nThe first one was Lucifer, as proven in Lessons Six and Seven. The second one was Adam, as proven in Lessons Eight and Nine.\n\nThere will not be another worldwide dictator until Christ comes to reign on the Earth forever. This we shall see in Lesson Forty-eight.\n\n**5. That Hell has literal fire and not spiritual fire?**\n\nOne reading of the following passages will prove this:\n- "I am tormented in this flame" (Lk. 16:19-31)\n- "Into the fire that never shall be quenched" (Mt. 25:41, 46; Mk. 9:42-50; Isa. 66:22-24)\n- "He shall be tormented with fire and brimstone . . . And the smoke of their torment ascendeth up for ever and ever" (Rev. 14:9-11; 19:20; 20:10)\n\nThe idea of spiritual fire could never be understood in such plain literal passages that speak of fire, smoke, and brimstone. There is no statement in Scripture that even hints of spiritual fire that will torment people, so to even question the reality and literalness of Hell is showing opposition to the Bible.\n\n**6. That the soul and spirit or the inner man is immortal?**\n\nThis is definitely stated in 1 Pet. 3:4: "But let it be the hidden man of the heart in that which is not corruptible, even the ornament of a quiet spirit." If the spirit is not corruptible, then it is immortal.\n\n**7. The righteous are in a conscious state of bliss between death and resurrection?**\n\nThis was true of Lazarus and all the Old Testament saints who were held captive in the lower parts of the Earth before Christ captured them and led them to Heaven when He ascended on High (Lk. 16:19-31; Mt. 12:40; Eph. 4:7-11; Heb. 2:14-15).\n\nThis was true of Moses who appeared with Christ on the mount while his body was in corruption in Moab (Mt. 17:3; Deut. 34:5-6; Jude 9).\n\nThis will be true of the future martyrs of the Tribulation (Rev. 6:9-11). And this will be true of all who die in Christ now and go to Heaven until the resurrection (2 Cor. 5:8; Phil. 1:21-23; 1 Thess. 4:16).\n\n**8. That the wicked are in a conscious state of torment between death and resurrection?**\n\nThis is proven by the rich man in Hell in torment after death (Lk. 16:19-31). This is also proven by the fact that there are conversations and other manifestations of consciousness in Hell (Ezek. 32:21; Isa. 14:9; 2 Sam. 22:6; Ps. 55:15; 116:3).\n\n**9. That the soul does not sleep in the grave after death?**\n\nThis is proven by the Scriptures in the two points mentioned above. All passages used to teach soul-sleep really refer to the body, which alone sees corruption and goes to the grave.\n\nThis is clear from an examination of all passages that speak of the dead knowing nothing in the grave. According to Jas. 2:26, it is the body only that dies, and therefore this is the only thing that is put in the grave. The souls go to two different places where they are conscious after death, as proven in Points 7 and 8 above.\n\n**10. That the dead cannot communicate with the living after death?**\n\nThis is clear from what was said of the rich man in Hell, who was told that the dead cannot go back on Earth to warn the living (Lk. 16:19-31).\n\nIt is true that Moses appeared with Christ on the mount, but this was a divine plan to bear witness to the sonship of Christ and to show witnesses what the coming kingdom was to be like (Mt. 16:28–17:8). There is not one authentic case of the dead communicating with the living to teach that men in general who die can so communicate.\n\n---\n\nGod's provision was complete before Adam sinned, and it's been restored in Christ. The gap is always on the human side — unbelief, ignorance, or failure to meet the conditions. So here's the question: Think of one specific area where God's provision should be meeting your need but isn't. Which of the barriers covered in this supplement is most likely operating in that area — and what specific step can you take to remove it?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgbl001h10b8s9l8ry5w	cmq76cgbj001f10b883ni3dl8	Lesson 20 — The Final Battle and Christ's Triumph	READING	900	0	\N	t	![Lesson 20 — The Final Battle and Christ's Triumph](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os43yYpVL3Ls52XczwCYNqdZVf8hMUGlEvQ0nD)\n\n## The Final Battle and Christ's Triumph\n\nThe Bible does not end with Satan in power. It ends with his complete and eternal defeat. From the first promise in Eden — "it shall bruise thy head" (Genesis 3:15) — to the final scene in Revelation, Scripture moves toward the triumph of Christ over every power of darkness.\n\n### The Binding of Satan\n\nRevelation 20 describes the Millennium — a thousand-year reign of Christ on earth during which Satan is bound and cast into the bottomless pit:\n\n> Revelation 20:2-3 — "And he laid hold on the dragon, that old serpent, which is the Devil, and Satan, and bound him a thousand years, and cast him into the bottomless pit, and shut him up, and set a seal upon him, that he should deceive the nations no more."\n\nDuring this time, the earth will experience unprecedented peace, justice, and prosperity. The curse will be partially lifted, and the nations will worship the Lord.\n\n### The Final Rebellion\n\nAt the end of the Millennium, Satan is released for a brief season. He deceives the nations one final time, gathering them for battle against the camp of the saints. But fire comes down from God out of heaven and devours them. Satan is cast into the lake of fire, where the beast and the false prophet already are:\n\n> Revelation 20:10 — "And the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are, and shall be tormented day and night for ever and ever."\n\nThis is the final end of evil. Not rehabilitation, not reconciliation, not annihilation — but **eternal, conscious punishment** for the one who introduced sin and death into God's good creation.\n\n### The New Heaven and New Earth\n\nAfter Satan's final defeat, God creates a new heaven and a new earth where righteousness dwells:\n\n> Revelation 21:4 — "And God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away."\n\nThe curse is reversed. Death is destroyed. Evil is extinguished. And the people of God live forever in the presence of the Lamb who overcame.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76cgbp001l10b8u4wkcogr	cmq76cgbj001f10b883ni3dl8	Supplement 8 — A Final Synthesis	SUPPLEMENT	600	2	\N	t	![Supplement 8 — A Final Synthesis](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Osw6yRLqbNv3tcSjXbK960OEaP1ghrDBudGzUT)\n\n## Supplement 8 — A Final Synthesis: The Theology of Spiritual Warfare\n\n### Three Levels of Demonic Opposition\n\nThe Church's tradition identifies three levels at which demonic opposition operates in human life:\n\n**1. Personal Temptation and Oppression**\nIndividual demons attack believers through temptation, accusation, and affliction. This is the most common form of spiritual warfare.\n\n**2. Corporate and Cultural Deception**\nPrincipalities and powers influence churches, institutions, and entire cultures with doctrines of devils, moral corruption, and social decay.\n\n**3. Cosmic and Eschatological Conflict**\nSatan's ultimate rebellion against God unfolds across history and culminates in the final battle of Revelation. This level is God's domain, but believers participate through prayer, proclamation, and holy living.\n\n---\n\n### Key Theological Principles\n\n**I. All demonic power is derivative and temporary.** Demons have no authority except what God permits, and their time is short (Revelation 12:12).\n\n**II. The believer's authority is absolute in Christ.** No demon can withstand the Name of Jesus, the blood of the Lamb, and the Word of God.\n\n**III. Spiritual warfare requires both truth and Spirit.** Knowledge without the Spirit produces arrogance; the Spirit without truth produces fanaticism. Both are essential.\n\n**IV. Holiness is the best defense.** A life of prayer, purity, and obedience creates an environment where demons cannot operate.\n\n**V. The final victory is certain.** Satan's doom is sealed at the cross and executed at the end of the age. Every battle we fight is part of a war already won.\n\n---\n\n### Scripture Memory\n\n> 1 John 4:4 — "Ye are of God, little children, and have overcome them: because greater is he that is in you, than he that is in the world."\n\n> Romans 8:37-39 — "Nay, in all these things we are more than conquerors through him that loved us. For I am persuaded, that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor powers, nor things present, nor things to come, nor height, nor depth, nor any other creature, shall be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in Christ Jesus our Lord."\n\n> Revelation 12:11 — "And they overcame him by the blood of the Lamb, and by the word of their testimony; and they loved not their lives unto the death."\n\n---\n\n### Questions for Reflection\n\n1. How has your understanding of demons and spiritual warfare changed through this course?\n\n2. Which of the three levels of demonic opposition do you face most often in your own life?\n\n3. What specific practice — prayer, fasting, Scripture memorization, worship — will you commit to strengthening as part of your daily warfare?\n\n4. Write a brief prayer of authority, using the Name of Jesus, the blood of the Lamb, and the Word of God, declaring freedom over any area where you have experienced demonic attack.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xn7f000hbep927l41fvy	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Transcendental Meditation and Mindfulness	READING	\N	11	\N	t	![Transcendental Meditation and Mindfulness](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsWHB5Yh19Elc9Cf1yMTquZF6SO8bsvVX7eRiY)\n\n## Transcendental Meditation and Mindfulness\n\nHis pediatrician recommended it. The school had implemented a mindfulness program — ten minutes before first period, the children sitting in silence, following the instruction to "observe thoughts without judgment and let them pass." Research showed improved focus, reduced anxiety. Teachers loved it. Parents signed permission slips without reading them.\n\nHis son came home from the first week of the program and said something strange: "There's someone at school who talks to me when I'm quiet." He described it as a pleasant voice. It told him what to do. He liked it.\n\nHis father was a pastor. He sat with his son for a long time. He prayed. He was not angry. He was very careful about what he said next, because what his son had described was a familiar spirit, established during the daily practice of deliberately emptying his mind, finding the unoccupied swept house Jesus described in Matthew 12.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nTranscendental Meditation (TM) is a Hindu-derived practice in which practitioners repeat personally assigned *mantras* — sounds given by a trained TM teacher — until thought subsides and a state of "pure awareness" is achieved. TM traces to Advaita Vedanta, the non-dualistic Hindu philosophy that the individual self (*atman*) is identical with universal consciousness (*Brahman*).\n\nWhat is not disclosed to beginning practitioners: the mantras are not meaningless sounds. They are names and invocations of Hindu deities. "Shring" invokes Lakshmi. "Hreem" invokes the divine mother. Repeating these is summoning, whether or not the practitioner understands that.\n\nMindfulness, stripped of its Buddhist framing for Western consumption, retains its Buddhist goal: through non-judgmental observation of thought, the practitioner achieves *anatta* (non-self) — the realization that the self is an illusion. This is not a neutral psychological technique. It is a Buddhist theological proposition practiced daily.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nBiblical meditation is filling the mind. [Joshua 1:8](data-scripture="Joshua 1:8"): *"This book of the law shall not depart out of thy mouth; but thou shalt meditate therein day and night."* The Hebrew *hagah* — meditate — means to mutter, speak aloud, ponder actively. It is a full-engagement, Word-centered activity.\n\nEastern meditation is emptying the mind. It is the explicit and deliberate production of the condition Jesus warned about in [Matthew 12:43-45](data-scripture="Matthew 12:43-45"): *"When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man... he findeth it empty, swept, and garnished... and the last state of that man is worse than the first."* A swept, empty mind is not peaceful. It is, in the spiritual architecture Jesus describes, an occupied house waiting to be re-occupied.\n\nThe mantra in TM is a spiritual phone number connecting the practitioner to the entity it names. "Christian mindfulness" and "centering prayer" (see the next lesson) teach the same empty-mind technique with biblical vocabulary — making the demonic feel sanctified.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Mantra repetition is invocation.** Repeating a Hindu deity's name functions as repeated summoning, whether the practitioner knows the deity's name or not. Long-term TM teachers report that sustained practice leads to "cosmic consciousness" — progressive demonic possession described in the vocabulary of Hindu enlightenment.\n\n**The empty mind creates vulnerability for everyone, including children.** School mindfulness programs are training children to sweep their minds empty on command and observe thoughts without moral judgment — including the thoughts that the Holy Spirit uses to convict of sin. The conscience being trained to observe without response is the conscience being trained into spiritual passivity.\n\n**Personality dissolution is a documented long-term effect.** Long-term mindfulness practitioners report depersonalization, anxiety, and dissociation — the self dissolving as Buddhist theology predicts and as demonic blending produces.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nHave you practiced TM or been given a mantra? Name the specific mantra. Repent for the invocation it represented. Renounce the entity its name addressed, and command its departure.\n\nHave you practiced mindfulness meditation in a way that involved deliberately emptying your mind of thought and moral evaluation? Repent for the spiritual passivity that practice cultivated. Ask the Holy Spirit to restore active discernment to your mind.\n\nTo parents: ask your children what happens in the mindfulness sessions their school provides. Listen carefully to what they describe. A child who encounters a "pleasant voice" during silence is not experiencing spiritual growth.\n\n---\n\n*Meditation empties the mind. The next lesson examines a system that arranges the home — and invites the same forces in through the front door.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Has mindfulness meditation been recommended to you by a doctor, therapist, or church leader? How did you respond?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xn77000bbep9b3jh9o13	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Reiki and Energy Healing	READING	\N	13	\N	t	![Reiki and Energy Healing](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsCmurkSe78vbPqVLiKnDy6up93CGaNzkh5HsQ)\n\n## Reiki and Energy Healing\n\nShe was a nurse practitioner. She added Reiki certification to her practice because patients asked for it and because the research on touch-based therapies was promising. She was also a Christian. She told herself the energy she channeled was the Holy Spirit.\n\nThe first time she performed an attunement on a new student — the ritual process of "opening" someone to the Reiki channel — the student's eyes rolled back and she spoke in a voice that was not her own for several seconds. The Reiki teacher who trained her said this was "a strong energy response." It happened at every attunement thereafter.\n\nShe had never been taught what an attunement actually is: a ritual initiation connecting the student to the entities that power the Reiki system. What she was doing, every time she performed one, was opening another person to demonic possession.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nReiki is a Japanese energy healing system founded by Mikao Usui following a 21-day fast on Mount Kurama that he described as a mystical initiation — the classic format of occult transmission. Practitioners channel what they call "universal life force energy" (*Rei* = universal, *Ki* = life energy) into clients through prescribed hand placements on the body.\n\nVariants include Therapeutic Touch, Healing Touch, Pranic Healing, and Quantum Touch. "Christian Reiki" attempts to baptize the practice with Christian language while retaining its entire spiritual architecture.\n\nTraining involves "attunements" — ritual initiations connecting students to the Reiki source. The symbols used (Cho Ku Rei, Sei He Ki, Hon Sha Ze Sho Nen) are occult sigils functioning as conduits to specific spiritual forces. Practitioners are explicitly taught to work under the guidance of "Reiki guides" — named spiritual entities.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe central deception: the energy being channeled is from God.\n\n[James 5:14-15](data-scripture="James 5:14-15") describes legitimate Christian healing: *"Is any sick among you? let him call for the elders of the church; and let them pray over him, anointing him with oil in the name of the Lord."* The mechanism is prayer, anointing, faith, and the sovereign will of God. The Holy Spirit is a Person who moves as He wills, not a force channeled through prescribed hand positions.\n\nAny system in which the practitioner becomes a conduit for spiritual power on demand — by technique, by position, by ritual — is not the Holy Spirit. The Holy Spirit cannot be systematized. What can be systematized is a demonic counterfeit.\n\n"Christian Reiki" is more dangerous than secular Reiki because it eliminates the only warning signal that might otherwise trigger discernment — it makes the demonic feel divine.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Spirit transfer through attunement.** The attunement process is a spiritual initiation that connects the student to demonic entities. This is not metaphor — attunements frequently produce physical phenomena (shaking, heat, involuntary vocalizations) in recipients who were not aware of their spiritual nature.\n\n**The practitioner becomes a medium.** As Reiki practice deepens, practitioners enter an increasingly intimate working relationship with their "guides" — demonic entities they have been taught to follow and consult. The deeper the practice, the more fully they function as mediums.\n\n**Recipients carry the transfer home.** Clients who receive Reiki frequently report subsequent spiritual disturbance — nightmares, oppressive atmospheres, felt presences. The demonic entities involved in the session do not confine themselves to the table.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf you have received Reiki treatments — in a clinical setting, from a friend, at a wellness center, from a "Christian Reiki" practitioner — you have received a spiritual transfer. The therapeutic framing and the setting do not determine the spiritual nature of what occurred.\n\nRepent for seeking healing outside God's ordained means. Renounce every Reiki guide by name if they were named. Break the spiritual transfer that occurred in each session. Ask the Holy Spirit to cleanse your body from every demonic energy that entered through the practice.\n\nIf you practice Reiki: the practice must stop. Destroy all Reiki symbols, manuals, and materials — [Acts 19:19](data-scripture="Acts 19:19"). Renounce your attunement and break every agreement with the entities involved. Seek deliverance prayer.\n\n---\n\n*Reiki works from the outside in. The next lesson examines the system designed to work from the inside out — awakening the serpentine energy the practitioner was always trying to reach.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you received Reiki, therapeutic touch, or any energy healing session? What did the practitioner tell you was happening?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xn7c000fbep9j5hzs2o7	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Chakras and Kundalini	READING	\N	14	\N	t	![Chakras and Kundalini](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsTBMEY3zI0Sg3uieQlJxkWsZOR6bnzGDtEw9a)\n\n## Chakras and Kundalini\n\nShe was a worship leader in a charismatic church. She also practiced kundalini yoga. She told herself there was no conflict — the shaking she felt during worship and the shaking she felt during yoga practice were both the Holy Spirit. Both felt supernatural. Both felt powerful. Both involved loss of physical control.\n\nOne Sunday morning she stood at the front of the congregation to lead worship and felt something move up her spine. She began to shake violently. She fell. She made sounds that she could not describe afterward — animal-like, involuntary. The congregation prayed over her. Her pastor said it was a deep move of the Spirit.\n\nHer husband was a student of Scripture. He asked her what she had been doing in her personal practice. When she told him about the kundalini yoga, he went quiet for a long time. He said, "I think we need to get you some help."\n\nHe was right.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nThe chakra system describes seven "energy centers" along the human spine — from the base (*muladhara*) to the crown (*sahasrara*) — that, in Hindu and tantric theology, govern different dimensions of physical, emotional, and spiritual experience. Kundalini (*"coiled one"*) is the dormant feminine divine energy (Shakti) believed to lie at the base of the spine, awakened through yoga, meditation, breathwork, or initiation, and rising through the chakra system toward the crown where it unites with the masculine divine (Shiva) in an experience of enlightenment.\n\nThe symbolism is explicitly sexual and explicitly serpentine.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\n*Kundalini* means "coiled serpent." [Revelation 12:9](data-scripture="Revelation 12:9"): *"And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world."* The entity that kundalini practice is designed to awaken carries the Scripture's name for the enemy.\n\nEach chakra corresponds to a specific demonic contamination when activated:\n- Root: survival anxiety and fear\n- Sacral: sexual perversion and addiction\n- Solar plexus: pride and domination\n- Heart: counterfeit love and sentimentality replacing truth\n- Throat: psychic communication and false prophecy\n- Third eye: clairvoyance and familiar spirit activity\n- Crown: full spiritual possession\n\nThe awakened person becomes a vessel that demonic entities enter and exit at will — eventually unable to distinguish their own thoughts from implanted ones. This is not metaphor or theological speculation. It is the documented experience of deliverance ministers across multiple continents who have worked with people who have undergone kundalini awakenings.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The "coiled serpent" is not metaphor.** Scripture uses this specific image for the enemy. Deliberately inviting the activation of "serpent power" in your body is a prayer for demonic inhabitation, however poorly understood.\n\n**Kundalini syndrome is documented and severe.** Practitioners who experience full or partial kundalini awakening report: involuntary physical movements and vocalizations, seizure-like episodes, extreme heat traveling through the body, sexual arousal unrelated to any external stimulus, temporary psychic phenomena, and progressive loss of autonomous mental function. Medical literature describes this as kundalini syndrome, noting that it sometimes produces permanent psychological damage.\n\n**Church infiltration is a documented risk.** A Christian who undergoes kundalini awakening and brings the activated energy into a congregational worship setting can create a corporate spiritual opening. Not everyone present will be affected equally — but the corporate spiritual atmosphere is changed.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf you have experienced kundalini phenomena — the rising heat, the involuntary shaking, the temporary psychic experiences — in the context of yoga, meditation, breathwork, or any other practice, you have experienced the activation of demonic energy in your nervous system. This requires specific targeted deliverance ministry.\n\nRenounce kundalini by name. Renounce each chakra activation specifically. Pray over your spine and nervous system, pleading the blood of Jesus over every vertebra. Seek an experienced deliverance minister — not merely pastoral prayer, but someone who understands the specific spiritual mechanics involved.\n\nThe Holy Spirit does not require your spine to be a channel. His temple is the whole person, sanctified and indwelt — not a nervous system converted into a serpentine conduit.\n\n---\n\n*Kundalini works on the body's energy centers. The next lesson examines a system that works on something even more intimate — your understanding of your own identity.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you done kundalini yoga, somatic breathwork, or any practice aimed at activating spiritual energy centers in the body? What did you experience?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xn79000dbep98kithhns	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Hypnosis and Past-Life Regression	READING	\N	16	\N	t	![Hypnosis and Past-Life Regression](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsuU39BbVZIJS2tQ1kPsY7EcO3rv8DqhnMN9ly)\n\n## Hypnosis and Past-Life Regression\n\nShe booked the session for weight loss. The hypnotherapist was professional, credentialed, gentle. The induction took eleven minutes. She came out of the session calm and resolved about her eating habits.\n\nShe also came out of the session with three new "memories" she had not carried going in: vivid emotional recollections of a life in 18th-century France, a violent death by drowning, a face she had never seen but now saw clearly in dreams. The hypnotherapist called these "past-life bleed-throughs." She said they were healing. She suggested a regression session to process them.\n\nShe did not know that the memories were not memories. She did not know that the beings that had provided them in the trance state had not left.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nHypnosis is an induced state of narrowed attention and heightened suggestibility in which the subject's critical faculty is suspended and unconscious material becomes more accessible. In deep somnambulistic trance, post-hypnotic suggestions can execute hours later without conscious memory. The will is not merely relaxed — it is temporarily subordinated to the hypnotist's directing voice.\n\nPast-life regression uses hypnosis to "recover" supposed memories of previous incarnations. It has been popularized through Brian Weiss's *Many Lives, Many Masters* and Michael Newton's *Journey of Souls* — both of which recount information allegedly received from regression subjects about previous lives, between-life "spirit realms," and communications with guides.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe Bible knows nothing of past lives. [Hebrews 9:27](data-scripture="Hebrews 9:27"): *"It is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment."* One life. One death. One judgment. The reincarnation framework is not an alternative Christian theology — it is a non-Christian theological structure adopted from Eastern religions in which the cross is unnecessary because death is simply a transition to another iteration of the same journey.\n\nThe "memories" recovered in regression are not genuine. They are either demonic implants or familiar spirit deception — fabricated narratives provided by entities that have extensive historical knowledge and can produce convincing period-accurate detail. The emotional distress experienced during regression is real. The narrative producing it is false. And the entities that provided the narrative during the trance state frequently remain attached.\n\n[Isaiah 26:3](data-scripture="Isaiah 26:3"): *"Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee."* The mind stayed on God — anchored, directed, engaged. The deliberate opposite of the surrendered, passive mind that hypnosis requires.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Voluntary surrender of the will creates a spiritual vacancy.** God designed the human will to be the executive function of the soul — the faculty through which we choose God, resist the enemy, and govern our inner life. Hypnosis requires the deliberate subordination of the will to another voice. In the spiritual realm, this is a voluntary opening — the will's defensive function temporarily removed.\n\n**Familiar spirits provide false memories that produce lasting spiritual attachment.** The entity that gave a regression subject her 18th-century "memories" established a relationship during the trance that it maintains afterward. Regression clients often report that the entity they encountered felt more familiar and trustworthy than any human relationship — because it has been presenting itself as their companion across "multiple lifetimes."\n\n**Progressive deepening is the design.** Smoking cessation hypnosis leads to anxiety management, which leads to regression, which leads to "between-life" sessions, which leads to spirit guide contact. Each step is the natural next step in a progression the enemy designed.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf you have been hypnotized — for any stated purpose, by any credentialed practitioner — you have voluntarily surrendered your will to a directing voice that is not God's. The therapeutic benefit does not change the spiritual reality of what occurred.\n\nRepent for the surrender of your will. Renounce every entity that entered during trance states. Renounce every false memory implanted during regression, and specifically break the attachment of each entity that provided those memories. Ask the Holy Spirit to restore full sovereignty to your will and your mind.\n\nOne clarifying note on involuntary altered states: this lesson addresses voluntary hypnotic submission. People who have experienced trauma dissociation or involuntary altered states are not in the same category — those experiences require healing rather than repentance.\n\n---\n\n*Hypnosis opens the mind to external direction. Smudging attempts to clean the space afterward. The next lesson reveals why that cleaning makes the problem worse.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you undergone hypnosis — clinical or recreational? What was the stated purpose, and what did you experience?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xn740009bep9wtocb75c	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Psychedelics and Plant Medicine	READING	\N	24	\N	t	![Psychedelics and Plant Medicine](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OskXAxcd8rZcMaXYe27SivEmH1t8Ad0OozjUKI)\n\n## Psychedelics and Plant Medicine\n\nHe was a venture capitalist. Stanford MBA, two successful exits, a Range Rover in the garage and a hollow place in his chest that nothing had touched. His therapist recommended an ayahuasca retreat in Costa Rica. The brochure used words like "integration," "healing," and "ancient wisdom." His therapist had done it herself. His business partner had done it. Johns Hopkins was running clinical trials. It seemed almost medical.\n\nHe came back from Costa Rica different. Not in the way the brochure had promised. He could not sleep without the entities appearing. He quit his job. His marriage ended. He describes himself now as "guided by the medicine" — which means, in practice, guided by the entities that never left after the ceremony.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nPsychedelics — ayahuasca, psilocybin mushrooms, DMT, ketamine, peyote, MDMA — are powerful psychoactive substances that shatter the normal boundary between conscious and subconscious, producing hallucinations, altered states of consciousness, and what users consistently describe as encounters with intelligent non-human entities.\n\nArchaeological evidence places psilocybin mushroom use in religious ritual at 6,000 years ago. The Aztecs called them *teonanácatl* — "flesh of the gods." Ayahuasca means "vine of the dead" in Quechua. Every culture that has used these substances has understood them as tools for spirit contact, not merely for neurological experience.\n\nThe modern therapeutic rebranding — university research centers, ketamine clinics, trauma-treatment retreats — has succeeded in persuading many Christians that these are medical treatments rather than what they have always been: chemical keys to forbidden spiritual doors.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe entities are real. Rick Strassman's DMT research at the University of New Mexico documented that participants consistently and independently reported encounters with autonomous, intelligent beings — "machine elves," insectile intelligences, serpentine entities — that communicated telepathically and performed examinations. Strassman, beginning the study as a materialist, concluded these experiences could not be explained purely by brain chemistry.\n\nWhat they are: fallen angels. Interdimensional beings who have waited for humanity to voluntarily remove the cognitive defenses that God built into ordinary consciousness. [Deuteronomy 18:10-12](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 18:10-12") lists the categories of forbidden spiritual access. The psychedelic removes the barrier chemically. The forbidden access takes place immediately.\n\n*Ayahuasca* means "vine of the dead." The brew is prepared under occult ritual, and the vomiting — called *la purga* — is described by shamans as "purging of demons." The demons are precisely what the ceremony invites in.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Voluntary surrender of the defensive architecture God built.** The default mode network — the brain system responsible for stable identity and memory — is specifically disrupted by psychedelics. God designed human identity to be stable and anchored in Him. Chemically dissolving it opens the person to deception about who they are and Whose they are.\n\n**Entity attachment that follows the user home.** Users report persistent entities — visible in peripheral vision, present in dreams, audible as voices — following psychedelic use. These are demonic attachments that treated the voluntary chemical opening as a legal invitation.\n\n**Generational contamination.** Entity attachments pass to children and affect households. One ayahuasca ceremony can create a generational spiritual assignment.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThe therapeutic framing is not a spiritual exemption. The Johns Hopkins approval does not change the spiritual reality. If you have used psychedelics in any context — recreational, ceremonial, therapeutic, or "just once to see" — you have opened a door through chemical means that requires spiritual closure.\n\nRepent specifically for each substance and each use. Renounce every entity encountered by name if it gave one, or by the description of its appearance. Command their departure in Jesus' name. Pray specifically over your mind, perceptual faculties, and identity architecture, asking the Holy Spirit to restore the boundaries God designed.\n\nDo not return to these substances. [Ephesians 5:18](data-scripture="Ephesians 5:18"): *"Be not drunk with wine, wherein is excess; but be filled with the Spirit."* There is an authorized altered state: the infilling of the Holy Spirit. It requires no chemical key — only surrender to Christ.\n\n---\n\n*Psychedelics force spiritual doors open through chemistry. Astral projection attempts to walk through those doors deliberately, without chemical assistance. The next lesson examines what waits on the other side.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you used psychedelics recreationally or in a ceremonial context — including ayahuasca, psilocybin, or DMT? What entities or experiences did you encounter?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xshk000118pfwuffhwb7	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Tattoos with Occult Symbols	READING	\N	34	\N	t	![Tattoos with Occult Symbols](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsIoamvdDFm5fHMlhCe2Nngyo6VzaWuJEO4Dj7)\n\n## Tattoos with Occult Symbols\n\nShe got the pentagram at nineteen, at the peak of her Wiccan involvement. She was thirty-four now, a committed believer for eight years. The tattoo was on her wrist, covered most days with a wide bracelet.\n\nShe had repented of Wicca thoroughly. She had been through deliverance prayer. Her life was genuinely different. But she had a persistent sense that something was still attached — a specific pattern of oppression that seemed to localize around her left hand and forearm, something that resisted the freedom she had in every other area.\n\nHer deliverance minister asked her if there were any remaining objects or markings from her Wiccan practice that had not been addressed. She showed him the wrist. He said, "We need to pray specifically over this."\n\nThey did. The persistent pattern broke.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nTattoos are permanent markings created by inserting ink into the skin. When those markings carry occult symbolism — pentagrams, all-seeing eyes, Baphomet imagery, astrological signs, serpents, sigils, runes, or imagery from false religious systems — they function spiritually as declarations of allegiance and territory.\n\n[Leviticus 19:28](data-scripture="Leviticus 19:28"): *"Ye shall not make any cuttings in your flesh for the dead, nor print any marks upon you: I am the LORD."* The biblical prohibition is specifically connected to the dead — to rituals that involved marking the body as part of spirit-world practice. The context is covenantal identity: the marks declared whose you were.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe secular framing of occult tattoos as "just art" or "a phase I was going through" is the deception. What the symbols were designed to represent and invoke does not change because the person who bears them has lost interest in the system they came from. The marking is still present. The spiritual declaration it represents is still active in the spirit realm.\n\nThe blood involved in tattooing creates a spiritual transaction. Skin is the boundary of the body — the interface between self and world. To permanently mark it with symbols dedicated to demonic systems is to make a lasting declaration about ownership and allegiance. That declaration was made in blood.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The symbol retains its spiritual function regardless of the bearer's current beliefs.** A person who received a pentagram tattoo during Wiccan involvement and has since come to faith still bears a spiritual declaration of allegiance to the entity that pentagram represents. The salvation is real. The unaddressed marking continues to provide legal ground.\n\n**Demonic attachment localizes around marked areas.** The documented experience of deliverance ministers is that occult tattoos sometimes correlate with specific, localized patterns of oppression — physical problems, emotional patterns, or spiritual interference that cluster around the marked area and break when the marking is specifically addressed in prayer.\n\n**Children bear the spiritual effects of their parents' markings.** This is speculative in terms of mechanism, but consistent with the documented experience of generational spiritual transmission.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf you have occult tattoos — from a previous period of involvement, from cultural adoption of symbols whose meaning you did not fully understand, from a phase you have since left — the physical marking remains, but its spiritual legal claim can be completely revoked.\n\nThe action required: name the specific symbol and the spiritual system it came from. Repent for the marking. Renounce the allegiance it represented. Pray specifically over the marking, pleading the blood of Jesus Christ over it. Command every demonic entity associated with the symbol to leave.\n\nThe tattoo may remain physically. Its spiritual claim, once specifically renounced and covered by the blood of Christ, is revoked. You are not permanently marked for the enemy because you were foolish at nineteen. [1 Corinthians 6:11](data-scripture="1 Corinthians 6:11"): *"Such were some of you: but ye are washed, but ye are sanctified."*\n\n---\n\n*The body carries what is marked on it. The home carries what is placed in it. The next lesson examines the objects that anchor spiritual assignments to the spaces we live in.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Do you have tattoos with occult symbolism received before you understood their spiritual significance? Have you ever prayed specifically over them?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xn6w0003bep9l7cksrqe	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Freemasonry	READING	\N	37	\N	t	![Freemasonry](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsaG97xGEhtesUMivpomO8x4WSPknRFTuAI75Q)\n\n## Freemasonry\n\nHis grandfather was a 32nd-degree Scottish Rite Mason. His father was a Master Mason who died of a heart attack at 51. His uncle died of a throat tumor at 49. His cousin is being treated for unexplained chest pain — every cardiac test normal. He himself has struggled with financial patterns he cannot explain: businesses that start well and collapse without obvious cause, income that cannot stay in his hands regardless of how much comes in.\n\nHe is a committed believer. He tithes. He serves. He has never set foot in a lodge. He has never been told that his grandfather's oaths — specifically their penalties — invoked demonic assignments against the bloodline targeting the throat, the heart, and the financial capacity of his descendants.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nFreemasonry is a fraternal organization with worldwide membership estimated at three to six million. Its foundational three degrees — Entered Apprentice, Fellow Craft, and Master Mason — are conferred through elaborate ritual in Blue Lodges. Beyond these, Scottish Rite, York Rite, Shriners International, and the Order of the Eastern Star extend the system.\n\nFreemasonry claims to be a fraternal organization, not a religion. This claim does not survive examination. Masonic lodges have altars. Prayers are offered at those altars. Freemasonry has a deity: the Great Architect of the Universe (GAOTU), explicitly designed to be generic enough to include all members regardless of their personal faith, which requires specifically excluding Jesus Christ from Masonic prayer. And Freemasonry has a mock death and resurrection ritual in the Master Mason degree — the legend of Hiram Abiff — that is a counterfeit of the death and resurrection of Christ.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe blood oaths are the mechanism. At each Blue Lodge degree, the candidate swears a solemn oath of secrecy under specific physical penalty — and these are sworn before the candidate knows what he is committing to keep secret:\n\n*Entered Apprentice:* "...under no less penalty than having my throat cut across, my tongue torn out by its roots..."\n\n*Fellow Craft:* "...having my left breast torn open, and my heart and vitals taken from thence..."\n\n*Master Mason:* "...having my body severed in two, my bowels burnt to ashes..."\n\n[Matthew 5:34-37](data-scripture="Matthew 5:34-37") prohibits all oath-swearing. [James 5:12](data-scripture="James 5:12"): *"But above all things, my brethren, swear not."* These oaths are not only forbidden — they invoke specific demonic assignments against the swearer and, through the generational mechanism of [Exodus 20:5](data-scripture="Exodus 20:5"), against his bloodline.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The oath penalties become generational assignments.** Deliverance ministers consistently document in Masonic bloodlines: throat and neck problems, heart disease, abdominal disorders, premature death, financial failure that resets each generation, mental illness, and an unusual spiritual dullness that lifts dramatically when the Masonic covenants are specifically renounced.\n\n**The GAOTU replaces Christ.** Masonic prayer specifically excludes Jesus Christ. The Mason who prays in the lodge is praying to a deity designed to be not Jesus. This is not a technicality — it is a formal spiritual renunciation of the exclusive protection available only through the name of Jesus Christ.\n\n**The mock resurrection blasphemes the only resurrection that saves.** The Master Mason degree's ritual death and raising by the "Lion's Paw" grip is a spiritual identification with a counterfeit resurrection. This is not theater — it is a spiritual transaction that must be specifically renounced.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nResearch your family history. Ask parents and grandparents directly about Masonic involvement — Blue Lodge, Scottish Rite, York Rite, Shriners, Eastern Star, DeMolay for young men. Go back as far as you can. One Masonic ancestor creates a covenantal claim that the Supplement's prayer guide will walk you through breaking specifically, degree by degree.\n\nRemove every Masonic object from your home. Aprons, rings, Bibles, certificates, regalia. These are not sentimental keepsakes — they are covenantal objects with demonic attachments. Destroyed, not donated.\n\nAnd if you yourself are a Mason: the moment of decision is now. Every degree taken, every oath sworn, every session in the lodge deepens covenants that affect your family line.\n\n---\n\n*Masonic oaths create generational spiritual assignments. The next lesson examines a more direct weapon — the words spoken over a person's life with intent to harm.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Is there a Mason in your family history? Do you know what lodge they joined, what degree they achieved, and what oaths they took?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xn6z0005bep98c8oz3lv	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Curses	READING	\N	38	\N	t	![Curses](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os8Fzyz9wQn65F0NSyXfv2WGAqVjL7icrDpPIo)\n\n## Curses\n\nShe heard it the first time when she was seven. Her father said it in the middle of an argument with her mother, pointing at her: *"That girl is going to end up just like my sister."* His sister had been institutionalized for schizophrenia.\n\nShe is forty-one. She has been diagnosed with bipolar disorder. Three hospitalizations. She has prayed. She has received prayer from others. She has done everything her doctors, her pastor, and her own faith have suggested.\n\nShe has never been told that her father's words — spoken in anger over a child, invoking a specific generational destiny — functioned as a spiritual pronouncement. That words spoken by authority figures over children carry particular spiritual weight. That the demonic assignment her father's words created may still be operating, waiting for someone with the authority of Christ to revoke it.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nA curse is a spoken or enacted pronouncement of harm, misfortune, or binding upon a person, place, or bloodline. Scripture takes curses with complete seriousness — they are real spiritual forces operating within covenant law, not folk superstition.\n\n[Proverbs 18:21](data-scripture="Proverbs 18:21"): *"Death and life are in the power of the tongue."* This verse is not metaphorical. It is a statement about the mechanism of spoken words in the spiritual realm.\n\nCurses take several biblical forms: divine pronouncements for covenant violation ([Deuteronomy 27-28](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 27")), parental declarations over children (Noah over Canaan in [Genesis 9:25](data-scripture="Genesis 9:25")), prophetic pronouncements over nations, occult curses sent through ritual magic, and self-imposed curses — vows and declarations spoken in despair, anger, or agreement with lies.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe fundamental deception about curses is that they are either superstitious nonsense or exclusively ancient phenomena. Both positions leave contemporary people completely unprotected against a mechanism Scripture affirms is operative.\n\n[Proverbs 26:2](data-scripture="Proverbs 26:2") is the governing principle: *"As the bird by wandering, as the swallow by flying, so the curse causeless shall not come."* A curse requires legal ground to land. A believer walking in righteousness, covered by the blood of Christ, has substantial protection. But where legal ground exists — through sin, ancestral covenants, or opened spiritual doors — curses find footing and produce real effects.\n\nThis is important in both directions: the believer who claims blanket immunity regardless of spiritual state is as mistaken as the person who fears curses from strangers on the street.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Word curses from authority figures have specific spiritual weight.** Parents, teachers, pastors — people in positions of authority over others — carry spiritual authority that amplifies the impact of their spoken words. *"You'll never amount to anything." "You're stupid." "You're just like your father."* These function as spiritual assignments over the person addressed.\n\n**Occult curses find footing through legal ground.** Witchcraft practitioners do send curses against Christians, particularly Christian leaders who represent a threat to the enemy's territory. These curses land where sin, spiritual compromise, or unresolved legal ground provides entry.\n\n**Self-imposed curses through vows and agreement with lies.** *"I will never trust again." "I want to die." "I am fundamentally broken and will never be loved."* These are not merely damaging thought patterns. They are spoken agreements with demonic assignments that the enemy treats as invitations.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThree specific inventories to take:\n\n**Authority figure declarations.** What did your parents, grandparents, teachers, or other authority figures speak over you in your formative years? What specific negative declarations do you still hear in your own inner voice as established facts? Name them. Renounce the spiritual assignment behind each one. Declare the opposite in the name of Jesus.\n\n**Vows made in pain.** What have you declared in anger or despair? Unforgiveness vows. Death wishes. Agreements with lies about your identity or destiny. Name each one. Renounce it. [Romans 12:14](data-scripture="Romans 12:14"): *"Bless, and curse not."* Replace each curse with its corresponding blessing.\n\n**Occult curses sent against you.** If you are in Christian leadership, intercession, or deliverance ministry, there are likely curses currently aimed at you. [Isaiah 54:17](data-scripture="Isaiah 54:17"): *"No weapon that is formed against thee shall prosper."* This is covenant protection — but it applies in proportion to your covenant standing.\n\n---\n\n*Spoken curses strike individuals. The next lesson examines the mechanism by which a single act of covenant sin becomes a multigenerational assignment.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *What are the most destructive statements spoken over your life — by parents, partners, or authority figures? Write them down. This is the first step to breaking them.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xn720007bep93na4fli6	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Generational Curses	READING	\N	39	\N	t	![Generational Curses](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsmnlCyaTjs8MAGw2JgFBiIXKDThNCyqSVfZL3)\n\n## Generational Curses\n\nThe pattern has run through four generations of the same family. The men drink. Not all of them, not always catastrophically, but reliably — in a way that the family has normalized as "just how the men in our family are." Her great-grandfather. Her grandfather. Her father. Her brother.\n\nShe does not drink. She is a committed Christian. She is the first person in her line who talks about Jesus openly. But her marriage is in its third year, and she is watching the same patterns that destroyed her mother's marriage — the same emotional unavailability, the same defensiveness, the same inexplicable fear of intimacy — beginning to appear in her husband, who did not grow up in her family, who has no genetic connection to it.\n\nShe does not know that her family has not just a genetic and behavioral legacy. It has a demonic one.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\n[Exodus 20:5](data-scripture="Exodus 20:5"): *"I the LORD thy God am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children unto the third and fourth generation of them that hate me."*\n\nThis verse is not a statement about divine punishment of innocent children. It describes the spiritual mechanism by which sin propagates: when an ancestor opens a demonic door through idolatry, occult involvement, or serious covenant violation, the demons that enter claim *generational access* — they follow the bloodline and reproduce the same patterns in successive generations until the covenant is specifically broken.\n\nThe mechanism explains patterns that genetic and environmental models cannot fully account for: adopted children manifesting the same specific addictions as biological family members they have never met; the same disease presenting at the same age across multiple generations; families where the same relationship pattern destroys every marriage despite each generation's stated intention to break the cycle.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe deception is not that generational curses exist — it is that conversion automatically eliminates them. Many Christians receive genuine salvation and genuine transformation and still carry demonic assignments inherited from their family line — because salvation purchases the legal right to close those doors, but the doors must be specifically, deliberately closed.\n\n[Galatians 3:13](data-scripture="Galatians 3:13"): *"Christ hath redeemed us from the curse of the law, being made a curse for us."* The complete answer was purchased at Calvary. The appropriation of that provision is a separate act — as specific and intentional as the original covenants that created the assignments were.\n\n[Jeremiah 31:29-30](data-scripture="Jeremiah 31:29-30") anticipates the new covenant's power to break generational chains. [2 Corinthians 5:17](data-scripture="2 Corinthians 5:17"): *"Old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new."* But "all things become new" is a position that must be occupied deliberately — through the intentional revocation of what the old things established.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Common generational sources:** Freemasonry (see the previous lesson), occult practice or witchcraft in the ancestral line, idolatry in any form, sexual sin including incest and prostitution, bloodshed and murder, and explicit rejection of Christ or apostasy.\n\n**The patterns that indicate generational assignment:** The same addiction across multiple generations. Men dying young of the same disease at the same age. Divorce and relational destruction as a family norm. Chronic inability to build or retain wealth. Unusual rates of miscarriage, infertility, or infant death. Mental illness appearing at the same life stage in multiple generations.\n\n**The biblical precedent for breaking generational covenants** is identificational repentance — confessing the sins of one's ancestors as if they were one's own, as Nehemiah ([Nehemiah 1:6-7](data-scripture="Nehemiah 1:6-7")), Daniel ([Daniel 9:4-20](data-scripture="Daniel 9:4-20")), and Ezra ([Ezra 9:6-15](data-scripture="Ezra 9:6-15")) all modeled. This is not taking personal guilt for others' sins. It is breaking the covenantal chain.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nTake a family history inventory. Not a medical history — a spiritual history. Ask your parents and grandparents directly about:\n- Any Masonic involvement at any level\n- Any occult practice, folk magic, or spiritism\n- Any participation in non-Christian religious systems\n- Family patterns of addiction, mental illness, premature death, relational destruction\n\nThe goal is not to assign blame. The goal is to identify which doors were opened so they can be specifically closed.\n\nThe Supplement's prayer guide provides the specific language for breaking each category of generational covenant. Work through it with the Holy Spirit's leading, as slowly and specifically as it requires.\n\n[Acts 16:31](data-scripture="Acts 16:31"): *"Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved, and thy house."* The gospel's scope is not merely individual. The salvation purchased by Christ's blood is designed to cover a house.\n\n---\n\n*Generational curses bind through bloodline covenants. The next lesson examines a more dangerous trap — one that binds through theological covenant and presents itself as the way of escape.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Name a pattern — addiction, divorce, poverty, rage, mental illness, early death — that appears in multiple generations of your family. When did it start?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq6jccpf0001p9ahxwqhjunv	cmq6612ug0001geo0aum7jawk	Quiz — Part I: The Nature and Origin of Angels	QUIZ	\N	6	\N	t	## Quiz — Part I: The Nature and Origin of Angels\n\n*Review your understanding of the first four lessons and their supplements. Read each question, form your answer, then check the explanation below.*\n\n---\n\n### Question 1\n\n**What does it mean to say that angels are "pure spirits"? What does this tell us about how they relate to the material world?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nAngels have no physical body and no material component. They are intellect and will without matter. This means they do not occupy physical space as bodies do, do not experience physical hunger or fatigue, and do not perceive the world through senses. When they interact with the material world — appearing to humans, speaking, acting — they do so by producing effects in matter while remaining themselves incorporeal. This also means each angel is its own species: without matter to individuate them, two angels cannot be "the same kind" of thing in the way two humans can.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 2\n\n**Scripture presents the "Angel of the Lord" appearing in many contexts in the Old Testament. What are two different interpretations the Church tradition holds about who this figure is?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nOne tradition, especially prevalent in the patristic period, reads many "Angel of the Lord" appearances as pre-Incarnate appearances of the Second Person of the Trinity — Christ before the Incarnation. Evidence includes the divine speech in the first person, worship being accepted, and the figures being identified with God Himself (e.g., the burning bush). A second tradition treats the Angel of the Lord as a very high-ranking angelic being who speaks with divine authority because he fully represents and carries God's word. Both readings are within the range of orthodox interpretation; neither is defined doctrine.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 3\n\n**Explain the concept of "infused knowledge" in angels. How does this differ from how human beings acquire knowledge?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nHuman beings acquire knowledge by a process that moves from sense experience → abstraction → understanding → judgment. We learn by gathering data from the physical world and building up our understanding over time. Angels have no senses and no developmental process. Their knowledge was infused — given directly — at the moment of their creation. They know the natures of things, the structure of creation, and (by God's gift) supernatural truths not by discovering them but because they were given this knowledge instantaneously and completely. Their understanding does not grow or change by experience in the way ours does.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 4\n\n**Thomas Aquinas teaches that the angels were created and confirmed in grace in a single moment. What does "confirmed in grace" mean, and why does it matter?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\n"Confirmed in grace" means that the faithful angels, having made their definitive choice for God, cannot now sin or fall. Their will is now permanently ordered toward God. This is not a limitation but a perfection — they have achieved the full freedom that comes from complete union with the Good. It matters because it means the angels who serve us now are absolutely reliable. Their love is not contingent on mood or temptation. The guardian angel at your side has been serving without failure for the entire span of your life, and will continue to do so.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 5\n\n**Looking across the biblical survey of angelic appearances (Lesson 4), identify the five consistent "movements" of angelic Scripture. Give one biblical example for any two of them.**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThe five movements are: (1) **Worship first** — before any mission, angels praise God. Example: Job 38:7, the morning stars/sons of God shouting for joy at creation. (2) **Guard the sacred** — Example: Genesis 3:24, the Cherubim placed at the east of Eden. (3) **Announce the new** — Example: Luke 1:26-38, Gabriel's Annunciation to Mary. (4) **Minister to the vulnerable** — Example: 1 Kings 19:5-7, the angel feeding the exhausted Elijah. (5) **Interpret the mysterious** — Example: Daniel 8:16, Gabriel explaining the vision of the ram and goat to Daniel.\n\n</details>	\N	\N	\N
cmq6jccpr0005p9ahyptu3zw8	cmq6612ve000tgeo0b9n1d4af	Quiz — Part III: The Second Hierarchy	QUIZ	\N	4	\N	t	## Quiz — Part III: The Second Hierarchy: Governing Creation\n\n*Five questions covering Lessons 9–10 and Supplements 5–6. Think through each answer before reading.*\n\n---\n\n### Question 1\n\n**Describe the specific function of the Dominations within the angelic hierarchy. How do they relate to the first hierarchy above them and the Virtues below them?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThe Dominations are the executive layer of God's governance of creation. They receive the light of the first hierarchy — the burning love, profound wisdom, and stable authority of the Seraphim, Cherubim, and Thrones — and translate it into the orders that direct the lower choirs. They do not themselves go and act in the physical world directly; they direct. They set in motion. They distribute the blueprint of divine providence to the Virtues who implement it. The Dominations are served; they do not serve in the way the lower choirs serve. Their dignity consists in real authority: they have been given governance over all the choirs below them within the proper order.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 2\n\n**What is the difference between "ordinary" and "extraordinary" work of the Virtues? How does this understanding reframe what a miracle is?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThe Virtues' *ordinary* work is the consistent sustaining of physical law — every rotation of the earth, every heartbeat, every law of chemistry and physics operating as expected. Their *extraordinary* work is miracles: special operations of the same power directed by God to override the ordinary course of nature for a specific divine purpose. This reframes miracles entirely: a miracle is not a "break" in the laws of nature, as if God or angels had to smash through their own creation. It is the same power that sustains natural law, used in an extraordinary way, to make God's presence and purpose unmistakably visible at a particular moment. The Virtues do not experience miracles as contradiction; they experience them as one more act of obedience.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 3\n\n**Romans 8:38-39 lists "powers" as one of the potential separators from the love of God — and then immediately dismisses the threat. What is the theological significance of this?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nPaul names the Powers — real angelic beings with real authority in the cosmic order — and then places them subordinate to one thing: the love of God in Christ Jesus. This is not a small claim. It is the entire ordering of the cosmos placed under one supreme fact. The Powers maintain the structure of creation; they are genuine authorities. But they cannot undo what God has done in Christ. The love of God for the redeemed outranks every cosmic power, visible or invisible. For the believer, this means that no force in the structure of the universe — however vast, however ancient — stands between you and God. The cosmos is ordered, and the one supreme fact of that order is your redemption.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 4\n\n**Explain the difference between what the Principalities govern and what guardian angels govern. Why does this distinction matter for understanding God's economy of care?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThe Principalities govern *collective human organization* — nations, peoples, civilizations, and ecclesial structures. Their domain is the group, the centuries-long arc of a civilization or religious movement. Guardian angels, by contrast, govern *individuals* — one person, specifically, for the whole of their life. The distinction matters because it shows God's care operating at every scale simultaneously. The macro (civilizations, history, the Church as a whole) is administered by Principalities; the micro (you, your name, your specific life) is administered by a guardian angel. God is not choosing between governance-at-scale and governance-of-persons. He does both, through a hierarchy designed for exactly that purpose.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 5\n\n**What does Daniel 10 reveal about the Principalities and the spiritual dimension of political history?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nIn Daniel 10, Gabriel explains to Daniel that his prayer was delayed for twenty-one days because "the prince of the kingdom of Persia" withstood him — and that Michael had to come and help break through. This reveals that the rise and fall of empires, the political structures of nations, have a corresponding spiritual dimension: angelic (or demonic) Principalities governing the spiritual direction of those nations. The "prince of Persia" is apparently a demonic Principality governing that empire. Gabriel — an archangel of the highest distinction — was opposed for three weeks and needed Michael's intervention. This is a window into political history that the secular historian does not see: behind the armies and economies and diplomacy, there is a warfare at the level of the Principalities, within the sovereign plan of God.\n\n</details>	\N	\N	\N
cmq6jccpp0003p9ahk5a8nwm4	cmq6612v0000fgeo0goukqfcs	Quiz — Part II: The First Hierarchy	QUIZ	\N	6	\N	t	## Quiz — Part II: The First Hierarchy: Before the Throne of God\n\n*Five questions covering Lessons 5–8 and Supplement 4. Form your answer before reading each explanation.*\n\n---\n\n### Question 1\n\n**What does the triple "Holy, holy, holy" cry of the Seraphim (Isaiah 6:3) signify, and why is it placed at the center of Christian liturgy?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThe triple repetition (*hagios, hagios, hagios* in Greek; *qadosh, qadosh, qadosh* in Hebrew) is the Hebrew superlative — it means "the most holy, utterly and completely holy, beyond all comparison." The cry declares that God is wholly unlike everything else that exists: not merely a better version of created goodness but categorically different, transcendent, the source of all being. It is placed at the center of the Eucharistic prayer (*Sanctus*) because the Mass is understood as an earthly participation in the heavenly liturgy already ongoing before the throne. When the congregation sings the Sanctus, they are joining a choir that has not stopped since the first moment of creation.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 2\n\n**The Cherubim are consistently associated with guardianship of the divine presence. Give three biblical locations where Cherubim stand guard and identify what each guards.**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\n(1) **The east gate of Eden** (Genesis 3:24) — guarding the way to the Tree of Life after the Fall. (2) **The Ark of the Covenant** (Exodus 25:22) — two golden Cherubim atop the mercy seat, flanking the earthly throne of God; the meeting place of heaven and earth. (3) **The heavenly throne-chariot** (*merkabah*, Ezekiel 1) — the four living creatures who bear the divine chariot-throne through the cosmos. (Bonus: Revelation 4–5 — the living creatures around the heavenly throne, leading the eternal worship of the Lamb.)\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 3\n\n**What does the name "Thrones" reveal about the defining quality of this angelic choir? How does their function differ from the Seraphim and Cherubim?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThe name *thronoi* (throne, seat of authority) reveals that the Thrones' defining quality is the stable, judicial, immoveable authority of God. A throne in the ancient world declared: *this will not change.* The Seraphim embody burning love — their identity is pure desire for God and ceaseless adoration. The Cherubim embody fullness of knowledge and guardianship. The Thrones embody *stability and sovereignty* — they contemplate the whole of God's providential plan as a unified, unfailing judicial act. While the Seraphim burn and the Cherubim guard, the Thrones *hold* — they are the living expression of the fact that God's sovereignty has never, not for one moment, wavered.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 4\n\n**Describe the vision of the Living Creatures in Revelation 4–5 and explain how it relates to Ezekiel's chariot-throne vision (Ezekiel 1).**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nIn Revelation 4, John sees four living creatures (*zoa*) placed "in the midst of the throne and around the throne," each with four faces (lion, ox, man, eagle), six wings, and eyes within and around. They cry "Holy, holy, holy, is the Lord God Almighty" without ceasing. This vision directly echoes Ezekiel 1, where four living creatures with the same four faces bear the divine chariot-throne, also called the *merkabah*. John's vision appears to synthesize the Seraphim of Isaiah 6 (six wings, ceaseless triple-holy) with the Cherubim of Ezekiel (four faces, bearing the throne). Theologians generally read the Revelation living creatures as a composite image of the first hierarchy's angelic worship, representing all the throne-room angelic beings in a single overwhelming vision.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 5\n\n**Lesson 7 opens with the Sennacherib incident (Isaiah 37:36). In your own words, explain what theological point this historical event illustrates about the Thrones and angelic power.**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThe angel who struck down 185,000 Assyrian soldiers in a single night demonstrates, in a concrete historical event, what the theological doctrine of the Thrones describes in the abstract: the authority of God is not passive, abstract, or distant. It is active, precise, and overwhelming in its application. Sennacherib mocked the throne of God; the Thrones embody the reality that such mockery cannot stand. The event also shows that angelic authority is not self-directed — the angel acted in response to Hezekiah's prayer, within God's specific will. The Thrones do not exercise authority for themselves; they manifest God's sovereign judgment in history at the moment God commands it.\n\n</details>	\N	\N	\N
cmq6jccpt0009p9ah2izmgyyl	cmq6612vy001hgeo0djva1vnw	Quiz — Part V: Angels in the Life of the Believer	QUIZ	\N	7	\N	t	## Quiz — Part V: Angels in the Life of the Believer\n\n*Final course quiz — five questions covering Lessons 15–18 and all final supplements. This is the capstone of the Angels course.*\n\n---\n\n### Question 1\n\n**The Church teaches that every human being, without exception, has a guardian angel. On what scriptural basis does she teach this? Give at least two texts.**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\n(1) **Matthew 18:10** — "See that you do not despise one of these little ones. For I tell you that in heaven their angels always see the face of my Father who is in heaven." Jesus explicitly attributes personal angels to "the little ones" — and by extension, to all who belong to the Kingdom. (2) **Psalm 91:11-12** — "For he will command his angels concerning you to guard you in all your ways; they will lift you up in their hands, so that you will not strike your foot against a stone." (3) **Hebrews 1:14** — "Are they not all ministering spirits sent out to serve for the sake of those who are to inherit salvation?" The angels are described as servants sent to serve the heirs of salvation — the entire people of God.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 2\n\n**How does Hebrews 12:22-23 understand what happens when Christians gather for worship? What does this say about the relationship between earthly liturgy and the angels?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nHebrews 12:22-23 describes Christian worship as a present, real entry into the heavenly Jerusalem: "You have come to Mount Zion and to the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem, and to innumerable angels in festal gathering, and to the assembly of the firstborn who are enrolled in heaven, and to God, the judge of all." This means Christian worship is not a human gathering that angels observe. It is a human gathering that joins what the angels are already doing. Every time the Church worships — in a cathedral or a house church — she is present in the heavenly throne room, surrounded by the angels in their eternal *festal gathering*. You have never gone to church alone.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 3\n\n**Revelation 8:3-4 describes an angel offering the prayers of all the saints before God's throne. What is the theological significance of this image for Christian prayer?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThe image declares that human prayers do not dissipate into silence when they are spoken. They are gathered — *all* of them, from the first human prayer to the last before the end — and carried before the throne of God by a personal being acting in loving obedience. This means no prayer is lost. The prayer you offered in your car this morning, the prayer you murmured half-asleep last night, the prayer you offered in childhood with your eyes closed tight — all of it gathered, offered, presented before God from the hand of an angel. Prayer is not a monologue thrown into the void. It is a word spoken to a God who has appointed a messenger to carry it directly to His throne.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 4\n\n**The Angels course included Lesson 4's note about the "shadow side of the story" — the fallen angels. How should awareness of the demonic dimension of the angelic world shape how we relate to the holy angels?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nAwareness of the fallen angels should intensify, not complicate, relationship with the holy angels in three ways: (1) **Gratitude** — the angels who remain faithful have chosen to remain so; their love for God and for us is not the result of incapacity to fall but of the perfection of their free choice. This makes their loyalty more, not less, meaningful. (2) **Realism** — the world is not a neutral space; there is an ongoing spiritual conflict in which both the faithful angels and the fallen ones are active. The guardian angel who accompanies you is accompanying you through a field with active opposition. (3) **Intercession** — the Church prays to Michael specifically because the warfare is real. Devotion to the holy angels is not pietistic decoration; it is participation in an actual covenant of protection in the context of actual spiritual conflict.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 5\n\n**This course began with the claim: "Right now, as you read this, a being of pure intelligence that has existed since before the first star was formed is present with you." After eighteen lessons, give the fullest description you can of who that being is.**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nA complete answer would include: The being is a pure spirit, created instantaneously by God before or at the moment of creation, confirmed in grace and therefore incapable of sin. It belongs to the ninth and final choir of a nine-choir hierarchy, the Angels, who are closest to human beings and most directly involved in individual human lives. It is its own species — there is no other angel of its exact kind in existence. Its knowledge was infused at the moment of its creation: it knows the structure of creation, the nature of souls, the spiritual realities you cannot perceive, and the specific shape of your life. It has accompanied you from before your birth and will be present with you at the moment of your death. Its number you do not know, its face you have not seen, and its name you may learn when you see it. It worships God without ceasing and serves you without complaint. It has never failed its commission and never will. It is standing beside you right now.\n\n</details>	\N	\N	\N
cmq6jccps0007p9ahirwml0ro	cmq6612vm0013geo0kqjj27k2	Quiz — Part IV: The Third Hierarchy	QUIZ	\N	6	\N	t	## Quiz — Part IV: The Third Hierarchy: Ministers of Salvation\n\n*Five questions covering Lessons 11–14 and Supplements 7–8.*\n\n---\n\n### Question 1\n\n**What are the three archangels named in Scripture? Give each one's name, the meaning of that name, and the specific mission for which they appear in the Bible.**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\n**Michael** — "Who is like God?" (a rhetorical challenge, not a question). Appears in Daniel 10 and 12 as the great prince protecting God's covenant people; in Jude 9 disputing with the devil over Moses' body; in Revelation 12 leading the heavenly army against the dragon. His mission: warfare and protection of the elect.\n\n**Gabriel** — "God is my strength" or "Man of God." Appears in Daniel 8 and 9 to explain prophetic visions; in Luke 1 to announce the birth of John to Zechariah and the Incarnation to Mary. His mission: announcement and explanation of God's plans at decisive moments.\n\n**Raphael** — "God heals." Appears in Tobit as the companion and healer who accompanies Tobias on his journey, drives away the demon Asmodeus, and heals Tobit's blindness. His mission: healing, guidance, and the companionship of those in need.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 2\n\n**The prayer of Michael ends: "By the power of God, thrust into hell Satan and all evil spirits who wander through the world seeking the ruin of souls." What theological picture of Michael does this prayer presuppose, and where in Scripture does this picture come from?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThe prayer presupposes Michael as the appointed warrior-Principality of God's covenant people, whose specific commission includes direct opposition to Satan and the demonic host. The picture comes from: (1) Daniel 10 and 12, where Michael fights the demonic princes governing nations and is named "the great prince who has charge of your people"; (2) Jude 9, where Michael disputes with the devil over Moses' body — even in dispute, invoking God's authority rather than his own; (3) Revelation 12:7-9, where Michael and his angels fight the dragon in heaven and cast him to the earth. The prayer is not invented piety; it is a direct petition to the being whose scriptural commission is precisely what the prayer describes.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 3\n\n**The Annunciation (Luke 1:26-38) is Gabriel's central appearance in the New Testament. What does the scene reveal about how God uses angelic messengers? What is Mary's role, and why does it matter?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThe scene reveals that God entrusts the announcement of the most important event in history — the Incarnation of the Son of God — to a created messenger. Gabriel does not simply transmit a divine fiat; he asks Mary's consent: "How will this be?" She questions, he explains, and she then gives her *fiat*: "Let it be to me according to your word." Her role matters because the Incarnation required the free cooperation of a human being. God did not override Mary's freedom. He sent Gabriel to ask, explain, and receive her yes. The whole history of redemption turns on that free human response. Gabriel's mission is not complete until Mary speaks.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 4\n\n**How does the Book of Tobit (Raphael's story) serve as a model for the ministry of guardian angels, even though the guardian angel theology is technically separate from archangel theology?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nRaphael's ministry to Tobias in the Book of Tobit is a concrete, narrative picture of the four things guardian angels do for the individuals assigned to them: (1) **Accompaniment** — Raphael walks with Tobias through the entire journey, present at every step. (2) **Guidance** — he knows where to go, what fish organs to use, how to approach Raguel's household. (3) **Protection** — he binds the demon Asmodeus who had killed Sarah's previous husbands. (4) **Healing** — he instructs Tobias in how to heal his father's blindness. Each of these is a specific form of the ministry the tradition ascribes to guardian angels for every human being. The archangel's mission to Tobias is an *emblematic* version of what angels do for individuals, even though Raphael's scale and nature exceed a typical guardian.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Question 5\n\n**What does it mean that "the number of angels equals the number of species, and the number of species equals the number of individual angels"? Why did Thomas teach this, and what does it imply about your guardian angel?**\n\n<details>\n<summary>See Answer</summary>\n\nThomas reasoned that in the material world, a species is a kind (e.g., *human*), and individuals of a species are distinguished by matter — this human, not that one. Angels have no matter. Therefore there is nothing to distinguish two angels of the "same kind" — so each angel *is* its own kind. No two angels are the same species; there are as many species as there are individual angels. The tradition places the number of angels as extraordinarily large — "ten thousand times ten thousand" (Daniel 7:10). What this implies about your guardian angel: the being at your side is not a generic representative of "the angel type." It is a unique species of created intelligence — a being unlike any other that exists — assigned to you specifically. Your angel is, in the most literal theological sense, one of a kind.\n\n</details>	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xoof000d80716wo8uaic	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Halloween	READING	\N	1	\N	t	![Halloween](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsVDGI08931DSEv9r4BQbmhHPx2ALYz3ynujqd)\n\n## Halloween\n\nShe put the argument together carefully because she expected resistance. She told her children's pastor that Halloween was just cultural, not spiritual — that it was pumpkins and costumes and candy, that the kids were not thinking about the occult, that refusing to participate would isolate her children from their neighborhood. She said most Christians she knew let their kids participate. She said the church's "Harvest Festival" was just Halloween with better lighting.\n\nThe pastor listened. He said: "You're right that most children are not thinking about the occult. The question is whether the enemy requires their conscious participation to benefit from the night."\n\nShe did not have a ready answer.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nHalloween is the modern commercial descendant of Samhain — the Celtic festival of the dead observed on October 31, the night believed to be when the boundary between the living and the dead thinned to its annual minimum. Bonfires were lit to guide wandering spirits. Costumes were worn to confuse or appease them. Offerings were left at doorsteps.\n\nThe "All Saints" framing added by medieval Christianity represents an attempt to Christianize a pagan festival that was never fully baptized — the same syncretism problem that appears throughout church history when pagan celebrations were adopted and renamed rather than replaced.\n\nToday, Halloween generates approximately $12 billion in annual U.S. retail spending, including costumes, candy, and decorations that explicitly feature death, demons, witches, and occult imagery. It is the enemy's highest calendar day — the night when witchcraft rituals are performed openly, when occult activity peaks, and when the spiritual atmosphere in Western culture most closely resembles what Samhain was designed to produce.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe deception is the trivializaton. Pumpkins are not spiritually dangerous. Orange candy corn is not spiritually dangerous. But Halloween is not about pumpkins — it is a cultural covenant with the spiritual atmosphere of the enemy's most celebrated night.\n\n[Ephesians 5:11](data-scripture="Ephesians 5:11"): *"Have no fellowship with the unfruitful works of darkness, but rather reprove them."* The word *fellowship* — Greek *synkoinōneō* — means shared participation. Shared participation in the cultural celebration of the night that the demonic world marks as its highest festival is not spiritually neutral regardless of personal intent.\n\nThe costume dimension is worth specific examination. Dressing as demons, witches, warlocks, and death figures is a form of identification with those entities. In many spiritual traditions across multiple cultures, wearing the costume of an entity was understood as invoking that entity's presence and character. The Western secularization of costume play does not change the spiritual architecture of that act.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Covenant by participation** does not require conscious intent. When Israel mixed with the nations at their festivals, the spiritual contamination was real regardless of individual Israelites' intentions. The biblical principle is repeated throughout the Prophets: participation creates identification, and identification creates covenant.\n\n**Desensitization is the long-term damage.** Halloween trains children — over years — to find death, the occult, and demonic imagery entertaining, aesthetically appealing, and identity-expressive. The child who spends twelve years of Halloweens immersed in occult imagery is not spiritually unaffected. Their conscience has been trained to experience what Scripture calls abomination as fun.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThe alternative to Halloween is not isolation. It is deliberate replacement — filling the night with light, celebration, community, and the explicit honoring of God. A neighborhood gathering that celebrates the harvest, the goodness of God, and the community itself is both more genuinely festive and spiritually sound.\n\nThe question is whether you are willing to be in your neighborhood the one family that does something different, and to explain why graciously when asked. That willingness is itself a form of the reproof [Ephesians 5:11](data-scripture="Ephesians 5:11") commands.\n\n---\n\n*The veil grew thin one night a year. The next lesson examines what happens when the entertainment industry keeps it open permanently.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Where did you first encounter Halloween growing up — and was the spiritual dimension ever discussed by your church or family?*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk4bq0022ewhjd4x8a334	cmnknk4bp001qewhjk5bcqnfj	Supplement 22 — For Lessons 43 & 44	SUPPLEMENT	2569	11	\N	t	The Rapture could happen at any moment — and Matthew 24-25 tells us exactly what the signs will look like for those who are left behind. This supplement helps you hold both truths simultaneously: imminence (the Rapture is always near) and readiness (the signs of the end are identifiable).\n\nMany preachers continually declare to their congregations that such is the will of God. They're told this kind of experience must be God's will in order to keep them saved and train them in Christian graces.\n\n![Supplement 22 — For Lessons 43 & 44](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsQcPILuhQWkP21SLEA3tZrcs70u6UjOq5zopY)\n\n## Of What Christian Sufferings Consist\n\nPreachers give various reasons to prove their claim that the sufferings mentioned above must be God's will—otherwise, He wouldn't have allowed them. One preacher writes, "Our trials are not accidents which have come into our lives, neither are they calamities which will ruin us. Our trials are our opportunities from which we learn many lessons which better prepare us for the service of God... No Christian is exempt from trials."\n\nThis teaching is perfectly fine if applied to ordinary tests of faith, persecutions, suffering injustices for the cause of Christ, or simply because we live in a fallen world where ungodly people cause the godly to suffer in the course of life. But if this teaching is used to suggest that Christians must suffer sin, sickness, and pain as being God's will—that they must live in poverty to keep their salvation, or suffer failure in business—then such an argument is completely wrong.\n\nThe preacher mentioned above offers proof that Christians must suffer sicknesses and other afflictions because Abraham was tested to offer up Isaac (Gen. 22), Joseph was tested when he was put in prison for no personal wrongdoings (Gen. 39-41), and Paul suffered beatings, buffeting, dangers, perils, slander, distresses, hungers, nakedness, stonings, imprisonments, and shipwrecks.\n\nAs we've said before, if preachers would limit their doctrine to these kinds of sufferings and trials and not include sickness, sin, and failure in life—things Christ died to deliver us from here and now—there would be some truth to their doctrine of suffering for Christians.\n\nNaturally, God did test Abraham to see if he would withhold Isaac from Him, and there's no doubt God will test every Christian in this respect to learn whether they'll submit to Him completely or not. It's true that Joseph suffered wrongfully, but this doesn't mean every Christian will go to jail sometime in their life. This doesn't mean God sent Joseph to jail to teach him lessons.\n\nGod did not send Joseph to jail at all. Wicked men caused this, but since it happened, God used it as a means of exalting Joseph. He could and would have exalted him otherwise if Joseph had never seen a jail.\n\nIt's also true that Paul suffered because of wicked men seeking to eradicate the gospel, but this doesn't mean God sent every trial upon Paul. God was not responsible for one stone thrown at Paul, nor for one stripe laid upon him. He did not directly send or will for such things to happen to Paul. God knew the first pioneers of Christianity would suffer, and He selected Paul because he had qualities that would go through any kind of suffering for the sake of the gospel and still remain true to God.\n\n## God Does Not Send Sufferings\n\nGod uses all trials to teach us lessons, and He can turn our trials into great blessings for us and others. But this doesn't mean God sends the trials just to teach these lessons or to make us a blessing through such sufferings.\n\nThink of it like this: If my son gets into trouble by committing sin or by being wrongfully accused, it's my duty to come to his rescue and help him out of trouble. Whether or not he sinned or is to blame is irrelevant—it's still my duty to teach him certain lessons and help him become a better man by helping him through his trouble. Without tribulations, some lessons might not have been learned. But it would be foolish to say I was responsible for getting him into these troubles just to teach him these lessons. That would be unjust, ungodly, and unlike a true parent.\n\nSo it is with God. He is never guilty of causing any of His children to get in jail, be stoned, beaten with rods, shipwrecked, defamed, hungry, thirsty, naked, sick, poverty-stricken, or suffer failure of any kind just to teach them certain lessons.\n\nThe lesson we must learn from Scripture is that God is not the direct cause of such suffering. He will stand by us and help us out of our troubles, regardless of how we got there. Or, as in the case of Stephen, James, and others, He will take us to eternal glory should we suffer death for the cause of Christ on Earth.\n\n## We Must Use Common Sense\n\nThere are certain sufferings among Christians that are needless, and there are certain sufferings all will go through for the gospel. There are also certain sufferings some will go through for the sake of the gospel that others will never have to face for Christ and their faith.\n\nThere are certain sufferings that people in some countries and certain periods must endure that people in other countries—even in the same periods—won't suffer. For example, early Christians had to go through persecutions in many periods before Christianity was accepted. Today in America, Christians don't have to suffer for the gospel like the early believers did. In Russia and other lands where Christianity is rejected, people suffer certain persecutions we in this country don't face.\n\nTherefore, God is not the cause of sufferings for Christians in any age—much less sufferings in one land and not another, or in one period and not another. The sufferings in various lands and periods have depended on whether wicked men controlled the government and whether they intended to do away with Christianity. Clearly, sufferings of this kind depend on circumstances in these various countries at different times.\n\n## Christians Often Suffer Needlessly\n\nThere are certain sufferings no Christian needs to go through in any land at any time. A Christian doesn't have to live in sin and suffer for their own wrongdoing at any time or place. If they do live in sin, they're no longer a Christian, as we saw in Lesson Thirty-five. If someone has never been saved from their sins, they've never been a Christian.\n\nA Christian doesn't have to suffer sickness—Christ died to take it away, as we saw in Lesson Fourteen. They don't have to suffer failure in business if they live in a land of equal opportunity, for they can have assurance that God will prosper their business.\n\nWhy? Because they have hundreds of promises that sinners don't have. They have God and His help that sinners don't have. They can know and practice the laws of prosperity as much as sinners—and they have the advantage of God's blessings on their business that sinners cannot claim.\n\nA Christian doesn't have to tolerate bad habits and be defeated in life when God's Word promises deliverance. Thus, it's clear that needless sufferings are not God's will. If any Christian goes through them, it's because of their ignorance and failure to appropriate the benefits of God's promises.\n\n## Why Christians Suffer Needlessly\n\nAs we've seen above, no Christian has to suffer sin, bad habits, sickness, or submit to poverty, failure in business, or failure in getting answers to prayers. If they do suffer these things, naturally there's a cause—but that cause is not God.\n\nThey suffer because of ignorance in not studying the Bible, or failing to understand the truths of the gospel they've read. They suffer because they've been taught wrong, because they refuse to accept the truth, because they don't have faith, because they don't get down to business in rebuking the devil, or because they tolerate these conditions in their own lives.\n\nThey suffer needlessly if they fail to seek the truth and walk in it exactly as they find it in the plain Word of God. God will honor anyone who honors Him. He will meet every person according to their faith—that's the law of divine operation.\n\nHe will permit anyone and everyone to go without the benefits of His promises if they're careless and indifferent about them. You must not only know the truth mentally—you must act upon it before it will make you free.\n\n## Truth Concerning Suffering Made Clear\n\nTo teach that the sufferings and trials of Christians include the needless sufferings mentioned above is entirely unscriptural. When the Bible states that all Christians must suffer, go through tribulation, and undergo certain tests of faith, this doesn't mean it's God's will for them to suffer needlessly with things He has promised to deliver them from.\n\nYou can be an example and comfort to others without going through needless suffering. You can partake of God's holiness, grace, and power—and even of the sufferings of Christ—without suffering sin, sickness, and defeat. You can win more souls to Christ, witness better for Him, be a better example of the gospel, glorify God better, and demonstrate that you are more than a conqueror through Christ by living free from sin, sickness, pain, poverty, and failure—far better than by suffering defeat along these lines.\n\nYou can better promote the progress of the gospel by enjoying its benefits than by living in constant defeat before the very people you're seeking to save.\n\nChristians can be settled, established, and strengthened in the faith more by resisting needless sufferings than by giving in to the devil and demons who seek to rob them of the benefits of their faith. You can learn patience, obedience, trust, and faith in God more by resisting demons and temptations than by giving in and being defeated.\n\nLet us repeat: Christians do not have to live in sin, be sick, and be defeated in life in order to learn sympathy, love, and patience to help others. There will be plenty of opportunities to exercise faith, patience, sympathy, love, compassion, sincerity, grace, and Christian power—without needlessly suffering the things Jesus bore in His own body to deliver us from and over which God promises to give us victory.\n\n## Job's Experience No Excuse for Christians to Live in Defeat\n\nThousands of sick and defeated Christians use Job and his sufferings as the divine pattern for all people to be content in sickness and calamity. They use him as an excuse to continue in defeat and unbelief. They oppose God's Word and contend that they must be in God's will—special subjects of His grace—when in times of sickness, pain, or business failure.\n\nThey miss altogether the true teachings of Job's experience. God never intended anyone to use Job's case for any such purpose. God intended all people to see how He is glorified—not in sickness and calamity, but in deliverance from them.\n\nWhen the inspired writer used Job as an example, it wasn't to encourage the belief that it's God's will for a person to remain sick or tolerate sin, sickness, and financial defeat as being sent by God. On the contrary, Job illustrates failure to receive from God those things Christ died to deliver him from—things God promised to keep us from, provided we meet certain conditions.\n\nJob was used as an example of patience and deliverance. In Jas. 5, the writer predicted labor troubles in the last days and how rich men would face calamities because of their oppression of the poor (Jas. 5:1-6). James then advised Christians to be patient in such times, for the coming of the Lord draws near (Jas. 5:7-9). He stated that the prophets were examples of suffering affliction and of patience (Jas. 5:10).\n\nThe suffering of the prophets was not primarily sickness and disease, as can be seen in Heb. 11:4, 7, 19, 23-39. Not one example of sickness is given in all the list of sufferings in these passages. They were afflicted with wars and persecutions by the ungodly—but not with sickness. Job is the only example given concerning physical diseases among the prophets (Jas. 5:10-11).\n\nNaturally, God wants everyone to be patient in sickness as well as in other troubles. But this is no excuse to accept sickness as God's will or as being sent from Him. This is no excuse to make up our minds to remain sick and give in to the devil's attacks. Such attacks should never be accepted as God's work or as being sent from Him.\n\nThe sufferings Job endured were not sent by God—they were from the devil himself. It's true God permitted these things, just as He will permit anyone today to be attacked by Satan. But God's permission is not the same as the devil's attack. God will even permit someone to commit suicide, but this is not His will and He is not the cause of it.\n\nGod permits saints today to become sick and even die because they won't appropriate the benefits of the gospel and get healed (1 Cor. 11:29-30). In other words, Satan is free to attack people who will tolerate such attacks and who will permit him to do so. His works are manifest in the bodies of many Christians simply because they don't know his devices and because they won't rebuke the devil and get victory over him by the name of Jesus Christ.\n\nGod has made provision whereby every believer can ward off such attacks, get healed immediately, stay healed, and remain free from Satan and his works. But if you don't fight him and believe you're delivered from his works, you'll have to suffer. God longs to help, but He will not act contrary to His Word.\n\n## Job Teaches Many Lessons to Modern Saints\n\nThe following lessons can and should be learned by all modern believers. We should profit by Job's experience and determine to intelligently act to defeat Satan in our lives and get deliverance according to our needs. Note these lessons from Job's experience:\n\n> 1. Satan is the author of sickness and disease (Job 2:7; Acts 10:38).\n\n> 2. Satan causes calamities to come to men (Job 1:6-22; Rev. 12:9).\n\n> 3. Satan is the accuser of the righteous (Job 1:6-12; 2:1-8; Rev. 12:10).\n\n> 4. Satan is permitted to go only so far in testing God's people (Job 1:12; 2:6; 1 Cor. 10:12-13; 1 Pet. 5:8-9).\n\n> 5. God does permit Satan to test His own people (Job 1:6-12; 2:1-8; Lk. 22:31-34; 1 Pet. 5:8-9).\n\n> 6. Satan has access to God's throne (Job 1:6-12; 2:1-8; Rev. 12:10).\n\n> 7. Satan has many helpers in disguise (Job 1:6-22; 2 Cor. 11:13-14; Rev. 12:7-12).\n\n> 8. God will not utterly forsake the righteous in times of trial (Job 42:1-17; Ps. 34:6; 37:23-24; 2 Cor. 4:8-12; 6:5-10; Jas. 5:10-11).\n\n> 9. God is the deliverer of His people in sickness and trouble (Job 42; Jas. 5:10-11; Acts 10:38; Jn. 10:10; 1 Cor. 10:12-13).\n\n> 10. God always delivers those whom Satan is permitted to attack for the purpose of testing (Job 42; Jas. 5:10-11; Ps. 91:1-12; 103:1-4).\n\n> 11. God uses troubles to purify and refine men just like any father would use any trouble his child got into to help him be a better man (Job 33:14-30).\n\n> 12. God is not the cause of the trouble any more than a wise and righteous earthly parent would be, but since men are attacked by Satan He works it out to their best good if they will simply turn to Him for help and deliverance (Job 42; Ps. 34:6-19; 37:1-10; Heb. 11:6; Jas. 1:5-8).\n\n> 13. God is not to be judged concerning His acts (Job 2:10; 1 Cor. 13:12-13).\n\n> 14. Men must learn that cooperating with God is His method of deliverance (Job 33:14-30; Jas. 4:7; 1 Pet. 5:8-9; Acts 10:38; Jas. 5:10-16).\n\n> 15. God is greater than all and can and will deliver from any power that afflicts His people (Job 42; Jn. 10:10; Acts 10:38; Lk. 13:14; Ps. 103:1-4).\n\n> 16. Man is frail and helpless in himself to defeat Satan (Job 1:6-22; 2:1-10; Eph 6:10-18; 2 Cor. 10:4-7; Rev. 12:10-11; Jas. 4:7; 1 Pet. 5:8-9).\n\n> 17. Man should depend upon God and have faith before he gets into trouble (Ps. 91; 2 Cor. 10:4-7; Eph. 6:10-18; Jas. 4:7; 1 Pet. 5:8-9).\n\n> 18. Sickness is not always experienced because of some personal sin (Job 1:1-12; 2:1-10; Jn. 9:1-3; Jas. 5:14-16).\n\n> 19. Man's friends are always ready to criticize, find fault and wrongly interpret divine providence in time of sickness or calamity (Job 4:1–37:24).\n\n> 20. Attacks of Satan are part of the destiny of the best Christians (Job 1:1-12; Eph. 6:10-18; Jn. 10:10; Jas. 4:7; 1 Pet. 5:8-9).\n\n> 21. Men must learn patience and trust in God (Jas. 5:10-11; Rom. 5:1-11).\n\n> 22. Men must learn to give thanks to God in trouble (Job 1:21; Phil. 4:6).\n\n> 23. Men under trial generally accuse God falsely of being responsible for the trouble (Job 42:3).\n\n> 24. Satan gets men to accuse God and blame Him for the devil's own works (Rev. 12:10).\n\n> 25. It is God's purpose and will to test men through the attacks of Satan (1 Cor. 10:12-13).\n\n> 26. God seeks to get glory by men remaining true to Him and by delivering them from the works of the devil (Jn. 10:10).\n\n> 27. Under test it is only natural to defend one's self, as did Job (Job 42:1-6).\n\n> 28. It does not pay to criticize those who are in trouble. God, and sometimes man, will make critics humble themselves before the ones they talked about (Job 42:7-9).\n\n> 29. It does not pay to find fault with God (Job 42:1-6; Gal. 6:7-8).\n\n> 30. Men must learn to trust God in sickness and calamity (Jas. 5:10-11).\n\n> 31. God does not always reveal Himself the very moment we pray, but He will answer if men have faith (Job 40:1-6; 42:1-6; Lk. 18:1-8).\n\n> 32. It does not pay to argue or to defend one's self in time of trouble (Job 40:1-6; 42:1-6; Ps. 37:1-9; 1 Pet. 4:12-19).\n\n> 33. The godly are always vindicated in the end and right always prevails in time (Job 42:1-17; Heb. 10:30-36; 1 Pet. 4:12-19).\n\n> 34. Even the best of men are weak and discouraged at times (Job 3).\n\n> 35. Seek to help and encourage men in trouble instead of condemning them (Job 13:1-4; 16:1-6; 19:3; 21:3; Mt. 7:1-5; Gal. 6:7-8).\n\n> 36. Riches and honor are insecure (Job 29:1–30:31).\n\n> 37. Satan is the adversary of God's people (Job 1:1-22; 2:1-12; Rev. 12:10).\n\n> 38. Trials and sicknesses should not cause men to backslide (Job 1:1-22; 2:1-12; 1 Cor. 10:12-13; Jas. 5:10-11; 1 Pet. 4:12-19).\n\n> 39. Bodily sickness need not affect the status of the soul (Job 2:1-12).\n\n> 40. Do not permit wives or husbands to discourage us or cause us to backslide (Job 2:1-12; 1 Cor. 7:15-17).\n\n> 41. Satan is sometimes given permission by God to cause storms (Job 1:6-22).\n\n> 42. Do not give your own theories in seeking to help others. Give the Bible and seek to be led of the Holy Spirit in all such cases (Job 42:7-9; 2 Tim. 3:15-17; 4:1-5).\n\n> 43. Let God deal with people who sin instead of constantly nagging them, as Job's friends did in his trial (Job 42:7-9; Gal. 6:7-8).\n\n> 44. Seek God when in trouble and do not blame or criticize Him as the source of the trouble (Job 13:15; Jas. 5:10-11).\n\n> 45. God's grace sustains us in the greatest calamities (Job 19:25-26; 42:1-17; 2 Cor. 12:1-12; Heb. 11; Jas. 5:10-11).\n\n> 46. Many counselors are not always right (Job 42:1-9).\n\n> 47. All the suffering that could be heaped upon a man who is down is not enough to satisfy self-righteous hypocrites or make them sympathetic to the suffering one (Job 42:7-9; Acts 7:54-60).\n\n> 48. God takes account of all criticism against His people (Job 42:7-9; Mt. 12:37).\n\n> 49. Troubles are no proof of a man's wickedness (Job 1:1-22; 2:1-12; 42:1-6).\n\n> 50. God is very compassionate and of tender mercy toward those who are in need (Jas. 5:10-11; Ps. 103:1-19; Rom. 8:32).\n\nThese and many other lessons can be learned from Job's experience. But to get from it the many fallacies taught today is regretful. God never intended anyone to use Job as the basis for any of the following theories:\n\n- That sickness is sent by God.\n\n- That pain, poverty, and failure is the will of God.\n\n- That children of God have to go through like experiences.\n\n- That sickness, pain, and calamity should be accepted as being sent by God.\n\n- That men should tolerate such conditions in their lives as being God's best or highest will.\n\n- That men have to go through such things in order to be kept humble and finally be saved in the end.\n\n- That men should not seek to get out of the will of God by refusing to accept these conditions as the best for them.\n\n- That men should passively accept such conditions in order to be examples of suffering for others and to demonstrate the grace of God in the lives of sufferers.\n\n- That such suffering glorifies God.\n\n- That this is the best way to develop character and win souls to Christ.\n\n- That such furthers the gospel and makes men humble and godly.\n\n- That such must be endured by all in order to be rewarded in the life to come.\n\nThese fallacies are all modern doctrines of the devil, and there's no excuse for anyone today to endure this kind of suffering in order to get the benefits listed above. These blessings can come without children of God being sick, full of pain, helpless, and defeated in life by the devil and demons. Children of God can learn lessons, become refined, purified, humbled, and made godly by other means than suffering like Job of old, as we'll see below.\n\n## Job's Great Mistake\n\nJob, like most Christians today, made the big mistake of blaming God for his suffering and trouble. This is clear from the following statements Job made while going through his trouble:\n\n"The Lord gave, and the Lord taketh away; blessed be the name of the Lord" (Job 1:21). "What? shall we receive good at the hand of God, and shall we not receive evil" (Job 2:10). "Why is light given to the man whose way is hid, and in whom God hath hedged in" (Job 3:23). "The arrows of the Almighty are within me, the poison whereof drinketh up my spirit: the terrors of God do set themselves in array against me" (Job 6:4).\n\n"I will speak in the anguish of my spirit; I will complain in the bitterness of my soul... thou [God] scarest me with dreams, and terrifiest me through visions: so that my soul chooseth strangling and death rather than life. I loathe it... What is man, that thou shouldst magnify him... and try him every moment?... Why hast thou set me as a mark against thee, so that I am a burden to myself? And why dost thou not pardon my transgression, and take away mine iniquity?" (Job 7:11-21).\n\n"For he breaketh me with tempest, and multiplieth my wounds without cause. He will not suffer me to take my breath, but filleth me with bitterness... He destroyeth the perfect and the wicked... Yet thou shalt plunge me into the ditch" (Job 9:17, 18, 22).\n\n"I will say unto God, do not condemn me; shew me wherefore thou contendest with me. Is it good for thee that thou shouldst oppress, that thou shouldst despise the work of thine hands, and shine upon the council of the wicked... thou dost destroy me... Hast thou not poured me out as milk, and curdled me like cheese?... Thou huntest me as a fierce lion.... Thou renewest thy witnesses against me, and increasest thine indignation upon me... cease then, and let me alone, that I may take comfort a little" (Job 10:2, 3, 8, 10, 16, 17).\n\n"The tabernacles of robbers prosper, and they that provoke God are secure; into whose hand God bringeth abundantly" (Job 12:6). "Withdraw thine hand far from me: and let not thy dread make me afraid... wherefore hidest thou thy face, and holdest me for thine enemy" (Job 13:21-24). "Thou destroyest the hope of man" (Job 14:19).\n\n"God hath delivered me to the ungodly, and turned me over into the hands of the wicked. I was at ease, but he hath broken me asunder: he hath also taken me by my neck, and shaken me to pieces, and set me up for his mark. His archers compass me round about, he cleaveth my reins asunder, and he doth not spare; he poureth out my gall upon the ground. He breaketh me with breach upon breach, he runneth upon me like a giant... Not for any injustice in my hands" (Job 16:11-17).\n\n"He hath made me also a byword of the people" (Job 17:6). "Know now that God hath overthrown me, and hath compassed me with his net. Behold, I cry out of wrong, but I am not heard: I cry aloud, but there is no judgment... He hath set darkness in my paths. He hath stripped me of my glory, and taken the crown of my head. He hath destroyed me on every side... He hath kindled his wrath against me, and he counteth me unto him as one of his enemies. He hath put my brethren far from me... the hand of God hath touched me" (Job 19:6-13, 21).\n\n"The Almighty troubleth me" (Job 23:16). "As God liveth, who hath taken away my judgment; and the Almighty, who hath vexed my soul" (Job 27:2). "He hath loosed my cord, and afflicted me... He hath cast me into the mire" (Job 30:11, 19).\n\nThese statements are from Job during his sufferings. They don't speak the truth any more than modern statements of people who accuse God of being the cause of their sicknesses, calamities, and failures.\n\nGod did not do even one of the above-mentioned things to a child of His—and He never will. It was the devil who afflicted Job, as plainly stated in Job 2:7. Not one of Job's statements above should be taken as true of God's dealings with His children. They were uttered by a man in great distress, causing him to have a wrong perception of God and His dealings with mankind.\n\nIt's no wonder that when God came to Job and rebuked him for these accusations, Job said, "Who is he that hideth council without knowledge? therefore have I uttered that I understood not; things too wonderful for me, which I knew not... Wherefore I abhor myself, and repent in dust and ashes" (Job 42:1-6).\n\nTo consider God as the cause of Job's miseries is to make Him the most unjust, inhuman, and unmerciful being one could conceive of. God's main purpose in recording Job's experience is to show people of all ages that He is not this kind of God—as the devil and many people constantly portray Him to be.\n\nUnfortunately, people have missed this all-important truth about Job. They've used his experience to magnify sickness as God's will, as caused by God, and as necessary for God's children to undergo in order to learn patience. They have completely missed the mark.\n\nGod did not take away Job's riches, kill his children, take away his health and position, or cause his wife and friends to become estranged from him. Job did not receive evil from God. God did not hedge him in, shoot him with His arrows, poison him, send him terrors, scare him with dreams and visions, cause him to choose death rather than life, set him up for a mark to shoot at, break him with tempest, multiply his wounds without cause, take his breath, fill him with bitterness, plunge him in the ditch, condemn him without cause, oppress him, despise him, destroy him, hunt him as a lion, witness against him, increase His wrath upon him, torment him, count him as an enemy, destroy his hope, deliver him to the ungodly, be unmerciful to him, refuse to hear him, or afflict him with suffering.\n\nGod did not destroy the perfect, prosper the wicked, make the ungodly secure, and oppress the godly. These are false lies of the devil that he got Job to utter. God is not this kind of evil being.\n\nThe devil is the cause of all these misfortunes—and this is the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth. Anyone who accuses God of doing these things is falsely accusing Him of wrongdoing.\n\nThese are the kinds of doctrines constantly expressed in modern churches by preachers who know infinitely less about God after studying the 66 books of the Bible than Job knew without the Bible. These false doctrines are taught by most modern religious teachers—this is what they teach about God and His dealings with men.\n\nTherefore, when someone comes along contradicting such teachings, they're classed as fanatical and heretical in the extreme. The truth is: they are the heretics.\n\n## God is a Real and True Parent\n\nWhat parent on Earth would choose or will for their children to suffer like Job? Which one would deliberately take away their children's riches and give them to others? Which one would kill their children, take away their health and exalted position among men, and cause their spouses and friends to become estranged from them? Which one would claim any degree of love for their children and at the same time do everything in their power to impose upon them sickness, sin, suffering, poverty, and failure in life?\n\nSuch things are unthinkable of any earthly parent who is normally sane. Yet so-called sane people go around accusing God of being this kind of parent. On the other hand, these same people will say—when directly confronted with the question of God's love—that He loves His children more than any earthly parent.\n\nThink of it like this: It's similar to praising a parent's unconditional love while simultaneously describing them torturing their children. Such contradictory theories don't make sense, to say the least. You cannot believe both theories about God. You must either believe that God is the most loving, just, holy, righteous, and merciful Heavenly Father—or that God is the most unjust, unmerciful, unloving, unrighteous, unholy, tyrannical, and despotic Heavenly Father that could be conceived of.\n\nWhich are we to believe to be in harmony with the Bible and to have the right understanding of what God as a Father should be?\n\n## The Trouble is Willful Ignorance of Truth\n\nJesus Christ taught us that if men who were sinful knew how to be true parents and give good things to their children, how much more would God give good things to those who ask Him (Mt. 7:7-11). Jesus taught that the devil seeks to kill, steal, and\n\n---\n\nImminence doesn't produce passivity — it produces urgency. Watching for signs doesn't produce anxiety — it produces clarity. So here's the question: What one relationship in your life are you aware needs to be invested in before it's too late — a person who doesn't know Christ, a reconciliation that hasn't happened, a conversation that keeps getting postponed? The Rapture is imminent. What are you waiting for?	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xooi000f8071glp17vrf	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Occult Entertainment	READING	\N	2	\N	t	![Occult Entertainment](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsuJ4iMzVZIJS2tQ1kPsY7EcO3rv8DqhnMN9ly)\n\n## Occult Entertainment\n\nShe had read all seven Harry Potter books twice and watched all eight films at least three times. She would tell you they were children's stories about good triumphing over evil — that Voldemort was the villain, that Harry represented sacrifice and love. She would be right about the narrative.\n\nShe had never been told about mirror neurons — the neurological mechanism through which the brain rehearses what the eyes observe, forming neural pathways that make observed behaviors feel familiar and eventually normal. She had never been told that twelve years of absorbing detailed descriptions of spell mechanics, wizarding culture, and dark magic had trained her brain to experience the occult as comfortable and familiar rather than as something Scripture describes as abomination.\n\nWhen her college roommate introduced her to a Wiccan circle, she did not experience the visceral alarm she should have. It felt surprisingly familiar. She had, neurologically, been practicing for years.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nOccult entertainment includes books, films, video games, tabletop games, streaming series, and music that glorify, normalize, or aestheticize witchcraft, sorcery, demonology, and occult themes. Key examples include Harry Potter, Dungeons & Dragons, occult horror films, and the growing catalog of streaming content built around witchcraft, vampirism, and demonic entities as sympathetic protagonists.\n\nThe global entertainment market exceeds $2 trillion annually. Occult-themed content is one of its fastest-growing categories. Marvel and DC productions regularly feature sorcerers, dimensional entities, and "dark magic" as heroic forces. Disney has increasingly incorporated spell-casting and "dark magic" as plot elements. What was fringe in the 1980s is now considered family entertainment.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\n[Philippians 4:8](data-scripture="Philippians 4:8"): *"Whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely... think on these things."* The instruction is not about the danger of impure thoughts but about the formative power of what the mind dwells on. What you think on, you become.\n\nThe neurological reality: the brain does not fully distinguish between observed and experienced behavior. Mirror neurons fire when watching characters cast spells, summon entities, or practice occult rituals — creating neural rehearsal of the observed actions. Repeated exposure creates pathways that make actual occult involvement feel familiar and accessible. This is not theoretical. It is documented mechanism.\n\nEntertainment is formation. The question is not whether your children understand that Harry Potter is fiction. It is what their neural pathways are being trained to find normal.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Desensitization of the conscience.** The conscience is trained by what it accepts as normal. A conscience that has spent years accepting occult themes as entertainment will not reliably produce alarm when occult involvement becomes available in real life. This is the pipeline: entertainment normalizes → conscience desensitizes → real participation feels like a natural next step.\n\n**Demons are drawn to attention.** Sustained, entertained attention directed at demonic themes is a form of invitation — not the formal invitation of a séance, but an invitation nonetheless. The demonic entities associated with the themes being focused on are drawn to the attention being paid to them.\n\n**The gateway progression is documented.** Harry Potter's enormous cultural influence coincided with measurable increases in self-identified Wiccan and pagan practitioners, particularly among young adults who grew up with the books. Correlation is not causation, but the pipeline from occult entertainment to occult practice is not invented.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThis is the lesson that requires the most personal inventory because occult entertainment is so thoroughly normalized that examining it feels like cultural fanaticism.\n\nHere is the simple test: [Psalm 101:3](data-scripture="Psalm 101:3") — *"I will set no wicked thing before mine eyes."* Not "I will not set deliberately occult things before my eyes." Not "I will avoid clearly Satanic content." *No wicked thing.*\n\nThe standard is high. The question is not what you can justify watching. The question is what you want your mind's formation to look like — what neural landscape you want for yourself and your children. That landscape is built one evening of entertainment at a time.\n\n---\n\n*Books and films normalize the occult. The next lesson examines how music goes further — it doesn't just normalize it, it makes you worship.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *What was the first piece of occult-themed media that genuinely fascinated you? What do you think drew you to it?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76y46s0003w0ylmdo7ynwt	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Wave 1 Checkpoint: Cultural Entry Points	QUIZ	\N	7	\N	t	## Wave 1 Checkpoint: Cultural Entry Points\n\nBefore moving into Wave 2, confirm your understanding of the six cultural entry points. Three questions — return to any lesson where your answer is uncertain.\n\n---\n\n**1. According to this course, what distinguishes horoscopes and astrology from innocent entertainment?**\n\nA) Astrology is only spiritually dangerous when practiced by professionals\nB) Any engagement — even "just for fun" — constitutes a divination transaction with the familiar spirits that staff the system, regardless of the user's intent\nC) Horoscopes are harmless because planetary bodies are part of God's creation\nD) The danger is purely psychological: people make worse decisions when they follow astrology\n\n---\n\n**2. The course argues that Halloween's spiritual danger lies not in costumes or candy but in:**\n\nA) Its commercial exploitation of death imagery\nB) Its historical roots as a Celtic agricultural festival\nC) Its function as a recognized occult high holy day — a covenant by participation, knowingly or not, with the spiritual system that consecrated it\nD) The glorification of violence in modern Halloween decorations\n\n---\n\n**3. Celebrity and political idolatry are identified as spiritual attacks rather than mere cultural habits because:**\n\nA) Celebrities and politicians are statistically more likely to be involved in the occult\nB) The emotional and devotional architecture of fan culture and political tribalism mirrors the structure of worship — loyalty, sacrifice of relationships, identity formation — directed at a creature rather than the Creator\nC) Admiring successful people violates the biblical command to avoid comparison\nD) Social media platforms are designed by people with occult affiliations\n\n---\n\n**Answer Key**\n\n1. **B** — Every divination engagement is a transaction regardless of intent. [Deuteronomy 18:12](data-scripture="Deuteronomy 18:12") has no exception for casual use.\n2. **C** — Halloween functions as covenant by participation. Ignorance does not revoke the spiritual transaction.\n3. **B** — [1 John 5:21](data-scripture="1 John 5:21") and [Exodus 20:5](data-scripture="Exodus 20:5"): idolatry is structural, not merely aesthetic.\n\n---\n\n*If you missed any answer, return to that lesson before continuing. Wave 2 begins with what everyone called exercise.*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xoo900078071regervtm	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	The Enneagram	READING	\N	15	\N	t	![The Enneagram](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Os4EK9jsL3Ls52XczwCYNqdZVf8hMUGlEvQ0nD)\n\n## The Enneagram\n\nThe church small group had been working through the Enneagram for six weeks. People were finding it genuinely useful — understanding why they reacted the way they did, recognizing patterns, experiencing the relief of being typed and named. The pastor said it was the best tool for community self-understanding he had ever used.\n\nOne member did not say what she was thinking: that she had researched the system's origins before the study started, and that what she found had troubled her deeply enough that she had spent two weeks in prayer about whether to mention it. She had decided to be quiet. The group seemed to be benefiting. She did not want to be the one who took that away.\n\nShe was choosing community peace over spiritual clarity. And the entity that had channeled the Enneagram was counting on exactly that calculation.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nThe Enneagram is a nine-type personality system that has gained widespread adoption in Christian churches, seminaries, and counseling programs as a tool for self-understanding and spiritual growth. Each of the nine types has corresponding "wings," "arrows," and growth paths creating a complex map of human character.\n\nIts psychological utility is real — people find it genuinely illuminating for self-understanding. The question is not whether it produces insight but where those insights come from.\n\nThe Enneagram was not developed through psychological research. George Gurdjieff, a 20th-century mystic who blended Sufism, Eastern philosophy, and occultism, introduced the nine-pointed figure in esoteric teaching. Its development into a personality system occurred largely through automatic writing — a state of dissociation in which the writer yields conscious control to an external intelligence. This is the definition of channeling. The personality typology was received from demonic sources.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe deception is utility. The Enneagram is genuinely useful as a personality framework — because familiar spirits are ancient students of human psychology who understand human behavioral patterns with a depth no living psychologist can match. An occult personality system could be expected to be insightful, for the same reason a psychic reading can be accurate: the entities behind it have extensive knowledge.\n\nBut the usefulness of a system does not establish its spiritual safety. The question is: what enters through the system alongside its insights?\n\n[2 Corinthians 5:17](data-scripture="2 Corinthians 5:17"): *"If any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away."* [Ephesians 2:10](data-scripture="Ephesians 2:10"): *"We are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus."* Scripture defines human identity through the lens of new creation in Christ — not through occult typology. When a believer spends more time understanding themselves through their Enneagram type than through Scripture's description of who they are in Christ, their identity formation has been partially captured by a system built to serve a different framework.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Channeling contamination.** The system was received through channeling. Its architects were, knowingly or unknowingly, operating as mediums. The spirits that authored the system are invited back into the classroom when the system is taught.\n\n**Identity replacement is progressive.** Type 4 who sees their melancholy as a spiritually significant feature of their type rather than as something the Holy Spirit wants to transform is less likely to pursue sanctification in that area. The Enneagram's tendency to normalize rather than challenge character patterns works directly against the Spirit's work of transformation.\n\n**Church-wide deception when leadership endorses it.** When a pastor endorses the Enneagram as a discipleship tool, they bring the spiritual architecture of its origins into the congregation's spiritual formation process. The people who have no interest in the occult attend the Enneagram study without knowing what they are bringing into their lives.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThis is one of the more sensitive lessons in this course because many people have received genuine benefit from the Enneagram and are invested in it. Acknowledging the problem feels like losing something useful.\n\nHere is the honest exchange: you can gain everything the Enneagram offers about yourself — and more — through sustained engagement with Scripture, the work of the Holy Spirit, and the honest input of people in covenant community who know you well. You do not need a channeled occult system to know yourself.\n\nThe action required is simple: stop using it, stop teaching it, and repent for the times you built your spiritual identity on a type rather than on who Christ says you are.\n\n---\n\n*The Enneagram reframes identity through a personality grid. The next lesson examines what happens when someone reaches past identity altogether — into the unconscious mind.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Has your church used the Enneagram for spiritual formation or small groups? What was your reaction when you first encountered the information in this lesson?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xony00018071ieo7r1uj	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Smudging and Burning Sage	READING	\N	17	\N	t	![Smudging and Burning Sage](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Osk1y22w8rZcMaXYe27SivEmH1t8Ad0OozjUKI)\n\n## Smudging and Burning Sage\n\nShe bought the sage bundle at a boutique wellness shop between a candle store and a juice bar. It cost eleven dollars. The card attached explained how to wave the smoke through every room to "clear negative energy." She did it after every difficult conversation. She did it when she moved into a new apartment. She did it when her ex-boyfriend's energy felt "stuck."\n\nShe was not consciously doing anything spiritual. It was just a pleasant ritual, like burning incense. She did not know that the ritual she was performing had been developed within animistic traditions specifically to invite spirit entities to inhabit a space and drive out the spirits of enemies.\n\nShe did not know the clearing she felt afterward was sometimes the departure of one spirit that had completed its assignment, making room for the invitation she had just sent.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nSmudging is the burning of dried sage, palo santo, sweetgrass, or other herbs in a ritual intended to cleanse a space of negative energy and invite positive spiritual presences. It originates primarily in Plains Native American and Pacific Northwest indigenous traditions, though similar practices exist in shamanic cultures worldwide.\n\nThe wellness industry has commodified it into a billion-dollar aesthetic — sold in boutiques, recommended by interior design influencers, performed at yoga studios and wellness retreats. The ritualistic intent of the indigenous practice has been stripped of its context but retained in its spiritual function.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nSage and palo santo are plants. They have no inherent spiritual power. But the ritual structure through which they are used — developed within animistic spiritual traditions, often accompanied by directional invocations and prayers to nature spirits — is designed to invite specific spiritual entities and establish their authority over a space.\n\nThe "clearing" felt after smudging is not the removal of negative energy in any biblical sense. Only the blood of Jesus Christ has power to cleanse a space spiritually. When smudging produces a felt sense of clearing, the most common explanation is one of two things: either the practitioner has experienced a temporary placebo response, or a demonic presence has temporarily vacated the space as part of a deeper strategy — creating the experiential confirmation that keeps the person using the practice.\n\n[Psalm 51:7](data-scripture="Psalm 51:7"): *"Purge me with hyssop, and I shall be clean."* David knew what cleansed. It was not sage.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Directional invocations summon spirits.** Many smudging rituals include prayers to the spirits of the four directions — East, South, West, North. This is functionally identical to pagan worship condemned throughout the Hebrew scriptures. The spirits being addressed are real and respond to the invitation.\n\n**False cleansing displaces Christ's sufficiency.** When a person smudges their home to spiritually cleanse it, they are acting on the premise that a plant can do what only Christ's blood can do. This is an implicit denial of Christ's sufficiency — which is a topos, a legal ground, that the enemy exploits.\n\n**Syncretism is the specific sin.** The Christian who smudges "just in case" is performing the precise mixture of the holy and profane that the entire sacrificial system of the Old Testament was designed to prevent. [Leviticus 10:1-2](data-scripture="Leviticus 10:1-2") records what happened when Nadab and Abihu offered "strange fire" before the Lord — fire He had not commanded. The combination of genuine faith and unauthorized spiritual practice is not a safer version of spirituality. It is its own category of danger.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nIf you have smudged your home — once, regularly, at a wellness event — the space was used as a ritual platform for spirit invocation, regardless of your intent.\n\nThe biblical cleansing of a home: confession of sin before God, application of the blood of Jesus through prayer spoken in every room, anointing with oil in the name of the Lord, reading Scripture aloud through the entire space, playing worship music, and where possible having mature believers pray through the home together. This is the protocol of [James 5:14-15](data-scripture="James 5:14-15") applied to a dwelling.\n\nThe aesthetic appeal of smudging is real. The spiritual emptiness of its alternative — authoritative prayer in the name of Jesus Christ — is zero. The fire of the Holy Spirit does not require a ritual to grant permission for its entry.\n\n---\n\n*Ten practices. All marketed as healing. All doing something else. The next lesson opens Wave 3 — what happened when people went looking for God in the wrong places.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you smudged your home or allowed it to be smudged? What were you told it was accomplishing — and has any pattern of oppression continued afterward?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xoo600058071h2k759e0	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	The Contemplative Prayer Movement	READING	\N	21	\N	t	![The Contemplative Prayer Movement](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsCapOyye78vbPqVLiKnDy6up93CGaNzkh5HsQ)\n\n## The Contemplative Prayer Movement\n\nShe had been in Christian ministry for twelve years when the seminary offered a course in "spiritual formation." The professor was gentle, deeply read, clearly sincere. He taught them centering prayer: choose a sacred word, sit in silence, and when thoughts arise, return to the word and let them pass without engagement.\n\nShe practiced for three months. In the fourth month, during a session, she felt a presence — warm, deeply peaceful, unmistakably "there." She was certain it was God. She began to structure her entire devotional life around these encounters. The Bible felt dry and distant by comparison. The presence felt alive.\n\nA visiting speaker at her church preached on testing spirits. She went home and tested the presence. She asked it directly: *Is Jesus Christ come in the flesh?* [1 John 4:2](data-scripture="1 John 4:2"). The presence did not answer. She asked again. The warmth became cold. The session ended.\n\nShe spent two weeks processing what that meant.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nThe contemplative prayer movement encompasses practices including centering prayer, lectio divina (as currently taught), soaking prayer, and the spiritual formation curriculum associated with figures like Richard Rohr, Thomas Merton, Thomas Keating, and Henri Nouwen.\n\nCentering prayer, as formalized by Thomas Keating, instructs practitioners to select a "sacred word," sit in silence for twenty minutes twice daily, and use the word to dismiss all thoughts as they arise. The goal is described as "resting in God's presence beyond thoughts, words, and images."\n\nRichard Rohr openly teaches that all religions access the same divine reality, denies the necessity of the cross, and promotes universalism. This is not merely heterodox — it is the content of another gospel.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nBiblical prayer is communication. [Philippians 4:6](data-scripture="Philippians 4:6"): *"Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God."* Speaking. Petitioning. Thanking. Active, verbal, relational.\n\nCentering prayer is the deliberate emptying of the mind — functionally identical to Transcendental Meditation, with a Christian sacred word substituted for a Hindu mantra. The theological framing is different. The spiritual mechanics are the same. Both produce the empty swept house that Jesus described as vulnerable to worse possession than the original.\n\nThe "presence" experienced in centering prayer is frequently a demonic spirit mimicking God's peace. The test of [1 John 4:1](data-scripture="1 John 4:1") — *"test the spirits"* — requires active discernment, precisely the faculty that centering prayer trains practitioners to suspend. A system that teaches you to turn off your discernment and receive whatever presence arrives is a system designed to make you unable to detect what arrives.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The empty-mind technique creates the same vulnerability regardless of framing.** The demonic does not care whether the practitioner says "Om" or "Jesus" while sweeping their mind clean. The swept mind is the swept mind. The entities that occupy it are the same.\n\n**Contemplative teachers drift consistently toward universalism.** This is not coincidence. The demonic entities that staff the contemplative encounter deliver consistent content: all religions lead to God, the cross is one path among many, orthodox doctrine is a limitation on spirituality. Practitioners who submit to these encounters over years become systematically unable to hold biblical theology. Their doctrine dissolves from the inside.\n\n**The subtlety is the danger.** Contemplative practice is endorsed in seminaries and by otherwise orthodox teachers. It feels more spiritual than it is. The person who says "I stopped reading Scripture because I prefer just sitting in God's presence" has replaced the Word with an encounter they cannot verify — and may not be able to distinguish from an encounter with a deceiving spirit.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nThe test for any spiritual encounter: [1 John 4:2](data-scripture="1 John 4:2") — *"Hereby know ye the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesseth that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is of God."* Ask the presence directly. A genuine encounter with the Holy Spirit does not fail [1 John 4:2](data-scripture="1 John 4:2"). A familiar spirit cannot pass it.\n\nIf you have practiced centering prayer and experienced encounters that have not been tested, test them now. If they cannot be identified as the Holy Spirit bearing witness with Scripture, repent for the practice, renounce the spirits that provided the counterfeit encounters, and return to the biblical model of prayer: spoken, petitionary, Scripture-anchored, relational.\n\nThe God who desires to be known does not hide from those who seek Him in His Word. [Jeremiah 29:13](data-scripture="Jeremiah 29:13"): *"And ye shall seek me, and find me, when ye shall search for me with all your heart."*\n\n---\n\n*Contemplative prayer empties the mind in private. The next lesson examines a ritual that enacts the same emptying in public, in stone, in the churchyard.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Has your church offered centering prayer, silent retreat, or lectio divina as an emptying practice? Did you participate — and what did you experience?*	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xoob00098071t52r8je0	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Labyrinth Walking	READING	\N	22	\N	t	![Labyrinth Walking](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsS1C5YbJ9p8Osi7f2L3jgeayVJxF6MbNCPdun)\n\n## Labyrinth Walking\n\nShe was on a church retreat at a beautiful conference center. The schedule included an optional "labyrinth walk" — a large circular stone path on the grounds. The retreat leader described it as an ancient Christian practice for contemplative prayer, walking toward the center as a symbol of drawing near to God.\n\nShe walked it. She felt something. She could not say what — a presence, a heaviness, something that felt spiritual but not quite right. She asked the retreat leader about it afterward. The leader said the feeling of presence during labyrinth walks was exactly the point.\n\nShe did not know that the labyrinth predates Christianity by millennia, that it was used in goddess worship and mystery religion initiation rites, and that "an ancient Christian practice" was not quite the accurate description she had been given.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nA labyrinth is a circular walking path with a single route leading to a center and back out. Labyrinths have been installed in churches, hospitals, universities, and retreat centers as tools for contemplative prayer and "spiritual pilgrimage." Their use has been championed particularly within progressive Christian communities and contemplative spirituality networks.\n\nThe claim that labyrinth walking is an ancient Christian practice is historically misleading. Labyrinths predate Christianity by thousands of years. The Cretan labyrinth of Greek mythology — the site of the Minotaur, the dwelling place of a monster — is the oldest documented example. Similar designs appear in ancient Egypt, Rome, and pre-Columbian Americas. All of these contexts are explicitly pagan.\n\nSome medieval Christian churches did incorporate labyrinth designs into their floors. But the practice of deliberately walking them for spiritual encounter was reintroduced to Christianity in the late 20th century by neo-pagans and New Age practitioners who claimed — without strong historical evidence — a continuous Christian contemplative tradition.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe journey toward the center and back out is a symbolic structure with deep roots in mystery religion and occult initiation. In ancient Mystery cults, initiation involved a symbolic descent into the underworld and a return — death and resurrection as mystical experience. The labyrinth encodes this structure spatially.\n\nWalking a labyrinth is, in its original symbolic framework, an initiation rite — an enactment of the soul's descent into the underworld and return. Whether the contemporary Christian who walks one understands this is irrelevant to its spiritual function. The symbols carry what they were built to carry, regardless of the walker's intention.\n\n[Jeremiah 10:2](data-scripture="Jeremiah 10:2"): *"Thus saith the LORD, Learn not the way of the heathen."* The instruction does not say "Learn not the way of the heathen unless it has a nice contemplative frame around it."\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**Pagan symbolism carries pagan spiritual reality.** The slow, rhythmic walking of a labyrinth induces the same meditative state as any other slow repetitive physical practice — a state of reduced analytical function and heightened spiritual receptivity. The labyrinth's symbolic architecture, derived from mystery religion initiation, shapes what that receptivity opens toward.\n\n**False spiritual encounters are produced and attributed to God.** Participants frequently report "profound encounters" during labyrinth walks. These encounters feel spiritual — because they are. The question is the source. Spiritual experiences produced through pagan ritual architecture are not encounters with the Holy Spirit; they are encounters with spirits that have operated through that architecture for millennia.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nChristians walk by faith, not by ritual geometry. There is no biblical precedent for walking in circles to encounter God. God encounters His people through His Word, through prayer, through corporate worship, through the sacraments, and through His sovereign movement in ordinary life.\n\nIf you have participated in labyrinth walks and experienced what felt like spiritual encounters, test those encounters. Apply [1 John 4:2](data-scripture="1 John 4:2"). If they do not confirm Christ, repent for the participation and renounce whatever produced the encounter.\n\nThe retreat center is beautiful. The stone path is peaceful. But God does not require ancient pagan initiation geometry to be found by those who seek Him.\n\n---\n\n*The labyrinth is ancient spiritual architecture. The next lesson examines what happens when people go looking for spiritual entities in places they were never meant to be found.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you walked a prayer labyrinth? What were you taught it was for — and what actually happened spiritually while you walked?*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk44j0002ewhjsrq3llcx	cmnknk44i0001ewhju56drbw5	Course Overview: God's Universal Plan Chart	IMAGE	\N	0	/gods-plan.png	t	Study this chart carefully before diving into the lessons. It provides a visual overview of God's complete plan from eternity past to eternity future — the very blueprint of the Bible.	\N	\N	\N
cmq76xood000b80710cltfl0m	cmq76xgul000jhks877ughys4	Paranormal Investigation	READING	\N	23	\N	t	![Paranormal Investigation](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8Oson0Xm7WxwEUd728la9hHriMsfOkGYRKDCuLZ)\n\n## Paranormal Investigation\n\nHe thought he was doing science. EMF meter, spirit box, full-spectrum camera, digital voice recorder. He had documented seventeen locations across four states. His YouTube channel had 40,000 subscribers. He believed he was proving the existence of an afterlife — that consciousness persisted beyond death, that the dead could communicate with the living.\n\nHe was right that something was communicating. He was wrong about what it was.\n\nTwo years after he started the channel, his marriage ended. His daughter told her therapist she was afraid of him. He slept three to four hours a night because something was in his room. He had brought home from every investigation exactly what he had gone to find — except it was not the dead.\n\n---\n\n## What It Is\n\nParanormal investigation uses electronic devices — EMF (electromagnetic field) meters, spirit boxes (radio-frequency sweeping devices), EVP (electronic voice phenomena) recorders, thermal cameras — to detect and communicate with entities believed to be the spirits of deceased people. The practice has been popularized through television programs and a growing amateur community that views it as a legitimate form of spiritual inquiry.\n\nThe underlying premise is that the dead remain in locations where they lived or died, retaining consciousness and the capacity to communicate with the living.\n\n## The Demonic Deception\n\nThe dead do not roam accessible dimensions. [Hebrews 9:27](data-scripture="Hebrews 9:27"): *"It is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment."* One life. Death. Judgment. The dead are not in abandoned buildings at midnight responding to spirit box frequencies.\n\nWhat investigators encounter are familiar spirits — demons that have observed people's lives and can impersonate them with sufficient accuracy to produce the experiences investigators are seeking. The EVP that sounds like your grandmother's voice is not your grandmother. It is a demon that knows what your grandmother's voice sounded like.\n\n[Leviticus 19:31](data-scripture="Leviticus 19:31"): *"Regard not them that have familiar spirits, neither seek after wizards, to be defiled by them."* The word *defile* is precise — this is not merely a moral prohibition, it is a description of what occurs spiritually when humans seek communication with these entities.\n\n## How It Opens the Door\n\n**The deliberate seeking is the legal invitation.** The investigator who enters a location with equipment designed to facilitate spirit communication has performed a voluntary act of spirit contact — identical in spiritual function to visiting a medium, with different hardware.\n\n**Entities follow investigators home.** Every experienced deliverance minister who has worked with paranormal investigators reports the same phenomenon: entities encountered at investigation locations attach to investigators and accompany them home. The investigator who can no longer sleep, whose children are frightened, whose relationships are deteriorating — these are the typical post-investigation symptoms of carried demonic attachment.\n\n**Media amplification extends the exposure.** Watching paranormal investigation programs opens the viewer to the same spiritual atmosphere operating through the screen. This is not about pixels. It is about sustained attention directed at demonic activity — which functions as an invitation regardless of the physical distance.\n\n## What This Means for You Right Now\n\nHave you watched paranormal investigation programming regularly? Have you visited supposedly haunted locations? Have you participated in any investigation activity?\n\nEach of these represents a degree of voluntary engagement with familiar spirits seeking communication. The degree of engagement corresponds roughly to the degree of spiritual exposure.\n\nRepent for the seeking. Renounce every entity encountered or observed, whether in person or through a screen. If entities followed you home — if there have been disturbances in your home, disturbances in your sleep, or felt presences since engaging with this content — pray specifically for the cleansing of your home and the severing of every attachment.\n\nAnd if you have children who watch these programs: the children in haunted homes are the most vulnerable targets for the spirits that investigators invite. What you allow through the screen enters the spiritual atmosphere of your house.\n\n---\n\n*Ghost hunters seek spirit contact through technology. The next lesson examines a method that uses chemistry to open the same doors — with consequences technology cannot produce.*\n\n> **Community Discussion:** *Have you watched ghost-hunting content regularly? Has that content changed your working understanding of what death and the afterlife look like?*	\N	\N	\N
cmnknk4br002eewhj3yc5srij	cmnknk4bp001qewhjk5bcqnfj	Supplement 26 — For Lessons 51 & 52	SUPPLEMENT	1983	23	\N	t	![Supplement 26 — For Lessons 51 & 52](https://hm8qhte0o7.ufs.sh/f/tgGixBSSw8OsEhjyCZtdLWqJHyu8Q5MfmIRAjonSBKDvC0V2)\n\nYou've arrived at the final reference point of God's Universal Plan for Creation. Fifty-two lessons, twenty-five supplements, and one unbroken argument: that God has always known exactly what He was doing — from the dateless past to the eternal future — and that every word of Scripture fits perfectly into that plan. This supplement serves as your complete course index: a navigational map for everything you've studied.\n\nTable of Contents                                                                  +\n                                                                                    +\n Title Page                                                                         +\n                                                                                    +\n Lesson 1: General Subjects Concerning God's Universal Plan for Creation Discussed  +\n                                                                       \n\n             +\n > I. Importance of the Study of “God’s Universal Plan for Creation”                +\n                                                                                    +\n > II. The Simplicity of the Plan of God for Man                                    +\n                                                                                    +\n > III. Definition of the Terms and Expressions of the Ages                         +\n                                                                                    +\n > IV. The Dispensation of Angels                                                   +\n                                                                                    +\n > V. The Seven Dispensations of Man Between the Two Eternities                     +\n           \n\n                    